{"type":"message","id":"3bbd55af","parentId":"80bc466c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:49:21.989Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8VPvUlsv5N5WDBAakvkaNzxr|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590a189e487d09c015147f7f7f711","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: rp-build\ndescription: Plan and implement substantial changes with RepoPrompt Context Builder. Use for unfamiliar repositories or changes spanning several files.\ncompatibility: Requires RepoPrompt MCP and Pi file tools.\n---\n\n# RepoPrompt Build\n\nUse the user's request as the task.\n\nStart with Git status. Locate the repository root before asking RepoPrompt to inspect anything.\n\nCall `repoprompt_context_builder` with a precise task description and `response_type: \"plan\"`. Review its plan and assumptions before changing files. Call `repoprompt_workspace_context` when you need the complete selected context. Ask the user only when an unresolved choice would materially change behavior or scope.\n\nImplement through Pi `edit` and `write`. The OrbStack repository mount is read-only, so never use RepoPrompt `apply_edits` or `file_actions`. Follow repository test-first rules for behavior changes. Run focused tests after each change, then run broader relevant checks.\n\nDo not improvise.\n\nUse `repoprompt_oracle_send` only for a specific question left open by Context Builder. Continue with the returned `chat_id` rather than starting an unrelated conversation.\n\nFor substantial changes, run RepoPrompt review against the final Git diff. Report changed files and commands run. Include validation results and remaining risks. Do not claim completion while required checks fail.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789235361989}}
{"type":"message","id":"e6749d39","parentId":"3bbd55af","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:49:32.443Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning transfer publication context builder**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590a4723c87d0a1b2025f51da4b00\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning transfer publication context builder**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_HBPxBSlK6UncfHuPs8shAAC8|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590a518bc87d0b14c06ec7d86b8aa","name":"repoprompt_context_builder","arguments":{"instructions":"<task>Implement next Phase 6 milestone after committed artifact codec and committed Git bundle support: bounded authenticated atomic publication of the paired committed bundle and exact worktree artifact, with a typed receipt binding both artifact digests and lengths, immutable declared limits, source-state digest, replica identity and generation. Then wire verification and publication into broker-owned replica lifecycle without carrying artifact bytes in SQLite and without holding SQLite handles across external effects or await.</task><context>Current HEAD includes abff2b2d artifact/reconciliation and 2c781b53 bounded Git bundle. Existing uncommitted Phase 6 files include broker_replica_journal.py, broker_protocol.py, broker_runtime.py, execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, root_launcher.py, relay, and tests. Preserve broker lifecycle v2 and legacy v1. Replica journal stages are ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Root actions remain prepare, launch, reclaim only. Publication must fail closed on unsafe paths, symlinks, digest mismatch, partial pairs, overwrite, timeout, cancellation, or uncertain acknowledgement. Artifact bytes stay outside SQLite. Use atomic same-filesystem rename and sync ordering. Signed broker frames supply end-to-end authentication. All gates remain disabled by default. Do not conflate logical authority with physical execution ownership.</context><discovery_agent-guidelines>Find existing publication durability patterns, broker protocol signing, replica journal receipt APIs, runtime path policy, and root staging/promotion semantics. Produce implementation-ready boundaries, exact types and call flow, red tests, and focused checks. Identify whether this milestone should first be a standalone transfer store before broker wiring.</discovery_agent-guidelines>","response_type":"plan"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":573,"output":380,"cacheRead":84096,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":15,"totalTokens":85049,"cost":{"input":0.0028650000000000004,"output":0.0114,"cacheRead":0.042047999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.056312999999999995}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789235362001,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590a29bc087d0b871471bd5674214","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"31459ba2","parentId":"e6749d39","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:50:33.746Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_HBPxBSlK6UncfHuPs8shAAC8|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590a518bc87d0b14c06ec7d86b8aa","toolName":"repoprompt_context_builder","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"backend\":\"headless\",\"chat_id\":\"3D5B7714-92C0-49C4-9EF0-1A187871500D\",\"response\":\"I’m blocked because the target repository is not present in this workspace.\\n\\nI checked every Git repository under `/workspace` and `/tmp`, including all reachable Git objects and branches:\\n\\n- Commits `abff2b2d` and `2c781b53` do not exist.\\n- None contains `broker_replica_journal.py`, `broker_protocol.py`, `broker_runtime.py`, `execution_broker.py`, `execution_daemons.py`, or `root_launcher.py`.\\n- `/workspace` itself is not a Git repository.\\n\\nPlease mount the intended checkout or provide its path. Once available, I can implement and verify the Phase 6 milestone without touching the unrelated dirty repositories currently present.\"}"}],"details":{"server":"repoprompt","tool":"context_builder"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789235433746}}
{"type":"message","id":"d1d32c0f","parentId":"31459ba2","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:50:39.037Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning subagent delegation strategy**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590ec801c87d0a1c0297220e2a205\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning subagent delegation strategy**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_42amoOjDwcPMHyuqLkDpyZyM|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590eec5f487d09be12fcd152a4158","name":"subagent","arguments":{"action":"list"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":770,"output":69,"cacheRead":84480,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":49,"totalTokens":85319,"cost":{"input":0.00385,"output":0.0020700000000000002,"cacheRead":0.04224,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.04816}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789235433754,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590ea383c87d0b5b8e429d9bdfdd1","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"876dbfc6","parentId":"d1d32c0f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:50:39.757Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_42amoOjDwcPMHyuqLkDpyZyM|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590eec5f487d09be12fcd152a4158","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Executable agents:\n- delegate (builtin): Lightweight subagent that inherits the parent model with no default reads\n- final-review (user, aliases: production-final-review): Sol Max independent design and correctness review with a remediation plan.\n- oracle (builtin, context: fork, aliases: advisor): High-context decision-consistency oracle that protects inherited state and prevents drift\n- planner (user): Read-only Sol planning for parent-approved implementation tasks.\n- qwen-implementer (user): Local Qwen implementation worker for approved file-scoped task packets\n- researcher (builtin): Autonomous web researcher — searches, evaluates, and synthesizes a focused research brief\n- reviewer (user): Read-only local Qwen reviewer for optional mechanical pre-review.\n- scout (user): Fast read-only repository reconnaissance using local Qwen.\n- test-writer (user): Local Qwen test writer for explicit behavior through an existing test interface.\n- worker (user): Default GLM High implementation worker for settled behavior and architecture.\n- worker-advanced (user): GLM Max worker for approved invariants across interacting states and failure paths.\n- worker-expert (user): Sol xhigh diagnosis and expert implementation for uncertain causes or novel algorithms.\n- worker-simple (user): Local Qwen implementation for fully specified mechanical changes.\n\nChains:\n- (none)"}],"details":{"mode":"management","results":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789235439757}}
{"type":"message","id":"8add2b6a","parentId":"876dbfc6","timestamp":"2026-09-12T17:50:49.845Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting key files for mapping**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590f19dac87d0a892027aaf77700a\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Inspecting key files for mapping**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_MnJ5DtRngmsiAcdDU8ZYRnFU|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590f2acf487d096bc6962c99dbc1e","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"return runs.run('transfer-publication-plan', {agent:'planner', task:[\n  'Plan next Phase 6 milestone in /Users/user/projects/yinshi. Read-only.',\n  'Current committed modules: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py and workspace_replica_bundle.py. Current uncommitted Phase 6 modules include broker_replica_journal.py, broker_protocol.py, broker_runtime.py, execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, root_launcher.py, workspace_publication.py, workspace_runtime_paths.py, and tests.',\n  'Goal: bounded authenticated atomic publication of paired committed bundle and exact worktree artifact, with typed receipt binding both digests and lengths, immutable declared limits, source-state digest, replica identity and generation. Wire verify and publish stages to broker-owned replica authority only if boundary is settled.',\n  'Constraints: artifact bytes outside SQLite. No SQLite handle crosses external effect or await. Root protocol remains prepare, launch, reclaim. No fourth action. Broker signed protocol is end-to-end authentication. Atomic same-filesystem rename plus directory sync. Reject unsafe paths, symlinks, preexisting targets, partial pairs, digest mismatch, length mismatch, timeout/cancellation, and uncertain acknowledgement. All gates disabled. Preserve broker lifecycle v2 and read-only v1.',\n  'Inspect current files and existing patterns. Return implementation-ready plan with exact module boundaries, types, stage ordering, owners, permitted transitions, failure outcomes, red tests, commands, and whether standalone publication store should precede broker wiring. Do not edit.'\n].join('\\n')})","async":false,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","timeoutMs":1200000,"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":8,"graceTurns":2},"toolBudget":{"soft":30,"hard":45,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"]},"chatProgress":"live-card"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":475,"output":443,"cacheRead":85120,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":31,"totalTokens":86038,"cost":{"input":0.0023750000000000004,"output":0.01329,"cacheRead":0.04256,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.058225}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789235439762,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590f0365c87d0a85ab85c7f8cdd10","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a9f594c8","parentId":"8add2b6a","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:03:21.981Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_MnJ5DtRngmsiAcdDU8ZYRnFU|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa590f2acf487d096bc6962c99dbc1e","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"transfer-publication-plan\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"1efdabcb\",\n  \"output\": \"# Recommendation\\n\\nBuild standalone publication store before broker wiring.\\n\\nBroker boundary is not settled. Artifact transport, authority binding, publication meaning, and persistence ownership still need approval.\\n\\nDo not modify root protocol. Do not activate gates.\\n\\n## Current behavior\\n\\n- `workspace_replica_artifact.py` provides deterministic in-memory encoding and decoding. It enforces immutable `ArtifactLimits` and computes `source_state_sha256`.\\n- Source-state digest covers all four artifact sections. See `compute_source_state_sha256` and `decode_worktree_artifact`.\\n- Artifact codec accepts representable symlink entries. See `WorktreeEntryKind.SYMLINK` and `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py`.\\n- `workspace_replica_bundle.py:create_committed_bundle` creates bounded bundle bytes and detects source-ref changes.\\n- Bundle verification remains private and producer-oriented. See `_verify_bundle` at `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py:220-248`.\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` models `ingest`, `verify`, `publish`, `admission`, `drain`, `export`, then `reclaim`.\\n- `BrokerService` only accepts `executor.launch`. See `_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE` in `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py`.\\n- Root launcher accepts only `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`. See `_ALLOWED_ACTIONS` in `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py`.\\n- Root prepare expects an operation containing `repo` and `home`, not artifact files. See `ReplicaLifecycleValidator.prepared`.\\n- Existing workspace publication owns tenant checkout repair and SQLite transitions. It is not an artifact store. See `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`.\\n- `workspace_runtime_paths.py` still invokes existing tenant checkout publication. It should remain unchanged.\\n- Root gates default disabled in `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:26-28`.\\n- Daemon gate environment names remain in `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:78-80`.\\n- Existing v2 tests preserve prepare, runtime setup, then launch. Legacy v1 inspection remains read-only in `backend/tests/test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py`.\\n\\n## Review findings\\n\\n1. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:_validate_replica_payload` omits physical target, generation, execution owner, and declared limits.\\n\\n   `BrokerReplicaJournal.accept` receives `ReplicaAuthority` separately. Application signature therefore does not bind accepted authority end to end.\\n\\n2. **Blocker:** No authenticated artifact transport exists.\\n\\n   `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX` is 65,536 bytes in `broker_protocol.py`. Current artifacts allow hundreds of megabytes.\\n\\n3. **Blocker:** Root staging shape differs from artifact-pair shape.\\n\\n   Publishing bundle and worktree files directly under launcher staging would violate root prepare invariants.\\n\\n4. **High:** `VerifyReceipt` binds digests but omits both lengths, declared limits, replica identity, and generation.\\n\\n5. **High:** `PublishReceipt` binds target and generation but omits pair digests, pair lengths, source-state digest, and declared limits.\\n\\n6. **High:** Worktree is optional in `IngestReceipt` and request validation. Required paired publication needs worktree to be mandatory.\\n\\n7. **High:** `_validate_response_frame` checks signature encoding length only. It does not verify the broker Ed25519 signature.\\n\\n8. **High:** There is no public consumer verifier for untrusted committed bundle bytes.\\n\\n9. **Medium:** Default bundle plus artifact bounds can exceed practical broker memory. Current APIs hold complete payloads in memory.\\n\\n10. **Medium:** “Reject symlinks” is ambiguous.\\n\\n    Existing artifact contract intentionally preserves worktree symlinks. Store-control symlinks should be rejected without changing artifact semantics.\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite.\\n- Journal calls must finish before filesystem effects or awaits begin.\\n- Root protocol remains exactly three actions.\\n- Every request and terminal receipt must remain cryptographically request-bound.\\n- Pair publication uses one same-directory no-replace rename.\\n- Destination parent must be synced before success.\\n- Preexisting destinations are never adopted or overwritten.\\n- All production gates remain disabled.\\n- Broker lifecycle v2 remains unchanged.\\n- Legacy v1 inspection remains read-only.\\n\\n## Next milestone\\n\\n### Observable result\\n\\nCaller supplies an explicit immutable declaration plus exact bundle and worktree bytes.\\n\\nStore publishes one directory containing both artifacts and canonical metadata. Caller receives a typed receipt only after rename, parent sync, and final verification.\\n\\nNo daemon or root path invokes this store during this milestone.\\n\\n### Affected paths\\n\\n1. Modify `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`.\\n2. Add `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`.\\n3. Update `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py`.\\n4. Add `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py`.\\n\\nDo not modify these paths during standalone milestone:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_runtime_paths.py`\\n\\n## Types and module boundaries\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_bundle.py`\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n- `VerifiedCommittedBundle`\\n  - `object_format`\\n  - `byte_length`\\n  - `sha256`\\n  - canonical `refs`\\n\\n- `verify_committed_bundle`\\n  - Accept exact `bytes`, expected object format, and explicit `BundleLimits`.\\n  - Reject empty or oversized input before filesystem work.\\n  - Verify through a fresh private bare repository.\\n  - Reject duplicate or malformed advertised refs.\\n  - Prove each advertised object peels to a commit.\\n  - Keep `GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1`.\\n  - Return no artifact bytes inside its receipt.\\n\\nRefactor `create_committed_bundle` to use this verifier. Preserve existing public results.\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nKeep this module independent from SQLite, broker protocol, daemon code, and root launcher.\\n\\nAdd frozen types:\\n\\n- `ReplicaArtifactBinding`\\n  - `artifact_id`\\n  - `sha256`\\n  - `byte_length`\\n\\n- `ReplicaIdentity`\\n  - `physical_target_id`\\n  - `replica_generation`\\n  - `execution_owner_id`\\n\\n- `ReplicaDeclaredLimits`\\n  - exact `BundleLimits`\\n  - exact `ArtifactLimits`\\n  - `max_pair_bytes`\\n\\n- `ReplicaPairDeclaration`\\n  - `operation_id`\\n  - `repository_id`\\n  - `workspace_id`\\n  - `ReplicaIdentity`\\n  - required bundle binding\\n  - required worktree binding\\n  - `source_state_sha256`\\n  - `reconciliation_fingerprint`\\n  - declared limits\\n\\n- `ReplicaVerificationReceipt`\\n  - complete declaration binding\\n  - actual bundle digest and length\\n  - actual worktree digest and length\\n  - actual source-state digest\\n  - object format\\n  - canonical bundle-ref digest\\n  - verified marker digest\\n\\n- `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`\\n  - verification receipt\\n  - publication receipt ID\\n  - final directory identity\\n  - publication marker digest\\n  - synchronization receipt ID\\n\\nAdd errors with stable classifications:\\n\\n- `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError`\\n- `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError`\\n- `ReplicaPublicationCollisionError`\\n\\nAdd `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`:\\n\\n- Constructor receives absolute publication root, immutable ceilings, expected UID, and expected GID.\\n- `verify_pair` writes and validates one private pending directory.\\n- `publish_pair` performs atomic no-replace publication.\\n- `inspect_published_pair` performs read-only exact verification.\\n- Caller never supplies final filesystem paths.\\n\\n### Storage layout\\n\\nUse one validated publication root.\\n\\nFor operation `O`:\\n\\n- Pending directory: hidden store-derived name for `O`.\\n- Final directory: store-derived canonical name for `O`.\\n- Pair entries:\\n  - `bundle.gitbundle`\\n  - `worktree.yra`\\n  - `pair.json`\\n\\nReject unknown entries, missing entries, non-regular artifact files, hard links, and storage symlinks.\\n\\nDo not reject encoded worktree symlink entries unless parent changes artifact policy.\\n\\n## Store transition order\\n\\n1. Validate all declaration types and declared limits.\\n2. Confirm declared limits do not exceed store ceilings.\\n3. Confirm combined declared lengths do not exceed `max_pair_bytes`.\\n4. Open publication root descriptor without following symlinks.\\n5. Create private pending directory with exclusive ownership.\\n6. Create both artifact files with `O_EXCL`, `O_NOFOLLOW`, and mode `0600`.\\n7. Write complete bytes while computing lengths and SHA-256 values.\\n8. Sync each artifact file.\\n9. Decode worktree using declared `ArtifactLimits`.\\n10. Match decoded source-state digest exactly.\\n11. Verify bundle using declared `BundleLimits`.\\n12. Match bundle and worktree object formats.\\n13. Apply approved bundle-root pairing rule.\\n14. Write canonical `pair.json` with exclusive creation.\\n15. Sync `pair.json`, then sync pending directory.\\n16. Reopen pending entries and recheck names, identities, lengths, and digests.\\n17. Confirm final target is absent.\\n18. Rename pending directory to final name with atomic no-replace semantics.\\n19. Sync publication root directory.\\n20. Reopen final directory without following symlinks.\\n21. Recheck exact entries and marker binding.\\n22. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\\n\\nReceipt ID should be a domain-separated digest of canonical receipt content. It must not be an unrelated random token.\\n\\n## Mutable-state ownership\\n\\n| Value | Owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Signed declaration | Application until broker acceptance |\\n| Broker-approved authority | Broker journal after acceptance |\\n| Pending directory | Publication store |\\n| Pending artifact files | Publication store |\\n| Canonical pair marker | Publication store |\\n| Final artifact-pair directory | Publication store |\\n| Verification and publication receipts | Immutable returned values |\\n| Journal stage state | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Launcher staging replica tree | Broker before root `prepare` |\\n| Prepared runnable tree | Root launcher, then selected executor |\\n\\nNo SQLite connection may exist while store or Git verification code runs.\\n\\n## Proposed failure outcomes\\n\\nExternal-effect policy needs parent approval before implementation.\\n\\n| Failure | Outcome |\\n|---|---|\\n| Invalid identifier, path component, limit, or type | Rejected, no final target |\\n| Bundle digest or length mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Worktree digest or length mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Source-state mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Bundle verification failure | Rejected before rename |\\n| Semantic pair mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Root, pending, artifact, marker, or final symlink | Rejected |\\n| Preexisting final file, directory, or symlink | Collision rejection, untouched |\\n| Partial preexisting pair | Collision rejection, untouched |\\n| Confirmed cross-filesystem condition | Rejected before rename |\\n| Failure before rename | Remove only pinned private pending directory |\\n| Rename outcome cannot be confirmed | Unresolved, retain possible states |\\n| Parent sync failure after rename | Unresolved, retain final directory |\\n| Final verification failure after rename | Unresolved, retain final directory |\\n| Cancellation before effect starts | Cancelled rejection with no effect |\\n| Cancellation after effect starts | Unresolved |\\n| Timeout after effect starts | Unresolved |\\n| Lost acknowledgment | Unresolved and never repeat publication |\\n\\nA successful retry may replay a journaled receipt. It must not adopt an unjournaled preexisting target.\\n\\n## Red tests\\n\\n### `test_workspace_replica_bundle.py`\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n- `test_public_verifier_accepts_exact_created_bundle`\\n- `test_public_verifier_rejects_digest_or_length_over_limit`\\n- `test_public_verifier_rejects_non_commit_advertisement`\\n- `test_public_verifier_rejects_object_format_mismatch`\\n- `test_creator_uses_same_consumer_verifier`\\n\\n### `test_workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n- `test_receipt_binds_both_digests_and_lengths`\\n- `test_receipt_binds_declared_limits_source_state_identity_and_generation`\\n- `test_mutating_any_receipt_binding_invalidates_inspection`\\n- `test_pair_becomes_visible_with_one_directory_rename`\\n- `test_files_and_pending_directory_sync_before_rename`\\n- `test_destination_parent_sync_precedes_success`\\n- `test_exact_limit_passes_and_one_byte_less_rejects`\\n- `test_bundle_digest_and_length_mismatches_reject_before_rename`\\n- `test_worktree_digest_and_length_mismatches_reject_before_rename`\\n- `test_source_state_mismatch_rejects_before_rename`\\n- `test_preexisting_file_directory_and_symlink_are_untouched`\\n- `test_partial_pair_is_never_accepted`\\n- `test_storage_root_and_pending_symlinks_are_rejected`\\n- `test_unknown_final_entries_are_rejected`\\n- `test_cross_filesystem_publication_is_rejected`\\n- `test_failure_before_rename_cleans_only_owned_pending_state`\\n- `test_failure_after_rename_is_unresolved_and_retains_final_state`\\n- `test_sync_failure_never_returns_receipt`\\n- `test_error_text_excludes artifact bytes and raw worktree paths`\\n\\nExisting artifact coverage is sufficient for codec behavior. New store coverage is required.\\n\\n## Broker wiring gate\\n\\nDo not wire verify or publish yet.\\n\\nThree decisions block safe wiring:\\n\\n1. Artifact transport.\\n2. Broker authority source.\\n3. Meaning of publish relative to root `prepare`.\\n\\nValid transport options:\\n\\n- Signed JSON header followed by two bounded binary frames.\\n- `SCM_RIGHTS` with two pinned read-only descriptors.\\n- Shared ingress spool followed by broker-private copying.\\n\\nShared spool has lowest daemon cost but highest ownership and cleanup risk. Descriptor passing has strongest object pinning but largest Unix transport change.\\n\\nAfter approval, future order is:\\n\\n1. Authenticate peer UID and Ed25519 request.\\n2. Validate signed pair declaration.\\n3. Resolve broker-owned authority without retaining an application SQLite handle.\\n4. Accept and claim journal authority.\\n5. Persist `ingest` start.\\n6. Receive or copy both artifacts into broker-owned storage.\\n7. Persist exact ingest receipt.\\n8. Persist `verify` start.\\n9. Await store verification.\\n10. Persist typed verification receipt.\\n11. Persist `publish` start.\\n12. Await atomic publication or approved replica materialization.\\n13. Persist typed publication receipt.\\n14. Continue later lifecycle stages only through their existing owner.\\n15. Sign terminal response with actual broker key.\\n\\nKeep `BrokerService` lifecycle v2 unchanged. Prefer a separate replica service after routing policy is approved.\\n\\nDo not add a root action. Existing `prepare` must remain the only ownership-transfer action.\\n\\n## Migration and rollback\\n\\nStandalone store requires no tenant SQLite migration.\\n\\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` schema is exact and currently uncommitted. Change its shape before first supported deployment.\\n\\nDo not auto-migrate an existing replica journal. Refuse unsupported state.\\n\\nEmpty development journals may be removed after confirming no accepted rows. Nonempty journals require explicit operator disposition.\\n\\nRollback remains safe while gates stay disabled. Published directories must remain retained after any uncertain publication.\\n\\nAtomic rename is the first irreversible visibility point. Root `prepare` remains a later irreversible ownership transition.\\n\\n## Commands for implementation\\n\\nFocused checks:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npytest -q \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\\nruff check \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\\nmypy \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\\ngit diff --check\\n```\\n\\nRun after any broker contract change:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npytest -q \\\\\\n  tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_broker_foundation.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_execution_daemons.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_root_launcher.py\\n```\\n\\n## Completion conditions\\n\\n- Final target never exposes one artifact without the other.\\n- Receipt binds both exact digests, both lengths, limits, source state, identity, and generation.\\n- No success occurs before destination-parent sync.\\n- Every preexisting target remains untouched.\\n- Any post-rename uncertainty returns unresolved.\\n- Store contains no SQLite import or database callback.\\n- Broker, daemon, root launcher, and gates remain behaviorally unchanged.\\n- Existing bundle and artifact tests remain green.\\n- New fault-window tests pass.\\n\\n## Unresolved decisions\\n\\nParent approval remains required for:\\n\\n- Broker-owned artifact persistence root and retention policy.\\n- Artifact transport mechanism.\\n- Authority authorization and signed payload shape.\\n- Broker protocol version compatibility policy.\\n- Exact bundle-ref to artifact-root relationship.\\n- Whether worktree symlinks remain valid artifact entries.\\n- Production limit ceilings.\\n- Timeout and cancellation disposition.\\n- Whether “publish” means artifact-pair publication or runnable replica-tree publication.\\n- Mapping of publication completion to root `prepare`.\\n\\n## Handoff\\n\\nApprove persistence ownership, transport, symlink scope, pairing rule, and failure policy before writer starts.\\n\\nFirst action after approval: add red receipt-binding and atomic-directory tests in `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py`.\\n\\nStill inspect `workspace_publication.atomic_rename_no_replace` before reuse. Reuse it only if its descriptor and sync guarantees match this contract.\\n\\nMost plan-changing assumption: “publication” means artifact-pair directory publication, not reconstruction of runnable `repo` and `home` trees.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/1efdabcb/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"planner\",\n      \"task\": \"Plan next Phase 6 milestone in /Users/user/projects/yinshi. Read-only.\\nCurrent committed modules: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py and workspace_replica_bundle.py. Current uncommitted Phase 6 modules include broker_replica_journal.py, broker_protocol.py, broker_runtime.py, execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, root_launcher.py, workspace_publication.py, workspace_runtime_paths.py, and tests.\\nGoal: bounded authenticated atomic publication of paired committed bundle and exact worktree artifact, with typed receipt binding both digests and lengths, immutable declared limits, source-state digest, replica identity and generation. Wire verify and publish stages to broker-owned replica authority only if boundary is settled.\\nConstraints: artifact bytes outside SQLite. No SQLite handle crosses external effect or await. Root protocol remains prepare, launch, reclaim. No fourth action. Broker signed protocol is end-to-end authentication. Atomic same-filesystem rename plus directory sync. Reject unsafe paths, symlinks, preexisting targets, partial pairs, digest mismatch, length mismatch, timeout/cancellation, and uncertain acknowledgement. All gates disabled. Preserve broker lifecycle v2 and read-only v1.\\nInspect current files and existing patterns. Return implementation-ready plan with exact module boundaries, types, stage ordering, owners, permitted transitions, failure outcomes, red tests, commands, and whether standalone publication store should precede broker wiring. Do not edit.\",\n      \"routingContract\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"agent\": \"planner\",\n        \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n        \"thinking\": \"max\",\n        \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n      },\n      \"launchContractDigest\": \"28088adf29938ed54b178ac5bc115b33060d61be1be75df20e5312c3d3764542\",\n      \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n        \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n        \"runtime\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"configured\": [],\n        \"effective\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"omitted\": {\n          \"runtime\": 0,\n          \"configured\": 0,\n          \"effective\": 0\n        }\n      },\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"outputState\": \"present\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"input\": 149857,\n        \"output\": 28385,\n        \"cacheRead\": 183808,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n        \"cost\": 1.692739,\n        \"turns\": 7\n      },\n      \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\",\n      \"thinking\": \"max\",\n      \"artifactPaths\": {\n        \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1efdabcb_planner_0_input.md\",\n        \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1efdabcb_planner_0_output.md\",\n        \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1efdabcb_planner_0.jsonl\",\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1efdabcb_planner_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n        \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1efdabcb_planner_0_meta.json\"\n      },\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1efdabcb_planner_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n      \"turnBudget\": {\n        \"maxTurns\": 8,\n        \"graceTurns\": 2,\n        \"outcome\": \"within-budget\",\n        \"turnCount\": 7\n      },\n      \"toolBudget\": {\n        \"hard\": 45,\n        \"soft\": 30,\n        \"block\": [\n          \"read\",\n          \"grep\",\n          \"find\",\n          \"ls\"\n        ],\n        \"toolCount\": 35,\n        \"outcome\": \"soft-reached\",\n        \"softReachedAt\": 30\n      },\n      \"context\": \"fresh\",\n      \"progressSummary\": {\n        \"toolCount\": 35,\n        \"tokens\": 178242,\n        \"durationMs\": 751441\n      },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"fileMutation\": {\n          \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n          \"expected\": false,\n          \"attempted\": true\n        }\n      },\n      \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n      \"finalOutput\": \"# Recommendation\\n\\nBuild standalone publication store before broker wiring.\\n\\nBroker boundary is not settled. Artifact transport, authority binding, publication meaning, and persistence ownership still need approval.\\n\\nDo not modify root protocol. Do not activate gates.\\n\\n## Current behavior\\n\\n- `workspace_replica_artifact.py` provides deterministic in-memory encoding and decoding. It enforces immutable `ArtifactLimits` and computes `source_state_sha256`.\\n- Source-state digest covers all four artifact sections. See `compute_source_state_sha256` and `decode_worktree_artifact`.\\n- Artifact codec accepts representable symlink entries. See `WorktreeEntryKind.SYMLINK` and `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py`.\\n- `workspace_replica_bundle.py:create_committed_bundle` creates bounded bundle bytes and detects source-ref changes.\\n- Bundle verification remains private and producer-oriented. See `_verify_bundle` at `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py:220-248`.\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` models `ingest`, `verify`, `publish`, `admission`, `drain`, `export`, then `reclaim`.\\n- `BrokerService` only accepts `executor.launch`. See `_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE` in `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py`.\\n- Root launcher accepts only `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`. See `_ALLOWED_ACTIONS` in `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py`.\\n- Root prepare expects an operation containing `repo` and `home`, not artifact files. See `ReplicaLifecycleValidator.prepared`.\\n- Existing workspace publication owns tenant checkout repair and SQLite transitions. It is not an artifact store. See `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`.\\n- `workspace_runtime_paths.py` still invokes existing tenant checkout publication. It should remain unchanged.\\n- Root gates default disabled in `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:26-28`.\\n- Daemon gate environment names remain in `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:78-80`.\\n- Existing v2 tests preserve prepare, runtime setup, then launch. Legacy v1 inspection remains read-only in `backend/tests/test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py`.\\n\\n## Review findings\\n\\n1. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:_validate_replica_payload` omits physical target, generation, execution owner, and declared limits.\\n\\n   `BrokerReplicaJournal.accept` receives `ReplicaAuthority` separately. Application signature therefore does not bind accepted authority end to end.\\n\\n2. **Blocker:** No authenticated artifact transport exists.\\n\\n   `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX` is 65,536 bytes in `broker_protocol.py`. Current artifacts allow hundreds of megabytes.\\n\\n3. **Blocker:** Root staging shape differs from artifact-pair shape.\\n\\n   Publishing bundle and worktree files directly under launcher staging would violate root prepare invariants.\\n\\n4. **High:** `VerifyReceipt` binds digests but omits both lengths, declared limits, replica identity, and generation.\\n\\n5. **High:** `PublishReceipt` binds target and generation but omits pair digests, pair lengths, source-state digest, and declared limits.\\n\\n6. **High:** Worktree is optional in `IngestReceipt` and request validation. Required paired publication needs worktree to be mandatory.\\n\\n7. **High:** `_validate_response_frame` checks signature encoding length only. It does not verify the broker Ed25519 signature.\\n\\n8. **High:** There is no public consumer verifier for untrusted committed bundle bytes.\\n\\n9. **Medium:** Default bundle plus artifact bounds can exceed practical broker memory. Current APIs hold complete payloads in memory.\\n\\n10. **Medium:** “Reject symlinks” is ambiguous.\\n\\n    Existing artifact contract intentionally preserves worktree symlinks. Store-control symlinks should be rejected without changing artifact semantics.\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite.\\n- Journal calls must finish before filesystem effects or awaits begin.\\n- Root protocol remains exactly three actions.\\n- Every request and terminal receipt must remain cryptographically request-bound.\\n- Pair publication uses one same-directory no-replace rename.\\n- Destination parent must be synced before success.\\n- Preexisting destinations are never adopted or overwritten.\\n- All production gates remain disabled.\\n- Broker lifecycle v2 remains unchanged.\\n- Legacy v1 inspection remains read-only.\\n\\n## Next milestone\\n\\n### Observable result\\n\\nCaller supplies an explicit immutable declaration plus exact bundle and worktree bytes.\\n\\nStore publishes one directory containing both artifacts and canonical metadata. Caller receives a typed receipt only after rename, parent sync, and final verification.\\n\\nNo daemon or root path invokes this store during this milestone.\\n\\n### Affected paths\\n\\n1. Modify `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`.\\n2. Add `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`.\\n3. Update `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py`.\\n4. Add `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py`.\\n\\nDo not modify these paths during standalone milestone:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_runtime_paths.py`\\n\\n## Types and module boundaries\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_bundle.py`\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n- `VerifiedCommittedBundle`\\n  - `object_format`\\n  - `byte_length`\\n  - `sha256`\\n  - canonical `refs`\\n\\n- `verify_committed_bundle`\\n  - Accept exact `bytes`, expected object format, and explicit `BundleLimits`.\\n  - Reject empty or oversized input before filesystem work.\\n  - Verify through a fresh private bare repository.\\n  - Reject duplicate or malformed advertised refs.\\n  - Prove each advertised object peels to a commit.\\n  - Keep `GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1`.\\n  - Return no artifact bytes inside its receipt.\\n\\nRefactor `create_committed_bundle` to use this verifier. Preserve existing public results.\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nKeep this module independent from SQLite, broker protocol, daemon code, and root launcher.\\n\\nAdd frozen types:\\n\\n- `ReplicaArtifactBinding`\\n  - `artifact_id`\\n  - `sha256`\\n  - `byte_length`\\n\\n- `ReplicaIdentity`\\n  - `physical_target_id`\\n  - `replica_generation`\\n  - `execution_owner_id`\\n\\n- `ReplicaDeclaredLimits`\\n  - exact `BundleLimits`\\n  - exact `ArtifactLimits`\\n  - `max_pair_bytes`\\n\\n- `ReplicaPairDeclaration`\\n  - `operation_id`\\n  - `repository_id`\\n  - `workspace_id`\\n  - `ReplicaIdentity`\\n  - required bundle binding\\n  - required worktree binding\\n  - `source_state_sha256`\\n  - `reconciliation_fingerprint`\\n  - declared limits\\n\\n- `ReplicaVerificationReceipt`\\n  - complete declaration binding\\n  - actual bundle digest and length\\n  - actual worktree digest and length\\n  - actual source-state digest\\n  - object format\\n  - canonical bundle-ref digest\\n  - verified marker digest\\n\\n- `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`\\n  - verification receipt\\n  - publication receipt ID\\n  - final directory identity\\n  - publication marker digest\\n  - synchronization receipt ID\\n\\nAdd errors with stable classifications:\\n\\n- `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError`\\n- `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError`\\n- `ReplicaPublicationCollisionError`\\n\\nAdd `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`:\\n\\n- Constructor receives absolute publication root, immutable ceilings, expected UID, and expected GID.\\n- `verify_pair` writes and validates one private pending directory.\\n- `publish_pair` performs atomic no-replace publication.\\n- `inspect_published_pair` performs read-only exact verification.\\n- Caller never supplies final filesystem paths.\\n\\n### Storage layout\\n\\nUse one validated publication root.\\n\\nFor operation `O`:\\n\\n- Pending directory: hidden store-derived name for `O`.\\n- Final directory: store-derived canonical name for `O`.\\n- Pair entries:\\n  - `bundle.gitbundle`\\n  - `worktree.yra`\\n  - `pair.json`\\n\\nReject unknown entries, missing entries, non-regular artifact files, hard links, and storage symlinks.\\n\\nDo not reject encoded worktree symlink entries unless parent changes artifact policy.\\n\\n## Store transition order\\n\\n1. Validate all declaration types and declared limits.\\n2. Confirm declared limits do not exceed store ceilings.\\n3. Confirm combined declared lengths do not exceed `max_pair_bytes`.\\n4. Open publication root descriptor without following symlinks.\\n5. Create private pending directory with exclusive ownership.\\n6. Create both artifact files with `O_EXCL`, `O_NOFOLLOW`, and mode `0600`.\\n7. Write complete bytes while computing lengths and SHA-256 values.\\n8. Sync each artifact file.\\n9. Decode worktree using declared `ArtifactLimits`.\\n10. Match decoded source-state digest exactly.\\n11. Verify bundle using declared `BundleLimits`.\\n12. Match bundle and worktree object formats.\\n13. Apply approved bundle-root pairing rule.\\n14. Write canonical `pair.json` with exclusive creation.\\n15. Sync `pair.json`, then sync pending directory.\\n16. Reopen pending entries and recheck names, identities, lengths, and digests.\\n17. Confirm final target is absent.\\n18. Rename pending directory to final name with atomic no-replace semantics.\\n19. Sync publication root directory.\\n20. Reopen final directory without following symlinks.\\n21. Recheck exact entries and marker binding.\\n22. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\\n\\nReceipt ID should be a domain-separated digest of canonical receipt content. It must not be an unrelated random token.\\n\\n## Mutable-state ownership\\n\\n| Value | Owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Signed declaration | Application until broker acceptance |\\n| Broker-approved authority | Broker journal after acceptance |\\n| Pending directory | Publication store |\\n| Pending artifact files | Publication store |\\n| Canonical pair marker | Publication store |\\n| Final artifact-pair directory | Publication store |\\n| Verification and publication receipts | Immutable returned values |\\n| Journal stage state | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Launcher staging replica tree | Broker before root `prepare` |\\n| Prepared runnable tree | Root launcher, then selected executor |\\n\\nNo SQLite connection may exist while store or Git verification code runs.\\n\\n## Proposed failure outcomes\\n\\nExternal-effect policy needs parent approval before implementation.\\n\\n| Failure | Outcome |\\n|---|---|\\n| Invalid identifier, path component, limit, or type | Rejected, no final target |\\n| Bundle digest or length mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Worktree digest or length mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Source-state mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Bundle verification failure | Rejected before rename |\\n| Semantic pair mismatch | Rejected before rename |\\n| Root, pending, artifact, marker, or final symlink | Rejected |\\n| Preexisting final file, directory, or symlink | Collision rejection, untouched |\\n| Partial preexisting pair | Collision rejection, untouched |\\n| Confirmed cross-filesystem condition | Rejected before rename |\\n| Failure before rename | Remove only pinned private pending directory |\\n| Rename outcome cannot be confirmed | Unresolved, retain possible states |\\n| Parent sync failure after rename | Unresolved, retain final directory |\\n| Final verification failure after rename | Unresolved, retain final directory |\\n| Cancellation before effect starts | Cancelled rejection with no effect |\\n| Cancellation after effect starts | Unresolved |\\n| Timeout after effect starts | Unresolved |\\n| Lost acknowledgment | Unresolved and never repeat publication |\\n\\nA successful retry may replay a journaled receipt. It must not adopt an unjournaled preexisting target.\\n\\n## Red tests\\n\\n### `test_workspace_replica_bundle.py`\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n- `test_public_verifier_accepts_exact_created_bundle`\\n- `test_public_verifier_rejects_digest_or_length_over_limit`\\n- `test_public_verifier_rejects_non_commit_advertisement`\\n- `test_public_verifier_rejects_object_format_mismatch`\\n- `test_creator_uses_same_consumer_verifier`\\n\\n### `test_workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n- `test_receipt_binds_both_digests_and_lengths`\\n- `test_receipt_binds_declared_limits_source_state_identity_and_generation`\\n- `test_mutating_any_receipt_binding_invalidates_inspection`\\n- `test_pair_becomes_visible_with_one_directory_rename`\\n- `test_files_and_pending_directory_sync_before_rename`\\n- `test_destination_parent_sync_precedes_success`\\n- `test_exact_limit_passes_and_one_byte_less_rejects`\\n- `test_bundle_digest_and_length_mismatches_reject_before_rename`\\n- `test_worktree_digest_and_length_mismatches_reject_before_rename`\\n- `test_source_state_mismatch_rejects_before_rename`\\n- `test_preexisting_file_directory_and_symlink_are_untouched`\\n- `test_partial_pair_is_never_accepted`\\n- `test_storage_root_and_pending_symlinks_are_rejected`\\n- `test_unknown_final_entries_are_rejected`\\n- `test_cross_filesystem_publication_is_rejected`\\n- `test_failure_before_rename_cleans_only_owned_pending_state`\\n- `test_failure_after_rename_is_unresolved_and_retains_final_state`\\n- `test_sync_failure_never_returns_receipt`\\n- `test_error_text_excludes artifact bytes and raw worktree paths`\\n\\nExisting artifact coverage is sufficient for codec behavior. New store coverage is required.\\n\\n## Broker wiring gate\\n\\nDo not wire verify or publish yet.\\n\\nThree decisions block safe wiring:\\n\\n1. Artifact transport.\\n2. Broker authority source.\\n3. Meaning of publish relative to root `prepare`.\\n\\nValid transport options:\\n\\n- Signed JSON header followed by two bounded binary frames.\\n- `SCM_RIGHTS` with two pinned read-only descriptors.\\n- Shared ingress spool followed by broker-private copying.\\n\\nShared spool has lowest daemon cost but highest ownership and cleanup risk. Descriptor passing has strongest object pinning but largest Unix transport change.\\n\\nAfter approval, future order is:\\n\\n1. Authenticate peer UID and Ed25519 request.\\n2. Validate signed pair declaration.\\n3. Resolve broker-owned authority without retaining an application SQLite handle.\\n4. Accept and claim journal authority.\\n5. Persist `ingest` start.\\n6. Receive or copy both artifacts into broker-owned storage.\\n7. Persist exact ingest receipt.\\n8. Persist `verify` start.\\n9. Await store verification.\\n10. Persist typed verification receipt.\\n11. Persist `publish` start.\\n12. Await atomic publication or approved replica materialization.\\n13. Persist typed publication receipt.\\n14. Continue later lifecycle stages only through their existing owner.\\n15. Sign terminal response with actual broker key.\\n\\nKeep `BrokerService` lifecycle v2 unchanged. Prefer a separate replica service after routing policy is approved.\\n\\nDo not add a root action. Existing `prepare` must remain the only ownership-transfer action.\\n\\n## Migration and rollback\\n\\nStandalone store requires no tenant SQLite migration.\\n\\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` schema is exact and currently uncommitted. Change its shape before first supported deployment.\\n\\nDo not auto-migrate an existing replica journal. Refuse unsupported state.\\n\\nEmpty development journals may be removed after confirming no accepted rows. Nonempty journals require explicit operator disposition.\\n\\nRollback remains safe while gates stay disabled. Published directories must remain retained after any uncertain publication.\\n\\nAtomic rename is the first irreversible visibility point. Root `prepare` remains a later irreversible ownership transition.\\n\\n## Commands for implementation\\n\\nFocused checks:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npytest -q \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\\nruff check \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\\nmypy \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py \\\\\\n  src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\\ngit diff --check\\n```\\n\\nRun after any broker contract change:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npytest -q \\\\\\n  tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_broker_foundation.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_execution_daemons.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py \\\\\\n  tests/test_root_launcher.py\\n```\\n\\n## Completion conditions\\n\\n- Final target never exposes one artifact without the other.\\n- Receipt binds both exact digests, both lengths, limits, source state, identity, and generation.\\n- No success occurs before destination-parent sync.\\n- Every preexisting target remains untouched.\\n- Any post-rename uncertainty returns unresolved.\\n- Store contains no SQLite import or database callback.\\n- Broker, daemon, root launcher, and gates remain behaviorally unchanged.\\n- Existing bundle and artifact tests remain green.\\n- New fault-window tests pass.\\n\\n## Unresolved decisions\\n\\nParent approval remains required for:\\n\\n- Broker-owned artifact persistence root and retention policy.\\n- Artifact transport mechanism.\\n- Authority authorization and signed payload shape.\\n- Broker protocol version compatibility policy.\\n- Exact bundle-ref to artifact-root relationship.\\n- Whether worktree symlinks remain valid artifact entries.\\n- Production limit ceilings.\\n- Timeout and cancellation disposition.\\n- Whether “publish” means artifact-pair publication or runnable replica-tree publication.\\n- Mapping of publication completion to root `prepare`.\\n\\n## Handoff\\n\\nApprove persistence ownership, transport, symlink scope, pairing rule, and failure policy before writer starts.\\n\\nFirst action after approval: add red receipt-binding and atomic-directory tests in `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py`.\\n\\nStill inspect `workspace_publication.atomic_rename_no_replace` before reuse. Reuse it only if its descriptor and sync guarantees match this contract.\\n\\nMost plan-changing assumption: “publication” means artifact-pair directory publication, not reconstruction of runnable `repo` and `home` trees.\",\n      \"controlEvents\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"ts\": 1789235690856,\n          \"runId\": \"1efdabcb\",\n          \"agent\": \"planner\",\n          \"index\": 0,\n          \"message\": \"planner is still active but long-running\",\n          \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n          \"turns\": 6,\n          \"tokens\": 152032,\n          \"toolCount\": 35,\n          \"elapsedMs\": 240647\n        }\n      ],\n      \"attemptedModels\": [\n        \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAttempts\": [\n        {\n          \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\",\n          \"success\": true,\n          \"exitCode\": 0,\n          \"usage\": {\n            \"input\": 149857,\n            \"output\": 28385,\n            \"cacheRead\": 183808,\n            \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n            \"cost\": 1.692739,\n            \"turns\": 7\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/1efdabcb/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n      \"acceptance\": {\n        \"status\": \"attested\",\n        \"evidenceStatus\": \"attested\",\n        \"explicit\": false,\n        \"effectiveAcceptance\": {\n          \"level\": \"attested\",\n          \"explicit\": false,\n          \"inferredReason\": [\n            \"read-only task wording\"\n          ],\n          \"criteria\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"mus