{"type":"message","id":"ba0352a9","parentId":"cdd2a70c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:03:41.673Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_lXdok2mvXXBe6EzG0oABIfcg|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa593fd05f887d0b00bad06548b0e60","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:31:        head_oid=OID,\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:48:        root_oids=(OTHER_OID, OID),\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:71:    count = 8 + len(value.head_target) + len(value.head_oid)\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:84:    assert decoded.head_oid == source.head_oid\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:85:    assert decoded.root_oids == (OID, OTHER_OID)\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:96:        head_oid=sha256_oid,\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:97:        root_oids=(sha256_oid,),\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:101:    assert decoded.root_oids == (sha256_oid,)\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:107:    assert decoded_unborn.head_oid == b\"\"\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:180:        encode_worktree_artifact(replace(artifact_input(), head_oid=b\"c\" * 20))\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:218:            replace(artifact_input(), head_oid=b\"\\x00\" * 20, root_oids=(b\"\\x00\" * 20,))\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:221:        encode_worktree_artifact(replace(artifact_input(), root_oids=(OID, OID)))\nbackend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py:434:        max_roots=len(source.root_oids),\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789236221673}}
{"type":"message","id":"e4bc2919","parentId":"ba0352a9","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:03:55.491Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Analyzing Git object root dependencies**\n\n**Planning staged-only Git object transport**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa59400d62487d09fac3ed65ef3800d\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Analyzing Git object root dependencies**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning staged-only Git object transport**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_J771SkZwZIkDf3ko8vmXv7fw|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5940ae34487d093b9698720da3e3c","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1b2159d0_worker-expert_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":260}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":787,"output":373,"cacheRead":100224,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":321,"totalTokens":101384,"cost":{"input":0.003935,"output":0.01119,"cacheRead":0.050112,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06523699999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789236221684,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa593fe1e0087d0b2d7c77c830f1362","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"00068aa1","parentId":"e4bc2919","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:03:55.505Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_J771SkZwZIkDf3ko8vmXv7fw|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5940ae34487d093b9698720da3e3c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Causal account\n\nCurrent snapshot flow preserves parent index locally, but does not preserve its semantics in replica artifacts.\n\n`thread_workspaces.py:_write_tree_through_alternate_index` seeds a private index, then runs `git add -A`. This collapses staged plus unstaged state into one tree. Finalization repeats this flow.\n\n`workspace_replica.py` can carry exact index storage bytes. Its semantic validator still rejects conflict stages and duplicate paths across stages.\n\nNo bounded authenticated worktree artifact codec exists. Broker journal stores artifact digests and lengths, but export references are not included in signed terminal responses.\n\n## Review findings\n\n1. **Blocker: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica.py:616-635`**\n   - `_corrected_validate_index_entry` rejects every stage except stage zero.\n   - Conflict stages 1, 2, and 3 cannot enter reconciliation.\n\n2. **Blocker: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica.py:671-687`**\n   - Index uniqueness uses raw path alone.\n   - Valid conflict entries sharing one path would be rejected.\n   - Uniqueness must use `(raw_path, stage)`.\n\n3. **High: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:406-459`**\n   - Alternate-index staging runs `git add -A`.\n   - This protects the original index from mutation, but flattens staged and unstaged state.\n   - Intent-to-add, assume-unchanged, skip-worktree, conflict entries, and exact index bytes are lost from the snapshot representation.\n\n4. **High: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1845-1884`**\n   - Child finalization produces only a synthetic commit tree.\n   - Unstaged versus staged distinctions cannot survive this boundary.\n   - Ignored files remain absent even when an explicit policy permits them.\n\n5. **High: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:206-216,508-512`**\n   - `ExportReceipt` contains artifact references.\n   - `_validate_response_frame` signs only stage, state, code, and receipt ID.\n   - A caller cannot authenticate exported artifact IDs, lengths, or digests from the terminal response.\n\n6. **High: `backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py:run_git_bytes`**\n   - `process.communicate()` buffers stdout and stderr completely.\n   - Claimed artifact size limits do not provide bounded streaming.\n   - Pack generation, pack verification, and large tree listings need chunked subprocess I/O.\n\n7. **Medium: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:27,112-127`**\n   - The 8 GiB bound applies per reference.\n   - `bundle` plus `worktree` can claim 16 GiB.\n   - No aggregate, section, inflated-object, path-count, or entry-count limit exists here.\n\n8. **Medium: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:789-796`**\n   - Verification compares `source_state_sha256` with the request value.\n   - Journal code does not establish that this digest came from decoded artifact state.\n   - Artifact verifier must create this receipt from computed state only.\n\n9. **Medium: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:2080-2110`**\n   - Snapshot bounds are checked after `run_git_bytes` buffers complete `ls-tree` output.\n   - Oversized inputs can exceed memory before rejection.\n\n## Proposed module\n\nCreate `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`.\n\n### Public types\n\n```python\nObjectFormat = Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"]\nNodeKind = Literal[\"directory\", \"file\", \"symlink\"]\nArtifactRole = Literal[\"objects\", \"worktree\"]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaArtifactLimits:\n    max_set_bytes: int\n    max_object_pack_bytes: int\n    max_inflated_object_bytes: int\n    max_index_bytes: int\n    max_manifest_bytes: int\n    max_content_bytes: int\n    max_entries: int\n    max_objects: int\n    max_path_bytes: int\n    max_depth: int\n    chunk_bytes: int = 1024 * 1024\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IgnoredInclusionGrant:\n    grant_id: str\n    policy_sha256: str\n    raw_paths: tuple[bytes, ...]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaCaptureAuthority:\n    operation_id: str\n    workspace_id: str\n    repository_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    drain_receipt_id: str\n    export_receipt_id: str\n    ignored_grant: IgnoredInclusionGrant | None\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ArtifactMeasurement:\n    sha256: str\n    byte_length: int\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass PreparedArtifactSet:\n    set_id: str\n    staging_directory: str\n    objects: ArtifactMeasurement\n    worktree: ArtifactMeasurement\n    source_state_sha256: str\n    policy_sha256: str | None\n    object_format: ObjectFormat\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ArtifactReferenceV2:\n    role: ArtifactRole\n    artifact_id: str\n    media_type: str\n    sha256: str\n    byte_length: int\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ArtifactSetReference:\n    set_id: str\n    objects: ArtifactReferenceV2\n    worktree: ArtifactReferenceV2\n    source_state_sha256: str\n    policy_sha256: str | None\n    object_format: ObjectFormat\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass AuthenticatedArtifactSetReference:\n    reference: ArtifactSetReference\n    broker_incarnation: str\n    database_incarnation: str\n    operation_id: str\n    payload_digest: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ParsedIndexEntry:\n    raw_path: bytes\n    stage: int\n    mode: str\n    object_id: str\n    intent_to_add: bool\n    skip_worktree: bool\n    assume_unchanged: bool\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass WorkingEntry:\n    raw_path: bytes\n    kind: NodeKind\n    content: bytes\n    executable: bool\n    allowed_ignored: bool\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass VerifiedReplicaArtifact:\n    object_format: ObjectFormat\n    index_present: bool\n    index_bytes: bytes\n    index_entries: tuple[ParsedIndexEntry, ...]\n    manifest: tuple[WorkingEntry, ...]\n    object_roots: tuple[str, ...]\n    source_state_sha256: str\n    policy_sha256: str | None\n```\n\n`VerifiedReplicaArtifact` may hold index bytes only after enforcing `max_index_bytes`. File content should remain in bounded spool descriptors during real implementation.\n\n### Public operations\n\n```python\nasync def capture_replica_artifacts(\n    *,\n    repository_fd: int,\n    worktree_fd: int,\n    authority: ReplicaCaptureAuthority,\n    staging_parent_fd: int,\n    limits: ReplicaArtifactLimits,\n) -> PreparedArtifactSet:\n    ...\n\n\ndef publish_prepared_artifact_set(\n    prepared: PreparedArtifactSet,\n    *,\n    staging_parent_fd: int,\n    publication_parent_fd: int,\n) -> ArtifactSetReference:\n    ...\n\n\nasync def verify_replica_artifacts(\n    reference: AuthenticatedArtifactSetReference,\n    *,\n    artifact_root_fd: int,\n    quarantine_parent_fd: int,\n    limits: ReplicaArtifactLimits,\n) -> VerifiedReplicaArtifact:\n    ...\n\n\ndef build_reconciliation_spec(\n    *,\n    verified: VerifiedReplicaArtifact,\n    baseline: ReplicaState,\n    authority: OperationIdentity,\n    retained_inputs: RetainedInputs,\n    limits: InventoryLimits,\n) -> ReconciliationSpec:\n    ...\n```\n\nOnly `broker_protocol.parse_signed_request` or `verify_broker_response` may create `AuthenticatedArtifactSetReference`. Artifact resolvers must not accept raw dictionaries, paths, URLs, or plain references.\n\n## Worktree binary format\n\nMedia type:\n\n```text\napplication/vnd.yinshi.replica-worktree.v1\n```\n\nAll integers use unsigned big-endian encoding.\n\n### File envelope\n\n```text\nmagic                 8 bytes  b\"YNSHRA1\\n\"\nversion               u16      1\nflags                 u16      bit 0 = complete manifest\nsection_count         u32      exactly 4\ntotal_byte_length     u64\n\nFour ordered sections:\n  CONTROL  type 1\n  INDEX    type 2\n  MANIFEST type 3\n  ROOTS    type 4\n```\n\nEach section has:\n\n```text\ntype                  u32\nflags                 u32      zero\npayload_length        u64\npayload_sha256        32 bytes\npayload               payload_length bytes\n\n[304 more lines in file. Use offset=261 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789236235505}}
{"type":"message","id":"84a86c2c","parentId":"00068aa1","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:03:58.960Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b9Cl9q7Jk2TWltnAV1oODgMW|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5940dddc087d0b1a003ae943ee25f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/1b2159d0_worker-expert_0_output.md","offset":261,"limit":260}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":2404,"output":50,"cacheRead":100864,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":103318,"cost":{"input":0.012020000000000001,"output":0.0015,"cacheRead":0.050432,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.063952}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789236235510,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5940c0f5887d08f4b561ec7888f2b","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"d5855194","parentId":"84a86c2c","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:03:58.963Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b9Cl9q7Jk2TWltnAV1oODgMW|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5940dddc087d0b1a003ae943ee25f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n\nReject unknown types, reordered sections, unknown flags, length overflow, truncation, trailing bytes, or digest mismatch.\n\n### CONTROL payload\n\n```text\nobject_format         u8       1 = SHA-1, 2 = SHA-256\nindex_present         u8       0 or 1\nhead_kind             u8       0 = unborn, 1 = detached, 2 = symbolic\nreserved              u8       zero\nhead_target_length    u32\nhead_oid_length       u32      0, 20, or 32\nindex_entry_count     u64\nmanifest_entry_count  u64\nmanifest_content_sum  u64\npolicy_digest_present u8\nreserved              7 bytes  zero\npolicy_sha256         32 bytes, zero when absent\nhead_target           raw bytes\nhead_oid              raw digest bytes\n```\n\nA symbolic target must be a canonical raw `refs/heads/...` path. Detached state has no target. Unborn state has no OID.\n\n### INDEX payload\n\nPayload contains exact index file bytes. Absence uses an empty payload with `index_present=0`.\n\nSupport index versions 2 and 3 initially. Reject version 4, split-index `link`, sparse-directory entries, unknown mandatory extensions, and unsupported entry flags.\n\nAllowed extensions should be an explicit set:\n\n```text\nTREE, REUC, UNTR, FSMN, EOIE, IEOT\n```\n\nValidate:\n\n- `DIRC` signature.\n- Version and entry count.\n- SHA-1 or SHA-256 trailer.\n- Entry padding and path lengths.\n- Canonical Git entry ordering.\n- Modes `100644`, `100755`, and `120000`.\n- Stages 0 through 3.\n- Uniqueness by `(raw_path, stage)`.\n- Stage zero cannot coexist with conflict stages for one path.\n- Conflict OIDs must be nonzero.\n- Every path passes canonical path checks.\n\nExact bytes remain unchanged during installation.\n\n### MANIFEST payload\n\nEntries are sorted by raw path bytes.\n\n```text\nkind                  u8       1 directory, 2 file, 3 symlink\nflags                 u8       bit 0 executable, bit 1 allowed ignored\nreserved              u16      zero\npath_length           u32\ncontent_length        u64\npath                  raw path bytes\ncontent               raw bytes\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Directories carry zero content and no executable flag.\n- Files preserve executable state as one Boolean.\n- Symlink content is exact `readlink` bytes. Targets are never followed.\n- Symlinks cannot be executable.\n- Regular files and symlinks require `st_nlink == 1`.\n- Setuid, setgid, and sticky bits are rejected.\n- FIFOs, sockets, devices, doors, and unknown kinds are rejected.\n- Every ancestor is an explicit directory entry.\n- No descendant may exist below a file or symlink.\n- Manifest is complete. Any destination entry absent from it is a deletion.\n- `.git` is always excluded from working entries.\n- Ignored leaves require an exact path in `IgnoredInclusionGrant`.\n- Non-ignored untracked files remain included unless security policy rejects them.\n\n### ROOTS payload\n\n```text\nroot_count            u64\nroot_oid              20 or 32 bytes, repeated\n```\n\nRoots are unique and sorted by raw OID bytes. They equal:\n\n- Current HEAD OID when present.\n- Every nonzero OID referenced by all index stages.\n\n### Source-state digest\n\n```text\nSHA256(\n    b\"yinshi-replica-source-v1\\x00\"\n    + control_section_sha256\n    + index_section_sha256\n    + manifest_section_sha256\n    + roots_section_sha256\n).hexdigest()\n```\n\nThis computed value must equal the signed `source_state_sha256`.\n\n## Object artifact\n\nMedia type:\n\n```text\napplication/vnd.yinshi.git-pack.v1\n```\n\nUse a complete, non-thin Git pack.\n\nGeneration algorithm:\n\n1. Parse and validate exact index first.\n2. Collect HEAD plus every nonzero index-stage OID.\n3. Verify regular and symlink modes reference blobs.\n4. Enumerate complete object closure with replacement objects disabled.\n5. Enforce object count and inflated-byte limits before packing.\n6. Run `git pack-objects --stdout --revs` without thin-pack options.\n7. Stream stdout into an exclusive staging file.\n8. Hash and count every chunk.\n9. Kill and drain the child when any bound fails.\n10. Reject missing promisor objects or unexpected object kinds.\n\nVerification uses an isolated object quarantine. Run `index-pack --strict`, enumerate pack contents, and require the expected closure. Do not use target alternates while proving self-containment.\n\n## Capture checks\n\n- Retain repository and worktree through no-follow directory descriptors.\n- Require broker ownership plus a current drain receipt.\n- Scan through descriptor-relative operations.\n- Exclude `.git` without following it.\n- Open files with `O_NOFOLLOW`.\n- Compare directory entries and node identities during two scans.\n- Compare index identity and bytes before and after manifest capture.\n- Fail if any source mutation is observed.\n- Enforce path count, depth, path-byte, content-byte, index-byte, object-count, inflated-object, pack, and aggregate bounds.\n- Check protected-secret policy independently from Git ignore policy.\n- Never log raw paths, symlink text, file bytes, or artifact storage names.\n\n## Import and reconciliation algorithm\n\n1. Verify signed broker message before resolving any artifact ID.\n2. Open final artifact-set directory through retained parent descriptor.\n3. Require exact owner, mode, directory identity, and fixed child names.\n4. Require both files to be regular, single-link files.\n5. Stream-check signed lengths and SHA-256 values.\n6. Parse worktree format with allocation checks before each read.\n7. Validate index checksum and semantic entries.\n8. Verify pack in isolated quarantine.\n9. Require every index OID to exist with correct object type.\n10. Convert index entries and manifest into `workspace_replica` types.\n11. Create same-filesystem preparation files with new inodes.\n12. Write content in bounded chunks. Fsync each file and changed parent.\n13. Promote Git objects with no-replace operations. Never hardlink them.\n14. Run `bind_specification` before destination mutation.\n15. Journal intent before each effect.\n16. Quarantine old working nodes deepest-first.\n17. Install directories parent-first, then files and opaque symlinks.\n18. Derive deletions from complete-manifest absence.\n19. Install exact index bytes after working-node reconciliation.\n20. Verify complete desired state and object availability.\n21. Publish generation marker using no-replace rename.\n22. Fsync marker and parent before publication receipt.\n23. Resume after restart only from authenticated journal facts plus fresh observations.\n\n## Atomic artifact publication\n\nPublish one directory, not two independent files.\n\n```text\nartifact-root/\n  staging/<set-id>.tmp/\n    objects.pack\n    worktree.yra\n  sets/<set-id>/\n    objects.pack\n    worktree.yra\n```\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Create staging directory with mode `0700`.\n2. Create both files using `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW`, mode `0600`.\n3. Stream, verify, and fsync both files.\n4. Fsync staging directory.\n5. Rename staging directory to `sets/<set-id>` with `RENAME_NOREPLACE`.\n6. Fsync `sets`.\n7. Commit export receipt containing both exact references.\n8. Sign response containing both references.\n9. Expose references only after durable receipt and signature exist.\n\nCrash before rename leaves removable staging state. Crash after rename leaves an unpublished orphan. It must not be adopted without matching journal authority.\n\nCancellation before mutation removes only owned staging state. Cancellation after any journaled destination effect enters replay. It must not report ordinary completion.\n\n## Required supporting Git API\n\n`git.py` needs one bounded subprocess primitive:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass GitStreamResult:\n    stdout_bytes: int\n    stdout_sha256: str\n\n\nasync def run_git_stream(\n    args: Sequence[str],\n    *,\n    cwd_fd: int,\n    stdin_chunks: AsyncIterable[bytes] | None,\n    stdout_fd: int,\n    max_stdout_bytes: int,\n    max_stderr_bytes: int = 16_384,\n    pass_fds: Sequence[int] = (),\n) -> GitStreamResult:\n    ...\n```\n\nIt must preserve current sanitized environment, stable directory checks, timeout behavior, and cancellation draining.\n\n## Reconciliation-core changes\n\n`workspace_replica.py` needs these focused changes:\n\n- Permit stages 0 through 3.\n- Key duplicate checks by `(raw_path, stage)`.\n- Enforce stage-zero versus conflict-stage exclusivity.\n- Permit supported extended flags because exact index bytes preserve them.\n- Keep unsupported modes rejected.\n- Preserve `IndexState.storage.content` byte-for-byte.\n- Include stage and flags in canonical specification fingerprints.\n- Add tests proving conflict-stage ordering does not collapse.\n\n## Test plan\n\n1. Golden binary vectors for SHA-1 and SHA-256 repositories.\n2. Deterministic manifest encoding with non-UTF-8 paths.\n3. Exact index-byte equality after round trip.\n4. Index versions 2 and 3.\n5. Conflict stages 1, 2, and 3 on one path.\n6. Stage-zero plus conflict-stage rejection.\n7. Staged content differs from working content.\n8. Staged-only blob unreachable from refs remains available.\n9. Staged deletion and unstaged deletion remain distinct.\n10. Executable file bit survives.\n11. Dangling symlink and non-UTF-8 symlink text survive.\n12. Allowed ignored file appears. Non-allowed ignored file does not.\n13. Protected ignored file is rejected despite allow grant.\n14. Hardlinked file and symlink are rejected.\n15. FIFO, socket, device, gitlink, sparse index, split index, and index v4 are rejected.\n\n[44 more lines in file. Use offset=521 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789236238963}}
