{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent-notify","content":"Background task completed: **worker-expert**\n\nworker-expert:\n## Decision\n\nA third artifact is required.\n\nEach publication contains exactly three files:\n\n1. `committed.bundle`\n2. `worktree.yra`\n3. `index-objects.pack`\n\n`index-objects.pack` contains each required index object absent from the committed bundle.\n\nAn empty missing set produces a valid zero-object pack. This keeps artifact count fixed.\n\nSQLite stores only identifiers, lengths, digests, roles, receipts, plus state metadata.\n\n## Causal account\n\n`workspace_replica_bundle.py` passes only refs plus optional `HEAD` to `git bundle create`.\n\nGit therefore includes only objects reachable from those revisions.\n\nStaged-only blobs have no committed ref. Conflict-stage blobs can also remain unreachable.\n\n`workspace_replica_artifact.py` stores OIDs in `ROOTS`. It stores no Git object bytes.\n\nTwo existing artifacts cannot transport unreachable index objects. Changing either format would violate an existing boundary.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py:405-433,704-724`\n   - ROOTS only requires valid, unique OIDs.\n   - It only checks that HEAD appears.\n   - It never parses index bytes.\n   - It cannot prove ROOTS equals HEAD plus all nonzero index OIDs.\n\n2. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:112-141,206-216`\n   - Receipt models support only `bundle` plus optional `worktree`.\n   - No supplemental-object role exists.\n\n3. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:549-570,691-768`\n   - Request and receipt schemas reject a third artifact field.\n   - This needs a versioned schema change.\n\n4. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py:219-248`\n   - Verification checks bundle validity plus advertised refs.\n   - It does not enumerate actual packed objects.\n   - It cannot prove every packed object is reachable from advertised refs.\n\n5. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py:634-776`\n   - Bounded subprocess reads still return complete output bytes.\n   - Pack creation can allocate up to the configured maximum.\n   - Artifact transport needs descriptor-based streaming.\n\n6. **Medium:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py:671-737`\n   - `decode_worktree_artifact` accepts an already allocated `bytes`.\n   - The caller can allocate oversized input before decoder rejection.\n\n7. **Resolved prior finding:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica.py:616-705`\n   - Current reconciliation accepts stages zero through three.\n   - Duplicate identity uses `(raw_path, stage)`.\n   - Stage zero cannot coexist with conflict stages.\n   - Earlier artifact notes are stale here.\n\n## Public types\n\n```python\nArtifactRole = Literal[\n    \"committed_bundle\",\n    \"worktree\",\n    \"index_objects\",\n]\n\nObjectFormat = Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ArtifactReferenceV2:\n    role: ArtifactRole\n    media_type: str\n    artifact_id: str\n    sha256: str\n    byte_length: int\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaArtifactSetReference:\n    version: Literal[2]\n    object_format: ObjectFormat\n    source_state_sha256: str\n    reconciliation_fingerprint: str\n    bundle: ArtifactReferenceV2\n    worktree: ArtifactReferenceV2\n    index_objects: ArtifactReferenceV2\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IndexObjectPackLimits:\n    max_pack_bytes: int\n    max_objects: int\n    max_object_bytes: int\n    max_inflated_bytes: int\n    max_listing_bytes: int\n    max_set_bytes: int\n    chunk_bytes: int = 1024 * 1024\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass PackedObject:\n    object_id: str\n    kind: Literal[\"blob\"]\n    byte_length: int\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass VerifiedIndexObjectPack:\n    object_format: ObjectFormat\n    pack_sha256: str\n    pack_bytes: int\n    objects: tuple[PackedObject, ...]\n```\n\nMedia types:\n\n```text\napplication/vnd.yinshi.git-bundle.v1\napplication/vnd.yinshi.replica-worktree.v1\napplication/vnd.yinshi.git-index-objects-pack.v1\n```\n\nRoles and media types prevent artifact swaps.\n\n## Missing-object definition\n\nLet `I` contain every distinct, nonzero index-stage OID.\n\nLet `B` contain every object physically stored in the verified committed bundle.\n\nThe supplemental set is:\n\n```text\nE = I - B\n```\n\n`HEAD` must exist in `B`. Supplemental transport cannot repair a missing committed HEAD.\n\nEvery object in `I` must be a blob. Supported modes remain `100644`, `100755`, plus `120000`.\n\nConflict stages must use nonzero OIDs. Zero OIDs need explicit intent-to-add validation.\n\n## Generation algorithm\n\n1. Confirm broker ownership and a current drain receipt.\n2. Capture object format, HEAD, refs, index identity, plus exact index bytes.\n3. Parse index versions two or three.\n4. Derive `I` from every index stage.\n5. Derive ROOTS as sorted unique `HEAD ∪ I`.\n6. Create the committed bundle.\n7. Verify its actual object inventory and reachability.\n8. Compute `E = I - B`.\n9. Preflight every object in `E`.\n10. Reject missing objects or non-blob objects.\n11. Enforce object count and inflated-byte limits.\n12. Create a complete non-thin pack from exactly `E`.\n13. Verify the generated pack in an empty quarantine.\n14. Capture the bounded worktree artifact.\n15. Re-read HEAD, refs, index bytes, plus node identities.\n16. Reject any observed source mutation.\n17. Fsync all three files and their staging directory.\n18. Rename one artifact-set directory with no replacement.\n19. Fsync the published sets directory.\n20. Record and sign `ExportReceiptV2`.\n\n## Generation commands\n\nUse this environment for every source Git command:\n\n```text\nGIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\nGIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1\nGIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null\nGIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0\n```\n\nRun Git inside a network-denied sandbox.\n\nCapture format and HEAD:\n\n```bash\ngit rev-parse --show-object-format\ngit symbolic-ref --quiet --no-recurse HEAD\ngit rev-parse --verify 'HEAD^{commit}'\n```\n\nCreate SHA-1 bundle:\n\n```bash\ngit bundle create --version=2 - <committed-ref>... HEAD\n```\n\nCreate SHA-256 bundle:\n\n```bash\ngit bundle create --version=3 - <committed-ref>... HEAD\n```\n\nPreflight missing objects:\n\n```bash\ngit cat-file --batch-check='%(objectname) %(objecttype) %(objectsize)'\n```\n\nSend sorted `E` OIDs through standard input.\n\nCreate supplemental pack:\n\n```bash\ngit pack-objects --stdout --no-reuse-delta --no-reuse-object --window=0\n```\n\nSend sorted `E` OIDs through standard input. Do not use `--revs`.\n\nDo not use `--thin`. Window zero prevents external delta bases.\n\nStream stdout directly into an exclusive file. Hash each chunk during writing.\n\nKill and drain Git after any limit violation or cancellation.\n\n## Consumer verification\n\nAuthenticate the request before resolving any artifact identifier.\n\nOpen artifacts through a retained directory descriptor. Reject symlinks and non-regular files.\n\nRequire mode `0600`, one link, expected ownership, exact names, plus matching file identities.\n\nStream-check each signed length and SHA-256 digest.\n\n### Bundle quarantine\n\n```bash\ngit init --bare --object-format=<sha1-or-sha256> \"$q/bundle.git\"\ngit -C \"$q/bundle.git\" bundle verify \"$bundle\"\ngit -C \"$q/bundle.git\" bundle list-heads \"$bundle\"\ngit -C \"$q/bundle.git\" bundle unbundle \"$bundle\"\ngit -C \"$q/bundle.git\" cat-file --batch-all-objects --batch-check='%(objectname) %(objecttype) %(objectsize)'\ngit -C \"$q/bundle.git\" rev-list --objects --no-object-names <advertised-tip>...\n```\n\nCompare actual bundle objects with the advertised-tip closure.\n\nReject extra packed objects. Reject missing closure objects.\n\nRequire every advertised ref to peel to a commit.\n\nRequire worktree HEAD to match advertised `HEAD`.\n\nReject `refs/replace/*` advertisements. Never activate replacement refs.\n\n### Supplemental quarantine\n\n```bash\ngit init --bare --object-format=<sha1-or-sha256> \"$q/index.git\"\ngit -C \"$q/index.git\" index-pack --strict --stdin < \"$index_pack\"\ngit -C \"$q/index.git\" cat-file --batch-all-objects --batch-check='%(objectname) %(objecttype) %(objectsize)'\ngit -C \"$q/index.git\" cat-file --batch-check='%(objectname) %(objecttype) %(objectsize)'\n```\n\nThe first command verifies pack structure, deltas, trailer checksum, plus repository hash format.\n\nRequire the actual supplemental inventory to equal `E`.\n\nReject every non-blob object. Reject missing, duplicate, or unexpected OIDs.\n\nFinally require:\n\n```text\nROOTS == sorted_unique(HEAD ∪ I)\nHEAD ∈ B\nI ⊆ B ∪ E\nE ∩ B == ∅\n```\n\nNever use destination alternates during verification.\n\nPromisor configuration is absent in consumer quarantines. Missing objects therefore fail closed.\n\n## Bounds\n\nCheck signed artifact lengths before opening destination spools.\n\nEnforce separate bundle, worktree, supplemental-pack, plus aggregate limits.\n\nRead only fixed headers before accepting declared lengths.\n\nParse the Git pack header before invoking `index-pack`. Reject excessive object counts immediately.\n\nParse the index entry count before allocating entry storage.\n\nCheck every index path length before copying path bytes.\n\nCheck every manifest content length before materialization.\n\nUse overflow-safe subtraction for all remaining-byte checks.\n\nBound these dimensions:\n\n- Artifact-set bytes\n- Per-artifact bytes\n- Pack object count\n- Per-object inflated bytes\n- Aggregate inflated bytes\n- Index bytes\n- Index entries\n- Manifest bytes\n- Manifest entries\n- Per-file content bytes\n- Aggregate content bytes\n- Path bytes\n- Path depth\n- Ref count\n- Git listing output\n- Git stderr output\n\nRun `index-pack` inside memory, CPU, file-size, plus disk quotas.\n\nGit may decompress attacker-controlled input internally. Process quotas provide the final resource boundary.\n\nApplication code must never call `decode_worktree_artifact` on unbounded transport bytes.\n\nAdd a descriptor-based streaming decoder. Keep content in bounded spool files.\n\n## Race handling\n\nGit objects are immutable after OID verification. Source names and index bytes remain mutable.\n\nCapture HEAD, refs, and exact index bytes before generation.\n\nCapture them again after all three artifacts exist.\n\nCompare content plus filesystem identity. Abort on any difference.\n\nScan worktree directories twice. Compare entry sets, node types, identities, sizes, plus timestamps.\n\nOpen regular files with `O_NOFOLLOW`. Compare `fstat` before and after each read.\n\nCancellation before publication removes only owned staging files.\n\nCancellation after publication enters journal replay. It must not report normal completion.\n\n## Receipt binding\n\nCompute:\n\n```text\nartifact_set_sha256 =\nSHA256(\n    b\"yinshi-replica-artifact-set-v2\\x00\"\n    + canonical_json({\n        \"version\": 2,\n        \"object_format\": object_format,\n        \"source_state_sha256\": source_state_sha256,\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": reconciliation_fingerprint,\n        \"bundle\": full_bundle_reference,\n        \"worktree\": full_worktree_reference,\n        \"index_objects\": full_index_objects_reference\n    })\n).hexdigest()\n```\n\n`ExportReceiptV2` contains:\n\n```text\nexport_receipt_id\nartifact_set_sha256\nobject_format\nsource_state_sha256\nbundle\nworktree\nindex_objects\n```\n\n`VerifyReceiptV2` contains:\n\n```text\nreceipt_id\nartifact_set_sha256\nbundle_sha256\nworktree_sha256\nindex_objects_sha256\ncomputed_source_state_sha256\nreconciliation_fingerprint\n```\n\n`PublishReceiptV2` contains:\n\n```text\nreceipt_id\nartifact_set_sha256\nverify_receipt_id\nphysical_target_id\nreplica_generation\npublication_marker_sha256\nsynchronization_receipt_id\n```\n\nThe publication marker also stores `artifact_set_sha256`.\n\nThe signed export response must carry full `ExportReceiptV2`. A receipt identifier alone is insufficient.\n\nThe signed publish response must carry `artifact_set_sha256`.\n\nThis chain binds all artifacts, verification, target identity, generation, plus durable publication.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdd tests in this order:\n\n1. Real Git index parsing for SHA-1 and SHA-256.\n2. ROOTS equality against all index stages.\n3. ROOT omission and injection rejection.\n4. Conflict stages one, two, plus three.\n5. Staged-only blob survives transport.\n6. Staged content differs from working content.\n7. Bundle-reachable index blob is excluded from `E`.\n8. Zero-object supplemental pack verifies.\n9. Supplemental inventory rejects extra objects.\n10. Wrong object type rejects.\n11. Missing promisor object rejects without network access.\n12. Replacement objects never affect bytes or reachability.\n13. Thin packs and external delta bases reject.\n14. Bundle extra unreachable objects reject.\n15. SHA-1 pack trailer verifies.\n16. SHA-256 pack trailer verifies.\n17. Declared size rejects before allocation.\n18. Inflated-size bomb hits process quotas.\n19. Artifact role swaps reject.\n20. Tampered set digest or receipt field rejects.\n21. Capture mutation aborts publication.\n22. Cancellation drains Git and enters replay.\n23. Restart handles staging and published orphans.\n24. Exact index bytes survive reconciliation.\n\n## Integration order\n\n1. Add strict index parser and ROOTS equality checks.\n2. Add bounded subprocess streaming.\n3. Add committed-bundle inventory and reachability verification.\n4. Add supplemental-pack creation and verification.\n5. Add protocol version two artifact-set types.\n6. Add journal receipt version two.\n7. Add atomic three-file publication.\n8. Add consumer quarantine import.\n9. Connect verified objects to reconciliation inventory.\n10. Add restart and cancellation recovery.\n\n## Rejected explanations\n\n“ROOTS already transports objects” is false. ROOTS contains only fixed-width OIDs.\n\n“The bundle contains staged blobs” is false. Its command receives only refs plus HEAD.\n\n“Reconciliation still rejects conflict stages” is stale. Current validation accepts stages zero through three.\n\n“Current output limits provide streaming” is false. `run_git_bytes` returns complete output bytes.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `index-pack` can consume substantial CPU before semantic size checks.\n- Git index extension behavior varies across Git versions.\n- SHA-256 support depends on installed Git.\n- Worktree stability depends on effective drain ownership.\n- Object promotion requires restart-safe journaling.\n- Existing dirty workspace may obscure unrelated integration failures.\n- POSIX raw-byte paths remain unsuitable for Windows replicas.\n\nNo files changed. No tests ran.\n\nSession file: /Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/125925b9/run-0/session.jsonl","display":false,"id":"2d39a417","parentId":"52be4753","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:19:15.871Z"}
