{"type":"message","id":"6851c90a","parentId":"f95d8eaf","timestamp":"2026-09-12T18:45:16.193Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_fbAgmPPa7055rejgRBkxGc0b|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa59c5c633887d0b906a67dedad29df","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"artifact-index-corrected-review\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"6da2f58f\",\n  \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 5 assistant turns (soft limit 5, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n### Medium: Valid zero-OID intent-to-add entries remain rejected\\n\\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py:386-387`, with root handling at `:430-437`.\\n\\nParser rejects every zero object ID. Git index v3 permits zero OIDs for exact stage-zero intent-to-add entries. Approved behavior also derives roots from nonzero index OIDs only.\\n\\nImpact: A valid intent-to-add index can fail artifact encoding or decoding. Workspace replication becomes unavailable for that repository state.\\n\\nCorrection:\\n- Permit zero OID only for an exact version-3, stage-zero intent-to-add entry.\\n- Keep rejecting other zero-OID entries.\\n- Exclude zero OIDs from `_expected_roots`.\\n- Add SHA-1 and SHA-256 regression cases covering accepted intent-to-add entries.\\n- Add rejection coverage for zero OIDs without valid intent-to-add state.\\n\\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`. Parser validity and exact-root guarantees interact.\\n\\nRequired checks:\\n- Artifact plus bundle tests, including new intent-to-add cases.\\n- Final Ruff lint and format checks.\\n- Strict source mypy.\\n- `py_compile`.\\n- `git diff --check`.\\n\\n## Prior Findings\\n\\nEOIE ordering finding is resolved at `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py:410-425`. Later extensions and duplicate EOIE records are rejected. IEO