{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent_supervisor_request","content":"Subagent needs a supervisor decision.\nRun: 9ba166a3\nAgent: worker-advanced\nChild index: 0\nChild intercom target: subagent-worker-advanced-9ba166a3-1\n\nBlocked: TDD Guard rejects every file write (edit and write tools) with \"TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch\". This includes Green-legal red-test authoring in backend/tests/test_git_bytes_runner.py. No file in my allowed set can be created or modified, so the Phase 6 packet cannot start.\n\nState so far (no files changed):\n- Mapped owners/state: source Git repo owns immutable objects; run_git_bytes is the single executable/env/timeout/kill-and-drain owner; existing 144 unrelated working-tree changes preserved; my six allowed files are currently untouched.\n- Verified Git 2.39.3 (Apple) behaviors needed by the design: rev-list --objects --no-object-names includes tag objects (exact closure equality is derivable); pack-objects --stdout plain-oid stdin packs the exact object set; empty stdin yields a valid 32-byte zero-object pack; index-pack --strict --stdin fails \"pack has 1 unresolved delta\" on a genuine thin pack in an empty bare quarantine; pack trailer digest is sha1(20B)/sha256(32B) over the prefix; cat-file --batch-check echoes \"<oid> <type> <size>|missing\"; bundle v3 sha256 verify/unbundle work; asyncio Process.communicate() is safely re-callable with no input after a cancelled communicate(input).\n\nOptions:\n1. Rebind/initialize TDD Guard phase state for this session branch so test writes are accepted (preferred), then I proceed red-first as instructed.\n2. Confirm the guard is unavailable for this run and authorize proceeding without enforcement while I still follow red-first manually (tests written and observed failing before each production write).\n\nI cannot proceed with either implementation or tests until one of these is granted.\n\nReply with: subagent_supervisor({ action: \"reply\", rep