{"type":"compaction","id":"2adf664f","parentId":"cd0832da","timestamp":"2026-09-12T20:24:59.406Z","summary":"## Goal\nFinish Phases 6 and 7 of `/Users/user/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md` in `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`, validate independently, then commit, rebase, and push.\n\n- Phase 6 covers managed child integration, deterministic Git application and recovery, broker-backed Linux isolation, authenticated desktop-to-VM transport, bounded repository ingestion, durable replica authority, and drain/export/reclaim.\n- Managed integration does not require Linux. Native Darwin execution remains fail-closed.\n- Phase 7 covers nested delegation, budgets, steering, and persisted delivery semantics. It remains blocked until Phase 6 is accepted.\n- The immediate milestone is implementing the third, supplemental Git-object pack, then authenticated atomic publication of the three-artifact set and broker lifecycle wiring.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Continue implementation without waiting, but request approval before material privileged infrastructure changes. Disabled VM qualification was explicitly approved.\n- Use at least five subagents where practical; the parent controls integration, commits, rebases, and pushes.\n- Preserve the heavily dirty inherited Phase 6 worktree and unrelated changes.\n- Use `read`, `edit`, and `write` for source changes. Do not use shell source writes, mutating formatters, permission bypasses, manufactured failures, or production reversions merely to create red tests.\n- Do not disable or bypass TDD Guard. Worker branches have reported `TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.` Parent-authorized red→green writes remain the fallback.\n- RepoPrompt Context Builder sees a stale or missing `/workspace/yinshi` checkout and cannot inspect current commits `abff2b2d`, `2c781b53`, or the dirty broker files.\n- Use `backend/.venv` for backend tests. Ruff is `/Users/user/.pyenv/versions/3.12.3/bin/ruff`, version 0.16.5.\n- Required checks include focused and broad pytest, Ruff, format, isort, Flake8, strict mypy, `py_compile`, `git diff --check`, prose checks, Linux qualification, and independent review.\n- No SQLite handle may cross an external effect or `await`.\n- Unknown transport, timeout, cancellation, verification, delivery, acknowledgment, effect, presence, absence, or SQLite commit results remain stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n- Preserve exact ownership, runtime acknowledgment, markers, receipts, synchronization facts, and A4 authenticated journal positions.\n- Root protocol remains exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`; all gates remain independently disabled by default.\n- Drain is graceful broker-to-executor only. Missing acknowledgment or a live unit remains unresolved and blocks reclaim. Do not add a fourth root stop action.\n- Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Only bounded IDs, roles, media types, digests, lengths, limits, and typed receipts may enter the journal.\n- Broker lifecycle v2 and the read-only legacy v1 journal must remain unchanged by replica-authority work.\n- The stdio relay is opaque, uses the signed broker protocol for end-to-end authentication, and exposes no caller-selected socket path.\n- Preserve fixed executor identities `yinshi-executor-00` through `yinshi-executor-31`; callers cannot select them.\n- Keep `rft-sandbox` stopped and untouched.\n- Git replacement objects and lazy/promisor fetches must remain disabled for artifact generation and verification.\n- Artifact verification must use independent, empty bare quarantine repositories with the matching SHA-1 or SHA-256 object format.\n- Publication must reject unsafe paths, symlinks, digest or length mismatch, partial sets, overwrite, timeout, cancellation, and uncertain acknowledgment.\n- Publication must use same-filesystem atomic rename and correct file/directory synchronization ordering.\n- Do not stage unrelated dirty files. Milestone commits may include only reviewed files.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Phases 0–1 committed as `bebd2ccc`; Phase 2 as `e4a80b43`, `b488b502`, and `0cddd4bb`; Phase 3 as `2fd220b9`; Phase 4 as `ff7e6e81`; Phase 5 pushed as `1fa5d789 feat: add agent thread delegation and structured results`.\n- [x] Historical Phase 5 validation completed: backend 2137 with one skip, sidecar 119 with one skip, frontend 427, plus build, style, and mypy.\n- [x] Large Phase 6 candidate implements integration, immutable trials/results, physical admission, execution receipts, publication/recovery UI, migrations, and fixture Playwright coverage.\n- [x] Architecture A1–A7, corrected gate acceptance, publication acceptance, F6 acceptance, and offline A4 F1–F15 implementation/review were completed and recorded under `/tmp`.\n- [x] Integrated `workspace_replica.py`, its reconciliation suite, and `docs/workspace-os-isolation.md`.\n- [x] Trusted-Git gates, stable descriptor-backed Git operations, publication crash recovery, workspace repair, prompt-journal settlement, frontend repair handling, and durable repository deletion recovery were implemented.\n- [x] Repository deletion distinguishes imported and managed ownership, preserves imported metadata, uses durable receipts, handles unbound targets, and keeps malformed or legacy state unresolved.\n- [x] Root prepare/reclaim/launch use fixed paths, validated accounts, no-follow descriptors, mount checks, allocation locking, socket pinning, iterative reclaim, and default-disabled gates.\n- [x] Root persists `.executor-identity`, uses synced `.executor-identity.pending` publication, retains quarantine tombstones, and supports interrupted pin states.\n- [x] Linux recovery qualification passed for zero-byte and three-byte pending markers through prepare and existing-allocation paths.\n- [x] Linux reclaim qualification passed with `repo=0000` and `home=0777`.\n- [x] Broker lifecycle v2 implements immutable `accepted`, `lifecycle_claimed`, `stage_started`, `stage_outcome`, and `stage_unresolved` events with fixed `prepare → runtime_setup → launch` ordering.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py` and action-bound `LauncherSocketClient.prepare()`, `launch()`, and `reclaim()`.\n- [x] Implemented read-only legacy v1 admission through `inspect_legacy_v1_journal()`, including malformed schema, unsupported version, accepted work, and WAL/SHM sidecar rejection.\n- [x] Implemented fresh-connection exact-event verification after uncertain SQLite commits.\n- [x] Added `JournalCommitAbsent`; post-effect missing commits become durable `sqlite_commit_unknown` and never repeat an effect.\n- [x] Added `ManagedRootWorker` with bounded framing, serialized actions, a separate process group, startup readiness, and kill/reap behavior on timeout or cancellation.\n- [x] Established nested deadlines: root worker 30 seconds, launcher client 35 seconds, broker effect 40 seconds, connection 120 seconds.\n- [x] Separated `LauncherTimeoutError`, `LauncherTransportError`, and `LauncherVerificationError`.\n- [x] Clean launcher EOF maps to `LauncherTransportError` and durable `transport_unknown`; complete invalid framing remains `verification_unknown`.\n- [x] Exact replay coverage confirms clean-EOF uncertainty contacts the launcher once.\n- [x] Final independent broker review run `d00755d6` found no remaining findings.\n- [x] Focused broker/root lifecycle checks passed 172 tests. Strict mypy passed all 126 source files. Changed-file Ruff, format, isort, Flake8, `py_compile`, and diff checks passed.\n- [x] Latest broad backend run had 2797 passes, one skip, and three unrelated thread-integration failures from missing `HOST`; those three passed with `HOST=127.0.0.1`. An earlier corrected broad run passed 2799 tests with one skip.\n- [x] User approved disabled Linux qualification on `yinshi-runtime`.\n- [x] Installed the current wheel, systemd units, hardening drop-ins, and tmpfiles configuration in `yinshi-runtime`.\n- [x] `systemd-analyze verify` passed. Unit properties retain `NoNewPrivileges=yes`, private networking/devices/tmp, strict filesystem protection, AF_UNIX restriction, and bounded launcher capabilities.\n- [x] Root-worker Linux tests confirmed timeout and cancellation kill and reap the process group while the event loop stays responsive.\n- [x] Broker v2 Linux qualification preserved stage order, exact replay, and one effect execution.\n- [x] Root launcher returned disabled responses for all three actions.\n- [x] Legacy accepted v1 work blocked broker startup. Its hash and metadata stayed unchanged, WAL/SHM remained absent, and no production v2 journal was created.\n- [x] Broker and launcher sockets remain static and inactive. Services were reset to inactive. Every effect gate remains false. `rft-sandbox` remains stopped.\n- [x] Architecture oracle selected a separate broker-owned replica journal instead of extending launch lifecycle v2.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py`, `backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py`, and the `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay` entry point in `backend/pyproject.toml`.\n- [x] The relay reads one bounded framed stdin request, connects only to `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, forwards exact bytes, half-closes writes, reads one bounded response, and writes stdout only after complete success.\n- [x] Relay outcomes use `transport_unknown`, `timeout_unknown`, and `verification_unknown`; diagnostics expose stable codes without payload bytes.\n- [x] Relay timeout and caller cancellation abort `writer.transport` before cleanup waits.\n- [x] Relay CLI uses `add_help=False` and `allow_abbrev=False`; help spellings, abbreviations, positional values, and socket overrides fail.\n- [x] Relay packaging tests verify the exact script mapping.\n- [x] Corrected relay and daemon checks passed 68 tests. Ruff lint/format and strict mypy passed.\n- [x] Corrected independent relay review run `096e5eb4` found no remaining issue.\n- [x] Built and installed the relay wheel on `yinshi-runtime`. Exact-frame forwarding succeeded as `yinshi-app`; legacy-v1 fail-closed returned `transport_unknown` without modifying the journal.\n- [x] `RELAY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` is 125 seconds, longer than `CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py` and `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py`.\n- [x] Recorded a genuine journal red result: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal'`.\n- [x] Implemented replica schema version 1 with immutable metadata/events, ordered `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`, typed receipts, artifact references only, restart reporting, exact duplicate handling, and fresh-connection commit verification.\n- [x] Added explicit `complete_ingest()`, `complete_verify()`, `complete_publish()`, `complete_admission()`, `complete_drain()`, `complete_export()`, and `complete_reclaim()`, plus `record_rejected()` and `record_unresolved()`.\n- [x] Strengthened journal identity, contiguous event sequence, request-frame digest, stage-aware uncertain-commit, concurrent duplicate, and receipt/request/authority validation.\n- [x] `_validate_response_frame()` binds durable terminal state, stage, exact error code, and applicable receipt ID. Completed reclaim requires `status=\"ok\"` and null error; rejected/unresolved require `status=\"error\"` and the exact bounded code.\n- [x] Terminal response results use an exact flat schema. Direct and nested inline artifact content and error-field sentinels are rejected during append and replay.\n- [x] Replica journal validation passed: 21 journal tests and 144 combined broker/relay/daemon tests. Corrected review `e4184ba7` found no remaining findings.\n- [x] Added exact conflict-index support in `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica.py`.\n- [x] `_corrected_validate_index_entry()` accepts exact integer stages 0–3 and preserves `intent_to_add`, `skip_worktree`, and `assume_unchanged`.\n- [x] `_corrected_validate_entries()` rejects duplicate `(raw_path, stage)` entries and stage-zero/conflict mixtures while allowing unique stages 1–3.\n- [x] Canonical index ordering is `(raw_path, stage)` and exact index storage bytes remain preserved.\n- [x] Workspace replica reconciliation passed 211 tests; corrected review `823991c7` found no remaining issue.\n- [x] Implemented the deterministic bounded `YNSHRA1\\n` version-1 artifact codec in `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`.\n- [x] The artifact codec preserves `CONTROL`, exact `INDEX`, `MANIFEST`, and `ROOTS`, with `source_state_sha256 = SHA256(b\"yinshi-replica-source-v1\\0\" + four section digests)`.\n- [x] Artifact validation covers symbolic/detached/unborn HEAD, symlinks, ignored-policy binding, topology, immutable limits, pre-allocation bounds, digest corruption, and privacy.\n- [x] Committed reconciliation and artifact codec as `abff2b2d feat: add durable workspace replica reconciliation`; combined suite passed 266 tests.\n- [x] Implemented bounded Git subprocess output handling in `backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py`.\n- [x] Bounded readers kill on overflow, continue draining without accumulation, shield cleanup through repeated cancellation, and reap the child before returning.\n- [x] Explicit stderr limits work with unbounded stdout; bounded stdout defaults stderr to 16 KiB.\n- [x] Added narrowly validated `accepted_returncodes`, actual live overflow PID tests, repeated-cancellation tests, and stderr-only overflow coverage.\n- [x] Implemented `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py` and tests.\n- [x] Bundle creation supports SHA-1 bundle v2 and SHA-256 bundle v3, explicit committed refs, annotated and nested tags, detached HEAD, unborn HEAD, nonbranch and nested symbolic HEAD, and replacement-object isolation.\n- [x] HEAD capture uses `git symbolic-ref --quiet --no-recurse HEAD`, preserving the direct nested symbolic target.\n- [x] Requested refs and HEAD must peel to commits. Source refs, HEAD, and object format are recaptured after creation to detect races.\n- [x] Bundle verification uses a private empty bare repository with matching object format.\n- [x] Bundle/Git runner focused validation passed 69 tests; Ruff, format, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and diff checks passed.\n- [x] Corrected bundle review `2551c774` found no confirmed defects and required no remediation.\n- [x] Committed bounded bundle support as `2c781b53 feat: add bounded committed replica bundles`.\n- [x] Determined that a third artifact is required because artifact `ROOTS` carries OIDs but no object bytes, while committed bundles contain only objects reachable from committed refs and optional HEAD.\n- [x] Added strict Git-index parsing to `workspace_replica_artifact.py`.\n- [x] Added frozen `ArtifactIndexEntry` and `VerifiedWorktreeArtifact.index_entries`.\n- [x] Parser supports exact Git index versions 2 and 3 for SHA-1 and SHA-256, exact checksums, fixed-width OIDs, canonical paths, modes `100644`, `100755`, and `120000`, stages 0–3, extended flags, conflict-stage rules, and canonical `(raw_path, stage)` ordering.\n- [x] Parser rejects version 4, split-index `link`, sparse `sdir`, gitlinks, unsupported modes, zero OIDs, malformed framing, bad checksums, duplicates, stage-zero/conflict mixtures, and unsupported extensions.\n- [x] Approved opaque extensions are `TREE`, `REUC`, `UNTR`, `FSMN`, `IEOT`, and final unique `EOIE`; extensions after or duplicate `EOIE` are rejected.\n- [x] `ROOTS` now equals the canonical sorted unique set of HEAD OID, when present, and every index-entry OID on both encode and decode.\n- [x] Root input order remains semantically canonical while omissions, injections, and duplicates fail closed.\n- [x] Live SHA-1/SHA-256 tests confirm Git intent-to-add uses a nonzero empty-blob OID and preserves `intent_to_add`.\n- [x] Artifact plus bundle validation passed 91 tests locally; final clearance reran a broader relevant set and reported 111 passing.\n- [x] Ruff lint/format, strict source mypy, `py_compile`, and diff checks passed. Final clearance `fca93394` found no remaining findings.\n- [x] Committed strict index validation as `533df501 feat: validate replica Git index state`.\n- [x] Publication planner recommended implementing the standalone artifact store before broker wiring because transport, authority binding, and persistence ownership should remain isolated.\n- [x] Supplemental object-pack design was completed in worker-expert run `125925b9`/`94d9c6de`.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Implement `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py` for the fixed third artifact, `index-objects.pack`.\n- [ ] Extend `run_git_bytes()` with exact stdin bytes while preserving bounded cleanup and deadlock guarantees.\n- [ ] Add public committed-bundle verification that proves exact object inventory equals advertised-tip closure.\n- [ ] Generate and independently verify the supplemental set `E = required index OIDs - committed bundle inventory`.\n- [ ] Implement authenticated atomic publication of the fixed three-file artifact set.\n- [ ] Wire broker-owned replica authority to verify, publish, admission, graceful drain, export, and reclaim.\n- [ ] Implement verified broker-backed Linux execution admission while keeping native Darwin fail-closed.\n- [ ] Obtain a clean repository-deletion corrected review.\n- [ ] Integrate accepted fail-closed gate tests still absent from the main checkout.\n- [ ] Obtain current-blob reviews for remaining Phase 6 surfaces.\n\n### Blocked\n- Worker-advanced run `9ba166a3` for the object-pack milestone detached for intercom coordination. Recover with `subagent_supervisor({ action: \"pending\" })`, reply to its request, then use `subagent_wait({ id: \"9ba166a3\" })` and `subagent({ action: \"status\", id: \"9ba166a3\" })`. Do not resume or launch a replacement while it remains detached.\n- Phase 6 remains incomplete because supplemental object transport, authenticated publication, lifecycle wiring, broker-backed execution admission, drain/export/reclaim orchestration, gate-test integration, and full acceptance remain unfinished.\n- Production execution remains unsupported because `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py` has no verified broker-backed Linux profile.\n- Repository-wide Ruff, format, isort, and Flake8 still include unrelated pre-existing failures, including two `F841` failures in `backend/tests/test_api.py`.\n- Phase 7 remains blocked until Phase 6 receives full independent acceptance.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Managed integration scope**: Git worktrees provide isolated child results and deterministic application; Linux is not required for integration itself.\n- **VM purpose**: `yinshi-runtime` supplies stronger OS isolation for untrusted execution.\n- **Privileged launcher**: Root accepts only fixed `prepare`, `launch`, or `reclaim` actions and a lowercase hexadecimal operation ID.\n- **No root stop action**: Drain is graceful only; missing acknowledgment or a live runtime becomes unresolved.\n- **Separate privileged gates**: Prepare, launch, and reclaim each require independent opt-in.\n- **Dedicated roots**: Staging, replicas, quarantine, workload sockets, and protected pins use fixed launcher-owned namespaces.\n- **Prepared namespace**: Broker writes staging; root atomically promotes into protected storage.\n- **Promotion durability**: Sync the destination parent before the source parent.\n- **Executor pool**: Use 32 distinct host UIDs/GIDs named `yinshi-executor-00` through `yinshi-executor-31`.\n- **Allocation authority**: Root-owned `.executor-identity` is the durable allocation record.\n- **Quarantine tombstones**: Reclaim retains only `.executor-identity`.\n- **Private workload `/run`**: Each transient executor receives only protected `/run/session.sock`.\n- **Broker authentication**: Canonical Ed25519-signed frames supplement Unix peer credentials.\n- **Broker lifecycle v2**: Keep fixed launch stages and preserve legacy v1 as read-only.\n- **Separate replica journal**: Repository ingestion and replica lifecycle state belong in a broker-owned append-only journal, not launch journal v2 or application database rows.\n- **Replica stages**: Use `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`.\n- **Replica public model**: Use `ReplicaAuthority(physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id)`. Bind `owner_token` and `broker_incarnation` at `claim_authority()`.\n- **Replica decisions and positions**: `ReplicaJournalDecision` exposes `owner_broker_incarnation`, not the private owner token. `ReplicaJournalPosition` contains `journal_id`, `sequence`, and `append_receipt_id`.\n- **Replica completion API**: Prefer explicit per-stage completion methods with typed evidence; retain generic rejection and unresolved recording only for terminal failures.\n- **Replica milestone boundary**: The standalone journal performs no external effects and does not modify root actions.\n- **Terminal response semantics**: Durable state, stage, error code, and receipt ID must match the signed terminal response exactly during append and replay.\n- **Artifact storage**: Store only bounded IDs, roles, media types, digests, lengths, limits, and typed receipts in SQLite; artifact bytes remain outside it.\n- **Fixed artifact set**: Every publication contains exactly three files: `committed.bundle`, `worktree.yra`, and `index-objects.pack`. An empty missing-object set still produces a valid zero-object pack.\n- **Committed-bundle boundary**: Bundles carry only explicit committed refs and optional committed HEAD. They must not absorb staged-only object transport.\n- **Supplemental object definition**: Let `I` be every distinct nonzero index OID and `B` the verified committed-bundle inventory. `index-objects.pack` contains exactly `E = I - B`.\n- **Supplemental object types**: Every object in `E` must be a blob. `HEAD` must already exist in `B`.\n- **Object-pack generation**: Use `git pack-objects --stdout --no-reuse-delta --no-reuse-object --window=0` without `--revs` or `--thin`, with sorted OIDs on stdin.\n- **Object-pack verification**: Verify in an empty bare quarantine using `git index-pack --strict --stdin`, then require exact inventory, blob types, and configured per-object and aggregate bounds.\n- **Artifact-set identity**: Bind object format, source-state digest, reconciliation fingerprint, all three typed artifact references, replica identity, and generation into the receipt and `artifact_set_sha256`.\n- **Standalone store first**: Build and validate the publication store before broker wiring. Do not modify root protocol or activate gates.\n- **Conflict-index semantics**: One path has either one stage-zero entry or unique conflict stages 1–3. Modeled flags and exact storage bytes are preserved and fingerprinted.\n- **Git-index format**: Support versions 2 and 3 only. Preserve exact bytes while deriving typed entries and exact roots.\n- **Intent-to-add**: Actual Git uses the nonzero empty-blob OID for SHA-1 and SHA-256 intent-to-add entries; zero index OIDs remain rejected.\n- **Artifact envelope**: Keep deterministic magic `YNSHRA1\\n`, version 1, complete flag, and exactly four ordered sections.\n- **Artifact source digest**: Compute `source_state_sha256` from `SHA256(b\"yinshi-replica-source-v1\\0\" + four raw section digests)`.\n- **Artifact path policy**: Raw POSIX paths only; reject unsafe paths, `.git` components, missing parents, descendants below non-directories, duplicate paths, hardlinks, unsupported kinds, and privilege bits.\n- **Artifact bounds**: Immutable limits cover total and per-section bytes, index bytes, manifest count, path bytes, depth, per-content and aggregate content bytes, roots, pack bytes, object count, per-object inflated bytes, and aggregate inflated bytes.\n- **Durable stage boundaries**: Accepted intent and stage starts precede effects; confirmed or unresolved outcomes precede progression.\n- **Verified commits**: Close the failed SQLite connection, then compare the exact intended event through a fresh connection.\n- **Startup handling**: Claimed nonterminal work becomes stage-specific `broker_restart_unknown`; unclaimed accepted work remains accepted.\n- **Action-bound launcher protocol**: Requests and responses bind action and operation ID.\n- **Failure classification**: Deadlines use `timeout_unknown`, transport loss uses `transport_unknown`, and complete invalid framing uses `verification_unknown`.\n- **Managed root process**: Timeout or cancellation kills, reaps, and disables the worker instance.\n- **Database boundary**: Use read-copy-close, external effect, and reopen-transactional-CAS phases.\n- **Deletion policy**: Imported repositories preserve user Git metadata; whole-tree quarantine requires explicit managed ownership.\n- **Trusted path policy**: Path location alone never confers ownership.\n- **Gate backstop**: `run_git_bytes` refuses trusted Git when isolation is unsupported.\n- **A4 ownership**: Application owns logical reservation/binding; broker owns effects, synchronization, publication, markers, and physical release.\n- **Stdio relay**: Keep it opaque, fixed to `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, one request per process, with no caller path override.\n- **Relay cleanup**: Exceptional and cancelled exchanges abort transport immediately; normal close/wait happens only after complete response framing and EOF.\n- **Guard handling**: Never disable TDD Guard; use parent-applied packets and manual red→green checks when worker branches cannot bind the request.\n- **Phase 7**: Preserve the 20,000-byte contract, 100 pending inbox items, FIFO identity/generation, stop/seal/release ordering, unknown-cost retention, eventual depth three, persisted deadlines, and no scheduler. Default depth remains 1.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Recover worker-advanced run `9ba166a3`, answer its supervisor request, and inspect its object-pack changes.\n2. Validate red→green coverage for exact stdin handling, public bundle inventory verification, SHA-1/SHA-256 supplemental packs, empty packs, tampering, thin packs, replacements, limits, timeout, and cancellation.\n3. Run focused Git runner, bundle, object-pack, and artifact tests plus Ruff, format, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check`.\n4. Obtain independent corrected review and commit the supplemental-object milestone.\n5. Implement a standalone three-file publication store using descriptor-safe opens, exclusive staging, file and directory `fsync`, no-replacement same-filesystem rename, and restart-safe cleanup.\n6. Add typed artifact-set, verify, publish, and export receipts binding all three artifacts, immutable limits, source-state digest, replica identity, and generation.\n7. Wire replica verify and publish stages to broker-owned authority without carrying bytes in SQLite or retaining database handles across effects.\n8. Implement broker-backed admission, graceful drain, bounded export acknowledgment, and reclaim without adding a root stop action.\n9. Integrate remaining fail-closed gate tests and obtain repository-deletion acceptance.\n10. Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime` after source changes.\n11. Run complete backend, sidecar, frontend, desktop, documentation, and platform validation.\n12. Obtain full current-blob Phase 6 acceptance, then implement Phase 7 from `.pi-subagents/artifacts/8a18879f_planner_0_output.md`.\n13. Rebase and push only after final approval.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Main checkout: `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`; branch `main`.\n- Latest milestone commits:\n  - `abff2b2d feat: add durable workspace replica reconciliation`\n  - `2c781b53 feat: add bounded committed replica bundles`\n  - `533df501 feat: validate replica Git index state`\n- Before the last two commits, `main` was already one commit ahead of `origin/main`; it is now expected to be three commits ahead, subject to verification.\n- Worktree remains heavily dirty with unrelated Phase 6 changes. The three milestone commits were scoped to reviewed files.\n- Current detached worker: `9ba166a3`, mission `3160a290-ec07-4ecc-b927-caa06db969f7`.\n- Object-pack worker’s allowed files:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_git_bytes_runner.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n- Artifact files:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_artifact.py`\n- Bundle files:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n- Runner files:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_git.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_git_bytes_runner.py`\n- Replica-journal files:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py`\n- Supplemental object-pack design:\n  - `.pi-subagents/artifacts/1b2159d0_worker-expert_0_output.md`\n  - Run `125925b9`, follow-up `94d9c6de`\n  - Output `/var/folders/sp/rk1j_1ws7rqdyg8245gpw5hh0000gn/T/pi-subagents-uid-501/async-subagent-runs/94d9c6de/output-0.log`\n- Publication planner run: `1efdabcb`.\n- RepoPrompt publication-plan chat: `3D5B7714-92C0-49C4-9EF0-1A187871500D`, blocked because the target checkout was unavailable in its workspace.\n- Bundle reviews:\n  - Initial `1e66da98`\n  - Corrected `839a50b2`\n  - Final clearance `2551c774`\n- Index parser/reviews:\n  - Worker `021aa4e8`\n  - Initial review `e46c95b1`\n  - Corrected review `6da2f58f`\n  - Final clearance `fca93394`\n- A discarded test-writer patch added 1,147 lines of invalid synthetic index fixtures. It was reverted before the accepted parser implementation.\n- Phase 7 plan remains `.pi-subagents/artifacts/8a18879f_planner_0_output.md`.\n- `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json` predates the latest bundle and strict-index commits and should be refreshed.\n- VM sockets are static and inactive; all related services are inactive. Every effect gate remains false.\n- VM `yinshi-runtime` is running with the previously qualified wheel, not the latest local commits.\n- Production v2 journal is absent; accepted legacy v1 state intentionally blocks broker startup.\n- `rft-sandbox` remains stopped.\n- Full backend validation must use `/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/.venv/bin/pytest`.\n- Passing local and disabled-VM checks do not establish full Phase 6 acceptance.\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nThe user requested a supervisor decision for blocked subagent run `9ba166a3`: either rebind TDD Guard or authorize bypassing it.\n\n## Early Progress\n- Replied: do not bypass TDD Guard; switch the subagent to read-only delivery. The subagent later timed out without a useful packet.\n- Parent proceeded red-first and implemented:\n  - Binary `stdin_bytes` support in `run_git_bytes`, including bounded writer cleanup and cancellation safety.\n  - Public committed-bundle verification with exact reachable-object inventory and SHA-1/SHA-256 support.\n  - New supplemental index-object pack creation/verification with exact blob inventory, empty-pack support, quarantine verification, limits, and thin-pack rejection.\n- Added extensive tests for stdin blocking/cancellation, bundle tampering, replacement refs, non-commit refs, object limits, SHA-1/SHA-256, staged/worktree divergence, lazy-fetch exclusion, and thin packs.\n- Validation passed: 163 focused tests, Ruff, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and diff checks.\n- Final review found no remaining issues.\n- Committed these six files as `4242985d` (`feat: transport staged replica objects`).\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- Work then moved to an uncommitted standalone three-artifact publication store:\n  - New `workspace_replica_publication.py` and publication tests.\n  - Declaration and receipts bind bundle/worktree/index-pack roles, IDs, digests, lengths, object format, source-state digest, authority identity, reconciliation fingerprint, and limits.\n  - Publication uses private pending directories, synced 0600 files, canonical marker JSON, atomic no-replace directory rename, and final reinspection.\n- Initial publication tests passed: 7 tests; broader artifact suite passed 115 tests; Ruff and strict mypy passed before subsequent redesign edits.\n- Final review identified multiple high-severity race/classification concerns, notably:\n  - Staged files were not fully revalidated immediately before rename.\n  - `rename_attempted` did not distinguish pre-effect failures from possibly published outcomes.\n  - Pending cleanup was not sufficiently bound to the originally created directory/file identities.\n  - Final inspection needed pinned descriptors and post-verification identity/content rechecks.\n- Redesign started:\n  - Added strict nested-limit and runtime string validation.\n  - Added `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` to separate inspection from publication authority.\n  - Enforced that bundle-reachable index objects are blobs.\n  - Replaced simple reads with pinned regular-file descriptors plus identity/content rechecks.\n  - Added `_same_identity`.\n  - Most recently imported `require_atomic_no_replace_support` from `workspace_publication`.\n- These publication redesign changes have not yet been fully completed or revalidated.\n\n<read-files>\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/027713c4_planner_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/05bb63fe_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/0a089013_worker-expert_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/1499b7eb_scout_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/274e0d6c_oracle_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/3777e15d_final-review_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/3c61b813_test-writer_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/4596118a_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subage