      \"medium: incomplete_lifecycles returns request_frame but no request_from_frame method — caller must reconstruct BrokerRequest\",\n              \"low: _commit_transaction lacks rollback path; if commit succeeds but close fails, _append falls through but event_id may not propagate to confirmation\",\n              \"low: unbounded journal growth — no pruning of completed lifecycles\",\n              \"low: incomplete_lifecycles loads all identities into memory without pagination\"\n            ],\n            \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n            \"diffSummary\": \"No files modified. Read-only review of broker_replica_journal.py and test suite.\",\n            \"reviewFindings\": [\n              \"no blockers\",\n              \"medium risk: incomplete_lifecycles returns request_frame bytes but journal provides no request reconstruction method — lifecycle coordinator must hold or reconstruct BrokerRequest objects separately\",\n              \"low risk: _commit_transaction override path has no rollback; success-but-close-failure could leave _append returning stale position\",\n              \"gap: no lifecycle pruning — journal grows without bound as completed operations accumulate\",\n              \"gap: no pagination on incomplete_lifecycles — all identities loaded at once\"\n            ],\n            \"manualNotes\": \"The journal design is solid for append-only immutable event sourcing with SQLite. Idempotency is well-handled via unique partial indexes and idempotent completion checks. The commit-unknown recovery via append_receipt_id inspection is thorough. The main operational gap for a lifecycle coordinator is handling restart: incomplete_lifecycles provides the frame and owner_token, but the coordinator must independently manage BrokerRequest deserialization or store it alongside.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"toolCalls\": [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/broker_replica_journal*\\\"}\",\n            \"exp