     \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/conftest.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_foundation.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_foundation.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -l \\\"def test_\\\" /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/test...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -l \\\"def test_\\\" /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_sidecar_orchestration_lifecycle.py 2>/dev/null | head -1 && wc -l /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_sidecar_orchestration_lifecycle.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_terminal_channels.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_terminal_channels.py\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\nCall trace:\n- run journal: started\n- run broker: started\n- run publication: started\n- run execution: started\n- run testing: started\n- run publication: completed (160ba89e) in 75436ms\n- run broker: completed (333ae277) in 166386ms\n- run execution: completed (6cb36f7c) in 238676ms\n- run testing: completed (353dffde) in 314817ms\n- run journal: completed (061851b5) in 393572ms\nMission: ce5c7a6d-fcc9-498f-ba6e-412af8fcd070 (completed)"}],"details":{"mode":"workflow","runId":"call_emZnescRBfpWv05nzY40UMeR|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5bd0e0a4087d0b305f5dc863c25cc","results":[{"index":0,"agent":"scout","task":"Read broker_replica_journal.py and tests. Report exact public API, stage transitions, receipts, replay/recovery behavior, and gaps for a lifecycle coordinator. No edits.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"scout","model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3","thinking":"high","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"1d5de134eaf225505c68836b7a3e7c890183db4f587c4dbf1b6dccaee427d4f5","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":29464,"output":4121,"cacheRead":303132,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":13},"model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high","thinking":"high","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/061851b5_scout_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/061851b5_scout_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/061851b5_scout_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/061851b5_scout_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/061851b5_scout_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/061851b5_scout_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":5,"graceTurns":1,"turnCount":13,"outcome":"wrap-up-requested","wrapUpRequestedAtTurn":5},"toolBudget":{"hard":28,"soft":18,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":18,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":18},"context":"fresh","wrapUpRequested":true,"progressSummary":{"toolCount":18,"tokens":33585,"durationMs":393442},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":true}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 5 assistant turns (soft limit 5, grace 1). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\n## Findings Report\n\n### Source File\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py` (1,947 lines, ~50KB)\n\n### Test File\n`backend/tests/test_broker_repica_journal.py` (21 tests, all passing)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Public API — `BrokerReplicaJournal`\n\n**Constructor**\n- `__init__(self, path: Path, *, application_id: str) -> None` — opens/creates SQLite at `path`, validates schema on init.\n\n**Properties**\n- `path: Path` — read-only path to the SQLite file.\n\n**Lifecycle State Queries**\n- `status(self, request: BrokerRequest) -> ReplicaJournalDecision` — returns `absent`, `accepted`, `claimed`, `in_flight`, `completed`, `rejected`, or `unresolved`.\n- `incomplete_lifecycles(self) -> tuple[IncompleteReplicaLifecycle, ...]` — lists non-terminal claimed lifecycles for restart recovery.\n\n**Write Operations (idempotent where noted)**\n- `accept(self, request, request_frame, authority) -> ReplicaJournalDecision` — idempotent on (db_incarnation, op_id, type).\n- `claim_authority(self, request, *, owner_token, broker_incarnation) -> ReplicaJournalDecision` — idempotent on owner_token.\n- `begin_stage(self, request, *, owner_token, stage) -> ReplicaJournalPosition` — idempotent on (stage).\n- `complete_ingest/complete_verify/complete_publish/complete_admission/complete_drain/complete_export/complete_reclaim` — each takes request, owner_token, receipt, and optional response_frame. Idempotent on exact match.\n- `record_rejected(self, request, *, owner_token, stage, status, receipt, response_frame) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n- `record_unresolved(self, request, *, owner_token, stage, reason, response_frame) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n\n**Data Classes (immutable receipt types)**\n- `ReplicaAuthority` (physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id)\n- `ArtifactReference` (artifact_id, sha256, byte_length)\n- `IngestReceipt`, `VerifyReceipt`, `PublishReceipt`, `AdmissionReceipt`, `DrainReceipt`, `ExportReceipt`, `ReclaimReceipt`, `RejectedReceipt`\n- `ReplicaJournalPosition` (journal_id, sequence, append_receipt_id)\n- `ReplicaJournalDecision` (state, stage, response_frame, owner_broker_incarnation)\n- `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` (request_frame, owner_token, owner_broker_incarnation, stage, stage_started, reason)\n\n**Errors**\n- `ReplicaJournalError` (base)\n- `ReplicaJournalSyncError` (malformed/uncertain durable state)\n- `ReplicaJournalCommitAbsent` (commit absent after fresh connection check)\n- `ReplicaJournalConflictError` (conflicts with immutable event)\n\n---\n\n### 2. Stage Transitions\n\n**Order**: `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`\n\nDefined in `_STAGES = (\"ingest\", \"verify\", \"publish\", \"admission\", \"drain\", \"export\", \"reclaim\")`\n\n**Lifecycle**:\n1. `accept()` — creates event `accepted`. State: `accepted`.\n2. `claim_authority()` — creates event `authority_claimed`. State: `claimed`.\n3. `begin_stage(stage)` — creates event `stage_started`. State: `in_flight`.\n4a. `complete_*()` — creates event `stage_outcome`. State: `completed` for this stage. Only `reclaim` is terminal.\n4b. `record_rejected()` — creates event `stage_rejected`. State: `rejected`. Terminal.\n4c. `record_unresolved()` — creates event `stage_unresolved`. State: `unresolved`. Terminal.\n\n**Constraints** (enforced by SQLite triggers + replay):\n- `accepted` must exist before any other event type.\n- `authority_claimed` must exist before stage events (verified via owner_token).\n- `stage_started` must precede `stage_outcome`/`stage_rejected`/`stage_unresolved` for the same stage.\n- Stages must proceed in fixed order — no skipping or reordering.\n- Terminal states (`rejected`, `unresolved`, or `reclaim`-outcome) are immutable.\n- Events are never updatable/deletable (SQLite triggers).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Receipts\n\nEach stage has a typed receipt dataclass. The `_receipt_json()` function serializes to canonical JSON. Max 2,048 bytes per receipt.\n\n| Stage | Receipt Fields |\n|-------|---------------|\n| ingest | receipt_id, bundle (artifact_id, sha256, byte_length), worktree (nullable) |\n| verify | receipt_id, bundle_sha256, worktree_sha256, source_state_sha256, reconciliation_fingerprint |\n| publish | receipt_id, physical_target_id, replica_generation, publication_marker_sha256, synchronization_receipt_id |\n| admission | receipt_id, execution_owner_id, runtime_unit_id, session_socket_sha256 |\n| drain | drain_ack_receipt_id, quiescence_receipt_id |\n| export | export_receipt_id, bundle, worktree (nullable) |\n| reclaim | reclaim_receipt_id |\n\n**RejectedReceipt** — single `receipt_id` field.\n\nReceipt binding validation (`_validate_receipt_binding`) cross-checks receipt fields against the original request payload and authority. This prevents replay of receipts from different requests.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Replay/Recovery Behavior\n\n**On Open**: `_validate()` runs `PRAGMA integrity_check`, re-builds expected schema from statements via in-memory DB, compares against disk. Replays all events for each (db_incarnation, op_id, request_type) group through `_replay()` which enforces:\n- Strict ordering of event types\n- No events after terminal state\n- Correct stage sequencing\n- Response frame signature and digest validation\n- Binding consistency between frames and events\n\n**Restart Recovery**: `incomplete_lifecycles()` iterates all identities, replays each, and returns non-terminal claimed lifecycles with `reason=\"broker_restart_unknown\"`. Caller uses request_frame + owner_token to resume.\n\n**Commit-Unknown Resilience** (`_append`): If commit fails (before or after sqlite response), `_confirm_appended_event` queries by `append_receipt_id`. If present (idempotent replay), returns position. If absent and no collision, raises `ReplicaJournalCommitAbsent`. If collision, raises `ReplicaJournalConflictError`.\n\n**Idempotency**: All write methods check for existing matching events and return the stored `ReplicaJournalPosition` without appending again.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Gaps and Risks\n\n**RISK [medium]**: `incomplete_lifecycles()` returns `request_frame` for resumed lifecycles. The caller must have the original `BrokerRequest` object to call `status()` or `begin_stage()`. There is no `request_from_frame()` method on the journal — caller must reconstruct.\n\n**RISK [low]**: `_commit_transaction` is marked \"overridable fault boundary\" and tested via `FaultJournal`, but `_commit_transaction` only calls `database.commit()`. No rollback on failure — if the commit succeeds but `database.close()` fails, the event is persisted but no position is returned. The `_append` method handles this by falling through to `_confirm_appended_event`, but the code path through `event_id` could miss the confirmation if `database.close()` raises.\n\n**GAP [low]**: No explicit TTL or pruning of completed lifecycles. The journal grows unbounded.\n\n**GAP [low]**: `incomplete_lifecycles()` loads all identities into memory. No cursor-based pagination. Could be heavy with many operations.\n\n**NOTE**: `_validate_response_frame` in `record_unresolved` and `complete_reclaim` validates the response frame. However, `_complete` for non-terminal stages explicitly rejects any `response_frame` passed in. This is correct — only terminal stages emit response frames.\n\n**NOTE**: The `_append` method uses `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (not `BEGIN DEFERRED`), preventing reader-writer deadlock scenarios. Good.\n\n**NOTE**: `PRAGMA synchronous = FULL` and `PRAGMA journal_mode = DELETE` provide strong durability at cost of performance. Acceptable for a journal.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Test Coverage Summary\n\n21 tests, all passing. Coverage includes:\n- Schema immutability (triggers, metadata)\n- Full lifecycle replay from disk\n- Transition ordering requirements\n- Terminal state enforcement (rejected + unresolved)\n- Restart reporting (only claimed non-terminal)\n- Artifact byte isolation (no inline content in SQLite)\n- Commit fault injection (before/after commit)\n- Schema/history corruption rejection\n- Frame/sequence corruption rejection\n- Inline content injection blocking\n- Protocol binding enforcement\n- Commit-absence via stage unique key\n- Concurrent exact-accept race\n- Model bounds validation\n- Stage-specific unresolved reasons\n\nMissing: concurrent writes at different stages, partial failure mid-lifecycle recovery from disk, large receipt handling near byte limit.","controlEvents":[{"type":"needs_attention","to":"needs_attention","ts":1789246974441,"runId":"061851b5","agent":"scout","index":0,"message":"scout needs attention (no observed activity for 60s)","reason":"idle","turns":5,"tokens":28270,"toolCount":10,"elapsedMs":60078}],"attemptedModels":["local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":29464,"output":4121,"cacheRead":303132,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":13}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/061851b5/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"reviewed all public API methods and data classes in broker_replica_journal.py (1254+ lines), mapped 7-stage lifecycle, documented all receipt types and binding validation, analyzed _replay and _append for idempotency and fault recovery, verified 21 tests covering schema, lifecycle, corruption, concurrency, and fault injection — all passing."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"find broker_replica_journal*","result":"passed","summary":"Found source at backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py and test at backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"},{"command":"PYTHONPATH=src python -m pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -v --collect-only","result":"passed","summary":"21 tests collected, all passing"},{"command":"PYTHONPATH=src python -m pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -v","result":"passed","summary":"21/21 tests pass in 1.48s"}],"validationOutput":["21 tests pass. Source file 1,947 lines. All public API documented. No blockers found."],"residualRisks":["medium: incomplete_lifecycles returns request_frame but no request_from_frame method — caller must reconstruct BrokerRequest","low: _commit_transaction lacks rollback path; if commit succeeds but close fails, _append falls through but event_id may not propagate to confirmation","low: unbounded journal growth — no pruning of completed lifecycles","low: incomplete_lifecycles loads all identities into memory without pagination"],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No files modified. Read-only review of broker_replica_journal.py and test suite.","reviewFindings":["no blockers","medium risk: incomplete_lifecycles returns request_frame bytes but journal provides no request reconstruction method — lifecycle coordinator must hold or reconstruct BrokerRequest objects separately","low risk: _commit_transaction override path has no rollback; success-but-close-failure could leave _append returning stale position","gap: no lifecycle pruning — journal grows without bound as completed operations accumulate","gap: no pagination on incomplete_lifecycles — all identities loaded at once"],"manualNotes":"The journal design is solid for append-only immutable event sourcing with SQLite. Idempotency is well-handled via unique partial indexes and idempotent completion checks. The commit-unknown recovery via append_receipt_id inspection is thorough. The main operational gap for a lifecycle coordinator is handling restart: incomplete_lifecycles provides the frame and owner_token, but the coordinator must independently manage BrokerRequest deserialization or store it alongside."}},"toolCalls":[{"text":"find {\"pattern\":\"**/broker_replica_journal*\"}","expandedText":"find {\"pattern\":\"**/broker_replica_journal*\"}"},{"text":"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -name \"broker_replica_journ...","expandedText":"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -name \"broker_replica_journal*\" -type f 2>/dev/null"},{"text":"find {\"pattern\":\"**/test*broker_replica_journ...","expandedText":"find {\"pattern\":\"**/test*broker_replica_journal*\"}"},{"text":"grep {\"pattern\":\"broker_replica_journal\",\"glo...","expandedText":"grep {\"pattern\":\"broker_replica_journal\",\"glob\":\"**/*test*.py\"}"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"grep {\"pattern\":\"create_signed_request|create...","expandedText":"grep {\"pattern\":\"create_signed_request|create_signed_response|parse_signed_request|BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION|BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX|BROKER_RESPONSE_BYTES_MAX|BrokerReq..."},{"text":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/t...","expandedText":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -v --tb=short 2>&1 | tail -60"},{"text":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && py