_stdio_relay.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"}]},{"index":0,"agent":"scout","task":"Read workspace_replica_publication.py plus artifact/bundle/object-pack modules. Report exact callable contract, receipts, failure classes, byte ownership, and coordinator integration constraints. No edits.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"scout","model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3","thinking":"high","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"d9473d5507a6bb5e7387809587f73d9c3b9cbeff8a38fcde8c0324fe673b0143","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":28804,"output":3452,"cacheRead":9660,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":3},"model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high","thinking":"high","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/160ba89e_scout_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/160ba89e_scout_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/160ba89e_scout_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/160ba89e_scout_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/160ba89e_scout_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/160ba89e_scout_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":5,"graceTurns":1,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":3},"toolBudget":{"hard":28,"soft":18,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":8,"outcome":"within-budget"},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":8,"tokens":32256,"durationMs":75384},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":false}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"All four files read. Here is the structured report.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Callable Contracts\n\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\n**Class: `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`**\n\n| Method | Signature | Returns |\n|--------|-----------|---------|\n| `__init__` | `(root: str \\| Path, *, ceilings: ReplicaStoreLimits, expected_uid: int, expected_gid: int)` | `None` |\n| `verify_artifact_set` | `(declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration, bundle_bytes: bytes, worktree_bytes: bytes, index_object_bytes: bytes) -> awaitable[ReplicaVerificationReceipt]` | `ReplicaVerificationReceipt` |\n| `publish_artifact_set` | `(declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration, bundle_bytes: bytes, worktree_bytes: bytes, index_object_bytes: bytes) -> awaitable[ReplicaPublicationReceipt]` | `ReplicaPublicationReceipt` |\n| `inspect_published_artifact_set` | `(declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration) -> awaitable[ReplicaInspectionReceipt]` | `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` |\n\n**Module-level public functions:**\n- `_validate_declaration(declaration, ceilings) -> ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration`\n- `_validate_binding(binding, *, role, maximum) -> ReplicaArtifactBinding`\n- `_limits_fit(declared, ceiling) -> bool`\n- `_canonical_json(value) -> bytes`\n- `_domain_digest(domain, value) -> str`\n- `_match_content(binding, content) -> bytes`\n- `_inventory_digest(items) -> str`\n- `_publication_receipt(declaration, inspection) -> ReplicaPublicationReceipt`\n\n**Private helpers (all prefixed `_`):**\n- `_verify_artifact_set(...)` — validates declaration + content + decodes all 3 artifacts\n- `_root_identity(root, expected_uid, expected_gid)` — validates root dir ownership\n- `_write_regular(parent, name, content)` — writes file atomically with O_EXCL\n- `_read_descriptor(descriptor, byte_length)` — reads exact byte count\n- `_open_pinned_regular(parent, name, maximum, uid, gid)` — opens file, pins identity\n- `_recheck_pinned_regular(parent, pinned, uid, gid)` — revalidates pinned content\n- `_directory_identity(descriptor)` — JSON identity string from dev+inode\n- `_same_identity(value, identity)` — identity comparison\n- `_inspect_pending(...)` — re-verify staging directory\n- `_cleanup_pending(...)` — quarantine to `.abandoned`\n- `_rename_state(...)` — determines move status\n- `_inspect_final(...)` — final verification of published set\n\n---\n\n### `workspace_replica_artifact.py`\n\n**Public functions:**\n- `encode_worktree_artifact(artifact: WorktreeArtifactInput, *, limits: ArtifactLimits) -> bytes`\n- `decode_worktree_artifact(data: bytes, *, limits: ArtifactLimits) -> VerifiedWorktreeArtifact`\n- `compute_source_state_sha256(control_digest, index_digest, manifest_digest, roots_digest) -> bytes`\n\n**Dataclasses:**\n- `ArtifactLimits` (with `__post_init__` validation)\n- `ManifestEntry(raw_path, kind, content, executable, allowed_ignored, nlink, privilege_bits)`\n- `ArtifactIndexEntry(raw_path, mode, object_id, stage, intent_to_add, skip_worktree, assume_unchanged)`\n- `WorktreeArtifactInput(object_format, head_state, head_target, head_oid, index_bytes, entries, root_oids, policy_digest)`\n- `VerifiedWorktreeArtifact(object_format, has_index, index_bytes, index_entries, head_state, head_target, head_oid, policy_digest, entries, root_oids, source_state_sha256, total_bytes)`\n\n**Constants:** `MAGIC = b\"YNSHRA1\\n\"`, `DEFAULT_ARTIFACT_LIMITS`, version 1\n\n---\n\n### `workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n\n**Public async functions:**\n- `verify_committed_bundle(content: bytes, *, object_format: Literal[\"sha1\",\"sha256\"], limits: BundleLimits) -> awaitable[VerifiedCommittedBundle]`\n- `create_committed_bundle(repository, ref_names, *, include_head: bool, limits: BundleLimits) -> awaitable[CommittedBundle]`\n\n**Dataclasses:** `BundleLimits`, `BundleRef(name, object_id)`, `GitObject(object_id, kind, byte_length)`, `VerifiedCommittedBundle`, `HeadCapture`, `CommittedBundle`\n\n---\n\n### `workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n\n**Public async functions:**\n- `verify_index_object_pack(content: bytes, *, object_format: Literal[\"sha1\",\"sha256\"], expected_oids: Sequence[str], limits: IndexObjectPackLimits) -> awaitable[VerifiedIndexObjectPack]`\n- `create_index_object_pack(repository, required_oids, committed_objects, *, limits: IndexObjectPackLimits) -> awaitable[CreatedIndexObjectPack]`\n\n**Dataclasses:** `IndexObjectPackLimits`, `PackedObject(object_id, kind, byte_length)`, `VerifiedIndexObjectPack`, `CreatedIndexObjectPack`\n\n---\n\n## 2. Receipt Types\n\n| Receipt | Module | Purpose |\n|---------|--------|---------|\n| `ReplicaVerificationReceipt` | publication | Immutable verification result (no bytes) |\n| `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` | publication | Read-only storage inspection without publication authority |\n| `ReplicaPublicationReceipt` | publication | Durable publication result with sync receipt |\n| `VerifiedCommittedBundle` | bundle | Bundle verification metadata |\n| `VerifiedIndexObjectPack` | object_pack | Pack verification metadata |\n| `CreatedIndexObjectPack` | object_pack | Pack bytes plus verified metadata |\n| `CommittedBundle` | bundle | Full bundle bytes + metadata + head capture |\n| `VerifiedWorktreeArtifact` | artifact | Decoded worktree with source-state digest |\n\nAll receipts use `_domain_digest` with explicit versioned domain labels (e.g., `yinshi-replica-verification-receipt-v2`) for deterministic ID generation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Failure Classes\n\n**Publication module:**\n| Class | Base | Meaning |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError` | `Exception` | Input/declaration invalid |\n| `ReplicaPublicationCollisionError` | `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError` | Name already exists |\n| `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError` | `Exception` | Durable outcome unknown |\n\n**Artifact module:**\n| Class | Base | Meaning |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `WorktreeArtifactError` | `Exception` | Base |\n| `WorktreeArtifactEncodeError` | `WorktreeArtifactError` | Encode failure |\n| `WorktreeArtifactDecodeError` | `WorktreeArtifactError` | Decode/validation failure |\n\n**Bundle/Object-pack modules:**\n- `GitError` (from `yinshi.exceptions`) — raised by bundle/pack validation failures\n\n**Cross-cutting:** `WorkspacePublicationCollisionError`, `WorkspacePublicationError` (from `workspace_publication` module) — used for underlying atomic-rename failures.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Byte Ownership\n\n**Strict `bytes` ownership enforced:**\n\n1. `verify_artifact_set()` and `publish_artifact_set()` take `bundle_bytes`, `worktree_bytes`, `index_object_bytes` as `bytes`. Content is hash-checked immediately via `_match_content()`.\n\n2. `_match_content()` returns the input bytes only after verifying SHA-256 and length. No copies made — bytes are reused.\n\n3. `_read_descriptor()` reads content from open file descriptors during inspection. Returns `bytes`.\n\n4. `_open_pinned_regular()` stores raw `content: bytes` inside `_PinnedRegular` for re-check via `_recheck_pinned_regular()`.\n\n5. `_write_regular()` uses `memoryview(content)` for zero-copy writes.\n\n6. Bundle/pack modules receive `content: bytes`, pass to subprocess stdin via `run_git_bytes(..., stdin_bytes=content)`.\n\n**Ownership invariant:** The caller owns the bytes. The store does NOT free or mutate them. Receipts contain `ReplicaArtifactBinding` which carries `sha256` and `byte_length` — references, not copies.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Coordinator Integration Constraints\n\n**Dependencies on `workspace_publication` module:**\n- `atomic_rename_no_replace` — atomic rename with identity checks\n- `require_atomic_no_replace_support` — platform capability probe\n- `WorkspacePublicationCollisionError`, `WorkspacePublicationError` — underlying errors\n\n**Dependencies on submodule modules:**\n- `decode_worktree_artifact()` — called inside `_verify_artifact_set()` for the worktree\n- `verify_committed_bundle()` — called inside `_verify_artifact_set()` for the bundle\n- `verify_index_object_pack()` — called inside `_verify_artifact_set()` for the pack\n\n**Cross-artifact consistency checks (inside `_verify_artifact_set()`):**\n- Worktree `object_format` must match declaration\n- Worktree `source_state_sha256` must match declaration\n- Bundle HEAD must match worktree HEAD (or both absent for unborn)\n- Index OIDs not in bundle must be present in pack (completeness check)\n- Pack objects must all be `blob` kind\n\n**Publication flow constraints:**\n1. Verification first (`verify_artifact_set`), then staging\n2. Staging writes 4 files atomically (O_EXCL) with 0o600 perms\n3. Pending dir renamed to final via `atomic_rename_no_replace` (one rename = atomic visibility)\n4. If rename fails: state checked via `_rename_state()` — quarantine or reject\n5. Final inspection re-reads all files from disk to confirm durability\n6. `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError` raised if rename outcome is indeterminate\n\n**Process constraints:**\n- `expected_uid == os.geteuid()` and `expected_gid == os.getegid()` enforced in `__init__`\n- All temp directories are 0o700, all files 0o600\n- `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`, `GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1` — no remote/replace mutations during verification\n- `asyncio.CancelledError` re-raised in critical paths, wrapped in `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError` if already moved\n\n**No broker/SQLite/network dependency** — these modules are self-contained. All external interaction is via `git` subprocess (`run_git_bytes`).\n\n---","attemptedModels":["local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":28804,"output":3452,"cacheRead":9660,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":3}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/160ba89e/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"All 4 source files fully read. Publication module: 3 public async methods on WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore. Artifact module: encode/decode/public constants. Bundle module: create/verify_committed_bundle. Object-pack: create/verify_index_object_pack. Receipt types documented. Failure classes enumerated. Byte ownership model traced through _match_content, _PinnedRegular, and memoryview usage. Coordinator integration: depends on workspace_publication.atomic_rename_no_replace, workspace_replica_artifact.decode_worktree_artifact, workspace_replica_bundle.verify_committed_bundle, workspace_replica_object_pack.verify_index_object_pack."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"find for module files","result":"passed","summary":"Found 4 source modules and 4 test modules"},{"command":"read workspace_replica_publication.py","result":"passed","summary":"26KB, 640 lines"},{"command":"read workspace_replica_artifact.py","result":"passed","summary":"10KB, ~900 lines"},{"command":"read workspace_replica_bundle.py","result":"passed","summary":"8KB, ~400 lines"},{"command":"read workspace_replica_object_pack.py","result":"passed","summary":"7KB, ~350 lines"}],"validationOutput":["All public async methods verified: verify_artifact_set, publish_artifact_set, inspect_published_artifact_set, verify_committed_bundle, create_committed_bundle, verify_index_object_pack, create_index_object_pack, encode_worktree_artifact, decode_worktree_artifact, compute_source_state_sha256","3 rejection classes, 1 unresolved class in publication module; 2 encode/decode classes in artifact module; GitError in bundle/pack modules","Byte ownership: caller-owned bytes, zero-copy memoryview writes, receipt bindings are references not copies","Coordinator constraint: one rename atomic visibility via atomic_rename_no_replace; CancelledError handling with moved-flag; gid/uid self-check; 0o600/0o700 permission policy"],"residualRisks":["No evidence of how consumers consume ReplicaPublicationReceipt - downstream integration unverified","Cancellation handling in publish_artifact_set has multiple paths to ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError - exact semantics depend on race windows not visible in code","Test files exist but not read - coverage unknown","_inventory_digest uses domain label yinshi-replica-inventory-v1 (no version suffix on receipt domain labels) - potential future compatibility risk"],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No files modified. Read-only analysis of 4 source modules.","reviewFindings":["no blockers - all contracts, receipts, failure classes, byte ownership, and coordinator constraints documented"],"manualNotes":"Modules are self-contained with no SQLite/broker/network access. All external interaction is via git subprocess. The publication module is the coordinator-facing entry point; it composes artifact/bundle/object-pack verification internally. Receipt IDs are all deterministically derived from domain-labeled SHA-256 digests with version suffixes."}},"toolCalls":[{"te