{"type":"message","id":"e51975d7","parentId":"8793541d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T21:21:52.528Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_gvNbK1EZpU2UQqaoLA9A7c7P|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c26ff94c87d09402099b78bace2e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 10 assistant turns (soft limit 10, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nThe supervisor confirmed: stop writes, deliver a precise targeted edit packet. Here is the complete deliverable.\n\n---\n\n# Task Report: Fixed three-artifact contract in broker replica journal\n\n## Execution status\n\nAll `edit`/`write` calls were blocked by TDD Guard with `TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch` (persistent across retries; a session-binding failure, not a red/green phase verdict — on-disk guard state at `.claude/tdd-guard/data/` is stale and references an unrelated old session). Per the task packet and the supervisor's reply, I did **not** bypass the guard and made **zero working-tree changes**. Baseline was verified green before blocking. Below is the exact edit packet.\n\n## Files inspected\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py` (1947 lines, full read)\n- `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py` (full read)\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py` (canonical_json, signed request/response framing)\n- `CLAUDE.md`, `PYTHON.md`, `backend/pyproject.toml` (line-length 100, ruff, strict mypy, pytest config)\n- Git state: both target files are untracked (`??`); many unrelated modified files exist and are preserved; nothing staged.\n\n## Key design decision (flag for parent)\n\n`artifact_set_sha256` is **not** in the accepted payload (packet enumerates exactly 8 fields), so the packet below derives it broker-side: `sha256(canonical_json([bundle, worktree, index_objects] as artifact-JSON, fixed lifecycle order))`. Verify and publish receipts are bound to this journal-derived value. If the application must own/propose this value instead, the payload contract changes → needs parent decision before applying.\n\n---\n\n## EDIT PACKET\n\n### Part A — Red-phase test edits: `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py`\n\n**A1** — import (old block unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import (\n    BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n    BrokerRequest,\n    JsonValue,\n    create_signed_request,\n    create_signed_response,\n    parse_signed_request,\n)\n=======\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import (\n    BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n    BrokerRequest,\n    JsonValue,\n    canonical_json,\n    create_signed_request,\n    create_signed_response,\n    parse_signed_request,\n)\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**A2** — constants + helpers + fixed 8-field payload (old block unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\nWORKTREE = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"worktree_0000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"2\" * 64,\n    byte_length=456,\n)\n\n\ndef request_payload() -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"bundle\": {\n            \"artifact_id\": BUNDLE.artifact_id,\n            \"byte_length\": BUNDLE.byte_length,\n            \"sha256\": BUNDLE.sha256,\n        },\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": \"3\" * 64,\n        \"repository_id\": \"repository_0000000000000000000000\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\": \"4\" * 64,\n        \"workspace_id\": \"workspace_000000000000000000000000\",\n        \"worktree\": {\n            \"artifact_id\": WORKTREE.artifact_id,\n            \"byte_length\": WORKTREE.byte_length,\n            \"sha256\": WORKTREE.sha256,\n        },\n    }\n=======\nWORKTREE = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"worktree_0000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"2\" * 64,\n    byte_length=456,\n)\nINDEX_OBJECTS = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"index_objects_0000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"7\" * 64,\n    byte_length=789,\n)\nFOREIGN = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"foreign_00000000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"9\" * 64,\n    byte_length=1,\n)\n\n\ndef artifact_json(reference: ArtifactReference) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_id\": reference.artifact_id,\n        \"byte_length\": reference.byte_length,\n        \"sha256\": reference.sha256,\n    }\n\n\ndef artifact_set_sha256(*references: ArtifactReference) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Mirror the broker derivation over the fixed bundle/worktree/index order.\"\"\"\n    encoded = canonical_json([artifact_json(item) for item in references])\n    return hashlib.sha256(encoded).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef request_payload() -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"bundle\": artifact_json(BUNDLE),\n        \"index_objects\": artifact_json(INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        \"object_format\": \"sha256\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": \"3\" * 64,\n        \"repository_id\": \"repository_0000000000000000000000\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\": \"4\" * 64,\n        \"workspace_id\": \"workspace_000000000000000000000000\",\n        \"worktree\": artifact_json(WORKTREE),\n    }\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**A3** — receipt factory, four branch updates (each old block unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old (ingest branch)\n    if stage == \"ingest\":\n        return IngestReceipt(receipt_id=receipt_id, bundle=BUNDLE, worktree=WORKTREE)\n=======\n    if stage == \"ingest\":\n        return IngestReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            bundle=BUNDLE,\n            worktree=WORKTREE,\n            REDACTED,\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (verify branch)\n    if stage == \"verify\":\n        return VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n        )\n=======\n    if stage == \"verify\":\n        return VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=artifact_set_sha256(BUNDLE, WORKTREE, INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (publish branch)\n    if stage == \"publish\":\n        return PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n        )\n=======\n    if stage == \"publish\":\n        return PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n            artifact_set_sha256=artifact_set_sha256(BUNDLE, WORKTREE, INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (export branch)\n    if stage == \"export\":\n        return ExportReceipt(\n            export_receipt_id=\"export_000000000000000000000000\",\n            bundle=BUNDLE,\n            worktree=WORKTREE,\n        )\n=======\n    if stage == \"export\":\n        return ExportReceipt(\n            export_receipt_id=\"export_000000000000000000000000\",\n            bundle=BUNDLE,\n            worktree=WORKTREE,\n            REDACTED,\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**A4** — extend inline-bytes sentinel test (old block unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n    database_bytes = replica.path.read_bytes()\n    assert bytes.fromhex(BUNDLE.sha256) not in database_bytes\n    assert b\"artifact-content-sentinel\" not in database_bytes\n=======\n    database_bytes = replica.path.read_bytes()\n    assert bytes.fromhex(BUNDLE.sha256) not in database_bytes\n    assert bytes.fromhex(INDEX_OBJECTS.sha256) not in database_bytes\n    assert b\"artifact-content-sentinel\" not in database_bytes\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**A5** — append new tests after the final test (anchor = end of `test_unresolved_reason_is_stage_specific`; old block unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        replica.record_unresolved(\n            request,\n            owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n            stage=\"drain\",\n            reason=\"foreign_reason\",\n            response_frame=response_frame(\n                request,\n                state=\"unresolved\",\n                stage=\"drain\",\n                code=\"foreign_reason\",\n            ),\n        )\n=======\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        replica.record_unresolved(\n            request,\n            owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n            stage=\"drain\",\n            reason=\"foreign_reason\",\n            response_frame=response_frame(\n                request,\n                state=\"unresolved\",\n                stage=\"drain\",\n                code=\"foreign_reason\",\n            ),\n        )\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"object_format\", [\"sha1\", \"sha256\"])\ndef test_object_format_accepts_sha1_and_sha256(tmp_path: Path, object_format: str) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    payload = request_payload()\n    payload[\"object_format\"] = object_format\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate(), payload=payload)\n    assert replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY).state == \"accepted\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"object_format\", [\"md5\", \"SHA256\", \"\", 256, None])\ndef test_object_format_rejects_unsupported_values(\n    tmp_path: Path, object_format: JsonValue\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    payload = request_payload()\n    payload[\"object_format\"] = object_format\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate(), payload=payload)\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert rows(replica.path) == []\n\n\ndef test_accept_requires_fixed_three_artifact_payload_shape(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    key = Ed25519PrivateKey.generate()\n\n    legacy_optional_worktree = request_payload()\n    del legacy_optional_worktree[\"index_objects\"]\n    del legacy_optional_worktree[\"object_format\"]\n    legacy_optional_worktree[\"worktree\"] = None\n    null_worktree = request_payload()\n    null_worktree[\"worktree\"] = None\n    null_index_objects = request_payload()\n    null_index_objects[\"index_objects\"] = None\n    extra_field = request_payload()\n    extra_field[\"content\"] = \"artifact-content-sentinel\"\n\n    for payload in (\n        legacy_optional_worktree,\n        null_worktree,\n        null_index_objects,\n        extra_field,\n    ):\n        request, frame = signed_request(key, payload=payload)\n        with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n            replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n        assert rows(replica.path) == []\n\n    valid_request, valid_frame = signed_request(key)\n    assert replica.accept(valid_request, valid_frame, AUTHORITY).state == \"accepted\"\n\n\ndef test_artifact_reference_rejects_inline_content(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    payload = request_payload()\n    payload[\"bundle\"] = {\n        \"artifact_id\": BUNDLE.artifact_id,\n        \"byte_length\": BUNDLE.byte_length,\n        \"sha256\": BUNDLE.sha256,\n        \"content\": \"artifact-content-sentinel\",\n    }\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate(), payload=payload)\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert b\"artifact-content-sentinel\" not in replica.path.read_bytes()\n\n\ndef test_exact_duplicate_ingest_is_idempotent(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate())\n    accept_and_claim(replica, request, frame)\n    begin(replica, request, \"ingest\")\n    first = complete(replica, request, \"ingest\")\n    assert complete(replica, request, \"ingest\") == first\n    completions = [row for row in rows(replica.path) if row[2] == \"stage_outcome\"]\n    assert len(completions) == 1\n\n\ndef test_receipts_bind_three_artifacts_and_artifact_set(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate())\n    accept_and_claim(replica, request, frame)\n    accepted_set = artifact_set_sha256(BUNDLE, WORKTREE, INDEX_OBJECTS)\n\n    begin(replica, request, \"ingest\")\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        replica.complete_ingest(\n            request,\n            owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n            receipt=IngestReceipt(\n                receipt_id=\"receipt_ingest_000000000000000000\",\n                bundle=BUNDLE,\n                worktree=WORKTREE,\n                index_objects=FOREIGN,\n            ),\n        )\n    complete(replica, request, \"ingest\")\n\n    begin(replica, request, \"verify\")\n    verify_id = \"receipt_verify_000000000000000000\"\n    wrong_verifies = (\n        VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=verify_id,\n            bundle_sha256=FOREIGN.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=verify_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=FOREIGN.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=verify_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=verify_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=FOREIGN.sha256,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=verify_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=FOREIGN.sha256,\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=verify_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=FOREIGN.sha256,\n        ),\n    )\n    for receipt in wrong_verifies:\n        with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n            replica.complete_verify(request, owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN, receipt=receipt)\n    complete(replica, request, \"verify\")\n    verify_rows = [row for row in rows(replica.path) if row[3] == \"verify\"]\n    verify_receipt = json.loads(bytes(verify_rows[-1][4]))\n    assert verify_receipt[\"artifact_set_sha256\"] == accepted_set\n\n    begin(replica, request, \"publish\")\n    wrong_publish = (\n        PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=\"receipt_publish_00000000000000000\",\n            physical_target_id=\"other_target_000000000000000000\",\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=\"receipt_publish_00000000000000000\",\n            physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation + 1,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n            artifact_set_sha256=accepted_set,\n        ),\n        PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=\"receipt_publish_00000000000000000\",\n            physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n            artifact_set_sha256=FOREIGN.sha256,\n        ),\n    )\n    for receipt in wrong_publish:\n        with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n            replica.complete_publish(request, owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN, receipt=receipt)\n    complete(replica, request, \"publish\")\n\n\ndef test_export_receipt_may_differ_but_stays_bounded(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate())\n    drive(replica, request, frame, through=\"export\")\n    export_bundle = ArtifactReference(\n        artifact_id=\"export_bundle_000000000000000000\",\n        sha256=\"a\" * 64,\n        byte_length=10,\n    )\n    export_worktree = ArtifactReference(\n        artifact_id=\"export_worktree_0000000000000000\",\n        sha256=\"b\" * 64,\n        byte_length=11,\n    )\n    export_index = ArtifactReference(\n        artifact_id=\"export_index_0000000000000000000\",\n        sha256=\"c\" * 64,\n        byte_length=12,\n    )\n    replica.complete_export(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        receipt=ExportReceipt(\n            export_receipt_id=\"export_000000000000000000000000\",\n            bundle=export_bundle,\n            worktree=export_worktree,\n            index_objects=export_index,\n        ),\n    )\n    export_rows = [row for row in rows(replica.path) if row[3] == \"export\"]\n    assert json.loads(bytes(export_rows[-1][4])) == {\n        \"bundle\": artifact_json(export_bundle),\n        \"export_receipt_id\": \"export_000000000000000000000000\",\n        \"index_objects\": artifact_json(export_index),\n        \"worktree\": artifact_json(export_worktree),\n    }\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError):\n        ExportReceipt(\n            export_receipt_id=\"export_000000000000000000000001\",\n            bundle=export_bundle,\n            worktree=None,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            index_objects=export_index,\n        )\n\n\ndef test_replay_rejects_legacy_request_frame_and_receipt(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    key = Ed25519PrivateKey.generate()\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request(key)\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    legacy_payload = request_payload()\n    del legacy_payload[\"index_objects\"]\n    del legacy_payload[\"object_format\"]\n    legacy_payload[\"worktree\"] = None\n    legacy_request, legacy_frame = signed_request(key, payload=legacy_payload)\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        replica.accept(legacy_request, legacy_frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert len(rows(replica.path)) == 1\n\n    with sqlite3.connect(replica.path) as database:\n        database.execute(\"DROP TRIGGER replica_journal_reject_update\")\n        database.execute(\n            \"UPDATE replica_journal_events SET request_frame = ?, request_frame_sha256 = ? \"\n            \"WHERE event_type = 'accepted'\",\n            (legacy_frame, hashlib.sha256(legacy_frame).hexdigest()),\n        )\n        database.execute(_schema_statement(\"CREATE TRIGGER replica_journal_reject_update\"))\n        database.commit()\n    with pytest.raises(ReplicaJournalSyncError):\n        BrokerReplicaJournal(replica.path, application_id=APPLICATION_ID)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"tamper\", [\"legacy_optional\", \"extra_field\", \"null_index_objects\"])\ndef test_replay_rejects_old_and_malformed_receipts(tmp_path: Path, tamper: str) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request(Ed25519PrivateKey.generate())\n    drive(replica, request, frame, through=\"ingest\")\n    complete(replica, request, \"ingest\")\n\n    bundle_json = artifact_json(BUNDLE)\n    worktree_json = artifact_json(WORKTREE)\n    index_json = artifact_json(INDEX_OBJECTS)\n    receipt_id = \"receipt_ingest_000000000000000000\"\n    if tamper == \"legacy_optional\":\n        receipt_json = canonical_json(\n            {\"bundle\": bundle_json, \"receipt_id\": receipt_id, \"worktree\": None}\n        )\n    elif tamper == \"extra_field\":\n        receipt_json = canonical_json(\n            {\n                \"bundle\": bundle_json,\n                \"content\": \"artifact-content-sentinel\",\n                \"index_objects\": index_json,\n                \"receipt_id\": receipt_id,\n                \"worktree\": worktree_json,\n            }\n        )\n    else:\n        receipt_json = canonical_json(\n            {\n                \"bundle\": bundle_json,\n                \"index_objects\": None,\n                \"receipt_id\": receipt_id,\n                \"worktree\": worktree_json,\n            }\n        )\n    with sqlite3.connect(replica.path) as database:\n        database.execute(\"DROP TRIGGER replica_journal_reject_update\")\n        database.execute(\n            \"UPDATE replica_journal_events SET receipt_json = ? \"\n            \"WHERE event_type = 'stage_outcome' AND stage = 'ingest'\",\n            (receipt_json,),\n        )\n        database.execute(_schema_statement(\"CREATE TRIGGER replica_journal_reject_update\"))\n        database.commit()\n    with pytest.raises(ReplicaJournalSyncError):\n        BrokerReplicaJournal(replica.path, application_id=APPLICATION_ID)\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n### Part B — Red run\n\n```bash\ncd backend && venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -q\n```\nExpected (against unchanged production code): 37 collected; **~29 failed / 8 passed**. Failures dominated by `ValueError(\"replica request payload fields are invalid\")` raised by `accept()` for every 8-field payload (full-lifecycle, transitions, terminal, restart, corruption, commit-fault, concurrent, export, binding, idempotency, replay tests); `test_accept_requires_fixed_three_artifact_payload_shape` fails on the final valid-payload accept; `test_object_format_accepts_*` fail with uncaught ValueError. Accidental passes (for the wrong reason — field-set mismatch) are acceptable in red: `test_request_payload_rejects_inline_or_unknown_content`, `test_model_bounds_are_independent`, `test_object_format_rejects_unsupported_values` (×5), `test_artifact_reference_rejects_inline_content`.\n\n### Part C — Production edits: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py`\n\n**C1** — constant (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n_DIGEST_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\")\n_HEX_ID_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[0-9a-f]{32}$\")\n=======\n_DIGEST_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\")\n_HEX_ID_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[0-9a-f]{32}$\")\n_OBJECT_FORMATS = (\"sha1\", \"sha256\")\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C2** — `IngestReceipt` (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IngestReceipt:\n    receipt_id: str\n    bundle: ArtifactReference\n    worktree: ArtifactReference | None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.receipt_id, \"ingest receipt ID\")\n        if not isinstance(self.bundle, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica bundle reference is invalid\")\n        if self.worktree is not None and not isinstance(self.worktree, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica worktree reference is invalid\")\n=======\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IngestReceipt:\n    receipt_id: str\n    bundle: ArtifactReference\n    worktree: ArtifactReference\n    index_objects: ArtifactReference\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.receipt_id, \"ingest receipt ID\")\n        if not isinstance(self.bundle, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica bundle reference is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(self.worktree, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica worktree reference is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(self.index_objects, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica index objects reference is invalid\")\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C3** — `VerifyReceipt` (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass VerifyReceipt:\n    receipt_id: str\n    bundle_sha256: str\n    worktree_sha256: str | None\n    source_state_sha256: str\n    reconciliation_fingerprint: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.receipt_id, \"verification receipt ID\")\n        _digest(self.bundle_sha256, \"verified bundle SHA-256\")\n        if self.worktree_sha256 is not None:\n            _digest(self.worktree_sha256, \"verified worktree SHA-256\")\n        _digest(self.source_state_sha256, \"verified source state SHA-256\")\n        _digest(\n            self.reconciliation_fingerprint,\n            \"verified reconciliation fingerprint\",\n        )\n=======\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass VerifyReceipt:\n    receipt_id: str\n    bundle_sha256: str\n    worktree_sha256: str\n    index_objects_sha256: str\n    source_state_sha256: str\n    reconciliation_fingerprint: str\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.receipt_id, \"verification receipt ID\")\n        _digest(self.bundle_sha256, \"verified bundle SHA-256\")\n        _digest(self.worktree_sha256, \"verified worktree SHA-256\")\n        _digest(self.index_objects_sha256, \"verified index objects SHA-256\")\n        _digest(self.source_state_sha256, \"verified source state SHA-256\")\n        _digest(\n            self.reconciliation_fingerprint,\n            \"verified reconciliation fingerprint\",\n        )\n        _digest(self.artifact_set_sha256, \"verified artifact set SHA-256\")\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C4** — `PublishReceipt` (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass PublishReceipt:\n    receipt_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    publication_marker_sha256: str\n    synchronization_receipt_id: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.receipt_id, \"publication receipt ID\")\n        _token(self.physical_target_id, \"published physical target ID\")\n        if type(self.replica_generation) is not int or self.replica_generation < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"published replica generation is invalid\")\n        _digest(self.publication_marker_sha256, \"publication marker SHA-256\")\n        _token(self.synchronization_receipt_id, \"synchronization receipt ID\")\n=======\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass PublishReceipt:\n    receipt_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    publication_marker_sha256: str\n    synchronization_receipt_id: str\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.receipt_id, \"publication receipt ID\")\n        _token(self.physical_target_id, \"published physical target ID\")\n        if type(self.replica_generation) is not int or self.replica_generation < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"published replica generation is invalid\")\n        _digest(self.publication_marker_sha256, \"publication marker SHA-256\")\n        _token(self.synchronization_receipt_id, \"synchronization receipt ID\")\n        _digest(self.artifact_set_sha256, \"published artifact set SHA-256\")\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C5** — `ExportReceipt` (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ExportReceipt:\n    export_receipt_id: str\n    bundle: ArtifactReference\n    worktree: ArtifactReference | None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.export_receipt_id, \"export receipt ID\")\n        if not isinstance(self.bundle, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica export bundle reference is invalid\")\n        if self.worktree is not None and not isinstance(self.worktree, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica export worktree reference is invalid\")\n=======\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ExportReceipt:\n    export_receipt_id: str\n    bundle: ArtifactReference\n    worktree: ArtifactReference\n    index_objects: ArtifactReference\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        _token(self.export_receipt_id, \"export receipt ID\")\n        if not isinstance(self.bundle, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica export bundle reference is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(self.worktree, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica export worktree reference is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(self.index_objects, ArtifactReference):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica export index objects reference is invalid\")\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C6** — derivation helper, inserted after `_artifact_json` (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\ndef _artifact_json(reference: ArtifactReference) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_id\": reference.artifact_id,\n        \"byte_length\": reference.byte_length,\n        \"sha256\": reference.sha256,\n    }\n=======\ndef _artifact_json(reference: ArtifactReference) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_id\": reference.artifact_id,\n        \"byte_length\": reference.byte_length,\n        \"sha256\": reference.sha256,\n    }\n\n\ndef _artifact_set_sha256(\n    bundle: ArtifactReference, worktree: ArtifactReference, index_objects: ArtifactReference\n) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Derive the broker-owned digest binding the accepted three-artifact set.\"\"\"\n    encoded = canonical_json(\n        [_artifact_json(bundle), _artifact_json(worktree), _artifact_json(index_objects)]\n    )\n    return hashlib.sha256(encoded).hexdigest()\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C7** — `_receipt_json` branches (each old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old (ingest)\n    if stage == \"ingest\" and isinstance(receipt, IngestReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"bundle\": _artifact_json(receipt.bundle),\n            \"receipt_id\": receipt.receipt_id,\n            \"worktree\": (None if receipt.worktree is None else _artifact_json(receipt.worktree)),\n        }\n=======\n    if stage == \"ingest\" and isinstance(receipt, IngestReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"bundle\": _artifact_json(receipt.bundle),\n            \"index_objects\": _artifact_json(receipt.index_objects),\n            \"receipt_id\": receipt.receipt_id,\n            \"worktree\": _artifact_json(receipt.worktree),\n        }\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (verify)\n    elif stage == \"verify\" and isinstance(receipt, VerifyReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"bundle_sha256\": receipt.bundle_sha256,\n            \"receipt_id\": receipt.receipt_id,\n            \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": receipt.reconciliation_fingerprint,\n            \"source_state_sha256\": receipt.source_state_sha256,\n            \"worktree_sha256\": receipt.worktree_sha256,\n        }\n=======\n    elif stage == \"verify\" and isinstance(receipt, VerifyReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"artifact_set_sha256\": receipt.artifact_set_sha256,\n            \"bundle_sha256\": receipt.bundle_sha256,\n            \"index_objects_sha256\": receipt.index_objects_sha256,\n            \"receipt_id\": receipt.receipt_id,\n            \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": receipt.reconciliation_fingerprint,\n            \"source_state_sha256\": receipt.source_state_sha256,\n            \"worktree_sha256\": receipt.worktree_sha256,\n        }\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (publish)\n    elif stage == \"publish\" and isinstance(receipt, PublishReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"physical_target_id\": receipt.physical_target_id,\n            \"publication_marker_sha256\": receipt.publication_marker_sha256,\n            \"receipt_id\": receipt.receipt_id,\n            \"replica_generation\": receipt.replica_generation,\n            \"synchronization_receipt_id\": receipt.synchronization_receipt_id,\n        }\n=======\n    elif stage == \"publish\" and isinstance(receipt, PublishReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"artifact_set_sha256\": receipt.artifact_set_sha256,\n            \"physical_target_id\": receipt.physical_target_id,\n            \"publication_marker_sha256\": receipt.publication_marker_sha256,\n            \"receipt_id\": receipt.receipt_id,\n            \"replica_generation\": receipt.replica_generation,\n            \"synchronization_receipt_id\": receipt.synchronization_receipt_id,\n        }\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (export)\n    elif stage == \"export\" and isinstance(receipt, ExportReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"bundle\": _artifact_json(receipt.bundle),\n            \"export_receipt_id\": receipt.export_receipt_id,\n            \"worktree\": (None if receipt.worktree is None else _artifact_json(receipt.worktree)),\n        }\n=======\n    elif stage == \"export\" and isinstance(receipt, ExportReceipt):\n        value = {\n            \"bundle\": _artifact_json(receipt.bundle),\n            \"export_receipt_id\": receipt.export_receipt_id,\n            \"index_objects\": _artifact_json(receipt.index_objects),\n            \"worktree\": _artifact_json(receipt.worktree),\n        }\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C8** — `_validate_replica_payload` (old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old\ndef _validate_replica_payload(value: object) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    required = {\n        \"bundle\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\",\n        \"repository_id\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\",\n        \"workspace_id\",\n        \"worktree\",\n    }\n    if not isinstance(value, dict) or set(value) != required:\n        raise ValueError(\"replica request payload fields are invalid\")\n    _token(value[\"workspace_id\"], \"request workspace ID\")\n    _token(value[\"repository_id\"], \"request repository ID\")\n    _digest(value[\"source_state_sha256\"], \"request source state SHA-256\")\n    _digest(\n        value[\"reconciliation_fingerprint\"],\n        \"request reconciliation fingerprint\",\n    )\n    _parse_artifact(value[\"bundle\"])\n    if value[\"worktree\"] is not None:\n        _parse_artifact(value[\"worktree\"])\n    return cast(dict[str, JsonValue], value)\n=======\ndef _validate_replica_payload(value: object) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    required = {\n        \"bundle\",\n        \"index_objects\",\n        \"object_format\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\",\n        \"repository_id\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\",\n        \"workspace_id\",\n        \"worktree\",\n    }\n    if not isinstance(value, dict) or set(value) != required:\n        raise ValueError(\"replica request payload fields are invalid\")\n    _token(value[\"workspace_id\"], \"request workspace ID\")\n    _token(value[\"repository_id\"], \"request repository ID\")\n    if value[\"object_format\"] not in _OBJECT_FORMATS:\n        raise ValueError(\"replica request object format is invalid\")\n    _digest(value[\"source_state_sha256\"], \"request source state SHA-256\")\n    _digest(\n        value[\"reconciliation_fingerprint\"],\n        \"request reconciliation fingerprint\",\n    )\n    _parse_artifact(value[\"bundle\"])\n    _parse_artifact(value[\"worktree\"])\n    _parse_artifact(value[\"index_objects\"])\n    return cast(dict[str, JsonValue], value)\n>>>>>>> new\n```\n\n**C9** — `_validate_receipt` branches (each old unique):\n```python\n<<<<<<< old (ingest)\n    if stage == \"ingest\" and set(value) == {\"bundle\", \"receipt_id\", \"worktree\"}:\n        worktree = value[\"worktree\"]\n        return IngestReceipt(\n            receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"receipt_id\"]),\n            bundle=_parse_artifact(value[\"bundle\"]),\n            worktree=None if worktree is None else _parse_artifact(worktree),\n        )\n=======\n    if stage == \"ingest\" and set(value) == {\"bundle\", \"index_objects\", \"receipt_id\", \"worktree\"}:\n        return IngestReceipt(\n            receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"receipt_id\"]),\n            bundle=_parse_artifact(value[\"bundle\"]),\n            worktree=_parse_artifact(value[\"worktree\"]),\n            index_objects=_parse_artifact(value[\"index_objects\"]),\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (verify)\n    if stage == \"verify\" and set(value) == {\n        \"bundle_sha256\",\n        \"receipt_id\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\",\n        \"worktree_sha256\",\n    }:\n        return VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"receipt_id\"]),\n            bundle_sha256=cast(str, value[\"bundle_sha256\"]),\n            worktree_sha256=cast(str | None, value[\"worktree_sha256\"]),\n            source_state_sha256=cast(str, value[\"source_state_sha256\"]),\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=cast(str, value[\"reconciliation_fingerprint\"]),\n        )\n=======\n    if stage == \"verify\" and set(value) == {\n        \"artifact_set_sha256\",\n        \"bundle_sha256\",\n        \"index_objects_sha256\",\n        \"receipt_id\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\",\n        \"worktree_sha256\",\n    }:\n        return VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"receipt_id\"]),\n            bundle_sha256=cast(str, value[\"bundle_sha256\"]),\n            worktree_sha256=cast(str, value[\"worktree_sha256\"]),\n            index_objects_sha256=cast(str, value[\"index_objects_sha256\"]),\n            source_state_sha256=cast(str, value[\"source_state_sha256\"]),\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=cast(str, value[\"reconciliation_fingerprint\"]),\n            artifact_set_sha256=cast(str, value[\"artifact_set_sha256\"]),\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (publish)\n    if stage == \"publish\" and set(value) == {\n        \"physical_target_id\",\n        \"publication_marker_sha256\",\n        \"receipt_id\",\n        \"replica_generation\",\n        \"synchronization_receipt_id\",\n    }:\n        return PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"receipt_id\"]),\n            physical_target_id=cast(str, value[\"physical_target_id\"]),\n            replica_generation=cast(int, value[\"replica_generation\"]),\n            publication_marker_sha256=cast(str, value[\"publication_marker_sha256\"]),\n            synchronization_receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"synchronization_receipt_id\"]),\n        )\n=======\n    if stage == \"publish\" and set(value) == {\n        \"artifact_set_sha256\",\n        \"physical_target_id\",\n        \"publication_marker_sha256\",\n        \"receipt_id\",\n        \"replica_generation\",\n        \"synchronization_receipt_id\",\n    }:\n        return PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"receipt_id\"]),\n            physical_target_id=cast(str, value[\"physical_target_id\"]),\n            replica_generation=cast(int, value[\"replica_generation\"]),\n            publication_marker_sha256=cast(str, value[\"publication_marker_sha256\"]),\n            synchronization_receipt_id=cast(str, value[\"synchronization_receipt_id\"]),\n            artifact_set_sha256=cast(str, value[\"artifact_set_sha256\"]),\n        )\n>>>>>>> new\n\n<<<<<<< old (export)\n    if stage == \"export\" and set(value) == {\n