{"type":"message","id":"8cc6d69a","parentId":"9d273dba","timestamp":"2026-09-12T21:36:49.333Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Pt8U7KEBBk3v7lG9ms1wwZo0|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c5efd5b087d0b2668d5dcde481b5","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[gh-router] GitHub URL routing extension loaded\nTask: You are reviving a previous subagent conversation.\nOriginal run: c4cbc25b\nOriginal agent: final-review\nOriginal session file: /Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/c4cbc25b/run-0/session.jsonl\nUse the stored session context as background. Answer the orchestrator's follow-up below. Do not assume the original child process is still alive.\nFollow-up:\nYour review output was lost to prose lint. Return terse findings only. Include severity, location, impact, correction, validation. If none, state no remediation needed. Avoid semicolons. Read-only.\n## Acceptance Contract\nAcceptance level: attested\nCompletion is not accepted from prose alone. End with a structured acceptance report.\nCriteria:\n- criterion-1: Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\nRequired evidence: review-findings, residual-risks\nFinish with a fenced JSON block tagged `acceptance-report` in this shape:\nUse empty arrays when no items apply; array fields contain strings unless object entries are shown.\n`criteriaSatisfied[].status` must be exactly one of: satisfied, not-satisfied, not-applicable.\n`commandsRun[].result` must be exactly one of: passed, failed, not-run.\n`manualNotes` and `notes` are optional strings; an empty string means no note and does not satisfy `manual-notes` evidence.\n```acceptance-report\n{\n  \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n      \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n      \"evidence\": \"specific proof\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    \"src/file.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [\n    \"test/file.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"commandsRun\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"command\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"short result\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validationOutput\": [\n    \"validation output or concise summary\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"none\"\n  ],\n  \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n  \"diffSummary\": \"short description of the diff\",\n  \"reviewFindings\": [\n    \"blocker: file.ts:12 - issue found, or no blockers\"\n  ],\n  \"manualNotes\": \"anything else the parent should know\"\n}\n```\nReview blocked. Three findings remain.\n### 1. High\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:172-187`, `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:839-845`\n**Impact:** `PublishReceipt` omits `execution_owner_id`. Publication can bind one owner while journal authority records another owner.\n**Correction:** Add `execution_owner_id` to `PublishReceipt`, serialization, replay parsing, and authority validation.\n**Validation:** Reject every authority-field mismatch. Confirm legacy publish receipts fail during replay.\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced` due authority and persistence guarantees.\n### 2. High\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:828-837`, `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1470-1478`, `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:587-601`\n**Impact:** No production coordinator compares actual `ReplicaVerificationReceipt.artifact_set_sha256` with signed request value. Callers can construct journal receipts independently.\n**Correction:** Add one coordinator adapter that consumes actual publication receipts. Compare artifact digest and full authority before journal completion.\n**Validation:** Add integration tests for mismatched verifier digest, mismatched identity, SHA1, and SHA256.\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced` due cross-module authentication guarantees.\n### 3. Medium\n**Location:** `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py:885-931`\n**Impact:** Legacy request test leaves `request_payload_digest` unchanged. It can pass through binding failure even if legacy payload parsing regresses.\n**Correction:** Store matching legacy payload digest. Add replay cases for legacy verify, publish, and export receipts.\n**Validation:** Confirm each case passes current source and fails against prior source.\n**Remediation:** `worker` for settled persistence-test corrections.\n```acceptance-report\n{\n  \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n      \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Three findings include severity, exact paths, impact, correction, validation, and remediation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    \"backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n    \"backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n  ],\n  \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [\n    \"backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n  ],\n  \"commandsRun\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"git status --short && git diff --stat && git diff --name-status && git diff --cached --name-status\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Candidate files were untracked. No staged files existed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"sha256sum backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Captured reviewed candidate identities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"reported test, Ruff, mypy, py_compile, and diff-check commands\",\n      \"result\": \"not-run\",\n      \"summary\": \"Reported results were not independently repeated.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validationOutput\": [\n    \"Static review confirmed incomplete authority projection in PublishReceipt.\",\n    \"Repository search found no production coordinator joining publication receipts to journal receipts.\",\n    \"Legacy replay coverage does not isolate request-shape rejection.\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"Reported 32-test result and static checks were not independently repeated.\",\n    \"Task files remain untracked within a broadly dirty worktree.\"\n  ],\n  \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n  \"diffSummary\": \"Candidate adds fixed three-artifact references, object-format validation, and authenticated artifact-set bindings without changing SQL or schema version.\",\n  \"reviewFindings\": [\n    \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:172-187 - PublishReceipt drops execution_owner_id.\",\n\n[7 more lines in file. Use offset=121 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789249009333}}
