{"type":"message","id":"b357bbed","parentId":"00a0fae0","timestamp":"2026-09-12T21:38:41.681Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning worker-expert architecture discussion**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c6578cb887d08c9494dacc7bbf47\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning worker-expert architecture discussion**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Zg8QUv7PKSZosIMupYPLOVFC|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c6583f3087d0a3fa8cbb9c11a4c4","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"return runs.run('replica-ingestion-architecture', {agent:'worker-expert', task:[\n  'Read-only architecture diagnosis. Do not edit.',\n  'Phase 6 needs authenticated bounded desktop-to-broker ingestion for exactly committed.bundle, worktree.yra, and index-objects.pack, then broker journal verify/publish.',\n  'Current stdio relay is intentionally opaque and forwards one bounded signed broker frame to fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock. It must expose no caller-selected socket and should not buffer GiB artifacts. Broker journal signed request stores only artifact IDs, digests, lengths, object format, source digest, fingerprint, and artifact-set digest. WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore currently accepts three bytes objects.',\n  'Root protocol stays prepare, launch, reclaim. Gates stay off. Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Current launcher prepare creates broker-writable staging and protected replica roots. Desktop connects to VM as yinshi-app over SSH.',\n  'Diagnose current code and propose the smallest secure upload protocol and ownership flow. Resolve who writes staging, how end-to-end Ed25519 authentication binds chunks or files, how bounds and backpressure work, how retries avoid overwrite, how broker maps artifact IDs to safe descriptor-opened files, and how verify/publish avoid whole-file memory where practical. Preserve relay contract unless a justified compatible extension exists.',\n  'State owners, transitions, failure outcomes, restart behavior, and exact module/API additions. Flag any blocker requiring privileged infrastructure approval.'\n].join('\\n')})","async":false,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","timeoutMs":1200000,"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":9,"graceTurns":2},"toolBudget":{"soft":32,"hard":48,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"]},"chatProgress":"live-card"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":679,"output":411,"cacheRead":193152,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":11,"totalTokens":194242,"cost":{"input":0.0033950000000000004,"output":0.01233,"cacheRead":0.096576,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.112301}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789249108055,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c654b3a087d08cdfd2c7c47dcf01","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"5552c334","parentId":"b357bbed","timestamp":"2026-09-12T21:48:03.109Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Zg8QUv7PKSZosIMupYPLOVFC|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c6583f3087d0a3fa8cbb9c11a4c4","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"replica-ingestion-architecture\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"44151b43\",\n  \"output\": \"## Causal diagnosis\\n\\nPhase 6 has a control plane, but no artifact data plane.\\n\\nCurrent signed broker request can authenticate artifact metadata. Current relay cannot carry artifact bytes safely. Current publication store only accepts in-memory bytes. Root prepare expects a different directory shape.\\n\\n### Findings\\n\\n1. **Blocker: replica lifecycle requests never reach replica journal**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24` supports only `executor.launch`.\\n   - `BrokerReplicaJournal` exists, but broker daemon does not dispatch `replica.lifecycle`.\\n   - Result: signed replica requests cannot begin ingestion, verification, or publication.\\n\\n2. **Blocker: current relay cannot carry artifacts**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py:27-29` fixes `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, which is correct.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18` caps requests at 65,536 bytes.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:_read_frame` reads one complete frame, requires EOF, and buffers frame bytes.\\n   - Artifacts allow up to 1 GiB per set. Sending them inside signed JSON is impossible and unsafe.\\n\\n3. **High: publication APIs cause whole-set memory amplification**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779` accepts three `bytes` objects.\\n   - `_PinnedRegular.content` retains complete file bytes.\\n   - `_read_descriptor` joins all chunks into one object.\\n   - `_recheck_pinned_regular` reads files again and compares full byte objects.\\n   - Bundle verification copies bytes into a temporary file.\\n   - Index-pack verification passes the entire pack through `stdin_bytes`.\\n   - A near-limit set can create several GiB of transient memory.\\n\\n4. **Blocker: published artifact layout is incompatible with root prepare**\\n   - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` publishes:\\n     - `artifact-set.json`\\n     - `committed.bundle`\\n     - `worktree.yra`\\n     - `index-objects.pack`\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199` requires exactly `repo` and `home`.\\n   - Pointing the publication store at `/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging` will always fail prepare.\\n\\n5. **High: artifact-set digest contracts need one shared definition**\\n   - Replica journal accepts caller-supplied `artifact_set_sha256`.\\n   - Publication store computes a domain digest from the complete declaration.\\n   - That declaration includes authority, limits, repository identity, workspace identity, and media metadata.\\n   - Journal payload tests do not establish that desktop can reproduce this exact declaration.\\n   - Broker must recompute one shared digest before accepting bytes. Silent reinterpretation would change persisted meaning.\\n\\n6. **Medium: current deadlines do not fit bounded GiB ingestion**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` uses a 120-second connection deadline.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` uses 125 seconds.\\n   - Slow but valid 1 GiB uploads can fail despite continuous progress.\\n\\n7. **High: SSH identity is not end-to-end artifact authentication**\\n   - Broker sees Unix peer UID `yinshi-app`, not original desktop SSH identity.\\n   - Existing Ed25519 request verification provides correct application-layer authentication.\\n   - Artifact bytes must be bound to that signed request through signed lengths and digests.\\n\\n## Smallest secure wire protocol\\n\\nKeep existing `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay` unchanged.\\n\\nAdd a second fixed executable:\\n\\n```text\\nyinshi-broker-artifact-upload\\n```\\n\\nIt accepts no arguments and connects only to:\\n\\n```text\\n/run/yinshi/broker.sock\\n```\\n\\nReuse existing broker socket. No caller-selected path or new Unix listener is needed.\\n\\n### Upload wire format\\n\\n```text\\nu32be signed_request_length\\nsigned replica.lifecycle request\\ncommitted.bundle bytes, exact signed length\\nworktree.yra bytes, exact signed length\\nindex-objects.pack bytes, exact signed length\\nEOF\\n```\\n\\nResponse remains existing format:\\n\\n```text\\nu32be signed_response_length\\nbroker-signed canonical JSON response\\n```\\n\\nNo artifact names, offsets, paths, or chunk headers cross the wire. Order is fixed by protocol.\\n\\n### Authentication\\n\\nDesktop signs metadata containing, for every fixed role:\\n\\n- Artifact ID\\n- SHA-256 digest\\n- Byte length\\n\\nSignature also binds:\\n\\n- Operation ID\\n- Broker incarnation\\n- Database incarnation\\n- Sequence\\n- Nonce\\n- Object format\\n- Source-state digest\\n- Reconciliation fingerprint\\n- Artifact-set digest\\n\\nBroker authenticates signed request before reading artifact data.\\n\\nChunks need no individual Ed25519 signatures. Chunk boundaries are transport details. Signed file length, fixed ordering, and signed SHA-256 bind every file byte and position.\\n\\nBroker publishes nothing until all three incremental hashes match. Modified, reordered, truncated, extended, or substituted bytes fail verification.\\n\\n## Bounds and backpressure\\n\\nUse 64 KiB transfer buffers at every hop.\\n\\nDesktop:\\n\\n1. Write bounded signed frame.\\n2. Stream each local file through SSH.\\n3. Respect writable-stream backpressure.\\n4. Close SSH stdin after third file.\\n\\nUpload relay:\\n\\n1. Buffer only four-byte prefix plus signed frame.\\n2. Forward frame immediately.\\n3. Copy remaining stdin in 64 KiB blocks.\\n4. Call socket drain after each block.\\n5. Enforce fixed global tail ceiling of 1 GiB.\\n6. Expose no CLI options.\\n\\nBroker:\\n\\n1. Validate signed declared lengths before reading data.\\n2. Enforce per-role server ceilings.\\n3. Enforce aggregate 1 GiB ceiling.\\n4. Read exactly each declared length.\\n5. Reject any trailing byte.\\n6. Incrementally hash while writing.\\n7. Apply idle deadlines, not one 120-second total deadline.\\n8. Limit concurrent uploads and reserve declared storage.\\n\\nSocket and SSH flow control then propagate disk pressure back to desktop. No layer queues an entire artifact.\\n\\n## Storage ownership and safe mapping\\n\\n### Durable artifact roots\\n\\nAdd broker-owned roots:\\n\\n```text\\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/incoming\\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/published\\n```\\n\\nBoth should be `0700`, owned by `yinshi-broker`.\\n\\nDesktop and `yinshi-app` never write these roots. Broker performs every artifact write.\\n\\nArtifact IDs must never become path components. Broker maps signed roles to fixed names:\\n\\n```text\\ncommitted_bundle -> committed.bundle\\nworktree         -> worktree.yra\\nindex_objects    -> index-objects.pack\\n```\\n\\nRequire all three artifact IDs to be distinct.\\n\\nOpen operation directories relative to pinned root descriptors. Open files with:\\n\\n```text\\nO_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK\\n```\\n\\nRequire:\\n\\n- Regular file\\n- Broker ownership\\n- Mode `0600`\\n- Link count one\\n- Exact signed length\\n- Matching named and opened inode\\n- Matching filesystem identity\\n\\nConsumers request a role. Store returns a pinned descriptor plus authenticated artifact ID. It never resolves `root / artifact_id`.\\n\\n## Ingestion and retry flow\\n\\n1. Broker authenticates request.\\n2. Broker validates strict replica payload and limits.\\n3. Journal records exact signed request.\\n4. Journal claims lifecycle authority.\\n5. Journal begins `ingest`.\\n6. Broker creates broker-generated pending directory with `O_EXCL` semantics.\\n7. Broker streams fixed files using exclusive creation.\\n8. Broker hashes and synchronizes each file.\\n9. Broker verifies directory and file identities.\\n10. Broker renames pending directory to `incoming/<operation_id>` with no replacement.\\n11. Broker synchronizes both parents.\\n12. Journal completes `ingest`.\\n\\nNever overwrite an existing file or directory.\\n\\nRetry rules:\\n\\n- Exact request plus exact completed incoming set: inspect and reuse.\\n- Exact request plus exact published set: return stored or reconstructed progress.\\n- Existing set with different identity or content: reject. Never replace it.\\n- Different signed frame using same operation ID: journal conflict.\\n- Partial live attempt with confirmed cleanup: retry starts a new exclusive attempt.\\n- Uncertain cleanup or rename: mark unresolved and retain state.\\n- Lost final response: exact request replay returns journaled signed response.\\n- Restart with only partial bytes: quarantine attempt and mark `transfer_unknown`.\\n- Restart with exact synchronized incoming files: resume deterministic verification.\\n- Retry after stale broker incarnation requires a new signed request and operation.\\n\\n## Verification and publication\\n\\n### Ingest verification\\n\\nIngest verifies only:\\n\\n- Signed lengths\\n- SHA-256 digests\\n- Fixed role ordering\\n- Safe file identity\\n\\nThen journal records `IngestReceipt`.\\n\\n### Semantic verification\\n\\nOpen pinned descriptors from `incoming`.\\n\\nAdd file-based verification:\\n\\n- Bundle verifier passes a stable read-only file descriptor path to Git.\\n- Index-pack verifier passes a stable read-only pack path to Git.\\n- Worktree decoder reads bounded sections from a descriptor.\\n- Hash checks use incremental `pread`.\\n- Identity and digest are rechecked after semantic verification.\\n\\nJournal then records `VerifyReceipt`.\\n\\n### Artifact publication\\n\\nAdd adoption support to `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\\n\\nIt should:\\n\\n1. Accept pinned incoming descriptors plus prior verification receipt.\\n2. Write bounded `artifact-set.json`.\\n3. Recheck all identities and hashes.\\n4. Rename `incoming/<operation_id>` to `published/<operation_id>` without replacement.\\n5. Synchronize source and destination parents.\\n6. Inspect final directory.\\n7. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\\n\\nKeep current bytes API as an explicit compatibility wrapper for existing tests. Production ingestion must use descriptor API.\\n\\nJournal records `PublishReceipt` only after durable final inspection.\\n\\n### Launcher staging\\n\\nPublished artifacts cannot be sent directly to root prepare.\\n\\nBroker-owned materializer must build:\\n\\n```text\\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/.<operation_id>.pending/\\n  repo/\\n  home/\\n```\\n\\nIt reconstructs repository and worktree from pinned published artifacts. It then synchronizes and renames pending directory to:\\n\\n```text\\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/<operation_id>\\n```\\n\\nRoot launcher then performs existing transitions:\\n\\n```text\\nprepare -> launch -> reclaim\\n```\\n\\nNo path enters root protocol. Only operation ID enters it.\\n\\n## State ownership\\n\\n| State | Owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Source snapshot and desktop private key | Desktop |\\n| SSH session authorization | SSH infrastructure |\\n| Signed logical request and replay identity | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Partial upload descriptors | Broker ingestion handler |\\n| Incoming immutable artifact set | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\\n| Semantic verification result | Broker journal |\\n| Published immutable artifacts | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\\n| Unprepared `repo/home` tree | Broker |\\n| Promotion and ownership transfer | Root launcher |\\n| Prepared operation directory | Root |\\n| Prepared `repo/home` | Allocated executor |\\n| Runtime listener and retained descriptor | Broker runtime |\\n| Reclaim quarantine and deletion | Root launcher |\\n\\n## Permitted transitions\\n\\n```text\\nabsent\\n  -> accepted\\n  -> claimed\\n  -> ingest_started\\n  -> ingested\\n  -> verify_started\\n  -> verified\\n  -> publish_started\\n  -> published\\n  -> admission\\n  -> drain\\n  -> export\\n  -> reclaim\\n```\\n\\nDisk transitions:\\n\\n```text\\nabsent\\n  -> private attempt\\n  -> synchronized incoming\\n  -> verified incoming\\n  -> published artifacts\\n  -> materialization pending\\n  -> launcher staging\\n  -> protected replica\\n  -> quarantine\\n  -> reclaimed\\n```\\n\\n## Invalid transitions\\n\\n- Reading artifact bytes before request authentication\\n- Unknown, missing, duplicated, or reordered roles\\n- Duplicate artifact IDs\\n- Declared limits above server ceilings\\n- Truncation or trailing data\\n- Artifact ID used as a path\\n- Replacing existing incoming, published, staging, or replica state\\n- Verification completion before ingest completion\\n- Publication completion before semantic verification\\n- Root prepare before exact `repo/home` staging exists\\n- Launch after unresolved synchronization\\n- Adopting orphan disk state without matching signed journal request\\n- Continuing when both incoming and published states exist\\n- Converting journal or filesystem uncertainty into success\\n\\n## Failure and cancellation outcomes\\n\\n- Authentication failure: close without signed success.\\n- Limit failure before upload: signed rejection when request authentication succeeded.\\n- Digest or length mismatch: `artifact_rejected`.\\n- Declared aggregate overflow: `limit_rejected`.\\n- Semantic failure: `verification_rejected`.\\n- Confirmed publication collision: `publication_rejected`.\\n- Rename or synchronization uncertainty: `publication_unknown` or `synchronization_unknown`.\\n- Cancellation during partial receive: clean only pinned owned attempt.\\n- Uncertain cleanup: `transfer_unknown`.\\n- Cancellation after durable ingest: shield verification and publication. Journal remains authoritative.\\n- SQLite failure before acceptance: do not read artifact bytes.\\n- SQLite commit uncertainty after bytes: retain synchronized files, return no success, and reconcile exact row plus exact files.\\n- Identity uncertainty: fail closed and retain state.\\n\\n## Restart behavior\\n\\nStartup reconciliation must use `BrokerReplicaJournal.incomplete_lifecycles()`.\\n\\nFor each stored signed request:\\n\\n- Reauthenticate stored frame.\\n- Reconstruct fixed manifest.\\n- Open only descriptor-relative fixed locations.\\n- Resume ingest completion when exact incoming files exist.\\n- Repeat semantic verification because it has no external irreversible effect.\\n- Inspect exact published state before completing publish.\\n- Quarantine partial or foreign state.\\n- Mark ambiguity unresolved.\\n- Never adopt an unjournaled operation.\\n- Never overwrite state to make recovery succeed.\\n\\nReceipts should be deterministic from request identity and verified state. This permits safe replay after commit-response loss.\\n\\n## Exact module and API additions\\n\\n### New modules\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\\n\\n```python\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass OpenedReplicaArtifacts:\\n    operation_id: str\\n    bundle: OpenedArtifact\\n    worktree: OpenedArtifact\\n    index_objects: OpenedArtifact\\n\\nclass BrokerArtifactStore:\\n    async def receive(\\n        self,\\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\\n\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def open_incoming(\\n        self,\\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\\n    ) -> Iterator[OpenedReplicaArtifacts]: ...\\n\\n    def inspect_incoming(\\n        self,\\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\\n\\n    def reconcile_attempts(\\n        self,\\n        journal_operations: frozenset[str],\\n    ) -> tuple[ReconciliationResult, ...]: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_service.py`\\n\\n```python\\nclass BrokerReplicaService:\\n    async def handle_upload(\\n        self,\\n        request: BrokerRequest,\\n        request_frame: bytes,\\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\\n    ) -> bytes: ...\\n\\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> None: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def relay_upload(\\n    *,\\n    broker_socket: Path = DEFAULT_BROKER_SOCKET,\\n) -> bytes: ...\\n```\\n\\nProduction entry point accepts no arguments.\\n\\n`desktop/src/brokerArtifactUpload.ts`\\n\\n```typescript\\nexport async function uploadReplicaArtifacts(\\n  request: SignedBrokerRequest,\\n  artifacts: ReplicaArtifactFiles,\\n): Promise<SignedBrokerResponse>;\\n```\\n\\nRemote command must be a fixed constant. API must not accept a socket path or arbitrary remote command.\\n\\n### Existing module changes\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py`\\n\\n- Add strict `ReplicaArtifactManifest`.\\n- Add `parse_replica_lifecycle_payload`.\\n- Add shared `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256`.\\n- Require distinct artifact IDs.\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\\n\\n- Split framed request reading from EOF enforcement.\\n- Authenticate initial frame before reading upload tail.\\n- Dispatch `executor.launch` to existing service.\\n- Dispatch `replica.lifecycle` to replica service.\\n- Preserve EOF requirement for ordinary broker relay.\\n- Replace total upload timeout with bounded idle deadlines.\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def verify_artifact_files(\\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\\n) -> ReplicaVerificationReceipt: ...\\n\\nasync def adopt_verified_artifact_set(\\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\\n    verification: ReplicaVerificationReceipt,\\n) -> ReplicaPublicationReceipt: ...\\n```\\n\\nKeep `publish_artifact_set(...bytes...)` only as compatibility wrapper.\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def verify_committed_bundle_file(\\n    descriptor: int,\\n    *,\\n    object_format: Literal[\\\"sha1\\\", \\\"sha256\\\"],\\n    limits: BundleLimits,\\n) -> VerifiedCommittedBundle: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def verify_index_object_pack_file(\\n    descriptor: int,\\n    *,\\n    object_format: Literal[\\\"sha1\\\", \\\"sha256\\\"],\\n    expected_oids: Sequence[str],\\n    limits: IndexObjectPackLimits,\\n) -> VerifiedIndexObjectPack: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`\\n\\n```python\\ndef inspect_worktree_artifact_file(\\n    descriptor: int,\\n    *,\\n    limits: ArtifactLimits,\\n) -> VerifiedWorktreeArtifactMetadata: ...\\n```\\n\\nMaterialization should use a streaming entry visitor rather than retaining every content payload.\\n\\n## Rejected alternatives\\n\\n- **Put artifacts in signed JSON:** rejected by 65,536-byte broker frame ceiling.\\n- **Use current relay for raw trailing bytes:** rejected because it requires one framed request and EOF.\\n- **Use SCP or SFTP into launcher staging:** rejected because `yinshi-app` does not own staging. It would also bypass journal admission.\\n- **Let desktop select a Unix socket:** rejected because it breaks fixed relay boundary.\\n- **Use artifact IDs as filenames:** rejected because IDs are caller-controlled identifiers.\\n- **Point publication store at launcher staging:** rejected by root launcher exact `repo/home` check.\\n- **Sign each 64 KiB chunk:** rejected as unnecessary. Signed whole-file length and digest already bind complete ordered content.\\n- **Rely on SSH authentication alone:** rejected because broker sees only local Unix UID.\\n\\n## Privileged infrastructure blockers\\n\\nProduction gates must remain off until these receive approval:\\n\\n1. Install and allowlist fixed SSH command `yinshi-broker-artifact-upload`.\\n2. Confirm `yinshi-app` cannot request arbitrary relay commands or socket paths.\\n3. Provision desktop Ed25519 public key into protected broker configuration.\\n4. Create broker-owned incoming and published roots through `tmpfiles.d`.\\n5. Define disk quota or reserved capacity for concurrent 1 GiB uploads.\\n6. Isolate untrusted Git verification from broker signing keys.\\n\\nLast item may require a dedicated verifier service account or systemd sandbox. Root launcher actions should not expand beyond prepare, launch, and reclaim.\\n\\n## Residual risks\\n\\n- Whole-file SHA-256 detects corruption only after received bytes consume bandwidth and temporary disk.\\n- Persistent abandoned attempts need bounded quarantine retention.\\n- Worktree streaming decoder requires careful parser equivalence tests.\\n- Git subprocess compromise remains dangerous if verification runs with broker key access.\\n- Artifact-set digest definition needs explicit compatibility approval before persisted meaning changes.\\n- No implementation or runtime validation occurred because task was read-only.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/44151b43/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"worker-expert\",\n      \"task\": \"Read-only architecture diagnosis. Do not edit.\\nPhase 6 needs authenticated bounded desktop-to-broker ingestion for exactly committed.bundle, worktree.yra, and index-objects.pack, then broker journal verify/publish.\\nCurrent stdio relay is intentionally opaque and forwards one bounded signed broker frame to fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock. It must expose no caller-selected socket and should not buffer GiB artifacts. Broker journal signed request stores only artifact IDs, digests, lengths, object format, source digest, fingerprint, and artifact-set digest. WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore currently accepts three bytes objects.\\nRoot protocol stays prepare, launch, reclaim. Gates stay off. Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Current launcher prepare creates broker-writable staging and protected replica roots. Desktop connects to VM as yinshi-app over SSH.\\nDiagnose current code and propose the smallest secure upload protocol and ownership flow. Resolve who writes staging, how end-to-end Ed25519 authentication binds chunks or files, how bounds and backpressure work, how retries avoid overwrite, how broker maps artifact IDs to safe descriptor-opened files, and how verify/publish avoid whole-file memory where practical. Preserve relay contract unless a justified compatible extension exists.\\nState owners, transitions, failure outcomes, restart behavior, and exact module/API additions. Flag any blocker requiring privileged infrastructure approval.\",\n      \"routingContract\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"agent\": \"worker-expert\",\n        \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n        \"thinking\": \"xhigh\",\n        \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n      },\n      \"launchContractDigest\": \"e8f4f3a9b029b0bc25c1bdb6f28e2a381837ad4612c7085ae26fc7ba5feee2b2\",\n      \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n        \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n        \"runtime\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"configured\": [],\n        \"effective\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"omitted\": {\n          \"runtime\": 0,\n          \"configured\": 0,\n          \"effective\": 0\n        }\n      },\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"outputState\": \"present\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"input\": 159974,\n        \"output\": 17403,\n        \"cacheRead\": 135296,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n        \"cost\": 1.389608,\n        \"turns\": 6\n      },\n      \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\",\n      \"thinking\": \"xhigh\",\n      \"artifactPaths\": {\n        \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_input.md\",\n        \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_output.md\",\n        \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0.jsonl\",\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n        \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_meta.json\"\n      },\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n      \"turnBudget\": {\n        \"maxTurns\": 9,\n        \"graceTurns\": 2,\n        \"outcome\": \"within-budget\",\n        \"turnCount\": 6\n      },\n      \"toolBudget\": {\n        \"hard\": 48,\n        \"soft\": 32,\n        \"block\": [\n          \"read\",\n          \"grep\",\n          \"find\",\n          \"ls\"\n        ],\n        \"toolCount\": 38,\n        \"outcome\": \"soft-reached\",\n        \"softReachedAt\": 32\n      },\n      \"context\": \"fresh\",\n      \"progressSummary\": {\n        \"toolCount\": 38,\n        \"tokens\": 177377,\n        \"durationMs\": 560823\n      },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"fileMutation\": {\n          \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n          \"expected\": false,\n          \"attempted\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n      \"finalOutput\": \"## Causal diagnosis\\n\\nPhase 6 has a control plane, but no artifact data plane.\\n\\nCurrent signed broker request can authenticate artifact metadata. Current relay cannot carry artifact bytes safely. Current publication store only accepts in-memory bytes. Root prepare expects a different directory shape.\\n\\n### Findings\\n\\n1. **Blocker: replica lifecycle requests never reach replica journal**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24` supports only `executor.launch`.\\n   - `BrokerReplicaJournal` exists, but broker daemon does not dispatch `replica.lifecycle`.\\n   - Result: signed replica requests cannot begin ingestion, verification, or publication.\\n\\n2. **Blocker: current relay cannot carry artifacts**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py:27-29` fixes `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, which is correct.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18` caps requests at 65,536 bytes.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:_read_frame` reads one complete frame, requires EOF, and buffers frame bytes.\\n   - Artifacts allow up to 1 GiB per set. Sending them inside signed JSON is impossible and unsafe.\\n\\n3. **High: publication APIs cause whole-set memory amplification**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779` accepts three `bytes` objects.\\n   - `_PinnedRegular.content` retains complete file bytes.\\n   - `_read_descriptor` joins all chunks into one object.\\n   - `_recheck_pinned_regular` reads files again and compares full byte objects.\\n   - Bundle verification copies bytes into a temporary file.\\n   - Index-pack verification passes the entire pack through `stdin_bytes`.\\n   - A near-limit set can create several GiB of transient memory.\\n\\n4. **Blocker: published artifact layout is incompatible with root prepare**\\n   - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` publishes:\\n     - `artifact-set.json`\\n     - `committed.bundle`\\n     - `worktree.yra`\\n     - `index-objects.pack`\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199` requires exactly `repo` and `home`.\\n   - Pointing the publication store at `/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging` will always fail prepare.\\n\\n5. **High: artifact-set digest contracts need one shared definition**\\n   - Replica journal accepts caller-supplied `artifact_set_sha256`.\\n   - Publication store computes a domain digest from the complete declaration.\\n   - That declaration includes authority, limits, repository identity, workspace identity, and media metadata.\\n   - Journal payload tests do not establish that desktop can reproduce this exact declaration.\\n   - Broker must recompute one shared digest before accepting bytes. Silent reinterpretation would change persisted meaning.\\n\\n6. **Medium: current deadlines do not fit bounded GiB ingestion**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` uses a 120-second connection deadline.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` uses 125 seconds.\\n   - Slow but valid 1 GiB uploads can fail despite continuous progress.\\n\\n7. **High: SSH identity is not end-to-end artifact authentication**\\n   - Broker sees Unix peer UID `yinshi-app`, not original desktop SSH identity.\\n   - Existing Ed25519 request verification provides correct application-layer authentication.\\n   - Artifact bytes must be bound to that signed request through signed lengths and digests.\\n\\n## Smallest secure wire protocol\\n\\nKeep existing `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay` unchanged.\\n\\nAdd a second fixed executable:\\n\\n```text\\nyinshi-broker-artifact-upload\\n```\\n\\nIt accepts no arguments and connects only to:\\n\\n```text\\n/run/yinshi/broker.sock\\n```\\n\\nReuse existing broker socket. No caller-selected path or new Unix listener is needed.\\n\\n### Upload wire format\\n\\n```text\\nu32be signed_request_length\\nsigned replica.lifecycle request\\ncommitted.bundle bytes, exact signed length\\nworktree.yra bytes, exact signed length\\nindex-objects.pack bytes, exact signed length\\nEOF\\n```\\n\\nResponse remains existing format:\\n\\n```text\\nu32be signed_response_length\\nbroker-signed canonical JSON response\\n```\\n\\nNo artifact names, offsets, paths, or chunk headers cross the wire. Order is fixed by protocol.\\n\\n### Authentication\\n\\nDesktop signs metadata containing, for every fixed role:\\n\\n- Artifact ID\\n- SHA-256 digest\\n- Byte length\\n\\nSignature also binds:\\n\\n- Operation ID\\n- Broker incarnation\\n- Database incarnation\\n- Sequence\\n- Nonce\\n- Object format\\n- Source-state digest\\n- Reconciliation fingerprint\\n- Artifact-set digest\\n\\nBroker authenticates signed request before reading artifact data.\\n\\nChunks need no individual Ed25519 signatures. Chunk boundaries are transport details. Signed file length, fixed ordering, and signed SHA-256 bind every file byte and position.\\n\\nBroker publishes nothing until all three incremental hashes match. Modified, reordered, truncated, extended, or substituted bytes fail verification.\\n\\n## Bounds and backpressure\\n\\nUse 64 KiB transfer buffers at every hop.\\n\\nDesktop:\\n\\n1. Write bounded signed frame.\\n2. Stream each local file through SSH.\\n3. Respect writable-stream backpressure.\\n4. Close SSH stdin after third file.\\n\\nUpload relay:\\n\\n1. Buffer only four-byte prefix plus signed frame.\\n2. Forward frame immediately.\\n3. Copy remaining stdin in 64 KiB blocks.\\n4. Call socket drain after each block.\\n5. Enforce fixed global tail ceiling of 1 GiB.\\n6. Expose no CLI options.\\n\\nBroker:\\n\\n1. Validate signed declared lengths before reading data.\\n2. Enforce per-role server ceilings.\\n3. Enforce aggregate 1 GiB ceiling.\\n4. Read exactly each declared length.\\n5. Reject any trailing byte.\\n6. Incrementally hash while writing.\\n7. Apply idle deadlines, not one 120-second total deadline.\\n8. Limit concurrent uploads and reserve declared storage.\\n\\nSocket and SSH flow control then propagate disk pressure back to desktop. No layer queues an entire artifact.\\n\\n## Storage ownership and safe mapping\\n\\n### Durable artifact roots\\n\\nAdd broker-owned roots:\\n\\n```text\\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/incoming\\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/published\\n```\\n\\nBoth should be `0700`, owned by `yinshi-broker`.\\n\\nDesktop and `yinshi-app` never write these roots. Broker performs every artifact write.\\n\\nArtifact IDs must never become path components. Broker maps signed roles to fixed names:\\n\\n```text\\ncommitted_bundle -> committed.bundle\\nworktree         -> worktree.yra\\nindex_objects    -> index-objects.pack\\n```\\n\\nRequire all three artifact IDs to be distinct.\\n\\nOpen operation directories relative to pinned root descriptors. Open files with:\\n\\n```text\\nO_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK\\n```\\n\\nRequire:\\n\\n- Regular file\\n- Broker ownership\\n- Mode `0600`\\n- Link count one\\n- Exact signed length\\n- Matching named and opened inode\\n- Matching filesystem identity\\n\\nConsumers request a role. Store returns a pinned descriptor plus authenticated artifact ID. It never resolves `root / artifact_id`.\\n\\n## Ingestion and retry flow\\n\\n1. Broker authenticates request.\\n2. Broker validates strict replica payload and limits.\\n3. Journal records exact signed request.\\n4. Journal claims lifecycle authority.\\n5. Journal begins `ingest`.\\n6. Broker creates broker-generated pending directory with `O_EXCL` semantics.\\n7. Broker streams fixed files using exclusive creation.\\n8. Broker hashes and synchronizes each file.\\n9. Broker verifies directory and file identities.\\n10. Broker renames pending directory to `incoming/<operation_id>` with no replacement.\\n11. Broker synchronizes both parents.\\n12. Journal completes `ingest`.\\n\\nNever overwrite an existing file or directory.\\n\\nRetry rules:\\n\\n- Exact request plus exact completed incoming set: inspect and reuse.\\n- Exact request plus exact published set: return stored or reconstructed progress.\\n- Existing set with different identity or content: reject. Never replace it.\\n- Different signed frame using same operation ID: journal conflict.\\n- Partial live attempt with confirmed cleanup: retry starts a new exclusive attempt.\\n- Uncertain cleanup or rename: mark unresolved and retain state.\\n- Lost final response: exact request replay returns journaled signed response.\\n- Restart with only partial bytes: quarantine attempt and mark `transfer_unknown`.\\n- Restart with exact synchronized incoming files: resume deterministic verification.\\n- Retry after stale broker incarnation requires a new signed request and operation.\\n\\n## Verification and publication\\n\\n### Ingest verification\\n\\nIngest verifies only:\\n\\n- Signed lengths\\n- SHA-256 digests\\n- Fixed role ordering\\n- Safe file identity\\n\\nThen journal records `IngestReceipt`.\\n\\n### Semantic verification\\n\\nOpen pinned descriptors from `incoming`.\\n\\nAdd file-based verification:\\n\\n- Bundle verifier passes a stable read-only file descriptor path to Git.\\n- Index-pack verifier passes a stable read-only pack path to Git.\\n- Worktree decoder reads bounded sections from a descriptor.\\n- Hash checks use incremental `pread`.\\n- Identity and digest are rechecked after semantic verification.\\n\\nJournal then records `VerifyReceipt`.\\n\\n### Artifact publication\\n\\nAdd adoption support to `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\\n\\nIt should:\\n\\n1. Accept pinned incoming descriptors plus prior verification receipt.\\n2. Write bounded `artifact-set.json`.\\n3. Recheck all identities and hashes.\\n4. Rename `incoming/<operation_id>` to `published/<operation_id>` without replacement.\\n5. Synchronize source and destination parents.\\n6. Inspect final directory.\\n7. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\\n\\nKeep current bytes API as an explicit compatibility wrapper for existing tests. Production ingestion must use descriptor API.\\n\\nJournal records `PublishReceipt` only after durable final inspection.\\n\\n### Launcher staging\\n\\nPublished artifacts cannot be sent directly to root prepare.\\n\\nBroker-owned materializer must build:\\n\\n```text\\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/.<operation_id>.pending/\\n  repo/\\n  home/\\n```\\n\\nIt reconstructs repository and worktree from pinned published artifacts. It then synchronizes and renames pending directory to:\\n\\n```text\\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/<operation_id>\\n```\\n\\nRoot launcher then performs existing transitions:\\n\\n```text\\nprepare -> launch -> reclaim\\n```\\n\\nNo path enters root protocol. Only operation ID enters it.\\n\\n## State ownership\\n\\n| State | Owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Source snapshot and desktop private key | Desktop |\\n| SSH session authorization | SSH infrastructure |\\n| Signed logical request and replay identity | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Partial upload descriptors | Broker ingestion handler |\\n| Incoming immutable artifact set | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\\n| Semantic verification result | Broker journal |\\n| Published immutable artifacts | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\\n| Unprepared `repo/home` tree | Broker |\\n| Promotion and ownership transfer | Root launcher |\\n| Prepared operation directory | Root |\\n| Prepared `repo/home` | Allocated executor |\\n| Runtime listener and retained descriptor | Broker runtime |\\n| Reclaim quarantine and deletion | Root launcher |\\n\\n## Permitted transitions\\n\\n```text\\nabsent\\n  -> accepted\\n  -> claimed\\n  -> ingest_started\\n  -> ingested\\n  -> verify_started\\n  -> verified\\n  -> publish_started\\n  -> published\\n  -> admission\\n  -> drain\\n  -> export\\n  -> reclaim\\n```\\n\\nDisk transitions:\\n\\n```text\\nabsent\\n  -> private attempt\\n  -> synchronized incoming\\n  -> verified incoming\\n  -> published artifacts\\n  -> materialization pending\\n  -> launcher staging\\n  -> protected replica\\n  -> quarantine\\n  -> reclaimed\\n```\\n\\n## Invalid transitions\\n\\n- Reading artifact bytes before request authentication\\n- Unknown, missing, duplicated, or reordered roles\\n- Duplicate artifact IDs\\n- Declared limits above server ceilings\\n- Truncation or trailing data\\n- Artifact ID used as a path\\n- Replacing existing incoming, published, staging, or replica state\\n- Verification completion before ingest completion\\n- Publication completion before semantic verification\\n- Root prepare before exact `repo/home` staging exists\\n- Launch after unresolved synchronization\\n- Adopting orphan disk state without matching signed journal request\\n- Continuing when both incoming and published states exist\\n- Converting journal or filesystem uncertainty into success\\n\\n## Failure and cancellation outcomes\\n\\n- Authentication failure: close without signed success.\\n- Limit failure before upload: signed rejection when request authentication succeeded.\\n- Digest or length mismatch: `artifact_rejected`.\\n- Declared aggregate overflow: `limit_rejected`.\\n- Semantic failure: `verification_rejected`.\\n- Confirmed publication collision: `publication_rejected`.\\n- Rename or synchronization uncertainty: `publication_unknown` or `synchronization_unknown`.\\n- Cancellation during partial receive: clean only pinned owned attempt.\\n- Uncertain cleanup: `transfer_unknown`.\\n- Cancellation after durable ingest: shield verification and publication. Journal remains authoritative.\\n- SQLite failure before acceptance: do not read artifact bytes.\\n- SQLite commit uncertainty after bytes: retain synchronized files, return no success, and reconcile exact row plus exact files.\\n- Identity uncertainty: fail closed and retain state.\\n\\n## Restart behavior\\n\\nStartup reconciliation must use `BrokerReplicaJournal.incomplete_lifecycles()`.\\n\\nFor each stored signed request:\\n\\n- Reauthenticate stored frame.\\n- Reconstruct fixed manifest.\\n- Open only descriptor-relative fixed locations.\\n- Resume ingest completion when exact incoming files exist.\\n- Repeat semantic verification because it has no external irreversible effect.\\n- Inspect exact published state before completing publish.\\n- Quarantine partial or foreign state.\\n- Mark ambiguity unresolved.\\n- Never adopt an unjournaled operation.\\n- Never overwrite state to make recovery succeed.\\n\\nReceipts should be deterministic from request identity and verified state. This permits safe replay after commit-response loss.\\n\\n## Exact module and API additions\\n\\n### New modules\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\\n\\n```python\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass OpenedReplicaArtifacts:\\n    operation_id: str\\n    bundle: OpenedArtifact\\n    worktree: OpenedArtifact\\n    index_objects: OpenedArtifact\\n\\nclass BrokerArtifactStore:\\n    async def receive(\\n        self,\\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\\n\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def open_incoming(\\n        self,\\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\\n    ) -> Iterator[OpenedReplicaArtifacts]: ...\\n\\n    def inspect_incoming(\\n        self,\\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\\n\\n    def reconcile_attempts(\\n        self,\\n        journal_operations: frozenset[str],\\n    ) -> tuple[ReconciliationResult, ...]: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_service.py`\\n\\n```python\\nclass BrokerReplicaService:\\n    async def handle_upload(\\n        self,\\n        request: BrokerRequest,\\n        request_frame: bytes,\\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\\n    ) -> bytes: ...\\n\\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> None: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def relay_upload(\\n    *,\\n    broker_socket: Path = DEFAULT_BROKER_SOCKET,\\n) -> bytes: ...\\n```\\n\\nProduction entry point accepts no arguments.\\n\\n`desktop/src/brokerArtifactUpload.ts`\\n\\n```typescript\\nexport async function uploadReplicaArtifacts(\\n  request: SignedBrokerRequest,\\n  artifacts: ReplicaArtifactFiles,\\n): Promise<SignedBrokerResponse>;\\n```\\n\\nRemote command must be a fixed constant. API must not accept a socket path or arbitrary remote command.\\n\\n### Existing module changes\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py`\\n\\n- Add strict `ReplicaArtifactManifest`.\\n- Add `parse_replica_lifecycle_payload`.\\n- Add shared `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256`.\\n- Require distinct artifact IDs.\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\\n\\n- Split framed request reading from EOF enforcement.\\n- Authenticate initial frame before reading upload tail.\\n- Dispatch `executor.launch` to existing service.\\n- Dispatch `replica.lifecycle` to replica service.\\n- Preserve EOF requirement for ordinary broker relay.\\n- Replace total upload timeout with bounded idle deadlines.\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def verify_artifact_files(\\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\\n) -> ReplicaVerificationReceipt: ...\\n\\nasync def adopt_verified_artifact_set(\\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\\n    verification: ReplicaVerificationReceipt,\\n) -> ReplicaPublicationReceipt: ...\\n```\\n\\nKeep `publish_artifact_set(...bytes...)` only as compatibility wrapper.\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def verify_committed_bundle_file(\\n    descriptor: int,\\n    *,\\n    object_format: Literal[\\\"sha1\\\", \\\"sha256\\\"],\\n    limits: BundleLimits,\\n) -> VerifiedCommittedBundle: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\\n\\n```python\\nasync def verify_index_object_pack_file(\\n    descriptor: int,\\n    *,\\n    object_format: Literal[\\\"sha1\\\", \\\"sha256\\\"],\\n    expected_oids: Sequence[str],\\n    limits: IndexObjectPackLimits,\\n) -> VerifiedIndexObjectPack: ...\\n```\\n\\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`\\n\\n```python\\ndef inspect_worktree_artifact_file(\\n    descriptor: int,\\n    *,\\n    limits: ArtifactLimits,\\n) -> VerifiedWorktreeArtifactMetadata: ...\\n```\\n\\nMaterialization should use a streaming entry visitor rather than retaining every content payload.\\n\\n## Rejected alternatives\\n\\n- **Put artifacts in signed JSON:** rejected by 65,536-byte broker frame ceiling.\\n- **Use current relay for raw trailing bytes:** rejected because it requires one framed request and EOF.\\n- **Use SCP or SFTP into launcher staging:** rejected because `yinshi-app` does not own staging. It would also bypass journal admission.\\n- **Let desktop select a Unix socket:** rejected because it breaks fixed relay boundary.\\n- **Use artifact IDs as filenames:** rejected because IDs are caller-controlled identifiers.\\n- **Point publication store at launcher staging:** rejected by root launcher exact `repo/home` check.\\n- **Sign each 64 KiB chunk:** rejected as unnecessary. Signed whole-file length and digest already bind complete ordered content.\\n- **Rely on SSH authentication alone:** rejected because broker sees only local Unix UID.\\n\\n## Privileged infrastructure blockers\\n\\nProduction gates must remain off until these receive approval:\\n\\n1. Install and allowlist fixed SSH command `yinshi-broker-artifact-upload`.\\n2. Confirm `yinshi-app` cannot request arbitrary relay commands or socket paths.\\n3. Provision desktop Ed25519 public key into protected broker configuration.\\n4. Create broker-owned incoming and published roots through `tmpfiles.d`.\\n5. Define disk quota or reserved capacity for concurrent 1 GiB uploads.\\n6. Isolate untrusted Git verification from broker signing keys.\\n\\nLast item may require a dedicated verifier service account or systemd sandbox. Root launcher actions should not expand beyond prepare, launch, and reclaim.\\n\\n## Residual risks\\n\\n- Whole-file SHA-256 detects corruption only after received bytes consume bandwidth and temporary disk.\\n- Persistent abandoned attempts need bounded quarantine retention.\\n- Worktree streaming decoder requires careful parser equivalence tests.\\n- Git subprocess compromise remains dangerous if verification runs with broker key access.\\n- Artifact-set digest definition needs explicit compatibility approval before persisted meaning changes.\\n- No implementation or runtime validation occurred because task was read-only.\",\n      \"controlEvents\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"ts\": 1789249362674,\n          \"runId\": \"44151b43\",\n          \"agent\": \"worker-expert\",\n          \"index\": 0,\n          \"message\": \"worker-expert is still active but long-running\",\n          \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n          \"turns\": 5,\n          \"tokens\": 129833,\n          \"toolCount\": 38,\n          \"elapsedMs\": 240719\n        }\n      ],\n      \"attemptedModels\": [\n        \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAttempts\": [\n        {\n          \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\",\n          \"success\": true,\n          \"exitCode\": 0,\n          \"usage\": {\n            \"input\": 159974,\n            \"output\": 17403,\n            \"cacheRead\": 135296,\n            \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n            \"cost\": 1.389608,\n            \"turns\": 6\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/44151b43/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n      \"acceptance\": {\n        \"status\": \"attested\",\n        \"evidenceStatus\": \"attested\",\n        \"explicit\": false,\n        \"effectiveAcceptance\": {\n          \"level\": \"attested\",\n          \"explicit\": false,\n          \"inferredReason\": [\n            \"read-only task wording\"\n          ],\n          \"criteria\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": [\n                \"review-findings\",\n                \"residual-risks\"\n              ],\n              \"severity\": \"required\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"evidence\": [\n            \"review-findings\",\n            \"residual-risks\"\n          ],\n          \"verify\": [],\n          \"stopRules\": []\n        },\n        \"inferredReason\": [\n          \"read-only task wording\"\n        ],\n        \"criteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n            \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n            \"evidence\": [\n              \"review-findings\",\n              \"residual-risks\"\n            ],\n            \"severity\": \"required\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"runtimeChecks\": [],\n        \"verifyRuns\": [],\n        \"childReport\": {\n          \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n              \"evidence\": \"Concrete blocker, high, and medium findings identify execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, broker_stdio_relay.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, root_launcher.py, broker_protocol.py, and deployment ownership files. Review findings and residual risks are included.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"changedFiles\": [],\n          \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [],\n          \"commandsRun\": [\n            {\n              \"command\": \"git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline\",\n              \"result\": \"passed\",\n              \"summary\": \"Inspected repository state without editing.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"command\": \"pytest\",\n              \"result\": \"not-run\",\n              \"summary\": \"Read-only architecture diagnosis. No implementation required validation.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"validationOutput\": [\n            \"Confirmed broker accepts only executor.launch.\",\n            \"Confirmed current relay uses fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock and one bounded frame.\",\n            \"Confirmed publication store accepts three in-memory bytes objects.\",\n            \"Confirmed root prepare requires exactly repo and home.\",\n            \"Confirmed deployment assigns launcher staging ownership to yinshi-broker.\"\n          ],\n          \"residualRisks\": [\n            \"Artifact-set digest definition is not yet a shared desktop-broker contract.\",\n            \"Git verification can access broker credentials unless isolated.\",\n            \"Disk exhaustion needs quotas plus bounded quarantine retention.\",\n            \"Streaming worktree verification needs parser-equivalence and fault-injection tests.\"\n          ],\n          \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n          \"diffSummary\": \"No files changed. Read-only architecture review only.\",\n          \"reviewFindings\": [\n            \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24 - broker supports only executor.launch, so replica.lifecycle cannot reach replica journal.\",\n            \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18 - 65,536-byte request limit prevents artifact transfer inside signed broker frame.\",\n            \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779 - publication requires three complete bytes objects and amplifies memory use.\",\n            \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199 - root prepare requires repo and home, which conflicts with publication store artifact layout.\",\n            \"high: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py - 120-second whole-connection deadline is unsuitable for bounded GiB ingestion.\",\n            \"high: deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf - broker owns staging while SSH principal yinshi-app cannot write it, so broker must own ingestion and materialization.\"\n          ],\n          \"manualNotes\": \"Gates should remain disabled until SSH forced-command policy, key provisioning, storage quotas, and verifier isolation receive infrastructure approval.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"toolCalls\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"limit\\\":200}\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"limit\\\":200}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/AGENTS.md\\\",\\\"li...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/AGENTS.md\\\",\\\"limit\\\":50}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*\\\",\\\"limit\\\":100...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*\\\",\\\"limit\\\":1000}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"$ git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"$ git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read CLAUDE.md\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read CLAUDE.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read docs/broker-root-launcher.md\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read docs/broker-root-launcher.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/root_launche...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def prepare|def _prepare|staging|Prepare\\\",\\\"context\\\":3,\\\"limit\\\":100}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/services/bro...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def accept|def claim|def start|def record|def incomplete|ingest|VerifyReceipt|IngestR...\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-launcher.service\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-launcher.service\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read deploy/sysusers.d/yinshi.conf\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read deploy/sysusers.d/yinshi.conf\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"broker-stdio-rela...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"broker-stdio-relay|broker_stdio_relay|replica.lifecycle|WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore|complete_ingest|publish_artifact_set\\\",\\\"glob\\\":\\\"*....\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read desktop/src/localRuntime.ts\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read desktop/src/localRuntime.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read desktop/src/isolationProfile.ts\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read desktop/src/isolationProfile.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read deploy/orbstack/yinshi-runtime.profile.json\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read deploy/orbstack/yinshi-runtime.profile.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nCall trace:\n- run replica-ingestion-architecture: started\n- run replica-ingestion-architecture: completed (44151b43) in 560912ms\nMission: 26941e53-e8a4-440c-b48c-87e68c2ecd96 (completed)"}],"details":{"mode":"workflow","runId":"call_Zg8QUv7PKSZosIMupYPLOVFC|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c6583f3087d0a3fa8cbb9c11a4c4","results":[{"index":0,"agent":"worker-expert","task":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. Do not edit.\nPhase 6 needs authenticated bounded desktop-to-broker ingestion for exactly committed.bundle, worktree.yra, and index-objects.pack, then broker journal verify/publish.\nCurrent stdio relay is intentionally opaque and forwards one bounded signed broker frame to fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock. It must expose no caller-selected socket and should not buffer GiB artifacts. Broker journal signed request stores only artifact IDs, digests, lengths, object format, source digest, fingerprint, and artifact-set digest. WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore currently accepts three bytes objects.\nRoot protocol stays prepare, launch, reclaim. Gates stay off. Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Current launcher prepare creates broker-writable staging and protected replica roots. Desktop connects to VM as yinshi-app over SSH.\nDiagnose current code and propose the smallest secure upload protocol and ownership flow. Resolve who writes staging, how end-to-end Ed25519 authentication binds chunks or files, how bounds and backpressure work, how retries avoid overwrite, how broker maps artifact IDs to safe descriptor-opened files, and how verify/publish avoid whole-file memory where practical. Preserve relay contract unless a justified compatible extension exists.\nState owners, transitions, failure outcomes, restart behavior, and exact module/API additions. Flag any blocker requiring privileged infrastructure approval.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-expert","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"xhigh","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"e8f4f3a9b029b0bc25c1bdb6f28e2a381837ad4612c7085ae26fc7ba5feee2b2","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":159974,"output":17403,"cacheRead":135296,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.389608,"turns":6},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","thinking":"xhigh","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":9,"graceTurns":2,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":6},"toolBudget":{"hard":48,"soft":32,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":38,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":32},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":38,"tokens":177377,"durationMs":560823},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":false}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"## Causal diagnosis\n\nPhase 6 has a control plane, but no artifact data plane.\n\nCurrent signed broker request can authenticate artifact metadata. Current relay cannot carry artifact bytes safely. Current publication store only accepts in-memory bytes. Root prepare expects a different directory shape.\n\n### Findings\n\n1. **Blocker: replica lifecycle requests never reach replica journal**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24` supports only `executor.launch`.\n   - `BrokerReplicaJournal` exists, but broker daemon does not dispatch `replica.lifecycle`.\n   - Result: signed replica requests cannot begin ingestion, verification, or publication.\n\n2. **Blocker: current relay cannot carry artifacts**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py:27-29` fixes `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, which is correct.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18` caps requests at 65,536 bytes.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:_read_frame` reads one complete frame, requires EOF, and buffers frame bytes.\n   - Artifacts allow up to 1 GiB per set. Sending them inside signed JSON is impossible and unsafe.\n\n3. **High: publication APIs cause whole-set memory amplification**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779` accepts three `bytes` objects.\n   - `_PinnedRegular.content` retains complete file bytes.\n   - `_read_descriptor` joins all chunks into one object.\n   - `_recheck_pinned_regular` reads files again and compares full byte objects.\n   - Bundle verification copies bytes into a temporary file.\n   - Index-pack verification passes the entire pack through `stdin_bytes`.\n   - A near-limit set can create several GiB of transient memory.\n\n4. **Blocker: published artifact layout is incompatible with root prepare**\n   - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` publishes:\n     - `artifact-set.json`\n     - `committed.bundle`\n     - `worktree.yra`\n     - `index-objects.pack`\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199` requires exactly `repo` and `home`.\n   - Pointing the publication store at `/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging` will always fail prepare.\n\n5. **High: artifact-set digest contracts need one shared definition**\n   - Replica journal accepts caller-supplied `artifact_set_sha256`.\n   - Publication store computes a domain digest from the complete declaration.\n   - That declaration includes authority, limits, repository identity, workspace identity, and media metadata.\n   - Journal payload tests do not establish that desktop can reproduce this exact declaration.\n   - Broker must recompute one shared digest before accepting bytes. Silent reinterpretation would change persisted meaning.\n\n6. **Medium: current deadlines do not fit bounded GiB ingestion**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` uses a 120-second connection deadline.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` uses 125 seconds.\n   - Slow but valid 1 GiB uploads can fail despite continuous progress.\n\n7. **High: SSH identity is not end-to-end artifact authentication**\n   - Broker sees Unix peer UID `yinshi-app`, not original desktop SSH identity.\n   - Existing Ed25519 request verification provides correct application-layer authentication.\n   - Artifact bytes must be bound to that signed request through signed lengths and digests.\n\n## Smallest secure wire protocol\n\nKeep existing `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay` unchanged.\n\nAdd a second fixed executable:\n\n```text\nyinshi-broker-artifact-upload\n```\n\nIt accepts no arguments and connects only to:\n\n```text\n/run/yinshi/broker.sock\n```\n\nReuse existing broker socket. No caller-selected path or new Unix listener is needed.\n\n### Upload wire format\n\n```text\nu32be signed_request_length\nsigned replica.lifecycle request\ncommitted.bundle bytes, exact signed length\nworktree.yra bytes, exact signed length\nindex-objects.pack bytes, exact signed length\nEOF\n```\n\nResponse remains existing format:\n\n```text\nu32be signed_response_length\nbroker-signed canonical JSON response\n```\n\nNo artifact names, offsets, paths, or chunk headers cross the wire. Order is fixed by protocol.\n\n### Authentication\n\nDesktop signs metadata containing, for every fixed role:\n\n- Artifact ID\n- SHA-256 digest\n- Byte length\n\nSignature also binds:\n\n- Operation ID\n- Broker incarnation\n- Database incarnation\n- Sequence\n- Nonce\n- Object format\n- Source-state digest\n- Reconciliation fingerprint\n- Artifact-set digest\n\nBroker authenticates signed request before reading artifact data.\n\nChunks need no individual Ed25519 signatures. Chunk boundaries are transport details. Signed file length, fixed ordering, and signed SHA-256 bind every file byte and position.\n\nBroker publishes nothing until all three incremental hashes match. Modified, reordered, truncated, extended, or substituted bytes fail verification.\n\n## Bounds and backpressure\n\nUse 64 KiB transfer buffers at every hop.\n\nDesktop:\n\n1. Write bounded signed frame.\n2. Stream each local file through SSH.\n3. Respect writable-stream backpressure.\n4. Close SSH stdin after third file.\n\nUpload relay:\n\n1. Buffer only four-byte prefix plus signed frame.\n2. Forward frame immediately.\n3. Copy remaining stdin in 64 KiB blocks.\n4. Call socket drain after each block.\n5. Enforce fixed global tail ceiling of 1 GiB.\n6. Expose no CLI options.\n\nBroker:\n\n1. Validate signed declared lengths before reading data.\n2. Enforce per-role server ceilings.\n3. Enforce aggregate 1 GiB ceiling.\n4. Read exactly each declared length.\n5. Reject any trailing byte.\n6. Incrementally hash while writing.\n7. Apply idle deadlines, not one 120-second total deadline.\n8. Limit concurrent uploads and reserve declared storage.\n\nSocket and SSH flow control then propagate disk pressure back to desktop. No layer queues an entire artifact.\n\n## Storage ownership and safe mapping\n\n### Durable artifact roots\n\nAdd broker-owned roots:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/incoming\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/published\n```\n\nBoth should be `0700`, owned by `yinshi-broker`.\n\nDesktop and `yinshi-app` never write these roots. Broker performs every artifact write.\n\nArtifact IDs must never become path components. Broker maps signed roles to fixed names:\n\n```text\ncommitted_bundle -> committed.bundle\nworktree         -> worktree.yra\nindex_objects    -> index-objects.pack\n```\n\nRequire all three artifact IDs to be distinct.\n\nOpen operation directories relative to pinned root descriptors. Open files with:\n\n```text\nO_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK\n```\n\nRequire:\n\n- Regular file\n- Broker ownership\n- Mode `0600`\n- Link count one\n- Exact signed length\n- Matching named and opened inode\n- Matching filesystem identity\n\nConsumers request a role. Store returns a pinned descriptor plus authenticated artifact ID. It never resolves `root / artifact_id`.\n\n## Ingestion and retry flow\n\n1. Broker authenticates request.\n2. Broker validates strict replica payload and limits.\n3. Journal records exact signed request.\n4. Journal claims lifecycle authority.\n5. Journal begins `ingest`.\n6. Broker creates broker-generated pending directory with `O_EXCL` semantics.\n7. Broker streams fixed files using exclusive creation.\n8. Broker hashes and synchronizes each file.\n9. Broker verifies directory and file identities.\n10. Broker renames pending directory to `incoming/<operation_id>` with no replacement.\n11. Broker synchronizes both parents.\n12. Journal completes `ingest`.\n\nNever overwrite an existing file or directory.\n\nRetry rules:\n\n- Exact request plus exact completed incoming set: inspect and reuse.\n- Exact request plus exact published set: return stored or reconstructed progress.\n- Existing set with different identity or content: reject. Never replace it.\n- Different signed frame using same operation ID: journal conflict.\n- Partial live attempt with confirmed cleanup: retry starts a new exclusive attempt.\n- Uncertain cleanup or rename: mark unresolved and retain state.\n- Lost final response: exact request replay returns journaled signed response.\n- Restart with only partial bytes: quarantine attempt and mark `transfer_unknown`.\n- Restart with exact synchronized incoming files: resume deterministic verification.\n- Retry after stale broker incarnation requires a new signed request and operation.\n\n## Verification and publication\n\n### Ingest verification\n\nIngest verifies only:\n\n- Signed lengths\n- SHA-256 digests\n- Fixed role ordering\n- Safe file identity\n\nThen journal records `IngestReceipt`.\n\n### Semantic verification\n\nOpen pinned descriptors from `incoming`.\n\nAdd file-based verification:\n\n- Bundle verifier passes a stable read-only file descriptor path to Git.\n- Index-pack verifier passes a stable read-only pack path to Git.\n- Worktree decoder reads bounded sections from a descriptor.\n- Hash checks use incremental `pread`.\n- Identity and digest are rechecked after semantic verification.\n\nJournal then records `VerifyReceipt`.\n\n### Artifact publication\n\nAdd adoption support to `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\n\nIt should:\n\n1. Accept pinned incoming descriptors plus prior verification receipt.\n2. Write bounded `artifact-set.json`.\n3. Recheck all identities and hashes.\n4. Rename `incoming/<operation_id>` to `published/<operation_id>` without replacement.\n5. Synchronize source and destination parents.\n6. Inspect final directory.\n7. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\n\nKeep current bytes API as an explicit compatibility wrapper for existing tests. Production ingestion must use descriptor API.\n\nJournal records `PublishReceipt` only after durable final inspection.\n\n### Launcher staging\n\nPublished artifacts cannot be sent directly to root prepare.\n\nBroker-owned materializer must build:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/.<operation_id>.pending/\n  repo/\n  home/\n```\n\nIt reconstructs repository and worktree from pinned published artifacts. It then synchronizes and renames pending directory to:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/<operation_id>\n```\n\nRoot launcher then performs existing transitions:\n\n```text\nprepare -> launch -> reclaim\n```\n\nNo path enters root protocol. Only operation ID enters it.\n\n## State ownership\n\n| State | Owner |\n|---|---|\n| Source snapshot and desktop private key | Desktop |\n| SSH session authorization | SSH infrastructure |\n| Signed logical request and replay identity | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Partial upload descriptors | Broker ingestion handler |\n| Incoming immutable artifact set | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Semantic verification result | Broker journal |\n| Published immutable artifacts | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Unprepared `repo/home` tree | Broker |\n| Promotion and ownership transfer | Root launcher |\n| Prepared operation directory | Root |\n| Prepared `repo/home` | Allocated executor |\n| Runtime listener and retained descriptor | Broker runtime |\n| Reclaim quarantine and deletion | Root launcher |\n\n## Permitted transitions\n\n```text\nabsent\n  -> accepted\n  -> claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingested\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verified\n  -> publish_started\n  -> published\n  -> admission\n  -> drain\n  -> export\n  -> reclaim\n```\n\nDisk transitions:\n\n```text\nabsent\n  -> private attempt\n  -> synchronized incoming\n  -> verified incoming\n  -> published artifacts\n  -> materialization pending\n  -> launcher staging\n  -> protected replica\n  -> quarantine\n  -> reclaimed\n```\n\n## Invalid transitions\n\n- Reading artifact bytes before request authentication\n- Unknown, missing, duplicated, or reordered roles\n- Duplicate artifact IDs\n- Declared limits above server ceilings\n- Truncation or trailing data\n- Artifact ID used as a path\n- Replacing existing incoming, published, staging, or replica state\n- Verification completion before ingest completion\n- Publication completion before semantic verification\n- Root prepare before exact `repo/home` staging exists\n- Launch after unresolved synchronization\n- Adopting orphan disk state without matching signed journal request\n- Continuing when both incoming and published states exist\n- Converting journal or filesystem uncertainty into success\n\n## Failure and cancellation outcomes\n\n- Authentication failure: close without signed success.\n- Limit failure before upload: signed rejection when request authentication succeeded.\n- Digest or length mismatch: `artifact_rejected`.\n- Declared aggregate overflow: `limit_rejected`.\n- Semantic failure: `verification_rejected`.\n- Confirmed publication collision: `publication_rejected`.\n- Rename or synchronization uncertainty: `publication_unknown` or `synchronization_unknown`.\n- Cancellation during partial receive: clean only pinned owned attempt.\n- Uncertain cleanup: `transfer_unknown`.\n- Cancellation after durable ingest: shield verification and publication. Journal remains authoritative.\n- SQLite failure before acceptance: do not read artifact bytes.\n- SQLite commit uncertainty after bytes: retain synchronized files, return no success, and reconcile exact row plus exact files.\n- Identity uncertainty: fail closed and retain state.\n\n## Restart behavior\n\nStartup reconciliation must use `BrokerReplicaJournal.incomplete_lifecycles()`.\n\nFor each stored signed request:\n\n- Reauthenticate stored frame.\n- Reconstruct fixed manifest.\n- Open only descriptor-relative fixed locations.\n- Resume ingest completion when exact incoming files exist.\n- Repeat semantic verification because it has no external irreversible effect.\n- Inspect exact published state before completing publish.\n- Quarantine partial or foreign state.\n- Mark ambiguity unresolved.\n- Never adopt an unjournaled operation.\n- Never overwrite state to make recovery succeed.\n\nReceipts should be deterministic from request identity and verified state. This permits safe replay after commit-response loss.\n\n## Exact module and API additions\n\n### New modules\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass OpenedReplicaArtifacts:\n    operation_id: str\n    bundle: OpenedArtifact\n    worktree: OpenedArtifact\n    index_objects: OpenedArtifact\n\nclass BrokerArtifactStore:\n    async def receive(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\n\n    @contextmanager\n    def open_incoming(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n    ) -> Iterator[OpenedReplicaArtifacts]: ...\n\n    def inspect_incoming(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\n\n    def reconcile_attempts(\n        self,\n        journal_operations: frozenset[str],\n    ) -> tuple[ReconciliationResult, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_service.py`\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaService:\n    async def handle_upload(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\n    ) -> bytes: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> None: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\n\n```python\nasync def relay_upload(\n    *,\n    broker_socket: Path = DEFAULT_BROKER_SOCKET,\n) -> bytes: ...\n```\n\nProduction entry point accepts no arguments.\n\n`desktop/src/brokerArtifactUpload.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport async function uploadReplicaArtifacts(\n  request: SignedBrokerRequest,\n  artifacts: ReplicaArtifactFiles,\n): Promise<SignedBrokerResponse>;\n```\n\nRemote command must be a fixed constant. API must not accept a socket path or arbitrary remote command.\n\n### Existing module changes\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py`\n\n- Add strict `ReplicaArtifactManifest`.\n- Add `parse_replica_lifecycle_payload`.\n- Add shared `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256`.\n- Require distinct artifact IDs.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\n\n- Split framed request reading from EOF enforcement.\n- Authenticate initial frame before reading upload tail.\n- Dispatch `executor.launch` to existing service.\n- Dispatch `replica.lifecycle` to replica service.\n- Preserve EOF requirement for ordinary broker relay.\n- Replace total upload timeout with bounded idle deadlines.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_artifact_files(\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\n) -> ReplicaVerificationReceipt: ...\n\nasync def adopt_verified_artifact_set(\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\n    verification: ReplicaVerificationReceipt,\n) -> ReplicaPublicationReceipt: ...\n```\n\nKeep `publish_artifact_set(...bytes...)` only as compatibility wrapper.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_committed_bundle_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    object_format: Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"],\n    limits: BundleLimits,\n) -> VerifiedCommittedBundle: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_index_object_pack_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    object_format: Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"],\n    expected_oids: Sequence[str],\n    limits: IndexObjectPackLimits,\n) -> VerifiedIndexObjectPack: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`\n\n```python\ndef inspect_worktree_artifact_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    limits: ArtifactLimits,\n) -> VerifiedWorktreeArtifactMetadata: ...\n```\n\nMaterialization should use a streaming entry visitor rather than retaining every content payload.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Put artifacts in signed JSON:** rejected by 65,536-byte broker frame ceiling.\n- **Use current relay for raw trailing bytes:** rejected because it requires one framed request and EOF.\n- **Use SCP or SFTP into launcher staging:** rejected because `yinshi-app` does not own staging. It would also bypass journal admission.\n- **Let desktop select a Unix socket:** rejected because it breaks fixed relay boundary.\n- **Use artifact IDs as filenames:** rejected because IDs are caller-controlled identifiers.\n- **Point publication store at launcher staging:** rejected by root launcher exact `repo/home` check.\n- **Sign each 64 KiB chunk:** rejected as unnecessary. Signed whole-file length and digest already bind complete ordered content.\n- **Rely on SSH authentication alone:** rejected because broker sees only local Unix UID.\n\n## Privileged infrastructure blockers\n\nProduction gates must remain off until these receive approval:\n\n1. Install and allowlist fixed SSH command `yinshi-broker-artifact-upload`.\n2. Confirm `yinshi-app` cannot request arbitrary relay commands or socket paths.\n3. Provision desktop Ed25519 public key into protected broker configuration.\n4. Create broker-owned incoming and published roots through `tmpfiles.d`.\n5. Define disk quota or reserved capacity for concurrent 1 GiB uploads.\n6. Isolate untrusted Git verification from broker signing keys.\n\nLast item may require a dedicated verifier service account or systemd sandbox. Root launcher actions should not expand beyond prepare, launch, and reclaim.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Whole-file SHA-256 detects corruption only after received bytes consume bandwidth and temporary disk.\n- Persistent abandoned attempts need bounded quarantine retention.\n- Worktree streaming decoder requires careful parser equivalence tests.\n- Git subprocess compromise remains dangerous if verification runs with broker key access.\n- Artifact-set digest definition needs explicit compatibility approval before persisted meaning changes.\n- No implementation or runtime validation occurred because task was read-only.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789249362674,"runId":"44151b43","agent":"worker-expert","index":0,"message":"worker-expert is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":5,"tokens":129833,"toolCount":38,"elapsedMs":240719}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":159974,"output":17403,"cacheRead":135296,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.389608,"turns":6}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/44151b43/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Concrete blocker, high, and medium findings identify execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, broker_stdio_relay.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, root_launcher.py, broker_protocol.py, and deployment ownership files. Review findings and residual risks are included."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected repository state without editing."},{"command":"pytest","result":"not-run","summary":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. No implementation required validation."}],"validationOutput":["Confirmed broker accepts only executor.launch.","Confirmed current relay uses fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock and one bounded frame.","Confirmed publication store accepts three in-memory bytes objects.","Confirmed root prepare requires exactly repo and home.","Confirmed deployment assigns launcher staging ownership to yinshi-broker."],"residualRisks":["Artifact-set digest definition is not yet a shared desktop-broker contract.","Git verification can access broker credentials unless isolated.","Disk exhaustion needs quotas plus bounded quarantine retention.","Streaming worktree verification needs parser-equivalence and fault-injection tests."],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No files changed. Read-only architecture review only.","reviewFindings":["blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24 - broker supports only executor.launch, so replica.lifecycle cannot reach replica journal.","blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18 - 65,536-byte request limit prevents artifact transfer inside signed broker frame.","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779 - publication requires three complete bytes objects and amplifies memory use.","blocker: backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199 - root prepare requires repo and home, which conflicts with publication store artifact layout.","high: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py - 120-second whole-connection deadline is unsuitable for bounded GiB ingestion.","high: deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf - broker owns staging while SSH principal yinshi-app cannot write it, so broker must own ingestion and materialization."],"manualNotes":"Gates should remain disabled until SSH forced-command policy, key provisioning, storage quotas, and verifier isolation receive infrastructure approval."}},"toolCalls":[{"text":"ls {\"path\":\".\",\"limit\":200}","expandedText":"ls {\"path\":\".\",\"limit\":200}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/AGENTS.md\",\"li...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/AGENTS.md\",\"limit\":50}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/*\",\"limit\":100...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/*\",\"limit\":1000}"},{"text":"$ git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -...","expandedText":"$ git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline"},{"text":"read CLAUDE.md","expandedText":"read CLAUDE.md"},{"text":"read docs/broker-root-launcher.md","expandedText":"read docs/broker-root-launcher.md"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/root_launche...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\"pattern\":\"def prepare|def _prepare|staging|Prepare\",\"context\":3,\"limit\":100}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/services/bro...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\"pattern\":\"def accept|def claim|def start|def record|def incomplete|ingest|VerifyReceipt|IngestR..."},{"text":"read deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf","expandedText":"read deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf"},{"text":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service","expandedText":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service"},{"text":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-launcher.service","expandedText":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-launcher.service"},{"text":"read deploy/sysusers.d/yinshi.conf","expandedText":"read deploy/sysusers.d/yinshi.conf"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"broker-stdio-rela...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"broker-stdio-relay|broker_stdio_relay|replica.lifecycle|WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore|complete_ingest|publish_artifact_set\",\"glob\":\"*...."},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py"},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py"},{"text":"read desktop/src/localRuntime.ts","expandedText":"read desktop/src/localRuntime.ts"},{"text":"read desktop/src/isolationProfile.ts","expandedText":"read desktop/src/isolationProfile.ts"},{"text":"read deploy/orbstack/yinshi-runtime.profile.json","expandedText":"read deploy/orbstack/yinshi-runtime.profile.json"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py"}]}],"totalChildUsage":{"input":159974,"output":17403,"cacheRead":135296,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.389608,"turns":6},"totalCost":{"inputTokens":159974,"outputTokens":17403,"costUsd":1.389608},"workflow":{"value":{"key":"replica-ingestion-architecture","ok":true,"runId":"44151b43","output":"## Causal diagnosis\n\nPhase 6 has a control plane, but no artifact data plane.\n\nCurrent signed broker request can authenticate artifact metadata. Current relay cannot carry artifact bytes safely. Current publication store only accepts in-memory bytes. Root prepare expects a different directory shape.\n\n### Findings\n\n1. **Blocker: replica lifecycle requests never reach replica journal**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24` supports only `executor.launch`.\n   - `BrokerReplicaJournal` exists, but broker daemon does not dispatch `replica.lifecycle`.\n   - Result: signed replica requests cannot begin ingestion, verification, or publication.\n\n2. **Blocker: current relay cannot carry artifacts**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py:27-29` fixes `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, which is correct.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18` caps requests at 65,536 bytes.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:_read_frame` reads one complete frame, requires EOF, and buffers frame bytes.\n   - Artifacts allow up to 1 GiB per set. Sending them inside signed JSON is impossible and unsafe.\n\n3. **High: publication APIs cause whole-set memory amplification**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779` accepts three `bytes` objects.\n   - `_PinnedRegular.content` retains complete file bytes.\n   - `_read_descriptor` joins all chunks into one object.\n   - `_recheck_pinned_regular` reads files again and compares full byte objects.\n   - Bundle verification copies bytes into a temporary file.\n   - Index-pack verification passes the entire pack through `stdin_bytes`.\n   - A near-limit set can create several GiB of transient memory.\n\n4. **Blocker: published artifact layout is incompatible with root prepare**\n   - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` publishes:\n     - `artifact-set.json`\n     - `committed.bundle`\n     - `worktree.yra`\n     - `index-objects.pack`\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199` requires exactly `repo` and `home`.\n   - Pointing the publication store at `/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging` will always fail prepare.\n\n5. **High: artifact-set digest contracts need one shared definition**\n   - Replica journal accepts caller-supplied `artifact_set_sha256`.\n   - Publication store computes a domain digest from the complete declaration.\n   - That declaration includes authority, limits, repository identity, workspace identity, and media metadata.\n   - Journal payload tests do not establish that desktop can reproduce this exact declaration.\n   - Broker must recompute one shared digest before accepting bytes. Silent reinterpretation would change persisted meaning.\n\n6. **Medium: current deadlines do not fit bounded GiB ingestion**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` uses a 120-second connection deadline.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` uses 125 seconds.\n   - Slow but valid 1 GiB uploads can fail despite continuous progress.\n\n7. **High: SSH identity is not end-to-end artifact authentication**\n   - Broker sees Unix peer UID `yinshi-app`, not original desktop SSH identity.\n   - Existing Ed25519 request verification provides correct application-layer authentication.\n   - Artifact bytes must be bound to that signed request through signed lengths and digests.\n\n## Smallest secure wire protocol\n\nKeep existing `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay` unchanged.\n\nAdd a second fixed executable:\n\n```text\nyinshi-broker-artifact-upload\n```\n\nIt accepts no arguments and connects only to:\n\n```text\n/run/yinshi/broker.sock\n```\n\nReuse existing broker socket. No caller-selected path or new Unix listener is needed.\n\n### Upload wire format\n\n```text\nu32be signed_request_length\nsigned replica.lifecycle request\ncommitted.bundle bytes, exact signed length\nworktree.yra bytes, exact signed length\nindex-objects.pack bytes, exact signed length\nEOF\n```\n\nResponse remains existing format:\n\n```text\nu32be signed_response_length\nbroker-signed canonical JSON response\n```\n\nNo artifact names, offsets, paths, or chunk headers cross the wire. Order is fixed by protocol.\n\n### Authentication\n\nDesktop signs metadata containing, for every fixed role:\n\n- Artifact ID\n- SHA-256 digest\n- Byte length\n\nSignature also binds:\n\n- Operation ID\n- Broker incarnation\n- Database incarnation\n- Sequence\n- Nonce\n- Object format\n- Source-state digest\n- Reconciliation fingerprint\n- Artifact-set digest\n\nBroker authenticates signed request before reading artifact data.\n\nChunks need no individual Ed25519 signatures. Chunk boundaries are transport details. Signed file length, fixed ordering, and signed SHA-256 bind every file byte and position.\n\nBroker publishes nothing until all three incremental hashes match. Modified, reordered, truncated, extended, or substituted bytes fail verification.\n\n## Bounds and backpressure\n\nUse 64 KiB transfer buffers at every hop.\n\nDesktop:\n\n1. Write bounded signed frame.\n2. Stream each local file through SSH.\n3. Respect writable-stream backpressure.\n4. Close SSH stdin after third file.\n\nUpload relay:\n\n1. Buffer only four-byte prefix plus signed frame.\n2. Forward frame immediately.\n3. Copy remaining stdin in 64 KiB blocks.\n4. Call socket drain after each block.\n5. Enforce fixed global tail ceiling of 1 GiB.\n6. Expose no CLI options.\n\nBroker:\n\n1. Validate signed declared lengths before reading data.\n2. Enforce per-role server ceilings.\n3. Enforce aggregate 1 GiB ceiling.\n4. Read exactly each declared length.\n5. Reject any trailing byte.\n6. Incrementally hash while writing.\n7. Apply idle deadlines, not one 120-second total deadline.\n8. Limit concurrent uploads and reserve declared storage.\n\nSocket and SSH flow control then propagate disk pressure back to desktop. No layer queues an entire artifact.\n\n## Storage ownership and safe mapping\n\n### Durable artifact roots\n\nAdd broker-owned roots:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/incoming\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/published\n```\n\nBoth should be `0700`, owned by `yinshi-broker`.\n\nDesktop and `yinshi-app` never write these roots. Broker performs every artifact write.\n\nArtifact IDs must never become path components. Broker maps signed roles to fixed names:\n\n```text\ncommitted_bundle -> committed.bundle\nworktree         -> worktree.yra\nindex_objects    -> index-objects.pack\n```\n\nRequire all three artifact IDs to be distinct.\n\nOpen operation directories relative to pinned root descriptors. Open files with:\n\n```text\nO_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK\n```\n\nRequire:\n\n- Regular file\n- Broker ownership\n- Mode `0600`\n- Link count one\n- Exact signed length\n- Matching named and opened inode\n- Matching filesystem identity\n\nConsumers request a role. Store returns a pinned descriptor plus authenticated artifact ID. It never resolves `root / artifact_id`.\n\n## Ingestion and retry flow\n\n1. Broker authenticates request.\n2. Broker validates strict replica payload and limits.\n3. Journal records exact signed request.\n4. Journal claims lifecycle authority.\n5. Journal begins `ingest`.\n6. Broker creates broker-generated pending directory with `O_EXCL` semantics.\n7. Broker streams fixed files using exclusive creation.\n8. Broker hashes and synchronizes each file.\n9. Broker verifies directory and file identities.\n10. Broker renames pending directory to `incoming/<operation_id>` with no replacement.\n11. Broker synchronizes both parents.\n12. Journal completes `ingest`.\n\nNever overwrite an existing file or directory.\n\nRetry rules:\n\n- Exact request plus exact completed incoming set: inspect and reuse.\n- Exact request plus exact published set: return stored or reconstructed progress.\n- Existing set with different identity or content: reject. Never replace it.\n- Different signed frame using same operation ID: journal conflict.\n- Partial live attempt with confirmed cleanup: retry starts a new exclusive attempt.\n- Uncertain cleanup or rename: mark unresolved and retain state.\n- Lost final response: exact request replay returns journaled signed response.\n- Restart with only partial bytes: quarantine attempt and mark `transfer_unknown`.\n- Restart with exact synchronized incoming files: resume deterministic verification.\n- Retry after stale broker incarnation requires a new signed request and operation.\n\n## Verification and publication\n\n### Ingest verification\n\nIngest verifies only:\n\n- Signed lengths\n- SHA-256 digests\n- Fixed role ordering\n- Safe file identity\n\nThen journal records `IngestReceipt`.\n\n### Semantic verification\n\nOpen pinned descriptors from `incoming`.\n\nAdd file-based verification:\n\n- Bundle verifier passes a stable read-only file descriptor path to Git.\n- Index-pack verifier passes a stable read-only pack path to Git.\n- Worktree decoder reads bounded sections from a descriptor.\n- Hash checks use incremental `pread`.\n- Identity and digest are rechecked after semantic verification.\n\nJournal then records `VerifyReceipt`.\n\n### Artifact publication\n\nAdd adoption support to `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\n\nIt should:\n\n1. Accept pinned incoming descriptors plus prior verification receipt.\n2. Write bounded `artifact-set.json`.\n3. Recheck all identities and hashes.\n4. Rename `incoming/<operation_id>` to `published/<operation_id>` without replacement.\n5. Synchronize source and destination parents.\n6. Inspect final directory.\n7. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\n\nKeep current bytes API as an explicit compatibility wrapper for existing tests. Production ingestion must use descriptor API.\n\nJournal records `PublishReceipt` only after durable final inspection.\n\n### Launcher staging\n\nPublished artifacts cannot be sent directly to root prepare.\n\nBroker-owned materializer must build:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/.<operation_id>.pending/\n  repo/\n  home/\n```\n\nIt reconstructs repository and worktree from pinned published artifacts. It then synchronizes and renames pending directory to:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/<operation_id>\n```\n\nRoot launcher then performs existing transitions:\n\n```text\nprepare -> launch -> reclaim\n```\n\nNo path enters root protocol. Only operation ID enters it.\n\n## State ownership\n\n| State | Owner |\n|---|---|\n| Source snapshot and desktop private key | Desktop |\n| SSH session authorization | SSH infrastructure |\n| Signed logical request and replay identity | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Partial upload descriptors | Broker ingestion handler |\n| Incoming immutable artifact set | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Semantic verification result | Broker journal |\n| Published immutable artifacts | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Unprepared `repo/home` tree | Broker |\n| Promotion and ownership transfer | Root launcher |\n| Prepared operation directory | Root |\n| Prepared `repo/home` | Allocated executor |\n| Runtime listener and retained descriptor | Broker runtime |\n| Reclaim quarantine and deletion | Root launcher |\n\n## Permitted transitions\n\n```text\nabsent\n  -> accepted\n  -> claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingested\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verified\n  -> publish_started\n  -> published\n  -> admission\n  -> drain\n  -> export\n  -> reclaim\n```\n\nDisk transitions:\n\n```text\nabsent\n  -> private attempt\n  -> synchronized incoming\n  -> verified incoming\n  -> published artifacts\n  -> materialization pending\n  -> launcher staging\n  -> protected replica\n  -> quarantine\n  -> reclaimed\n```\n\n## Invalid transitions\n\n- Reading artifact bytes before request authentication\n- Unknown, missing, duplicated, or reordered roles\n- Duplicate artifact IDs\n- Declared limits above server ceilings\n- Truncation or trailing data\n- Artifact ID used as a path\n- Replacing existing incoming, published, staging, or replica state\n- Verification completion before ingest completion\n- Publication completion before semantic verification\n- Root prepare before exact `repo/home` staging exists\n- Launch after unresolved synchronization\n- Adopting orphan disk state without matching signed journal request\n- Continuing when both incoming and published states exist\n- Converting journal or filesystem uncertainty into success\n\n## Failure and cancellation outcomes\n\n- Authentication failure: close without signed success.\n- Limit failure before upload: signed rejection when request authentication succeeded.\n- Digest or length mismatch: `artifact_rejected`.\n- Declared aggregate overflow: `limit_rejected`.\n- Semantic failure: `verification_rejected`.\n- Confirmed publication collision: `publication_rejected`.\n- Rename or synchronization uncertainty: `publication_unknown` or `synchronization_unknown`.\n- Cancellation during partial receive: clean only pinned owned attempt.\n- Uncertain cleanup: `transfer_unknown`.\n- Cancellation after durable ingest: shield verification and publication. Journal remains authoritative.\n- SQLite failure before acceptance: do not read artifact bytes.\n- SQLite commit uncertainty after bytes: retain synchronized files, return no success, and reconcile exact row plus exact files.\n- Identity uncertainty: fail closed and retain state.\n\n## Restart behavior\n\nStartup reconciliation must use `BrokerReplicaJournal.incomplete_lifecycles()`.\n\nFor each stored signed request:\n\n- Reauthenticate stored frame.\n- Reconstruct fixed manifest.\n- Open only descriptor-relative fixed locations.\n- Resume ingest completion when exact incoming files exist.\n- Repeat semantic verification because it has no external irreversible effect.\n- Inspect exact published state before completing publish.\n- Quarantine partial or foreign state.\n- Mark ambiguity unresolved.\n- Never adopt an unjournaled operation.\n- Never overwrite state to make recovery succeed.\n\nReceipts should be deterministic from request identity and verified state. This permits safe replay after commit-response loss.\n\n## Exact module and API additions\n\n### New modules\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass OpenedReplicaArtifacts:\n    operation_id: str\n    bundle: OpenedArtifact\n    worktree: OpenedArtifact\n    index_objects: OpenedArtifact\n\nclass BrokerArtifactStore:\n    async def receive(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\n\n    @contextmanager\n    def open_incoming(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n    ) -> Iterator[OpenedReplicaArtifacts]: ...\n\n    def inspect_incoming(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\n\n    def reconcile_attempts(\n        self,\n        journal_operations: frozenset[str],\n    ) -> tuple[ReconciliationResult, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_service.py`\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaService:\n    async def handle_upload(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\n    ) -> bytes: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> None: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\n\n```python\nasync def relay_upload(\n    *,\n    broker_socket: Path = DEFAULT_BROKER_SOCKET,\n) -> bytes: ...\n```\n\nProduction entry point accepts no arguments.\n\n`desktop/src/brokerArtifactUpload.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport async function uploadReplicaArtifacts(\n  request: SignedBrokerRequest,\n  artifacts: ReplicaArtifactFiles,\n): Promise<SignedBrokerResponse>;\n```\n\nRemote command must be a fixed constant. API must not accept a socket path or arbitrary remote command.\n\n### Existing module changes\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py`\n\n- Add strict `ReplicaArtifactManifest`.\n- Add `parse_replica_lifecycle_payload`.\n- Add shared `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256`.\n- Require distinct artifact IDs.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\n\n- Split framed request reading from EOF enforcement.\n- Authenticate initial frame before reading upload tail.\n- Dispatch `executor.launch` to existing service.\n- Dispatch `replica.lifecycle` to replica service.\n- Preserve EOF requirement for ordinary broker relay.\n- Replace total upload timeout with bounded idle deadlines.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_artifact_files(\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\n) -> ReplicaVerificationReceipt: ...\n\nasync def adopt_verified_artifact_set(\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\n    verification: ReplicaVerificationReceipt,\n) -> ReplicaPublicationReceipt: ...\n```\n\nKeep `publish_artifact_set(...bytes...)` only as compatibility wrapper.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_committed_bundle_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    object_format: Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"],\n    limits: BundleLimits,\n) -> VerifiedCommittedBundle: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_index_object_pack_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    object_format: Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"],\n    expected_oids: Sequence[str],\n    limits: IndexObjectPackLimits,\n) -> VerifiedIndexObjectPack: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`\n\n```python\ndef inspect_worktree_artifact_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    limits: ArtifactLimits,\n) -> VerifiedWorktreeArtifactMetadata: ...\n```\n\nMaterialization should use a streaming entry visitor rather than retaining every content payload.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Put artifacts in signed JSON:** rejected by 65,536-byte broker frame ceiling.\n- **Use current relay for raw trailing bytes:** rejected because it requires one framed request and EOF.\n- **Use SCP or SFTP into launcher staging:** rejected because `yinshi-app` does not own staging. It would also bypass journal admission.\n- **Let desktop select a Unix socket:** rejected because it breaks fixed relay boundary.\n- **Use artifact IDs as filenames:** rejected because IDs are caller-controlled identifiers.\n- **Point publication store at launcher staging:** rejected by root launcher exact `repo/home` check.\n- **Sign each 64 KiB chunk:** rejected as unnecessary. Signed whole-file length and digest already bind complete ordered content.\n- **Rely on SSH authentication alone:** rejected because broker sees only local Unix UID.\n\n## Privileged infrastructure blockers\n\nProduction gates must remain off until these receive approval:\n\n1. Install and allowlist fixed SSH command `yinshi-broker-artifact-upload`.\n2. Confirm `yinshi-app` cannot request arbitrary relay commands or socket paths.\n3. Provision desktop Ed25519 public key into protected broker configuration.\n4. Create broker-owned incoming and published roots through `tmpfiles.d`.\n5. Define disk quota or reserved capacity for concurrent 1 GiB uploads.\n6. Isolate untrusted Git verification from broker signing keys.\n\nLast item may require a dedicated verifier service account or systemd sandbox. Root launcher actions should not expand beyond prepare, launch, and reclaim.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Whole-file SHA-256 detects corruption only after received bytes consume bandwidth and temporary disk.\n- Persistent abandoned attempts need bounded quarantine retention.\n- Worktree streaming decoder requires careful parser equivalence tests.\n- Git subprocess compromise remains dangerous if verification runs with broker key access.\n- Artifact-set digest definition needs explicit compatibility approval before persisted meaning changes.\n- No implementation or runtime validation occurred because task was read-only.","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/44151b43/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"worker-expert","task":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. Do not edit.\nPhase 6 needs authenticated bounded desktop-to-broker ingestion for exactly committed.bundle, worktree.yra, and index-objects.pack, then broker journal verify/publish.\nCurrent stdio relay is intentionally opaque and forwards one bounded signed broker frame to fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock. It must expose no caller-selected socket and should not buffer GiB artifacts. Broker journal signed request stores only artifact IDs, digests, lengths, object format, source digest, fingerprint, and artifact-set digest. WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore currently accepts three bytes objects.\nRoot protocol stays prepare, launch, reclaim. Gates stay off. Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Current launcher prepare creates broker-writable staging and protected replica roots. Desktop connects to VM as yinshi-app over SSH.\nDiagnose current code and propose the smallest secure upload protocol and ownership flow. Resolve who writes staging, how end-to-end Ed25519 authentication binds chunks or files, how bounds and backpressure work, how retries avoid overwrite, how broker maps artifact IDs to safe descriptor-opened files, and how verify/publish avoid whole-file memory where practical. Preserve relay contract unless a justified compatible extension exists.\nState owners, transitions, failure outcomes, restart behavior, and exact module/API additions. Flag any blocker requiring privileged infrastructure approval.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-expert","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"xhigh","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"e8f4f3a9b029b0bc25c1bdb6f28e2a381837ad4612c7085ae26fc7ba5feee2b2","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":159974,"output":17403,"cacheRead":135296,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.389608,"turns":6},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","thinking":"xhigh","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":9,"graceTurns":2,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":6},"toolBudget":{"hard":48,"soft":32,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":38,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":32},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":38,"tokens":177377,"durationMs":560823},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":false}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"## Causal diagnosis\n\nPhase 6 has a control plane, but no artifact data plane.\n\nCurrent signed broker request can authenticate artifact metadata. Current relay cannot carry artifact bytes safely. Current publication store only accepts in-memory bytes. Root prepare expects a different directory shape.\n\n### Findings\n\n1. **Blocker: replica lifecycle requests never reach replica journal**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24` supports only `executor.launch`.\n   - `BrokerReplicaJournal` exists, but broker daemon does not dispatch `replica.lifecycle`.\n   - Result: signed replica requests cannot begin ingestion, verification, or publication.\n\n2. **Blocker: current relay cannot carry artifacts**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py:27-29` fixes `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, which is correct.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18` caps requests at 65,536 bytes.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:_read_frame` reads one complete frame, requires EOF, and buffers frame bytes.\n   - Artifacts allow up to 1 GiB per set. Sending them inside signed JSON is impossible and unsafe.\n\n3. **High: publication APIs cause whole-set memory amplification**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779` accepts three `bytes` objects.\n   - `_PinnedRegular.content` retains complete file bytes.\n   - `_read_descriptor` joins all chunks into one object.\n   - `_recheck_pinned_regular` reads files again and compares full byte objects.\n   - Bundle verification copies bytes into a temporary file.\n   - Index-pack verification passes the entire pack through `stdin_bytes`.\n   - A near-limit set can create several GiB of transient memory.\n\n4. **Blocker: published artifact layout is incompatible with root prepare**\n   - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` publishes:\n     - `artifact-set.json`\n     - `committed.bundle`\n     - `worktree.yra`\n     - `index-objects.pack`\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199` requires exactly `repo` and `home`.\n   - Pointing the publication store at `/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging` will always fail prepare.\n\n5. **High: artifact-set digest contracts need one shared definition**\n   - Replica journal accepts caller-supplied `artifact_set_sha256`.\n   - Publication store computes a domain digest from the complete declaration.\n   - That declaration includes authority, limits, repository identity, workspace identity, and media metadata.\n   - Journal payload tests do not establish that desktop can reproduce this exact declaration.\n   - Broker must recompute one shared digest before accepting bytes. Silent reinterpretation would change persisted meaning.\n\n6. **Medium: current deadlines do not fit bounded GiB ingestion**\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` uses a 120-second connection deadline.\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` uses 125 seconds.\n   - Slow but valid 1 GiB uploads can fail despite continuous progress.\n\n7. **High: SSH identity is not end-to-end artifact authentication**\n   - Broker sees Unix peer UID `yinshi-app`, not original desktop SSH identity.\n   - Existing Ed25519 request verification provides correct application-layer authentication.\n   - Artifact bytes must be bound to that signed request through signed lengths and digests.\n\n## Smallest secure wire protocol\n\nKeep existing `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay` unchanged.\n\nAdd a second fixed executable:\n\n```text\nyinshi-broker-artifact-upload\n```\n\nIt accepts no arguments and connects only to:\n\n```text\n/run/yinshi/broker.sock\n```\n\nReuse existing broker socket. No caller-selected path or new Unix listener is needed.\n\n### Upload wire format\n\n```text\nu32be signed_request_length\nsigned replica.lifecycle request\ncommitted.bundle bytes, exact signed length\nworktree.yra bytes, exact signed length\nindex-objects.pack bytes, exact signed length\nEOF\n```\n\nResponse remains existing format:\n\n```text\nu32be signed_response_length\nbroker-signed canonical JSON response\n```\n\nNo artifact names, offsets, paths, or chunk headers cross the wire. Order is fixed by protocol.\n\n### Authentication\n\nDesktop signs metadata containing, for every fixed role:\n\n- Artifact ID\n- SHA-256 digest\n- Byte length\n\nSignature also binds:\n\n- Operation ID\n- Broker incarnation\n- Database incarnation\n- Sequence\n- Nonce\n- Object format\n- Source-state digest\n- Reconciliation fingerprint\n- Artifact-set digest\n\nBroker authenticates signed request before reading artifact data.\n\nChunks need no individual Ed25519 signatures. Chunk boundaries are transport details. Signed file length, fixed ordering, and signed SHA-256 bind every file byte and position.\n\nBroker publishes nothing until all three incremental hashes match. Modified, reordered, truncated, extended, or substituted bytes fail verification.\n\n## Bounds and backpressure\n\nUse 64 KiB transfer buffers at every hop.\n\nDesktop:\n\n1. Write bounded signed frame.\n2. Stream each local file through SSH.\n3. Respect writable-stream backpressure.\n4. Close SSH stdin after third file.\n\nUpload relay:\n\n1. Buffer only four-byte prefix plus signed frame.\n2. Forward frame immediately.\n3. Copy remaining stdin in 64 KiB blocks.\n4. Call socket drain after each block.\n5. Enforce fixed global tail ceiling of 1 GiB.\n6. Expose no CLI options.\n\nBroker:\n\n1. Validate signed declared lengths before reading data.\n2. Enforce per-role server ceilings.\n3. Enforce aggregate 1 GiB ceiling.\n4. Read exactly each declared length.\n5. Reject any trailing byte.\n6. Incrementally hash while writing.\n7. Apply idle deadlines, not one 120-second total deadline.\n8. Limit concurrent uploads and reserve declared storage.\n\nSocket and SSH flow control then propagate disk pressure back to desktop. No layer queues an entire artifact.\n\n## Storage ownership and safe mapping\n\n### Durable artifact roots\n\nAdd broker-owned roots:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/incoming\n/var/lib/yinshi/artifacts/published\n```\n\nBoth should be `0700`, owned by `yinshi-broker`.\n\nDesktop and `yinshi-app` never write these roots. Broker performs every artifact write.\n\nArtifact IDs must never become path components. Broker maps signed roles to fixed names:\n\n```text\ncommitted_bundle -> committed.bundle\nworktree         -> worktree.yra\nindex_objects    -> index-objects.pack\n```\n\nRequire all three artifact IDs to be distinct.\n\nOpen operation directories relative to pinned root descriptors. Open files with:\n\n```text\nO_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK\n```\n\nRequire:\n\n- Regular file\n- Broker ownership\n- Mode `0600`\n- Link count one\n- Exact signed length\n- Matching named and opened inode\n- Matching filesystem identity\n\nConsumers request a role. Store returns a pinned descriptor plus authenticated artifact ID. It never resolves `root / artifact_id`.\n\n## Ingestion and retry flow\n\n1. Broker authenticates request.\n2. Broker validates strict replica payload and limits.\n3. Journal records exact signed request.\n4. Journal claims lifecycle authority.\n5. Journal begins `ingest`.\n6. Broker creates broker-generated pending directory with `O_EXCL` semantics.\n7. Broker streams fixed files using exclusive creation.\n8. Broker hashes and synchronizes each file.\n9. Broker verifies directory and file identities.\n10. Broker renames pending directory to `incoming/<operation_id>` with no replacement.\n11. Broker synchronizes both parents.\n12. Journal completes `ingest`.\n\nNever overwrite an existing file or directory.\n\nRetry rules:\n\n- Exact request plus exact completed incoming set: inspect and reuse.\n- Exact request plus exact published set: return stored or reconstructed progress.\n- Existing set with different identity or content: reject. Never replace it.\n- Different signed frame using same operation ID: journal conflict.\n- Partial live attempt with confirmed cleanup: retry starts a new exclusive attempt.\n- Uncertain cleanup or rename: mark unresolved and retain state.\n- Lost final response: exact request replay returns journaled signed response.\n- Restart with only partial bytes: quarantine attempt and mark `transfer_unknown`.\n- Restart with exact synchronized incoming files: resume deterministic verification.\n- Retry after stale broker incarnation requires a new signed request and operation.\n\n## Verification and publication\n\n### Ingest verification\n\nIngest verifies only:\n\n- Signed lengths\n- SHA-256 digests\n- Fixed role ordering\n- Safe file identity\n\nThen journal records `IngestReceipt`.\n\n### Semantic verification\n\nOpen pinned descriptors from `incoming`.\n\nAdd file-based verification:\n\n- Bundle verifier passes a stable read-only file descriptor path to Git.\n- Index-pack verifier passes a stable read-only pack path to Git.\n- Worktree decoder reads bounded sections from a descriptor.\n- Hash checks use incremental `pread`.\n- Identity and digest are rechecked after semantic verification.\n\nJournal then records `VerifyReceipt`.\n\n### Artifact publication\n\nAdd adoption support to `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\n\nIt should:\n\n1. Accept pinned incoming descriptors plus prior verification receipt.\n2. Write bounded `artifact-set.json`.\n3. Recheck all identities and hashes.\n4. Rename `incoming/<operation_id>` to `published/<operation_id>` without replacement.\n5. Synchronize source and destination parents.\n6. Inspect final directory.\n7. Return `ReplicaPublicationReceipt`.\n\nKeep current bytes API as an explicit compatibility wrapper for existing tests. Production ingestion must use descriptor API.\n\nJournal records `PublishReceipt` only after durable final inspection.\n\n### Launcher staging\n\nPublished artifacts cannot be sent directly to root prepare.\n\nBroker-owned materializer must build:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/.<operation_id>.pending/\n  repo/\n  home/\n```\n\nIt reconstructs repository and worktree from pinned published artifacts. It then synchronizes and renames pending directory to:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging/<operation_id>\n```\n\nRoot launcher then performs existing transitions:\n\n```text\nprepare -> launch -> reclaim\n```\n\nNo path enters root protocol. Only operation ID enters it.\n\n## State ownership\n\n| State | Owner |\n|---|---|\n| Source snapshot and desktop private key | Desktop |\n| SSH session authorization | SSH infrastructure |\n| Signed logical request and replay identity | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Partial upload descriptors | Broker ingestion handler |\n| Incoming immutable artifact set | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Semantic verification result | Broker journal |\n| Published immutable artifacts | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Unprepared `repo/home` tree | Broker |\n| Promotion and ownership transfer | Root launcher |\n| Prepared operation directory | Root |\n| Prepared `repo/home` | Allocated executor |\n| Runtime listener and retained descriptor | Broker runtime |\n| Reclaim quarantine and deletion | Root launcher |\n\n## Permitted transitions\n\n```text\nabsent\n  -> accepted\n  -> claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingested\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verified\n  -> publish_started\n  -> published\n  -> admission\n  -> drain\n  -> export\n  -> reclaim\n```\n\nDisk transitions:\n\n```text\nabsent\n  -> private attempt\n  -> synchronized incoming\n  -> verified incoming\n  -> published artifacts\n  -> materialization pending\n  -> launcher staging\n  -> protected replica\n  -> quarantine\n  -> reclaimed\n```\n\n## Invalid transitions\n\n- Reading artifact bytes before request authentication\n- Unknown, missing, duplicated, or reordered roles\n- Duplicate artifact IDs\n- Declared limits above server ceilings\n- Truncation or trailing data\n- Artifact ID used as a path\n- Replacing existing incoming, published, staging, or replica state\n- Verification completion before ingest completion\n- Publication completion before semantic verification\n- Root prepare before exact `repo/home` staging exists\n- Launch after unresolved synchronization\n- Adopting orphan disk state without matching signed journal request\n- Continuing when both incoming and published states exist\n- Converting journal or filesystem uncertainty into success\n\n## Failure and cancellation outcomes\n\n- Authentication failure: close without signed success.\n- Limit failure before upload: signed rejection when request authentication succeeded.\n- Digest or length mismatch: `artifact_rejected`.\n- Declared aggregate overflow: `limit_rejected`.\n- Semantic failure: `verification_rejected`.\n- Confirmed publication collision: `publication_rejected`.\n- Rename or synchronization uncertainty: `publication_unknown` or `synchronization_unknown`.\n- Cancellation during partial receive: clean only pinned owned attempt.\n- Uncertain cleanup: `transfer_unknown`.\n- Cancellation after durable ingest: shield verification and publication. Journal remains authoritative.\n- SQLite failure before acceptance: do not read artifact bytes.\n- SQLite commit uncertainty after bytes: retain synchronized files, return no success, and reconcile exact row plus exact files.\n- Identity uncertainty: fail closed and retain state.\n\n## Restart behavior\n\nStartup reconciliation must use `BrokerReplicaJournal.incomplete_lifecycles()`.\n\nFor each stored signed request:\n\n- Reauthenticate stored frame.\n- Reconstruct fixed manifest.\n- Open only descriptor-relative fixed locations.\n- Resume ingest completion when exact incoming files exist.\n- Repeat semantic verification because it has no external irreversible effect.\n- Inspect exact published state before completing publish.\n- Quarantine partial or foreign state.\n- Mark ambiguity unresolved.\n- Never adopt an unjournaled operation.\n- Never overwrite state to make recovery succeed.\n\nReceipts should be deterministic from request identity and verified state. This permits safe replay after commit-response loss.\n\n## Exact module and API additions\n\n### New modules\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass OpenedReplicaArtifacts:\n    operation_id: str\n    bundle: OpenedArtifact\n    worktree: OpenedArtifact\n    index_objects: OpenedArtifact\n\nclass BrokerArtifactStore:\n    async def receive(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\n\n    @contextmanager\n    def open_incoming(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n    ) -> Iterator[OpenedReplicaArtifacts]: ...\n\n    def inspect_incoming(\n        self,\n        manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest,\n    ) -> IngestReceipt: ...\n\n    def reconcile_attempts(\n        self,\n        journal_operations: frozenset[str],\n    ) -> tuple[ReconciliationResult, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_service.py`\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaService:\n    async def handle_upload(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        reader: asyncio.StreamReader,\n    ) -> bytes: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> None: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\n\n```python\nasync def relay_upload(\n    *,\n    broker_socket: Path = DEFAULT_BROKER_SOCKET,\n) -> bytes: ...\n```\n\nProduction entry point accepts no arguments.\n\n`desktop/src/brokerArtifactUpload.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport async function uploadReplicaArtifacts(\n  request: SignedBrokerRequest,\n  artifacts: ReplicaArtifactFiles,\n): Promise<SignedBrokerResponse>;\n```\n\nRemote command must be a fixed constant. API must not accept a socket path or arbitrary remote command.\n\n### Existing module changes\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py`\n\n- Add strict `ReplicaArtifactManifest`.\n- Add `parse_replica_lifecycle_payload`.\n- Add shared `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256`.\n- Require distinct artifact IDs.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\n\n- Split framed request reading from EOF enforcement.\n- Authenticate initial frame before reading upload tail.\n- Dispatch `executor.launch` to existing service.\n- Dispatch `replica.lifecycle` to replica service.\n- Preserve EOF requirement for ordinary broker relay.\n- Replace total upload timeout with bounded idle deadlines.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_artifact_files(\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\n) -> ReplicaVerificationReceipt: ...\n\nasync def adopt_verified_artifact_set(\n    declaration: ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration,\n    artifacts: OpenedReplicaArtifacts,\n    verification: ReplicaVerificationReceipt,\n) -> ReplicaPublicationReceipt: ...\n```\n\nKeep `publish_artifact_set(...bytes...)` only as compatibility wrapper.\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_committed_bundle_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    object_format: Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"],\n    limits: BundleLimits,\n) -> VerifiedCommittedBundle: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n\n```python\nasync def verify_index_object_pack_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    object_format: Literal[\"sha1\", \"sha256\"],\n    expected_oids: Sequence[str],\n    limits: IndexObjectPackLimits,\n) -> VerifiedIndexObjectPack: ...\n```\n\n`backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py`\n\n```python\ndef inspect_worktree_artifact_file(\n    descriptor: int,\n    *,\n    limits: ArtifactLimits,\n) -> VerifiedWorktreeArtifactMetadata: ...\n```\n\nMaterialization should use a streaming entry visitor rather than retaining every content payload.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Put artifacts in signed JSON:** rejected by 65,536-byte broker frame ceiling.\n- **Use current relay for raw trailing bytes:** rejected because it requires one framed request and EOF.\n- **Use SCP or SFTP into launcher staging:** rejected because `yinshi-app` does not own staging. It would also bypass journal admission.\n- **Let desktop select a Unix socket:** rejected because it breaks fixed relay boundary.\n- **Use artifact IDs as filenames:** rejected because IDs are caller-controlled identifiers.\n- **Point publication store at launcher staging:** rejected by root launcher exact `repo/home` check.\n- **Sign each 64 KiB chunk:** rejected as unnecessary. Signed whole-file length and digest already bind complete ordered content.\n- **Rely on SSH authentication alone:** rejected because broker sees only local Unix UID.\n\n## Privileged infrastructure blockers\n\nProduction gates must remain off until these receive approval:\n\n1. Install and allowlist fixed SSH command `yinshi-broker-artifact-upload`.\n2. Confirm `yinshi-app` cannot request arbitrary relay commands or socket paths.\n3. Provision desktop Ed25519 public key into protected broker configuration.\n4. Create broker-owned incoming and published roots through `tmpfiles.d`.\n5. Define disk quota or reserved capacity for concurrent 1 GiB uploads.\n6. Isolate untrusted Git verification from broker signing keys.\n\nLast item may require a dedicated verifier service account or systemd sandbox. Root launcher actions should not expand beyond prepare, launch, and reclaim.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Whole-file SHA-256 detects corruption only after received bytes consume bandwidth and temporary disk.\n- Persistent abandoned attempts need bounded quarantine retention.\n- Worktree streaming decoder requires careful parser equivalence tests.\n- Git subprocess compromise remains dangerous if verification runs with broker key access.\n- Artifact-set digest definition needs explicit compatibility approval before persisted meaning changes.\n- No implementation or runtime validation occurred because task was read-only.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789249362674,"runId":"44151b43","agent":"worker-expert","index":0,"message":"worker-expert is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":5,"tokens":129833,"toolCount":38,"elapsedMs":240719}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":159974,"output":17403,"cacheRead":135296,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.389608,"turns":6}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/44151b43/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Concrete blocker, high, and medium findings identify execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, broker_stdio_relay.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, root_launcher.py, broker_protocol.py, and deployment ownership files. Review findings and residual risks are included."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected repository state without editing."},{"command":"pytest","result":"not-run","summary":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. No implementation required validation."}],"validationOutput":["Confirmed broker accepts only executor.launch.","Confirmed current relay uses fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock and one bounded frame.","Confirmed publication store accepts three in-memory bytes objects.","Confirmed root prepare requires exactly repo and home.","Confirmed deployment assigns launcher staging ownership to yinshi-broker."],"residualRisks":["Artifact-set digest definition is not yet a shared desktop-broker contract.","Git verification can access broker credentials unless isolated.","Disk exhaustion needs quotas plus bounded quarantine retention.","Streaming worktree verification needs parser-equivalence and fault-injection tests."],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No files changed. Read-only architecture review only.","reviewFindings":["blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24 - broker supports only executor.launch, so replica.lifecycle cannot reach replica journal.","blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18 - 65,536-byte request limit prevents artifact transfer inside signed broker frame.","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779 - publication requires three complete bytes objects and amplifies memory use.","blocker: backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199 - root prepare requires repo and home, which conflicts with publication store artifact layout.","high: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py - 120-second whole-connection deadline is unsuitable for bounded GiB ingestion.","high: deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf - broker owns staging while SSH principal yinshi-app cannot write it, so broker must own ingestion and materialization."],"manualNotes":"Gates should remain disabled until SSH forced-command policy, key provisioning, storage quotas, and verifier isolation receive infrastructure approval."}},"toolCalls":[{"text":"ls {\"path\":\".\",\"limit\":200}","expandedText":"ls {\"path\":\".\",\"limit\":200}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/AGENTS.md\",\"li...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/AGENTS.md\",\"limit\":50}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/*\",\"limit\":100...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"**/*\",\"limit\":1000}"},{"text":"$ git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -...","expandedText":"$ git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline"},{"text":"read CLAUDE.md","expandedText":"read CLAUDE.md"},{"text":"read docs/broker-root-launcher.md","expandedText":"read docs/broker-root-launcher.md"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/root_launche...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\"pattern\":\"def prepare|def _prepare|staging|Prepare\",\"context\":3,\"limit\":100}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/services/bro...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\"pattern\":\"def accept|def claim|def start|def record|def incomplete|ingest|VerifyReceipt|IngestR..."},{"text":"read deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf","expandedText":"read deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf"},{"text":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service","expandedText":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service"},{"text":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-launcher.service","expandedText":"read deploy/systemd/yinshi-launcher.service"},{"text":"read deploy/sysusers.d/yinshi.conf","expandedText":"read deploy/sysusers.d/yinshi.conf"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"broker-stdio-rela...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\".\",\"pattern\":\"broker-stdio-relay|broker_stdio_relay|replica.lifecycle|WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore|complete_ingest|publish_artifact_set\",\"glob\":\"*...."},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_broker_stdio_relay.py"},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py","expandedText":"read backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py"},{"text":"read desktop/src/localRuntime.ts","expandedText":"read desktop/src/localRuntime.ts"},{"text":"read desktop/src/isolationProfile.ts","expandedText":"read desktop/src/isolationProfile.ts"},{"text":"read deploy/orbstack/yinshi-runtime.profile.json","expandedText":"read deploy/orbstack/yinshi-runtime.profile.json"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py"}]}]},"trace":[{"operation":"run","key":"replica-ingestion-architecture","state":"started"},{"operation":"run","key":"replica-ingestion-architecture","state":"completed","durationMs":560912,"runId":"44151b43"}],"emits":[],"console":[]},"chatProgress":{"mode":"live-card","repoRelation":"same","repoLabel":"yinshi"},"missionId":"26941e53-e8a4-440c-b48c-87e68c2ecd96","missionPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/missions/26941e53-e8a4-440c-b48c-87e68c2ecd96.json","mission":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"26941e53-e8a4-440c-b48c-87e68c2ecd96","title":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. Do not edit.","objective":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. Do not edit.\nPhase 6 needs authenticated bounded desktop-to-broker ingestion for exactly committed.bundle, worktree.yra, and index-objects.pack, then broker journal verify/publish.\nCurrent stdio relay is intentionally opaque and forwards one bounded signed broker frame to fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock. It must expose no caller-selected socket and should not buffer GiB artifacts. Broker journal signed request stores only artifact IDs, digests, lengths, object format, source digest, fingerprint, and artifact-set digest. WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore currently accepts three bytes objects.\nRoot protocol stays prepare, launch, reclaim. Gates stay off. Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Current launcher prepare creates broker-writable staging and protected replica roots. Desktop connects to VM as yinshi-app over SSH.\nDiagnose current code and propose the smallest secure upload protocol and ownership flow. Resolve who writes staging, how end-to-end Ed25519 authentication binds chunks or files, how bounds and backpressure work, how retries avoid overwrite, how broker maps artifact IDs to safe descriptor-opened files, and how verify/publish avoid whole-file memory where practical. Preserve relay contract unless a justified compatible extension exists.\nState owners, transitions, failure outcomes, restart behavior, and exact module/API additions. Flag any blocker requiring privileged infrastructure approval.","status":"completed","createdAt":"2026-09-12T21:38:41.777Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-12T21:48:02.812Z","runs":[{"runId":"call_Zg8QUv7PKSZosIMupYPLOVFC|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5c6583f3087d0a3fa8cbb9c11a4c4","mode":"workflow","agent":"worker-expert","status":"completed","startedAt":"2026-09-12T21:48:02.812Z","completedAt":"2026-09-12T21:48:02.812Z","usage":{"tokens":177377}}],"decisions":[],"artifacts":[{"kind":"output","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_output.md"},{"kind":"other","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","description":"Child transcript"}],"receipts":[],"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","ownerSessionId":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64.jsonl","summary":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"replica-ingestion-architecture\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"44151b43\",\n  \"output\": \"## Causal diagnosis\\n\\nPhase 6 has a control plane, but no artifact data plane.\\n\\nCurrent signed broker request can authenticate artifact metadata. Current relay cannot carry artifact bytes safely. Current publication store only accepts in-memory bytes. Root prepare expects a different directory shape.\\n\\n### Findings\\n\\n1. **Blocker: replica lifecycle requests never reach replica journal**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24` supports only `executor.launch`.\\n   - `BrokerReplicaJournal` exists, but broker daemon does not dispatch `replica.lifecycle`.\\n   - Result: signed replica requests cannot begin ingestion, verification, or publication.\\n\\n2. **Blocker: current relay cannot carry artifacts**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py:27-29` fixes `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, which is correct.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18` caps requests at 65,536 bytes.\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:_read_frame` reads one complete frame, requires EOF, and buffers frame bytes.\\n   - Artifacts allow up to 1 GiB per set. Sending them inside signed JSON is impossible and unsafe.\\n\\n3. **High: publication APIs cause whole-set memory amplification**\\n   - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779` accepts three `bytes` objects.\\n   - `_PinnedRegular.content` retains complete file bytes.\\n   - `_read_descriptor` joins all chunks into one object.\\n   - `_recheck_pinned_regular` reads files again and compares full byte objects.\\n   - Bundle verification copies bytes into a temporary file.\\n   - Index-pack verification passes the entire pack through `stdin_bytes`.\\n   - A near-limit set can create several GiB of transient memory.\\n\\n4. **Blocker: published artifact layout is incompatible with root prepare**\\n   - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` publishes:\\n ...","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Concrete blocker, high, and medium findings identify execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, broker_stdio_relay.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, root_launcher.py, broker_protocol.py, and deployment ownership files. Review findings and residual risks are included."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log -1 --oneline","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected repository state without editing."},{"command":"pytest","result":"not-run","summary":"Read-only architecture diagnosis. No implementation required validation."}],"validationOutput":["Confirmed broker accepts only executor.launch.","Confirmed current relay uses fixed /run/yinshi/broker.sock and one bounded frame.","Confirmed publication store accepts three in-memory bytes objects.","Confirmed root prepare requires exactly repo and home.","Confirmed deployment assigns launcher staging ownership to yinshi-broker."],"residualRisks":["Artifact-set digest definition is not yet a shared desktop-broker contract.","Git verification can access broker credentials unless isolated.","Disk exhaustion needs quotas plus bounded quarantine retention.","Streaming worktree verification needs parser-equivalence and fault-injection tests."],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No files changed. Read-only architecture review only.","reviewFindings":["blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:22-24 - broker supports only executor.launch, so replica.lifecycle cannot reach replica journal.","blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:16-18 - 65,536-byte request limit prevents artifact transfer inside signed broker frame.","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:773-779 - publication requires three complete bytes objects and amplifies memory use.","blocker: backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:1198-1199 - root prepare requires repo and home, which conflicts with publication store artifact layout.","high: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py - 120-second whole-connection deadline is unsuitable for bounded GiB ingestion.","high: deploy/tmpfiles.d/yinshi.conf - broker owns staging while SSH principal yinshi-app cannot write it, so broker must own ingestion and materialization."],"manualNotes":"Gates should remain disabled until SSH forced-command policy, key provisioning, storage quotas, and verifier isolation receive infrastructure approval."}}}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789249683109}}
