Call trace:\n- run broker-artifact-store-review: started\n- run broker-artifact-store-review: completed (d2ea7e81) in 593060ms\nMission: bbbe70ad-8d0b-43cc-b432-5a3b1291fac8 (completed)"}],"details":{"mode":"workflow","runId":"call_I14EaNVdYpUS3Hf9EEAowz8l|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5cb364dec87d0acad3af8a5f43f51","results":[{"index":0,"agent":"final-review","task":"Read-only review using software-design. Read CLAUDE.md and PYTHON.md first.\nReview new broker_artifact_store.py and tests, plus broker_replica_journal.py fixed-artifact contract where needed.\nContract: broker-owned 0700 incoming root. Fixed filenames only. Caller artifact IDs never become paths. Three required distinct references. Per-role and aggregate bounds before effects. 64 KiB streaming with idle timeouts and backpressure. Exact lengths, SHA-256, EOF, 0600 regular files, link count one, owner, descriptor/name identity. File and directory sync precede atomic no-replace rename. Exact retry consumes and verifies all bytes. Failure quarantines owned pending state without deleting contents. Cancellation waits for blocking writes before descriptor close, then quarantines. Opened descriptor context permits post-await recheck.\nRed: missing module. Current: 47 artifact-store+journal tests passed. Ruff lint passes. Format was corrected after reported diffs. Strict mypy, py_compile, and diff check pass.\nInspect current files. Find races, cancellation faults, descriptor leaks, classification errors, blocking event-loop paths, unbounded allocations, path attacks, replay gaps, or API contract issues. Report every finding with severity, location, impact, correction, validation, and remediation. If none, state no remediation needed. Do not edit.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"final-review","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"f92b1392d5e967bb32f96f1eb9645c32e30cc843f27f1d3bdb21adcda29fe685","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":168303,"output":26420,"cacheRead":172800,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.7205150000000002,"turns":8},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","thinking":"max","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/d2ea7e81_final-review_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/d2ea7e81_final-review_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/d2ea7e81_final-review_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/d2ea7e81_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/d2ea7e81_final-review_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/d2ea7e81_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","skills":["software-design"],"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":8,"graceTurns":2,"turnCount":8,"outcome":"wrap-up-requested","wrapUpRequestedAtTurn":8},"toolBudget":{"hard":46,"soft":30,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":31,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":30},"context":"fresh","wrapUpRequested":true,"progressSummary":{"toolCount":31,"tokens":194723,"durationMs":592838},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":true}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 8 assistant turns (soft limit 8, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nReview blocked. Ten findings remain. No files changed.\n\n## Review findings\n\n### F1. High: Attempt state can publish one outcome, then report another\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:436-469`\n\n- Rename collision quarantines at line 445.\n- Raised collision reaches the outer rejection handler.\n- Outer handler quarantines the same missing pending directory again.\n- Successful publication leaves `pending_identity` active.\n- Cancellation during final inspection then tries to quarantine the already-published source.\n\nImpact: Confirmed collision becomes unresolved. Post-publication cancellation can leave durable files while replacing `CancelledError` with an unresolved error.\n\nCorrection: Model attempt state explicitly as live, quarantined, or published. Centralize cleanup. Mark state immediately after each rename.\n\nValidation: Inject a late publication collision. Cancel during final inspection. Assert one durable outcome and one quarantine attempt.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F2. Medium: Quarantine is neither repeat-safe nor complete\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:340-358, 389-405`\n\nQuarantine always targets `.<operation>.pending.abandoned`. A second failed attempt collides with the first quarantine.\n\nAn error after `mkdir` but before `pending_identity` assignment leaves `.pending` unquarantined.\n\nImpact: Failed retries leave live pending state. Later attempts collide permanently.\n\nCorrection: Use broker-generated unique quarantine names. Track created state before reopening it. Quarantine through verified descriptor-relative identity.\n\nValidation: Fail two consecutive attempts. Inject pending-directory open and `fstat` failures. Confirm no live `.pending` remains.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F3. High: Storage and transport faults become conclusive rejection\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:189-200, 268-306, 417-425, 471-474`\n\nUnhandled `OSError` reaches the generic handler and becomes `BrokerArtifactStoreRejectedError`.\n\nThis includes disk-full, write, sync, open, and connection-reset failures.\n\nImpact: Infrastructure uncertainty can become durable client rejection. Retry or recovery may then be blocked incorrectly.\n\nCorrection: Reserve rejection for proven invalid input. Map storage and uncertain transport faults to unresolved outcomes.\n\nValidation: Inject `ENOSPC`, `EIO`, sync failure, and connection reset. Assert unresolved classification plus retained quarantine.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F4. High: Existing FIFO can block inspection and cancellation forever\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:478-494`\n\n`_open_artifact` omits `O_NONBLOCK`. A fixed-name FIFO blocks during `os.open` before regular-file validation.\n\nImpact: Exact retry can hang a worker forever. `_run_blocking` then waits forever during cancellation.\n\nCorrection: Open candidate files with `O_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK`. Reject non-regular files after `fstat`.\n\nValidation: Place a FIFO at each fixed role name. Inspection and cancellation must finish promptly.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F5. High: Journal does not enforce one canonical fixed-artifact identity\n\nLocation:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:131-145`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:217-230`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:569-596`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:717-740`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:797-807`\n\nJournal payload validation accepts duplicate artifact IDs. It also accepts any syntactically valid `artifact_set_sha256`.\n\nReplay repeats the same incomplete validation. Store validation separately rejects duplicate IDs.\n\nImpact: Durable journal authority can contain contradictory artifact identity. Accepted requests can later fail only at storage.\n\nCorrection: Create one shared fixed-artifact validator. Enforce distinct IDs and recompute the canonical artifact-set digest during acceptance and replay.\n\nValidation: Reject duplicate IDs and mismatched set digests before journal writes. Inject both forms into persisted events and reject replay.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F6. High: Approved restart reconciliation API is absent\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`, class ends at line 757.\n\nApproved design requires `reconcile_attempts(...)`. Current class has no restart reconciliation operation.\n\nImpact: Crash-left `.pending` state cannot be classified or quarantined against journal authority. Such state blocks future attempts.\n\nCorrection: Implement bounded, descriptor-relative reconciliation. Never delete contents. Preserve ambiguous state and report unresolved outcomes.\n\nValidation: Cover restart with partial pending, exact final, pending plus final, malformed names, foreign identities, and unknown journal operations.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F7. Medium: Timeout measures chunk duration, not idle duration\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:245-265`\n\n`readexactly(count)` runs under one timeout. Progress does not reset the deadline until the entire chunk arrives.\n\nImpact: A continuously progressing slow upload becomes unresolved despite never being idle.\n\nCorrection: Read partial chunks in a loop. Apply a fresh timeout to each progress-producing read.\n\nValidation: A drip feed below the idle threshold must succeed. A gap above the threshold must become unresolved.\n\nRemediation: `worker`.\n\n### F8. High: Large file and durable rename work can block the event loop\n\nLocation:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:340-354, 436-453, 478-757`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:251-344`\n\n`open_incoming`, `inspect_incoming`, and `recheck_opened` hash files synchronously.\n\nPublication and quarantine call synchronous parent-directory `fsync` from async `receive`.\n\nImpact: Large artifacts or slow storage can freeze the broker loop. Cancellation cannot be delivered during synchronous publication.\n\nCorrection: Provide async inspection and recheck boundaries. Offload hashing, publication, quarantine, and sync work while retaining descriptors.\n\nValidation: Run an event-loop heartbeat during delayed hashing and `fsync`. Verify bounded latency and cancellation behavior.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\n### F9. Medium: Post-open failures leak descriptors\n\nLocation:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:189-211`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:295-307`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:478-526`\n\n`_open_root`, `_create_file`, and `_open_artifact` lack complete ownership guards after successful `os.open`.\n\nFailures in `fstat`, `fchmod`, named `stat`, or `pread` can leak descriptors.\n\nImpact: Repeated races or filesystem faults can exhaust broker descriptors.\n\nCorrection: Wrap every post-open path in `try/finally`. Transfer descriptor ownership only on successful return.\n\nValidation: Fault-inject each post-open operation. Compare descriptor counts before and after every failure.\n\nRemediation: `worker`.\n\n### F10. Medium: Fixed-set inspection allocates from unbounded directory contents\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:602, 735`\n\n`set(os.listdir(...))` materializes every entry before rejecting unknown names.\n\nImpact: Corrupt or same-owner foreign state can cause excessive memory use and long synchronous work.\n\nCorrection: Scan entries incrementally. Reject the first unknown entry or any fourth entry.\n\nValidation: Inspect a directory containing many unexpected entries. Confirm prompt bounded rejection.\n\nRemediation: `worker`.\n\n## Required checks\n\nCurrent targeted test result is not confirmed.\n\n- `pytest -q tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py` failed with two collection errors.\n- Repetition with `-x -vv` failed during first collection.\n- Project output did not expose the collection traceback.\n- Reported Ruff, format, mypy, and `py_compile` results were not independently repeated.\n- `git diff --check` returned success but ignored all four untracked candidate files.\n\nRun targeted tests after every correction. Add fault, cancellation, FIFO, restart, replay, idle-progress, and descriptor-leak tests.\n\n## Residual risks and review limits\n\n- All four candidate files are untracked. No final staged candidate exists.\n- No production caller imports `BrokerArtifactStore`. End-to-end backpressure and journal integration remain unverified.\n- Review covered journal fixed-artifact validation and replay paths. Unrelated journal behavior was outside scope.\n- Persistent quarantine retention and disk quota remain deployment risks.\n\nRemediation is required. All findings block completion.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789250609577,"runId":"d2ea7e81","agent":"final-review","index":0,"message":"final-review is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":7,"tokens":162445,"toolCount":31,"elapsedMs":240284}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":168303,"output":26420,"cacheRead":172800,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.7205150000000002,"turns":8}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/d2ea7e81/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"rejected","evidenceStatus":"rejected","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","resid