configured entry bound. Existing concurrency test uses one store instance, so it misses this race.\\n\\nCorrection: Use root-scoped inter-process locking around final lookup, entry counting, and pending-directory creation.\\n\\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`. Concurrency, cancellation, and persistent-root ownership interact.\\n\\nRequired checks:\\n\\n- Add a test using two store instances in separate threads or processes.\\n- Force both reservations to overlap with `max_root_entries=1`.\\n- Assert one reservation succeeds and root never exceeds one entry.\\n- Rerun `test_broker_artifact_store.py`.\\n\\n## Region status\\n\\n1. `reconcile_attempts`: **Resolved.** Root identity revalidation prevents verification through a replaced root. Named test covers replacement before inspection.\\n2. Root capacity reservation: **Not resolved.** See confirmed finding.\\n3. Publication pending cleanup and allocation: **Resolved.** Unique pending and quarantine names preserve legacy state without blocking retries. Repeated failures remain distinct.\\n4. Journal authority replay: **Resolved.** Claimed broker incarnation must match authenticated request incarnation.\\n5. Operation validation: **Resolved.** Shared strict validator covers canonical request parsing and persisted event val...","acceptance":{"status":"not-required","evidenceStatus":"not-required","explicit":true,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"none","explicit":true,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":[],"verify":[],"stopRules":[],"reason":"disabled by deprecated false shorthand"},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[]}}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789258677180}}
