{"type":"message","id":"9161d25f","parentId":"42b82753","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:22:17.924Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_qSmaPQfKcqZA8Zy2YOEUGcCv|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5ec0b7d4087d0934de032b95370d2","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"artifact-capacity-clearance\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"bf648f5f\",\n  \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 3 assistant turns (soft limit 3, grace 1). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Confirmed defect\\n\\n**High — `broker_artifact_store.py:446,450`**\\n\\n`flock` acquisition is cancelable before entering `try`. The receive timeout can cancel while blocking. The worker may acquire the lock later without running `LOCK_UN`.\\n\\nA retained descriptor can then hold the root lock indefinitely. Later receives from other instances or processes can hang and repeat this leak.\\n\\n**Correction:** Make acquisition cancellation-safe. Prefer nonblocking `LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB` retries. After acquisition, release synchronously in `finally`.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. Cancellation and cross-process ownership guarantees interact.\\n\\n**Required checks:**\\n\\n1. Hold the flock from another process.\\n2. Start and cancel `receive` while it waits.\\n3. Release the external lock.\\n4. Confirm a fresh store can receive within a timeout.\\n\\nThe test at `test_broker_artifact_store.py:363` does not cover this race. It starts the second receive after the first pending directory already exists.\\n\\nCore cross-instance capacity serialization works during normal completion. Cancellation safety remains unresolved, so prior finding is not fully resolved. Reported 22 passing tests do not validate this path.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06a