{"type":"message","id":"d9396e99","parentId":"9a05beac","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:32:01.106Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6KedPaVTCvj6yRCdkUKrRsWi|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5eefff81887d09be0fa504aafb126","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Confirmed finding\n\n- **Medium — `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1825-1831, 2367-2373`**\n  - Cancellation can discard `_RetainedPrivateStage` returned through `_await_local_effect`.\n  - Assignment never occurs after cancellation. Both raw descriptors remain open because no destructor closes them.\n  - Durable state remains `planned`, while created stage remains present without persisted identity.\n  - Next retry can mark publication unresolved. Repeated cancellation can exhaust file descriptors.\n  - **Correction:** Add resource-aware cancellation handling. Drain creation, then safely remove empty stage through retained parent or persist identity before re-raising. Always close both descriptors.\n  - **Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. Fix spans cancellation, filesystem ownership, and durable recovery guarantees.\n  - **Required checks:** Add deterministic cancellation tests for both stage-creation callers. Verify descriptor closure, safe retry, and no orphan stage. Repeat focused tests and static checks.\n\n## Prior findings\n\n- **Dropped stage identity:** Not fully resolved. Normal flow retains identity, but cancellation still drops descriptor ownership as described above.\n- **No-replace source gap:** Resolved. `atomic_rename_no_replace` retains both parents and source, uses descriptor-relative native rename, then checks published identity.\n- **Backlink replace gap:** Resolved. `_replace_owned_regular_file` retains parent and old file, checks identity before replacement, then verifies replacement content and ownership.\n- **Cleanup or worktree reopen gap:** Resolved. Cleanup is descriptor-relative. Reopened metadata is identity-checked. `delete_worktree` retains