{"type":"message","id":"b4554635","parentId":"dee8ac41","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:32:18.995Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_g46PUsUITtHVRfnXFHMzZY7P|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5ef11a8c087d0982039225dd3d638","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review result: blocked. Eight findings remain. Trusted `software-design` skill content guided review.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Blocker: Read-only inspection mints publication authority\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:728-766`\n- Impact: Inspection creates `ReplicaPublicationReceipt` and `synchronization_receipt_id` without proving rename or publication-root sync.\n- Impact: It can upgrade unresolved state or adopt an externally copied directory as successful publication.\n- Correction: Return a distinct inspection receipt. Only successful publish flow may create publication and synchronization receipts.\n- Validation: Inject root-sync failure, then inspect. Inspection must not return a publication receipt.\n- Validation: Create an exact directory externally. Inspection must not attest publication.\n- Remediation: `worker-advanced`\n\n### 2. Blocker: Final verification uses stale storage state\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:646-757`\n- Impact: Descriptors close before awaited Git verification. Stored names and bytes can change while stale in-memory copies verify.\n- Impact: Returned receipt can conflict with current stored artifacts.\n- Correction: Retain descriptors and identities through verification. Repeat descriptor-relative metadata, names, lengths, and digests after the last await.\n- Validation: Pause verifier, replace one artifact or final directory, then resume. Publish must be unresolved. Inspection must reject.\n- Remediation: `worker-advanced`\n\n### 3. Blocker: Bundled index objects need not be blobs\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:308-317`\n- Impact: Missing-set calculation subtracts every bundle object ID without checking object kind.\n- Impact: A regular index entry can reference a bundled tree or commit and still pass verification.\n- Correction: Map bundled IDs to `GitObject`. Reject every index OID whose bundled object is not a blob.\n- Validation: Build an index entry referencing a reachable tree object. Use a zero-object supplemental pack. Verification must reject.\n- Remediation: `worker-advanced`\n\n### 4. High: Pending contents are not reinspected before rename\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:388-409,532-568`\n- Impact: Code syncs the pending directory, then renames without checking exact entries, identities, modes, link counts, lengths, or digests.\n- Impact: Wrong umask results or same-owner tamper can publish invalid state before rejection.\n- Correction: Enforce exact modes with descriptor operations. Perform full descriptor-bound pending inspection before rename.\n- Validation: Inject wrong modes, hardlinks, unknown entries, and replaced files before rename. No final target may appear.\n- Remediation: `worker-advanced`\n\n### 5. High: Rename attempt flag does not represent rename outcome\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:528-605`\n- Boundary: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:251-369`\n- Impact: `rename_attempted` becomes true before helper preflight completes.\n- Impact: Unsupported primitives, parent changes, or source validation failures become unresolved and retain pending state despite no rename.\n- Correction: Expose typed pre-effect and post-effect failures. Otherwise inspect exact source and target identities after helper failure.\n- Validation: Inject support failure, source validation failure, pre-move syscall failure, and post-move root-sync failure. Require correct classifications.\n- Remediation: `worker-advanced`\n\n### 6. High: Cleanup is not bound to created identities\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:602-644`\n- Impact: Cleanup closes the pinned root, reopens its pathname, and deletes entries without matching recorded identities.\n- Impact: A replacement pending directory containing expected names can lose foreign state.\n- Impact: Cleanup errors are swallowed. Ordinary rejection can leave a blocking orphan.\n- Correction: Use retained parent authority and recorded directory and file identities. Never unlink mismatched objects. Report retained cleanup state.\n- Validation: Replace the pending directory or one file before cleanup. Foreign state must remain untouched.\n- Validation: Inject unlink and sync failures. Caller must not receive a clean retry signal.\n- Remediation: `worker-advanced`\n\n### 7. Medium: Malformed declaration types escape stable rejection\n\n- Location: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:177-235`\n- Impact: `ReplicaStoreLimits` does not validate nested field types. `_limits_fit` can raise raw `TypeError`.\n- Impact: Role, media type, and object format also lack exact primitive type checks.\n- Correction: Validate nested dataclass types and primitive types before `asdict`, equality checks, or canonicalization.\n- Validation: Supply malformed nested limits and custom field values. All declaration failures must use `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError`.\n- Remediation: `worker`\n\n### 8. High: Required fault-window tests are absent\n\n- Location: `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py:152-287`\n- Impact: Seven tests omit sync ordering, cancellation, cleanup ownership, hardlinks, pending tamper, marker canonicalization, and non-blob relationships.\n- Impact: Line 173 explicitly expects read-only inspection to mint a publication receipt.\n- Correction: Add fault-injection tests for every transition and authority boundary listed above.\n- Validation: Run focused artifact, bundle, object-pack, and publication suites after remediation.\n-