{"type":"message","id":"322d8425","parentId":"1caefe88","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:32:27.270Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YQqV0F2mzezIV0drqk7OCsZw|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5ef1a19a487d09678c26378628dbb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Confirmed finding\n\n1. **Medium — cancellation ownership still ends before durable handoff**\n\nLocations:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1848-1867`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:2391-2410`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:2064-2066`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:2655-2657`\n- Supporting failure path: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1162-1188`\n- Supporting suppression: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1268-1272`\n- Missing coverage: `backend/tests/test_workspace_publication.py:998-1049`\n\nImpact:\n\nCancellation during `_persist_materializing` closes descriptors but leaves an empty stage. Receipt remains `planned` without `staging_identity_json`. Retry then marks repair unresolved and blocks automatic recovery.\n\nCreation failure after `os.mkdir`, such as parent `fsync` failure, also leaves an empty stage. Pending cancellation hides that failure.\n\nFix:\n\nCreate one deep helper that owns stage creation through durable identity persistence. Drain persistence during cancellation. Remove exact empty stage when persistence did not commit. Fence ambiguous outcomes as unresolved.\n\nMake `_create_private_stage` roll back failures after `os.mkdir`. Normalize cleanup filesystem errors into `WorkspacePublicationError`.\n\nRemediation tier: `worker-advanced`. Filesystem durability, database handoff, and cancellation guarantees interact.\n\n## Verified behavior\n\n- Both creation call sites pass `_remove_cancelled_private_stage`.\n- Successful delayed results preserve `CancelledError`.\n- Cleanup validates inode identity and emptiness.\n- Cleanup uses retained parent descriptor and synchronizes it.\n- Replacement test preserved both original and replacement directories.\n- Both retained descriptors reported `EBADF` after cleanup.\n\n## Required checks after correction\n\n1. Cancel each actual caller while `_persist_materializing` is suspended.\n2. Assert no orphan, closed descriptors, preserved cancellation, and successful retry.\n3. Inject failures after `mkdir`, including `open`, identity validation, and `fsync`.\n4. Repeat full publication test file.\n\n## Unanswered questions\n\nNone.\n\n## Inspection limit\n\n\n[1 more lines in file. Use offset=51 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789259547270}}
