{"type":"message","id":"896a61c8","parentId":"c97b55ae","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:33:44.569Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_I4f9olLvDLvTEF7UmkTXuvCq|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5ef5e54e487d0b417c9bed0ed2877","name":"repoprompt_context_builder","arguments":{"instructions":"<task>Plan broker-owned replica lifecycle coordinator for Phase 6. Wire accepted BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerArtifactStore, and WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore across ingest, verify, publish, admission, graceful drain, bounded three-artifact export acknowledgment, and reclaim. Preserve root protocol actions exactly prepare, launch, reclaim. Keep all gates independently disabled. Native Darwin stays fail-closed.</task><context>Current main includes commits through 7f91105f. Required ownership: journal owns durable stage authority, coordinator sequences effects, executor owns drain/export effects, broker owns acknowledgment and reclaim eligibility. Use read-copy-close, external effect, reopen transactional CAS. No SQLite handle crosses await or effect. Missing acknowledgments, live units, unknown transport, timeouts, cancellation, verification, or commit results become stage-specific unresolved and block reclaim. Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Export must acknowledge exactly three external references. Publication and journal use one configured immutable limits profile and authenticated broker keyring. Existing broker launch lifecycle v2 and legacy v1 remain unchanged. Reclaim uses existing root reclaim action only. Managed Linux execution admission must be verified and native Darwin unsupported. RepoPrompt mount may be stale, so state all assumptions and do not invent missing APIs.</context><discovery_agent-guidelines>Inspect current coordinator candidates, journal public API, broker runtime, launcher client, workspace admission/execution, root reclaim, and tests. Prefer one new deep coordinator module with injected effect interfaces.</discovery_agent-guidelines>","response_type":"plan"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1072,"output":322,"cacheRead":204160,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":205554,"cost":{"input":0.00536,"output":0.00966,"cacheRead":0.10207999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.1171}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789259609126,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5ef5a189487d0bfbc200ba80160e7","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"3bedfaa2","parentId":"896a61c8","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:35:52.863Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_I4f9olLvDLvTEF7UmkTXuvCq|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5ef5e54e487d0b417c9bed0ed2877","toolName":"repoprompt_context_builder","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"backend\":\"headless\",\"chat_id\":\"D2C26BA8-46F5-4C12-B0D1-9A89490E8D3B\",\"response\":\"## Phase 6 implementation plan\\n\\nThis should be implemented as one broker-owned lifecycle coordinator that sequences existing stores and effects without absorbing their ownership. No existing root protocol action changes: the action set remains exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`.\\n\\n### Repository assumption\\n\\nThe mounted `/workspace` is stale or missing the target repository:\\n\\n- Commit `7f91105f` is not present in any mounted Git object database.\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal`, `BrokerArtifactStore`, and `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` do not occur in checked-out files or available refs.\\n- The broker runtime, launcher client, admission path, and relevant tests therefore could not be inspected.\\n\\nConsequently, names below describe required capabilities, not invented method signatures or file paths. Before implementation, resolve each capability against the public APIs on current `main`.\\n\\n## 1. Coordinator boundary\\n\\nAdd one deep module, conceptually `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator`, owned and invoked by the broker.\\n\\nInject:\\n\\n- Accepted `BrokerReplicaJournal`\\n- Accepted `BrokerArtifactStore`\\n- Accepted `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`\\n- Existing broker launch lifecycle v2 adapter\\n- Existing legacy v1 adapter, unchanged\\n- Existing launcher/executor client\\n- Existing workspace admission service\\n- Existing root `reclaim` client\\n- One immutable limits profile\\n- One authenticated broker keyring\\n- Clock/cancellation source\\n- Independently configurable lifecycle gates\\n\\nThe coordinator owns sequencing only. It must not:\\n\\n- Become durable stage authority.\\n- Execute drain/export itself.\\n- Decide acknowledgment authenticity outside broker policy.\\n- Add root actions.\\n- Store artifact bytes in SQLite.\\n- Keep a SQLite connection, transaction, row object, or lazy iterator across an `await` or external effect.\\n\\n## 2. Ownership model\\n\\n| Concern | Owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Durable lifecycle stage and CAS authority | Journal |\\n| Ordering reads, effects, and transitions | Coordinator |\\n| Graceful drain and three-artifact export effects | Executor |\\n| Authentication and acceptance of export acknowledgment | Broker |\\n| Reclaim eligibility decision | Broker, based on journal authority |\\n| Artifact byte storage | Artifact store, outside SQLite |\\n| Published workspace references | Publication store |\\n| Root resource destruction | Existing `reclaim` action |\\n\\nThe journal remains the sole source of truth after retries, cancellation, or broker restart. In-memory coordinator state is never authoritative.\\n\\n## 3. Lifecycle stages\\n\\nMap these concepts to existing journal stages rather than creating parallel state if equivalent stages already exist:\\n\\n```text\\ningested\\n  → verification_pending\\n  → verified\\n  → publication_pending\\n  → published\\n  → admission_pending\\n  → admitted\\n  → launched\\n  → drain_pending\\n  → drained\\n  → export_pending\\n  → export_acknowledged\\n  → reclaim_eligible\\n  → reclaimed\\n```\\n\\nEvery effect-bearing stage also needs a stage-specific unresolved outcome, using the journal’s accepted error/result representation:\\n\\n- ingest unresolved\\n- verification unresolved\\n- publication unresolved\\n- admission unresolved\\n- launch unresolved\\n- drain unresolved\\n- export unresolved\\n- acknowledgment unresolved\\n- reclaim-eligibility unresolved\\n- reclaim unresolved\\n\\n“Unresolved” must retain retry/reconciliation information and must never be treated as success. It blocks advancement and, especially, blocks reclaim.\\n\\nTerminal rejection may be distinct from unresolved if the journal already supports it. Do not invent a new failure taxonomy until its accepted API is inspected.\\n\\n## 4. Mandatory effect pattern\\n\\nEvery asynchronous or external operation follows:\\n\\n1. Open journal/store access.\\n2. Read immutable inputs and expected version.\\n3. Record or confirm an effect-intent stage transactionally.\\n4. Copy all required values into owned memory.\\n5. Close transaction and SQLite handle.\\n6. Perform the external effect.\\n7. Reopen storage.\\n8. Transactionally CAS from the expected intent/version to the result stage.\\n9. If CAS loses, reread authority and reconcile without replaying a known-completed destructive effect.\\n\\nThis applies to verification, publication, admission, launch, drain, export, acknowledgment processing, and reclaim.\\n\\nNo SQLite-backed value may escape as a cursor, reference, stream, callback, or lazy collection.\\n\\n## 5. Flow by phase\\n\\n### Ingest\\n\\n- Authenticate the broker-supplied request with the configured keyring.\\n- Validate identifiers and limits using the single configured immutable limits profile.\\n- Store artifact bytes only through `BrokerArtifactStore`.\\n- Journal only durable metadata, hashes, sizes, references, stage, and concurrency/version information.\\n- Use idempotency identity already accepted by the journal.\\n- A partial byte write or unknown commit result becomes ingest unresolved.\\n- Do not advance based solely on the existence of artifact bytes; the journal transition is authoritative.\\n\\n### Verify\\n\\n- Read-copy-close the artifact reference, expected digest, limits identity, and journal version.\\n- Verify externally, including size/digest/content requirements defined by current policy.\\n- Reopen and CAS to verified only for a definite successful result.\\n- Mismatch is a definite verification failure if supported; timeout, cancellation, unavailable bytes, unknown verifier result, or unknown journal commit becomes verification unresolved.\\n- Publication and admission cannot infer verification from artifact-store presence.\\n\\n### Publish\\n\\n- Require durable verified authority.\\n- Use the same immutable limits profile and authenticated broker keyring supplied to the journal path.\\n- Copy the verified manifest/reference data, close storage, then invoke `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\\n- Reopen and CAS the publication result into the journal.\\n- Treat an already-existing identical publication as idempotent success only if the accepted publication-store contract guarantees equivalence.\\n- Conflict, timeout, cancellation, unverifiable signature, or unknown commit result becomes publication unresolved.\\n\\n### Admission and launch\\n\\nManaged Linux admission requires all of:\\n\\n- Journal says verified.\\n- Publication is durably complete.\\n- Target transport is recognized.\\n- Execution target is managed Linux.\\n- Any current v2 admission requirements remain satisfied.\\n\\nNative Darwin remains unsupported and fail-closed. It must not fall through to legacy execution or a generic local launcher.\\n\\nUnknown platform, unknown transport, missing verification, disabled admission gate, or indeterminate policy result does not admit execution.\\n\\nRoute successful launches through existing broker launch lifecycle v2 unchanged. Preserve legacy v1 behavior and wire format unchanged; Phase 6 must not reinterpret v1 state as replica verification or publication.\\n\\n### Graceful drain\\n\\n- Broker/coordinator records drain intent through journal CAS.\\n- After read-copy-close, executor performs the drain.\\n- Reopen and CAS the definite result.\\n- Live units after the bounded drain attempt block export completion and reclaim.\\n- Timeout, cancellation, unknown executor result, or unknown commit produces drain unresolved.\\n- Do not silently escalate graceful drain into root reclaim.\\n\\n### Bounded three-artifact export\\n\\nThe executor must return exactly three external artifact references in one bounded export result.\\n\\nBroker validation must ensure:\\n\\n- Count is exactly three—not at least three.\\n- Each reference is external, structurally valid, nonempty, and distinct if required by existing policy.\\n- Each reference belongs to the expected replica/workspace scope.\\n- The acknowledgment is authenticated by the configured broker keyring.\\n- The acknowledgment binds replica identity, export attempt/nonce, all three references, and the applicable limits/profile identity.\\n- The operation completed within configured bounds.\\n- The journal can durably CAS that precise acknowledgment.\\n\\nArtifact bytes remain external to SQLite. Store only references and integrity/authentication metadata.\\n\\nZero, one, two, or more than three references is acknowledgment unresolved. So are duplicate or malformed references, unknown transport, missing acknowledgment, timeout, cancellation, signature failure, executor ambiguity, and unknown persistence outcome.\\n\\n### Reclaim eligibility\\n\\nThe broker may declare reclaim eligibility only when the journal authoritatively proves:\\n\\n- Successful verified state.\\n- Successful publication/admission lineage as required by accepted policy.\\n- Definite drain completion.\\n- No live units.\\n- Exactly three authenticated external references acknowledged.\\n- No unresolved stage in the lifecycle.\\n- No timeout/cancellation/unknown result awaiting reconciliation.\\n\\nEligibility should be journal-CASed before the destructive effect.\\n\\nThen:\\n\\n1. Read and copy the reclaim token/identity and expected journal version.\\n2. Close database access.\\n3. Invoke the existing root `reclaim` action.\\n4. Reopen.\\n5. CAS the definite result to reclaimed.\\n\\nDo not add `drain`, `export`, or any Phase 6 operation to the root protocol. A missing or ambiguous root response becomes reclaim unresolved; it must not be recorded as reclaimed.\\n\\n## 6. Independent gates\\n\\nDefine separate, default-disabled gates using the project’s existing configuration mechanism:\\n\\n- Replica ingest\\n- Verification\\n- Publication\\n- Managed-Linux admission\\n- Coordinated launch\\n- Graceful drain\\n- Three-artifact export\\n- Broker acknowledgment\\n- Reclaim eligibility\\n- Root reclaim invocation\\n\\nEach gate controls only its named transition/effect. Enabling one must not implicitly enable another.\\n\\nWhen disabled:\\n\\n- Do not perform its effect.\\n- Do not fabricate successful journal state.\\n- Preserve enough authority for later retry after explicit enablement.\\n- Never weaken verification, acknowledgment, platform, or reclaim conditions.\\n\\nNative Darwin rejection is invariant and cannot be overridden by these gates.\\n\\n## 7. Recovery and concurrency\\n\\nProvide a reconciler entry point that scans only journal-defined recoverable stages within immutable batch/time limits.\\n\\nFor each candidate:\\n\\n- Reread current authority.\\n- Determine whether an external result is safely queryable.\\n- Resume only idempotent effects or effects protected by an accepted attempt token.\\n- CAS against the exact observed version/stage.\\n- Treat a lost CAS as benign concurrency, then reread.\\n- Never “repair” ambiguity by assuming success.\\n- Never make reclaim eligible while any prior effect is unresolved.\\n\\nThe coordinator should serialize per-replica work logically, but correctness must depend on journal CAS rather than process-local locking.\\n\\n## 8. Integration points to locate on current `main`\\n\\nBefore writing code, identify the exact existing entry points for:\\n\\n1. Broker request ingestion and authentication.\\n2. The three accepted store constructors/public APIs.\\n3. Journal stage/version/CAS and recovery-query methods.\\n4. Artifact-store put/open/delete semantics.\\n5. Publication-store idempotency and conflict semantics.\\n6. Broker launch lifecycle v2.\\n7. Legacy v1 routing.\\n8. Launcher/executor request and result types.\\n9. Workspace admission policy and platform detection.\\n10. Root protocol action validation and `reclaim` client.\\n11. Existing configuration and feature-gate conventions.\\n12. Test fixtures for restart, cancellation, SQLite locking, and protocol compatibility.\\n\\nIf any accepted store lacks the required intent/result CAS capability, stop and propose the smallest API addition rather than bypassing it with coordinator-owned authority.\\n\\n## 9. Test plan\\n\\nAdd focused coordinator tests with injected deterministic effects.\\n\\nCore success:\\n\\n- Ingest → verify → publish → managed-Linux admission → launch.\\n- Launch → graceful drain → exactly-three export acknowledgment → eligibility → existing root reclaim.\\n- Restart/reconciliation from every pending stage.\\n- Duplicate delivery is idempotent.\\n\\nSafety and unresolved behavior:\\n\\n- Verification mismatch and verifier ambiguity.\\n- Publication failure and unknown commit.\\n- Unknown transport.\\n- Native Darwin rejection under every gate combination.\\n- Admission without verification.\\n- Drain timeout/cancellation.\\n- Live units after drain.\\n- Export returns 0, 1, 2, 4, duplicates, malformed, or non-external references.\\n- Missing, invalid, stale, replayed, or wrong-key acknowledgment.\\n- Export and journal commit ambiguity.\\n- Reclaim response timeout or cancellation.\\n- CAS races at every effect boundary.\\n- Broker restart between effect completion and result CAS.\\n- No reclaim while any stage is unresolved.\\n\\nProtocol compatibility:\\n\\n- Root accepted actions remain exactly `prepare`, `launch`, `reclaim`.\\n- No new root wire messages or action aliases.\\n- Existing launch lifecycle v2 golden tests remain unchanged.\\n- Existing legacy v1 golden tests remain unchanged.\\n\\nStorage discipline:\\n\\n- Instrumented tests assert no SQLite handle/transaction remains open during injected effects or awaits.\\n- Artifact bytes never appear in journal/publication SQLite rows.\\n- Journal and publication receive the same limits-profile identity and broker keyring configuration.\\n- Every gate defaults disabled and is independent, preferably with a parameterized gate matrix.\\n\\n## 10. Suggested implementation order\\n\\n1. Confirm current APIs and capture compatibility tests before edits.\\n2. Add coordinator types, injected effect interfaces, and gate configuration.\\n3. Implement ingest/verify/publication using read-copy-close/effect/reopen-CAS.\\n4. Integrate fail-closed admission and existing launch v2 without touching v1.\\n5. Add drain and bounded exactly-three export processing.\\n6. Add authenticated broker acknowledgment and reclaim eligibility.\\n7. Call only existing root `reclaim`.\\n8. Add restart reconciliation and concurrency tests.\\n9. Run focused tests, SQLite-handle instrumentation, protocol goldens, then the complete suite.\\n\\nThe main review invariant is simple: reclaim must be impossible unless the journal durably proves a definite drain, zero live units, and an authenticated acknowledgment containing exactly three valid external artifact references.\"}"}],"details":{"server":"repoprompt","tool":"context_builder"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789259752862}}
{"type":"message","id":"69295fe7","parentId":"3bedfaa2","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:36:09.681Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Launching five read-only scouts for APIs**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5efee621887d08da34684aa50a2e6\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Launching five read-only scouts for APIs**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9wVQBLCTheEMo8Rt0mNcymgt|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5eff0672887d092cab1b1b760f233","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"const tasks=[['journal','Inspect current BrokerReplicaJournal API and exact stage semantics for a coordinator. Report usable methods, return types, idempotency/CAS behavior, restart handling, and smallest required additions. Read only.'],['stores','Inspect BrokerArtifactStore and WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore current APIs. Map how coordinator can convert signed payload to manifest/declaration, stream ingest, pin external bytes for verification, and publish. Report gaps. Read only.'],['broker','Inspect broker_runtime.py, broker_protocol.py, broker_journal.py, execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, root_launcher.py, and relay. Map exact integration points for replica requests without altering lifecycle v2, legacy v1, or root actions. Read only.'],['execution','Inspect workspace_admission.py, workspace_execution.py, workspace_isolation.py, launcher client, and relevant settings. Determine exact verified managed-Linux admission, graceful drain, live-unit query, export acknowledgment, and reclaim interfaces. Report missing interfaces. Read only.'],['tests','Inspect current tests and configuration for broker replica lifecycle gates, coordinator test patterns, fake effects, SQLite-handle checks, restart, cancellation, and root protocol action assertions. Propose exact new test file structure and fixtures. Read only.']]; return runs.all(tasks.map(([key,task])=>({key,agent:'scout',task})))","async":false,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","timeoutMs":900000,"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":5,"graceTurns":1},"toolBudget":{"soft":20,"hard":30,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"]},"chatProgress":"auto"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":3476,"output":411,"cacheRead":205056,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":52,"totalTokens":208943,"cost":{"input":0.017380000000000003,"output":0.01233,"cacheRead":0.102528,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.132238}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789259752901,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5efe9d9b487d099bab5434fda6cfd","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"0846ce58","parentId":"69295fe7","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:43:54.120Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9wVQBLCTheEMo8Rt0mNcymgt|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5eff0672887d092cab1b1b760f233","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"journal\",\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"runId\": \"bf54b4a3\",\n    \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 5 assistant turns (soft limit 5, grace 1). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nThe response did not pass the STE check. Pi requested a new response.\",\n    \"artifactPaths\": [\n      \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/bf54b4a3/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n    ],\n    \"results\": [\n      {\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"agent\": \"scout\",\n        \"task\": \"Inspect current BrokerReplicaJournal API and exact stage semantics for a coordinator. Report usable methods, return types, idempotency/CAS behavior, restart handling, and smallest required additions. Read only.\",\n        \"routingContract\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"agent\": \"scout\",\n          \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3\",\n          \"thinking\": \"high\",\n          \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n        },\n        \"launchContractDigest\": \"b62fd508cc1acda133692f596ea82f3dd054cc037f04dc00966e424fe6f5ba0f\",\n        \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n          \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n          \"runtime\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n          ],\n          \"configured\": [],\n          \"effective\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n          ],\n          \"omitted\": {\n            \"runtime\": 0,\n            \"configured\": 0,\n            \"effective\": 0\n          }\n        },\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"outputState\": \"present\",\n        \"usage\": {\n          \"input\": 36809,\n          \"output\": 4492,\n          \"cacheRead\": 409023,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n          \"cost\": 0,\n          \"turns\": 14\n        },\n        \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\",\n        \"thinking\": \"high\",\n        \"artifactPaths\": {\n          \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/bf54b4a3_scout_0_input.md\",\n          \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/bf54b4a3_scout_0_output.md\",\n          \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/bf54b4a3_scout_0.jsonl\",\n          \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/bf54b4a3_scout_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n          \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/bf54b4a3_scout_0_meta.json\"\n        },\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/bf54b4a3_scout_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n        \"turnBudget\": {\n          \"maxTurns\": 5,\n          \"graceTurns\": 1,\n          \"turnCount\": 14,\n          \"outcome\": \"wrap-up-requested\",\n          \"wrapUpRequestedAtTurn\": 5\n        },\n        \"toolBudget\": {\n          \"hard\": 30,\n          \"soft\": 20,\n          \"block\": [\n            \"read\",\n            \"grep\",\n            \"find\",\n            \"ls\"\n          ],\n          \"toolCount\": 20,\n          \"outcome\": \"soft-reached\",\n          \"softReachedAt\": 20\n        },\n        \"context\": \"fresh\",\n        \"wrapUpRequested\": true,\n        \"progressSummary\": {\n          \"toolCount\": 20,\n          \"tokens\": 41301,\n          \"durationMs\": 463009\n        },\n        \"effects\": {\n          \"fileMutation\": {\n            \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n            \"expected\": false,\n            \"attempted\": false\n          }\n        },\n        \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n        \"finalOutput\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 5 assistant turns (soft limit 5, grace 1). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nThe response did not pass the STE check. Pi requested a new response.\",\n        \"controlEvents\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"ts\": 1789260011034,\n            \"runId\": \"bf54b4a3\",\n            \"agent\": \"scout\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": \"scout is still active but long-running\",\n            \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n            \"turns\": 9,\n            \"tokens\": 38187,\n            \"toolCount\": 16,\n            \"currentTool\": \"bash\",\n            \"currentToolDurationMs\": 6197,\n            \"currentPath\": \"&1\",\n            \"elapsedMs\": 240766\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"needs_attention\",\n            \"from\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"to\": \"needs_attention\",\n            \"ts\": 1789260074435,\n            \"runId\": \"bf54b4a3\",\n            \"agent\": \"scout\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": \"scout needs attention (no observed activity for 60s)\",\n            \"reason\": \"idle\",\n            \"turns\": 9,\n            \"tokens\": 38187,\n            \"toolCount\": 16,\n            \"elapsedMs\": 60024\n          }\n        ],\n        \"attemptedModels\": [\n          \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\"\n        ],\n        \"modelAttempts\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\",\n            \"success\": true,\n            \"exitCode\": 0,\n            \"usage\": {\n              \"input\": 36809,\n              \"output\": 4492,\n              \"cacheRead\": 409023,\n              \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n              \"cost\": 0,\n              \"turns\": 14\n            }\n          }\n        ],\n        \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/bf54b4a3/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n        \"acceptance\": {\n          \"status\": \"rejected\",\n          \"evidenceStatus\": \"rejected\",\n          \"explicit\": false,\n          \"effectiveAcceptance\": {\n            \"level\": \"attested\",\n            \"explicit\": false,\n            \"inferredReason\": [\n              \"read-only/reviewer-style agent\"\n            ],\n            \"criteria\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n                \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n                \"evidence\": [\n                  \"review-findings\",\n                  \"residual-risks\"\n                ],\n                \"severity\": \"required\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"evidence\": [\n              \"review-findings\",\n              \"residual-risks\"\n            ],\n            \"verify\": [],\n            \"stopRules\": []\n          },\n          \"inferredReason\": [\n            \"read-only/reviewer-style agent\"\n          ],\n          \"criteria\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": [\n                \"review-findings\",\n                \"residual-risks\"\n              ],\n              \"severity\": \"required\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"runtimeChecks\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"attestation\",\n              \"status\": \"failed\",\n              \"message\": \"Structured acceptance report not found.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"verifyRuns\": [],\n          \"childReportParseError\": \"Structured acceptance report not found.\"\n        },\n        \"toolCalls\": [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"limit...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"limit\\\":50}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*BrokerReplicaJournal*\\\"}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*BrokerReplicaJournal*\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*replica*journal*\\\"}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*replica*journal*\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"class FaultJournal\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"class FaultJournal\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\\\",\\\"context\\\":30}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def (drive|complete|signed_r...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def (drive|complete|signed_request|request_payload|response_frame)\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\\\",\\\"context\\\":15}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"from.*broker_replica_journal...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"from.*broker_replica_journal|import.*BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"limit\\\":20}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"path\\\"...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/services\\\",\\\"limit\\\":20}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"broker_replica_journal\\\",\\\"pat...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"broker_replica_journal\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"limit\\\":30}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"path\\\"...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests\\\",\\\"limit\\\":5}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/t...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -q --tb=no 2>&1 | tail -5\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/t...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py --tb=short 2>&1 | tail -20\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/t...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py --tb=short 2>&1\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/t...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && python -m pytest backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py --tb=long 2>&1 | head -60\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && python -c \\\"import ...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && python -c \\\"import tests.test_broker_replica_journal\\\" 2>&1 | head -30\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/broker_protocol*\\\"}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/broker_protocol*\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"key\": \"stores\",\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"runId\": \"ce15eec9\",\n    \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 5 assistant turns (soft limit 5, grace 1). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Inspection Report\\n\\n### File Locations\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` — BrokerArtifactStore (761 lines)\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py` — WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore (585+ lines)\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py` — parse_signed_request, create_signed_request, BrokerRequest\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py` — ArtifactReference, IngestReceipt, VerifyReceipt, PublishReceipt\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Signed Payload to Manifest/Declaration Conversion\\n\\n**Broker side:** `parse_signed_request(frame, public_key)` in `broker_protocol.py` returns `BrokerRequest` with a `payload: dict[str, JsonValue]`. The payload is a flat dict with keys: `artifact_set_sha256`, `bundle`, `index_objects`, `limits_sha256`, `object_format`, `reconciliation_fingerprint`, `repository_id`, `source_state_sha256`, `workspace_id`, `worktree`. Each artifact key is a dict with `artifact_id`, `sha256`, `byte_length`.\\n\\n**BrokerArtifactStore path:** `receive(manifest, reader)` consumes a `ReplicaArtifactManifest` (dataclass wrapping three `ArtifactReference` objects + `operation_id`). No conversion from `BrokerRequest.payload` to `ReplicaArtifactManifest` exists in this file. Caller must construct `ReplicaArtifactManifest` manually.\\n\\n**WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore path:** `verify_artifact_set(declaration, bundle_bytes, worktree_bytes, index_object_bytes)` consumes `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration` (dataclass with `version`, `operation_id`, `repository_id`, `workspace_id`, `identity`, `object_format`, `source_state_sha256`, `reconciliation_fingerprint`, three `ReplicaArtifactBinding` objects, `limits`).\\n\\n**Gap (High):** No adapter between `BrokerRequest.payload` and `ReplicaArtifactManifest`. No adapter between `BrokerRequest.payload` and `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration`. The `BrokerRequest.payload` lacks `identity` (ReplicaIdentity with physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id). The journal layer handles authority_claimed separately. Coordinator must bridge signed request payload → `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration` externally.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Stream Ingest\\n\\n**BrokerArtifactStore.receive():** Takes `ReplicaArtifactManifest` + `asyncio.StreamReader`. Reads exactly three artifacts in fixed order (bundle, worktree, index_objects) using chunked reads with `idle_timeout_seconds` and `transfer_timeout_seconds`. Digests each artifact inline via SHA-256, writes to disk, verifies digest matches declaration, rejects trailing bytes. Returns `IngestReceipt`.\\n\\n**Key details:**\\n- Creates a `.{operation_id}.pending.{random}` directory under the root.\\n- Uses `O_EXCL` for atomic file creation.\\n- Calls `atomic_rename_no_replace` to publish from pending to final.\\n- Quarantines pending on any failure path via `_quarantine_pending`.\\n- Uses `fcntl.flock` + asyncio lock for reservation.\\n\\n**Gap (Medium):** `receive()` takes `asyncio.StreamReader` — the caller must supply the transport. No built-in wire protocol handler. The `broker_protocol.py` frame limit is 64KB but artifact bytes flow through the socket reader directly, bypassing frame limits. This is intentional but means the coordinator must handle the transport layer.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Pin External Bytes for Verification\\n\\n**WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set():** Takes three `bytes` objects (`bundle_bytes`, `worktree_bytes`, `index_object_bytes`) + `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration`. Matches each against declaration via `_match_content()` (verifies length + SHA-256 digest). Then decodes worktree, verifies committed bundle, verifies index object pack. Rechecks HEAD consistency. Returns `ReplicaVerificationReceipt`.\\n\\n**BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming() / inspect_incoming():** Opens already-stored artifacts from disk, re-reads and re-hashes them, returns `IngestReceipt`. Used after `receive()` to confirm durability.\\n\\n**Gap (Medium):** `verify_artifact_set()` loads all three artifacts entirely into memory. For a 1GB set, this means 3GB peak RSS (plus decoded data). The `_PinnedRegular` internal class in the publication store also reads full content into memory. No streaming verification path exists. Large bundles will OOM.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Publish Flow\\n\\n**WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set():**\\n1. Calls `verify_artifact_set()` — in-memory verification.\\n2. Validates declaration against ceilings.\\n3. Creates `.{operation_id}.pending.{random}` directory.\\n4. Writes four files: bundle, worktree, index_objects, `artifact-set.json` (containing canonical JSON of declaration + verification).\\n5. Reinspects all written files (identity + content re-read).\\n6. Calls `atomic_rename_no_replace` to publish.\\n7. Calls `_inspect_final()` to verify the published state (re-reads, re-verifies).\\n8. Returns `ReplicaPublicationReceipt` with synchronization receipt.\\n\\n**BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts():** Scans root for pending attempts, quarantines them. Verifies final named sets against journal manifests. Returns `ArtifactReconciliationResult` per entry with states: `incoming_verified`, `unverified_final_present`, `unjournaled_present`, `pending_quarantined`, `conflict_quarantined`, `retained_foreign`, `unresolved`.\\n\\n**Gap (High):** `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` and `BrokerArtifactStore` are separate stores with different root directories, different data models, and no shared API. They do not compose. The coordinator must:\\n1. Use `BrokerArtifactStore.receive()` to ingest bytes from the wire into broker-owned storage.\\n2. Use `BrokerArtifactStore.inspect_incoming()` to get `IngestReceipt`.\\n3. Somehow extract bytes from broker storage to feed into `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set()` (which needs raw bytes in memory, not disk paths).\\n4. Then call `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set()` to publish into its own root.\\n\\nNo bridge method exists. The `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming()` yields file descriptors — bytes would need to be read from disk (blocking I/O) into memory. The publication store does not accept file descriptors or paths.\\n\\n**Gap (High):** `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration` requires `limits` matching `ReplicaStoreLimits` exactly (via `_validate_declaration`). The `BrokerArtifactStore` uses `BrokerArtifactLimits` with different field names (`max_bundle_bytes` vs `bundle.max_bundle_bytes`). No conversion exists. Limits profiles are not interoperable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Gaps Summary\\n\\n| Severity | Gap | Location |\\n|----------|-----|----------|\\n| **High** | No bridge from `BrokerArtifactStore` disk storage to `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` in-memory verification. Bytes must be read from disk then loaded entirely into memory. | Between the two stores |\\n| **High** | No conversion from `BrokerRequest.payload` (signed wire format) to `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration`. Missing `ReplicaIdentity`. | broker_protocol.py → workspace_replica_publication.py |\\n| **High** | No conversion from `BrokerRequest.payload` to `ReplicaArtifactManifest`. Requires manual construction. | broker_protocol.py → broker_artifact_store.py |\\n| **High** | `BrokerArtifactLimits` and `ReplicaStoreLimits` are structurally different. No mapping. | Limits comparison |\\n| **Medium** | `verify_artifact_set()` causes whole-set memory amplification (~3x for 3 artifacts). No streaming path. | workspace_replica_publication.py |\\n| **Medium** | `receive()` requires caller to supply `asyncio.StreamReader`. No built-in socket/frame handler. | broker_artifact_store.py |\\n| **Low** | `_validate_declaration` checks `declaration.limits != ceilings` — requires exact equality. Tight coupling between declaration and store configuration. | workspace_replica_publication.py |\\n| **Low** | `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration.version` is hardcoded to `Literal[2]`. No forward compat. | workspace_replica_publication.py |\\n\\n---\",\n    \"artifactPaths\": [\n      \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ce15eec9/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n    ],\n    \"results\": [\n      {\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"agent\": \"scout\",\n        \"task\": \"Inspect BrokerArtifactStore and WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore current APIs. Map how coordinator can convert signed payload to manifest/declaration, stream ingest, pin external bytes for verification, and publish. Report gaps. Read only.\",\n        \"routingContract\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"agent\": \"scout\",\n          \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3\",\n          \"thinking\": \"high\",\n          \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n        },\n        \"launchContractDigest\": \"6bede6f4dd34ff52bb1682b633573fa6d316b10a84fc9bc8e262fd09f5614324\",\n        \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n          \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n          \"runtime\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n          ],\n          \"configured\": [],\n          \"effective\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n          ],\n          \"omitted\": {\n            \"runtime\": 0,\n            \"configured\": 0,\n            \"effective\": 0\n          }\n        },\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"outputState\": \"present\",\n        \"usage\": {\n          \"input\": 147234,\n          \"output\": 3841,\n          \"cacheRead\": 412272,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n          \"cost\": 0,\n          \"turns\": 11\n        },\n        \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\",\n        \"thinking\": \"high\",\n        \"artifactPaths\": {\n          \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ce15eec9_scout_0_input.md\",\n          \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ce15eec9_scout_0_output.md\",\n          \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ce15eec9_scout_0.jsonl\",\n          \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ce15eec9_scout_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n          \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ce15eec9_scout_0_meta.json\"\n        },\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/y