{"type":"message","id":"3d2233b3","parentId":"266caa55","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:47:44.299Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Delegating design to worker-expert**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f2a3cbb487d0a84007dab6167db4\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Delegating design to worker-expert**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_uPYuznt9lJlD1Aay5gacl3v3|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f2a6c1d887d099acf317f778ba51","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"const task=['Design exact implementation for broker replica lifecycle coordinator on current checkout. Read only.','Inspect current BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerArtifactStore, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, broker_runtime, execution_broker, workspace_admission, workspace_execution, workspace_isolation, execution_daemons, root_launcher, and tests.','Required fixed stages: ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal is sole authority. No SQLite handle crosses await or external effect. Unknown outcomes are stage-specific unresolved. Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or live unit blocks reclaim. Export returns exactly three external references. Root actions stay prepare, launch, reclaim. Native Darwin stays fail-closed. Gates stay independently disabled.','Resolve exact module boundaries, effect protocols, data adapters, deadline behavior, and smallest required additions to existing APIs. Identify which effects do not exist and propose injected interfaces without inventing production support.','Return implementation-ready method signatures, transition pseudocode, test cases, and escalation questions. Do not modify files.'].join('\\n'); return runs.run('coordinator-design', {agent:'worker-expert', task, reads:['backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py','backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py','backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py','backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py'], acceptance:false})","async":false,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","timeoutMs":1200000,"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":8,"graceTurns":2},"toolBudget":{"soft":30,"hard":50,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"]},"chatProgress":"auto"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":301,"output":511,"cacheRead":245632,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":89,"totalTokens":246444,"cost":{"input":0.001505,"output":0.01533,"cacheRead":0.122816,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.139651}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789260445598,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f29fd93087d0920b911b41b2f171","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a12047aa","parentId":"3d2233b3","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:51:31.460Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_uPYuznt9lJlD1Aay5gacl3v3|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f2a6c1d887d099acf317f778ba51","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"coordinator-design\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"ac665022\",\n  \"output\": \"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\\n\\n## Current causal account\\n\\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\\n\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\\n\\nNo coordinator connects them.\\n\\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\\n\\nMissing production effects:\\n\\n- Application-owned replica admission.\\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\\n- Post-drain workspace export.\\n- Export destination storage.\\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\\n\\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\\n\\n## Required ownership\\n\\n| State | Sole owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\\n| Exported object references | External export store |\\n\\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\\n\\n## Allowed transitions\\n\\n```text\\naccepted\\n  -> authority_claimed\\n  -> ingest_started\\n  -> ingest_completed\\n  -> verify_started\\n  -> verify_completed\\n  -> publish_started\\n  -> publish_completed\\n  -> admission_started\\n  -> admission_completed\\n  -> drain_started\\n  -> drain_completed\\n  -> export_started\\n  -> export_completed\\n  -> reclaim_started\\n  -> reclaim_completed\\n```\\n\\nAny active stage may instead become:\\n\\n```text\\nstage_rejected(stage, stable_reason)\\nstage_unresolved(stage, stable_reason)\\n```\\n\\nBoth outcomes are terminal under current journal semantics.\\n\\nInvalid transitions:\\n\\n- Skipping any stage.\\n- Replacing claimed authority.\\n- Completing without a matching start.\\n- Completing with a conflicting receipt.\\n- Retrying an unresolved lifecycle.\\n- Admitting before publication.\\n- Exporting before confirmed drain.\\n- Reclaiming before export.\\n- Reclaiming without a drain acknowledgment.\\n- Reclaiming while root observes a unit, cgroup member, or runtime directory.\\n\\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` already enforces order, receipt equality, authority binding, and exact replay.\\n\\n## New coordinator module\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n```text\\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\\n```\\n\\nKeep journal serialization and SQLite details inside `broker_replica_journal.py`.\\n\\n### Core types\\n\\n```python\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom typing import Generic, Literal, Protocol, TypeVar\\n\\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import BrokerRequest\\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\\n    AdmissionReceipt,\\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\\n    DrainReceipt,\\n    ExportReceipt,\\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\\n    IngestReceipt,\\n    PublishReceipt,\\n    ReclaimReceipt,\\n    ReplicaAuthority,\\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\\n    VerifyReceipt,\\n)\\n\\nReplicaStage = Literal[\\n    \\\"ingest\\\",\\n    \\\"verify\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\",\\n    \\\"admission\\\",\\n    \\\"drain\\\",\\n    \\\"export\\\",\\n    \\\"reclaim\\\",\\n]\\n\\nStageReceipt = (\\n    IngestReceipt\\n    | VerifyReceipt\\n    | PublishReceipt\\n    | AdmissionReceipt\\n    | DrainReceipt\\n    | ExportReceipt\\n    | ReclaimReceipt\\n)\\n\\nR = TypeVar(\\\"R\\\", bound=StageReceipt)\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\\n    request: BrokerRequest\\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\\n    owner_token: str\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass StageReconciliation(Generic[R]):\\n    outcome: Literal[\\\"completed\\\", \\\"not_applied\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"]\\n    receipt: R | None\\n\\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\\n        if (self.outcome == \\\"completed\\\") != (self.receipt is not None):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"reconciliation receipt does not match outcome\\\")\\n```\\n\\n### Effect protocol\\n\\nUse one typed effect per stage. This prevents force-drain flags or arbitrary stage dispatch.\\n\\n```python\\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol[R]):\\n    async def apply(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> R: ...\\n\\n    async def reconcile(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[R]: ...\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ReplicaLifecycleEffects:\\n    ingest: ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]\\n    verify: ReplicaStageEffect[VerifyReceipt]\\n    publish: ReplicaStageEffect[PublishReceipt]\\n    admission: ReplicaStageEffect[AdmissionReceipt]\\n    drain: ReplicaStageEffect[DrainReceipt]\\n    export: ReplicaStageEffect[ExportReceipt]\\n    reclaim: ReplicaStageEffect[ReclaimReceipt]\\n```\\n\\nDo not provide default effects. Missing effects must block construction.\\n\\n### Coordinator signature\\n\\n```python\\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\\n    def __init__(\\n        self,\\n        *,\\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\\n        effects: ReplicaLifecycleEffects,\\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float,\\n        monotonic: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic,\\n    ) -> None: ...\\n\\n    async def execute(\\n        self,\\n        request: BrokerRequest,\\n        request_frame: bytes,\\n        *,\\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\\n        owner_token: str,\\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\\n\\n    async def recover(\\n        self,\\n        lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\\n\\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> tuple[ReplicaJournalDecision, ...]: ...\\n```\\n\\n`execute` accepts immutable request data only. Artifact readers belong inside injected ingest effect adapters.\\n\\n## Transition pseudocode\\n\\n```python\\nasync def execute(...):\\n    decision = journal.accept(request, request_frame=request_frame)\\n\\n    if decision is terminal or completed:\\n        return decision\\n\\n    journal.claim_authority(\\n        request,\\n        owner_token=owner_token,\\n        authority=authority,\\n    )\\n\\n    context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(request, authority, owner_token)\\n\\n    for stage in FIXED_REPLICA_STAGES:\\n        decision = journal.status(request)\\n\\n        if decision is terminal:\\n            return decision\\n\\n        if stage is already completed:\\n            continue\\n\\n        journal.begin_stage(\\n            request,\\n            owner_token=owner_token,\\n            stage=stage,\\n        )\\n\\n        deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\\n\\n        try:\\n            receipt = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\\n                effect_for(stage).apply(context, deadline=deadline),\\n                deadline,\\n            )\\n        except StageRejected as error:\\n            journal.record_rejected(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                receipt=RejectedReceipt(reason_code=error.reason_code),\\n            )\\n            return journal.status(request)\\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\\n            journal.record_unresolved(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                reason=\\\"cancelled_unknown\\\",\\n            )\\n            raise\\n        except TimeoutError:\\n            journal.record_unresolved(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                reason=\\\"timeout_unknown\\\",\\n            )\\n            return journal.status(request)\\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as error:\\n            journal.record_unresolved(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                reason=error.reason_code,\\n            )\\n            return journal.status(request)\\n\\n        complete_stage(journal, request, owner_token, stage, receipt)\\n\\n    return journal.status(request)\\n```\\n\\n`complete_stage` must use existing typed methods:\\n\\n```python\\njournal.complete_ingest(...)\\njournal.complete_verify(...)\\njournal.complete_publish(...)\\njournal.complete_admission(...)\\njournal.complete_drain(...)\\njournal.complete_export(...)\\njournal.complete_reclaim(...)\\n```\\n\\nNever open a journal database around `await`. Every journal call must finish before an effect begins.\\n\\n### Recovery pseudocode\\n\\n```python\\nasync def recover(lifecycle):\\n    context = context_from_incomplete_lifecycle(lifecycle)\\n    stage = lifecycle.active_stage\\n    effect = effect_for(stage)\\n    deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\\n\\n    try:\\n        result = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\\n            effect.reconcile(context, deadline=deadline),\\n            deadline,\\n        )\\n    except BaseException classified as unknown:\\n        journal.record_unresolved(\\n            context.request,\\n            owner_token=context.owner_token,\\n            stage=stage,\\n            reason=\\\"recovery_unknown\\\",\\n        )\\n        return journal.status(context.request)\\n\\n    if result.outcome == \\\"completed\\\":\\n        complete_stage(..., result.receipt)\\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\\n\\n    if result.outcome == \\\"not_applied\\\":\\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\\n\\n    journal.record_unresolved(\\n        context.request,\\n        owner_token=context.owner_token,\\n        stage=stage,\\n        reason=\\\"recovery_unknown\\\",\\n    )\\n    return journal.status(context.request)\\n```\\n\\nA late result after timeout must never complete the journal. Reconciliation handles any later observable external state.\\n\\n## Existing adapters\\n\\n### Ingest adapter\\n\\n`BrokerArtifactStore` can support ingest.\\n\\nAdapter responsibilities:\\n\\n1. Decode the validated manifest from authenticated request payload.\\n2. Validate exactly three distinct roles.\\n3. Call `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(...)`.\\n4. Return its `IngestReceipt`.\\n5. Use `reconcile_attempts(...)` after a crash.\\n6. Return `unknown` for ambiguous pending or quarantine state.\\n\\nDo not retain `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` across journal calls.\\n\\n### Verify adapter\\n\\nUse:\\n\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async(...)`\\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set(...)`\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.recheck_opened_async(...)`\\n\\nRequired sequence:\\n\\n```text\\nopen incoming\\nverify bytes\\nrecheck same opened identities\\nclose every descriptor\\nreturn VerifyReceipt\\n```\\n\\nThe adapter must map publication bindings to journal `ArtifactReference` values without changing IDs, hashes, roles, media types, or lengths.\\n\\nA replacement during verification is rejection or unresolved according to existing store exceptions.\\n\\n### Publish adapter\\n\\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set(...)`.\\n\\nRecovery uses `inspect_published_artifact_set(...)`.\\n\\nConvert `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` or publication receipt into journal `PublishReceipt`. Preserve:\\n\\n- Physical target ID.\\n- Replica generation.\\n- Execution owner ID.\\n- Artifact set digest.\\n- Source state digest.\\n- Publication receipt ID.\\n\\nA post-rename failure remains unresolved unless inspection establishes exact completion.\\n\\n### Reclaim adapter\\n\\nUse existing `LauncherClient.reclaim(operation_id)`.\\n\\nDo not add `stop`, `drain`, `export`, or delete actions to root protocol.\\n\\nMap only exact result:\\n\\n```text\\nstatus == \\\"reclaimed\\\" and error is None\\n```\\n\\nto `ReclaimReceipt`.\\n\\nThese results are not success:\\n\\n- Missing reply.\\n- Timeout.\\n- Clean EOF.\\n- Malformed reply.\\n- Wrong action.\\n- Transport reset.\\n- `reclaim_disabled`.\\n- Root quiescence rejection.\\n\\nUnknown transport outcomes become unresolved. Explicit rejection becomes rejected.\\n\\nRoot already checks unit absence, empty cgroup, and runtime absence before deletion.\\n\\n## Missing injected effects\\n\\n### Admission\\n\\nCurrent `acquire_prompt_workspace(...)` is unsuitable. It depends on FastAPI request state and application SQLite ownership.\\n\\nAdd an application-owned boundary later:\\n\\n```python\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ReplicaAdmissionCommand:\\n    operation_id: str\\n    physical_target_id: str\\n    replica_generation: int\\n    execution_owner_id: str\\n    publication_receipt_id: str\\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\\n\\n\\nclass ReplicaAdmissionClient(Protocol):\\n    async def admit(\\n        self,\\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> AdmissionReceipt: ...\\n\\n    async def inspect(\\n        self,\\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[AdmissionReceipt]: ...\\n```\\n\\nNo SQLite connection may leave application-owned methods. Only immutable DTOs may cross transport.\\n\\nAdmission must invoke `require_isolated_execution(...)` before reservation, Git work, credentials, or provider access.\\n\\n### Graceful drain\\n\\nNo current graceful drain protocol exists.\\n\\n```python\\nclass GracefulReplicaDrainClient(Protocol):\\n    async def request_drain(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> DrainReceipt: ...\\n\\n    async def inspect_acknowledgement(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[DrainReceipt]: ...\\n```\\n\\nDo not include `force`, `signal`, `kill`, or `systemctl stop` options.\\n\\nAcknowledgment must bind:\\n\\n- Operation ID.\\n- Physical target ID.\\n- Replica generation.\\n- Execution owner ID.\\n- Drain request ID.\\n\\nMissing acknowledgment is unresolved. It must block export and reclaim.\\n\\n### Export\\n\\nNo current broker-side post-drain export exists.\\n\\n```python\\nclass ReplicaExportClient(Protocol):\\n    async def export(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> ExportReceipt: ...\\n\\n    async def inspect(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[ExportReceipt]: ...\\n```\\n\\n`ExportReceipt` must contain exactly three external references:\\n\\n1. `committed_bundle`\\n2. `worktree`\\n3. `index_objects`\\n\\nReject duplicate IDs, missing roles, extra roles, local paths, or inline bytes.\\n\\nExisting bundle, worktree, and object-pack builders may support a future executor-side implementation. They are not a broker export transport.\\n\\n## Smallest existing API additions\\n\\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\\n\\nNo transition API change appears necessary.\\n\\nAdd accessors only if `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` does not expose these values:\\n\\n```python\\nrequest: BrokerRequest\\nauthority: ReplicaAuthority\\nowner_token: str\\nactive_stage: ReplicaStage\\n```\\n\\nDo not expose SQLite connections, cursors, or row objects.\\n\\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\\n\\nNo ingest API change is required.\\n\\nA deletion API needs a separate retention decision. Do not silently remove incoming artifacts during root reclaim.\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nNo verify or publish API change is required.\\n\\nA published-set deletion API also needs a retention decision.\\n\\n### `execution_broker.py`\\n\\nKeep `LauncherClient` methods fixed:\\n\\n```python\\nasync def prepare(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\\nasync def launch(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\\nasync def reclaim(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\\n```\\n\\nAdd replica request dispatch only after request protocol approval.\\n\\n### `broker_runtime.py`\\n\\nDo not treat runtime directory cleanup as graceful drain acknowledgment. No safe drain API exists here.\\n\\n### `execution_daemons.py`\\n\\nLater wiring must:\\n\\n- Construct replica journal separately from broker launch journal.\\n- Construct coordinator only when every effect exists.\\n- Recover before accepting connections.\\n- Keep launch, prepare, reclaim, and replica lifecycle gates independent.\\n- Preserve current nested deadline invariant.\\n- Log stable reason codes only.\\n\\n### `root_launcher.py`\\n\\nNo action changes.\\n\\nActions remain exactly:\\n\\n```text\\nprepare\\nlaunch\\nreclaim\\n```\\n\\n### Darwin isolation\\n\\nDo not weaken `workspace_isolation.py`.\\n\\nNative Darwin execution remains fail-closed. Supported fixtures remain test-only behavior.\\n\\n## Deadline rules\\n\\nUse an absolute monotonic deadline per stage.\\n\\nCurrent nesting must remain:\\n\\n```text\\nroot worker timeout\\n< launcher client timeout\\n< broker effect timeout\\n< connection timeout\\n```\\n\\nRules:\\n\\n- Persist `begin_stage` before starting deadline.\\n- Never reset deadline during retries or response parsing.\\n- Treat timeout as unknown once an effect may have started.\\n- Record unresolved before returning.\\n- On cancellation, synchronously record unresolved, then re-raise.\\n- Discard late task results.\\n- Do not advance after unresolved state.\\n- Startup reconciliation receives a fresh bounded deadline.\\n- Persistence failure remains fail-closed and must escape as journal failure.\\n\\n## Focused tests\\n\\nAdd `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`.\\n\\nRequired cases:\\n\\n1. Executes all seven stages in exact order.\\n2. Starts each stage durably before invoking its effect.\\n3. Completes each stage only after effect return.\\n4. Replays completed lifecycle without effects.\\n5. Resumes from each completed stage.\\n6. Rejects wrong authority before effects.\\n7. Rejects owner-token conflict.\\n8. Never skips a stage.\\n9. Verification rejection records `verify` rejection.\\n10. Publish post-visibility ambiguity records `publish` unresolved.\\n11. Admission timeout records `admission` unresolved.\\n12. Drain cancellation records `drain` unresolved and re-raises.\\n13. Missing drain acknowledgment blocks export.\\n14. Export rejects fewer than three references.\\n15. Export rejects more than three references.\\n16. Export rejects duplicate roles or artifact IDs.\\n17. Reclaim is never called before export completion.\\n18. Root live-unit rejection blocks reclaim completion.\\n19. Reclaim EOF records `reclaim` unresolved.\\n20. No unresolved request invokes an effect on replay.\\n21. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable ingest.\\n22. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable publication.\\n23. Unknown recovery evidence records stage-specific unresolved.\\n24. A late result after timeout cannot append completion.\\n25. Journal methods never execute while effect coroutine is active.\\n26. Startup recovery finishes before listener acceptance.\\n27. Root action set remains exactly three actions.\\n28. Each feature gate remains independently disabled.\\n29. Darwin admission performs no reservation or credential access.\\n30. Logs contain stable codes and omit paths, payloads, keys, and exception text.\\n\\n## Rejected alternatives\\n\\n- Reusing broker launch journal is invalid. Its stages are `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`.\\n- Adding root `stop` or `export` actions violates fixed root protocol tests.\\n- Treating runtime cleanup as drain acknowledgment provides no graceful executor acknowledgment.\\n- Using publication inspection as journal authority violates sole-authority requirement.\\n- Retrying unknown effects can duplicate admission, export, or reclaim effects.\\n- Holding application SQLite across broker calls violates process ownership and await boundaries.\\n- Enabling replica lifecycle through existing launch gate couples independent controls.\\n- Darwin local execution fallback violates current fail-closed isolation behavior.\\n\\n## Escalation questions\\n\\nProduct or architecture approval is required for these decisions:\\n\\n1. What authenticated request types start or continue replica lifecycle?\\n2. Which payload owns manifest, declaration, authority, and export destination?\\n3. What service owns durable admission acknowledgment?\\n4. What executor protocol defines graceful drain acknowledgment?\\n5. Where do exported artifacts live, and who signs their references?\\n6. Should root reclaim also trigger broker incoming or publication cleanup?\\n7. What retention applies after rejected or unresolved stages?\\n8. May operators resolve terminal unresolved states, or must they create a new generation?\\n9. What stage deadlines and byte limits become supported configuration?\\n10. Should startup block all broker traffic when one lifecycle cannot reconcile?\\n\\n## Report\\n\\nChanged files: none.\\n\\nCommands run:\\n\\n- Repository instruction reads.\\n- Source and focused test inspection.\\n- `git status --short`.\\n- `git diff --stat`.\\n\\nTests were not run. Task was read-only.\\n\\nMain remaining risk: admission, drain, and export lack production protocols. Wiring before those contracts exist would create hidden fallback behavior.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ac665022/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"worker-expert\",\n      \"task\": \"[Read from: /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py]\\n\\nDesign exact implementation for broker replica lifecycle coordinator on current checkout. Read only.\\nInspect current BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerArtifactStore, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, broker_runtime, execution_broker, workspace_admission, workspace_execution, workspace_isolation, execution_daemons, root_launcher, and tests.\\nRequired fixed stages: ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal is sole authority. No SQLite handle crosses await or external effect. Unknown outcomes are stage-specific unresolved. Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or live unit blocks reclaim. Export returns exactly three external references. Root actions stay prepare, launch, reclaim. Native Darwin stays fail-closed. Gates stay independently disabled.\\nResolve exact module boundaries, effect protocols, data adapters, deadline behavior, and smallest required additions to existing APIs. Identify which effects do not exist and propose injected interfaces without inventing production support.\\nReturn implementation-ready method signatures, transition pseudocode, test cases, and escalation questions. Do not modify files.\",\n      \"routingContract\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"agent\": \"worker-expert\",\n        \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n        \"thinking\": \"xhigh\",\n        \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n      },\n      \"launchContractDigest\": \"31c900eb14d57f54e67906cd307b7b50b5a70e634e3203588df7a70eb5e23511\",\n      \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n        \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n        \"runtime\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"configured\": [],\n        \"effective\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"omitted\": {\n          \"runtime\": 0,\n          \"configured\": 0,\n          \"effective\": 0\n        }\n      },\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"outputState\": \"present\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"input\": 159270,\n        \"output\": 10929,\n        \"cacheRead\": 119040,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n        \"cost\": 1.18374,\n        \"turns\": 6\n      },\n      \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\",\n      \"thinking\": \"xhigh\",\n      \"artifactPaths\": {\n        \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_input.md\",\n        \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_output.md\",\n        \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0.jsonl\",\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n        \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_meta.json\"\n      },\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n      \"turnBudget\": {\n        \"maxTurns\": 8,\n        \"graceTurns\": 2,\n        \"outcome\": \"within-budget\",\n        \"turnCount\": 6\n      },\n      \"toolBudget\": {\n        \"hard\": 50,\n        \"soft\": 30,\n        \"block\": [\n          \"read\",\n          \"grep\",\n          \"find\",\n          \"ls\"\n        ],\n        \"toolCount\": 37,\n        \"outcome\": \"soft-reached\",\n        \"softReachedAt\": 30\n      },\n      \"context\": \"fresh\",\n      \"progressSummary\": {\n        \"toolCount\": 37,\n        \"tokens\": 170199,\n        \"durationMs\": 225760\n      },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"fileMutation\": {\n          \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n          \"expected\": false,\n          \"attempted\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n      \"finalOutput\": \"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\\n\\n## Current causal account\\n\\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\\n\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\\n\\nNo coordinator connects them.\\n\\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\\n\\nMissing production effects:\\n\\n- Application-owned replica admission.\\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\\n- Post-drain workspace export.\\n- Export destination storage.\\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\\n\\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\\n\\n## Required ownership\\n\\n| State | Sole owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\\n| Exported object references | External export store |\\n\\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\\n\\n## Allowed transitions\\n\\n```text\\naccepted\\n  -> authority_claimed\\n  -> ingest_started\\n  -> ingest_completed\\n  -> verify_started\\n  -> verify_completed\\n  -> publish_started\\n  -> publish_completed\\n  -> admission_started\\n  -> admission_completed\\n  -> drain_started\\n  -> drain_completed\\n  -> export_started\\n  -> export_completed\\n  -> reclaim_started\\n  -> reclaim_completed\\n```\\n\\nAny active stage may instead become:\\n\\n```text\\nstage_rejected(stage, stable_reason)\\nstage_unresolved(stage, stable_reason)\\n```\\n\\nBoth outcomes are terminal under current journal semantics.\\n\\nInvalid transitions:\\n\\n- Skipping any stage.\\n- Replacing claimed authority.\\n- Completing without a matching start.\\n- Completing with a conflicting receipt.\\n- Retrying an unresolved lifecycle.\\n- Admitting before publication.\\n- Exporting before confirmed drain.\\n- Reclaiming before export.\\n- Reclaiming without a drain acknowledgment.\\n- Reclaiming while root observes a unit, cgroup member, or runtime directory.\\n\\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` already enforces order, receipt equality, authority binding, and exact replay.\\n\\n## New coordinator module\\n\\nAdd:\\n\\n```text\\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\\n```\\n\\nKeep journal serialization and SQLite details inside `broker_replica_journal.py`.\\n\\n### Core types\\n\\n```python\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom typing import Generic, Literal, Protocol, TypeVar\\n\\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import BrokerRequest\\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\\n    AdmissionReceipt,\\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\\n    DrainReceipt,\\n    ExportReceipt,\\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\\n    IngestReceipt,\\n    PublishReceipt,\\n    ReclaimReceipt,\\n    ReplicaAuthority,\\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\\n    VerifyReceipt,\\n)\\n\\nReplicaStage = Literal[\\n    \\\"ingest\\\",\\n    \\\"verify\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\",\\n    \\\"admission\\\",\\n    \\\"drain\\\",\\n    \\\"export\\\",\\n    \\\"reclaim\\\",\\n]\\n\\nStageReceipt = (\\n    IngestReceipt\\n    | VerifyReceipt\\n    | PublishReceipt\\n    | AdmissionReceipt\\n    | DrainReceipt\\n    | ExportReceipt\\n    | ReclaimReceipt\\n)\\n\\nR = TypeVar(\\\"R\\\", bound=StageReceipt)\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\\n    request: BrokerRequest\\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\\n    owner_token: str\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass StageReconciliation(Generic[R]):\\n    outcome: Literal[\\\"completed\\\", \\\"not_applied\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"]\\n    receipt: R | None\\n\\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\\n        if (self.outcome == \\\"completed\\\") != (self.receipt is not None):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"reconciliation receipt does not match outcome\\\")\\n```\\n\\n### Effect protocol\\n\\nUse one typed effect per stage. This prevents force-drain flags or arbitrary stage dispatch.\\n\\n```python\\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol[R]):\\n    async def apply(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> R: ...\\n\\n    async def reconcile(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[R]: ...\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ReplicaLifecycleEffects:\\n    ingest: ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]\\n    verify: ReplicaStageEffect[VerifyReceipt]\\n    publish: ReplicaStageEffect[PublishReceipt]\\n    admission: ReplicaStageEffect[AdmissionReceipt]\\n    drain: ReplicaStageEffect[DrainReceipt]\\n    export: ReplicaStageEffect[ExportReceipt]\\n    reclaim: ReplicaStageEffect[ReclaimReceipt]\\n```\\n\\nDo not provide default effects. Missing effects must block construction.\\n\\n### Coordinator signature\\n\\n```python\\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\\n    def __init__(\\n        self,\\n        *,\\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\\n        effects: ReplicaLifecycleEffects,\\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float,\\n        monotonic: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic,\\n    ) -> None: ...\\n\\n    async def execute(\\n        self,\\n        request: BrokerRequest,\\n        request_frame: bytes,\\n        *,\\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\\n        owner_token: str,\\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\\n\\n    async def recover(\\n        self,\\n        lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\\n\\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> tuple[ReplicaJournalDecision, ...]: ...\\n```\\n\\n`execute` accepts immutable request data only. Artifact readers belong inside injected ingest effect adapters.\\n\\n## Transition pseudocode\\n\\n```python\\nasync def execute(...):\\n    decision = journal.accept(request, request_frame=request_frame)\\n\\n    if decision is terminal or completed:\\n        return decision\\n\\n    journal.claim_authority(\\n        request,\\n        owner_token=owner_token,\\n        authority=authority,\\n    )\\n\\n    context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(request, authority, owner_token)\\n\\n    for stage in FIXED_REPLICA_STAGES:\\n        decision = journal.status(request)\\n\\n        if decision is terminal:\\n            return decision\\n\\n        if stage is already completed:\\n            continue\\n\\n        journal.begin_stage(\\n            request,\\n            owner_token=owner_token,\\n            stage=stage,\\n        )\\n\\n        deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\\n\\n        try:\\n            receipt = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\\n                effect_for(stage).apply(context, deadline=deadline),\\n                deadline,\\n            )\\n        except StageRejected as error:\\n            journal.record_rejected(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                receipt=RejectedReceipt(reason_code=error.reason_code),\\n            )\\n            return journal.status(request)\\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\\n            journal.record_unresolved(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                reason=\\\"cancelled_unknown\\\",\\n            )\\n            raise\\n        except TimeoutError:\\n            journal.record_unresolved(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                reason=\\\"timeout_unknown\\\",\\n            )\\n            return journal.status(request)\\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as error:\\n            journal.record_unresolved(\\n                request,\\n                owner_token=owner_token,\\n                stage=stage,\\n                reason=error.reason_code,\\n            )\\n            return journal.status(request)\\n\\n        complete_stage(journal, request, owner_token, stage, receipt)\\n\\n    return journal.status(request)\\n```\\n\\n`complete_stage` must use existing typed methods:\\n\\n```python\\njournal.complete_ingest(...)\\njournal.complete_verify(...)\\njournal.complete_publish(...)\\njournal.complete_admission(...)\\njournal.complete_drain(...)\\njournal.complete_export(...)\\njournal.complete_reclaim(...)\\n```\\n\\nNever open a journal database around `await`. Every journal call must finish before an effect begins.\\n\\n### Recovery pseudocode\\n\\n```python\\nasync def recover(lifecycle):\\n    context = context_from_incomplete_lifecycle(lifecycle)\\n    stage = lifecycle.active_stage\\n    effect = effect_for(stage)\\n    deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\\n\\n    try:\\n        result = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\\n            effect.reconcile(context, deadline=deadline),\\n            deadline,\\n        )\\n    except BaseException classified as unknown:\\n        journal.record_unresolved(\\n            context.request,\\n            owner_token=context.owner_token,\\n            stage=stage,\\n            reason=\\\"recovery_unknown\\\",\\n        )\\n        return journal.status(context.request)\\n\\n    if result.outcome == \\\"completed\\\":\\n        complete_stage(..., result.receipt)\\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\\n\\n    if result.outcome == \\\"not_applied\\\":\\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\\n\\n    journal.record_unresolved(\\n        context.request,\\n        owner_token=context.owner_token,\\n        stage=stage,\\n        reason=\\\"recovery_unknown\\\",\\n    )\\n    return journal.status(context.request)\\n```\\n\\nA late result after timeout must never complete the journal. Reconciliation handles any later observable external state.\\n\\n## Existing adapters\\n\\n### Ingest adapter\\n\\n`BrokerArtifactStore` can support ingest.\\n\\nAdapter responsibilities:\\n\\n1. Decode the validated manifest from authenticated request payload.\\n2. Validate exactly three distinct roles.\\n3. Call `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(...)`.\\n4. Return its `IngestReceipt`.\\n5. Use `reconcile_attempts(...)` after a crash.\\n6. Return `unknown` for ambiguous pending or quarantine state.\\n\\nDo not retain `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` across journal calls.\\n\\n### Verify adapter\\n\\nUse:\\n\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async(...)`\\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set(...)`\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.recheck_opened_async(...)`\\n\\nRequired sequence:\\n\\n```text\\nopen incoming\\nverify bytes\\nrecheck same opened identities\\nclose every descriptor\\nreturn VerifyReceipt\\n```\\n\\nThe adapter must map publication bindings to journal `ArtifactReference` values without changing IDs, hashes, roles, media types, or lengths.\\n\\nA replacement during verification is rejection or unresolved according to existing store exceptions.\\n\\n### Publish adapter\\n\\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set(...)`.\\n\\nRecovery uses `inspect_published_artifact_set(...)`.\\n\\nConvert `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` or publication receipt into journal `PublishReceipt`. Preserve:\\n\\n- Physical target ID.\\n- Replica generation.\\n- Execution owner ID.\\n- Artifact set digest.\\n- Source state digest.\\n- Publication receipt ID.\\n\\nA post-rename failure remains unresolved unless inspection establishes exact completion.\\n\\n### Reclaim adapter\\n\\nUse existing `LauncherClient.reclaim(operation_id)`.\\n\\nDo not add `stop`, `drain`, `export`, or delete actions to root protocol.\\n\\nMap only exact result:\\n\\n```text\\nstatus == \\\"reclaimed\\\" and error is None\\n```\\n\\nto `ReclaimReceipt`.\\n\\nThese results are not success:\\n\\n- Missing reply.\\n- Timeout.\\n- Clean EOF.\\n- Malformed reply.\\n- Wrong action.\\n- Transport reset.\\n- `reclaim_disabled`.\\n- Root quiescence rejection.\\n\\nUnknown transport outcomes become unresolved. Explicit rejection becomes rejected.\\n\\nRoot already checks unit absence, empty cgroup, and runtime absence before deletion.\\n\\n## Missing injected effects\\n\\n### Admission\\n\\nCurrent `acquire_prompt_workspace(...)` is unsuitable. It depends on FastAPI request state and application SQLite ownership.\\n\\nAdd an application-owned boundary later:\\n\\n```python\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ReplicaAdmissionCommand:\\n    operation_id: str\\n    physical_target_id: str\\n    replica_generation: int\\n    execution_owner_id: str\\n    publication_receipt_id: str\\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\\n\\n\\nclass ReplicaAdmissionClient(Protocol):\\n    async def admit(\\n        self,\\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> AdmissionReceipt: ...\\n\\n    async def inspect(\\n        self,\\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[AdmissionReceipt]: ...\\n```\\n\\nNo SQLite connection may leave application-owned methods. Only immutable DTOs may cross transport.\\n\\nAdmission must invoke `require_isolated_execution(...)` before reservation, Git work, credentials, or provider access.\\n\\n### Graceful drain\\n\\nNo current graceful drain protocol exists.\\n\\n```python\\nclass GracefulReplicaDrainClient(Protocol):\\n    async def request_drain(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> DrainReceipt: ...\\n\\n    async def inspect_acknowledgement(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[DrainReceipt]: ...\\n```\\n\\nDo not include `force`, `signal`, `kill`, or `systemctl stop` options.\\n\\nAcknowledgment must bind:\\n\\n- Operation ID.\\n- Physical target ID.\\n- Replica generation.\\n- Execution owner ID.\\n- Drain request ID.\\n\\nMissing acknowledgment is unresolved. It must block export and reclaim.\\n\\n### Export\\n\\nNo current broker-side post-drain export exists.\\n\\n```python\\nclass ReplicaExportClient(Protocol):\\n    async def export(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> ExportReceipt: ...\\n\\n    async def inspect(\\n        self,\\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\\n        *,\\n        deadline: float,\\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[ExportReceipt]: ...\\n```\\n\\n`ExportReceipt` must contain exactly three external references:\\n\\n1. `committed_bundle`\\n2. `worktree`\\n3. `index_objects`\\n\\nReject duplicate IDs, missing roles, extra roles, local paths, or inline bytes.\\n\\nExisting bundle, worktree, and object-pack builders may support a future executor-side implementation. They are not a broker export transport.\\n\\n## Smallest existing API additions\\n\\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\\n\\nNo transition API change appears necessary.\\n\\nAdd accessors only if `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` does not expose these values:\\n\\n```python\\nrequest: BrokerRequest\\nauthority: ReplicaAuthority\\nowner_token: str\\nactive_stage: ReplicaStage\\n```\\n\\nDo not expose SQLite connections, cursors, or row objects.\\n\\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\\n\\nNo ingest API change is required.\\n\\nA deletion API needs a separate retention decision. Do not silently remove incoming artifacts during root reclaim.\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nNo verify or publish API change is required.\\n\\nA published-set deletion API also needs a retention decision.\\n\\n### `execution_broker.py`\\n\\nKeep `LauncherClient` methods fixed:\\n\\n```python\\nasync def prepare(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\\nasync def launch(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\\nasync def reclaim(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\\n```\\n\\nAdd replica request dispatch only after request protocol approval.\\n\\n### `broker_runtime.py`\\n\\nDo not treat runtime directory cleanup as graceful drain acknowledgment. No safe drain API exists here.\\n\\n### `execution_daemons.py`\\n\\nLater wiring must:\\n\\n- Construct replica journal separately from broker launch journal.\\n- Construct coordinator only when every effect exists.\\n- Recover before accepting connections.\\n- Keep launch, prepare, reclaim, and replica lifecycle gates independent.\\n- Preserve current nested deadline invariant.\\n- Log stable reason codes only.\\n\\n### `root_launcher.py`\\n\\nNo action changes.\\n\\nActions remain exactly:\\n\\n```text\\nprepare\\nlaunch\\nreclaim\\n```\\n\\n### Darwin isolation\\n\\nDo not weaken `workspace_isolation.py`.\\n\\nNative Darwin execution remains fail-closed. Supported fixtures remain test-only behavior.\\n\\n## Deadline rules\\n\\nUse an absolute monotonic deadline per stage.\\n\\nCurrent nesting must remain:\\n\\n```text\\nroot worker timeout\\n< launcher client timeout\\n< broker effect timeout\\n< connection timeout\\n```\\n\\nRules:\\n\\n- Persist `begin_stage` before starting deadline.\\n- Never reset deadline during retries or response parsing.\\n- Treat timeout as unknown once an effect may have started.\\n- Record unresolved before returning.\\n- On cancellation, synchronously record unresolved, then re-raise.\\n- Discard late task results.\\n- Do not advance after unresolved state.\\n- Startup reconciliation receives a fresh bounded deadline.\\n- Persistence failure remains fail-closed and must escape as journal failure.\\n\\n## Focused tests\\n\\nAdd `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`.\\n\\nRequired cases:\\n\\n1. Executes all seven stages in exact order.\\n2. Starts each stage durably before invoking its effect.\\n3. Completes each stage only after effect return.\\n4. Replays completed lifecycle without effects.\\n5. Resumes from each completed stage.\\n6. Rejects wrong authority before effects.\\n7. Rejects owner-token conflict.\\n8. Never skips a stage.\\n9. Verification rejection records `verify` rejection.\\n10. Publish post-visibility ambiguity records `publish` unresolved.\\n11. Admission timeout records `admission` unresolved.\\n12. Drain cancellation records `drain` unresolved and re-raises.\\n13. Missing drain acknowledgment blocks export.\\n14. Export rejects fewer than three references.\\n15. Export rejects more than three references.\\n16. Export rejects duplicate roles or artifact IDs.\\n17. Reclaim is never called before export completion.\\n18. Root live-unit rejection blocks reclaim completion.\\n19. Reclaim EOF records `reclaim` unresolved.\\n20. No unresolved request invokes an effect on replay.\\n21. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable ingest.\\n22. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable publication.\\n23. Unknown recovery evidence records stage-specific unresolved.\\n24. A late result after timeout cannot append completion.\\n25. Journal methods never execute while effect coroutine is active.\\n26. Startup recovery finishes before listener acceptance.\\n27. Root action set remains exactly three actions.\\n28. Each feature gate remains independently disabled.\\n29. Darwin admission performs no reservation or credential access.\\n30. Logs contain stable codes and omit paths, payloads, keys, and exception text.\\n\\n## Rejected alternatives\\n\\n- Reusing broker launch journal is invalid. Its stages are `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`.\\n- Adding root `stop` or `export` actions violates fixed root protocol tests.\\n- Treating runtime cleanup as drain acknowledgment provides no graceful executor acknowledgment.\\n- Using publication inspection as journal authority violates sole-authority requirement.\\n- Retrying unknown effects can duplicate admission, export, or reclaim effects.\\n- Holding application SQLite across broker calls violates process ownership and await boundaries.\\n- Enabling replica lifecycle through existing launch gate couples independent controls.\\n- Darwin local execution fallback violates current fail-closed isolation behavior.\\n\\n## Escalation questions\\n\\nProduct or architecture approval is required for these decisions:\\n\\n1. What authenticated request types start or continue replica lifecycle?\\n2. Which payload owns manifest, declaration, authority, and export destination?\\n3. What service owns durable admission acknowledgment?\\n4. What executor protocol defines graceful drain acknowledgment?\\n5. Where do exported artifacts live, and who signs their references?\\n6. Should root reclaim also trigger broker incoming or publication cleanup?\\n7. What retention applies after rejected or unresolved stages?\\n8. May operators resolve terminal unresolved states, or must they create a new generation?\\n9. What stage deadlines and byte limits become supported configuration?\\n10. Should startup block all broker traffic when one lifecycle cannot reconcile?\\n\\n## Report\\n\\nChanged files: none.\\n\\nCommands run:\\n\\n- Repository instruction reads.\\n- Source and focused test inspection.\\n- `git status --short`.\\n- `git diff --stat`.\\n\\nTests were not run. Task was read-only.\\n\\nMain remaining risk: admission, drain, and export lack production protocols. Wiring before those contracts exist would create hidden fallback behavior.\",\n      \"attemptedModels\": [\n        \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAttempts\": [\n        {\n          \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\",\n          \"success\": true,\n          \"exitCode\": 0,\n          \"usage\": {\n            \"input\": 159270,\n            \"output\": 10929,\n            \"cacheRead\": 119040,\n            \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n            \"cost\": 1.18374,\n            \"turns\": 6\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ac665022/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n      \"acceptance\": {\n        \"status\": \"not-required\",\n        \"evidenceStatus\": \"not-required\",\n        \"explicit\": true,\n        \"effectiveAcceptance\": {\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"explicit\": true,\n          \"inferredReason\": [\n            \"read-only task wording\"\n          ],\n          \"criteria\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": [],\n              \"severity\": \"required\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"verify\": [],\n          \"stopRules\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"disabled by deprecated false shorthand\"\n        },\n        \"inferredReason\": [\n          \"read-only task wording\"\n        ],\n        \"criteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n            \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"severity\": \"required\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"runtimeChecks\": [],\n        \"verifyRuns\": []\n      },\n      \"toolCalls\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\\\",\\\"p...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/{AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md,CONTRIBUTING.md}\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\\\"}\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*broker*test*.py\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/test*{replica,publication,admission,workspace,daemon,launcher}*.py\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"^(class|@dataclass|    def|    async def|[A-Z_]+:)\\\",\\\"limi...\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"^(class|@dataclass|    def|    async def|[A-Z_]+:)\\\",\\\"limit...\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"replica|broker|isolation\\\",\\\"ignoreCase\\\":true,\\\"limit\\\":300}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def reclaim|def prepare|def execute|_validate_reclaim|class RootLauncher\\\",\\\"...\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"test_*replica*.py\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"test_*broker*.py\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaJournal|IngestReceipt|complete_ingest\\\",\\\"glob\\\":\\\"**/*.py\\\",\\\"limit\\\":200}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\\\",\\\"p...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"replica lifecycle coordinator|ingest, verify, publish|stage-specific unresolved|Drain is graceful\\\",\\\"ignoreCase\\\"...\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/PYTHON.md\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/PYTHON.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && git status --short && git ...\",\n          \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && git status --short && git diff --stat\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nCall trace:\n- run coordinator-design: started\n- run coordinator-design: completed (ac665022) in 226058ms\nMission: b86efc7a-1960-4557-938b-96359d2bfb78 (completed)"}],"details":{"mode":"workflow","runId":"call_uPYuznt9lJlD1Aay5gacl3v3|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f2a6c1d887d099acf317f778ba51","results":[{"index":0,"agent":"worker-expert","task":"[Read from: /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py]\n\nDesign exact implementation for broker replica lifecycle coordinator on current checkout. Read only.\nInspect current BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerArtifactStore, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, broker_runtime, execution_broker, workspace_admission, workspace_execution, workspace_isolation, execution_daemons, root_launcher, and tests.\nRequired fixed stages: ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal is sole authority. No SQLite handle crosses await or external effect. Unknown outcomes are stage-specific unresolved. Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or live unit blocks reclaim. Export returns exactly three external references. Root actions stay prepare, launch, reclaim. Native Darwin stays fail-closed. Gates stay independently disabled.\nResolve exact module boundaries, effect protocols, data adapters, deadline behavior, and smallest required additions to existing APIs. Identify which effects do not exist and propose injected interfaces without inventing production support.\nReturn implementation-ready method signatures, transition pseudocode, test cases, and escalation questions. Do not modify files.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-expert","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"xhigh","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"31c900eb14d57f54e67906cd307b7b50b5a70e634e3203588df7a70eb5e23511","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":159270,"output":10929,"cacheRead":119040,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.18374,"turns":6},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","thinking":"xhigh","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":8,"graceTurns":2,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":6},"toolBudget":{"hard":50,"soft":30,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":37,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":30},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":37,"tokens":170199,"durationMs":225760},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":false}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\n\n## Current causal account\n\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\n\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\n\nNo coordinator connects them.\n\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\n\nMissing production effects:\n\n- Application-owned replica admission.\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\n- Post-drain workspace export.\n- Export destination storage.\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\n\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\n\n## Required ownership\n\n| State | Sole owner |\n|---|---|\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\n| Exported object references | External export store |\n\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\n\n## Allowed transitions\n\n```text\naccepted\n  -> authority_claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingest_completed\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verify_completed\n  -> publish_started\n  -> publish_completed\n  -> admission_started\n  -> admission_completed\n  -> drain_started\n  -> drain_completed\n  -> export_started\n  -> export_completed\n  -> reclaim_started\n  -> reclaim_completed\n```\n\nAny active stage may instead become:\n\n```text\nstage_rejected(stage, stable_reason)\nstage_unresolved(stage, stable_reason)\n```\n\nBoth outcomes are terminal under current journal semantics.\n\nInvalid transitions:\n\n- Skipping any stage.\n- Replacing claimed authority.\n- Completing without a matching start.\n- Completing with a conflicting receipt.\n- Retrying an unresolved lifecycle.\n- Admitting before publication.\n- Exporting before confirmed drain.\n- Reclaiming before export.\n- Reclaiming without a drain acknowledgment.\n- Reclaiming while root observes a unit, cgroup member, or runtime directory.\n\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` already enforces order, receipt equality, authority binding, and exact replay.\n\n## New coordinator module\n\nAdd:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\n```\n\nKeep journal serialization and SQLite details inside `broker_replica_journal.py`.\n\n### Core types\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Generic, Literal, Protocol, TypeVar\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import BrokerRequest\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    AdmissionReceipt,\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    DrainReceipt,\n    ExportReceipt,\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    IngestReceipt,\n    PublishReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\n    VerifyReceipt,\n)\n\nReplicaStage = Literal[\n    \"ingest\",\n    \"verify\",\n    \"publish\",\n    \"admission\",\n    \"drain\",\n    \"export\",\n    \"reclaim\",\n]\n\nStageReceipt = (\n    IngestReceipt\n    | VerifyReceipt\n    | PublishReceipt\n    | AdmissionReceipt\n    | DrainReceipt\n    | ExportReceipt\n    | ReclaimReceipt\n)\n\nR = TypeVar(\"R\", bound=StageReceipt)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\n    request: BrokerRequest\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n    owner_token: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass StageReconciliation(Generic[R]):\n    outcome: Literal[\"completed\", \"not_applied\", \"unknown\"]\n    receipt: R | None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if (self.outcome == \"completed\") != (self.receipt is not None):\n            raise ValueError(\"reconciliation receipt does not match outcome\")\n```\n\n### Effect protocol\n\nUse one typed effect per stage. This prevents force-drain flags or arbitrary stage dispatch.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol[R]):\n    async def apply(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> R: ...\n\n    async def reconcile(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[R]: ...\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleEffects:\n    ingest: ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]\n    verify: ReplicaStageEffect[VerifyReceipt]\n    publish: ReplicaStageEffect[PublishReceipt]\n    admission: ReplicaStageEffect[AdmissionReceipt]\n    drain: ReplicaStageEffect[DrainReceipt]\n    export: ReplicaStageEffect[ExportReceipt]\n    reclaim: ReplicaStageEffect[ReclaimReceipt]\n```\n\nDo not provide default effects. Missing effects must block construction.\n\n### Coordinator signature\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        *,\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n        effects: ReplicaLifecycleEffects,\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float,\n        monotonic: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic,\n    ) -> None: ...\n\n    async def execute(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        *,\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\n        owner_token: str,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover(\n        self,\n        lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> tuple[ReplicaJournalDecision, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`execute` accepts immutable request data only. Artifact readers belong inside injected ingest effect adapters.\n\n## Transition pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def execute(...):\n    decision = journal.accept(request, request_frame=request_frame)\n\n    if decision is terminal or completed:\n        return decision\n\n    journal.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=owner_token,\n        authority=authority,\n    )\n\n    context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(request, authority, owner_token)\n\n    for stage in FIXED_REPLICA_STAGES:\n        decision = journal.status(request)\n\n        if decision is terminal:\n            return decision\n\n        if stage is already completed:\n            continue\n\n        journal.begin_stage(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n        )\n\n        deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n        try:\n            receipt = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n                effect_for(stage).apply(context, deadline=deadline),\n                deadline,\n            )\n        except StageRejected as error:\n            journal.record_rejected(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                receipt=RejectedReceipt(reason_code=error.reason_code),\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"cancelled_unknown\",\n            )\n            raise\n        except TimeoutError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"timeout_unknown\",\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as error:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=error.reason_code,\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n\n        complete_stage(journal, request, owner_token, stage, receipt)\n\n    return journal.status(request)\n```\n\n`complete_stage` must use existing typed methods:\n\n```python\njournal.complete_ingest(...)\njournal.complete_verify(...)\njournal.complete_publish(...)\njournal.complete_admission(...)\njournal.complete_drain(...)\njournal.complete_export(...)\njournal.complete_reclaim(...)\n```\n\nNever open a journal database around `await`. Every journal call must finish before an effect begins.\n\n### Recovery pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def recover(lifecycle):\n    context = context_from_incomplete_lifecycle(lifecycle)\n    stage = lifecycle.active_stage\n    effect = effect_for(stage)\n    deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n    try:\n        result = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n            effect.reconcile(context, deadline=deadline),\n            deadline,\n        )\n    except BaseException classified as unknown:\n        journal.record_unresolved(\n            context.request,\n            owner_token=context.owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n        )\n        return journal.status(context.request)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"completed\":\n        complete_stage(..., result.receipt)\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    journal.record_unresolved(\n        context.request,\n        owner_token=context.owner_token,\n        stage=stage,\n        reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n    )\n    return journal.status(context.request)\n```\n\nA late result after timeout must never complete the journal. Reconciliation handles any later observable external state.\n\n## Existing adapters\n\n### Ingest adapter\n\n`BrokerArtifactStore` can support ingest.\n\nAdapter responsibilities:\n\n1. Decode the validated manifest from authenticated request payload.\n2. Validate exactly three distinct roles.\n3. Call `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(...)`.\n4. Return its `IngestReceipt`.\n5. Use `reconcile_attempts(...)` after a crash.\n6. Return `unknown` for ambiguous pending or quarantine state.\n\nDo not retain `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` across journal calls.\n\n### Verify adapter\n\nUse:\n\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async(...)`\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set(...)`\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.recheck_opened_async(...)`\n\nRequired sequence:\n\n```text\nopen incoming\nverify bytes\nrecheck same opened identities\nclose every descriptor\nreturn VerifyReceipt\n```\n\nThe adapter must map publication bindings to journal `ArtifactReference` values without changing IDs, hashes, roles, media types, or lengths.\n\nA replacement during verification is rejection or unresolved according to existing store exceptions.\n\n### Publish adapter\n\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nRecovery uses `inspect_published_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nConvert `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` or publication receipt into journal `PublishReceipt`. Preserve:\n\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Artifact set digest.\n- Source state digest.\n- Publication receipt ID.\n\nA post-rename failure remains unresolved unless inspection establishes exact completion.\n\n### Reclaim adapter\n\nUse existing `LauncherClient.reclaim(operation_id)`.\n\nDo not add `stop`, `drain`, `export`, or delete actions to root protocol.\n\nMap only exact result:\n\n```text\nstatus == \"reclaimed\" and error is None\n```\n\nto `ReclaimReceipt`.\n\nThese results are not success:\n\n- Missing reply.\n- Timeout.\n- Clean EOF.\n- Malformed reply.\n- Wrong action.\n- Transport reset.\n- `reclaim_disabled`.\n- Root quiescence rejection.\n\nUnknown transport outcomes become unresolved. Explicit rejection becomes rejected.\n\nRoot already checks unit absence, empty cgroup, and runtime absence before deletion.\n\n## Missing injected effects\n\n### Admission\n\nCurrent `acquire_prompt_workspace(...)` is unsuitable. It depends on FastAPI request state and application SQLite ownership.\n\nAdd an application-owned boundary later:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaAdmissionCommand:\n    operation_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    execution_owner_id: str\n    publication_receipt_id: str\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n\nclass ReplicaAdmissionClient(Protocol):\n    async def admit(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> AdmissionReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[AdmissionReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nNo SQLite connection may leave application-owned methods. Only immutable DTOs may cross transport.\n\nAdmission must invoke `require_isolated_execution(...)` before reservation, Git work, credentials, or provider access.\n\n### Graceful drain\n\nNo current graceful drain protocol exists.\n\n```python\nclass GracefulReplicaDrainClient(Protocol):\n    async def request_drain(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> DrainReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect_acknowledgement(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[DrainReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nDo not include `force`, `signal`, `kill`, or `systemctl stop` options.\n\nAcknowledgment must bind:\n\n- Operation ID.\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Drain request ID.\n\nMissing acknowledgment is unresolved. It must block export and reclaim.\n\n### Export\n\nNo current broker-side post-drain export exists.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaExportClient(Protocol):\n    async def export(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> ExportReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[ExportReceipt]: ...\n```\n\n`ExportReceipt` must contain exactly three external references:\n\n1. `committed_bundle`\n2. `worktree`\n3. `index_objects`\n\nReject duplicate IDs, missing roles, extra roles, local paths, or inline bytes.\n\nExisting bundle, worktree, and object-pack builders may support a future executor-side implementation. They are not a broker export transport.\n\n## Smallest existing API additions\n\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\n\nNo transition API change appears necessary.\n\nAdd accessors only if `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` does not expose these values:\n\n```python\nrequest: BrokerRequest\nauthority: ReplicaAuthority\nowner_token: str\nactive_stage: ReplicaStage\n```\n\nDo not expose SQLite connections, cursors, or row objects.\n\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\n\nNo ingest API change is required.\n\nA deletion API needs a separate retention decision. Do not silently remove incoming artifacts during root reclaim.\n\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\nNo verify or publish API change is required.\n\nA published-set deletion API also needs a retention decision.\n\n### `execution_broker.py`\n\nKeep `LauncherClient` methods fixed:\n\n```python\nasync def prepare(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def launch(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def reclaim(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\n```\n\nAdd replica request dispatch only after request protocol approval.\n\n### `broker_runtime.py`\n\nDo not treat runtime directory cleanup as graceful drain acknowledgment. No safe drain API exists here.\n\n### `execution_daemons.py`\n\nLater wiring must:\n\n- Construct replica journal separately from broker launch journal.\n- Construct coordinator only when every effect exists.\n- Recover before accepting connections.\n- Keep launch, prepare, reclaim, and replica lifecycle gates independent.\n- Preserve current nested deadline invariant.\n- Log stable reason codes only.\n\n### `root_launcher.py`\n\nNo action changes.\n\nActions remain exactly:\n\n```text\nprepare\nlaunch\nreclaim\n```\n\n### Darwin isolation\n\nDo not weaken `workspace_isolation.py`.\n\nNative Darwin execution remains fail-closed. Supported fixtures remain test-only behavior.\n\n## Deadline rules\n\nUse an absolute monotonic deadline per stage.\n\nCurrent nesting must remain:\n\n```text\nroot worker timeout\n< launcher client timeout\n< broker effect timeout\n< connection timeout\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Persist `begin_stage` before starting deadline.\n- Never reset deadline during retries or response parsing.\n- Treat timeout as unknown once an effect may have started.\n- Record unresolved before returning.\n- On cancellation, synchronously record unresolved, then re-raise.\n- Discard late task results.\n- Do not advance after unresolved state.\n- Startup reconciliation receives a fresh bounded deadline.\n- Persistence failure remains fail-closed and must escape as journal failure.\n\n## Focused tests\n\nAdd `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`.\n\nRequired cases:\n\n1. Executes all seven stages in exact order.\n2. Starts each stage durably before invoking its effect.\n3. Completes each stage only after effect return.\n4. Replays completed lifecycle without effects.\n5. Resumes from each completed stage.\n6. Rejects wrong authority before effects.\n7. Rejects owner-token conflict.\n8. Never skips a stage.\n9. Verification rejection records `verify` rejection.\n10. Publish post-visibility ambiguity records `publish` unresolved.\n11. Admission timeout records `admission` unresolved.\n12. Drain cancellation records `drain` unresolved and re-raises.\n13. Missing drain acknowledgment blocks export.\n14. Export rejects fewer than three references.\n15. Export rejects more than three references.\n16. Export rejects duplicate roles or artifact IDs.\n17. Reclaim is never called before export completion.\n18. Root live-unit rejection blocks reclaim completion.\n19. Reclaim EOF records `reclaim` unresolved.\n20. No unresolved request invokes an effect on replay.\n21. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable ingest.\n22. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable publication.\n23. Unknown recovery evidence records stage-specific unresolved.\n24. A late result after timeout cannot append completion.\n25. Journal methods never execute while effect coroutine is active.\n26. Startup recovery finishes before listener acceptance.\n27. Root action set remains exactly three actions.\n28. Each feature gate remains independently disabled.\n29. Darwin admission performs no reservation or credential access.\n30. Logs contain stable codes and omit paths, payloads, keys, and exception text.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- Reusing broker launch journal is invalid. Its stages are `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`.\n- Adding root `stop` or `export` actions violates fixed root protocol tests.\n- Treating runtime cleanup as drain acknowledgment provides no graceful executor acknowledgment.\n- Using publication inspection as journal authority violates sole-authority requirement.\n- Retrying unknown effects can duplicate admission, export, or reclaim effects.\n- Holding application SQLite across broker calls violates process ownership and await boundaries.\n- Enabling replica lifecycle through existing launch gate couples independent controls.\n- Darwin local execution fallback violates current fail-closed isolation behavior.\n\n## Escalation questions\n\nProduct or architecture approval is required for these decisions:\n\n1. What authenticated request types start or continue replica lifecycle?\n2. Which payload owns manifest, declaration, authority, and export destination?\n3. What service owns durable admission acknowledgment?\n4. What executor protocol defines graceful drain acknowledgment?\n5. Where do exported artifacts live, and who signs their references?\n6. Should root reclaim also trigger broker incoming or publication cleanup?\n7. What retention applies after rejected or unresolved stages?\n8. May operators resolve terminal unresolved states, or must they create a new generation?\n9. What stage deadlines and byte limits become supported configuration?\n10. Should startup block all broker traffic when one lifecycle cannot reconcile?\n\n## Report\n\nChanged files: none.\n\nCommands run:\n\n- Repository instruction reads.\n- Source and focused test inspection.\n- `git status --short`.\n- `git diff --stat`.\n\nTests were not run. Task was read-only.\n\nMain remaining risk: admission, drain, and export lack production protocols. Wiring before those contracts exist would create hidden fallback behavior.","attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":159270,"output":10929,"cacheRead":119040,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.18374,"turns":6}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ac665022/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"not-required","evidenceStatus":"not-required","explicit":true,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"none","explicit":true,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":[],"verify":[],"stopRules":[],"reason":"disabled by deprecated false shorthand"},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[]},"toolCalls":[{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"p...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"pattern\":\"**/{AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md,CONTRIBUTING.md}\"}"},{"text":"ls {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\"}","expandedText":"ls {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\",\"pattern\":\"**/*broker*test*.py\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\",\"pattern\":\"**/test*{replica,publication,admission,workspace,daemon,launcher}*.py\"}"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\"pattern\":\"^(class|@dataclass|    def|    async def|[A-Z_]+:)\",\"limi..."},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\"pattern\":\"^(class|@dataclass|    def|    async def|[A-Z_]+:)\",\"limit..."},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\",\"pattern\":\"replica|broker|isolation\",\"ignoreCase\":true,\"limit\":300}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\"pattern\":\"def reclaim|def prepare|def execute|_validate_reclaim|class RootLauncher\",\"..."},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests\",\"pattern\":\"test_*replica*.py\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests\",\"pattern\":\"test_*broker*.py\"}"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\",\"pattern\":\"BrokerReplicaJournal|IngestReceipt|complete_ingest\",\"glob\":\"**/*.py\",\"limit\":200}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"p...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"pattern\":\"replica lifecycle coordinator|ingest, verify, publish|stage-specific unresolved|Drain is graceful\",\"ignoreCase\"..."},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/PYTHON.md","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/PYTHON.md"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py"},{"text":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && git status --short && git ...","expandedText":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && git status --short && git diff --stat"}]}],"totalChildUsage":{"input":159270,"output":10929,"cacheRead":119040,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.18374,"turns":6},"totalCost":{"inputTokens":159270,"outputTokens":10929,"costUsd":1.18374},"workflow":{"value":{"key":"coordinator-design","ok":true,"runId":"ac665022","output":"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\n\n## Current causal account\n\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\n\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\n\nNo coordinator connects them.\n\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\n\nMissing production effects:\n\n- Application-owned replica admission.\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\n- Post-drain workspace export.\n- Export destination storage.\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\n\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\n\n## Required ownership\n\n| State | Sole owner |\n|---|---|\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\n| Exported object references | External export store |\n\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\n\n## Allowed transitions\n\n```text\naccepted\n  -> authority_claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingest_completed\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verify_completed\n  -> publish_started\n  -> publish_completed\n  -> admission_started\n  -> admission_completed\n  -> drain_started\n  -> drain_completed\n  -> export_started\n  -> export_completed\n  -> reclaim_started\n  -> reclaim_completed\n```\n\nAny active stage may instead become:\n\n```text\nstage_rejected(stage, stable_reason)\nstage_unresolved(stage, stable_reason)\n```\n\nBoth outcomes are terminal under current journal semantics.\n\nInvalid transitions:\n\n- Skipping any stage.\n- Replacing claimed authority.\n- Completing without a matching start.\n- Completing with a conflicting receipt.\n- Retrying an unresolved lifecycle.\n- Admitting before publication.\n- Exporting before confirmed drain.\n- Reclaiming before export.\n- Reclaiming without a drain acknowledgment.\n- Reclaiming while root observes a unit, cgroup member, or runtime directory.\n\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` already enforces order, receipt equality, authority binding, and exact replay.\n\n## New coordinator module\n\nAdd:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\n```\n\nKeep journal serialization and SQLite details inside `broker_replica_journal.py`.\n\n### Core types\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Generic, Literal, Protocol, TypeVar\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import BrokerRequest\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    AdmissionReceipt,\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    DrainReceipt,\n    ExportReceipt,\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    IngestReceipt,\n    PublishReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\n    VerifyReceipt,\n)\n\nReplicaStage = Literal[\n    \"ingest\",\n    \"verify\",\n    \"publish\",\n    \"admission\",\n    \"drain\",\n    \"export\",\n    \"reclaim\",\n]\n\nStageReceipt = (\n    IngestReceipt\n    | VerifyReceipt\n    | PublishReceipt\n    | AdmissionReceipt\n    | DrainReceipt\n    | ExportReceipt\n    | ReclaimReceipt\n)\n\nR = TypeVar(\"R\", bound=StageReceipt)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\n    request: BrokerRequest\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n    owner_token: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass StageReconciliation(Generic[R]):\n    outcome: Literal[\"completed\", \"not_applied\", \"unknown\"]\n    receipt: R | None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if (self.outcome == \"completed\") != (self.receipt is not None):\n            raise ValueError(\"reconciliation receipt does not match outcome\")\n```\n\n### Effect protocol\n\nUse one typed effect per stage. This prevents force-drain flags or arbitrary stage dispatch.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol[R]):\n    async def apply(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> R: ...\n\n    async def reconcile(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[R]: ...\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleEffects:\n    ingest: ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]\n    verify: ReplicaStageEffect[VerifyReceipt]\n    publish: ReplicaStageEffect[PublishReceipt]\n    admission: ReplicaStageEffect[AdmissionReceipt]\n    drain: ReplicaStageEffect[DrainReceipt]\n    export: ReplicaStageEffect[ExportReceipt]\n    reclaim: ReplicaStageEffect[ReclaimReceipt]\n```\n\nDo not provide default effects. Missing effects must block construction.\n\n### Coordinator signature\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        *,\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n        effects: ReplicaLifecycleEffects,\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float,\n        monotonic: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic,\n    ) -> None: ...\n\n    async def execute(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        *,\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\n        owner_token: str,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover(\n        self,\n        lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> tuple[ReplicaJournalDecision, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`execute` accepts immutable request data only. Artifact readers belong inside injected ingest effect adapters.\n\n## Transition pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def execute(...):\n    decision = journal.accept(request, request_frame=request_frame)\n\n    if decision is terminal or completed:\n        return decision\n\n    journal.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=owner_token,\n        authority=authority,\n    )\n\n    context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(request, authority, owner_token)\n\n    for stage in FIXED_REPLICA_STAGES:\n        decision = journal.status(request)\n\n        if decision is terminal:\n            return decision\n\n        if stage is already completed:\n            continue\n\n        journal.begin_stage(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n        )\n\n        deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n        try:\n            receipt = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n                effect_for(stage).apply(context, deadline=deadline),\n                deadline,\n            )\n        except StageRejected as error:\n            journal.record_rejected(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                receipt=RejectedReceipt(reason_code=error.reason_code),\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"cancelled_unknown\",\n            )\n            raise\n        except TimeoutError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"timeout_unknown\",\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as error:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=error.reason_code,\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n\n        complete_stage(journal, request, owner_token, stage, receipt)\n\n    return journal.status(request)\n```\n\n`complete_stage` must use existing typed methods:\n\n```python\njournal.complete_ingest(...)\njournal.complete_verify(...)\njournal.complete_publish(...)\njournal.complete_admission(...)\njournal.complete_drain(...)\njournal.complete_export(...)\njournal.complete_reclaim(...)\n```\n\nNever open a journal database around `await`. Every journal call must finish before an effect begins.\n\n### Recovery pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def recover(lifecycle):\n    context = context_from_incomplete_lifecycle(lifecycle)\n    stage = lifecycle.active_stage\n    effect = effect_for(stage)\n    deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n    try:\n        result = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n            effect.reconcile(context, deadline=deadline),\n            deadline,\n        )\n    except BaseException classified as unknown:\n        journal.record_unresolved(\n            context.request,\n            owner_token=context.owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n        )\n        return journal.status(context.request)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"completed\":\n        complete_stage(..., result.receipt)\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    journal.record_unresolved(\n        context.request,\n        owner_token=context.owner_token,\n        stage=stage,\n        reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n    )\n    return journal.status(context.request)\n```\n\nA late result after timeout must never complete the journal. Reconciliation handles any later observable external state.\n\n## Existing adapters\n\n### Ingest adapter\n\n`BrokerArtifactStore` can support ingest.\n\nAdapter responsibilities:\n\n1. Decode the validated manifest from authenticated request payload.\n2. Validate exactly three distinct roles.\n3. Call `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(...)`.\n4. Return its `IngestReceipt`.\n5. Use `reconcile_attempts(...)` after a crash.\n6. Return `unknown` for ambiguous pending or quarantine state.\n\nDo not retain `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` across journal calls.\n\n### Verify adapter\n\nUse:\n\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async(...)`\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set(...)`\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.recheck_opened_async(...)`\n\nRequired sequence:\n\n```text\nopen incoming\nverify bytes\nrecheck same opened identities\nclose every descriptor\nreturn VerifyReceipt\n```\n\nThe adapter must map publication bindings to journal `ArtifactReference` values without changing IDs, hashes, roles, media types, or lengths.\n\nA replacement during verification is rejection or unresolved according to existing store exceptions.\n\n### Publish adapter\n\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nRecovery uses `inspect_published_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nConvert `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` or publication receipt into journal `PublishReceipt`. Preserve:\n\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Artifact set digest.\n- Source state digest.\n- Publication receipt ID.\n\nA post-rename failure remains unresolved unless inspection establishes exact completion.\n\n### Reclaim adapter\n\nUse existing `LauncherClient.reclaim(operation_id)`.\n\nDo not add `stop`, `drain`, `export`, or delete actions to root protocol.\n\nMap only exact result:\n\n```text\nstatus == \"reclaimed\" and error is None\n```\n\nto `ReclaimReceipt`.\n\nThese results are not success:\n\n- Missing reply.\n- Timeout.\n- Clean EOF.\n- Malformed reply.\n- Wrong action.\n- Transport reset.\n- `reclaim_disabled`.\n- Root quiescence rejection.\n\nUnknown transport outcomes become unresolved. Explicit rejection becomes rejected.\n\nRoot already checks unit absence, empty cgroup, and runtime absence before deletion.\n\n## Missing injected effects\n\n### Admission\n\nCurrent `acquire_prompt_workspace(...)` is unsuitable. It depends on FastAPI request state and application SQLite ownership.\n\nAdd an application-owned boundary later:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaAdmissionCommand:\n    operation_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    execution_owner_id: str\n    publication_receipt_id: str\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n\nclass ReplicaAdmissionClient(Protocol):\n    async def admit(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> AdmissionReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[AdmissionReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nNo SQLite connection may leave application-owned methods. Only immutable DTOs may cross transport.\n\nAdmission must invoke `require_isolated_execution(...)` before reservation, Git work, credentials, or provider access.\n\n### Graceful drain\n\nNo current graceful drain protocol exists.\n\n```python\nclass GracefulReplicaDrainClient(Protocol):\n    async def request_drain(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> DrainReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect_acknowledgement(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[DrainReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nDo not include `force`, `signal`, `kill`, or `systemctl stop` options.\n\nAcknowledgment must bind:\n\n- Operation ID.\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Drain request ID.\n\nMissing acknowledgment is unresolved. It must block export and reclaim.\n\n### Export\n\nNo current broker-side post-drain export exists.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaExportClient(Protocol):\n    async def export(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> ExportReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[ExportReceipt]: ...\n```\n\n`ExportReceipt` must contain exactly three external references:\n\n1. `committed_bundle`\n2. `worktree`\n3. `index_objects`\n\nReject duplicate IDs, missing roles, extra roles, local paths, or inline bytes.\n\nExisting bundle, worktree, and object-pack builders may support a future executor-side implementation. They are not a broker export transport.\n\n## Smallest existing API additions\n\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\n\nNo transition API change appears necessary.\n\nAdd accessors only if `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` does not expose these values:\n\n```python\nrequest: BrokerRequest\nauthority: ReplicaAuthority\nowner_token: str\nactive_stage: ReplicaStage\n```\n\nDo not expose SQLite connections, cursors, or row objects.\n\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\n\nNo ingest API change is required.\n\nA deletion API needs a separate retention decision. Do not silently remove incoming artifacts during root reclaim.\n\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\nNo verify or publish API change is required.\n\nA published-set deletion API also needs a retention decision.\n\n### `execution_broker.py`\n\nKeep `LauncherClient` methods fixed:\n\n```python\nasync def prepare(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def launch(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def reclaim(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\n```\n\nAdd replica request dispatch only after request protocol approval.\n\n### `broker_runtime.py`\n\nDo not treat runtime directory cleanup as graceful drain acknowledgment. No safe drain API exists here.\n\n### `execution_daemons.py`\n\nLater wiring must:\n\n- Construct replica journal separately from broker launch journal.\n- Construct coordinator only when every effect exists.\n- Recover before accepting connections.\n- Keep launch, prepare, reclaim, and replica lifecycle gates independent.\n- Preserve current nested deadline invariant.\n- Log stable reason codes only.\n\n### `root_launcher.py`\n\nNo action changes.\n\nActions remain exactly:\n\n```text\nprepare\nlaunch\nreclaim\n```\n\n### Darwin isolation\n\nDo not weaken `workspace_isolation.py`.\n\nNative Darwin execution remains fail-closed. Supported fixtures remain test-only behavior.\n\n## Deadline rules\n\nUse an absolute monotonic deadline per stage.\n\nCurrent nesting must remain:\n\n```text\nroot worker timeout\n< launcher client timeout\n< broker effect timeout\n< connection timeout\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Persist `begin_stage` before starting deadline.\n- Never reset deadline during retries or response parsing.\n- Treat timeout as unknown once an effect may have started.\n- Record unresolved before returning.\n- On cancellation, synchronously record unresolved, then re-raise.\n- Discard late task results.\n- Do not advance after unresolved state.\n- Startup reconciliation receives a fresh bounded deadline.\n- Persistence failure remains fail-closed and must escape as journal failure.\n\n## Focused tests\n\nAdd `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`.\n\nRequired cases:\n\n1. Executes all seven stages in exact order.\n2. Starts each stage durably before invoking its effect.\n3. Completes each stage only after effect return.\n4. Replays completed lifecycle without effects.\n5. Resumes from each completed stage.\n6. Rejects wrong authority before effects.\n7. Rejects owner-token conflict.\n8. Never skips a stage.\n9. Verification rejection records `verify` rejection.\n10. Publish post-visibility ambiguity records `publish` unresolved.\n11. Admission timeout records `admission` unresolved.\n12. Drain cancellation records `drain` unresolved and re-raises.\n13. Missing drain acknowledgment blocks export.\n14. Export rejects fewer than three references.\n15. Export rejects more than three references.\n16. Export rejects duplicate roles or artifact IDs.\n17. Reclaim is never called before export completion.\n18. Root live-unit rejection blocks reclaim completion.\n19. Reclaim EOF records `reclaim` unresolved.\n20. No unresolved request invokes an effect on replay.\n21. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable ingest.\n22. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable publication.\n23. Unknown recovery evidence records stage-specific unresolved.\n24. A late result after timeout cannot append completion.\n25. Journal methods never execute while effect coroutine is active.\n26. Startup recovery finishes before listener acceptance.\n27. Root action set remains exactly three actions.\n28. Each feature gate remains independently disabled.\n29. Darwin admission performs no reservation or credential access.\n30. Logs contain stable codes and omit paths, payloads, keys, and exception text.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- Reusing broker launch journal is invalid. Its stages are `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`.\n- Adding root `stop` or `export` actions violates fixed root protocol tests.\n- Treating runtime cleanup as drain acknowledgment provides no graceful executor acknowledgment.\n- Using publication inspection as journal authority violates sole-authority requirement.\n- Retrying unknown effects can duplicate admission, export, or reclaim effects.\n- Holding application SQLite across broker calls violates process ownership and await boundaries.\n- Enabling replica lifecycle through existing launch gate couples independent controls.\n- Darwin local execution fallback violates current fail-closed isolation behavior.\n\n## Escalation questions\n\nProduct or architecture approval is required for these decisions:\n\n1. What authenticated request types start or continue replica lifecycle?\n2. Which payload owns manifest, declaration, authority, and export destination?\n3. What service owns durable admission acknowledgment?\n4. What executor protocol defines graceful drain acknowledgment?\n5. Where do exported artifacts live, and who signs their references?\n6. Should root reclaim also trigger broker incoming or publication cleanup?\n7. What retention applies after rejected or unresolved stages?\n8. May operators resolve terminal unresolved states, or must they create a new generation?\n9. What stage deadlines and byte limits become supported configuration?\n10. Should startup block all broker traffic when one lifecycle cannot reconcile?\n\n## Report\n\nChanged files: none.\n\nCommands run:\n\n- Repository instruction reads.\n- Source and focused test inspection.\n- `git status --short`.\n- `git diff --stat`.\n\nTests were not run. Task was read-only.\n\nMain remaining risk: admission, drain, and export lack production protocols. Wiring before those contracts exist would create hidden fallback behavior.","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ac665022/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"worker-expert","task":"[Read from: /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py]\n\nDesign exact implementation for broker replica lifecycle coordinator on current checkout. Read only.\nInspect current BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerArtifactStore, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, broker_runtime, execution_broker, workspace_admission, workspace_execution, workspace_isolation, execution_daemons, root_launcher, and tests.\nRequired fixed stages: ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal is sole authority. No SQLite handle crosses await or external effect. Unknown outcomes are stage-specific unresolved. Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or live unit blocks reclaim. Export returns exactly three external references. Root actions stay prepare, launch, reclaim. Native Darwin stays fail-closed. Gates stay independently disabled.\nResolve exact module boundaries, effect protocols, data adapters, deadline behavior, and smallest required additions to existing APIs. Identify which effects do not exist and propose injected interfaces without inventing production support.\nReturn implementation-ready method signatures, transition pseudocode, test cases, and escalation questions. Do not modify files.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-expert","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"xhigh","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"31c900eb14d57f54e67906cd307b7b50b5a70e634e3203588df7a70eb5e23511","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":159270,"output":10929,"cacheRead":119040,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.18374,"turns":6},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","thinking":"xhigh","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":8,"graceTurns":2,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":6},"toolBudget":{"hard":50,"soft":30,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":37,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":30},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":37,"tokens":170199,"durationMs":225760},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":false}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\n\n## Current causal account\n\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\n\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\n\nNo coordinator connects them.\n\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\n\nMissing production effects:\n\n- Application-owned replica admission.\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\n- Post-drain workspace export.\n- Export destination storage.\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\n\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\n\n## Required ownership\n\n| State | Sole owner |\n|---|---|\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\n| Exported object references | External export store |\n\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\n\n## Allowed transitions\n\n```text\naccepted\n  -> authority_claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingest_completed\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verify_completed\n  -> publish_started\n  -> publish_completed\n  -> admission_started\n  -> admission_completed\n  -> drain_started\n  -> drain_completed\n  -> export_started\n  -> export_completed\n  -> reclaim_started\n  -> reclaim_completed\n```\n\nAny active stage may instead become:\n\n```text\nstage_rejected(stage, stable_reason)\nstage_unresolved(stage, stable_reason)\n```\n\nBoth outcomes are terminal under current journal semantics.\n\nInvalid transitions:\n\n- Skipping any stage.\n- Replacing claimed authority.\n- Completing without a matching start.\n- Completing with a conflicting receipt.\n- Retrying an unresolved lifecycle.\n- Admitting before publication.\n- Exporting before confirmed drain.\n- Reclaiming before export.\n- Reclaiming without a drain acknowledgment.\n- Reclaiming while root observes a unit, cgroup member, or runtime directory.\n\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` already enforces order, receipt equality, authority binding, and exact replay.\n\n## New coordinator module\n\nAdd:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\n```\n\nKeep journal serialization and SQLite details inside `broker_replica_journal.py`.\n\n### Core types\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Generic, Literal, Protocol, TypeVar\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import BrokerRequest\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    AdmissionReceipt,\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    DrainReceipt,\n    ExportReceipt,\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    IngestReceipt,\n    PublishReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\n    VerifyReceipt,\n)\n\nReplicaStage = Literal[\n    \"ingest\",\n    \"verify\",\n    \"publish\",\n    \"admission\",\n    \"drain\",\n    \"export\",\n    \"reclaim\",\n]\n\nStageReceipt = (\n    IngestReceipt\n    | VerifyReceipt\n    | PublishReceipt\n    | AdmissionReceipt\n    | DrainReceipt\n    | ExportReceipt\n    | ReclaimReceipt\n)\n\nR = TypeVar(\"R\", bound=StageReceipt)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\n    request: BrokerRequest\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n    owner_token: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass StageReconciliation(Generic[R]):\n    outcome: Literal[\"completed\", \"not_applied\", \"unknown\"]\n    receipt: R | None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if (self.outcome == \"completed\") != (self.receipt is not None):\n            raise ValueError(\"reconciliation receipt does not match outcome\")\n```\n\n### Effect protocol\n\nUse one typed effect per stage. This prevents force-drain flags or arbitrary stage dispatch.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol[R]):\n    async def apply(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> R: ...\n\n    async def reconcile(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[R]: ...\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleEffects:\n    ingest: ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]\n    verify: ReplicaStageEffect[VerifyReceipt]\n    publish: ReplicaStageEffect[PublishReceipt]\n    admission: ReplicaStageEffect[AdmissionReceipt]\n    drain: ReplicaStageEffect[DrainReceipt]\n    export: ReplicaStageEffect[ExportReceipt]\n    reclaim: ReplicaStageEffect[ReclaimReceipt]\n```\n\nDo not provide default effects. Missing effects must block construction.\n\n### Coordinator signature\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        *,\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n        effects: ReplicaLifecycleEffects,\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float,\n        monotonic: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic,\n    ) -> None: ...\n\n    async def execute(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        *,\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\n        owner_token: str,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover(\n        self,\n        lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> tuple[ReplicaJournalDecision, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`execute` accepts immutable request data only. Artifact readers belong inside injected ingest effect adapters.\n\n## Transition pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def execute(...):\n    decision = journal.accept(request, request_frame=request_frame)\n\n    if decision is terminal or completed:\n        return decision\n\n    journal.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=owner_token,\n        authority=authority,\n    )\n\n    context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(request, authority, owner_token)\n\n    for stage in FIXED_REPLICA_STAGES:\n        decision = journal.status(request)\n\n        if decision is terminal:\n            return decision\n\n        if stage is already completed:\n            continue\n\n        journal.begin_stage(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n        )\n\n        deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n        try:\n            receipt = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n                effect_for(stage).apply(context, deadline=deadline),\n                deadline,\n            )\n        except StageRejected as error:\n            journal.record_rejected(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                receipt=RejectedReceipt(reason_code=error.reason_code),\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"cancelled_unknown\",\n            )\n            raise\n        except TimeoutError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"timeout_unknown\",\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as error:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=error.reason_code,\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n\n        complete_stage(journal, request, owner_token, stage, receipt)\n\n    return journal.status(request)\n```\n\n`complete_stage` must use existing typed methods:\n\n```python\njournal.complete_ingest(...)\njournal.complete_verify(...)\njournal.complete_publish(...)\njournal.complete_admission(...)\njournal.complete_drain(...)\njournal.complete_export(...)\njournal.complete_reclaim(...)\n```\n\nNever open a journal database around `await`. Every journal call must finish before an effect begins.\n\n### Recovery pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def recover(lifecycle):\n    context = context_from_incomplete_lifecycle(lifecycle)\n    stage = lifecycle.active_stage\n    effect = effect_for(stage)\n    deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n    try:\n        result = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n            effect.reconcile(context, deadline=deadline),\n            deadline,\n        )\n    except BaseException classified as unknown:\n        journal.record_unresolved(\n            context.request,\n            owner_token=context.owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n        )\n        return journal.status(context.request)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"completed\":\n        complete_stage(..., result.receipt)\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    journal.record_unresolved(\n        context.request,\n        owner_token=context.owner_token,\n        stage=stage,\n        reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n    )\n    return journal.status(context.request)\n```\n\nA late result after timeout must never complete the journal. Reconciliation handles any later observable external state.\n\n## Existing adapters\n\n### Ingest adapter\n\n`BrokerArtifactStore` can support ingest.\n\nAdapter responsibilities:\n\n1. Decode the validated manifest from authenticated request payload.\n2. Validate exactly three distinct roles.\n3. Call `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(...)`.\n4. Return its `IngestReceipt`.\n5. Use `reconcile_attempts(...)` after a crash.\n6. Return `unknown` for ambiguous pending or quarantine state.\n\nDo not retain `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` across journal calls.\n\n### Verify adapter\n\nUse:\n\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async(...)`\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set(...)`\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.recheck_opened_async(...)`\n\nRequired sequence:\n\n```text\nopen incoming\nverify bytes\nrecheck same opened identities\nclose every descriptor\nreturn VerifyReceipt\n```\n\nThe adapter must map publication bindings to journal `ArtifactReference` values without changing IDs, hashes, roles, media types, or lengths.\n\nA replacement during verification is rejection or unresolved according to existing store exceptions.\n\n### Publish adapter\n\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nRecovery uses `inspect_published_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nConvert `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` or publication receipt into journal `PublishReceipt`. Preserve:\n\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Artifact set digest.\n- Source state digest.\n- Publication receipt ID.\n\nA post-rename failure remains unresolved unless inspection establishes exact completion.\n\n### Reclaim adapter\n\nUse existing `LauncherClient.reclaim(operation_id)`.\n\nDo not add `stop`, `drain`, `export`, or delete actions to root protocol.\n\nMap only exact result:\n\n```text\nstatus == \"reclaimed\" and error is None\n```\n\nto `ReclaimReceipt`.\n\nThese results are not success:\n\n- Missing reply.\n- Timeout.\n- Clean EOF.\n- Malformed reply.\n- Wrong action.\n- Transport reset.\n- `reclaim_disabled`.\n- Root quiescence rejection.\n\nUnknown transport outcomes become unresolved. Explicit rejection becomes rejected.\n\nRoot already checks unit absence, empty cgroup, and runtime absence before deletion.\n\n## Missing injected effects\n\n### Admission\n\nCurrent `acquire_prompt_workspace(...)` is unsuitable. It depends on FastAPI request state and application SQLite ownership.\n\nAdd an application-owned boundary later:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaAdmissionCommand:\n    operation_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    execution_owner_id: str\n    publication_receipt_id: str\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n\nclass ReplicaAdmissionClient(Protocol):\n    async def admit(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> AdmissionReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[AdmissionReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nNo SQLite connection may leave application-owned methods. Only immutable DTOs may cross transport.\n\nAdmission must invoke `require_isolated_execution(...)` before reservation, Git work, credentials, or provider access.\n\n### Graceful drain\n\nNo current graceful drain protocol exists.\n\n```python\nclass GracefulReplicaDrainClient(Protocol):\n    async def request_drain(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> DrainReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect_acknowledgement(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[DrainReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nDo not include `force`, `signal`, `kill`, or `systemctl stop` options.\n\nAcknowledgment must bind:\n\n- Operation ID.\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Drain request ID.\n\nMissing acknowledgment is unresolved. It must block export and reclaim.\n\n### Export\n\nNo current broker-side post-drain export exists.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaExportClient(Protocol):\n    async def export(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> ExportReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[ExportReceipt]: ...\n```\n\n`ExportReceipt` must contain exactly three external references:\n\n1. `committed_bundle`\n2. `worktree`\n3. `index_objects`\n\nReject duplicate IDs, missing roles, extra roles, local paths, or inline bytes.\n\nExisting bundle, worktree, and object-pack builders may support a future executor-side implementation. They are not a broker export transport.\n\n## Smallest existing API additions\n\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\n\nNo transition API change appears necessary.\n\nAdd accessors only if `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` does not expose these values:\n\n```python\nrequest: BrokerRequest\nauthority: ReplicaAuthority\nowner_token: str\nactive_stage: ReplicaStage\n```\n\nDo not expose SQLite connections, cursors, or row objects.\n\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\n\nNo ingest API change is required.\n\nA deletion API needs a separate retention decision. Do not silently remove incoming artifacts during root reclaim.\n\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\nNo verify or publish API change is required.\n\nA published-set deletion API also needs a retention decision.\n\n### `execution_broker.py`\n\nKeep `LauncherClient` methods fixed:\n\n```python\nasync def prepare(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def launch(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def reclaim(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\n```\n\nAdd replica request dispatch only after request protocol approval.\n\n### `broker_runtime.py`\n\nDo not treat runtime directory cleanup as graceful drain acknowledgment. No safe drain API exists here.\n\n### `execution_daemons.py`\n\nLater wiring must:\n\n- Construct replica journal separately from broker launch journal.\n- Construct coordinator only when every effect exists.\n- Recover before accepting connections.\n- Keep launch, prepare, reclaim, and replica lifecycle gates independent.\n- Preserve current nested deadline invariant.\n- Log stable reason codes only.\n\n### `root_launcher.py`\n\nNo action changes.\n\nActions remain exactly:\n\n```text\nprepare\nlaunch\nreclaim\n```\n\n### Darwin isolation\n\nDo not weaken `workspace_isolation.py`.\n\nNative Darwin execution remains fail-closed. Supported fixtures remain test-only behavior.\n\n## Deadline rules\n\nUse an absolute monotonic deadline per stage.\n\nCurrent nesting must remain:\n\n```text\nroot worker timeout\n< launcher client timeout\n< broker effect timeout\n< connection timeout\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Persist `begin_stage` before starting deadline.\n- Never reset deadline during retries or response parsing.\n- Treat timeout as unknown once an effect may have started.\n- Record unresolved before returning.\n- On cancellation, synchronously record unresolved, then re-raise.\n- Discard late task results.\n- Do not advance after unresolved state.\n- Startup reconciliation receives a fresh bounded deadline.\n- Persistence failure remains fail-closed and must escape as journal failure.\n\n## Focused tests\n\nAdd `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`.\n\nRequired cases:\n\n1. Executes all seven stages in exact order.\n2. Starts each stage durably before invoking its effect.\n3. Completes each stage only after effect return.\n4. Replays completed lifecycle without effects.\n5. Resumes from each completed stage.\n6. Rejects wrong authority before effects.\n7. Rejects owner-token conflict.\n8. Never skips a stage.\n9. Verification rejection records `verify` rejection.\n10. Publish post-visibility ambiguity records `publish` unresolved.\n11. Admission timeout records `admission` unresolved.\n12. Drain cancellation records `drain` unresolved and re-raises.\n13. Missing drain acknowledgment blocks export.\n14. Export rejects fewer than three references.\n15. Export rejects more than three references.\n16. Export rejects duplicate roles or artifact IDs.\n17. Reclaim is never called before export completion.\n18. Root live-unit rejection blocks reclaim completion.\n19. Reclaim EOF records `reclaim` unresolved.\n20. No unresolved request invokes an effect on replay.\n21. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable ingest.\n22. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable publication.\n23. Unknown recovery evidence records stage-specific unresolved.\n24. A late result after timeout cannot append completion.\n25. Journal methods never execute while effect coroutine is active.\n26. Startup recovery finishes before listener acceptance.\n27. Root action set remains exactly three actions.\n28. Each feature gate remains independently disabled.\n29. Darwin admission performs no reservation or credential access.\n30. Logs contain stable codes and omit paths, payloads, keys, and exception text.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- Reusing broker launch journal is invalid. Its stages are `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`.\n- Adding root `stop` or `export` actions violates fixed root protocol tests.\n- Treating runtime cleanup as drain acknowledgment provides no graceful executor acknowledgment.\n- Using publication inspection as journal authority violates sole-authority requirement.\n- Retrying unknown effects can duplicate admission, export, or reclaim effects.\n- Holding application SQLite across broker calls violates process ownership and await boundaries.\n- Enabling replica lifecycle through existing launch gate couples independent controls.\n- Darwin local execution fallback violates current fail-closed isolation behavior.\n\n## Escalation questions\n\nProduct or architecture approval is required for these decisions:\n\n1. What authenticated request types start or continue replica lifecycle?\n2. Which payload owns manifest, declaration, authority, and export destination?\n3. What service owns durable admission acknowledgment?\n4. What executor protocol defines graceful drain acknowledgment?\n5. Where do exported artifacts live, and who signs their references?\n6. Should root reclaim also trigger broker incoming or publication cleanup?\n7. What retention applies after rejected or unresolved stages?\n8. May operators resolve terminal unresolved states, or must they create a new generation?\n9. What stage deadlines and byte limits become supported configuration?\n10. Should startup block all broker traffic when one lifecycle cannot reconcile?\n\n## Report\n\nChanged files: none.\n\nCommands run:\n\n- Repository instruction reads.\n- Source and focused test inspection.\n- `git status --short`.\n- `git diff --stat`.\n\nTests were not run. Task was read-only.\n\nMain remaining risk: admission, drain, and export lack production protocols. Wiring before those contracts exist would create hidden fallback behavior.","attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":159270,"output":10929,"cacheRead":119040,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.18374,"turns":6}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ac665022/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"not-required","evidenceStatus":"not-required","explicit":true,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"none","explicit":true,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":[],"verify":[],"stopRules":[],"reason":"disabled by deprecated false shorthand"},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[]},"toolCalls":[{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"p...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"pattern\":\"**/{AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md,CONTRIBUTING.md}\"}"},{"text":"ls {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\"}","expandedText":"ls {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\",\"pattern\":\"**/*broker*test*.py\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\",\"pattern\":\"**/test*{replica,publication,admission,workspace,daemon,launcher}*.py\"}"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\"pattern\":\"^(class|@dataclass|    def|    async def|[A-Z_]+:)\",\"limi..."},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\"pattern\":\"^(class|@dataclass|    def|    async def|[A-Z_]+:)\",\"limit..."},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py\",\"pattern\":\"replica|broker|isolation\",\"ignoreCase\":true,\"limit\":300}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\"pattern\":\"def reclaim|def prepare|def execute|_validate_reclaim|class RootLauncher\",\"..."},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests\",\"pattern\":\"test_*replica*.py\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests\",\"pattern\":\"test_*broker*.py\"}"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/bac...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend\",\"pattern\":\"BrokerReplicaJournal|IngestReceipt|complete_ingest\",\"glob\":\"**/*.py\",\"limit\":200}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"p...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\",\"pattern\":\"replica lifecycle coordinator|ingest, verify, publish|stage-specific unresolved|Drain is graceful\",\"ignoreCase\"..."},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/PYTHON.md","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/PYTHON.md"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_root_replica_lifecycle.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py"},{"text":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && git status --short && git ...","expandedText":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && git status --short && git diff --stat"}]}]},"trace":[{"operation":"run","key":"coordinator-design","state":"started"},{"operation":"run","key":"coordinator-design","state":"completed","durationMs":226058,"runId":"ac665022"}],"emits":[],"console":[]},"chatProgress":{"mode":"live-card","repoRelation":"same","repoLabel":"yinshi"},"missionId":"b86efc7a-1960-4557-938b-96359d2bfb78","missionPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/missions/b86efc7a-1960-4557-938b-96359d2bfb78.json","mission":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"b86efc7a-1960-4557-938b-96359d2bfb78","title":"Design exact implementation for broker replica lifecycle coordinator on current checkout. Read only.","objective":"Design exact implementation for broker replica lifecycle coordinator on current checkout. Read only.\nInspect current BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerArtifactStore, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, broker_runtime, execution_broker, workspace_admission, workspace_execution, workspace_isolation, execution_daemons, root_launcher, and tests.\nRequired fixed stages: ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal is sole authority. No SQLite handle crosses await or external effect. Unknown outcomes are stage-specific unresolved. Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or live unit blocks reclaim. Export returns exactly three external references. Root actions stay prepare, launch, reclaim. Native Darwin stays fail-closed. Gates stay independently disabled.\nResolve exact module boundaries, effect protocols, data adapters, deadline behavior, and smallest required additions to existing APIs. Identify which effects do not exist and propose injected interfaces without inventing production support.\nReturn implementation-ready method signatures, transition pseudocode, test cases, and escalation questions. Do not modify files.","status":"completed","createdAt":"2026-09-13T00:47:44.675Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-13T00:51:31.221Z","runs":[{"runId":"call_uPYuznt9lJlD1Aay5gacl3v3|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f2a6c1d887d099acf317f778ba51","mode":"workflow","agent":"worker-expert","status":"completed","startedAt":"2026-09-13T00:51:31.220Z","completedAt":"2026-09-13T00:51:31.220Z","usage":{"tokens":170199}}],"decisions":[],"artifacts":[{"kind":"output","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_output.md"},{"kind":"other","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl","description":"Child transcript"}],"receipts":[],"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","ownerSessionId":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64.jsonl","summary":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"coordinator-design\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"ac665022\",\n  \"output\": \"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\\n\\n## Current causal account\\n\\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\\n\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\\n\\nNo coordinator connects them.\\n\\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\\n\\nMissing production effects:\\n\\n- Application-owned replica admission.\\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\\n- Post-drain workspace export.\\n- Export destination storage.\\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\\n\\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\\n\\n## Required ownership\\n\\n| State | Sole owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\\n| Exported object references | External export store |\\n\\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\\n\\n## Allowed transitions\\n\\n```text\\naccepted\\n  -> authority_claimed\\n  -> ingest_started\\n  -> ingest_completed\\n  -> verify_started\\n  -> verify_completed\\n  -> publish_started\\n  -> publish_completed\\n  -> admission_started\\n  -> admission_completed\\n  -> drain_started\\n  -> drain_completed\\n  -> export_started\\n  -> export_completed\\n  -> reclaim_started\\n  -> reclaim_completed...","acceptance":{"status":"not-required","evidenceStatus":"not-required","explicit":true,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"none","explicit":true,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":[],"verify":[],"stopRules":[],"reason":"disabled by deprecated false shorthand"},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":[],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[]}}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789260691460}}
{"type":"compaction","id":"bacc503e","parentId":"a12047aa","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:56:20.278Z","summary":"## Goal\nFinish Phases 6 and 7 of `/Users/user/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md` in `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`, validate independently, then commit, rebase, and push.\n\n- Phase 6 covers managed child integration, deterministic Git application and recovery, broker-backed Linux isolation, authenticated desktop-to-VM transport, bounded repository ingestion, durable replica authority, and drain/export/reclaim.\n- Managed integration does not require Linux. Native Darwin execution remains fail-closed.\n- Phase 7 covers nested delegation, budgets, steering, and persisted delivery semantics. It remains blocked until Phase 6 is accepted.\n- The immediate milestone now moves from the completed authenticated three-artifact journal/storage/publication layer to a broker-owned lifecycle coordinator for `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Continue implementation without waiting, but request approval before material privileged infrastructure changes. Disabled VM qualification was explicitly approved.\n- Use at least five subagents where practical; the parent controls integration, commits, rebases, and pushes.\n- Preserve the heavily dirty inherited Phase 6 worktree and unrelated changes.\n- Use `read`, `edit`, and `write` for source changes. Do not use shell source writes, mutating formatters, permission bypasses, manufactured failures, or production reversions merely to create red tests.\n- Do not disable or bypass TDD Guard. Parent-authorized red→green writes remain the fallback when worker branches report `TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.`\n- RepoPrompt Context Builder sees a stale or missing checkout and cannot inspect current commits or dirty broker files; resolve proposed capabilities against the actual checkout and do not invent APIs.\n- Use `backend/.venv` for backend tests. Ruff is `/Users/user/.pyenv/versions/3.12.3/bin/ruff`, version 0.16.5.\n- Required checks include focused and broad pytest, Ruff, format, isort, Flake8, strict mypy, `py_compile`, `git diff --check`, prose checks, Linux qualification, and independent review.\n- No SQLite handle may cross an external effect or `await`.\n- Unknown transport, timeout, cancellation, verification, delivery, acknowledgment, effect, presence, absence, rename-state lookup, or SQLite commit results remain stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n- Preserve exact ownership, runtime acknowledgment, markers, receipts, synchronization facts, and A4 authenticated journal positions.\n- Root protocol remains exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`; all gates remain independently disabled by default.\n- Drain is graceful broker-to-executor only. Missing acknowledgment or a live unit remains unresolved and blocks reclaim. Do not add a fourth root stop action.\n- Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Only bounded IDs, roles, media types, digests, lengths, limits, and typed receipts may enter the journal.\n- Broker lifecycle v2 and the read-only legacy v1 journal must remain unchanged by replica-authority work.\n- The stdio relay is opaque, uses the signed broker protocol for end-to-end authentication, and exposes no caller-selected socket path.\n- Preserve fixed executor identities `yinshi-executor-00` through `yinshi-executor-31`; callers cannot select them.\n- Keep `rft-sandbox` stopped and untouched.\n- Git replacement objects and lazy/promisor fetches must remain disabled for artifact generation and verification.\n- Artifact verification must use independent, empty bare quarantine repositories with matching SHA-1 or SHA-256 object format.\n- Publication must reject unsafe paths, symlinks, digest or length mismatch, partial sets, overwrite, timeout, cancellation, uncertain acknowledgment, root/final replacement, late metadata changes, hardlinks, FIFOs, and malformed declarations.\n- Publication requires exact root mode `0700`, pending/final directory mode `0700`, artifact file mode `0600`, expected ownership, and link count one.\n- Publication must use same-filesystem atomic no-replace rename and correct file/directory synchronization ordering.\n- Public storage inspection returns `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` and cannot mint synchronization or publication authority.\n- Failed pre-visibility stages are atomically moved to unique retained `.pending.abandoned.<attempt>.<random>` quarantine names. Mutable names are never deleted.\n- `limits_sha256` must equal one broker-owned immutable configured profile. Arbitrary signed limit profiles are prohibited; acceptance and replay fail closed on mismatch.\n- Request frames must authenticate with the configured Ed25519 request key. Response frames must authenticate with the key configured for the signed broker incarnation.\n- Artifact-root entry capacity must be enforced across store instances and processes with cancellation-safe root-scoped locking.\n- Do not stage unrelated dirty files. Milestone commits may include only reviewed files.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Phases 0–1 committed as `bebd2ccc`; Phase 2 as `e4a80b43`, `b488b502`, and `0cddd4bb`; Phase 3 as `2fd220b9`; Phase 4 as `ff7e6e81`; Phase 5 pushed as `1fa5d789 feat: add agent thread delegation and structured results`.\n- [x] Historical Phase 5 validation completed: backend 2137 with one skip, sidecar 119 with one skip, frontend 427, plus build, style, and mypy.\n- [x] Large Phase 6 candidate implements integration, immutable trials/results, physical admission, execution receipts, publication/recovery UI, migrations, and fixture Playwright coverage.\n- [x] Architecture A1–A7, corrected gate acceptance, publication acceptance, F6 acceptance, and offline A4 F1–F15 implementation/review were completed and recorded under `/tmp`.\n- [x] Integrated `workspace_replica.py`, its reconciliation suite, and `docs/workspace-os-isolation.md`.\n- [x] Trusted-Git gates, descriptor-backed Git operations, publication crash recovery, workspace repair, prompt-journal settlement, frontend repair handling, and durable repository deletion recovery were implemented.\n- [x] Repository deletion distinguishes imported and managed ownership, preserves imported metadata, uses durable receipts, handles unbound targets, and keeps malformed or legacy state unresolved.\n- [x] Root prepare/reclaim/launch use fixed paths, validated accounts, no-follow descriptors, mount checks, allocation locking, socket pinning, iterative reclaim, and default-disabled gates.\n- [x] Root persists `.executor-identity`, uses synced `.executor-identity.pending` publication, retains quarantine tombstones, and supports interrupted pin states.\n- [x] Linux recovery qualification passed for zero-byte and three-byte pending markers; Linux reclaim qualification passed with `repo=0000` and `home=0777`.\n- [x] Broker lifecycle v2 implements immutable `accepted`, `lifecycle_claimed`, `stage_started`, `stage_outcome`, and `stage_unresolved` events with fixed `prepare → runtime_setup → launch` ordering.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py` and action-bound `LauncherSocketClient.prepare()`, `launch()`, and `reclaim()`.\n- [x] Implemented read-only legacy v1 admission through `inspect_legacy_v1_journal()`, including malformed schema, unsupported version, accepted work, and WAL/SHM sidecar rejection.\n- [x] Implemented fresh-connection exact-event verification after uncertain SQLite commits and `JournalCommitAbsent`.\n- [x] Added `ManagedRootWorker` with bounded framing, serialized actions, separate process group, startup readiness, and kill/reap behavior on timeout or cancellation.\n- [x] Established nested deadlines: root worker 30 seconds, launcher client 35 seconds, broker effect 40 seconds, connection 120 seconds.\n- [x] Separated `LauncherTimeoutError`, `LauncherTransportError`, and `LauncherVerificationError`; clean EOF maps to `transport_unknown`, invalid complete framing to `verification_unknown`.\n- [x] Final independent broker review `d00755d6` found no remaining findings.\n- [x] Focused broker/root lifecycle checks passed 172 tests; strict mypy passed all 126 source files; changed-file static checks passed.\n- [x] Latest broad backend run had 2797 passes, one skip, and three unrelated missing-`HOST` failures; those passed with `HOST=127.0.0.1`. An earlier corrected broad run passed 2799 with one skip.\n- [x] User approved disabled Linux qualification on `yinshi-runtime`; installed wheel, units, hardening drop-ins, and tmpfiles configuration.\n- [x] `systemd-analyze verify` passed; hardening remained intact; root-worker timeout/cancellation and broker v2 replay qualifications passed.\n- [x] Root launcher returned disabled responses for all three actions; legacy accepted v1 work blocked startup without mutation; sockets/services remained inactive; all effect gates remained false; `rft-sandbox` stayed stopped.\n- [x] Architecture oracle selected a separate broker-owned replica journal instead of extending launch lifecycle v2.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py`, tests, and `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay`; opaque fixed-socket relay validation and VM qualification passed. Review `096e5eb4` found no remaining issue.\n- [x] Implemented conflict-index support, deterministic `YNSHRA1\\n` artifact codec, bounded Git subprocess I/O, committed-bundle transport, strict Git-index parsing, and supplemental index-object packs.\n- [x] Committed durable workspace reconciliation as `abff2b2d`, bounded bundles as `2c781b53`, strict index validation as `533df501`, and staged object transport as `4242985d`.\n- [x] Implemented standalone three-artifact publication with descriptor-pinned verification, exact closure checks, safe atomic publication, authority-separated inspection, and broad race/failure coverage.\n- [x] Extended `broker_replica_journal.py` to require exactly `bundle`, `worktree`, and `index_objects`, object format, source-state digest, reconciliation fingerprint, `artifact_set_sha256`, and `limits_sha256`.\n- [x] Expanded `IngestReceipt`, `VerifyReceipt`, `PublishReceipt`, and `ExportReceipt` to bind the exact three-artifact contract and replica authority.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py`, centralizing:\n  - 32-character lowercase hexadecimal operation IDs.\n  - Shared identifier grammar.\n  - Fixed artifact filenames and media types.\n  - Distinct artifact-ID validation.\n  - Canonical limits and artifact-set SHA-256 computation.\n- [x] `BrokerReplicaJournal` now requires `expected_limits_sha256`, `request_public_key`, and a broker-incarnation-keyed `response_public_keys` mapping.\n- [x] Journal acceptance and replay authenticate signed request and response frames, reject unknown signers, bind claimed broker incarnation to the authenticated request, recompute artifact-set identity, and reject duplicate export IDs.\n- [x] Journal schema remains version 1 and SQL shape unchanged. The immutable `journal_id` now stores a random 32-hex prefix plus the 64-hex configuration digest, length 97, binding keys and limit profile.\n- [x] `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` now requires declaration limits to equal its exact configured profile and exposes `limits_sha256`.\n- [x] Implemented `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`:\n  - Fixed broker-owned filenames `committed.bundle`, `worktree.yra`, and `index-objects.pack`.\n  - Bounded partial-read streaming with per-read idle timeout and absolute transfer deadline.\n  - `0700` root/directories and `0600`, regular, single-link artifact enforcement.\n  - Descriptor/path identity checks, digest verification, exact fixed entry sets, and async pinned-open/recheck helpers.\n  - Random live pending names and unique retained quarantine names.\n  - Explicit `absent/live/quarantined/published` attempt state.\n  - Post-publication interruption classified unresolved without quarantining the published result.\n  - Manifest-aware `reconcile_attempts()` with `incoming_verified`, `unverified_final_present`, `unjournaled_present`, quarantine, foreign, and unresolved states.\n  - Root replacement protection by inspecting through retained root descriptors and identities.\n  - `max_root_entries` enforcement across instances/processes using cancellation-safe nonblocking `fcntl.flock`.\n- [x] Publication live pending and quarantine names are now randomized; retained legacy pending state no longer blocks exact retries.\n- [x] Cancellation during async descriptor acquisition drains acquisition and closes the context deterministically.\n- [x] Review cycles `763ded31`, `480936c7`, `0e505f45`, and `bf648f5f` exposed attempt-state, reconciliation, signature, policy, quarantine, and root-capacity issues; all were remediated.\n- [x] Final lock clearance `636247c9` confirmed no remaining findings and no remediation needed.\n- [x] Focused artifact/journal/publication tests reached 91 passes; artifact-store tests reached 23 passes.\n- [x] Combined publication/workspace checks passed 124 tests.\n- [x] Expanded artifact, journal, publication, workspace publication, Git, bundle, object-pack, and runner suite passed 287 tests with two dependency deprecation warnings.\n- [x] Ruff lint, strict mypy, `py_compile`, staged diff checks, and formatting checks passed or had their sole reported formatting discrepancy corrected before commit.\n- [x] Committed nine reviewed files as `7f91105f feat: add authenticated broker replica artifacts`:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\n  - Their four matching tests.\n- [x] Ran RepoPrompt Context Builder for the coordinator under chat `D2C26BA8-46F5-4C12-B0D1-9A89490E8D3B`; it recommended one deep broker-owned coordinator while explicitly noting its mounted checkout is stale.\n- [x] Launched five read-only scouts to map journal, stores, broker runtime, execution/admission, and test interfaces for coordinator implementation.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Recover the concise scout outputs for journal, broker, execution, and tests. Resumed runs include `f0194b0b`, `6a891c47`, `7f24cf81`, and `0f80ca71`; the latter three were explicitly steered to stop inspection and return concise findings.\n- [ ] Design and implement the broker-owned lifecycle coordinator around `BrokerReplicaJournal`, `BrokerArtifactStore`, and `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\n- [ ] Wire external artifact ingestion and pinned verification to typed journal receipts without placing bytes in SQLite.\n- [ ] Implement verified broker-backed managed-Linux admission while keeping native Darwin fail-closed and all gates independently disabled.\n- [ ] Implement graceful broker-to-executor drain, bounded exact-three-artifact export acknowledgment, live-unit checks, and reclaim through the existing root `reclaim` action.\n- [ ] Obtain a clean current-blob repository-deletion review and integrate remaining fail-closed gate tests.\n- [ ] Refresh `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json`.\n- [ ] Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime` after coordinator and admission changes.\n- [ ] Run full Phase 6 acceptance, then begin Phase 7.\n\n### Blocked\n- Phase 6 remains incomplete because lifecycle coordination, managed-Linux admission, drain/export/reclaim orchestration, remaining gate integration, and full acceptance are unfinished.\n- Production execution remains unsupported because `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py` has no verified broker-backed Linux profile.\n- Repository-wide Ruff, format, isort, and Flake8 still include unrelated pre-existing failures, including two `F841` failures in `backend/tests/test_api.py`.\n- Phase 7 remains blocked until Phase 6 receives full independent acceptance.\n- Rebase and push remain pending until all required Phase 6/7 work and validation are complete.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Managed integration scope**: Git worktrees provide isolated child results and deterministic application; Linux is not required for integration itself.\n- **VM purpose**: `yinshi-runtime` supplies stronger OS isolation for untrusted execution.\n- **Privileged launcher**: Root accepts only fixed `prepare`, `launch`, or `reclaim` actions and a lowercase hexadecimal operation ID.\n- **No root stop action**: Drain is graceful only; missing acknowledgment or a live runtime becomes unresolved.\n- **Separate privileged gates**: Prepare, launch, and reclaim each require independent opt-in.\n- **Dedicated roots**: Staging, replicas, quarantine, workload sockets, and protected pins use fixed launcher-owned namespaces.\n- **Prepared namespace**: Broker writes staging; root atomically promotes into protected storage.\n- **Promotion durability**: Sync the destination parent before the source parent.\n- **Executor pool**: Use 32 distinct host UIDs/GIDs named `yinshi-executor-00` through `yinshi-executor-31`.\n- **Allocation authority**: Root-owned `.executor-identity` is the durable allocation record.\n- **Quarantine tombstones**: Reclaim retains only `.executor-identity`; artifact/publication failures retain uniquely named quarantine directories and contents.\n- **Private workload `/run`**: Each transient executor receives only protected `/run/session.sock`.\n- **Broker authentication**: Canonical Ed25519-signed frames supplement Unix peer credentials.\n- **Broker lifecycle v2**: Keep fixed launch stages and preserve legacy v1 as read-only.\n- **Separate replica journal**: Repository ingestion and replica lifecycle state belong in a broker-owned append-only journal, not launch journal v2 or application database rows.\n- **Replica stages**: Use `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`.\n- **Replica public model**: Use `ReplicaAuthority(physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id)` and bind `owner_token` plus authenticated broker incarnation at `claim_authority()`.\n- **Replica decisions and positions**: `ReplicaJournalDecision` exposes `owner_broker_incarnation`; `ReplicaJournalPosition` contains `journal_id`, `sequence`, and `append_receipt_id`.\n- **Replica completion API**: Prefer explicit typed stage completion methods; retain generic rejection and unresolved recording only for terminal failures.\n- **Journal compatibility**: Keep replica schema metadata version 1 and SQL schema unchanged while tightening canonical request/receipt semantics.\n- **Journal configuration binding**: Bind configured request key, response keyring, and exact limits profile into the immutable journal identity; restart fails closed on mismatch.\n- **Terminal response semantics**: Durable state, stage, error code, receipt ID, request binding, broker incarnation, and signature must match exactly during append and replay.\n- **Artifact storage**: Store only bounded metadata and receipts in SQLite; artifact bytes remain external.\n- **Fixed artifact set**: Every publication contains exactly `committed.bundle`, `worktree.yra`, and `index-objects.pack`.\n- **Configured limit profile**: `limits_sha256` represents one broker-owned immutable profile, not an arbitrary caller-selected signed profile.\n- **Artifact-set identity**: Bind operation, repository/workspace IDs, object format, source state, reconciliation fingerprint, all typed references, authority, generation, and limit profile.\n- **Committed-bundle boundary**: Bundles carry only explicit committed refs and optional committed HEAD.\n- **Supplemental object definition**: `index-objects.pack` contains exactly `E = required index OIDs - committed bundle inventory`; all objects in `E` are blobs.\n- **Artifact inspection authority**: Inspection proves current storage only; publication/synchronization authority is minted solely after successful atomic publication.\n- **Artifact attempt naming**: Use broker-generated random live attempt and quarantine names so retained failures never block exact retries.\n- **Artifact capacity**: Enforce root entry limits under root-scoped inter-process `flock`; acquire with `LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB` polling so cancellation cannot retain a lock.\n- **Publication root invariant**: Require exact `0700` before staging and after awaited final verification.\n- **Publication failure classification**: Only confirmed matching pending plus absent final permits safe pre-visibility rejection; moved or unknowable outcomes are unresolved.\n- **Coordinator boundary**: Add one broker-owned deep coordinator. Journal owns durable authority, coordinator sequences effects, executor owns drain/export effects, and broker owns acknowledgment and reclaim eligibility.\n- **Coordinator database boundary**: Use read-copy-close, external effect, reopen-transactional-CAS; never retain SQLite state across `await`.\n- **Conflict-index semantics**: One path has either one stage-zero entry or unique conflict stages 1–3; modeled flags and exact bytes are preserved.\n- **Git-index format**: Support versions 2 and 3 only.\n- **Intent-to-add**: Actual Git uses the nonzero empty-blob OID; zero index OIDs remain rejected.\n- **Artifact envelope**: Keep deterministic magic `YNSHRA1\\n`, version 1, complete flag, and exactly four ordered sections.\n- **Artifact source digest**: Use `SHA256(b\"yinshi-replica-source-v1\\0\" + four raw section digests)`.\n- **Artifact path policy**: Reject unsafe paths, `.git` components, missing parents, invalid topology, duplicates, hardlinks, unsupported kinds, and privilege bits.\n- **Durable stage boundaries**: Accepted intent and stage starts precede effects; confirmed or unresolved outcomes precede progression.\n- **Verified commits**: Close the failed SQLite connection, then compare the exact intended event through a fresh connection.\n- **Startup handling**: Claimed nonterminal work becomes stage-specific `broker_restart_unknown`; unclaimed accepted work remains accepted.\n- **Action-bound launcher protocol**: Requests and responses bind action and operation ID.\n- **Failure classification**: Deadlines use `timeout_unknown`, transport loss uses `transport_unknown`, and complete invalid framing uses `verification_unknown`.\n- **Managed root process**: Timeout or cancellation kills, reaps, and disables the worker instance.\n- **Deletion policy**: Imported repositories preserve user Git metadata; whole-tree quarantine requires explicit managed ownership.\n- **Trusted path policy**: Path location alone never confers ownership.\n- **Gate backstop**: `run_git_bytes` refuses trusted Git when isolation is unsupported.\n- **A4 ownership**: Application owns logical reservation/binding; broker owns effects, synchronization, publication, markers, and physical release.\n- **Stdio relay**: Keep it opaque, fixed to `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, one request per process, with no caller path override.\n- **Relay cleanup**: Exceptional and cancelled exchanges abort transport immediately.\n- **Guard handling**: Never disable TDD Guard; use parent-applied packets and manual red→green checks when necessary.\n- **Phase 7**: Preserve the 20,000-byte contract, 100 pending inbox items, FIFO identity/generation, stop/seal/release ordering, unknown-cost retention, eventual depth three, persisted deadlines, and no scheduler. Default depth remains 1.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Recover and consolidate outputs from scout runs `f0194b0b`, `6a891c47`, `7f24cf81`, and `0f80ca71`; resolve exact production interfaces rather than relying on stale RepoPrompt assumptions.\n2. Write focused red tests for one broker-owned replica lifecycle coordinator, including gates, restart, cancellation, exact stage progression, no SQLite handle across effects, and idempotent duplicate handling.\n3. Implement coordinator ingestion, pinned verification, publication, and admission using `BrokerReplicaJournal`, `BrokerArtifactStore`, and `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`.\n4. Add fail-closed managed-Linux admission and keep native Darwin unsupported.\n5. Add graceful drain, exact three-reference export acknowledgment, live-unit verification, and reclaim through only `LauncherSocketClient.reclaim()`.\n6. Integrate remaining fail-closed gate tests and obtain repository-deletion acceptance.\n7. Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime`, preserving disabled gates, inactive sockets/services, and stopped `rft-sandbox`.\n8. Run complete backend, sidecar, frontend, desktop, documentation, static, and platform validation.\n9. Obtain full current-blob Phase 6 acceptance, refresh the checkpoint, then implement Phase 7 from `.pi-subagents/artifacts/8a18879f_planner_0_output.md`.\n10. Rebase and push only after final approval.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Main checkout: `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`; branch `main`.\n- Latest milestone commit: `7f91105f feat: add authenticated broker replica artifacts`.\n- Earlier Phase 6 commits:\n  - `4242985d feat: transport staged replica objects`\n  - `533df501 feat: validate replica Git index state`\n  - `2c781b53 feat: add bounded committed replica bundles`\n  - `abff2b2d feat: add durable workspace replica reconciliation`\n- The worktree remains heavily dirty with unrelated Phase 6 changes. The nine artifact/publication files are now committed rather than untracked.\n- Current coordinator RepoPrompt chat: `D2C26BA8-46F5-4C12-B0D1-9A89490E8D3B`; previous lifecycle-plan chat: `13DA0FE2-01E7-45DC-92FF-71B0D5AB9524`. Both mounted contexts are stale.\n- Coordinator scout runs:\n  - Initial journal `bf54b4a3`, broker `938d1772`, execution `ac89331f`, tests `87292d3b`.\n  - Resumed concise runs `f0194b0b`, `6a891c47`, `7f24cf81`, and `0f80ca71`.\n  - `6a891c47`, `7f24cf81`, and `0f80ca71` were steered to stop and return concise findings.\n- Final artifact review progression:\n  - `763ded31` and `480936c7` found blockers.\n  - `0e505f45` cleared five regions but found process-local capacity locking.\n  - `bf648f5f` found cancelable blocking `flock`.\n  - `636247c9` confirmed the nonblocking cancellation-safe lock fix and reported no remediation needed.\n- Final relevant validation:\n  - 23 artifact-store tests passed.\n  - 91 artifact/journal/publication tests passed.\n  - 124 workspace publication plus artifact/journal tests passed.\n  - 287 expanded artifact/Git/publication tests passed.\n  - Ruff lint, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and diff checks passed; the final reported formatting discrepancy was corrected before commit.\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` constructor now requires exact limit profile and trusted request/response keys.\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts()` requires a manifest mapping and only emits `incoming_verified` after exact retained-root inspection.\n- VM `yinshi-runtime` is running the previously qualified wheel, not the latest local commits.\n- Production v2 journal is absent; accepted legacy v1 state intentionally blocks broker startup.\n- VM sockets are static and inactive; all related services are inactive; every effect gate remains false.\n- `rft-sandbox` remains stopped.\n- Phase 7 plan remains `.pi-subagents/artifacts/8a18879f_planner_0_output.md`.\n- `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json` predates the latest artifact/journal/publication milestone and must be refreshed.\n- Full backend validation must use `/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/.venv/bin/pytest`.\n- Passing local and disabled-VM checks do not establish full Phase 6 acceptance.\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nThe user reported that async subagent `scout` run `0f80ca71` needed attention after 60 seconds of inactivity and asked that its status be inspected before deciding whether to steer, resume, or interrupt it.\n\n## Early Progress\n- Waited on all active async runs; three required attention: `7f24cf81`, `6a891c47`, and `0f80ca71`.\n- Inspected transcript/status for all three runs.\n- All three were still `running` in scout step 0, not paused or failed.\n- `6a891c47` and `0f80ca71` had each begun working and invoked one tool; their transcript tails showed session/log content but were heavily truncated.\n- `7f24cf81` showed no substantive activity yet beyond its task instructions/schema.\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- No steering, resume, or interrupt action had yet been taken.\n- The target run `0f80ca71` remained live and was recently inactive for about 17 seconds at inspection, so a top-level `steer` nudge would be the appropriate next action if inactivity persisted.\n- The two other live runs may likewise need monitoring or steering.\n\n<read-files>\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/027713c4_planner_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/05bb63fe_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/0a089013_worker-expert_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/1499b7eb_scout_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/274e0d6c_oracle_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/3777e15d_final-review_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/3c61b813_test-writer_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/4596118a_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/678fba88_worker-expert_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/678fba88_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/71db4063_worker-expert_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/b013399f_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/ea031cf8_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/f0d3d683_final-review_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/fcc14690_planner_0_output.md\n/Users/user/.agents/skills/rp-build/SKILL.md\n/Users/user/.agents/skills/rp-deep-plan/SKILL.md\n/Users/user/.agents/skills/rp-review/SKILL.md\n/Users/user/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/skills/pi-subagents/SKILL.md\n/Users/user/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/skills/pi-subagents/references/execution-controls.md\n/Users/user/.pi/agent/packages/pi-frontend-standards