{"type":"message","id":"99466145","parentId":"0a210bfe","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:56:33.331Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Investigating plan extraction inconsistencies**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f4bf076887d098451b0637849432\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Investigating plan extraction inconsistencies**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_II5avEwZa3p882iINprkENyt|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f4c0cf7887d0bf5d96b166b2e65f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/user/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md","offset":1160,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":2055,"output":78,"cacheRead":53504,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":38,"totalTokens":55637,"cost":{"input":0.010275000000000001,"output":0.00234,"cacheRead":0.026751999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.039367}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789260988425,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f4bcdf6487d081274c3fe1783381","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"2cb5635d","parentId":"99466145","timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:56:33.373Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_II5avEwZa3p882iINprkENyt|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f4c0cf7887d0bf5d96b166b2e65f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n- Detect parent cleanliness\n- Capture an immutable parent snapshot\n- Create child branches and worktrees from exact refs\n- Record and clean hidden refs\n- Finalize child filesystem state\n- Create a single synthetic result commit\n- Calculate changed files\n- Provision temporary integration worktrees\n- Remove partial workspaces after failed provisioning\n\nSuggested types:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ProvisionedChildWorkspace:\n    workspace_id: str\n    path: str\n    branch: str\n    base_kind: str\n    base_commit: str\n    snapshot_ref: str | None\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FinalizedThreadGitResult:\n    base_commit: str\n    result_commit: str\n    result_ref: str\n    changed_files: tuple[ChangedFile, ...]\n```\n\nSuggested methods:\n\n```python\nasync def provision_child(...)\nasync def finalize_child(...)\nasync def discard_partial_child(...)\nasync def check_integration(...)\nasync def integrate_child(...)\n```\n\nUse the existing repository lifecycle lock. Release all database connections before Git or filesystem work.\n\n### 13.3 Prompt-run terminal observer\n\nExtend `PromptJournal` with an optional observer:\n\n```python\nRunTerminalObserver = Callable[\n    [RuntimeContext, str, str, str],\n    Awaitable[None],\n]\n```\n\nArguments:\n\n```text\nruntime context\nsession ID\nrun ID\nterminal status\n```\n\nAfter the prompt journal commits the terminal run state:\n\n1. Invoke the observer.\n2. Preserve the prompt run's terminal state when finalization fails.\n3. Record a safe reconciliation error.\n4. Retry finalization during startup or thread-tree reads.\n\nBehavior:\n\n- Root session: no-op.\n- Delegated child `completed`: finalize Git and seal result.\n- Delegated child `failed`: preserve partial work and record failure.\n- Delegated child `cancelled`: preserve partial work and record cancellation.\n- Delegated child `interrupted`: preserve state and permit explicit retry.\n\n### 13.4 Sidecar orchestration bridge\n\nExtend:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/sidecar.py\n```\n\nAdd:\n\n- Connection write lock\n- Query-bound capability\n- Orchestration frame validation\n- Handler task tracking\n- Request and response bounds\n- Handler cancellation and draining\n- Safe error mapping\n- Internal-frame filtering\n\nKeep each child prompt run on its own sidecar connection.\n\n## 14. Spawn workflow\n\nImplement spawn as an idempotent, recoverable operation.\n\n### Step 1: Authorize and validate\n\nDerive the parent from the active authenticated execution context.\n\nValidate:\n\n- Parent exists\n- Parent belongs to the current tenant\n- Parent runtime is available\n- Feature flag is enabled\n- Requested model exists at that runtime\n- Task and context meet bounds\n- Parent depth permits another level\n- Direct-child, active-descendant, tree-total, and per-turn limits permit another child\n- Parent repository and workspace are valid\n\nUse `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` around limit checks and delegation reservation so concurrent spawn calls cannot exceed limits.\n\n### Step 2: Reserve the delegation\n\nInsert:\n\n```text\nstatus = provisioning\nchild_session_id = null\nchild_workspace_id = null\n```\n\nIdempotency:\n\n```text\nUNIQUE(parent_session_id, idempotency_key)\n```\n\nOn retry:\n\n- Return the existing queued, running, or terminal child.\n- Resume or reconcile a provisioning record.\n- Return a stable failed result for a failed reservation.\n- Require a new idempotency key for a deliberate new attempt.\n\n### Step 3: Capture the parent base\n\nFor a clean parent, resolve `HEAD`.\n\nFor a dirty parent, create a hidden snapshot without touching the real index, branch, or working tree.\n\nSuggested algorithm:\n\n1. Create a private temporary index file.\n2. Set `GIT_INDEX_FILE` only for the snapshot subprocesses.\n3. Run `git read-tree HEAD` against the alternate index.\n4. Apply existing secret guardrails.\n5. Run `git add -A -- .` against the alternate index.\n6. Run `git write-tree`.\n7. Run `git commit-tree` with the parent `HEAD` as parent.\n8. Update `refs/yinshi/snapshots/<delegation-id>`.\n9. Delete the temporary index.\n10. Verify the parent `HEAD`, branch, real index, and working tree are unchanged.\n\nInitial restrictions:\n\n- Reject dirty submodules.\n- Reject snapshots over configured file-count or byte limits.\n- Exclude ignored files.\n- Reject protected secret paths.\n- Preserve tracked symlinks as Git symlinks.\n- Support empty repositories through the existing empty-root logic.\n- Record `base_kind` as `head` or `snapshot`.\n\n### Step 4: Create the child worktree\n\nGenerate:\n\n```text\nyinshi/thread-<short-delegation-id>\n```\n\nCreate the child branch and worktree from the exact base commit.\n\nInsert a workspace row:\n\n```text\nkind = delegated\nparent_workspace_id = parent.workspace_id\n```\n\n### Step 5: Create the child session\n\nIn one transaction:\n\n1. Insert the child session against the child workspace.\n2. Set title and model.\n3. Update the delegation with child session and workspace IDs.\n4. Set delegation state to `queued`.\n5. Commit.\n\n[1132 more lines in file. Use offset=1360 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789260993373}}
