":{"mode":"live-card","repoRelation":"same","repoLabel":"yinshi"},"missionId":"a608bb03-0736-4ddf-86bb-75f3b87d8622","missionPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/missions/a608bb03-0736-4ddf-86bb-75f3b87d8622.json","mission":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"a608bb03-0736-4ddf-86bb-75f3b87d8622","title":"Implement broker-owned replica lifecycle coordinator on current shared checkout. Do not commit.","objective":"Implement broker-owned replica lifecycle coordinator on current shared checkout. Do not commit.\nRoute reason: GLM Max because seven ordered stages interact with durable journal authority, deadlines, cancellation, restart reconciliation, signed terminal responses, and idempotency.\nOnly modify or create: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py, backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py, and broker_replica_journal.py only if a minimal immutable incomplete-lifecycle field is required. Preserve all unrelated dirty changes.\nUse tests first. Run focused red test before production code, then green focused tests. TDD Guard must remain enabled. If TDD Guard blocks because no request is bound, report exact block and provide edit packets instead of bypassing it.\nCurrent exact journal API: accept(request, request_frame, authority), claim_authority(request, owner_token, broker_incarnation), begin_stage, typed complete_* methods, record_rejected(status, receipt, signed response), record_unresolved(reason, signed response), status, incomplete_lifecycles. Reclaim completion requires signed completed response. Rejections and unresolved outcomes require exact signed terminal responses.\nImplement one stateless BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator plus explicit typed stage effects. All seven effects are required at construction. Fixed order: ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal calls finish before each await. Coordinator receives authenticated BrokerRequest and raw signed frame. It owns one random owner token and configured broker private key. It must not authenticate peer UID or transport itself.\nUse an immutable ReplicaLifecycleContext containing request, authority, owner token. Define StageReconciliation with outcomes completed, not_applied, unknown. Require receipt only for completed. Define bounded domain exceptions StageRejected(status, receipt_id) and StageOutcomeUnknown(reason). Validate status/reason later through journal.\nApply behavior: accept and claim. Return terminal durable response for replays. If another owner is in flight, wait only boundedly by checking journal with sleep and then raise a stable owner-active error. Owner runs stages serially. Persist stage start before effect. Use absolute monotonic deadline per effect and an asyncio task with bounded wait. Do not cancel uncertain effect tasks on timeout or caller cancellation. Retain bounded abandoned tasks and consume their result later, matching execution_broker precedent. Timeout or caller cancellation records exact stage unresolved before returning or re-raising. Never append completion from late tasks.\nBuild terminal response frames with create_signed_response. Exact result fields must be stage, state, optional code, optional receipt_id. Error equals code for rejected and unresolved. Reclaim success response has state completed, stage reclaim, receipt_id.\nRecovery: extend IncompleteReplicaLifecycle minimally to include immutable ReplicaAuthority if needed. Parse and authenticate its stored request frame through journal-owned trusted request parsing. Better add a BrokerReplicaJournal public method that returns typed request plus authority only if essential. Do not expose database objects. For stage_started false, begin stage then apply normally. For stage_started true, call effect.reconcile once under fresh bounded deadline. completed persists receipt then continues later stages. not_applied reapplies same stage. unknown persists stage-specific unresolved. Any reconciliation timeout, cancellation, malformed result, or unexpected error persists unresolved. Startup recovery processes every incomplete serially. A lifecycle owned by another broker incarnation becomes broker_restart_unknown without effects.\nPersistence errors must escape. Do not catch ReplicaJournalError into effect outcomes. Catch effect errors only around awaited effects. Cancellation unresolved must be persisted synchronously, then re-raised.\nTests must cover exact seven-stage order, each start visible before effect, terminal replay without effects, rejection, unknown, timeout late task, cancellation late task, other-owner bounded wait, receipt type mismatch fail closed, started-stage reconciliation completed/not-applied/unknown, startup broker-incarnation mismatch, no journal call during active effect, and reclaim signed response. Keep tests deterministic and concise.\nUse backend/.venv/bin/pytest and repository style.","status":"waiting","createdAt":"2026-09-13T00:57:51.233Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-13T01:17:55.745Z","runs":[{"runId":"call_PNkiwM9VvymC3NmU4jbrybft|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5f4f49a6c87d09ab1a870d500776a","mode":"workflow","agent":"worker-advanced","status":"paused","startedAt":"2026-09-13T01:17:55.743Z","completedAt":"2026-09-13T01:17:55.743Z","usage":{"tokens":171980}}],"decisions":[],"artifacts":[{"kind":"output","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/8e834b23_worker-advanced_0_output.md"},{"kind":"other","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/8e834b23_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl","description":"Child transcript"}],"receipts":[],"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","ownerSessionId":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64.jsonl","summary":"Workflow failed: Error: Run 'coordinator-core' failed: Detached for intercom coordination: worker-advanced. Reply to the supervisor request first, then wait with subagent_wait({ id: \"8e834b23\" }). Use subagent({ action: