{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent_supervisor_request","content":"Subagent needs a supervisor decision.\nRun: 8e834b23\nAgent: worker-advanced\nChild index: 0\nChild intercom target: subagent-worker-advanced-8e834b23-1\n\nBLOCKED — exact TDD Guard block, repeated on two write attempts (backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py, then a probe file):\n\n\"TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.\"\n\nState: I have read-only tools + write/edit, but every source write is refused by the guard because no TDD request is bound to this child branch. No tdd_test/tdd_* tools are exposed to me, and shell-based file writes are blocked, so I cannot (a) write the test file, (b) observe the red failure, or (c) write production code. My planned work is fully designed: new module backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py (stateless BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator, immutable ReplicaLifecycleContext, StageReconciliation, StageRejected/StageOutcomeUnknown, bounded abandoned-task set per execution_broker precedent), new tests backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py (13 focused behaviors incl. seven-stage order, replay, rejection/unknown, timeout+cancellation late tasks, other-owner bounded wait, receipt-type fail-closed, recovery completed/not_applied/unknown, broker-restart-unknown, no-journal-during-effect, reclaim signed response), and a minimal broker_replica_journal.py extension (immutable authority field on IncompleteReplicaLifecycle + public authenticated_request(lifecycle) using journal-owned trusted parsing).\n\nDecision needed: (1) Can you bind/enable a TDD request for this branch so I can perform the real write→red→implement→green loop and run focused checks? or (2) Should I fall back per the task packet: report the exact block and deliver complete edit packets (full file contents + exact journal edits) in my final response without executed validation?\n\nReply with: subagent_supervisor({ action: \"reply\", replyTo: