{"type":"message","id":"3edd49c5","parentId":"516a1965","timestamp":"2026-09-13T01:23:52.760Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_VjV7HCUuVOEgMsajddAHfCuv|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa5fb28092c87d0a629e057c352c7c6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 12 assistant turns (soft limit 12, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nSupervisor confirmed fallback option 2. I'm delivering complete edit packets with no further write attempts. One detail to fix from my drafted test (the typed `complete_*` journal methods take no `stage` kwarg, so the recorded trace must expect `None` there), then I'll compose the full deliverable.\n\n---\n\n## Blocker report (exact)\n\nTDD Guard refused every source write (two attempts, including a probe) with:\n\n```\nTDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.\n```\n\nNo `tdd_*` tools are exposed to this child session, shell file writes are blocked, so neither the red test nor the implementation could be materialized on disk. Per supervisor decision (fallback option 2), the complete edit packets follow. **Nothing has been written to the working tree; no commits.**\n\n---\n\n## Packet A — new file: `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\n\nBehavior-facing tests, written first per TDD (apply alone → red; with Packets B+C → green).\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Check broker-owned replica lifecycle coordination against the durable journal.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport sqlite3\nfrom dataclasses import FrozenInstanceError\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom time import monotonic\n\nimport pytest\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import (\n    BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n    BrokerRequest,\n    JsonValue,\n    create_signed_request,\n    create_signed_response,\n    parse_signed_request,\n    verify_broker_response,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    AdmissionReceipt,\n    ArtifactReference,\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    DrainReceipt,\n    ExportReceipt,\n    IngestReceipt,\n    PublishReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    VerifyReceipt,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_lifecycle import (\n    BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator,\n    BrokerReplicaOwnerActive,\n    ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n    StageOutcomeUnknown,\n    StageRejected,\n    StageReconciliation,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.replica_artifact_contract import (\n    compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256,\n)\n\nAPPLICATION_ID = \"yinshi-desktop\"\nDATABASE_INCARNATION = \"d\" * 32\nBROKER_INCARNATION = \"b\" * 32\nRESTARTED_BROKER_INCARNATION = \"c\" * 32\nOWNER_TOKEN = \"owner_token_00000000000000000000\"\nREQUEST_PRIVATE_KEY = Ed25519PrivateKey.generate()\nRESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY = Ed25519PrivateKey.generate()\nSTAGES = (\"ingest\", \"verify\", \"publish\", \"admission\", \"drain\", \"export\", \"reclaim\")\nAUTHORITY = ReplicaAuthority(\n    physical_target_id=\"target_00000000000000000000000000\",\n    replica_generation=3,\n    execution_owner_id=\"execution_owner_0000000000000000\",\n)\nBUNDLE = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"bundle_00000000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"1\" * 64,\n    byte_length=123,\n)\nWORKTREE = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"worktree_0000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"2\" * 64,\n    byte_length=456,\n)\nINDEX_OBJECTS = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"index_objects_0000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"7\" * 64,\n    byte_length=789,\n)\nLIMITS_SHA256 = \"8\" * 64\nRECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID = \"reclaim_0000000000000000000000\"\nINGEST_RECEIPT = IngestReceipt(\n    receipt_id=\"receipt_ingest_000000000000000000\",\n    bundle=BUNDLE,\n    worktree=WORKTREE,\n    REDACTED,\n)\n\n\ndef artifact_json(reference: ArtifactReference) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_id\": reference.artifact_id,\n        \"byte_length\": reference.byte_length,\n        \"sha256\": reference.sha256,\n    }\n\n\ndef artifact_set_sha256(operation_id: str) -> str:\n    return compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256(\n        operation_id=operation_id,\n        repository_id=\"repository_0000000000000000000000\",\n        workspace_id=\"workspace_000000000000000000000000\",\n        physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n        replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n        execution_owner_id=AUTHORITY.execution_owner_id,\n        object_format=\"sha256\",\n        source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n        reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n        bundle={\n            \"role\": \"committed_bundle\",\n            \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.yinshi.git-bundle.v1\",\n            **artifact_json(BUNDLE),\n        },\n        worktree={\n            \"role\": \"worktree\",\n            \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.yinshi.replica-worktree.v1\",\n            **artifact_json(WORKTREE),\n        },\n        index_objects={\n            \"role\": \"index_objects\",\n            \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.yinshi.git-index-objects-pack.v1\",\n            **artifact_json(INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        },\n        limits_sha256=LIMITS_SHA256,\n    )\n\n\nARTIFACT_SET_SHA256 = artifact_set_sha256(\"a\" * 32)\n\n\ndef request_payload() -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_set_sha256\": ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n        \"bundle\": artifact_json(BUNDLE),\n        \"index_objects\": artifact_json(INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        \"limits_sha256\": LIMITS_SHA256,\n        \"object_format\": \"sha256\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": \"3\" * 64,\n        \"repository_id\": \"repository_0000000000000000000000\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\": \"4\" * 64,\n        \"workspace_id\": \"workspace_000000000000000000000000\",\n        \"worktree\": artifact_json(WORKTREE),\n    }\n\n\ndef signed_request() -> tuple[BrokerRequest, bytes]:\n    frame = create_signed_request(\n        private_key=REQUEST_PRIVATE_KEY,\n        protocol_version=BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n        database_incarnation=DATABASE_INCARNATION,\n        connection_sequence=1,\n        operation_id=\"a\" * 32,\n        request_type=\"replica.lifecycle\",\n        nonce=\"nonce_00000000001\",\n        payload=request_payload(),\n    )\n    return parse_signed_request(frame, public_key=REQUEST_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key()), frame\n\n\ndef receipt_for(stage: str) -> object:\n    receipt_id = f\"receipt_{stage}_000000000000000000\"\n    if stage == \"ingest\":\n        return INGEST_RECEIPT\n    if stage == \"verify\":\n        return VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n        )\n    if stage == \"publish\":\n        return PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n            execution_owner_id=AUTHORITY.execution_owner_id,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n            artifact_set_sha256=ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n        )\n    if stage == \"admission\":\n        return AdmissionReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            execution_owner_id=AUTHORITY.execution_owner_id,\n            runtime_unit_id=\"runtime_0000000000000000000000000\",\n            session_socket_sha256=\"6\" * 64,\n        )\n    if stage == \"drain\":\n        return DrainReceipt(\n            drain_ack_receipt_id=\"drain_ack_0000000000000000000000\",\n            quiescence_receipt_id=\"quiescence_00000000000000000000\",\n        )\n    if stage == \"export\":\n        return ExportReceipt(\n            export_receipt_id=\"export_000000000000000000000000\",\n            bundle=BUNDLE,\n            worktree=WORKTREE,\n            REDACTED,\n        )\n    if stage == \"reclaim\":\n        return ReclaimReceipt(reclaim_receipt_id=RECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID)\n    raise AssertionError(stage)\n\n\ndef completed_outcome(stage: str) -> StageReconciliation:\n    return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"completed\", receipt=receipt_for(stage))\n\n\ndef journal(tmp_path: Path) -> BrokerReplicaJournal:\n    return BrokerReplicaJournal(\n        tmp_path / \"replica.sqlite3\",\n        application_id=APPLICATION_ID,\n        expected_limits_sha256=LIMITS_SHA256,\n        REDACTED.public_key(),\n        response_public_keys={BROKER_INCARNATION: RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key()},\n    )\n\n\nclass ScriptedEffect:\n    \"\"\"Test double exposing apply and reconcile with scripted outcomes.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        stage: str,\n        *,\n        apply: object = None,\n        reconcile: object = None,\n        trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        self.stage = stage\n        self.contexts: list[ReplicaLifecycleContext] = []\n        self.apply_started = asyncio.Event()\n        self._apply = apply\n        self._reconcile = reconcile\n        self._trace = trace\n\n    async def apply(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        return await self._dispatch(\"apply\", self._apply, context)\n\n    async def reconcile(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        return await self._dispatch(\"reconcile\", self._reconcile, context)\n\n    async def _dispatch(\n        self,\n        method: str,\n        action: object,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation:\n        if self._trace is not None:\n            self._trace.append((\"effect\", method, self.stage))\n        self.contexts.append(context)\n        if method == \"apply\":\n            self.apply_started.set()\n        if action is None:\n            raise AssertionError(f\"replica {self.stage} {method} must not run\")\n        if isinstance(action, BaseException):\n            raise action\n        if isinstance(action, StageReconciliation):\n            return action\n        return await action(context)\n\n\nclass RecordingJournal:\n    \"\"\"Test double recording every journal call in issue order.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, inner: BrokerReplicaJournal) -> None:\n        self._inner = inner\n        self.calls: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n\n    def __getattr__(self, name: str) -> object:\n        attribute = getattr(self._inner, name)\n        if not callable(attribute):\n            return attribute\n\n        def record(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> object:\n            stage = kwargs.get(\"stage\")\n            self.calls.append((\"journal\", name, stage if isinstance(stage, str) else None))\n            return attribute(*args, **kwargs)\n\n        return record\n\n\ndef default_effects(\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, ScriptedEffect]:\n    return {\n        stage: ScriptedEffect(stage, apply=completed_outcome(stage), trace=trace)\n        for stage in STAGES\n    }\n\n\ndef configured_coordinator(\n    replica: object,\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] | None = None,\n    *,\n    broker_incarnation: str = BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    effects: dict[str, ScriptedEffect] | None = None,\n    **timing: float,\n) -> BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    staged = effects if effects is not None else default_effects(trace)\n    options: dict[str, float] = {\n        \"effect_timeout_seconds\": 5.0,\n        \"owner_wait_seconds\": 0.5,\n        \"owner_poll_seconds\": 0.02,\n    }\n    options.update(timing)\n    return BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator(\n        replica,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        broker_incarnation=broker_incarnation,\n        broker_private_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY,\n        effects=staged,\n        **options,\n    )\n\n\ndef start_started_lifecycle(\n    replica: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    request: BrokerRequest,\n    frame: bytes,\n    *,\n    stage: str = \"ingest\",\n) -> None:\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    replica.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n    replica.begin_stage(request, owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN, stage=stage)\n\n\ndef drive_journal_to_completed(replica: BrokerReplicaJournal, request: BrokerRequest) -> None:\n    for stage in STAGES:\n        replica.begin_stage(request, owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN, stage=stage)\n        receipt = receipt_for(stage)\n        final = None\n        if stage == \"reclaim\":\n            assert isinstance(receipt, ReclaimReceipt)\n            final = create_signed_response(\n                request,\n                private_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY,\n                status=\"ok\",\n                error=None,\n                result={\n                    \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n                    \"state\": \"completed\",\n                    \"receipt_id\": receipt.reclaim_receipt_id,\n                },\n            )\n        getattr(replica, f\"complete_{stage}\")(\n            request,\n            owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n            receipt=receipt,\n            response_frame=final,\n        )\n\n\ndef event_rows(path: Path) -> list[tuple[str, str | None]]:\n    with sqlite3.connect(path) as database:\n        return [\n            (str(event_type), stage)\n            for event_type, stage in database.execute(\n                \"SELECT event_type, stage FROM replica_journal_events ORDER BY event_id\"\n            ).fetchall()\n        ]\n\n\ndef result_json(frame: bytes | None) -> dict[str, object]:\n    assert frame is not None\n    value = json.loads(frame)\n    assert isinstance(value[\"result\"], dict)\n    return value[\"result\"]\n\n\ndef test_constructor_requires_all_seven_stage_effects(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    effects = default_effects()\n    del effects[\"drain\"]\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    incomplete = default_effects()\n    incomplete[\"export\"] = object()  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError):\n        configured_coordinator(replica, effects=incomplete)\n\n\nasync def test_run_follows_exact_stage_order_and_persists_each_start_before_effect(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    effects = default_effects(trace)\n    recorded = RecordingJournal(replica)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(recorded, trace=trace)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    expected: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = [\n        (\"journal\", \"accept\", None),\n        (\"journal\", \"claim_authority\", None),\n    ]\n    for stage in STAGES:\n        expected.append((\"journal\", \"begin_stage\", stage))\n        expected.append((\"effect\", \"apply\", stage))\n        expected.append((\"journal\", \"complete_\" + stage, None))\n    assert trace == expected\n    assert event_rows(replica.path)[-1] == (\"stage_outcome\", \"reclaim\")\n    assert result_json(response) == {\n        \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n        \"state\": \"completed\",\n        \"receipt_id\": RECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID,\n    }\n\n    context = effects[\"ingest\"].contexts[0]\n    assert isinstance(context, ReplicaLifecycleContext)\n    assert context.request == request\n    assert context.authority == AUTHORITY\n    with sqlite3.connect(replica.path) as database:\n        owner = database.execute(\n            \"SELECT owner_token FROM replica_journal_events \"\n            \"WHERE event_type = 'authority_claimed'\"\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n    assert context.owner_token == owner\n    with pytest.raises(FrozenInstanceError):\n        context.owner_token = \"mutated_owner_000000000000000\"\n\n\nasync def test_reclaim_success_returns_broker_signed_completed_response(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    value = json.loads(response)\n    assert value[\"status\"] == \"ok\"\n    assert value[\"error\"] is None\n    verified = verify_broker_response(\n        response,\n        public_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key(),\n        expected_request=request,\n    )\n    assert verified.result == value[\"result\"]\n    decision = replica.status(request)\n    assert decision.state == \"completed\"\n    assert decision.stage == \"reclaim\"\n    assert decision.response_frame == response\n\n\nasync def test_terminal_replay_returns_durable_frame_without_effects(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    first = configured_coordinator(replica)\n    response = await first.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    poison = {\n        stage: ScriptedEffect(\n            stage,\n            apply=RuntimeError(\"must not run\"),\n            reconcile=RuntimeError(\"must not run\"),\n            trace=trace,\n        )\n        for stage in STAGES\n    }\n    second = configured_coordinator(replica, trace=trace, effects=poison)\n    assert await second.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == response\n    assert trace == []\n\n\nasync def test_stage_rejection_records_exact_signed_terminal_response(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"ingest\",\n        apply=StageRejected(\"artifact_rejected\", \"rejected_receipt_00000000001\"),\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    value = json.loads(response)\n    assert value[\"status\"] == \"error\"\n    assert value[\"error\"] == \"artifact_rejected\"\n    assert value[\"result\"] == {\n        \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n        \"state\": \"rejected\",\n        \"code\": \"artifact_rejected\",\n        \"receipt_id\": \"rejected_receipt_00000000001\",\n    }\n    verify_broker_response(\n        response,\n        public_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key(),\n        expected_request=request,\n    )\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"rejected\"\n    assert event_rows(replica.path)[-1] == (\"stage_rejected\", \"ingest\")\n    assert await configured_coordinator(replica).run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == response\n\n\nasync def test_stage_unknown_reason_records_exact_unresolved_terminal_response(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"publish\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"publish\",\n        apply=StageOutcomeUnknown(\"publication_unknown\"),\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    value = json.loads(response)\n    assert value[\"status\"] == \"error\"\n    assert value[\"error\"] == \"publication_unknown\"\n    assert value[\"result\"] == {\n        \"stage\": \"publish\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"publication_unknown\",\n    }\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"unresolved\"\n    assert await configured_coordinator(replica).run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == response\n\n\nasync def test_effect_timeout_records_unresolved_and_consumes_late_task_result(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n\n    async def late_unknown(context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.4)\n        raise StageOutcomeUnknown(\"verification_unknown\")\n\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"verify\"] = ScriptedEffect(\"verify\", apply=late_unknown)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects, effect_timeout_seconds=0.05)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    assert result_json(response) == {\n        \"stage\": \"verify\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"timeout_unknown\",\n    }\n    snapshot = event_rows(replica.path)\n    assert snapshot[-2:] == [(\"stage_started\", \"verify\"), (\"stage_unresolved\", \"verify\")]\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"unresolved\"\n\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.45)\n    assert event_rows(replica.path) == snapshot\n    assert coordinator._abandoned_effects == set()\n\n\nasync def test_caller_cancellation_records_unresolved_and_late_task_completes(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    finished = asyncio.Event()\n\n    async def hanging(context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.4)\n        finished.set()\n        return completed_outcome(\"ingest\")\n\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\"ingest\", apply=hanging)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    runner = asyncio.create_task(coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY))\n    await asyncio.wait_for(effects[\"ingest\"].apply_started.wait(), timeout=2)\n    runner.cancel()\n    with pytest.raises(asyncio.CancelledError):\n        await runner\n\n    assert result_json(replica.status(request).response_frame) == {\n        \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"cancellation_unknown\",\n    }\n    snapshot = event_rows(replica.path)\n    assert not finished.is_set()\n\n    await asyncio.wait_for(finished.wait(), timeout=2)\n    assert event_rows(replica.path) == snapshot\n    assert coordinator._abandoned_effects == set()\n\n\nasync def test_other_owner_bounded_wait_raises_stable_owner_active_error(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    replica.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(\n        replica,\n        trace=trace,\n        owner_wait_seconds=0.1,\n        owner_poll_seconds=0.02,\n    )\n\n    started = monotonic()\n    with pytest.raises(BrokerReplicaOwnerActive):\n        await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert monotonic() - started >= 0.1\n    assert trace == []\n\n    drive_journal_to_completed(replica, request)\n    terminal = replica.status(request).response_frame\n    assert await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == terminal\n    assert trace == []\n\n\nasync def test_receipt_type_mismatch_fails_closed_before_completion(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    wrong = VerifyReceipt(\n        receipt_id=\"receipt_ingest_000000000000000000\",\n        bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n        worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n        REDACTED.sha256,\n        source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n        reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n        artifact_set_sha256=ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n    )\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"ingest\",\n        apply=StageReconciliation(outcome=\"completed\", receipt=wrong),\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError):\n        await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert event_rows(replica.path) == [\n        (\"accepted\", None),\n        (\"authority_claimed\", None),\n        (\"stage_started\", \"ingest\"),\n    ]\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"in_flight\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    (\"marker\", \"reconcile\", \"expected_state\", \"expected_code\"),\n    [\n        (\n            \"completed\",\n            StageReconciliation(outcome=\"completed\", receipt=INGEST_RECEIPT),\n            \"completed\",\n            None,\n        ),\n        (\"not_applied\", StageReconciliation(outcome=\"not_applied\"), \"completed\", None),\n        (\n            \"unknown\",\n            StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"verification_unknown\"),\n            \"unresolved\",\n            \"verification_unknown\",\n        ),\n        (\"error\", RuntimeError(\"unexpected effect failure\"), \"unresolved\", \"transfer_unknown\"),\n    ],\n)\nasync def test_recovery_of_started_stage_reconciles_outcomes(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n    marker: str,\n    reconcile: object,\n    expected_state: str,\n    expected_code: str | None,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    start_started_lifecycle(replica, request, frame)\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    effects = default_effects(trace)\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"ingest\",\n        apply=completed_outcome(\"ingest\"),\n        reconcile=reconcile,\n        trace=trace,\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, trace=trace, effects=effects)\n\n    await coordinator.recover_incomplete()\n\n    decision = replica.status(request)\n    assert decision.state == expected_state\n    if expected_code is None:\n        assert result_json(decision.response_frame) == {\n            \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n            \"state\": \"completed\",\n            \"receipt_id\": RECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID,\n        }\n    else:\n        assert result_json(decision.response_frame) == {\n            \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n            \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n            \"code\": expected_code,\n        }\n    reconciled = [entry for entry in trace if entry == (\"effect\", \"reconcile\", \"ingest\")]\n    applied = [entry for entry in trace if entry == (\"effect\", \"apply\", \"ingest\")]\n    assert len(reconciled) == 1\n    assert len(applied) == (1 if marker == \"not_applied\" else 0)\n\n\nasync def test_recovery_applies_unstarted_stage_and_completes(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    replica.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, trace=trace)\n\n    await coordinator.recover_incomplete()\n\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"completed\"\n    assert [entry for entry in trace if entry[0] == \"effect\"] == [\n        (\"effect\", \"apply\", stage) for stage in STAGES\n    ]\n\n\nasync def test_startup_records_broker_restart_unknown_without_effects(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    start_started_lifecycle(replica, request, frame)\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(\n        replica,\n        trace=trace,\n        broker_incarnation=RESTARTED_BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n\n    await coordinator.recover_incomplete()\n\n    decision = replica.status(request)\n    assert decision.state == \"unresolved\"\n    assert result_json(decision.response_frame) == {\n        \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"broker_restart_unknown\",\n    }\n    assert trace == []\n\n\nasync def test_no_journal_calls_run_during_active_effect(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    recorded = RecordingJournal(replica)\n    during: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n\n    async def quiet_apply(context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        baseline = len(recorded.calls)\n        for _ in range(3):\n            await asyncio.sleep(0)\n        during.extend(recorded.calls[baseline:])\n        return completed_outcome(\"ingest\")\n\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\"ingest\", apply=quiet_apply)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(recorded, effects=effects)\n\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    assert result_json(response)[\"state\"] == \"completed\"\n    assert during == []\n```\n\n---\n\n## Packet B — new file: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Broker-owned coordination of one replica lifecycle through seven stages.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport re\nimport secrets\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom time import monotonic\nfrom typing import Protocol, cast\n\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import (\n    BrokerRequest,\n    create_signed_response,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    RejectedReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    ReplicaJournalConflictError,\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\n)\n\nREPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"ingest\",\n    \"verify\",\n    \"publish\",\n    \"admission\",\n    \"drain\",\n    \"export\",\n    \"reclaim\",\n)\n_TOKEN_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,128}$\")\n_OWNER_TOKEN_BYTES = 32\n_MAX_ABANDONED_EFFECTS = 32\n_EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_DEFAULT = 30.0\n_EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_MAX = 3_600.0\n_OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_DEFAULT = 10.0\n_OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_MAX = 3_600.0\n_OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_DEFAULT = 0.05\n_OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_MAX = 60.0\n# Stage-specific fallback reason for unexpected effect failures; each entry is\n# valid for its stage in the journal-owned unresolved reason sets.\n_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"ingest\": \"transfer_unknown\",\n    \"verify\": \"verification_unknown\",\n    \"publish\": \"publication_unknown\",\n    \"admission\": \"admission_unknown\",\n    \"drain\": \"acknowledgment_unknown\",\n    \"export\": \"transfer_unknown\",\n    \"reclaim\": \"effect_unknown\",\n}\n\n\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Base class for bounded replica lifecycle coordination failures.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass BrokerReplicaOwnerActive(BrokerReplicaLifecycleError):\n    \"\"\"Report another owner holding the lifecycle beyond the bounded wait.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass StageRejected(BrokerReplicaLifecycleError):\n    \"\"\"Report one effect-rejected stage; the journal validates the status.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, status: str, receipt_id: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(f\"replica stage is rejected: {status}\")\n        self.status = status\n        self.receipt_id = receipt_id\n\n\nclass StageOutcomeUnknown(BrokerReplicaLifecycleError):\n    \"\"\"Report one effect with an unknown outcome; the journal validates the reason.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, reason: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(f\"replica stage outcome is unknown: {reason}\")\n        self.reason = reason\n\n\nclass _StageTerminal(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Carry one recorded terminal response out of the stage attempt flow.\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = (\"frame\",)\n\n    def __init__(self, frame: bytes) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\"replica stage terminal response is recorded\")\n        self.frame = frame\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass StageReconciliation:\n    \"\"\"One bounded effect result; only a completed outcome carries a receipt.\"\"\"\n\n    outcome: str\n    receipt: object | None = None\n    reason: str | None = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if self.outcome not in {\"completed\", \"not_applied\", \"unknown\"}:\n            raise ValueError(\"replica stage outcome is invalid\")\n        if self.outcome == \"completed\":\n            if self.receipt is None:\n                raise ValueError(\"replica completed outcome requires a receipt\")\n            if self.reason is not None:\n                raise ValueError(\"replica completed outcome must not carry a reason\")\n            return\n        if self.receipt is not None:\n            raise ValueError(\"only a completed outcome may carry a receipt\")\n        if self.outcome == \"unknown\":\n            if not isinstance(self.reason, str) or not self.reason:\n                raise ValueError(\"replica unknown outcome requires a reason\")\n            return\n        if self.reason is not None:\n            raise ValueError(\"replica not-applied outcome must not carry a reason\")\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\n    \"\"\"Immutable inputs for one stage effect invocation.\"\"\"\n\n    request: BrokerRequest\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n    owner_token: str\n\n\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"One explicit typed stage effect owned by the broker application.\"\"\"\n\n    async def apply(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        \"\"\"Apply the stage effect for the first time.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def reconcile(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        \"\"\"Reconcile one interrupted stage start after a restart.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n\ndef _next_stage(stage: str) -> str:\n    index = REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES.index(stage)\n    if index + 1 >= len(REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES):\n        raise BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(\"replica lifecycle has no stage after reclaim\")\n    return REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES[index + 1]\n\n\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    \"\"\"Drive one replica lifecycle through the journal-owned fixed stage order.\n\n    The coordinator is stateless between calls: it retains only its\n    configuration, its random owner token, and the bounded set of abandoned\n    effect tasks whose results are consumed later. It authenticates nothing\n    about the transport or peer itself; callers pass one already\n    authenticated request with its raw signed frame, and the journal\n    re-authenticates the frame before any durable effect.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n        *,\n        broker_incarnation: str,\n        broker_private_key: Ed25519PrivateKey,\n        effects: Mapping[str, ReplicaStageEffect],\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float = _EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_DEFAULT,\n        owner_wait_seconds: float = _OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_DEFAULT,\n        owner_poll_seconds: float = _OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_DEFAULT,\n    ) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(broker_private_key, Ed25519PrivateKey):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica broker private key is invalid\")\n        if (\n            not isinstance(broker_incarnation, str)\n            or _TOKEN_PATTERN.fullmatch(broker_incarnation) is None\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\"replica broker incarnation is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(effects, Mapping) or set(effects) != set(REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES):\n            raise ValueError(\"replica stage effects must cover exactly the seven fixed stages\")\n        for stage in REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES:\n            effect = effects[stage]\n            if not callable(getattr(effect, \"apply\", None)) or not callable(\n                getattr(effect, \"reconcile\", None)\n            ):\n                raise TypeError(f\"replica {stage} stage effect is invalid\")\n        self._journal = journal\n        self._broker_incarnation = broker_incarnation\n        self._broker_private_key = broker_private_key\n        self._effects: dict[str, ReplicaStageEffect] = dict(effects)\n        self._effect_timeout_seconds = self._bounded_seconds(\n            effect_timeout_seconds,\n            _EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_MAX,\n            \"effect timeout\",\n        )\n        self._owner_wait_seconds = self._bounded_seconds(\n            owner_wait_seconds,\n            _OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_MAX,\n            \"owner wait\",\n        )\n        self._owner_poll_seconds = self._bounded_seconds(\n            owner_poll_seconds,\n            _OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_MAX,\n            \"owner poll\",\n        )\n        self._owner_token = secrets.token_urlsafe(_OWNER_TOKEN_BYTES)\n        self._abandoned_effects: set[asyncio.Task[StageReconciliation]] = set()\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _bounded_seconds(value: float, maximum: float, description: str) -> float:\n        if type(value) not in {int, float} or not 0 < value <= maximum:\n            raise ValueError(f\"replica {description} seconds must be a positive bounded number\")\n        return float(value)\n\n    async def run(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\n    ) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"Accept, claim, and drive one lifecycle to its terminal response frame.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(request, BrokerRequest):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica request is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(request_frame, (bytes, bytearray)) or not request_frame:\n            raise TypeError(\"replica request frame is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(authority, ReplicaAuthority):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica authority is invalid\")\n        frame = bytes(request_frame)\n        decision = self._journal.accept(request, frame, authority)\n        replayed = decision.response_frame\n        if replayed is not None:\n            return replayed\n        decision = await self._claim_within_deadline(request)\n        replayed = decision.response_frame\n        if replayed is not None:\n            return replayed\n        if decision.stage is None:\n            raise BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(\"replica lifecycle decision has no stage\")\n        context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(\n            request=request,\n            authority=authority,\n            owner_token=self._owner_token,\n        )\n        terminal = await self._drive_from(context, decision.stage)\n        if terminal is None:\n            raise BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(\n                \"replica lifecycle ended without a terminal response\"\n            )\n        return terminal\n\n    async def recover_incomplete(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Resolve every incomplete lifecycle serially after a broker restart.\"\"\"\n        for incomplete in self._journal.incomplete_lifecycles():\n            await self._recover_one(incomplete)\n\n    async def _recover_one(self, incomplete: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle) -> None:\n        request = self._journal.authenticated_request(incomplete)\n        owner_token = incomplete.owner_token\n        stage = incomplete.stage\n        if incomplete.owner_broker_incarnation != self._broker_incarnation:\n            self._record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, \"broker_restart_unknown\")\n            return\n        context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(\n            request=request,\n            authority=incomplete.authority,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n        )\n        if not incomplete.stage_started:\n            await self._drive_from(context, stage)\n            return\n        outcome = await self._attempt(context, stage, \"reconcile\")\n        if outcome.outcome == \"completed\":\n            if await self._persist_completed(context, stage, outcome.receipt) is not None:\n                return\n            await self._drive_from(context, _next_stage(stage))\n            return\n        if outcome.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n            await self._drive_from(context, stage)\n            return\n        self._record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, cast(str, outcome.reason))\n\n    async def _claim_within_deadline(self, request: BrokerRequest) -> ReplicaJournalDecision:\n        \"\"\"Claim authority, waiting boundedly while another owner is in flight.\"\"\"\n        deadline = monotonic() + self._owner_wait_seconds\n        while True:\n            try:\n                return self._journal.claim_authority(\n                    request,\n                    owner_token=self._owner_token,\n                    broker_incarnation=self._broker_incarnation,\n                )\n            except ReplicaJournalConflictError:\n                current = self._journal.status(request)\n                if current.response_frame is not None:\n                    return current\n                if monotonic() >= deadline:\n                    raise BrokerReplicaOwnerActive(\n                        \"replica lifecycle is owned by another active broker\"\n                    ) from None\n                await asyncio.sleep(self._owner_poll_seconds)\n\n    async def _drive_from(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        start_stage: str,\n    ) -> bytes | None:\n        index = REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES.index(start_stage)\n        for stage in REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES[index:]:\n            frame = await self._apply_stage(context, stage)\n            if frame is not None:\n                return frame\n        return None\n\n    async def _apply_stage(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        stage: str,\n    ) -> bytes | None:\n        \"\"\"Persist the stage start, then run the effect under a bounded deadline.\n\n        A not-applied result is reapplied once through apply; a second\n        not-applied result is recorded as an unresolved stage.\n        \"\"\"\n        request = context.request\n        owner_token = context.owner_token\n        self._journal.begin_stage(request, owner_token=owner_token, stage=stage)\n        try:\n            outcome = await self._attempt(context, stage, \"apply\")\n            if outcome.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n                outcome = await self._attempt(context, stage, \"apply\")\n        except _StageTerminal as terminal:\n            return terminal.frame\n        if outcome.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n            return self._record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token,\n                stage,\n                _UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage],\n            )\n        if outcome.outcome == \"unknown\":\n            return self._record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token,\n                stage,\n                cast(str, outcome.reason),\n            )\n        return self._persist_completed(context, stage, outcome.receipt)\n\n    async def _attempt(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        stage: str,\n        method: str,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation:\n        \"\"\"Run one effect invocation under a fresh absolute monotonic deadline.\n\n        Uncertain effect tasks are never cancelled: timeouts and caller\n        cancellation abandon the task into a bounded set whose results are\n        consumed later, and the stage is recorded unresolved first.\n        \"\"\"\n        request = context.request\n        owner_token = context.owner_token\n        if len(self._abandoned_effects) >= _MAX_ABANDONED_EFFECTS:\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"timeout_unknown\")\n        effect = self._effects[stage]\n        call = effect.apply if method == \"apply\" else effect.reconcile\n        task = asyncio.create_task(call(context))\n        deadline = monotonic() + self._effect_timeout_seconds\n        try:\n            done, _pending = await asyncio.wait(\n                {task},\n                timeout=max(0.0, deadline - monotonic()),\n            )\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            self._abandon(task)\n            self._record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, \"cancellation_unknown\")\n            raise\n        if task not in done:\n            self._abandon(task)\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"timeout_unknown\")\n        try:\n            result = task.result()\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"cancellation_unknown\")\n        except StageRejected as rejected:\n            raise _StageTerminal(\n                self._record_rejected(request, owner_token, stage, rejected)\n            ) from None\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as unknown:\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=unknown.reason)\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n            return StageReconciliation(\n                outcome=\"unknown\",\n                reason=_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage],\n            )\n        if not isinstance(result, StageReconciliation):\n            return StageReconciliation(\n                outcome=\"unknown\",\n                reason=_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage],\n            )\n        return result\n\n    def _persist_completed(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        stage: str,\n        receipt: object | None,\n    ) -> bytes | None:\n        \"\"\"Persist one completed stage; reclaim requires its signed response.\"\"\"\n        request = context.request\n        owner_token = context.owner_token\n        if stage == \"reclaim\":\n            if not isinstance(receipt, ReclaimReceipt):\n                raise TypeError(\"replica reclaim receipt type is invalid\")\n            response = create_signed_response(\n                request,\n                private_key=self._broker_private_key,\n                status=\"ok\",\n                error=None,\n                result={\n                    \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n                    \"state\": \"completed\",\n                    \"receipt_id\": receipt.reclaim_receipt_id,\n                },\n            )\n            self._journal.complete_reclaim(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                receipt=receipt,\n                response_frame=response,\n            )\n            return response\n        completer = getattr(self._journal, f\"complete_{stage}\")\n        completer(request, owner_token=owner_token, receipt=receipt)\n        return None\n\n    def _record_rejected(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        owner_token: str,\n        stage: str,\n        rejected: StageRejected,\n    ) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"Record one rejected stage with its exact signed terminal response.\"\"\"\n        response = create_signed_response(\n            request,\n            private_key=self._broker_private_key,\n            status=\"error\",\n            error=rejected.status,\n            result={\n                \"stage\": stage,\n                \"state\": \"rejected\",\n                \"code\": rejected.status,\n                \"receipt_id\": rejected.receipt_id,\n            },\n        )\n        self._journal.record_rejected(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            status=rejected.status,\n            receipt=RejectedReceipt(receipt_id=rejected.receipt_id),\n            response_frame=response,\n        )\n        return response\n\n    def _record_unresolved(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        owner_token: str,\n        stage: str,\n        reason: str,\n    ) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"Record one unresolved stage with its exact signed terminal response.\"\"\"\n        response = create_signed_response(\n            request,\n            private_key=self._broker_private_key,\n            status=\"error\",\n            error=reason,\n            result={\"stage\": stage, \"state\": \"unresolved\", \"code\": reason},\n        )\n        self._journal.record_unresolved(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            reason=reason,\n            response_frame=response,\n        )\n        return response\n\n    def _abandon(self, task: asyncio.Task[StageReconciliation]) -> None:\n        self._abandoned_effects.add(task)\n        task.add_done_callback(self._consume_abandoned)\n\n    def _consume_abandoned(self, task: asyncio.Task[StageReconciliation]) -> None:\n        self._abandoned_effects.discard(task)\n        if not task.cancelled():\n            task.exception()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Packet C — minimal edits to `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py`\n\nThree targeted edits, each with unique anchors (verified against the current file):\n\n**C1. Add the immutable `ReplicaAuthority` field to `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle`** — oldText:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IncompleteReplicaLifecycle:\n    request_frame: bytes\n    owner_token: str\n    owner_broker_incarnation: str\n    stage: str\n    stage_started: bool\n    reason: str\n```\n\nnewText:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IncompleteReplicaLifecycle:\n    request_frame: bytes\n    owner_token: str\n    owner_broker_incarnation: str\n    stage: str\n    stage_started: bool\n    reason: str\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n```\n\n**C2. Populate the authority in `incomplete_lifecycles()`** — oldText:\n\n```python\n                pending.append(\n                    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle(\n                        request_frame=replay.request_frame,\n                        owner_token=replay.owner_token,\n                        owner_broker_incarnation=cast(str, replay.owner_broker_incarnation),\n                        stage=_STAGES[replay.next_stage_index],\n                        stage_started=replay.stage_started,\n                        reason=\"broker_restart_unknown\",\n                    )\n                )\n```\n\nnewText:\n\n```python\n                pending.append(\n                    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle(\n                        request_frame=replay.request_frame,\n                        owner_token=replay.owner_token,\n                        owner_broker_incarnation=cast(str, replay.owner_broker_incarnation),\n                        stage=_STAGES[replay.next_stage_index],\n                        stage_started=replay.stage_started,\n                        reason=\"broker_restart_unknown\",\n                        authority=replay.authority,\n                    )\n                )\n```\n\n**C3. Add the journal-owned trusted request parsing method** (inserted immediately before `_validate_stage`) — oldText:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_stage(stage: str) -> None:\n```\n\nnewText:\n\n```python\n    def authenticated_request(self, lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle) -> BrokerRequest:\n        \"\"\"Return the typed request authenticated from one incomplete lifecycle.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(lifecycle, IncompleteReplicaLifecycle):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica lifecycle is invalid\")\n        frame = lifecycle.request_frame\n        if not isinstance(frame, (bytes, bytearray)) or not frame:\n            raise ReplicaJournalSyncError(\"replica lifecycle request frame is invalid\")\n        try:\n            return _authenticate_request_frame(bytes(frame), self._request_public_key)\n        except ValueError as error:\n            raise ReplicaJournalSyncError(\n                \"replica lifecycle request authentication failed\"\n            ) from error\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_stage(stage: str) -> None:\n```\n\nDesign note: `authenticated_request` returns only the typed `BrokerRequest` because the authority travels on the immutable lifecycle itself (packet C1) — the journal keeps exposing no database objects, and parsing goes through the journal's own configured request public key.\n\n---\n\n## Packet D — ordered checks (run after applying Packets A–C under a bound TDD request)\n\n1. **Red (focused, tests only applied first):** `cd backend && .venv/bin/pytest tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py -q`\n   Expected clean failure: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yinshi.services.broker_replica_lifecycle'` — no partial passes.\n2. **Green (focused, after B+C):** same command. Expected: `17 passed` (14 test functions; the parametrized recovery test expands to 4).\n3. **Journal regression:** `.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -q` — expected: all pass (no external constructor of `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` exists; the new field is keyword-supplied inside the journal).\n4. **Broader:** `.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py tests/test_broker_foundation.py -q`, then the full suite `.venv/bin/pytest -q` if time permits. Expected: no new failures; unrelated dirty files untouched.\n5. **Lint/type:** `.venv/bin/black --check src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py` and `.venv/bin/mypy src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py` (strict profile configured in pyproject). Expected: clean.\n\n\n[Showing lines 1-1405 of 1406 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=1406 to continue.]"}],"details":{"truncation":{"content":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 12 assistant turns (soft limit 12, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nSupervisor confirmed fallback option 2. I'm delivering complete edit packets with no further write attempts. One detail to fix from my drafted test (the typed `complete_*` journal methods take no `stage` kwarg, so the recorded trace must expect `None` there), then I'll compose the full deliverable.\n\n---\n\n## Blocker report (exact)\n\nTDD Guard refused every source write (two attempts, including a probe) with:\n\n```\nTDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.\n```\n\nNo `tdd_*` tools are exposed to this child session, shell file writes are blocked, so neither the red test nor the implementation could be materialized on disk. Per supervisor decision (fallback option 2), the complete edit packets follow. **Nothing has been written to the working tree; no commits.**\n\n---\n\n## Packet A — new file: `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\n\nBehavior-facing tests, written first per TDD (apply alone → red; with Packets B+C → green).\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Check broker-owned replica lifecycle coordination against the durable journal.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport sqlite3\nfrom dataclasses import FrozenInstanceError\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom time import monotonic\n\nimport pytest\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import (\n    BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n    BrokerRequest,\n    JsonValue,\n    create_signed_request,\n    create_signed_response,\n    parse_signed_request,\n    verify_broker_response,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    AdmissionReceipt,\n    ArtifactReference,\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    DrainReceipt,\n    ExportReceipt,\n    IngestReceipt,\n    PublishReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    VerifyReceipt,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_lifecycle import (\n    BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator,\n    BrokerReplicaOwnerActive,\n    ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n    StageOutcomeUnknown,\n    StageRejected,\n    StageReconciliation,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.replica_artifact_contract import (\n    compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256,\n)\n\nAPPLICATION_ID = \"yinshi-desktop\"\nDATABASE_INCARNATION = \"d\" * 32\nBROKER_INCARNATION = \"b\" * 32\nRESTARTED_BROKER_INCARNATION = \"c\" * 32\nOWNER_TOKEN = \"owner_token_00000000000000000000\"\nREQUEST_PRIVATE_KEY = Ed25519PrivateKey.generate()\nRESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY = Ed25519PrivateKey.generate()\nSTAGES = (\"ingest\", \"verify\", \"publish\", \"admission\", \"drain\", \"export\", \"reclaim\")\nAUTHORITY = ReplicaAuthority(\n    physical_target_id=\"target_00000000000000000000000000\",\n    replica_generation=3,\n    execution_owner_id=\"execution_owner_0000000000000000\",\n)\nBUNDLE = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"bundle_00000000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"1\" * 64,\n    byte_length=123,\n)\nWORKTREE = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"worktree_0000000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"2\" * 64,\n    byte_length=456,\n)\nINDEX_OBJECTS = ArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id=\"index_objects_0000000000000000000\",\n    sha256=\"7\" * 64,\n    byte_length=789,\n)\nLIMITS_SHA256 = \"8\" * 64\nRECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID = \"reclaim_0000000000000000000000\"\nINGEST_RECEIPT = IngestReceipt(\n    receipt_id=\"receipt_ingest_000000000000000000\",\n    bundle=BUNDLE,\n    worktree=WORKTREE,\n    REDACTED,\n)\n\n\ndef artifact_json(reference: ArtifactReference) -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_id\": reference.artifact_id,\n        \"byte_length\": reference.byte_length,\n        \"sha256\": reference.sha256,\n    }\n\n\ndef artifact_set_sha256(operation_id: str) -> str:\n    return compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256(\n        operation_id=operation_id,\n        repository_id=\"repository_0000000000000000000000\",\n        workspace_id=\"workspace_000000000000000000000000\",\n        physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n        replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n        execution_owner_id=AUTHORITY.execution_owner_id,\n        object_format=\"sha256\",\n        source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n        reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n        bundle={\n            \"role\": \"committed_bundle\",\n            \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.yinshi.git-bundle.v1\",\n            **artifact_json(BUNDLE),\n        },\n        worktree={\n            \"role\": \"worktree\",\n            \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.yinshi.replica-worktree.v1\",\n            **artifact_json(WORKTREE),\n        },\n        index_objects={\n            \"role\": \"index_objects\",\n            \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.yinshi.git-index-objects-pack.v1\",\n            **artifact_json(INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        },\n        limits_sha256=LIMITS_SHA256,\n    )\n\n\nARTIFACT_SET_SHA256 = artifact_set_sha256(\"a\" * 32)\n\n\ndef request_payload() -> dict[str, JsonValue]:\n    return {\n        \"artifact_set_sha256\": ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n        \"bundle\": artifact_json(BUNDLE),\n        \"index_objects\": artifact_json(INDEX_OBJECTS),\n        \"limits_sha256\": LIMITS_SHA256,\n        \"object_format\": \"sha256\",\n        \"reconciliation_fingerprint\": \"3\" * 64,\n        \"repository_id\": \"repository_0000000000000000000000\",\n        \"source_state_sha256\": \"4\" * 64,\n        \"workspace_id\": \"workspace_000000000000000000000000\",\n        \"worktree\": artifact_json(WORKTREE),\n    }\n\n\ndef signed_request() -> tuple[BrokerRequest, bytes]:\n    frame = create_signed_request(\n        private_key=REQUEST_PRIVATE_KEY,\n        protocol_version=BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n        database_incarnation=DATABASE_INCARNATION,\n        connection_sequence=1,\n        operation_id=\"a\" * 32,\n        request_type=\"replica.lifecycle\",\n        nonce=\"nonce_00000000001\",\n        payload=request_payload(),\n    )\n    return parse_signed_request(frame, public_key=REQUEST_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key()), frame\n\n\ndef receipt_for(stage: str) -> object:\n    receipt_id = f\"receipt_{stage}_000000000000000000\"\n    if stage == \"ingest\":\n        return INGEST_RECEIPT\n    if stage == \"verify\":\n        return VerifyReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n            worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n            REDACTED.sha256,\n            source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n            reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n            artifact_set_sha256=ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n        )\n    if stage == \"publish\":\n        return PublishReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            physical_target_id=AUTHORITY.physical_target_id,\n            replica_generation=AUTHORITY.replica_generation,\n            execution_owner_id=AUTHORITY.execution_owner_id,\n            publication_marker_sha256=\"5\" * 64,\n            synchronization_receipt_id=\"sync_000000000000000000000000000\",\n            artifact_set_sha256=ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n        )\n    if stage == \"admission\":\n        return AdmissionReceipt(\n            receipt_id=receipt_id,\n            execution_owner_id=AUTHORITY.execution_owner_id,\n            runtime_unit_id=\"runtime_0000000000000000000000000\",\n            session_socket_sha256=\"6\" * 64,\n        )\n    if stage == \"drain\":\n        return DrainReceipt(\n            drain_ack_receipt_id=\"drain_ack_0000000000000000000000\",\n            quiescence_receipt_id=\"quiescence_00000000000000000000\",\n        )\n    if stage == \"export\":\n        return ExportReceipt(\n            export_receipt_id=\"export_000000000000000000000000\",\n            bundle=BUNDLE,\n            worktree=WORKTREE,\n            REDACTED,\n        )\n    if stage == \"reclaim\":\n        return ReclaimReceipt(reclaim_receipt_id=RECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID)\n    raise AssertionError(stage)\n\n\ndef completed_outcome(stage: str) -> StageReconciliation:\n    return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"completed\", receipt=receipt_for(stage))\n\n\ndef journal(tmp_path: Path) -> BrokerReplicaJournal:\n    return BrokerReplicaJournal(\n        tmp_path / \"replica.sqlite3\",\n        application_id=APPLICATION_ID,\n        expected_limits_sha256=LIMITS_SHA256,\n        REDACTED.public_key(),\n        response_public_keys={BROKER_INCARNATION: RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key()},\n    )\n\n\nclass ScriptedEffect:\n    \"\"\"Test double exposing apply and reconcile with scripted outcomes.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        stage: str,\n        *,\n        apply: object = None,\n        reconcile: object = None,\n        trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        self.stage = stage\n        self.contexts: list[ReplicaLifecycleContext] = []\n        self.apply_started = asyncio.Event()\n        self._apply = apply\n        self._reconcile = reconcile\n        self._trace = trace\n\n    async def apply(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        return await self._dispatch(\"apply\", self._apply, context)\n\n    async def reconcile(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        return await self._dispatch(\"reconcile\", self._reconcile, context)\n\n    async def _dispatch(\n        self,\n        method: str,\n        action: object,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation:\n        if self._trace is not None:\n            self._trace.append((\"effect\", method, self.stage))\n        self.contexts.append(context)\n        if method == \"apply\":\n            self.apply_started.set()\n        if action is None:\n            raise AssertionError(f\"replica {self.stage} {method} must not run\")\n        if isinstance(action, BaseException):\n            raise action\n        if isinstance(action, StageReconciliation):\n            return action\n        return await action(context)\n\n\nclass RecordingJournal:\n    \"\"\"Test double recording every journal call in issue order.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, inner: BrokerReplicaJournal) -> None:\n        self._inner = inner\n        self.calls: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n\n    def __getattr__(self, name: str) -> object:\n        attribute = getattr(self._inner, name)\n        if not callable(attribute):\n            return attribute\n\n        def record(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> object:\n            stage = kwargs.get(\"stage\")\n            self.calls.append((\"journal\", name, stage if isinstance(stage, str) else None))\n            return attribute(*args, **kwargs)\n\n        return record\n\n\ndef default_effects(\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, ScriptedEffect]:\n    return {\n        stage: ScriptedEffect(stage, apply=completed_outcome(stage), trace=trace)\n        for stage in STAGES\n    }\n\n\ndef configured_coordinator(\n    replica: object,\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] | None = None,\n    *,\n    broker_incarnation: str = BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    effects: dict[str, ScriptedEffect] | None = None,\n    **timing: float,\n) -> BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    staged = effects if effects is not None else default_effects(trace)\n    options: dict[str, float] = {\n        \"effect_timeout_seconds\": 5.0,\n        \"owner_wait_seconds\": 0.5,\n        \"owner_poll_seconds\": 0.02,\n    }\n    options.update(timing)\n    return BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator(\n        replica,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        broker_incarnation=broker_incarnation,\n        broker_private_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY,\n        effects=staged,\n        **options,\n    )\n\n\ndef start_started_lifecycle(\n    replica: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    request: BrokerRequest,\n    frame: bytes,\n    *,\n    stage: str = \"ingest\",\n) -> None:\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    replica.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n    replica.begin_stage(request, owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN, stage=stage)\n\n\ndef drive_journal_to_completed(replica: BrokerReplicaJournal, request: BrokerRequest) -> None:\n    for stage in STAGES:\n        replica.begin_stage(request, owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN, stage=stage)\n        receipt = receipt_for(stage)\n        final = None\n        if stage == \"reclaim\":\n            assert isinstance(receipt, ReclaimReceipt)\n            final = create_signed_response(\n                request,\n                private_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY,\n                status=\"ok\",\n                error=None,\n                result={\n                    \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n                    \"state\": \"completed\",\n                    \"receipt_id\": receipt.reclaim_receipt_id,\n                },\n            )\n        getattr(replica, f\"complete_{stage}\")(\n            request,\n            owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n            receipt=receipt,\n            response_frame=final,\n        )\n\n\ndef event_rows(path: Path) -> list[tuple[str, str | None]]:\n    with sqlite3.connect(path) as database:\n        return [\n            (str(event_type), stage)\n            for event_type, stage in database.execute(\n                \"SELECT event_type, stage FROM replica_journal_events ORDER BY event_id\"\n            ).fetchall()\n        ]\n\n\ndef result_json(frame: bytes | None) -> dict[str, object]:\n    assert frame is not None\n    value = json.loads(frame)\n    assert isinstance(value[\"result\"], dict)\n    return value[\"result\"]\n\n\ndef test_constructor_requires_all_seven_stage_effects(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    effects = default_effects()\n    del effects[\"drain\"]\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    incomplete = default_effects()\n    incomplete[\"export\"] = object()  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError):\n        configured_coordinator(replica, effects=incomplete)\n\n\nasync def test_run_follows_exact_stage_order_and_persists_each_start_before_effect(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    effects = default_effects(trace)\n    recorded = RecordingJournal(replica)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(recorded, trace=trace)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    expected: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = [\n        (\"journal\", \"accept\", None),\n        (\"journal\", \"claim_authority\", None),\n    ]\n    for stage in STAGES:\n        expected.append((\"journal\", \"begin_stage\", stage))\n        expected.append((\"effect\", \"apply\", stage))\n        expected.append((\"journal\", \"complete_\" + stage, None))\n    assert trace == expected\n    assert event_rows(replica.path)[-1] == (\"stage_outcome\", \"reclaim\")\n    assert result_json(response) == {\n        \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n        \"state\": \"completed\",\n        \"receipt_id\": RECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID,\n    }\n\n    context = effects[\"ingest\"].contexts[0]\n    assert isinstance(context, ReplicaLifecycleContext)\n    assert context.request == request\n    assert context.authority == AUTHORITY\n    with sqlite3.connect(replica.path) as database:\n        owner = database.execute(\n            \"SELECT owner_token FROM replica_journal_events \"\n            \"WHERE event_type = 'authority_claimed'\"\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n    assert context.owner_token == owner\n    with pytest.raises(FrozenInstanceError):\n        context.owner_token = \"mutated_owner_000000000000000\"\n\n\nasync def test_reclaim_success_returns_broker_signed_completed_response(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    value = json.loads(response)\n    assert value[\"status\"] == \"ok\"\n    assert value[\"error\"] is None\n    verified = verify_broker_response(\n        response,\n        public_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key(),\n        expected_request=request,\n    )\n    assert verified.result == value[\"result\"]\n    decision = replica.status(request)\n    assert decision.state == \"completed\"\n    assert decision.stage == \"reclaim\"\n    assert decision.response_frame == response\n\n\nasync def test_terminal_replay_returns_durable_frame_without_effects(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    first = configured_coordinator(replica)\n    response = await first.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    poison = {\n        stage: ScriptedEffect(\n            stage,\n            apply=RuntimeError(\"must not run\"),\n            reconcile=RuntimeError(\"must not run\"),\n            trace=trace,\n        )\n        for stage in STAGES\n    }\n    second = configured_coordinator(replica, trace=trace, effects=poison)\n    assert await second.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == response\n    assert trace == []\n\n\nasync def test_stage_rejection_records_exact_signed_terminal_response(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"ingest\",\n        apply=StageRejected(\"artifact_rejected\", \"rejected_receipt_00000000001\"),\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    value = json.loads(response)\n    assert value[\"status\"] == \"error\"\n    assert value[\"error\"] == \"artifact_rejected\"\n    assert value[\"result\"] == {\n        \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n        \"state\": \"rejected\",\n        \"code\": \"artifact_rejected\",\n        \"receipt_id\": \"rejected_receipt_00000000001\",\n    }\n    verify_broker_response(\n        response,\n        public_key=RESPONSE_PRIVATE_KEY.public_key(),\n        expected_request=request,\n    )\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"rejected\"\n    assert event_rows(replica.path)[-1] == (\"stage_rejected\", \"ingest\")\n    assert await configured_coordinator(replica).run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == response\n\n\nasync def test_stage_unknown_reason_records_exact_unresolved_terminal_response(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"publish\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"publish\",\n        apply=StageOutcomeUnknown(\"publication_unknown\"),\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    value = json.loads(response)\n    assert value[\"status\"] == \"error\"\n    assert value[\"error\"] == \"publication_unknown\"\n    assert value[\"result\"] == {\n        \"stage\": \"publish\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"publication_unknown\",\n    }\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"unresolved\"\n    assert await configured_coordinator(replica).run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == response\n\n\nasync def test_effect_timeout_records_unresolved_and_consumes_late_task_result(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n\n    async def late_unknown(context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.4)\n        raise StageOutcomeUnknown(\"verification_unknown\")\n\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"verify\"] = ScriptedEffect(\"verify\", apply=late_unknown)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects, effect_timeout_seconds=0.05)\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    assert result_json(response) == {\n        \"stage\": \"verify\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"timeout_unknown\",\n    }\n    snapshot = event_rows(replica.path)\n    assert snapshot[-2:] == [(\"stage_started\", \"verify\"), (\"stage_unresolved\", \"verify\")]\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"unresolved\"\n\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.45)\n    assert event_rows(replica.path) == snapshot\n    assert coordinator._abandoned_effects == set()\n\n\nasync def test_caller_cancellation_records_unresolved_and_late_task_completes(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    finished = asyncio.Event()\n\n    async def hanging(context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.4)\n        finished.set()\n        return completed_outcome(\"ingest\")\n\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\"ingest\", apply=hanging)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n    runner = asyncio.create_task(coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY))\n    await asyncio.wait_for(effects[\"ingest\"].apply_started.wait(), timeout=2)\n    runner.cancel()\n    with pytest.raises(asyncio.CancelledError):\n        await runner\n\n    assert result_json(replica.status(request).response_frame) == {\n        \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"cancellation_unknown\",\n    }\n    snapshot = event_rows(replica.path)\n    assert not finished.is_set()\n\n    await asyncio.wait_for(finished.wait(), timeout=2)\n    assert event_rows(replica.path) == snapshot\n    assert coordinator._abandoned_effects == set()\n\n\nasync def test_other_owner_bounded_wait_raises_stable_owner_active_error(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    replica.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(\n        replica,\n        trace=trace,\n        owner_wait_seconds=0.1,\n        owner_poll_seconds=0.02,\n    )\n\n    started = monotonic()\n    with pytest.raises(BrokerReplicaOwnerActive):\n        await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert monotonic() - started >= 0.1\n    assert trace == []\n\n    drive_journal_to_completed(replica, request)\n    terminal = replica.status(request).response_frame\n    assert await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY) == terminal\n    assert trace == []\n\n\nasync def test_receipt_type_mismatch_fails_closed_before_completion(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    wrong = VerifyReceipt(\n        receipt_id=\"receipt_ingest_000000000000000000\",\n        bundle_sha256=BUNDLE.sha256,\n        worktree_sha256=WORKTREE.sha256,\n        REDACTED.sha256,\n        source_state_sha256=\"4\" * 64,\n        reconciliation_fingerprint=\"3\" * 64,\n        artifact_set_sha256=ARTIFACT_SET_SHA256,\n    )\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"ingest\",\n        apply=StageReconciliation(outcome=\"completed\", receipt=wrong),\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, effects=effects)\n\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError):\n        await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    assert event_rows(replica.path) == [\n        (\"accepted\", None),\n        (\"authority_claimed\", None),\n        (\"stage_started\", \"ingest\"),\n    ]\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"in_flight\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    (\"marker\", \"reconcile\", \"expected_state\", \"expected_code\"),\n    [\n        (\n            \"completed\",\n            StageReconciliation(outcome=\"completed\", receipt=INGEST_RECEIPT),\n            \"completed\",\n            None,\n        ),\n        (\"not_applied\", StageReconciliation(outcome=\"not_applied\"), \"completed\", None),\n        (\n            \"unknown\",\n            StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"verification_unknown\"),\n            \"unresolved\",\n            \"verification_unknown\",\n        ),\n        (\"error\", RuntimeError(\"unexpected effect failure\"), \"unresolved\", \"transfer_unknown\"),\n    ],\n)\nasync def test_recovery_of_started_stage_reconciles_outcomes(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n    marker: str,\n    reconcile: object,\n    expected_state: str,\n    expected_code: str | None,\n) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    start_started_lifecycle(replica, request, frame)\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    effects = default_effects(trace)\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\n        \"ingest\",\n        apply=completed_outcome(\"ingest\"),\n        reconcile=reconcile,\n        trace=trace,\n    )\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, trace=trace, effects=effects)\n\n    await coordinator.recover_incomplete()\n\n    decision = replica.status(request)\n    assert decision.state == expected_state\n    if expected_code is None:\n        assert result_json(decision.response_frame) == {\n            \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n            \"state\": \"completed\",\n            \"receipt_id\": RECLAIM_RECEIPT_ID,\n        }\n    else:\n        assert result_json(decision.response_frame) == {\n            \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n            \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n            \"code\": expected_code,\n        }\n    reconciled = [entry for entry in trace if entry == (\"effect\", \"reconcile\", \"ingest\")]\n    applied = [entry for entry in trace if entry == (\"effect\", \"apply\", \"ingest\")]\n    assert len(reconciled) == 1\n    assert len(applied) == (1 if marker == \"not_applied\" else 0)\n\n\nasync def test_recovery_applies_unstarted_stage_and_completes(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    replica.accept(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n    replica.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=OWNER_TOKEN,\n        broker_incarnation=BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(replica, trace=trace)\n\n    await coordinator.recover_incomplete()\n\n    assert replica.status(request).state == \"completed\"\n    assert [entry for entry in trace if entry[0] == \"effect\"] == [\n        (\"effect\", \"apply\", stage) for stage in STAGES\n    ]\n\n\nasync def test_startup_records_broker_restart_unknown_without_effects(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    start_started_lifecycle(replica, request, frame)\n    trace: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(\n        replica,\n        trace=trace,\n        broker_incarnation=RESTARTED_BROKER_INCARNATION,\n    )\n\n    await coordinator.recover_incomplete()\n\n    decision = replica.status(request)\n    assert decision.state == \"unresolved\"\n    assert result_json(decision.response_frame) == {\n        \"stage\": \"ingest\",\n        \"state\": \"unresolved\",\n        \"code\": \"broker_restart_unknown\",\n    }\n    assert trace == []\n\n\nasync def test_no_journal_calls_run_during_active_effect(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    replica = journal(tmp_path)\n    request, frame = signed_request()\n    recorded = RecordingJournal(replica)\n    during: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = []\n\n    async def quiet_apply(context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        baseline = len(recorded.calls)\n        for _ in range(3):\n            await asyncio.sleep(0)\n        during.extend(recorded.calls[baseline:])\n        return completed_outcome(\"ingest\")\n\n    effects = default_effects()\n    effects[\"ingest\"] = ScriptedEffect(\"ingest\", apply=quiet_apply)\n    coordinator = configured_coordinator(recorded, effects=effects)\n\n    response = await coordinator.run(request, frame, AUTHORITY)\n\n    assert result_json(response)[\"state\"] == \"completed\"\n    assert during == []\n```\n\n---\n\n## Packet B — new file: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Broker-owned coordination of one replica lifecycle through seven stages.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport re\nimport secrets\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom time import monotonic\nfrom typing import Protocol, cast\n\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import (\n    BrokerRequest,\n    create_signed_response,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    RejectedReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    ReplicaJournalConflictError,\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\n)\n\nREPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"ingest\",\n    \"verify\",\n    \"publish\",\n    \"admission\",\n    \"drain\",\n    \"export\",\n    \"reclaim\",\n)\n_TOKEN_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,128}$\")\n_OWNER_TOKEN_BYTES = 32\n_MAX_ABANDONED_EFFECTS = 32\n_EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_DEFAULT = 30.0\n_EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_MAX = 3_600.0\n_OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_DEFAULT = 10.0\n_OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_MAX = 3_600.0\n_OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_DEFAULT = 0.05\n_OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_MAX = 60.0\n# Stage-specific fallback reason for unexpected effect failures; each entry is\n# valid for its stage in the journal-owned unresolved reason sets.\n_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"ingest\": \"transfer_unknown\",\n    \"verify\": \"verification_unknown\",\n    \"publish\": \"publication_unknown\",\n    \"admission\": \"admission_unknown\",\n    \"drain\": \"acknowledgment_unknown\",\n    \"export\": \"transfer_unknown\",\n    \"reclaim\": \"effect_unknown\",\n}\n\n\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Base class for bounded replica lifecycle coordination failures.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass BrokerReplicaOwnerActive(BrokerReplicaLifecycleError):\n    \"\"\"Report another owner holding the lifecycle beyond the bounded wait.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass StageRejected(BrokerReplicaLifecycleError):\n    \"\"\"Report one effect-rejected stage; the journal validates the status.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, status: str, receipt_id: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(f\"replica stage is rejected: {status}\")\n        self.status = status\n        self.receipt_id = receipt_id\n\n\nclass StageOutcomeUnknown(BrokerReplicaLifecycleError):\n    \"\"\"Report one effect with an unknown outcome; the journal validates the reason.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, reason: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(f\"replica stage outcome is unknown: {reason}\")\n        self.reason = reason\n\n\nclass _StageTerminal(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Carry one recorded terminal response out of the stage attempt flow.\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = (\"frame\",)\n\n    def __init__(self, frame: bytes) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\"replica stage terminal response is recorded\")\n        self.frame = frame\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass StageReconciliation:\n    \"\"\"One bounded effect result; only a completed outcome carries a receipt.\"\"\"\n\n    outcome: str\n    receipt: object | None = None\n    reason: str | None = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if self.outcome not in {\"completed\", \"not_applied\", \"unknown\"}:\n            raise ValueError(\"replica stage outcome is invalid\")\n        if self.outcome == \"completed\":\n            if self.receipt is None:\n                raise ValueError(\"replica completed outcome requires a receipt\")\n            if self.reason is not None:\n                raise ValueError(\"replica completed outcome must not carry a reason\")\n            return\n        if self.receipt is not None:\n            raise ValueError(\"only a completed outcome may carry a receipt\")\n        if self.outcome == \"unknown\":\n            if not isinstance(self.reason, str) or not self.reason:\n                raise ValueError(\"replica unknown outcome requires a reason\")\n            return\n        if self.reason is not None:\n            raise ValueError(\"replica not-applied outcome must not carry a reason\")\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\n    \"\"\"Immutable inputs for one stage effect invocation.\"\"\"\n\n    request: BrokerRequest\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n    owner_token: str\n\n\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"One explicit typed stage effect owned by the broker application.\"\"\"\n\n    async def apply(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        \"\"\"Apply the stage effect for the first time.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def reconcile(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation:\n        \"\"\"Reconcile one interrupted stage start after a restart.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n\ndef _next_stage(stage: str) -> str:\n    index = REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES.index(stage)\n    if index + 1 >= len(REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES):\n        raise BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(\"replica lifecycle has no stage after reclaim\")\n    return REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES[index + 1]\n\n\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    \"\"\"Drive one replica lifecycle through the journal-owned fixed stage order.\n\n    The coordinator is stateless between calls: it retains only its\n    configuration, its random owner token, and the bounded set of abandoned\n    effect tasks whose results are consumed later. It authenticates nothing\n    about the transport or peer itself; callers pass one already\n    authenticated request with its raw signed frame, and the journal\n    re-authenticates the frame before any durable effect.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n        *,\n        broker_incarnation: str,\n        broker_private_key: Ed25519PrivateKey,\n        effects: Mapping[str, ReplicaStageEffect],\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float = _EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_DEFAULT,\n        owner_wait_seconds: float = _OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_DEFAULT,\n        owner_poll_seconds: float = _OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_DEFAULT,\n    ) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(broker_private_key, Ed25519PrivateKey):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica broker private key is invalid\")\n        if (\n            not isinstance(broker_incarnation, str)\n            or _TOKEN_PATTERN.fullmatch(broker_incarnation) is None\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\"replica broker incarnation is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(effects, Mapping) or set(effects) != set(REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES):\n            raise ValueError(\"replica stage effects must cover exactly the seven fixed stages\")\n        for stage in REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES:\n            effect = effects[stage]\n            if not callable(getattr(effect, \"apply\", None)) or not callable(\n                getattr(effect, \"reconcile\", None)\n            ):\n                raise TypeError(f\"replica {stage} stage effect is invalid\")\n        self._journal = journal\n        self._broker_incarnation = broker_incarnation\n        self._broker_private_key = broker_private_key\n        self._effects: dict[str, ReplicaStageEffect] = dict(effects)\n        self._effect_timeout_seconds = self._bounded_seconds(\n            effect_timeout_seconds,\n            _EFFECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS_MAX,\n            \"effect timeout\",\n        )\n        self._owner_wait_seconds = self._bounded_seconds(\n            owner_wait_seconds,\n            _OWNER_WAIT_SECONDS_MAX,\n            \"owner wait\",\n        )\n        self._owner_poll_seconds = self._bounded_seconds(\n            owner_poll_seconds,\n            _OWNER_POLL_SECONDS_MAX,\n            \"owner poll\",\n        )\n        self._owner_token = secrets.token_urlsafe(_OWNER_TOKEN_BYTES)\n        self._abandoned_effects: set[asyncio.Task[StageReconciliation]] = set()\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _bounded_seconds(value: float, maximum: float, description: str) -> float:\n        if type(value) not in {int, float} or not 0 < value <= maximum:\n            raise ValueError(f\"replica {description} seconds must be a positive bounded number\")\n        return float(value)\n\n    async def run(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\n    ) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"Accept, claim, and drive one lifecycle to its terminal response frame.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(request, BrokerRequest):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica request is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(request_frame, (bytes, bytearray)) or not request_frame:\n            raise TypeError(\"replica request frame is invalid\")\n        if not isinstance(authority, ReplicaAuthority):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica authority is invalid\")\n        frame = bytes(request_frame)\n        decision = self._journal.accept(request, frame, authority)\n        replayed = decision.response_frame\n        if replayed is not None:\n            return replayed\n        decision = await self._claim_within_deadline(request)\n        replayed = decision.response_frame\n        if replayed is not None:\n            return replayed\n        if decision.stage is None:\n            raise BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(\"replica lifecycle decision has no stage\")\n        context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(\n            request=request,\n            authority=authority,\n            owner_token=self._owner_token,\n        )\n        terminal = await self._drive_from(context, decision.stage)\n        if terminal is None:\n            raise BrokerReplicaLifecycleError(\n                \"replica lifecycle ended without a terminal response\"\n            )\n        return terminal\n\n    async def recover_incomplete(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Resolve every incomplete lifecycle serially after a broker restart.\"\"\"\n        for incomplete in self._journal.incomplete_lifecycles():\n            await self._recover_one(incomplete)\n\n    async def _recover_one(self, incomplete: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle) -> None:\n        request = self._journal.authenticated_request(incomplete)\n        owner_token = incomplete.owner_token\n        stage = incomplete.stage\n        if incomplete.owner_broker_incarnation != self._broker_incarnation:\n            self._record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, \"broker_restart_unknown\")\n            return\n        context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(\n            request=request,\n            authority=incomplete.authority,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n        )\n        if not incomplete.stage_started:\n            await self._drive_from(context, stage)\n            return\n        outcome = await self._attempt(context, stage, \"reconcile\")\n        if outcome.outcome == \"completed\":\n            if await self._persist_completed(context, stage, outcome.receipt) is not None:\n                return\n            await self._drive_from(context, _next_stage(stage))\n            return\n        if outcome.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n            await self._drive_from(context, stage)\n            return\n        self._record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, cast(str, outcome.reason))\n\n    async def _claim_within_deadline(self, request: BrokerRequest) -> ReplicaJournalDecision:\n        \"\"\"Claim authority, waiting boundedly while another owner is in flight.\"\"\"\n        deadline = monotonic() + self._owner_wait_seconds\n        while True:\n            try:\n                return self._journal.claim_authority(\n                    request,\n                    owner_token=self._owner_token,\n                    broker_incarnation=self._broker_incarnation,\n                )\n            except ReplicaJournalConflictError:\n                current = self._journal.status(request)\n                if current.response_frame is not None:\n                    return current\n                if monotonic() >= deadline:\n                    raise BrokerReplicaOwnerActive(\n                        \"replica lifecycle is owned by another active broker\"\n                    ) from None\n                await asyncio.sleep(self._owner_poll_seconds)\n\n    async def _drive_from(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        start_stage: str,\n    ) -> bytes | None:\n        index = REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES.index(start_stage)\n        for stage in REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES[index:]:\n            frame = await self._apply_stage(context, stage)\n            if frame is not None:\n                return frame\n        return None\n\n    async def _apply_stage(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        stage: str,\n    ) -> bytes | None:\n        \"\"\"Persist the stage start, then run the effect under a bounded deadline.\n\n        A not-applied result is reapplied once through apply; a second\n        not-applied result is recorded as an unresolved stage.\n        \"\"\"\n        request = context.request\n        owner_token = context.owner_token\n        self._journal.begin_stage(request, owner_token=owner_token, stage=stage)\n        try:\n            outcome = await self._attempt(context, stage, \"apply\")\n            if outcome.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n                outcome = await self._attempt(context, stage, \"apply\")\n        except _StageTerminal as terminal:\n            return terminal.frame\n        if outcome.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n            return self._record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token,\n                stage,\n                _UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage],\n            )\n        if outcome.outcome == \"unknown\":\n            return self._record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token,\n                stage,\n                cast(str, outcome.reason),\n            )\n        return self._persist_completed(context, stage, outcome.receipt)\n\n    async def _attempt(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        stage: str,\n        method: str,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation:\n        \"\"\"Run one effect invocation under a fresh absolute monotonic deadline.\n\n        Uncertain effect tasks are never cancelled: timeouts and caller\n        cancellation abandon the task into a bounded set whose results are\n        consumed later, and the stage is recorded unresolved first.\n        \"\"\"\n        request = context.request\n        owner_token = context.owner_token\n        if len(self._abandoned_effects) >= _MAX_ABANDONED_EFFECTS:\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"timeout_unknown\")\n        effect = self._effects[stage]\n        call = effect.apply if method == \"apply\" else effect.reconcile\n        task = asyncio.create_task(call(context))\n        deadline = monotonic() + self._effect_timeout_seconds\n        try:\n            done, _pending = await asyncio.wait(\n                {task},\n                timeout=max(0.0, deadline - monotonic()),\n            )\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            self._abandon(task)\n            self._record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, \"cancellation_unknown\")\n            raise\n        if task not in done:\n            self._abandon(task)\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"timeout_unknown\")\n        try:\n            result = task.result()\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=\"cancellation_unknown\")\n        except StageRejected as rejected:\n            raise _StageTerminal(\n                self._record_rejected(request, owner_token, stage, rejected)\n            ) from None\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as unknown:\n            return StageReconciliation(outcome=\"unknown\", reason=unknown.reason)\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n            return StageReconciliation(\n                outcome=\"unknown\",\n                reason=_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage],\n            )\n        if not isinstance(result, StageReconciliation):\n            return StageReconciliation(\n                outcome=\"unknown\",\n                reason=_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage],\n            )\n        return result\n\n    def _persist_completed(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        stage: str,\n        receipt: object | None,\n    ) -> bytes | None:\n        \"\"\"Persist one completed stage; reclaim requires its signed response.\"\"\"\n        request = context.request\n        owner_token = context.owner_token\n        if stage == \"reclaim\":\n            if not isinstance(receipt, ReclaimReceipt):\n                raise TypeError(\"replica reclaim receipt type is invalid\")\n            response = create_signed_response(\n                request,\n                private_key=self._broker_private_key,\n                status=\"ok\",\n                error=None,\n                result={\n                    \"stage\": \"reclaim\",\n                    \"state\": \"completed\",\n                    \"receipt_id\": receipt.reclaim_receipt_id,\n                },\n            )\n            self._journal.complete_reclaim(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                receipt=receipt,\n                response_frame=response,\n            )\n            return response\n        completer = getattr(self._journal, f\"complete_{stage}\")\n        completer(request, owner_token=owner_token, receipt=receipt)\n        return None\n\n    def _record_rejected(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        owner_token: str,\n        stage: str,\n        rejected: StageRejected,\n    ) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"Record one rejected stage with its exact signed terminal response.\"\"\"\n        response = create_signed_response(\n            request,\n            private_key=self._broker_private_key,\n            status=\"error\",\n            error=rejected.status,\n            result={\n                \"stage\": stage,\n                \"state\": \"rejected\",\n                \"code\": rejected.status,\n                \"receipt_id\": rejected.receipt_id,\n            },\n        )\n        self._journal.record_rejected(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            status=rejected.status,\n            receipt=RejectedReceipt(receipt_id=rejected.receipt_id),\n            response_frame=response,\n        )\n        return response\n\n    def _record_unresolved(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        owner_token: str,\n        stage: str,\n        reason: str,\n    ) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"Record one unresolved stage with its exact signed terminal response.\"\"\"\n        response = create_signed_response(\n            request,\n            private_key=self._broker_private_key,\n            status=\"error\",\n            error=reason,\n            result={\"stage\": stage, \"state\": \"unresolved\", \"code\": reason},\n        )\n        self._journal.record_unresolved(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            reason=reason,\n            response_frame=response,\n        )\n        return response\n\n    def _abandon(self, task: asyncio.Task[StageReconciliation]) -> None:\n        self._abandoned_effects.add(task)\n        task.add_done_callback(self._consume_abandoned)\n\n    def _consume_abandoned(self, task: asyncio.Task[StageReconciliation]) -> None:\n        self._abandoned_effects.discard(task)\n        if not task.cancelled():\n            task.exception()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Packet C — minimal edits to `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py`\n\nThree targeted edits, each with unique anchors (verified against the current file):\n\n**C1. Add the immutable `ReplicaAuthority` field to `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle`** — oldText:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IncompleteReplicaLifecycle:\n    request_frame: bytes\n    owner_token: str\n    owner_broker_incarnation: str\n    stage: str\n    stage_started: bool\n    reason: str\n```\n\nnewText:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass IncompleteReplicaLifecycle:\n    request_frame: bytes\n    owner_token: str\n    owner_broker_incarnation: str\n    stage: str\n    stage_started: bool\n    reason: str\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n```\n\n**C2. Populate the authority in `incomplete_lifecycles()`** — oldText:\n\n```python\n                pending.append(\n                    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle(\n                        request_frame=replay.request_frame,\n                        owner_token=replay.owner_token,\n                        owner_broker_incarnation=cast(str, replay.owner_broker_incarnation),\n                        stage=_STAGES[replay.next_stage_index],\n                        stage_started=replay.stage_started,\n                        reason=\"broker_restart_unknown\",\n                    )\n                )\n```\n\nnewText:\n\n```python\n                pending.append(\n                    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle(\n                        request_frame=replay.request_frame,\n                        owner_token=replay.owner_token,\n                        owner_broker_incarnation=cast(str, replay.owner_broker_incarnation),\n                        stage=_STAGES[replay.next_stage_index],\n                        stage_started=replay.stage_started,\n                        reason=\"broker_restart_unknown\",\n                        authority=replay.authority,\n                    )\n                )\n```\n\n**C3. Add the journal-owned trusted request parsing method** (inserted immediately before `_validate_stage`) — oldText:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_stage(stage: str) -> None:\n```\n\nnewText:\n\n```python\n    def authenticated_request(self, lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle) -> BrokerRequest:\n        \"\"\"Return the typed request authenticated from one incomplete lifecycle.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(lifecycle, IncompleteReplicaLifecycle):\n            raise TypeError(\"replica lifecycle is invalid\")\n        frame = lifecycle.request_frame\n        if not isinstance(frame, (bytes, bytearray)) or not frame:\n            raise ReplicaJournalSyncError(\"replica lifecycle request frame is invalid\")\n        try:\n            return _authenticate_request_frame(bytes(frame), self._request_public_key)\n        except ValueError as error:\n            raise ReplicaJournalSyncError(\n                \"replica lifecycle request authentication failed\"\n            ) from error\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_stage(stage: str) -> None:\n```\n\nDesign note: `authenticated_request` returns only the typed `BrokerRequest` because the authority travels on the immutable lifecycle itself (packet C1) — the journal keeps exposing no database objects, and parsing goes through the journal's own configured request public key.\n\n---\n\n## Packet D — ordered checks (run after applying Packets A–C under a bound TDD request)\n\n1. **Red (focused, tests only applied first):** `cd backend && .venv/bin/pytest tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py -q`\n   Expected clean failure: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yinshi.services.broker_replica_lifecycle'` — no partial passes.\n2. **Green (focused, after B+C):** same command. Expected: `17 passed` (14 test functions; the parametrized recovery test expands to 4).\n3. **Journal regression:** `.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py -q` — expected: all pass (no external constructor of `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` exists; the new field is keyword-supplied inside the journal).\n4. **Broader:** `.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py tests/test_broker_foundation.py -q`, then the full suite `.venv/bin/pytest -q` if time permits. Expected: no new failures; unrelated dirty files untouched.\n5. **Lint/type:** `.venv/bin/black --check src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py` and `.venv/bin/mypy src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py` (strict profile configured in pyproject). Expected: clean.\n","truncated":true,"truncatedBy":"bytes","totalLines":1406,"totalBytes":51450,"outputLines":1405,"outputBytes":51047,"lastLinePartial":false,"firstLineExceedsLimit":false,"maxLines":2000,"maxBytes":51200}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789262632760}}
