n      \"wrapUpRequested\": true,\n      \"progressSummary\": {\n        \"toolCount\": 29,\n        \"tokens\": 176437,\n        \"durationMs\": 430212\n      },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"fileMutation\": {\n          \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n          \"expected\": false,\n          \"attempted\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n      \"finalOutput\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 8 assistant turns (soft limit 8, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Confirmed findings\\n\\n### High: effect evidence validation remains partial\\n\\nLocations:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:445-455`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:467-530`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1789-1794`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1818-1819`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1869-1870`\\n\\nRuntime checks reject wrong receipt classes. They do not handle correct receipt classes with invalid request or authority bindings.\\n\\nJournal binding validation then raises after the external effect has completed. Lifecycle remains `stage_started` without required stage-specific unresolved outcome.\\n\\nInvalid `StageOutcomeUnknown.reason` or `StageRejected` fields have the same failure. Journal validation rejects them instead of recording fallback unresolved state.\\n\\nImpact: adapter defects can strand durable lifecycles after external effects. Later stages stop, but callers receive exceptions instead of durable terminal responses.\\n\\nCorrection: classify effect evidence before persistence. Convert semantic evidence failures to `_UNEXPECTED_ERROR_REASONS[stage]`. Preserve journal I/O and commit failures as escaping errors.\\n\\nJournal should expose a specific evidence-validation exception. This avoids duplicating receipt policy in coordinator.\\n\\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Return each correct receipt class with mismatched authenticated bindings.\\n- Test invalid unknown reasons.\\n- Test invalid rejection status and receipt identifiers.\\n- Assert exact stage-specific unresolved responses.\\n- Assert no later effect runs.\\n- Assert commit and journal sync failures still escape.\\n\\n### High: signing-key mismatch is detected after external effects\\n\\nLocations:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:184-223`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:479-577`\\n\\nConstructor checks private-key type only. It does not verify that key matches journal signer authority for configured broker incarnation.\\n\\nA mismatched key can permit all effects through reclaim. Journal rejects signed terminal response only after reclaim has run.\\n\\nImpact: irreversible reclaim can complete externally while journal remains `reclaim_started`. Recovery can repeat this failure indefinitely.\\n\\nCorrection: add journal-owned signer compatibility validation. Invoke it before accepting requests or invoking effects.\\n\\nReject requests whose broker incarnation differs from coordinator incarnation. Different-incarnation recovery needs retained historical signing authority or an approved recovery signature contract.\\n\\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Construct coordinator with wrong private key.\\n- Assert failure occurs before acceptance and before any effect.\\n- Test recovery with distinct historical and current keys.\\n- Verify successful reclaim remains bound to exact request and receipt.\\n\\n## Prior findings\\n\\n- Prior concurrent-duplicate finding is resolved for normal `run()` calls. Gate ownership, waiter counts, terminal replay, and cleanup logic are coherent.\\n- Prior typed-effect finding is partially resolved. Wrong classes become unresolved, but semantically invalid evidence still escapes.\\n\\n## Other reviewed guarantees\\n\\n- No SQLite connection or cursor crosses an inspected `await`.\\n- Journal remains durable lifecycle authority.\\n- Started stages reconcile during same-incarnation recovery.\\n- Timeout and cancellation cannot publish late completion.\\n- Reclaim completion requires a signed, request-bound response.\\n- Short terminal codes retain strict lowercase code grammar.\\n- Operation-gate capacity is bounded and cleanup logic appears sound.\\n\\nUnanswered questions: none.\\n\\n## Required checks\\n\\nAfter correction:\\n\\n1. Add semantic receipt, malformed outcome, and signer mismatch tests.\\n2. Add cancellation tests for a waiting duplicate and active owner.\\n3. Run focused pytest, Ruff check, Ruff format, strict mypy, and `py_compile`.\\n\\nCurrent candidate results were reported as passing. This review did not repeat them because the task required read-only operation.\\n\\nCompletion remains blocked by both findings.\",\n      \"controlEvents\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"ts\": 1789263819968,\n          \"runId\": \"97862f63\",\n          \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n          \"index\": 0,\n          \"message\": \"final-review is still active but long-running\",\n          \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n          \"turns\": 7,\n          \"tokens\": 147974,\n          \"toolCount\": 29,\n          \"elapsedMs\": 240539\n        }\n      ],\n      \"attemptedModels\": [\n        \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAttempts\": [\n        {\n          \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\",\n          \"success\": true,\n          \"exitCode\": 0,\n          \"usage\": {\n            \"input\": 162549,\n            \"output\": 13888,\n            \"cacheRead\": 251392,\n            \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n            \"cost\": 1.3550810000000002,\n            \"turns\": 8\n          }\n        }\n   