design review rules from the loaded software-design skill.\nOriginal contract: exact ordered stages ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. Journal is sole durable authority. No SQLite handle crosses await or an external effect. Unknown outcomes become stage-specific unresolved. Timeout and cancellation discard late completion. Recovery inspects started effects. Reclaim completion is signed.\nPrior finding 1: concurrent duplicates could execute a stage twice. Disposition: added bounded per-operation gates with waiter counting, cancellation cleanup, and terminal replay after lock acquisition. Added concurrent duplicate test.\nPrior finding 2: untyped effect map permitted wrong receipts. Disposition: added generic ReplicaStageEffect, typed ReplicaLifecycleEffects, explicit receipt dispatch, runtime receipt checks, and seven wrong-receipt tests that persist stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\nAlso fixed terminal response code validation because existing token grammar rejected valid short reason codes. Added authority to immutable incomplete lifecycle plus authenticated request recovery accessor.\nCurrent results: 61 focused tests passed. Ruff lint passed. Strict mypy passed on both source files. py_compile passed. Ruff format had one test-only wrap discrepancy, now corrected.\nInspect actual files and diff. Check prior findings, concurrency cancellation, capacity cleanup, persistence boundaries, signed response bindings, started-stage recovery, and unexpected effect results.\nReturn all findings with severity, location, impact, correction, and validation. If none remain, state no remediation needed. Read only.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"final-review","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"743dbb296d84c994a3e53b6e390550851b4c83867111cc474cc36d42cdf375ac","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolve