replica_journal.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py"}]}],"totalChildUsage":{"input":110523,"output":14783,"cacheRead":74880,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.0335450000000002,"turns":6},"totalCost":{"inputTokens":110523,"outputTokens":14783,"costUsd":1.0335450000000002},"workflow":{"value":{"key":"coordinator-final-clearance","ok":true,"runId":"541cd5ae","output":"## Findings\n\n### Blocker: retries can reapply a durably started effect\n\nLocation:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\n- `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run()`, branch after `_claim_within_deadline()`\n- `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator._drive_from()`\n\n`run()` ignores `ReplicaJournalDecision.state == \"in_flight\"`. It sends that stage to `_drive_from()`, which calls `apply()` instead of `reconcile()`.\n\nImpact:\n\nA stage effect may complete while its completion append fails. A retry then executes that effect again. Publish, export, or reclaim can produce conflicting irreversible outcomes.\n\nCorrection:\n\nRoute every durable `in_flight` stage through reconciliation while holding its operation gate. Apply only after reconciliation returns `not_applied`. Share this logic with startup recovery.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired validation:\n\n- Inject `ReplicaJournalCommitAbsent` after an effect completes.\n- Retry through `run()`.\n- Assert reconciliation occurs before any second apply.\n- Cover completed, not-applied, and unknown reconciliation outcomes.\n\n### High: durable journal configuration prevents broker key rotation\n\nLocation:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1004-1059`\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal.__init__()`, `_configuration_sha256`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1138-1172`\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal._validate()`, journal ID configuration check\n\nConfiguration digest includes full `response_public_keys` mapping. Adding a new broker incarnation changes that digest. Existing journal then refuses to open.\n\nImpact:\n\nA restarted broker cannot add its new key while retaining the historical key. Historical recovery only works when future broker incarnations were preconfigured before journal creation.\n\nCorrection:\n\nPersist response authority per broker incarnation through an append-only authority registry. Another valid design stores accepted signer fingerprint with each lifecycle. Reject key substitution.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired validation:\n\n1. Create journal with old broker key only.\n2. Leave old lifecycle incomplete.\n3. Reopen with retained old key plus new current key.\n4. Recover old lifecycle using old signer.\n5. Accept new lifecycle using new signer.\n6. Reject missing or replaced historical keys.\n\n### High: malformed effect invocation bypasses unresolved recording\n\nLocation:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\n- `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator._attempt()`\n- Calls to `effect.apply()` or `effect.reconcile()` and `asyncio.create_task()`\n\nEffect invocation and task creation occur outside protected result handling. A callable can raise synchronously or return a non-coroutine despite passing constructor checks.\n\nImpact:\n\nJournal retains `stage_started` without a stage-specific unresolved result. Request can remain blocked. A retry can also reach the duplicate-effect defect above.\n\nCorrection:\n\nGuard invocation and task creation. Normalize supported awaitables before scheduling. Convert adapter failures to stage fallback unresolved. Preserve all journal write failures unchanged.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired validation:\n\n- Effect method raises synchronously.\n- Effect method returns a non-awaitable.\n- Effect method returns a supported custom awaitable.\n- Each malformed case records exact stage fallback.\n- Journal append failures still propagate.\n\n## Prior finding disposition\n\n- Concurrent duplicate gate: resolved for overlapping `run()` calls. Sequential in-flight retry remains unsafe.\n- Wrong receipt classes: resolved through typed effect fields plus runtime receipt validation.\n- Semantic receipt binding: resolved through journal-owned validators.\n- Signer mismatch: constructor matching and historical signer selection are resolved. Durable keyring evolution remains broken.\n- Timeout and cancellation: late results cannot append completion after terminal unresolved state.\n- Gate cleanup: waiter accounting and cancellation cleanup appear correct.\n- Journal I/O preservation: journal exceptions remain visible. Follow-up retry handling remains unsafe.\n\nCompletion blocked by three findings. Remediation is required.\n\n## Validation status\n\nReported `66 passed` was not repeated. Existing tests do not cover identified retry, key rotation, or malformed invocation paths.\n\nRuff, format, and strict mypy results were not repeated after final formatting changes. Run them against corrected final candidate.","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/541cd5ae/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"final-review","task":"[Read from: /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py]\n\nRead-only final review of corrected broker replica lifecycle milestone. Use software-design skill rules.\nContract: journal owns durable order. Coordinator serializes duplicates per operation, validates signer authority before effects, validates typed and semantic stage results, records stage-specific unresolved results for malformed effects, preserves journal I/O failures, and never accepts current requests for another broker incarnation. Historical recovery uses retained matching signing keys.\nPrior findings: duplicate execution fixed with bounded operation gates. Wrong receipt classes fixed with typed effect bundle and runtime checks. Semantic result failures fixed through journal-owned no-database validators. Signer mismatch fixed with constructor-time journal key verification and broker-incarnation keyring.\nCurrent results: 66 focused tests passed. Ruff and strict mypy passed before final formatting changes. Ruff format discrepancies were corrected manually.\nInspect actual current files and diff. Confirm each prior finding disposition. Check malformed rejection and unknown fallback, semantic receipt binding, current versus historical signer selection, cancellation, timeout, per-operation gate cleanup, restart handling, and journal persistence failures.\nReturn each finding with severity, location, impact, correction, and validation. If none remain, state no remediation needed. Read only.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"final-review","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"845bdbbb4f0e485a7a3a4da50f61539b13ff49c27f436232af8f4b5ddf88b259","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":110523,"output":14783,"cacheRead":74880,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.0335450000000002,"turns":6},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","thinking":"max","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/541cd5ae_final-review_0_input.md","outputP