       \"ls\"\n          ],\n          \"toolCount\": 26,\n          \"outcome\": \"soft-reached\",\n          \"softReachedAt\": 24\n        },\n        \"context\": \"fresh\",\n        \"wrapUpRequested\": true,\n        \"progressSummary\": {\n          \"toolCount\": 26,\n          \"tokens\": 148644,\n          \"durationMs\": 325281\n        },\n        \"effects\": {\n          \"fileMutation\": {\n            \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n            \"expected\": false,\n            \"attempted\": true\n          }\n        },\n        \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n        \"finalOutput\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 10 assistant turns (soft limit 10, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nNow I have sufficient context. Here is the structured inspection report.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Production Broker Inspection Report\\n\\n## 1. Broker Request Dispatch\\n\\n**Path:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py`\\n**Class:** `BrokerService` (line ~112)\\n**Entry point:** `BrokerService.handle(frame, *, peer_uid)` (line ~288)\\n\\n**Current API:**\\n- Accepts exactly one request type: `\\\"executor.launch\\\"` (constant `_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE`, line 18)\\n- Forbids specific payload fields (line 21-40) — `replica`, `socket`, `cgroup`, `capabilities`, etc.\\n- Authenticates via peer UID + Ed25519 signature on `BrokerProtocolError.parse_signed_request(frame)`\\n- Persists to `BrokerJournal` (3-stage: prepare, runtime_setup, launch)\\n- Owns ownership gate: single lifecycle owner per operation via `secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` owner token\\n- `LauncherClient` protocol (line 65-70) defines `prepare()`, `launch()`, `reclaim()`\\n- `BrokerRuntimeManager` protocol (line 72) defines `setup(operation_id)`\\n\\n**Constraints:**\\n- `BrokerService._authenticate()` (line 162) checks `request.request_type != \\\"executor.launch\\\"` — blocks `replica.lifecycle` requests\\n- `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS` includes `\\\"replica\\\"` and `\\\"socket\\\"` — replica payloads would be rejected even if the type check were changed\\n- No `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` wiring exists in `BrokerService`\\n\\n**Severity: blocker** — `execution_broker.py` does not support `replica.lifecycle` requests.\\n\\n## 2. Broker Runtime Connection Handling\\n\\n**Path:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py`\\n**Class:** `BrokerRuntime` (line 43)\\n\\n**Current API:**\\n- `BrokerRuntime.setup(operation_id) -> BrokerRuntimeSession` (line 85)\\n- Creates private Unix domain socket at `<runtime_root>/<operation_id>/session.sock`\\n- Validates root traversal via fd-atop-fd atomic traversal (line 60-75)\\n- Validates ownership: uid/gid/mode 0o711 on ancestors, 0o700 on operation dir, 0o600 on socket\\n- `BrokerRuntime.session(operation_id) -> BrokerRuntimeSession | None` (line 140)\\n- `BrokerRuntime.close(operation_id) -> None` (line 145)\\n- Thread-safe via `threading.RLock()` on `_sessions` dict\\n- Backlog: 8 (`_LISTEN_BACKLOG`, line 15)\\n- Max sessions: unbounded in-memory dict (limited by file descriptors)\\n\\n**Constraints:**\\n- `BrokerRuntime` expects absolute path root (line 52)\\n- `BrokerRuntimeLayout` is a frozen dataclass with `runtime_root: Path`\\n- Operation ID pattern: `[0-9a-f]{32,64}` (line 13) — replica operation IDs use 32 hex chars\\n- Session sockets are NOT automatically cleaned up on close (requires external cleanup)\\n\\n**Severity: none** — runtime is usable for replica lifecycle.\\n\\n## 3. Signed Protocol Types\\n\\n**Path:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py`\\n**Key symbols:** `BrokerRequest`, `BrokerResponse`, `parse_signed_request()`, `create_signed_response()`, `verify_broker_response()`\\n\\n**Current API:**\\n- `BROKER_PROTOCOL_VERSION = \\\"yinshi-broker-v1\\\"` (line 17)\\n- `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX = 65,536` (line 18)\\n- `BROKER_RESPONSE_BYTES_MAX = 4,096` (line 19)\\n- `BrokerRequest` dataclass (line 54): 9 fields, all frozen\\n- `BrokerResponse` dataclass (line 70): 12 fields, all frozen\\n- `create_signed_request()` (line 164): domain `YINSHI-BROKER-REQUEST-V1\\\\0`\\n- `create_signed_response()` (line 199): domain `YINSHI-BROKER-RESPONSE-V1\\\\0`\\n- `parse_signed_request(frame, *, public_key)` (line 181): strict schema validation, rejects unknown fields\\n- `verify_broker_response(frame, *, public_key, expected_request)` (line 222): binds response to request identity\\n- Canonical JSON: depth limit 8, max 64 elements, integers bounded to ±2^53, strings max 4096 bytes\\n- No floating-point support (`_reject_float`)\\n\\n**Constraints:**\\n- Request keys are frozen set of exactly 10 fields (line 28-38)\\n- Response keys are frozen set of exactly 12 fields (line 39-51)\\n- Payload is `dict[str, JsonValue]` — no nested structure beyond depth 8\\n- Operation ID pattern: `[0-9a-f]{32}` (line 25)\\n- Signature: base64url-encoded 64-byte Ed25519\\n\\n**Severity: none** — protocol is fully generic and reusable for replica lifecycle.\\n\\n## 4. Desktop-to-VM stdio Relay\\n\\n**Path:** `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_rely.py`\\n**Key functions:** `relay_broker_request()`, `read_blocking_frame()`, `write_blocking_frame()`\\n\\n**Current API:**\\n- `relay_broker_request(request: bytes, *, broker_socket: Path, timeout_seconds: float)` (line 120)\\n  - One-shot bounded opaque exchange with broker Unix socket\\n  - Uses `asyncio.open_unix_connection` for transport\\n  - Timeout default: 125 seconds (`RELAY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`)\\n- `read_blocking_frame(stream: BinaryIO, maximum: int) -> bytes` (line 90)\\n  - Reads one length-prefixed frame from stdin (4-byte big-endian length prefix)\\n  - Requires EOF after payload\\n- `write_blocking_frame(stream: BinaryIO, body: bytes) -> None` (line 107)\\n  - Writes one bounded response frame to stdout\\n  - Response bounded by `BROKER_RESPONSE_BYTES_MAX` (4096)\\n- `main(argv)` (line 153): CLI entry point, rejects all options\\n- Error codes (opaque to relay): `input_invalid`, `input_limit`, `output_invalid`, `output_limit`, `timeout_unknown`, `transport_unknown`, `verification_unknown`\\n\\n**Constraints:**\\n- Relay is opaque: never inspects payload bytes\\n- Default socket: `/run/yinshi/broker.sock` (line 31)\\n- Only supports one request at a time (synchronous)\\n- No multiplexing — each stdin read maps to exactly one response write\\n\\n**Severity: none** — relay works as a one-shot proxy. Does NOT support streaming artifact transfers.\\n\\n## 5. Replica Lifecycle Coordinator\\n\\n**Path:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\\n**Class:** `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` (line 147)\\n\\n**Current API:**\\n- `run(request, request_frame, authority) -> bytes` (line 207)\\n  - Accepts, claims, and drives one replica through the journal-owned fixed stage order\\n  - Stages: `ingest`, `verify`, `publish`, `admission`, `drain`, `export`, `reclaim`\\n- `recover_incomplete() -> None` (line 186): recovers incomplete lifecycles before serving\\n- `ReplicaLifecycleEffects` dataclass (line 131): binds each stage to `ReplicaStageEffect[T]` protocol\\n- `_drive_from(context, start_stage)` (line 271): advances through stages sequentially\\n- `_apply_stage(context, stage)` (line 281): begins stage, attempts effect, persists or records error\\n- Operation gates: max 256 concurrent operations (`_MAX_OPERATION_GATES`)\\n- Abandoned effects: max 32 (`_MAX_ABANDONED_EFFECTS`)\\n- Effect timeout: default 30s, max 3600s\\n- Owner wait: default 10s, max 3600s, poll 50ms\\n\\n**Severity: none** — coordinator is complete and wired to `BrokerReplicaJournal`.\\n\\n## 6. Artifact Store (Three Bounded Streams)\\n\\n**Path:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py`\\n**Class:** `BrokerArtifactStore` (line 131)\\n\\n**Current API:**\\n- `receive(manifest: ReplicaArtifactManifest, reader: asyncio.StreamReader) -> IngestReceipt` (line 311)\\n  - Receives exactly 3 artifact streams in fixed order: bundle, worktree, index_objects\\n  - Each stream: variable-length body + SHA-256 digest verification\\n  - Bounded by `BrokerArtifactLimits`:\\n    - `max_bundle_bytes = 512 MiB`\\n    - `max_worktree_bytes = 512 MiB`\\n    - `max_index_objects_bytes = 512 MiB`\\n    - `max_set_bytes = 1 GiB` (total)\\n    - `chunk_bytes = 64 KiB`\\n    - `idle_timeout_seconds = 30s`, `transfer_timeout_seconds = 120s`\\n- `RepliaArtifactManifest(operation_id, bundle, worktree, index_objects)` (line 80)\\n- `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` (line 111): descriptor handles for all 3 artifacts\\n- `open_incoming(manifest) -> Iterator[OpenedReplicaArtifacts]` (line 542)\\n- `inspect_incoming(manifest) -> IngestReceipt` (line 627)\\n- `reconcile_attempts(journal_manifests) -> tuple[ArtifactReconciliationResult]` (line 469)\\n- Atomic upload: pending directory -> write 3 files -> fsync -> atomic rename\\n\\n**Severity: none** — store fully supports three bounded artifact streams.\\n\\n## 7. Missing Contracts and Wiring\\n\\n### 7.1 Execution Broker does not dispatch replica lifecycle requests\\n`execution_broker.py` line 18: `_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE = \\\"executor.launch\\\"`\\n`execution_broker.py` line 170: `if request.request_type != _SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE` raises `BrokerProtocolError`\\n\\n**Impact:** `replica.lifecycle` requests are rejected at the broker's entry point.\\n\\n**Minimum wiring needed:** Either add `\\\"replica.lifecycle\\\"` to supported types OR create a separate `BrokerReplicaService` that wires `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` into the broker's accept-handling path.\\n\\n### 7.2 No artifact upload transport protocol defined for the stdio relay\\nThe `broker_stdio_relay.py` handles single-frame opaque exchanges. The artifact store's `BrokerArtifactStore.receive()` expects an `asyncio.StreamReader` with multi-chunk streaming (multiple chunks of up to `chunk_bytes` per artifact).\\n\\n**Impact:** The current relay cannot serve `ingest` stage artifact uploads.\\n\\n**Minimum wiring needed:** A transport layer that:\\n1. Authenticates the request via the relay\\n2. Opens a dedicated stream for artifact bytes (not the single-frame relay)\\n3. Streams bundle (512 MiB max), worktree (512 MiB max), index_objects (512 MiB max) with SHA-256 verification\\n\\n### 7.3 `BrokerReplicaJournal` and `BrokerJournal` are separate systems\\n- `BrokerJournal` (executor): 3 stages — prepare, runtime_setup, launch\\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` (replica): 7 stages — ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim\\n\\n**Impact:** These are parallel, unconnected journal systems. The `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` requires `BrokerReplicaJournal`, not `BrokerJournal`.\\n\\n**Minimum wiring needed:** A `BrokerReplicaService` (analogous to `BrokerService`) that:\\n1. Accepts signed `replica.lifecycle` frames\\n2. Authenticates via `BrokerReplicaJournal._authenticate_request_frame()`\\n3. Accepts into journal\\n4. Delegates to `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run()`\\n5. Returns signed response frames\\n\\n### 7.4 `ReplicaAuthority` is external to the broker\\n`broker_replica_journal.py` line 110: `ReplicaAuthority(physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id)`\\n\\n**Impact:** The authority must be supplied by the caller when invoking the coordinator. There is no internal authority derivation.\\n\\n**Minimum wiring needed:** The caller of `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run()` must construct `ReplicaAuthority` from trusted application state before passing it to the broker.\\n\\n### 7.5 No `ReplicaStageEffect` implementations exist\\n`broker_replica_lifecycle.py` line 126: `ReplicaStageEffect[ReceiptT_co]` protocol with `apply()` and `reconcile()` methods.\\n`broker_replica_lifecycle.py` line 127-134: `ReplicaLifecycleEffects` dataclass binds each of the 7 stages to an effect.\\n\\n**Impact:** Without concrete `ReplicaStageEffect` implementations for ingest/verify/publish/admission/drain/export/reclaim, the coordinator cannot drive any stage to completion.\\n\\n**Minimum wiring needed:** Implement `ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]` (and others) that:\\n- `apply()`: calls `BrokerArtifactStore.receive()` for ingest, or drives external runners for other stages\\n- `reconcile()`: checks if the stage outcome is already recorded in the journal\\n\\n### 7.6 Runner relay and broker relay are disconnected\\n- `runner_relay.py` `RunnerRelayBroker`: WebSocket relay between runner and clients (transfer grants, sessions)\\n- `runner_agent_relay.py` `RunnerAgentRelayRuntime`: runner-side multiplexing for encrypted RPC frames\\n- No bridge connects `BrokerRuntime` Unix sockets to `RunnerRelayBroker` WebSocket connections\\n\\n**Impact:** Replica runtime sockets created by `BrokerRuntime.setup()` are not accessible to runner relay sessions.\\n\\n**Minimum wiring needed:** A transport adapter that accepts connections on `BrokerRuntime` Unix sockets and routes them through `RunnerRelayBroker` or equivalent encrypted session.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Structured Acceptance Report\",\n        \"controlEvents\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"ts\": 1789266498896,\n            \"runId\": \"559f3557\",\n            \"agent\": \"scout\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": \"scout is still active but long-running\",\n            \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n            \"turns\": 11,\n            \"tokens\": 129989,\n            \"toolCount\": 26,\n            \"elapsedMs\": 240716\n          }\n        ],\n        \"attemptedModels\": [\n          \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\"\n        ],\n        \"modelAttempts\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\",\n            \"success\": true,\n            \"exitCode\": 0,\n            \"usage\": {\n              \"input\": 140421,\n              \"outpu