any of the 7 lifecycle stages. The coordinator can accept and drive stages but has no actual effect implementations.\",\n              \"The stdio relay only supports single-frame opaque exchanges. Artifact ingest requires multi-chunk streaming of up to 512 MiB per artifact (3 streams total). No transport protocol bridges the gap.\",\n              \"BrokerRuntime Unix sockets are not connected to RunnerRelayBroker WebSocket connections. No transport adapter exists to bridge the broker-owned runtime socket to encrypted runner sessions.\",\n              \"ReplicaAuthority must be supplied externally by the caller. No internal authority derivation or validation against a trusted data source is implemented.\",\n              \"BrokerJournal (executor) and BrokerReplicaJournal (replica) are separate SQLite files with incompatible schemas. No migration or cross-journal lookup mechanism exists.\",\n              \"Maximum 256 concurrent operation gates in BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator and 32 abandoned effects — unbounded in-memory state that could exhaust resources under load.\",\n              \"Artifact store enforces max 4096 root entries — may need expansion if many concurrent operations are pending.\"\n            ],\n            \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n            \"diffSummary\": \"No files were modified. Pure read-only inspection of the repository.\",\n            \"reviewFindings\": [\n              \"blocker: execution_broker.py:18 - _SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE is 'executor.launch'; replica.lifecycle requests are rejected at the broker entry point\",\n              \"blocker: execution_broker.py:170 - _FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS contains 'replica' and 'socket'; even if type were accepted, payload would be rejected\",\n              \"blocker: No BrokerReplicaService exists; BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator is constructed but never wired into the request handling path\",\n              \"blocker: No ReplicaStageEffect implementations exist for ingest/verify/publish/admission/drain/export/reclaim — coordinator cannot complete any stage\",\n              \"blocker: broker_stdio_relay.py is single-frame opaque only; cannot stream multi-chunk artifact bytes required by BrokerArtifactStore.receive()\",\n              \"warning: runner_relay.py and runner_agent_relay.py handle WebSocket/encrypted sessions but BrokerRuntime Unix sockets are not bridged to any relay session\",\n              \"warning: BrokerReplicaAuthority is constructed externally; no internal validation or trust chain is implemented for physical_target_id and execution_owner_id\",\n              \"info: three bounded artifact streams (bundle, worktree, index_objects) are fully specified in broker_artifact_store.py with SHA-256 verification, 512 MiB per-stream limits, and 1 GiB total limit\",\n              \"info: signed protocol types (broker_protocol.py) are fully reusable for replica lifecycle — no modifications needed to BrokerRequest/BrokerResponse schemas\",\n              \"info: desktop-to-VM stdio relay (broker_stdio_relay.py) is complete for single-request opaque exchange but does not support streaming artifact transfers\"\n            ],\n            \"manualNotes\": \"The repository has a mature but fragmented broker architecture. Executor lifecycle (3 stages) and replica lifecycle (7 stages) are implemented as parallel, unconnected systems. The signed protocol types, artifact store with three bounded streams, and stdio relay are all production-ready individually. The missing piece is the orchestration bridge: a BrokerReplicaService that accepts signed replica.lifecycle frames, delegates to BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator with ReplicaAuthority, and routes artifact upload streams through a transport adapter that connects the broker runtime socket to the runner relay. The artifact store itself already supports the three bounded streams (bundle, worktree, index_objects) — the gap is the transport protocol to deliver bytes to it.\"\n          }\n    