/yinshi && grep -rn \"external\" --include=\"*.py\" backend/src/yinshi/ | grep -v \"__pycache__\" | wc -l"},{"text":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && grep -rn \"class.*External\\...","expandedText":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && grep -rn \"class.*External\\|EXTERNAL\\|_EXTERNAL\\|extern_ref\" --include=\"*.py\" backend/src/yinshi/ | grep -v \"__pycache__\" | head -10"},{"text":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && grep -rn \"REPLICA_ARTIFACT...","expandedText":"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi && grep -rn \"REPLICA_ARTIFACT_FILENAMES\\|REPLICA_OPERATION_PATTERN\" --include=\"*.py\" backend/src/yinshi/ | grep -v \"__pycache__\" | head -10"}]},{"index":0,"agent":"scout","task":"Compare Phase 7 requirements in /Users/user/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md with the current checkout implementation and tests. Report a concise requirement-by-requirement gap list, noting what Phase 5 already supplies and what remains blocked by Phase 6. Do not modify files.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"scout","model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3","thinking":"high","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"46ddaae0d3110b012112542aed1b0fa198ec5144593e6a5dbaa8956ed5ee1d11","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":70989,"output":5682,"cacheRead":632503,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":16},"model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high","thinking":"high","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/866834bc_scout_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/866834bc_scout_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/866834bc_scout_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/866834bc_scout_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/866834bc_scout_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/866834bc_scout_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":10,"graceTurns":2,"turnCount":16,"outcome":"wrap-up-requested","wrapUpRequestedAtTurn":10},"toolBudget":{"hard":36,"soft":24,"block":["bash","read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":35,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":24},"context":"fresh","wrapUpRequested":true,"progressSummary":{"toolCount":35,"tokens":76671,"durationMs":501907},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":true}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 10 assistant turns (soft limit 10, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nPhase 7 gap analysis complete. Here are the findings.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7 Requirements vs Current Checkout\n\nPhase 7 covers three features: **nested delegation** (depth up to 3), **cost/usage budgets**, and **child steering** (`thread_inbox_messages`).\n\n### 1. Nested Delegation\n\n**What Phase 5 supplies:**\n- Tree queries resolve nested descendants to depth 32 (hard limit in `_ANCESTRY_HOP_LIMIT`). Tested in `test_thread_queries.py:127-172` with grandchild rows.\n- `ThreadOrchestrationService.spawn_child()` enforces depth via `allows_spawn(depth, ...)` at `thread_orchestration.py:2935-2942`.\n- Cascade cancellation exists at `thread_orchestration.py:1632-1652` with its own `depth >= 32` guard.\n- Authorization uses `check_session_owner()` which only validates tenant ownership, not descendant scope.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- **Default `thread_max_depth = 1` blocks nested spawns.** `config.py:216`. Changing to 3 enables the math but no tests validate depth > 1 spawn paths.\n- **Recursive deletion NOT implemented.** The spec requires `DELETE /api/threads/{id}?recursive=true`. The `threads.py` API has zero DELETE endpoints. `backend/src/yinshi/api/threads.py` has no `delete` route.\n- **No tests at depth > 1.** All `test_thread_queries.py` limit tests use `max_depth=1` implicitly. `test_thread_orchestration.py` has no `depth_3` or `grandchild_spawn` tests.\n- **Descendant authorization untested.** Agent tools restrict to descendants but only at depth 1. No test verifies that a depth-2 child cannot access depth-1 siblings' results.\n- **Recovery at depth > 1 untested.** `test_thread_recovery.py` covers single-level stalls only.\n\n### 2. Cost and Usage Budgets\n\n**What exists:**\n- `usage_log` table (`db.py:1121-1142`) tracks per-session `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `cost_cents`.\n- `get_thread_limits()` returns current usage counts.\n\n**Gaps — fully missing:**\n- **No cross-session aggregation.** `get_thread_limits()` returns only the current session's usage, not aggregated descendant totals. Spec requires summing across all descendant session IDs.\n- **No policy model.** No table for `max_cost_cents`, `max_input_tokens`, `max_output_tokens`, `max_wall_clock_duration`.\n- **No enforcement.** Spawn and wait do not check budget limits before proceeding.\n- **No wall-clock tracking.** No `started_at` aggregation or duration check.\n- **No deterministic fallback.** Spec says \"enforce deterministic thread and concurrency limits when provider usage data unavailable.\" Not implemented.\n\n### 3. Child Steering (thread_inbox_messages)\n\n**Status: Fully unimplemented.**\n- No `thread_inbox_messages` tool registered in `sidecar/src/orchestration_tools.js` (only 6 tools: spawn, list, get, wait, cancel, report).\n- No inbox database table.\n- No message queue service.\n- No attention indicators in tree nodes.\n- No reopening of completed children.\n- No result supersession/versioning.\n- No idempotent message submission.\n\n### What Blocks Phase 7 (Phase 6 dependencies)\n\nPhase 6 (managed integration) provides `thread_integration.py` which is already present. Phase 7 depends on Phase 6's clean integration path being stable. The integration table and cherry-pick workflow exist in `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py`.\n\n---","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789266498994,"runId":"866834bc","agent":"scout","index":0,"message":"scout is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":11,"tokens":70103,"toolCount":29,"elapsedMs":240603},{"type":"needs_attention","from":"active_long_running","to":"needs_attention","ts":1789266554154,"runId":"866834bc","agent":"scout","index":0,"message":"scout needs attention (no observed activity for 60s)","reason":"idle","turns":11,"tokens":70103,"toolCount":29,"elapsedMs":60540}],"attemptedModels":["local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":70989,"output":5682,"cacheRead":632503,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":16}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/866834bc/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Concrete findings with file paths: config.py:216 (thread_max_depth=1 blocks nested), threads.py (no DELETE routes), orchestration_tools.js (no thread_inbox tool), thread_queries.py:48 (allows_spawn depth check), db.py:1121 (usage_log exists but no aggregation)"}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"grep thread_max_depth config.py","result":"passed","summary":"Found thread_max_depth: int = 1 at config.py:216"},{"command":"grep -rn thread_inbox backend/sidecar","result":"passed","summary":"No thread_inbox or steering implementation found in backend or sidecar source"},{"command":"grep -rn recursive.*delete backend/tests","result":"passed","summary":"No recursive deletion tests found"},{"command":"grep -rn depth.*3 backend/tests","result":"passed","summary":"No depth-3 spawn tests found; only depth-1 limit tests exist"}],"validationOutput":["Phase 7 three sub-features: nested delegation (depth 3), cost budgets, child steering. Only nested infrastructure partially exists (tree queries work at depth 2-3 but spawn blocked by max_depth=1). Cost budgets and steering fully missing.","No DELETE endpoints in threads.py API. No inbox table or tool. No budget policy model. No cross-session aggregation."],"residualRisks":["nested: setting thread_max_depth=3 enables depth>1 spawns without tests. Race conditions on ancestor authorization at depth 2+ untested.","nested: recursive deletion not implemented. Phase 7 exit criteria require it.","budgets: usage_log captures per-session data but no enforcement mechanism. Spawning can exceed any budget.","steering: completely absent. Requires new DB table, tool registration, message queue, and UI attention indicators.","phase6: integration service exists but Phase 7 depends on it being stable before nesting on top of integrated children"],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No changes made. Read-only audit only.","reviewFindings":["gap: threads.py has zero DELETE endpoints; spec requires DELETE and DELETE recursive","gap: config.py:216 sets thread_max_depth=1; nested delegation requires 3","gap: no cost/budget policy model or enforcement; usage_log is per-session only","gap: no thread_inbox_messages tool or inbox table for child steering","gap: no tests at depth > 1 for cascade cancel, recursive deletion, or descendant auth"],"manualNotes":"Phase 5 (agent delegation) is fully implemented with all 6 Pi tools. Phase 6 (integration) is implemented. Phase 7 has the most gaps: nested depth needs tests and DELETE routes, budgets need a policy model and enforcement, steering is a greenfield feature requiring new tables and tools. The existing tree query infrastructure handles depth 2-3 correctly for reads, and cascade cancellation traverses depth 32, so the read/cancel path at depth>1 is mostly there. The main blockers are: DELETE endpoints, budget enforcement, inbox steering, and comprehensive depth>1 tests."}},"toolCalls":[{"text":"read ~/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md","expandedText":"read ~/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md"},{"text":"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -type f \\( -name \"*.go\" -o ...","expandedText":"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -type f \\( -name \"*.go\" -o -name \"*.md\" -o -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.json\" \\) | head -100"},{"text":"read ~/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md","expandedText":"read ~/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md"},{"text":"$ ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/ ...","expandedText":"$ ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/api/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/ 2>/dev/null | head -40"},{"text":"$ ls /Users/user/projec