{"type":"message","id":"9a10f3d5","parentId":"8802ab71","timestamp":"2026-09-13T03:00:38.085Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Q328csUJ0s0EFrEeoeL4neSh|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa60edcd63087d086ba5723d2912c49","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"delete_review\",\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"runId\": \"da83dbf6\",\n    \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 18 assistant turns (soft limit 18, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Confirmed finding\\n\\n### Blocker: Tenant recovery is not enforced before workspace operations\\n\\n**Locations**\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/repos.py::_delete_repo_locked`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py:190-276`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py::claim_workspace_deletion`\\n- Relevant caller: `backend/src/yinshi/main.py:410-415`\\n\\nRepository deletion invokes recovery through the repository delete path. Startup invokes recovery only with `tenant=None`.\\n\\nTenant workspace deletion does not first recover or reject a pending `repository_deletions` receipt. Repository lifecycle locking only prevents concurrent execution. It does not resolve durable state left by an earlier process.\\n\\n**Impact**\\n\\nA tenant process can crash after moving managed paths but before deleting repository rows. After restart, workspace deletion can claim the still-present workspace.\\n\\nThis creates competing durable deletion claims against partially quarantined storage. It can also turn recoverable state into a permanent source-target conflict.\\n\\nMalformed tenant receipts also fail closed only when repository deletion is retried. Other workspace operations can proceed before that retry.\\n\\n**Proposed correction**\\n\\nCreate one repository admission boundary that owns recovery and pending-receipt checks.\\n\\nEvery workspace claim, execution, repair, creation, or deletion must pass this boundary while holding the repository lifecycle lock.\\n\\nAt minimum, `claim_workspace_deletion` must reject any active repository deletion receipt inside its `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction.\\n\\nDo not duplicate receipt interpretation across APIs. Pull this policy into the repository lifecycle or recovery service.\\n\\n**Remediation plan**\\n\\nUse `worker-advanced`. Fix spans persistence, cross-process serialization, crash recovery, and authority transitions.\\n\\n**Required validation**\\n\\n1. Crash after one managed path enters quarantine.\\n2. Restart with tenant repository and workspace rows still present.\\n3. Attempt workspace deletion, execution, creation, and repair.\\n4. Confirm each operation blocks without filesystem or runtime effects.\\n5. Recover the receipt, then confirm normal workspace operations resume.\\n6. Race workspace deletion against repository recovery across processes.\\n7. Insert a malformed tenant receipt and confirm every affected admission fails closed.\\n8. Repeat focused repository and workspace deletion suites.\\n\\n## Confirmed behavior\\n\\n- Imported repositories require explicit imported ownership.\\n- Managed deletion requires managed ownership plus canonical managed path.\\n- Imported repositories with workspaces retain Git storage.\\n- Managed paths use durable quarantine receipts.\\n- Current recovery reconciles uncertain commits from fresh database state.\\n- Receipt cleanup remains retry-owned until authoritative restore or discard completes.\\n\\n## Review limits\\n\\nCombined diff output exceeded tool output limits. Complete current scoped blobs were read, but some tracked baseline hunks were unavailable.\\n\\nNo test command was repeated before the tool budget ended. Current behavior lacks independent runtime validation from this review.\\n\\nPotential callers of `services.workspace.delete_workspace` were not exhaustively inventoried. That path needs a final caller search before approval.\\n\\nRemediation remains required.\",\n    \"artifactPaths\": [\n      \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/da83dbf6/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n    ],\n    \"results\": [\n      {\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n        \"task\": \"Original request: finish Phase 6 managed integration before Phase 7. Current checkout has a heavily dirty inherited Phase 6 candidate plus committed broker foundations. Review only; do not modify files. Read the actual current diff and relevant callers/tests. First read /Users/user/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md and its referenced red-flags file, and apply that guidance. Every finding must include location or affected requirement, impact, proposed correction, and validation. If no findings remain, state that no remediation is needed. Scope: repository deletion and recovery only: backend/src/yinshi/api/repos.py, repository_lifecycle.py, services/repository_lifecycle.py, repository_deletion_recovery.py, workspace_deletion.py, related workspace deletion APIs and tests. Check imported versus managed ownership, quarantine ancestry, durable receipts, crash recovery, and fail-closed malformed state.\",\n        \"routingContract\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n          \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n          \"thinking\": \"max\",\n          \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n        },\n        \"launchContractDigest\": \"dbd58c1ec55f088c233eb296d347b5d55df41526837b4ae7f1eab4abeb2b37af\",\n        \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n          \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n          \"runtime\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n          ],\n          \"configured\": [],\n          \"e