/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/861fc52a_final-review_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/861fc52a_final-review_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/861fc52a_final-review_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/861fc52a_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/861fc52a_final-review_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/861fc52a_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","skills":["software-design"],"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":18,"graceTurns":3,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":15},"toolBudget":{"hard":80,"soft":55,"block":["bash","read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":58,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":55},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":58,"tokens":261170,"durationMs":340141},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":true}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"## Confirmed findings\n\n### Blocker: Phase 6 has no production-capable execution path\n\n**Locations:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py:52-63`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:68-75`\n- `docs/workspace-isolation.md:120-122`\n- Affected requirement: authenticated desktop-to-broker ingestion and managed integration before Phase 7.\n\nEvery production isolation profile returns `supported=False`. Managed integration therefore rejects even when its feature flag is enabled. Current docs explicitly state that Phase 6 remains incomplete. Broker lifecycle foundations also lack the required production desktop upload and dispatch path.\n\n**Impact:** No production environment can run managed integration. Phase 6 cannot satisfy its observable contract. Phase 7 remains blocked.\n\n**Correction:** Implement approved production wiring without adding an isolation bypass. Wire authenticated upload, broker dispatch, lifecycle recovery, Linux qualification, and desktop response verification.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-expert`. This correction spans authentication, durable lifecycle ownership, transport, privileged effects, and deployment qualification.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Run end-to-end integration inside the qualified Linux VM.\n- Verify signed request and response handling.\n- Restart after each lifecycle stage and confirm exact recovery.\n- Reject revoked keys, altered artifacts, replay mismatches, and native Darwin execution.\n- Verify root gates remain independently disabled by default.\n\n### High: successful integration invalidates its own idempotency identity\n\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py`, `_same_operation()` around lines 282-301, called by `integrate()` and `status()`.\n\nOperation creation stores the original `expected_parent_head`. Successful application advances parent `HEAD`. Later requests recompute current `parent_head`, then `_same_operation()` requires it to equal the stored original head.\n\n**Impact:** Same-key replay and status lookup can reject a successfully integrated operation as an identity mismatch. This breaks idempotency and durable result discovery.\n\n**Correction:** Compare stored expected head with the replay request value, not current checkout head. Validate current head separately using stage-specific durable facts such as `resulting_parent_head`.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. The fix interacts with Git state, durable replay, authorization, and recovery classification.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Replay the original request after integration. Confirm the same operation returns without another commit.\n- Fetch operation status after integration. Confirm HTTP 200.\n- Reuse the key with changed request facts. Confirm HTTP 409.\n- Change parent `HEAD` unexpectedly. Confirm a blocked recovery result rather than false success.\n- Run `test_thread_integration.py` and `test_thread_integration_discovery.py`.\n\n### Low: migration documentation reports obsolete schema versions\n\n**Locations:**  \n- `docs/thread-orchestration.md`, migration section\n- `backend/src/yinshi/db.py:24`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/tenant.py:52`\n- `backend/tests/test_tenant.py:1682`\n\nDocumentation reports shared schema version 10 and tenant version 7. Current constants are 11 and 9. One test comment also calls version 8 current while setting version 9.\n\n**Impact:** Operators and maintainers receive incorrect upgrade and rollback guidance.\n\n**Correction:** Update documented versions and stale comments. Prefer referencing named migrations where fixed numbers add no value.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-simple`.\n\n**Validation:** Compare documentation with `_SCHEMA_VERSION` and `_USER_SCHEMA_VERSION`. Run schema migration and ownership contract tests.\n\n## Review limits and residual risks\n\nNo test suite was repeated after tool-budget exhaustion. Earlier reported focused results apply to earlier review points, not attested final-candidate validation.\n\nCommitted broker lifecycle internals were not fully re-reviewed in this pass. Production Linux deployment and external lifecycle effects remain unvalidated.\n\nNo files were edited, staged, committed, or pushed. Findings remain unresolved, so completion is blocked.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789267931143,"runId":"861fc52a","agent":"final-review","index":0,"message":"final-review is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":14,"tokens":179561,"toolCount":58,"elapsedMs":240007}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":247610,"output":13560,"cacheRead":570112,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.929906,"turns":15}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7