c/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/api/repos.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/api/repos.py"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents/artifacts/outputs...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents/artifacts/outputs/d856fe34/.pi-subagents/artifacts/remaining-phase6-plan.md\",\"pattern\":\"repository deletion|Repository deletion|delete_re..."},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents/artifacts\",\"patte...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents/artifacts\",\"pattern\":\"durable repository deletion|repository deletion recovery|storage_ownership|Delete imported repository\",\"glob\":\"*_ou..."},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/62d8cd96_final-review_0_input.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/62d8cd96_final-review_0_input.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/62d8cd96_final-review_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/62d8cd96_final-review_0_output.md"},{"text":"$ find .pi-subagents/artifacts -name '*final-review*_output.md...","expandedText":"$ find .pi-subagents/artifacts -name '*final-review*_output.md' -maxdepth 1 -print0 | xargs -0 stat -f '%m %N' | sort -nr | head -15"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents/artifacts\",\"patte...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents/artifacts\",\"pattern\":\"repository deletion|quarantine ancestry|managed integration before Phase 7\",\"glob\":\"*final-review*_input.md\",\"ignor..."},{"text":"$ for n in 861fc52a 57965bef d04076ad 14e2aa4e 948be4db f72826...","expandedText":"$ for n in 861fc52a 57965bef d04076ad 14e2aa4e 948be4db f72826e6 35eebbc0 2ce57bd5 9819bae4 f802465a 188892e8 234b5f85 a45c676d; do for f in .pi-subagents/artifacts/${n}_final-review_0_{input,output}.md; do [ -f \"$f\" ] && stat -f '%m %Sm %N' ..."},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/f802465a_final-review_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/f802465a_final-review_0_output.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/188892e8_final-review_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/188892e8_final-review_0_output.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/234b5f85_final-review_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/234b5f85_final-review_0_output.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/35eebbc0_final-review_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/35eebbc0_final-review_0_output.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/f72826e6_final-review_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/f72826e6_final-review_0_output.md"},{"text":"$ find .pi-subagents/artifacts -maxdepth 1 \\( -name '*worker*_...","expandedText":"$ find .pi-subagents/artifacts -maxdepth 1 \\( -name '*worker*_output.md' -o -name '*final-review*_output.md' \\) -print0 | xargs -0 grep -ilE 'restore cleanup creates|remove_empty_quarantine|receipt deletion|repository deletion' | while read f..."}]}]},{"key":"integration_review","ok":true,"runId":"57965bef","output":"# Review verdict\n\nChanges required. Four unresolved findings block Phase 6 completion.\n\nSoftware-design guidance exposed one core problem: durable workflow states do not fully encapsulate Git effect ownership and recovery.\n\n## Confirmed findings\n\n### 1. High: Parent revalidation failures leave integration permanently active\n\n**Location:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:988-1000`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:493-632`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:728-788`\n\nA changed parent `HEAD` or newly dirty parent raises generic `GitError` before merge. `_execute()` retains `applying` state and admission marker.\n\n`status()` only reports a synthetic blocked response. `abort()` repeats the same validation and refuses cleanup.\n\n**Impact:** Users must restore the old parent state before aborting. New prompts and integrations remain blocked despite no managed application occurring.\n\n**Correction:** Add a durable pre-apply state distinct from uncertain `applying`. Safely fail and clean trials when pre-apply revalidation rejects the parent.\n\nOnly mark `applying` when a parent effect may have started. Recovery must distinguish prepared, applied, and ambiguous outcomes.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. This fix changes interacting persistence, Git effect, and recovery guarantees.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Change parent `HEAD` after trial creation.\n- Dirty the parent after trial creation.\n- Confirm both cases return HTTP 409 without changing parent bytes.\n- Confirm operation becomes terminal and admission marker disappears.\n- Inject interruption after apply intent and verify uncertain outcomes remain blocked.\n\n### 2. High: Cancellation after a committed terminal transition can strand admission\n\n**Location:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/deps.py:102-122`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:238-280`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:282-308`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:769-788`\n\nDatabase helpers drain a shielded write, then propagate cancellation. A terminal transition can therefore commit before `_execute()` sets `terminal = True`.\n\nThe `finally` block closes liveness but retains the durable marker. Same-key replay returns the terminal outcome without reconciling that marker.\n\n**Impact:** A successful, failed, or conflicted request can block its workspace after client cancellation or marker-release failure.\n\n**Correction:** Reconcile exact-owner admission on every terminal replay. Terminal transition cancellation also needs an authoritative, cancellation-safe state read before lease disposition.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. Cancellation and cross-resource ownership guarantees interact.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Cancel immediately after each terminal database commit.\n- Verify terminal database state has no stale marker.\n- Repeat the same idempotency key and verify marker reconciliation.\n- Inject marker-release failure and verify later replay safely repairs it.\n- Confirm no second parent commit appears.\n\n### 3. High: Recovery creates new trials instead of reconciling recorded trials\n\n**Location:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:680-719`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:761-945`\n\nEvery retry in `checking` appends a new trial intent. It does not reconcile an existing recorded worktree or ref.\n\nCancellation after cherry-pick or ref publication can leave an unrecorded candidate. A retry creates another candidate. Conflict completion also leaves its dirty trial registered permanently.\n\n**Impact:** One operation can accumulate hidden worktrees and refs, exhaust its eight-attempt limit, and obstruct later repository lifecycle work.\n\n**Correction:** Reconcile the latest recorded intent before allocating another. Reuse a verified candidate, clean known system-created conflicts, or persist `blocked` when ownership is uncertain.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. Fix requires deterministic restart classification and exact-owner cleanup.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Interrupt after worktree creation.\n- Interrupt after cherry-pick.\n- Interrupt after ref publication.\n- Verify retry reuses or safely cleans the recorded trial.\n- Verify conflict leaves no trial worktree, ref, or registration.\n- Verify user-modified trial content remains retained and blocked.\n\n### 4. Medium: Browser test does not exercise production integration UI\n\n**Location:** `frontend/e2e/thread-integration.spec.ts:1-238`\n\nFile identifies itself as fixture-only. It reproduces markup instead of mounting `ThreadIntegration.tsx` through production wiring.\n\n**Impact:** Real transport routing, state recovery, confirmation binding, and focus regressions can pass this test.\n\n**Correction:** Render production component with mocked `RuntimeTransport`, or run the real application with mocked external boundaries.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker`.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Run component tests against `ThreadIntegration.tsx`.\n- Run Playwright at configured mobile and desktop widths.\n- Cover confirmation, exact result binding, cancellation recovery, conflict paths, focus restoration, and runtime selection.\n\n## Unanswered questions\n\nNone.\n\n## Review limits\n\nTool budget prevented full line review of these changed regions:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/stream.py`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/sidecar.py`\n- `sidecar/src/sidecar.js`\n- Frontend API, panel, session, and runtime transport patches\n\nNo focused test suite ran against this final working candidate. Earlier artifact results were not treated as final-candidate evidence.\n\nRemediation is required.","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/57965bef/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"final-review","task":"Original request: finish Phase 6 managed integration before Phase 7. Current checkout has a heavily dirty inherited Phase 6 candidate plus committed broker foundations. Review only; do not modify files. Read the actual current diff and relevant callers/tests. First read /Users/user/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md and its referenced red-flags file, and apply that guidance. Every finding must include location or affected requirement, impact, proposed correction, and validation. If no findings remain, state that no remediation is needed. Scope: managed integration feature and UI only: thread_integration.py, thread_workspaces.py integration paths, API/sidecar/frontend integration files and focused tests. Check exact source/result commit binding, deterministic cherry-pick and conflict handling, cancellation, recovery, database boundaries, and no hidden native execution requirement.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"final-review","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"f5d04bb0001611028abf3aa5f929584827ece18357aaef30294a5351fc34544f","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":155211,"output":18404,"cacheRead":440064,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.548207,"turns":13},"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","thinking":"max","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/57965bef_final-review_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/57965bef_final-review_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/57965bef_final-review_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/57965bef_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/57965bef_final-review_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/57965bef_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","skills":["software-design"],"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":18,"graceTurns":3,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":13},"toolBudget":{"hard":80,"soft":55,"block":["bash","read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":56,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":55},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":56,"tokens":173615,"durationMs":574179},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":false}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"# Review verdict\n\nChanges required. Four unresolved findings block Phase 6 completion.\n\nSoftware-design guidance exposed one core problem: durable workflow states do not fully encapsulate Git effect ownership and recovery.\n\n## Confirmed findings\n\n### 1. High: Parent revalidation failures leave integration permanently active\n\n**Location:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:988-1000`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:493-632`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:728-788`\n\nA changed parent `HEAD` or newly dirty parent raises generic `GitError` before merge. `_execute()` retains `applying` state and admission marker.\n\n`status()` only reports a synthetic blocked response. `abort()` repeats the same validation and refuses cleanup.\n\n**Impact:** Users must restore the old parent state before aborting. New prompts and integrations remain blocked despite no managed application occurring.\n\n**Correction:** Add a durable pre-apply state distinct from uncertain `applying`. Safely fail and clean trials when pre-apply revalidation rejects the parent.\n\nOnly mark `applying` when a parent effect may have started. Recovery must distinguish prepared, applied, and ambiguous outcomes.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. This fix changes interacting persistence, Git effect, and recovery guarantees.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Change parent `HEAD` after trial creation.\n- Dirty the parent after trial creation.\n- Confirm both cases return HTTP 409 without changing parent bytes.\n- Confirm operation becomes terminal and admission marker disappears.\n- Inject interruption after apply intent and verify uncertain outcomes remain blocked.\n\n### 2. High: Cancellation after a committed terminal transition can strand admission\n\n**Location:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/deps.py:102-122`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:238-280`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:282-308`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:769-788`\n\nDatabase helpers drain a shielded write, then propagate cancellation. A terminal transition can therefore commit before `_execute()` sets `terminal = True`.\n\nThe `finally` block closes liveness but retains the durable marker. Same-key replay returns the terminal outcome without reconciling that marker.\n\n**Impact:** A successful, failed, or conflicted request can block its workspace after client cancellation or marker-release failure.\n\n**Correction:** Reconcile exact-owner admission on every terminal replay. Terminal transition cancellation also needs an authoritative, cancellation-safe state read before lease disposition.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. Cancellation and cross-resource ownership guarantees interact.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Cancel immediately after each terminal database commit.\n- Verify terminal database state has no stale marker.\n- Repeat the same idempotency key and verify marker reconciliation.\n- Inject marker-release failure and verify later replay safely repairs it.\n- Confirm no second parent commit appears.\n\n### 3. High: Recovery creates new trials instead of reconciling recorded trials\n\n**Location:**  \n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:680-719`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:761-945`\n\nEvery retry in `checking` appends a new trial intent. It does not reconcile an existing recorded worktree or ref.\n\nCancellation after cherry-pick or ref publication can leave an unrecorded candidate. A retry creates another candidate. Conflict completion also leaves its dirty trial registered permanently.\n\n**Impact:** One operation can accumulate hidden worktrees and refs, exhaust its eight-attempt limit, and obstruct later repository lifecycle work.\n\n**Correction:** Reconcile the latest recorded intent before allocating another. Reuse a verified candidate, clean known system-created conflicts, or persist `blocked` when ownership is uncertain.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`. Fix requires deterministic restart classification and exact-owner cleanup.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Interrupt after worktree creation.\n- Interrupt after cherry-pick.\n- Interrupt after ref publication.\n- Verify retry reuses or safely cleans the recorded trial.\n- Verify conflict leaves no trial worktree, ref, or registration.\n- Verify user-modified trial content remains retained and blocked.\n\n### 4. Medium: Browser test does not exercise production integration UI\n\n**Location:** `frontend/e2e/thread-integration.spec.ts:1-238`\n\nFile identifies itself as fixture-only. It reproduces markup instead of mounting `ThreadIntegration.tsx` through production wiring.\n\n**Impact:** Real transport routing, state recovery, confirmation binding, and focus regressions can pass this test.\n\n**Correction:** Render production component with mocked `RuntimeTransport`, or run the real application with mocked external boundaries.\n\n**Remediation:** `worker`.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Run component tests against `ThreadIntegration.tsx`.\n- Run Playwright at configured mobile and desktop widths.\n- Cover confirmation, exact result binding, cancellation recovery, conflict paths, focus restoration, and runtime selection.\n\n## Unanswered questions\n\nNone.\n\n## Review limits\n\nTool budget prevented full line review of these changed regions:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/stream.py`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/sidecar.py`\n- `sidecar/src/sidecar.js`\n- Frontend API, panel, session, and runtime transport patches\n\nNo focused test suite ran against this final working candidate. Earlier artifact results were not treated as final-candidate evidence.\n\nRemediation is required.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789267931662,"runId":"57965bef","agent":"final-review","index":0,"message":"final-review is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":12,"tokens":149867,"toolCount":56,"elapsedMs":240673}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":155211,"output":18404,"cacheRead":440064,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":1.548207,"turns":13}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yin