"29cd6dd8-5fe0-4ef0-9c4d-bbd551d899fc","missionPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/missions/29cd6dd8-5fe0-4ef0-9c4d-bbd551d899fc.json","mission":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"29cd6dd8-5fe0-4ef0-9c4d-bbd551d899fc","title":"Implement one narrow repository-deletion admission backstop in the current shared checkout. Do no...","objective":"Implement one narrow repository-deletion admission backstop in the current shared checkout. Do not inspect or alter TDD Guard configuration. Add a small helper in backend/src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py that, inside an already active SQLite transaction/read, rejects any repository_deletions row for the repo ID with a typed error. Call it before new workspace deletion claims, workspace execution reservation, workspace checkout repair/publication claim, workspace creation, and managed thread integration/trial admission. Do not call it from repository deletion recovery itself. Existing exact-owner continuations unrelated to repository deletion remain unchanged. Map the typed error at API/service boundaries to existing stable conflict responses rather than leaking repository state. Add focused tests: an active or malformed durable repository deletion row blocks workspace deletion, execution, creation, repair, and integration before filesystem/runtime/Git effects; after recovery removes the row, normal admission resumes. Preserve no SQLite handle across await/external effect and repository lifecycle lock ordering. Run focused tests, Ruff, and strict mypy for changed source. Do not commit. If a write is denied, return exact edit packets.","status":"waiting","createdAt":"2026-09-13T04:10:35.893Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-13T04:26:08.692Z","runs":[{"runId":"call_pAxkKTGP6tvKEeDyF0A6CiIG|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62234412087d087cc56e8043d63a4","mode":"workflow","agent":"worker-advanced","status":"paused","startedAt":"2026-09-13T04:26:08.691Z","completedAt":"2026-09-13T04:26:08.691Z","usage":{"tokens":147681}}],"decisions":[],"arti