{"type":"message","id":"ad05609f","parentId":"7aeafcd1","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:30:36.558Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_qsJFyo1KjpsREVj50zXMMLVb|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa626eb3ee087d0bc9b88d57ce3d4df","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 18 assistant turns (soft limit 18, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nUnderstood — option (b). No files in the shared checkout were modified (verified: only read-only operations occurred; all three write attempts were denied before any change landed, and nothing is staged). Below is the complete deliverable: mapped design, exact edit packets, expected red/green behavior, and validation commands.\n\n## Design summary\n\n**Helper** (`repository_lifecycle.py`): `require_no_repository_deletion(db, repo_id)` runs one parameterized existence read `SELECT 1 FROM repository_deletions WHERE repo_id = ? LIMIT 1` inside the caller's already-active transaction/read (it opens no transaction and keeps no handle across await) and raises the typed `RepositoryDeletionPendingError` (a `RuntimeError`) on **any** row — active or malformed phase. No lock acquisition, no lock-order change, no recovery-path use.\n\n**Call sites and boundary mappings** (existing stable conflict responses, no repository-state leak):\n\n| # | Admission point (file/function) | Placement | Mapped response |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | New workspace deletion claim — `workspace_deletion.py` `claim()` | On the new-claim branch (after adoption/`receipt is not None` branch, after the `repair_unresolved` check, before `prune_completed_execution_receipts` and the `state='deleting'` UPDATE) | `WorkspaceDeletionConflict(\"deletion_claim_unavailable\", \"Workspace deletion claim is unavailable\")` → 409 JSON |\n| 2 | Execution reservation — `workspace_execution.py` `ExecutionAdmission.reserve()` | After `self.authorize(db)`, before the duplicate-receipt query/INSERT | `WorkspaceAdmissionError()` → existing boundaries: `stream.py` 409 \"Workspace is busy\", `prompt_journal.py` `PromptRunConflictError(\"Workspace is busy\")` |\n| 3 | Checkout repair/publication claim — `workspace_publication.py` `_begin_repair_locked()` | After the exact-owner resume branch (unchanged), before the `return None` fast path and the `workspace_checkout_repairs` INSERT | `WorkspacePublicationError(\"Checkout repair conflicts with repository deletion\")` (parallel to existing \"…conflicts with workspace deletion\") → 409 at stream/terminal boundaries |\n| 4 | Workspace creation — `workspace.py` `_create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked()` | First statement, before `ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant`/`_fetch_repo`/Git | Typed error propagates; mapped at `api/workspaces.py::create_workspace` → `HTTPException(409, \"Repository deletion is pending; admission can be retried\")` |\n| 5 | Managed thread integration admission — `thread_integration.py` `integrate()` inner `reserve(db)` | After the `duplicate` check, before the `thread_integrations` INSERT, inside `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` | `HTTPException(409, \"Integration precondition changed\")` (existing stable detail) |\n\nDeliberate exclusions per packet: exact-owner continuations untouched (claim adoption, `_begin_repair_locked` resume branch, `_execute` resume, status/abort); `repository_deletion_recovery.py` never calls the helper; delegated-child workspace attach paths untouched.\n\n---\n\n## Edit packet 1 — `backend/src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py`\n\nInsert the typed error and helper immediately before `class ManagedPathQuarantine:`:\n\n**oldText**\n```\nclass ManagedPathQuarantine:\n```\n**newText**\n```\nclass RepositoryDeletionPendingError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"A durable repository deletion receipt still owns this repository.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\"Repository deletion is pending\")\n\n\ndef require_no_repository_deletion(database: sqlite3.Connection, repo_id: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reject admission while any durable repository deletion receipt exists.\n\n    Must run inside the caller's already active SQLite transaction or read so\n    the admission verdict shares one snapshot with its durable writes. Any\n    receipt row for the repository — including a malformed one — keeps the\n    repository owned by repository deletion recovery until recovery removes it.\n    \"\"\"\n    row = database.execute(\n        \"SELECT 1 FROM repository_deletions WHERE repo_id = ? LIMIT 1\",\n        (repo_id,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if row is not None:\n        raise RepositoryDeletionPendingError()\n\n\nclass ManagedPathQuarantine:\n```\n\n## Edit packet 2 — `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py`\n\n**2a. Import** — **oldText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    repository_lifecycle,\n    repository_lifecycle_root,\n)\n```\n**newText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    repository_lifecycle,\n    repository_lifecycle_root,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\n```\n\n**2b. Gate in `claim()`** — **oldText**\n```\n            if repair is not None:\n                raise WorkspaceDeletionConflict(\n                    \"repair_unresolved\",\n                    \"Workspace repair publication is not durably bound\",\n                )\n            prune_completed_execution_receipts(db, str(workspace[\"repo_id\"]))\n```\n**newText**\n```\n            if repair is not None:\n                raise WorkspaceDeletionConflict(\n                    \"repair_unresolved\",\n                    \"Workspace repair publication is not durably bound\",\n                )\n            try:\n                require_no_repository_deletion(db, str(workspace[\"repo_id\"]))\n            except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as exc:\n                raise WorkspaceDeletionConflict(\n                    \"deletion_claim_unavailable\",\n                    \"Workspace deletion claim is unavailable\",\n                ) from exc\n            prune_completed_execution_receipts(db, str(workspace[\"repo_id\"]))\n```\n\n## Edit packet 3 — `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py`\n\n**3a. Import** — **oldText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.sidecar import SidecarClient\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_git_ownership import ThreadGitOwnershipError\n```\n**newText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.sidecar import SidecarClient\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_git_ownership import ThreadGitOwnershipError\n```\n\n**3b. Gate in `reserve()`** — **oldText**\n```\n    async def reserve(self) -> None:\n        def record(db: sqlite3.Connection) -> None:\n            db.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n            try:\n                self.authorize(db)\n                if (\n```\n**newText**\n```\n    async def reserve(self) -> None:\n        def record(db: sqlite3.Connection) -> None:\n            db.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n            try:\n                self.authorize(db)\n                try:\n                    require_no_repository_deletion(db, self.workspace.repo_id)\n                except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as exc:\n                    raise WorkspaceAdmissionError() from exc\n                if (\n```\n\n## Edit packet 4 — `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`\n\n**4a. Import** — **oldText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_admission import (\n    WorkspaceAdmissionLease,\n    acquire_workspace_admission,\n    read_workspace_identity,\n    resume_workspace_admission_marker,\n)\n```\n**newText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_admission import (\n    WorkspaceAdmissionLease,\n    acquire_workspace_admission,\n    read_workspace_identity,\n    resume_workspace_admission_marker,\n)\n```\n\n**4b. Gate in `_begin_repair_locked`** (after the exact-owner resume `return`, before the fast path/INSERT) — **oldText**\n```\n        if not exact:\n            raise WorkspacePublicationError(\"Checkout repair has unresolved durable ownership\")\n        return str(row[0]), str(row[1]), str(row[2])\n    if current.repo_path == final_repo_path and not requires_publication:\n        return None\n```\n**newText**\n```\n        if not exact:\n            raise WorkspacePublicationError(\"Checkout repair has unresolved durable ownership\")\n        return str(row[0]), str(row[1]), str(row[2])\n    try:\n        require_no_repository_deletion(database, expected.repo_id)\n    except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as exc:\n        raise WorkspacePublicationError(\n            \"Checkout repair conflicts with repository deletion\"\n        ) from exc\n    if current.repo_path == final_repo_path and not requires_publication:\n        return None\n```\n\n## Edit packet 5 — `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py`\n\nFunction-level import (pattern already used in `api/stream.py`) to avoid touching the unverified top-of-file import block — **oldText**\n```\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree after repository lifecycle serialization.\"\"\"\n    if tenant is not None:\n```\n**newText**\n```\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree after repository lifecycle serialization.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import require_no_repository_deletion\n\n    require_no_repository_deletion(db, repo_id)\n    if tenant is not None:\n```\n\n## Edit packet 6 — `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py`\n\n**6a. Boundary import in `create_workspace`** — **oldText**\n```\n    email = get_user_email(request)\n    username = email.split(\"@\")[0] if email else None\n    tenant = get_tenant(request)\n```\n**newText**\n```\n    email = get_user_email(request)\n    username = email.split(\"@\")[0] if email else None\n    tenant = get_tenant(request)\n    from yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import RepositoryDeletionPendingError\n```\n\n**6b. Mapping** — **oldText**\n```\n        except RepoNotFoundError:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Repo not found\")\n        except GitError as exc:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=str(exc))\n```\n**newText**\n```\n        except RepoNotFoundError:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Repo not found\")\n        except RepositoryDeletionPendingError:\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=409,\n                detail=\"Repository deletion is pending; admission can be retried\",\n            )\n        except GitError as exc:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=str(exc))\n```\n\n## Edit packet 7 — `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py`\n\n**7a. Import** — **oldText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_git_ownership import (\n    ThreadGitOwnershipError,\n    ThreadGitWorktree,\n)\n```\n**newText**\n```\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_git_ownership import (\n    ThreadGitOwnershipError,\n    ThreadGitWorktree,\n)\n```\n\n**7b. Gate in `integrate()`'s `reserve(db)`** — **oldText**\n```\n                    duplicate = existing(db)\n                    if duplicate is not None:\n                        db.rollback()\n                        return duplicate\n                    db.execute(\n```\n**newText**\n```\n                    duplicate = existing(db)\n                    if duplicate is not None:\n                        db.rollback()\n                        return duplicate\n                    try:\n                        require_no_repository_deletion(db, current.context.repo_id)\n                    except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as error:\n                        raise HTTPException(\n                            status_code=409, detail=\"Integration precondition changed\"\n                        ) from error\n                    db.execute(\n```\n(The enclosing `except BaseException: db.rollback(); raise` in `reserve` rolls the transaction back cleanly before the HTTPException propagates.)\n\n## Edit packet 8 — new test file `backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py` (complete content)\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Repository-deletion admission backstop keeps receipts exclusive.\n\nAny durable repository_deletions row for a repository — active or malformed —\nmust block new workspace deletion claims, execution reservations, checkout\nrepair/publication claims, workspace creation, and managed thread integration\nadmission before filesystem, runtime, or Git effects. Removing the row (as\nrepository deletion recovery does) resumes normal admission.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n\nimport pytest\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\n\nfrom tests.test_thread_integration import head_commit, seed_parent_stack\nfrom tests.test_thread_workspaces import run_git as worktree_git\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace import WorkspaceCheckoutState, create_workspace_for_repo\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_deletion import (\n    WorkspaceDeletionConflict,\n    claim_workspace_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_execution import ExecutionAdmission, prompt_workspace\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_publication import (\n    WorkspacePublicationError,\n    _begin_repair,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_admission import WorkspaceAdmissionError\nfrom yinshi.tenant import TenantContext\n\nREPO_ID = \"backstop-repo\"\nWORKSPACE_ID = \"backstop-ws\"\nSESSION_ID = \"backstop-session\"\nBRANCH = \"wk/backstop\"\n\n\ndef _request() -> Request:\n    \"\"\"Build one minimal legacy request like the deletion tests.\"\"\"\n    app = SimpleNamespace(state=SimpleNamespace(mode=\"hosted\"))\n    return Request(\n        {\n            \"type\": \"http\",\n            \"http_version\": \"1.1\",\n            \"method\": \"POST\",\n            \"scheme\": \"http\",\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"raw_path\": b\"/\",\n            \"query_string\": b\"\",\n            \"headers\": [],\n            \"client\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 1),\n            \"server\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 80),\n            \"app\": app,\n            \"state\": {},\n        }\n    )\n\n\ndef _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Create one repo, one linked user worktree workspace, and one session.\"\"\"\n    worktree_path = str(Path(git_repo) / \".worktrees\" / BRANCH)\n    worktree_git(\"worktree\", \"add\", \"-b\", BRANCH, worktree_path, \"HEAD\", cwd=git_repo)\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO workspaces (id, repo_id, name, branch, path, state, kind) \"\n        \"VALUES (?, ?, 'backstop', ?, ?, 'ready', 'user')\",\n        (WORKSPACE_ID, REPO_ID, BRANCH, worktree_path),\n    )\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO sessions (id, workspace_id) VALUES (?, ?)\", (SESSION_ID, WORKSPACE_ID)\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    return worktree_path\n\n\ndef _insert_receipt(\n    db,\n    *,\n    repo_id: str = REPO_ID,\n    phase: str = \"quarantined\",\n    repo_root: str = \"/tmp/backstop-repo-root\",\n) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Insert one durable repository deletion receipt directly.\"\"\"\n    operation_id = uuid.uuid4().hex\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repository_deletions (operation_id, repo_id, repo_root, \"\n        \"database_identity, principal_authority, principal_identity_json, entries_json, \"\n        \"git_cleanup_path, git_worktrees_json, phase) \"\n        \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, 'identity', 'a', '{}', '[]', 'x', '[]', ?)\",\n        (operation_id, repo_id, repo_root, phase),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    return operation_id\n\n\ndef _remove_receipt(db, repo_id: str = REPO_ID) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Remove every receipt row exactly like successful recovery does.\"\"\"\n    db.execute(\"DELETE FROM repository_deletions WHERE repo_id = ?\", (repo_id,))\n    db.commit()\n\n\ndef test_receipt_row_rejects_active_and_malformed_phases(db) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Every receipt phase — including a malformed one — keeps the repository owned.\"\"\"\n    require_no_repository_deletion(db, REPO_ID)\n    for phase in (\"prepared\", \"quarantined\", \"delete_committed\", \"unexpected-phase\"):\n        _insert_receipt(db, phase=phase)\n        with pytest.raises(RepositoryDeletionPendingError, match=\"Repository deletion\"):\n            require_no_repository_deletion(db, REPO_ID)\n        _remove_receipt(db)\n    require_no_repository_deletion(db, REPO_ID)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"phase\", [\"quarantined\", \"unexpected-phase\"])\ndef test_receipt_blocks_new_workspace_deletion_claim_before_effects(\n    db, git_repo: str, phase: str\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A new deletion claim is refused durably untouched while a receipt exists.\"\"\"\n    _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    _insert_receipt(db, phase=phase)\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspaceDeletionConflict) as excinfo:\n        asyncio.run(claim_workspace_deletion(_request(), WORKSPACE_ID))\n    assert excinfo.value.status_code == 409\n    assert excinfo.value.detail == {\n        \"code\": \"deletion_claim_unavailable\",\n        \"message\": \"Workspace deletion claim is unavailable\",\n    }\n    assert (\n        db.execute(\"SELECT state FROM workspaces WHERE id = ?\", (WORKSPACE_ID,)).fetchone()[0]\n        == \"ready\"\n    )\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_deletions\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert not (Path(git_repo) / \".git\" / \".yinshi-workspace-admission-v1\").exists()\n\n\ndef test_removing_receipt_resumes_workspace_deletion_claim(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"After recovery removes the row, the normal claim path works unchanged.\"\"\"\n    _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    _remove_receipt(db)\n    claim = asyncio.run(claim_workspace_deletion(_request(), WORKSPACE_ID))\n    assert claim[\"state\"] == \"claiming\"\n    assert (\n        db.execute(\"SELECT state FROM workspaces WHERE id = ?\", (WORKSPACE_ID,)).fetchone()[0]\n        == \"deleting\"\n    )\n    assert (\n        db.execute(\n            \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_deletions WHERE workspace_id = ?\",\n            (WORKSPACE_ID,),\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n        == 1\n    )\n\n\ndef test_receipt_blocks_execution_reservation_before_receipt_insert(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Execution reservation refuses before any durable or runtime effect.\"\"\"\n    _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    admission = ExecutionAdmission(\n        lease=None,\n        workspace=prompt_workspace(db, _request(), SESSION_ID),\n        request=_request(),\n        session_id=SESSION_ID,\n        operation_id=uuid.uuid4().hex,\n        physical_identity=\"physical-identity-json\",\n        kind=\"prompt\",\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspaceAdmissionError):\n        asyncio.run(admission.reserve())\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_execution_receipts\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_execution_targets\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n\n\ndef test_receipt_blocks_workspace_creation_before_git_effects(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Workspace creation refuses before worktree or checkout work starts.\"\"\"\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    with pytest.raises(RepositoryDeletionPendingError):\n        asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(db, REPO_ID))\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspaces\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert not (Path(git_repo) / \".worktrees\").exists()\n\n\ndef test_removing_receipt_resumes_workspace_creation(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"After recovery removes the row, workspace creation resumes normally.\"\"\"\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    _remove_receipt(db)\n    created = asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(db, REPO_ID))\n    assert created[\"repo_id\"] == REPO_ID\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspaces\").fetchone()[0] == 1\n\n\ndef _repair_tenant() -> TenantContext:\n    \"\"\"Build one minimal tenant context for the repair claim seam.\"\"\"\n    return TenantContext(\n        user_id=\"tenant-user\",\n        email=\"tenant@example.com\",\n        data_dir=\"/tmp/backstop-tenant\",\n        db_path=\"/tmp/backstop-tenant/tenant.db\",\n    )\n\n\ndef test_receipt_blocks_checkout_repair_claim_before_publication(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The repair/publication claim refuses before creating a durable repair owner.\"\"\"\n    worktree_path = _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    state = WorkspaceCheckoutState(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo,\n        remote_url=None,\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspaces=((WORKSPACE_ID, BRANCH),),\n        workspace_paths=((WORKSPACE_ID, worktree_path),),\n    )\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspacePublicationError, match=\"repository deletion\"):\n        _begin_repair(\n            db,\n            authorize=lambda database: state,\n            expected=state,\n            tenant=_repair_tenant(),\n            authority_hash=\"a\" * 64,\n            database_identity=\"identity\",\n            execution_operation_id=None,\n            operation_id=uuid.uuid4().hex,\n            owner_token=\"d\" * 64,\n            final_repo_path=git_repo,\n            requires_publication=True,\n        )\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_checkout_repairs\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n\n\ndef test_removing_receipt_resumes_checkout_repair_claim(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"After recovery removes the row, the repair claim admits a new owner again.\"\"\"\n    worktree_path = _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    state = WorkspaceCheckoutState(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo,\n        remote_url=None,\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspaces=((WORKSPACE_ID, BRANCH),),\n        workspace_paths=((WORKSPACE_ID, worktree_path),),\n    )\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    _remove_receipt(db)\n    result = _begin_repair(\n        db,\n        authorize=lambda database: state,\n        expected=state,\n        tenant=_repair_tenant(),\n        authority_hash=\"a\" * 64,\n        database_identity=\"identity\",\n        execution_operation_id=None,\n        operation_id=uuid.uuid4().hex,\n        owner_token=\"d\" * 64,\n        final_repo_path=git_repo,\n        requires_publication=True,\n    )\n    assert result is not None\n    assert result[2] == \"active\"\n\n\ndef test_receipt_blocks_managed_integration_admission(\n    client, db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Managed integration admission refuses before any trial Git effect.\"\"\"\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"THREAD_MANAGED_INTEGRATION_ENABLED\", \"true\")\n    get_settings.cache_clear()\n    seed_parent_stack(db, git_repo)\n    spawned = client.post(\n        \"/api/threads/parent-session/children\",\n        json={\n            \"idempotency_key\": str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            \"title\": \"Backstop child\",\n            \"task\": \"Update README.md\",\n            \"start_immediately\": False,\n        },\n    )\n    assert spawned.status_code == 201\n    child = spawned.json()\n    workspace = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT w.path FROM workspaces w JOIN sessions s ON s.workspace_id = w.id \"\n        \"WHERE s.id = ?\",\n        (child[\"child_session_id\"],),\n    ).fetchone()\n    (Path(workspace[\"path\"]) / \"README.md\").write_bytes(b\"# Child result\\n\")\n    from yinshi.services.thread_orchestration import initial_run_idempotency_key\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO prompt_runs (id, session_id, idempotency_key, status) \"\n        \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, 'completed')\",\n        (\n            uuid.uuid4().hex,\n            child[\"child_session_id\"],\n            initial_run_idempotency_key(child[\"delegation_id\"]),\n        ),\n    )\n    db.execute(\n        \"UPDATE thread_delegations SET status = 'completed' WHERE id = ?\",\n        (child[\"delegation_id\"],),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    sealed = client.get(f\"/api/threads/{child['child_session_id']}/result\")\n    assert sealed.status_code == 200\n    path = f\"/api/threads/parent-session/children/{child['child_session_id']}/integrate\"\n    preview = client.get(path)\n    assert preview.status_code == 200\n    confirmation = preview.json()\n    assert confirmation[\"eligible\"] is True\n    payload = {\n        \"idempotency_key\": str(uuid.uuid4()),\n        \"result_id\": confirmation[\"result_id\"],\n        \"expected_parent_head\": confirmation[\"expected_parent_head\"],\n        \"confirmed\": True,\n    }\n    repo_id = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT w.repo_id FROM workspaces w JOIN sessions s ON s.workspace_id = w.id \"\n        \"WHERE s.id = 'parent-session'\"\n    ).fetchone()[0]\n    _insert_receipt(db, repo_id=str(repo_id))\n    parent_head = head_commit(git_repo)\n    applied = client.post(path, json=payload)\n    assert applied.status_code == 409\n    assert applied.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Integration precondition changed\"\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert head_commit(git_repo) == parent_head\n    _remove_receipt(db, str(repo_id))\n```\n\n## Expected red/green behavior\n\n- **Red (tests only, before edit packets 1–7):** collection fails on `ImportError: RepositoryDeletionPendingError` / `require_no_repository_deletion` — the missing helper is the first observed failure. After packet 1 only, the import succeeds and the five \"blocks\" tests fail at their `pytest.raises` points (pre-change behavior proceeds: claim inserts, reserve inserts, creation creates a worktree, repair returns a tuple, integrate returns 200) while the three \"resume\" tests pass as regression guards.\n- **Green (packets 1–7 applied):** all eleven tests pass; every \"blocks\" test additionally asserts no durable row, unchanged workspace state, and no filesystem/Git effect (no worktree dir, no admission directory, unchanged parent HEAD).\n\n## Validation commands (all not run — write-denied)\n\n1. `cd backend && python -m pytest tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py -v`\n2. `cd backend && python -m pytest tests/test_repository_deletion_recovery.py tests/test_workspace_deletion.py tests/test_workspace_execution_receipts.py tests/test_workspace_publication.py tests/test_thread_integration.py tests/test_prompt_journal_admission.py`\n3. `cd backend && ruff check src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py src/yinshi/services/workspace.py src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py`\n4. `cd backend && mypy src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py src/yinshi/services/workspace.py src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py src/yinshi