{"type":"message","id":"0e0b66d9","parentId":"1643665c","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:51:44.629Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Reviewing outdated documentation specifics**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62bdf507c87d099f556a6ce0e74c9\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Reviewing outdated documentation specifics**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mNkW2eHcRlJaJErJ7QvwND4R|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62be03fbc87d0b5f7f7a402b3ee94","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"docs/thread-orchestration.md","offset":45,"limit":25}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":369,"output":56,"cacheRead":242560,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":24,"totalTokens":242985,"cost":{"input":0.001845,"output":0.00168,"cacheRead":0.12128,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.124805}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789275100674,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62bdd542087d08ecb3a13d9d4e53a","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"038c8b77","parentId":"0e0b66d9","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:51:44.645Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mNkW2eHcRlJaJErJ7QvwND4R|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62be03fbc87d0b5f7f7a402b3ee94","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Valid terminal states are `completed`, `failed`, `cancelled`, and `interrupted`. Cancellation can use `cancelling` between `running` and `cancelled`.\n\nActive counts include `provisioning`, `queued`, `running`, and `cancelling`. A provisioning record without a child session reserves capacity and appears as a placeholder.\n\nLater recursive deletion must remove deepest descendants first. Parent workspaces are removed last. Phase 1 rejects parent deletion instead.\n\n## Database contract\n\nShared databases use schema version 10. Per-user databases use user version 7. Both migration paths support SQLite and SQLCipher.\n\nMigrations are additive and repeatable. Existing rows remain unchanged. Older restored databases migrate when opened. Whole-file backup and relay transfer require no format conversion.\n\nVersion 8 adds immutable result history and managed integration storage. `thread_result_versions` now holds one immutable row for every sealed generation. `thread_integrations` records confirmed application attempts. The admission receipts described under physical execution exclusion live in `workspace_execution_receipts`. Because a deletion must survive removal of the workspace row itself, its claim lives in `workspace_deletions`. A backfill gives sealed results a stable `result_id` and never rewrites drafts.\n\nVersion 10 uses tenant version 7 for durable private checkout publication. `workspace_checkout_repairs` owns each logical repair. `workspace_checkout_publications` records each published repository or worktree. These records retain path identities, marker ownership, backlink validation, and no-replace rename progress for restart recovery.\n\nExisting tables gain these fields:\n\n```sql\nALTER TABLE sessions ADD COLUMN title TEXT;\nALTER TABLE workspaces ADD COLUMN kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'user';\nALTER TABLE workspaces ADD COLUMN parent_workspace_id TEXT;\n```\n\nWorkspace kinds are `user`, `delegated`, and `integration`. Existing rows use `user`.\n\n[311 more lines in file. Use offset=70 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789275104645}}
{"type":"message","id":"ba3f12ed","parentId":"038c8b77","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:51:51.681Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Updating version and tenant references**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62be4d95c87d0aa19ed3633900c56\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Updating version and tenant references**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d5RgGq1NeOuGmyr3F4jLy8Vh|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62be6465087d0af60d839ae972104","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"docs/thread-orchestration.md","edits":[{"oldText":"Shared databases use schema version 10. Per-user databases use user version 7. Both migration paths support SQLite and SQLCipher.","newText":"Shared databases use schema version 11. Per-user databases use user version 9. Both migration paths support SQLite and SQLCipher."}]}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":567,"output":139,"cacheRead":242816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":51,"totalTokens":243522,"cost":{"input":0.0028350000000000003,"output":0.00417,"cacheRead":0.12140799999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.128413}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789275104655,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62be13a2087d096f10337b455ec46","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
