{"type":"message","id":"6d7ac4b8","parentId":"9ecf5965","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:53:03.572Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning safe session reclaim with socket tracking**\n\n**Designing robust session retirement with device verification**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62c1b641087d0acf5fe2d43bbf103\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning safe session reclaim with socket tracking**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing robust session retirement with device verification**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cpD60L7EAN6u8AI6ln7eJHNJ|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62c286d2487d0b53282bb5c6a83f9","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"return await runs.run('integration_corrected_review',{agent:'final-review',task:'Review the corrected managed-integration candidate in the current checkout. Read the actual current files and diff, including expert edits made after review 57965bef. First read /Users/user/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md and referenced red-flags. Original Phase 6 requirements: exact sealed child result, explicit confirmation, deterministic temporary Git trial, parent unchanged on refusal/conflict, exact one resulting parent commit on success, durable retry/recovery, exact-owner physical admission, no SQLite handle across await/external effect. Prior findings to verify: pre-mutation parent HEAD/dirtiness stranded applying; cancellation after terminal commit stranded admission; checking retries allocated new trials; conflict trial cleanup; same-key replay/status after success. Also assess the new create_or_resume trial logic and conflict fingerprint cleanup for unsafe deletion, false adoption, and crash windows. Treat the prior 404 seal failures as potentially caused by concurrent test processes; parent independently ran test_thread_integration.py alone with 10 passing. Do not modify files. Return findings with location, impact, correction, validation, or state no remediation needed.'});","chatProgress":"live-card","context":"fresh","cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","async":false,"timeoutMs":1800000,"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":20,"graceTurns":3},"toolBudget":{"soft":65,"hard":90,"block":["bash","read","grep","find","ls"]},"artifacts":true,"outputMode":"inline","usageBudget":{"tokens":{"hard":110000}}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":337,"output":772,"cacheRead":248704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":423,"totalTokens":249813,"cost":{"input":0.001685,"output":0.02316,"cacheRead":0.12435199999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.149197}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789275159587,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62c18332c87d0a68544811b2a3e86","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"2564f20a","parentId":"6d7ac4b8","timestamp":"2026-09-13T05:03:40.092Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cpD60L7EAN6u8AI6ln7eJHNJ|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62c286d2487d0b53282bb5c6a83f9","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"integration_corrected_review\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"cd2f0613\",\n  \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 20 assistant turns (soft limit 20, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nChanges required. Five findings remain. Nominal retries improved, but crash recovery still conflates safe refusal with uncertain parent mutation.\\n\\n## Confirmed findings\\n\\n### 1. High: `applying` recovery can report failure after parent mutation\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:895-949`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1242-1313`\\n\\n`applying` is persisted before parent preflight. Recovery later treats changed `HEAD` or dirtiness as safe `ThreadIntegrationApplyRefusedError`.\\n\\nA crash after merge can leave either:\\n\\n- Trial commit applied, followed by another parent commit.\\n- Partial index or working-tree mutation with unchanged `HEAD`.\\n\\nRetry records `failed/parent_collision` and releases admission in both cases.\\n\\n**Impact:** Durable state can deny a successful integration or claim safe refusal after partial parent mutation.\\n\\n**Correction:** Separate durable `prepared` and `applying` phases. Persist pre-effect evidence before merge. Recovery from `applying` must never infer safe refusal from current dirtiness or `HEAD` alone.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-expert`.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- Crash after merge changes `HEAD`, then advance parent.\\n- Crash after partial merge mutation with unchanged `HEAD`.\\n- Verify retry returns integrated or blocked, never failed.\\n- Verify blocked cases retain admission.\\n\\n### 2. High: Conflict becomes terminal before cleanup is durable\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:849-895`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:285-347`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:381-389`\\n\\nCode commits `conflict` before cleanup. `conflict` is terminal, so cancellation releases admission. Terminal replay only returns stored outcome.\\n\\nA crash before or during cleanup leaves dirty trial worktree registration behind. Replay never resumes cleanup.\\n\\n**Impact:** Temporary conflict artifacts leak permanently. They can obstruct later repository lifecycle operations.\\n\\n**Correction:** Persist a nonterminal cleanup-pending state with conflict fingerprint. Transition to terminal `conflict` only after cleanup is durable.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-expert`.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- Cancel after conflict persistence but before cleanup.\\n- Crash after worktree removal but before manifest removal.\\n- Replay and verify exact cleanup resumes.\\n- Verify admission remains until cleanup completes.\\n\\n### 3. High: Conflict cleanup can delete user-modified files\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:795-815`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:927-955`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1030-1099`\\n\\nConflict fingerprint hashes porcelain names and tracked diffs. It does not hash untracked or ignored file contents.\\n\\nCleanup also awaits reauthorization after its final fingerprint, then uses `git worktree remove --force`. A concurrent modification can occur before deletion.\\n\\n**Impact:** User-created trial content can match the fingerprint and be deleted.\\n\\n**Correction:** Do not force-delete mutable conflict worktrees without OS-enforced exclusive ownership. Otherwise quarantine and fully hash all content before cleanup.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-expert`.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- Modify untracked and ignored file contents after fingerprinting.\\n- Modify tracked conflict content during reauthorization.\\n- Verify cleanup retains modified worktrees and keeps admission blocked.\\n\\n### 4. High: Recovery can adopt a user-created commit\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:817-841`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:987-1028`\\n\\nRecovered trial validation checks only parent and tree. A different commit with matching parent and sealed tree passes.\\n\\nCommit message, author, committer, timestamps, signatures, and extra headers remain unbound.\\n\\n**Impact:** Untrusted trial state can claim backend ownership and publish unauthorized commit metadata into parent history.\\n\\n**Correction:** Derive and persist a deterministic expected trial commit. Require exact OID equality during recovery.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- Replace interrupted trial `HEAD` with a custom same-tree, same-parent commit.\\n- Verify retry blocks and retains it.\\n- Verify genuine interrupted cherry-pick still resumes.\\n\\n### 5. High: Admission claim has a physical-identity race\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:490-513`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:600-623`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:713-746`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py:420-449`\\n\\nStatus, abort, and execution compare physical identity before admission acquisition. They omit the supported `physical_identity` argument during acquisition.\\n\\nA replacement between those operations can receive a durable marker belonging to the old operation.\\n\\n**Impact:** Integration can strand admission on a replacement checkout that it never authorized.\\n\\n**Correction:** Pass recorded `physical_workspace_json` into every integration admission acquisition. Keep the acquisition-time identity check authoritative.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-advanced`.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- Replace checkout between preliminary identity read and admission claim.\\n- Verify claim fails.\\n- Verify no marker appears on replacement checkout.\\n\\n## Prior finding status\\n\\n- Checking retry trial reuse: resolved for complete root, worktree, successful cherry-pick, and ref-publication interruptions.\\n- Cancellation after integrated terminal commit: resolved for nominal integrated replay.\\n- Same-key success replay: resolved for unchanged or exactly applied parent state.\\n- Pre-mutation parent rejection: nominal cases pass, but durable phase ambiguity remains under finding 1.\\n- Conflict cleanup: unresolved under findings 2 and 3.\\n- Production UI test: now mounts `ThreadPanel.tsx`.\\n\\n## Review limits\\n\\nNo test command was independently repeated after final expert edits. Parent-reported `test_thread_integration.py` result covers 10 tests but not new recovery behavior.\\n\\nReview covered current integration service, integration Git paths, admission service, ownership checks, schema, routes, recovery tests, and production UI test. Broad unrelated dirty changes were outside this review.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/cd2f0613/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n      \"task\": \"Review the corrected managed-integration candidate in the current checkout. Read the actual current files and diff, including expert edits made after review 57965bef. First read /Users/user/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md and referenced red-flags. Original Phase 6 requirements: exact sealed child result, explicit confirmation, deterministic temporary Git trial, parent unchanged on refusal/conflict, exact one resulting parent commit on success, durable retry/recovery, exact-owner physical admission, no SQLite handle across await/external effect. Prior findings to verify: pre-mutation parent HEAD/dirtiness stranded applying; cancellation after terminal commit stranded admission; checking retries allocated new trials; conflict trial cleanup; same-key replay/status after success. Also assess the new create_or_resume trial logic and conflict fingerprint cleanup for unsafe deletion, false adoption, and crash windows. Treat the prior 404 seal failures as potentially caused by concurrent test processes; parent independently ran test_thread_integration.py alone with 10 passing. Do not modify files. Return findings with location, impact, correction, validation, or state no remediation needed.\",\n      \"routingContract\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n        \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n        \"thinking\": \"max\",\n        \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n      },\n      \"launchContractDigest\": \"329e57c6be01d44559e9f6ac6d6f7c59be5b15bcd1b4a77dcc86b0afb5c08c53\",\n      \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n        \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n        \"runtime\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"configured\": [],\n        \"effective\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"omitted\": {\n          \"runtime\": 0,\n          \"configured\": 0,\n          \"effective\": 0\n        }\n      },\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"outputState\": \"present\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"input\": 181949,\n        \"output\": 21640,\n        \"cacheRead\": 1205120,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n        \"cost\": 2.161505,\n        \"turns\": 25\n      },\n      \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\",\n      \"thinking\": \"max\",\n      \"artifactPaths\": {\n        \"inputPath\": \"