ate in the current checkout. Read the actual curre...","objective":"Review the corrected managed-integration candidate in the current checkout. Read the actual current files and diff, including expert edits made after review 57965bef. First read /Users/user/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md and referenced red-flags. Original Phase 6 requirements: exact sealed child result, explicit confirmation, deterministic temporary Git trial, parent unchanged on refusal/conflict, exact one resulting parent commit on success, durable retry/recovery, exact-owner physical admission, no SQLite handle across await/external effect. Prior findings to verify: pre-mutation parent HEAD/dirtiness stranded applying; cancellation after terminal commit stranded admission; checking retries allocated new trials; conflict trial cleanup; same-key replay/status after success. Also assess the new create_or_resume trial logic and conflict fingerprint cleanup for unsafe deletion, false adoption, and crash windows. Treat the prior 404 seal failures as potentially caused by concurrent test processes; parent independently ran test_thread_integration.py alone with 10 passing. Do not modify files. Return findings with location, impact, correction, validation, or state no remediation needed.","status":"completed","createdAt":"2026-09-13T04:53:03.745Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-13T05:03:39.882Z","runs":[{"runId":"call_cpD60L7EAN6u8AI6ln7eJHNJ|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa62c286d2487d0b53282bb5c6a83f9","mode":"workflow","agent":"final-review","status":"completed","startedAt":"2026-09-13T05:03:39.882Z","completedAt":"2026-09-13T05:03:39.882Z","usage":{"tokens":203589}}],"decisions":[],"artifacts":[{"kind":"output","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/cd2f0613_final-review_0_output.md"},{"kind":"other","path":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/cd2f0613_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl","description":"Child transcript"}],"receipts":[],"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","ownerSessionId":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64.jsonl","summary":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"integration_corrected_review\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"cd2f0613\",\n  \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 20 assistant turns (soft limit 20, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nChanges required. Five findings remain. Nominal retries improved, but crash recovery still conflates safe refusal with uncertain parent mutation.\\n\\n## Confirmed findings\\n\\n### 1. High: `applying` recovery can report failure after parent mutation\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:895-949`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1242-1313`\\n\\n`applying` is persisted before parent preflight. Recovery later treats changed `HEAD` or dirtiness as safe `ThreadIntegrationApplyRefusedError`.\\n\\nA crash after merge can leave either:\\n\\n- Trial commit applied, followed by another parent commit.\\n- Partial index or working-tree mutation with unchanged `HEAD`.\\n\\nRetry records `failed/parent_collision` and releases admission in both cases.\\n\\n**Impact:** Durable state can deny a successful integration or claim safe refusal after partial parent mutation.\\n\\n**Correction:** Separate durable `prepared` and `applying` phases. Persist pre-effect evidence before merge. Recovery from `applying` must never infer safe refusal from current dirtiness or `HEAD` alone.\\n\\n**Remediation:** `worker-expert`.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- Crash after merge changes `HEAD`, then advance parent.\\n- Crash after partial merge mutation with unchanged `HEAD`.\\n- Verify retry returns integrated or blocked, never failed.\\n- Verify blocked cases retain admission.\\n\\n### 2. High: Conflict becomes terminal before cleanup is durable\\n\\n**Location:**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:849-895`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:285-347`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integr...","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Five concrete findings include severity, exact file regions, impact, correction, remediation tier, and validation."}],"changedFiles":["backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py","backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py","frontend/e2e/thread-integration.spec.ts"],"testsAddedOrUpdated":["backend/tests/test_thread_integration.py","backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py","backend/tests/test_thread_integration_abort.py","backend/tests/test_thread_integration_target_identity.py","frontend/e2e/thread-integration.spec.ts"],"commandsRun":[{"command":"git status --short --branch && git log -8 --oneline --decorate","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected current unstaged candidate and repository history."},{"command":"git diff --stat and scoped git diff commands","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected current managed-integration diff and affected boundaries."},{"command":"pytest backend/tests/test_thread_integration.py","result":"passed","summary":"Parent-reported isolated run: 10 passed. Not independently repeated."},{"command":"pytest backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py","result":"not-run","summary":"Tool budget ended before independent execution."}],"validationOutput":["Current source reuses the latest durable checking trial instead of allocating another.","Fresh terminal reads and exact-owner replay repair exist for nominal terminal cancellation.","Crash recovery still conflates pre-apply refusal with uncertain post-merge state.","Conflict cleanup remains non-durable and can delete mutable untracked or ignored content."],"residualRisks":["Applying recovery can publish a false failed outcome after parent mutation.","Conflict artifacts can survive terminal persistence without recoverable cleanup.","Conflict force-cleanup can delete user-modified content.","Recovered same-tree commits can carry unauthorized metadata.","Admission can target a replacement physical checkout."],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"Candidate adds managed integration, durable trial recovery, admission coordination, conflict handling, APIs, and production UI coverage. Recovery and ownership gaps remain.","reviewFindings":["high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:895-949 - applying recovery can report safe failure after successful or partial parent mutation","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:849-895 - conflict becomes terminal before cleanup is durable","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:795-815 - conflict fingerprint omits untracked and ignored file contents before force deletion","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:817-841 - recovered commit validation permits same-tree commits with unauthorized metadata","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:490-513 - admission acquisition omits recorded physical identity and permits replacement race"],"manualNotes":"Review applies to current unstaged checkout. No files were modified. All findings block completion."}}}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789275820092}}
{"type":"compaction","id":"e88b8f0b","parentId":"2564f20a","timestamp":"2026-09-13T05:06:06.559Z","summary":"## Goal\nFinish Phases 6 and 7 of `/Users/user/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md` in `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`, validate independently, then commit, rebase, and push.\n\n- Phase 6 covers managed child integration, deterministic Git application and recovery, broker-backed Linux isolation, authenticated desktop-to-VM transport, bounded repository ingestion, durable replica authority, and drain/export/reclaim.\n- Managed integration does not require Linux. Native Darwin execution remains fail-closed.\n- Phase 7 covers nested delegation, budgets, steering, and persisted delivery semantics. It remains blocked until Phase 6 is accepted.\n- The lifecycle coordinator for `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim` is complete; immediate work is fixing reviewed managed-integration and repository-deletion recovery defects, then implementing production broker transport/dispatch and concrete lifecycle effects.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Continue implementation without waiting, but request approval before material privileged infrastructure changes. Disabled VM qualification was explicitly approved.\n- Use at least five subagents where practical; the parent controls integration, commits, rebases, and pushes.\n- Preserve the heavily dirty inherited Phase 6 worktree and unrelated changes.\n- Use `read`, `edit`, and `write` for source changes. Do not use shell source writes, mutating formatters, permission bypasses, manufactured failures, or production reversions merely to create red tests.\n- Do not disable, inspect, or bypass TDD Guard. Parent-authorized red→green writes and complete edit packets remain fallbacks when worker branches lack a bound request.\n- RepoPrompt Context Builder sees a stale or missing checkout; resolve capabilities against the actual checkout and do not invent APIs.\n- Use `backend/.venv` for backend tests. Ruff is `/Users/user/.pyenv/versions/3.12.3/bin/ruff`, version 0.16.5.\n- Required checks include focused and broad pytest, Ruff, format, isort, Flake8, strict mypy, `py_compile`, `git diff --check`, prose checks, Linux qualification, and independent review.\n- No SQLite handle may cross an external effect or `await`.\n- Unknown transport, timeout, cancellation, verification, delivery, acknowledgment, effect, presence, absence, rename-state lookup, or SQLite commit results remain stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n- Preserve exact ownership, runtime acknowledgment, markers, receipts, synchronization facts, and A4 authenticated journal positions.\n- Root protocol remains exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`; all gates remain independently disabled by default.\n- Drain is graceful broker-to-executor only. Missing acknowledgment or a live runtime blocks reclaim. Do not add a fourth root stop action.\n- Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Only bounded IDs, roles, media types, digests, lengths, limits, and typed receipts may enter the journal.\n- Broker lifecycle v2 and the read-only legacy v1 journal must remain unchanged by replica-authority work.\n- The stdio relay is opaque, uses signed broker protocol authentication, exposes no caller-selected socket path, and currently accepts one bounded request frame only.\n- Preserve fixed executor identities `yinshi-executor-00` through `yinshi-executor-31`; callers cannot select them.\n- Keep `rft-sandbox` stopped and untouched.\n- Git replacement objects and lazy/promisor fetches must remain disabled for artifact generation and verification.\n- Artifact verification must use independent, empty bare quarantine repositories with matching SHA-1 or SHA-256 object format.\n- Publication must reject unsafe paths, symlinks, digest or length mismatch, partial sets, overwrite, timeout, cancellation, uncertain acknowledgment, root/final replacement, late metadata changes, hardlinks, FIFOs, and malformed declarations.\n- Publication requires exact root mode `0700`, pending/final directory mode `0700`, artifact file mode `0600`, expected ownership, and link count one.\n- Publication must use same-filesystem atomic no-replace rename and correct file/directory synchronization ordering.\n- Public storage inspection returns `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` and cannot mint synchronization or publication authority.\n- Failed pre-visibility stages move atomically to unique retained `.pending.abandoned.<attempt>.<random>` quarantine names. Mutable names are never deleted.\n- `limits_sha256` must equal one broker-owned immutable configured profile.\n- Request frames authenticate with the configured Ed25519 request key. Responses authenticate with the key configured for the signed broker incarnation.\n- Artifact-root capacity must be enforced across store instances/processes with cancellation-safe root-scoped locking.\n- The coordinator is stateless; `BrokerReplicaJournal` is the sole lifecycle authority. All seven typed effects are required at construction.\n- Coordinator input is an authenticated `BrokerRequest` plus its raw signed frame; peer UID and transport authentication remain outside it.\n- Stage effects use absolute monotonic deadlines. Timeout/cancellation does not cancel an uncertain effect task; late results are consumed but never appended as completion.\n- Persistence errors, including `ReplicaJournalError`, escape rather than becoming effect outcomes.\n- Startup recovery is serial. Another broker incarnation’s lifecycle becomes `broker_restart_unknown` without effects.\n- Export returns exactly three external references.\n- Managed-integration recovery must distinguish safe pre-mutation rejection from uncertainty after a potentially mutating Git command.\n- Terminal integration replay/cancellation must reconcile and release only the exact-owner admission marker after a fresh authoritative durable read.\n- Checking-stage retry must reconcile durable trial intent before allocating another trial; exact owned state may be reused or cleaned, while modified/uncertain state remains blocked.\n- Repository deletion receipts must block workspace creation, deletion, execution, repair/publication, and managed integration before filesystem/runtime/Git effects.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Phases 0–1 committed as `bebd2ccc`; Phase 2 as `e4a80b43`, `b488b502`, and `0cddd4bb`; Phase 3 as `2fd220b9`; Phase 4 as `ff7e6e81`; Phase 5 pushed as `1fa5d789 feat: add agent thread delegation and structured results`.\n- [x] Historical Phase 5 validation completed: backend 2137 with one skip, sidecar 119 with one skip, frontend 427, plus build, style, and mypy.\n- [x] Large Phase 6 candidate implements integration, immutable trials/results, physical admission, execution receipts, publication/recovery UI, migrations, and fixture Playwright coverage.\n- [x] Architecture A1–A7, corrected gate acceptance, publication acceptance, F6 acceptance, and offline A4 F1–F15 implementation/review were completed and recorded under `/tmp`.\n- [x] Integrated `workspace_replica.py`, its reconciliation suite, and `docs/workspace-os-isolation.md`.\n- [x] Trusted-Git gates, descriptor-backed Git operations, publication crash recovery, workspace repair, prompt-journal settlement, frontend repair handling, and durable repository deletion recovery were implemented.\n- [x] Repository deletion distinguishes imported and managed ownership, preserves imported metadata, uses durable receipts, handles unbound targets, and keeps malformed or legacy state unresolved.\n- [x] Root prepare/reclaim/launch use fixed paths, validated accounts, no-follow descriptors, mount checks, allocation locking, socket pinning, iterative reclaim, and default-disabled gates.\n- [x] Root persists `.executor-identity`, uses synced `.executor-identity.pending` publication, retains quarantine tombstones, and supports interrupted pin states.\n- [x] Linux recovery qualification passed for zero-byte and three-byte pending markers; Linux reclaim qualification passed with `repo=0000` and `home=0777`.\n- [x] Broker lifecycle v2 implements immutable `accepted`, `lifecycle_claimed`, `stage_started`, `stage_outcome`, and `stage_unresolved` events with fixed `prepare → runtime_setup → launch` ordering.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py` and action-bound `LauncherSocketClient.prepare()`, `launch()`, and `reclaim()`.\n- [x] Implemented read-only legacy v1 admission through `inspect_legacy_v1_journal()`, including malformed schema, unsupported version, accepted work, and WAL/SHM sidecar rejection.\n- [x] Implemented fresh-connection exact-event verification after uncertain SQLite commits and `JournalCommitAbsent`.\n- [x] Added `ManagedRootWorker` with bounded framing, serialized actions, separate process group, startup readiness, and kill/reap behavior on timeout/cancellation.\n- [x] Established nested deadlines: root worker 30 seconds, launcher client 35 seconds, broker effect 40 seconds, connection 120 seconds.\n- [x] Separated `LauncherTimeoutError`, `LauncherTransportError`, and `LauncherVerificationError`; clean EOF maps to `transport_unknown`, invalid complete framing to `verification_unknown`.\n- [x] Final independent broker review `d00755d6` found no remaining findings.\n- [x] Focused broker/root lifecycle checks passed 172 tests; strict mypy passed all 126 source files; changed-file static checks passed.\n- [x] Latest broad backend run had 2797 passes, one skip, and three unrelated missing-`HOST` failures; those passed with `HOST=127.0.0.1`. An earlier corrected broad run passed 2799 with one skip.\n- [x] User approved disabled Linux qualification on `yinshi-runtime`; installed wheel, units, hardening drop-ins, and tmpfiles configuration.\n- [x] `systemd-analyze verify` passed; hardening remained intact; root-worker timeout/cancellation and broker v2 replay qualifications passed.\n- [x] Root launcher returned disabled responses for all three actions; legacy accepted v1 work blocked startup without mutation; sockets/services remained inactive; all effect gates remained false; `rft-sandbox` stayed stopped.\n- [x] Architecture oracle selected a separate broker-owned replica journal instead of extending launch lifecycle v2.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py`, tests, and `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay`; opaque fixed-socket relay validation and VM qualification passed. Review `096e5eb4` found no remaining issue.\n- [x] Implemented conflict-index support, deterministic `YNSHRA1\\n` artifact codec, bounded Git subprocess I/O, committed-bundle transport, strict Git-index parsing, and supplemental index-object packs.\n- [x] Committed durable workspace reconciliation as `abff2b2d`, bounded bundles as `2c781b53`, strict index validation as `533df501`, and staged object transport as `4242985d`.\n- [x] Implemented standalone three-artifact publication with descriptor-pinned verification, exact closure checks, safe atomic publication, authority-separated inspection, and broad race/failure coverage.\n- [x] Extended `broker_replica_journal.py` to require exactly `bundle`, `worktree`, and `index_objects`, object format, source-state digest, reconciliation fingerprint, `artifact_set_sha256`, and `limits_sha256`.\n- [x] Expanded `IngestReceipt`, `VerifyReceipt`, `PublishReceipt`, and `ExportReceipt` to bind the exact three-artifact contract and replica authority.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py`, centralizing operation IDs, identifier grammar, filenames/media types, distinct artifact IDs, limits hashing, and artifact-set hashing.\n- [x] `BrokerReplicaJournal` requires `expected_limits_sha256`, `request_public_key`, and a broker-incarnation-keyed `response_public_keys` mapping.\n- [x] Journal acceptance/replay authenticate signed frames, reject unknown signers, bind broker incarnation, recompute artifact-set identity, and reject duplicate export IDs.\n- [x] Journal schema remains version 1 and SQL shape unchanged. `journal_id` is a random 32-hex prefix plus the 64-hex configuration digest, length 97.\n- [x] `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` requires its exact configured limit profile and exposes `limits_sha256`.\n- [x] Implemented `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` with fixed filenames, bounded streaming, descriptor/path checks, quarantine, reconciliation, root replacement protection, and cancellation-safe cross-process capacity locking.\n- [x] Publication pending/quarantine names are randomized; retained failures do not block exact retries.\n- [x] Review cycles `763ded31`, `480936c7`, `0e505f45`, and `bf648f5f` exposed and remediated artifact issues; `636247c9` confirmed no remaining findings.\n- [x] Focused artifact/journal/publication tests reached 91 passes; artifact-store tests reached 23 passes; combined workspace checks passed 124; expanded artifact/Git/publication checks passed 287.\n- [x] Ruff lint, strict mypy, `py_compile`, staged diff checks, and formatting checks passed for the artifact milestone.\n- [x] Committed nine reviewed files as `7f91105f feat: add authenticated broker replica artifacts`.\n- [x] Completed current-checkout read-only coordinator design run `ac665022`.\n- [x] Implemented `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`, `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`, and minimal recovery support in `broker_replica_journal.py`.\n- [x] Implemented exact seven-stage order, immutable lifecycle context, typed effects/results, rejection/unknown handling, signed terminal responses, recovery, bounded owner waiting, timeout/cancellation handling, single-flight gates, reconcile-first retries, semantic receipt validation, signer verification, and same-process uncertainty barriers.\n- [x] Coordinator review found no remaining defects under the immutable journal-keyring invariant.\n- [x] Coordinator validation passed 74 focused tests, Ruff lint/format, strict mypy, and `py_compile`.\n- [x] Committed coordinator milestone as `922f197b feat: coordinate durable replica lifecycles`.\n- [x] Ran five current-checkout scouts for broker transport, admission, drain, export/reclaim, and Phase 7 requirements.\n- [x] Ran planner `d856fe34`, producing `.pi-subagents/artifacts/remaining-phase6-plan.md`.\n- [x] Confirmed production gaps:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py::BrokerService` accepts only `executor.launch`.\n  - `_authenticate()` blocks replica lifecycle requests.\n  - `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS` includes `replica` and `socket`.\n  - `broker_stdio_relay.py` and broker daemon currently carry one complete bounded frame and require EOF.\n  - Request size is limited to 65,536 bytes, while artifacts may approach 1 GiB.\n  - `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set()` accepts whole `bytes` values and can amplify memory.\n  - Published artifact layout is not yet wired to root prepare.\n  - No production caller instantiates `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator`.\n- [x] Ran five independent design/correctness reviews across deletion, integration, isolation, broker, and schema scopes.\n- [x] Confirmed repository-deletion admission defect: tenant workspace operations can proceed while a durable `repository_deletions` receipt remains unresolved.\n- [x] Confirmed managed-integration recovery defects around pre-mutation rejection, terminal marker cleanup, cancellation after terminal commit, and durable trial reconciliation.\n- [x] Added/updated managed-integration recovery work in `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py` and `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py`.\n- [x] Recovery tests now cover successful applied-trial reconciliation, latest durable trial reuse, user-modified trial retention, conflict persistence before cleanup, terminal pre-mutation rejection, cancellation after terminal commit, and stale-marker replay repair.\n- [x] `backend/tests/test_thread_integration.py` passed independently: 10 tests.\n- [x] Ruff passed for `thread_integration.py`, `thread_workspaces.py`, and recovery tests.\n- [x] Strict mypy passed for `thread_integration.py` and `thread_workspaces.py`.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Recover detached worker `c24c21c1` and integrate the repository-deletion admission backstop.\n- [ ] Finish validating and independently reviewing managed-integration recovery edits. A combined 23-test invocation produced 20 passes and 3 failures, while `test_thread_integration.py` passed alone; determine whether this is test-order/shared-state interference or a real defect.\n- [ ] Add the repository-deletion guard inside existing transactions before workspace deletion claims, execution reservation, checkout repair/publication, workspace creation, and managed-integration trial admission.\n- [ ] Wire external artifact ingestion and pinned verification to typed journal receipts without placing bytes in SQLite.\n- [ ] Design and implement a bounded authenticated artifact data-plane distinct from the existing 65,536-byte signed request frame.\n- [ ] Add broker dispatch for replica lifecycle requests without weakening `executor.launch` validation.\n- [ ] Implement verified broker-backed managed-Linux admission while keeping native Darwin fail-closed and all gates independently disabled.\n- [ ] Implement graceful broker-to-executor drain, exact-three-reference export acknowledgment, live-unit checks, and reclaim through existing root `reclaim`.\n- [ ] Obtain clean current-blob reviews for deletion, integration, isolation, broker wiring, and cross-cutting schema.\n- [ ] Refresh `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json`.\n- [ ] Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime` after production wiring changes.\n- [ ] Run full Phase 6 acceptance, then begin Phase 7.\n\n### Blocked\n- Repository-deletion worker is detached under run `c24c21c1`, mission `29cd6dd8-5fe0-4ef0-9c4d-bbd551d899fc`. Exact message: `Detached for intercom coordination: worker-advanced. Reply to the supervisor request first, then wait with subagent_wait({ id: \"c24c21c1\" }). Use subagent({ action: \"status\", id: \"c24c21c1\" }) to recover the result; do not resume or launch a replacement while it remains detached.`\n- Phase 6 remains incomplete because production artifact transport, broker dispatch, concrete admission/drain/export/reclaim adapters, repository-deletion admission, and final acceptance are unfinished.\n- Production execution remains unsupported because `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py` has no verified broker-backed Linux profile.\n- Current signed broker request/relay framing cannot safely carry the three potentially large artifact streams.\n- Production coordinator wiring remains blocked by absent admission, drain, export, export-store, cleanup, and artifact-stream transport effects; do not fabricate support.\n- Some transport ownership/enrollment details may require a product decision before production implementation.\n- Repository-wide Ruff, format, isort, and Flake8 still include unrelated pre-existing failures, including two `F841` failures in `backend/tests/test_api.py`.\n- Phase 7 remains blocked until Phase 6 receives full independent acceptance.\n- Rebase and push remain pending until all required Phase 6/7 work and validation are complete.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Managed integration scope**: Git worktrees provide isolated child results and deterministic application; Linux is not required for integration itself.\n- **VM purpose**: `yinshi-runtime` supplies stronger OS isolation for untrusted execution.\n- **Privileged launcher**: Root accepts only fixed `prepare`, `launch`, or `reclaim` actions and a lowercase hexadecimal operation ID.\n- **No root stop action**: Drain is graceful only; missing acknowledgment or a live runtime becomes unresolved.\n- **Separate privileged gates**: Prepare, launch, and reclaim each require independent opt-in.\n- **Dedicated roots**: Staging, replicas, quarantine, workload sockets, and protected pins use fixed launcher-owned namespaces.\n- **Prepared namespace**: Broker writes staging; root atomically promotes into protected storage.\n- **Promotion durability**: Sync the destination parent before the source parent.\n- **Executor pool**: Use 32 distinct host UID/GID identities.\n- **Allocation authority**: Root-owned `.executor-identity` is the durable allocation record.\n- **Quarantine tombstones**: Reclaim retains only `.executor-identity`; failed artifacts use unique retained quarantine directories.\n- **Private workload `/run`**: Each transient executor receives only protected `/run/session.sock`.\n- **Broker authentication**: Canonical Ed25519-signed frames supplement Unix peer credentials.\n- **Separate replica journal**: Replica lifecycle state belongs in a broker-owned append-only journal, not launch journal v2 or application rows.\n- **Replica stages**: Fixed order is `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`.\n- **Replica public model**: Use `ReplicaAuthority(physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id)` and bind ownership at `claim_authority()`.\n- **Replica decisions and positions**: `ReplicaJournalDecision` exposes `owner_broker_incarnation`; `ReplicaJournalPosition` contains `journal_id`, `sequence`, and `append_receipt_id`.\n- **Replica completion API**: Use explicit typed completion methods; generic terminal recording is only for rejection and unresolved outcomes.\n- **Journal compatibility**: Keep replica schema metadata version 1 and SQL shape unchanged.\n- **Journal configuration binding**: Bind request key, response keyring, and exact limits profile into immutable journal identity.\n- **Terminal responses**: Build with `create_signed_response`; result fields are `stage`, `state`, optional `code`, and optional `receipt_id`.\n- **Artifact storage**: Store only bounded metadata and receipts in SQLite.\n- **Fixed artifact set**: Every publication contains exactly `committed.bundle`, `worktree.yra`, and `index-objects.pack`.\n- **Configured limits**: `limits_sha256` is one broker-owned immutable profile.\n- **Artifact-set identity**: Bind operation, repository/workspace, object format, source state, reconciliation fingerprint, references, authority, generation, and limits.\n- **Committed-bundle boundary**: Bundles carry only explicit committed refs and optional committed HEAD.\n- **Supplemental objects**: `index-objects.pack` contains exactly required index blobs absent from the committed bundle.\n- **Artifact inspection authority**: Inspection proves storage only; publication authority is minted only after successful atomic publication.\n- **Artifact attempt naming**: Broker-generated random names prevent retained failures from blocking retries.\n- **Artifact capacity**: Use cancellation-safe root-scoped inter-process `flock`.\n- **Publication root invariant**: Require exact `0700` before staging and after awaited final verification.\n- **Publication failure classification**: Only confirmed matching pending plus absent final permits safe rejection; uncertain visibility is unresolved.\n- **Coordinator boundary**: One broker-owned stateless coordinator sequences injected typed effects; the journal owns all durable lifecycle position and outcomes.\n- **Coordinator ownership**: The coordinator uses one random owner token and its configured broker signing key; it does not authenticate transport or peer UID.\n- **Coordinator database boundary**: Journal calls complete before every `await`; use read-copy-close, effect, reopen-transactional-CAS.\n- **Effect deadlines**: Each apply/reconcile call receives a fresh absolute monotonic deadline.\n- **Late effects**: Timeout/cancellation records stage-specific unresolved state and does not cancel uncertain tasks or append later completion.\n- **Reconciliation**: `StageReconciliation` outcomes are `completed`, `not_applied`, or `unknown`; only `completed` carries a receipt.\n- **Started-stage recovery**: `completed` persists and advances, `not_applied` reapplies, and `unknown` records stage-specific unresolved.\n- **Owner mismatch recovery**: Another broker incarnation becomes `broker_restart_unknown` without effects.\n- **Missing effects**: Add injected protocols only; do not invent production admission, drain, export, cleanup, or transport support.\n- **Conflict-index semantics**: One path has either one stage-zero entry or unique conflict stages 1–3.\n- **Git-index format**: Support versions 2 and 3 only.\n- **Intent-to-add**: Actual Git uses the nonzero empty-blob OID; zero index OIDs remain rejected.\n- **Artifact envelope**: Keep deterministic magic `YNSHRA1\\n`, version 1, complete flag, and four ordered sections.\n- **Artifact source digest**: Use `SHA256(b\"yinshi-replica-source-v1\\0\" + four raw section digests)`.\n- **Artifact path policy**: Reject unsafe paths, `.git` components, missing parents, invalid topology, duplicates, hardlinks, unsupported kinds, and privilege bits.\n- **Durable stage boundaries**: Accepted intent and stage starts precede effects; confirmed or unresolved outcomes precede progression.\n- **Verified commits**: Close a failed SQLite connection, then compare the intended event through a fresh connection.\n- **Action-bound launcher protocol**: Requests and responses bind action and operation ID.\n- **Failure classification**: Deadlines use `timeout_unknown`, transport loss uses `transport_unknown`, and invalid framing uses `verification_unknown`.\n- **Managed root process**: Timeout or cancellation kills, reaps, and disables the worker instance.\n- **Deletion policy**: Imported repositories preserve user Git metadata; whole-tree quarantine requires explicit managed ownership.\n- **Trusted path policy**: Path location alone never confers ownership.\n- **Gate backstop**: `run_git_bytes` refuses trusted Git when isolation is unsupported.\n- **A4 ownership**: Application owns logical reservation/binding; broker owns effects, synchronization, publication, markers, and physical release.\n- **Stdio relay**: Keep it opaque and fixed to `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, one request per process.\n- **Relay cleanup**: Exceptional and cancelled exchanges abort transport immediately.\n- **Large artifact transport**: Do not place artifacts in the signed JSON request or relax `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX`; add a separately bounded exact-three-stream data plane authenticated by signed metadata.\n- **Broker dispatch separation**: Preserve strict `executor.launch` validation and route replica lifecycle through a separate authenticated path.\n- **Integration uncertainty boundary**: Parent HEAD/dirtiness rejection before mutation is safely terminal; only failures after a potentially mutating Git command retain uncertain admission.\n- **Integration replay cleanup**: Terminal replay and post-commit cancellation use a fresh durable read before releasing exact-owner admission.\n- **Integration trial recovery**: Reconcile the latest durable trial intent before creating another; reuse verified exact state, remove only exact-owned safe failures, retain modified/uncertain trials.\n- **Repository-deletion admission**: Centralize one typed transaction-local guard instead of duplicating receipt interpretation across APIs.\n- **Guard handling**: Never disable TDD Guard; use parent-applied packets and manual red→green checks if necessary.\n- **Phase 7**: Preserve the 20,000-byte contract, 100 pending inbox items, FIFO identity/generation, stop/seal/release ordering, unknown-cost retention, eventual depth three, persisted deadlines, and no scheduler. Default depth remains 1.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Reply to the supervisor request for detached run `c24c21c1`, then wait with `subagent_wait({ id: \"c24c21c1\" })`; do not resume or launch a replacement while detached.\n2. Inspect the repository-deletion worker’s edits and tests, then validate the typed guard at all required admission boundaries.\n3. Reproduce the three combined managed-integration test failures in isolated/order-controlled runs; fix real state leakage or defects and obtain an independent current-blob review.\n4. Commit the reviewed managed-integration and repository-deletion remediation separately from unrelated dirty files.\n5. Finalize a bounded authenticated exact-three-artifact transport framing and key/enrollment contract before implementation.\n6. Add replica lifecycle dispatch to the broker and concrete ingest/verify/publish effects.\n7. Implement fail-closed Linux admission, graceful drain, exact-three-reference export, live-unit verification, and root reclaim.\n8. Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime`, preserving disabled gates, inactive sockets/services, and stopped `rft-sandbox`.\n9. Run complete backend, sidecar, frontend, desktop, documentation, static, and platform validation.\n10. Obtain full current-blob Phase 6 acceptance, refresh `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json`, then implement Phase 7.\n11. Rebase and push only after final approval.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Main checkout: `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`; branch `main`.\n- Current latest milestone commit: `922f197b feat: coordinate durable replica lifecycles`.\n- Earlier Phase 6 commits: `7f91105f`, `4242985d`, `533df501`, `2c781b53`, and `abff2b2d`.\n- The worktree remains heavily dirty with unrelated Phase 6 changes; milestone commits must stage only reviewed files.\n- Production broker inspection run `559f3557` confirmed `BrokerService.handle()` supports only `executor.launch` and has no lifecycle coordinator wiring.\n- Remaining production plan is `.pi-subagents/artifacts/remaining-phase6-plan.md`, run `d856fe34`.\n- Five-domain final-review workflow identified concrete deletion and integration recovery defects; output was large/truncated and should be consulted from artifacts before final acceptance.\n- Managed-integration workers `1d6b483f` and `dc1396ad` timed out, but the latter left source/test changes in the shared checkout.\n- Current managed-integration focused evidence:\n  - `tests/test_thread_integration.py`: 10 passed independently.\n  - Combined integration invocation: 20 passed, 3 failed.\n  - Ruff: passed.\n  - Strict mypy: passed for both changed service files.\n- Detached repository-deletion run: `c24c21c1`, mission `29cd6dd8-5fe0-4ef0-9c4d-bbd551d899fc`.\n- Its authorized scope is a helper in `backend/src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py`, required callers, focused tests, and stable conflict mapping.\n- Coordinator APIs include `ReplicaLifecycleEffects`, generic `ReplicaStageEffect`, `StageReconciliation`, `StageRejected`, `StageOutcomeUnknown`, and `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator`.\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` exposes typed receipts and `accept`, `claim_authority`, `begin_stage`, seven `complete_*` methods, `record_rejected`, `record_unresolved`, `status`, and `incomplete_lifecycles`.\n- VM `yinshi-runtime` runs the previously qualified wheel, not the latest local commits.\n- Production v2 journal is absent; accepted legacy v1 state intentionally blocks broker startup.\n- VM sockets are static and inactive; all related services and effect gates remain inactive/false.\n- `rft-sandbox` remains stopped.\n- Phase 7 plan remains `.pi-subagents/artifacts/8a18879f_planner_0_output.md`.\n- `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json` is stale and still describes the pre-coordinator milestone.\n- Full backend validation must use `/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/.venv/bin/pytest`.\n- Passing local and disabled-VM checks do not establish full Phase 6 acceptance.\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nThe user requested a supervisor decision for subagent run `c24c21c1`: either reauthorize TDD Guard or use the fallback of returning exact, unexecuted edit packets for a repository-deletion admission backstop.\n\n## Early Progress\n- Directed the subagent to use fallback option (b), avoid altering TDD Guard, and return complete edit packets with validation marked not run.\n- The subagent finished with acceptance rejected because the required criterion was unsatisfied, but produced a detailed implementation packet.\n- The assistant then implemented the packet directly:\n  - Added `RepositoryDeletionPendingError` and `require_no_repository_deletion(...)`.\n  - Added repository-deletion receipt checks to workspace deletion claims, execution reservations, checkout repair/publication, workspace creation, and managed thread integration.\n  - Mapped failures to existing stable 409/conflict boundaries.\n  - Added `backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py`.\n- Backend targeted tests passed: `9 passed`.\n- Also tightened sidecar query admission so every query requires an exact prepared execution receipt, and added a corresponding test.\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- Modified files include:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py`\n  - `sidecar/src/sidecar.js`\n  - `sidecar/tests/execution-admission.test.js`\n- The helper treats any receipt row, regardless of phase or malformed JSON content, as authoritative until removed.\n- Checks are placed inside the same SQLite transaction as durable admission writes and before conflicting filesystem/admission effects.\n- A targeted sidecar test command was running across execution-admission, isolation, orchestration, session-limit, and prompt-lifecycle suites; its output was lengthy and truncated in the prefix, so final status must be confirmed in the retained suffix.\n\n<read-files>\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/027713c4_planner_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/05bb63fe_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/0a089013_worker-expert_output.md