{"type":"message","id":"b10ff299","parentId":"3db44b24","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:04:12.657Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_MoI1W9evuPk1qjS8YyU1E24i|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa63cdb63a887d09d1720626f3e2ef7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[gh-router] GitHub URL routing extension loaded\nTask: You are reviving a previous subagent conversation.\nOriginal run: ce7af64b\nOriginal agent: final-review\nOriginal session file: /Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/ce7af64b/run-0/session.jsonl\nUse the stored session context as background. Answer the orchestrator's follow-up below. Do not assume the original child process is still alive.\nFollow-up:\nRestate your completed review verdict now. Do not use semicolons. Include each prior finding disposition, every remaining finding with location, impact, correction, and validation, and an explicit no-remediation statement only if no findings remain. Do not browse further and do not modify files.\n## Acceptance Contract\nAcceptance level: attested\nCompletion is not accepted from prose alone. End with a structured acceptance report.\nCriteria:\n- criterion-1: Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\nRequired evidence: review-findings, residual-risks\nFinish with a fenced JSON block tagged `acceptance-report` in this shape:\nUse empty arrays when no items apply; array fields contain strings unless object entries are shown.\n`criteriaSatisfied[].status` must be exactly one of: satisfied, not-satisfied, not-applicable.\n`commandsRun[].result` must be exactly one of: passed, failed, not-run.\n`manualNotes` and `notes` are optional strings; an empty string means no note and does not satisfy `manual-notes` evidence.\n```acceptance-report\n{\n  \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n      \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n      \"evidence\": \"specific proof\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    \"src/file.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [\n    \"test/file.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"commandsRun\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"command\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"short result\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validationOutput\": [\n    \"validation output or concise summary\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"none\"\n  ],\n  \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n  \"diffSummary\": \"short description of the diff\",\n  \"reviewFindings\": [\n    \"blocker: file.ts:12 - issue found, or no blockers\"\n  ],\n  \"manualNotes\": \"anything else the parent should know\"\n}\n```\n## Verdict\nChanges required. Four findings remain. Remediation is required.\nParent validation passed on final candidate, but it does not cover remaining crash and race paths.\n## Prior finding dispositions\n1. **Applying ambiguity after potential merge: Resolved**\n   - Locations: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:983-1048`, `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1389-1520`\n   - Durable `applying` state now precedes merge execution.\n   - Recovery uses `allow_apply=False`.\n   - Only exact trial tip is accepted as integrated. Other uncertain states remain unresolved.\n2. **Durable conflict cleanup before terminal state: Not resolved**\n   - Conflict facts are persisted before cleanup.\n   - Terminal `conflict` follows successful cleanup.\n   - Quarantine replay and cancellation remain unsafe. See findings 1 and 2.\n3. **No deletion of user-modified content: Partially resolved**\n   - Conflict snapshots include tracked, untracked, ignored, and late content.\n   - Conflict cleanup quarantines content instead of deleting it.\n   - Abort cleanup can still delete a late ignored file. See finding 3.\n4. **Exact deterministic trial commit identity: Resolved**\n   - Locations: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:928-1018`\n   - Validation reconstructs the exact commit from source author data, exact message bytes, fixed committer data, tree, and parent.\n   - `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py:439-486` rejects a custom same-tree commit.\n5. **Acquisition-time physical identity on every admission path: Resolved**\n   - Locations: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:333-370,513-524,628-636,808-815`\n   - Execute, status, abort, and terminal repair pass recorded physical identity into acquisition.\n   - `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_target_identity.py` covers identity forwarding and replacement refusal.\n## Remaining findings\n### 1. High: Quarantined conflict state cannot recover after a crash\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:747-781,800-874,1208-1287`\n`_quarantine_conflict_trial()` creates `quarantine` and `metadata-quarantine`. `_check_trial_root()` only permits `owner.json` and `worktree`.\nA crash after either rename, or after helper completion but before terminal persistence, leaves a valid quarantine state. Replay rejects that state as foreign ownership.\n**Impact:** Operation becomes permanently blocked. Admission marker remains. Durable retry contract fails despite preserved user content.\n**Correction:** Add explicit phase-aware validation for each quarantine crash state. Resume exact owned states and persist terminal status only after required directory syncs.\n**Remediation tier:** `worker-expert`\n**Validation:** Ad hoc current-code probe produced:\n- `quarantine_result=True`\n- Root contained `metadata-quarantine`, `owner.json`, and `quarantine`\n- Replay validation raised `ThreadGitOwnershipError`\nRequired checks must inject crashes after each rename, after sync, and before terminal database transition.\n### 2. High: Cancellation releases ownership while quarantine thread continues\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1271-1287`, `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:303-331,941-960`\n`asyncio.to_thread()` does not stop its worker when its awaiting task is cancelled. Cancellation unwinds repository locks and closes the live admission lease while quarantine mutation can continue.\n**Impact:** A retry can race with the abandoned worker. Two executions can inspect or rename the same trial state. One operation can publish a blocked result while prior cleanup still mutates storage.\n**Correction:** Shield and drain the quarantine worker inside all ownership scopes. Keep repository locks and admission ownership until worker completion is observed.\n**Remediation tier:** `worker-expert`\n**Validation:** Existing cancellation test raises before real threaded mutation. It does not cover cancellation while hashing or between quarantine renames.\nRequired checks must pause the helper during each stage, cancel the request, and prove retry cannot acquire ownership until the worker settles.\n### 3. High: Abort cleanup can delete a late ignored file\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1332-1363`\n`cleanup_integration_trial()` checks status with ignored files included. It then awaits reauthorization and calls `git worktree remove`.\nA late ignored file can appear after the status check. Git removes the worktree and silently deletes that file.\n**Impact:** User-created ignored bytes can be lost during abort. This violates the no-silent-deletion contract.\n**Correction:** Atomically quarantine the worktree before destructive cleanup. Revalidate all bytes after the move. Retain quarantine whenever content changed.\n**Remediation tier:** `worker-expert`\n**Validation:** Temporary Git probe reported:\n- `precheck_bytes=0`\n- `late_file_survived=no`\nRequired checks must inject ignored content between final precheck and removal.\n### 4. Medium: Successful integrations permanently retain trial artifacts\n**Location:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:1054-1065,720-729`\nSuccess transitions directly from `applying` to `integrated`. Only abort calls `cleanup_integration_trial()`.\n**Impact:** Every successful integration retains its private worktree, integration ref, manifest, and storage. Imported repositories receive permanent internal metadata growth.\n**Correction:** Add durable post-application cleanup. Recovery must preserve the committed integration result while completing or safely quarantining exact owned artifacts.\n**Remediation tier:** `worker-advanced`\n**Validation:** Caller inspection found no successful-path call to `cleanup_integration_trial()`.\nRequired checks must assert that success removes the registered worktree, integration ref, and owned manifest. Add crash recovery around each cleanup stage.\n## Validation assessment\nParent reports these final-candidate results:\n- 30 focused integration and recovery tests passed.\n- Ruff check passed.\n- Ruff format check passed.\n- Strict mypy passed for both service files.\nThese checks remain valid for covered behavior. They do not cover findings above.\nReview limit: Shared checkout contains many unrelated changes. Review covered managed-integration production code, tests, admission caller boundary, and current untracked file contents.\n```acceptance-report\n{\n  \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n      \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Four concrete findings include severity, exact file locations, impact, correction, worker tier, and required validation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    \"backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py\",\n    \"backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py\",\n    \"backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_admission.py\",\n    \"backend/tests/test_thread_integration.py\",\n    \"backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py\",\n    \"backend/tests/test_thread_integration_target_identity.py\"\n  ],\n  \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [\n    \"backend/tests/test_thread_integration.py\",\n    \"backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py\",\n    \"backend/tests/test_thread_integration_target_identity.py\"\n  ],\n  \"commandsRun\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"parent-attested focused integration and recovery suite\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"30 focused tests passed on the final candidate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"parent-attested Ruff check and format check\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Ruff and formatting checks passed on the final candidate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"parent-attested strict mypy for both service files\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Strict mypy passed for thread_integration.py and thread_workspaces.py.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"ad hoc Python quarantine replay probe\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Reproduced rejection of the valid post-quarantine root state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"temporary Git late ignored-file probe\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Reproduced deletion of ignored content added after the status precheck.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"git diff --check for scoped tracked files\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"No tracked whitespace errors were reported.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validationOutput\": [\n    \"Parent validation reports 30 focused tests passing.\",\n    \"Quarantine replay probe raised ThreadGitOwnershipError after successful quarantine.\",\n    \"Late ignored-file probe reported precheck_bytes=0 and late_file_survived=no.\",\n    \"Existing tests do not cover threaded cancellation, intermediate quarantine crash states, late ignored cleanup, or successful artifact cleanup.\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"Conflict cleanup cannot recover from valid intermediate or completed quarantine states.\",\n    \"Cancelled quarantine workers can outlive repository and admission ownership.\",\n    \"Abort cleanup can delete late ignored user content.\",\n    \"Successful integrations retain trial worktrees, refs, and manifests.\",\n    \"Unrelated shared-checkout changes were outside this review.\"\n  ],\n  \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n  \"diffSummary\": \"Remediation added applying-state recovery, conflict quarantine, deterministic commit validation, full conflict snapshots, and physical identity forwarding. Four lifecycle defects remain.\",\n  \"reviewFindings\": [\n    \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:747-781,800-874,1208-1287 - valid quarantine crash states fail replay validation\",\n    \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1271-1287 and backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:303-331,941-960 - cancelled threaded cleanup continues after ownership release\",\n    \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1332-1363 - abort cleanup can delete a late ignored file\",\n    \"medium: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:1054-1065,720-729 - successful integrations retain all trial artifacts\"\n  ],\n  \"manualNotes\": \"Completion remains blocked. Remediation and new crash-injection coverage are required.\"\n}\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789279452657}}
{"type":"message","id":"36d3ab1c","parentId":"b10ff299","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:04:46.719Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning durable cleanup architecture**\n\n**Refining quarantine retention and cleanup strategy**\n\n**Designing atomic root quarantine rename**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa63ce0886887d083c824c77def21fd\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning durable cleanup architecture**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Refining quarantine retention and cleanup strategy**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing atomic root quarantine rename**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4xlPjvuWiUocPtjbbjr2n3ex|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa63cf2dd2487d0a2a0883bedd33055","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"return await runs.run('integration_cleanup_remediation',{agent:'worker-expert',task:'Implement the four remaining managed-integration lifecycle findings from final review 627849c2 in the current shared checkout. You are sole writer. Read coding-practices and software-design skills. Do not modify TDD Guard or unrelated files. Preserve prior fixes and no SQLite handle across await/effect. Findings: (1) `_check_trial_root` rejects valid `quarantine` and `metadata-quarantine` crash states. Add explicit phase-aware exact-owner validation and resumable handling after either rename, sync, and before terminal persistence. (2) cancellation of `asyncio.to_thread` cleanup can release repository/admission ownership while worker continues. Shield and drain real threaded mutation while retaining ownership and make cancellation authoritative only after settlement. (3) abort cleanup can delete a late ignored file between status check and `git worktree remove`. Never destructively remove mutable worktree bytes. Atomically quarantine all bytes with no-replace semantics, revalidate after move, retain changed content, and safely retire only exact Git registration/ref metadata. (4) successful integrations currently retain active trial worktree/ref/manifest. Add durable post-application cleanup/recovery. Preserve committed integration outcome even if cleanup is pending or artifacts must be retained. Prefer unique retained quarantine names for bytes that cannot be safely deleted. Do not claim cleanup if active Git registration/ref remains. Add crash/cancellation tests at every quarantine phase, late ignored write, success active-artifact cleanup, and replay after cleanup before terminal database transition. Existing focused suite was 30 passing. Run focused tests, Ruff, format check, strict mypy. Do not commit. If exact safe metadata retirement is impossible without OS exclusivity, retain metadata and expose unresolved state rather than risking deletion or corrupting another worktree.'});","chatProgress":"live-card","context":"fresh","cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","async":false,"timeoutMs":2400000,"turnBudget":{"maxTurns":45,"graceTurns":6},"toolBudget":{"soft":150,"hard":220,"block":["bash","read","grep","find","ls"]},"artifacts":true,"outputMode":"inline","usageBudget":{"tokens":{"hard":260000}}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":2894,"output":937,"cacheRead":113792,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":457,"totalTokens":117623,"cost":{"input":0.014470000000000002,"output":0.02811,"cacheRead":0.056895999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.099476}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789279452663,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa63cdd31c487d0adca3a671efd6e74","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
