{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent_supervisor_request","content":"Subagent needs a supervisor decision.\nRun: 8b4b4a1d\nAgent: worker-advanced\nChild index: 0\nChild intercom target: subagent-worker-advanced-8b4b4a1d-1\n\nBLOCKED: TDD Guard blocks all test-file writes in my session. Every `edit` and `write` targeting backend/tests/*.py is rejected with \"TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.\" I have no /tdd or tdd_test tool to establish the binding, and I am instructed not to touch the guard. Repo-side .claude/tdd-guard/data/config.json actually says {\"guardEnabled\": false}, so this looks like a session-binding misconfiguration rather than an active enforcement cycle.\n\nWork is fully planned and validated by source reading: (1) parametrized abort-endpoint test (3 stages: worktree rename before sync, before metadata retirement rename, after metadata rename before final sync) proving a cancelled abort holds repository_lifecycle + admission lease (endpoint 409, service WorkspaceAdmissionError probe, repo-lock timeout probe) until the drained worker settles, then replay completes retirement exactly once; (2) parametrized applied-cleanup replay test (3 stages: crash after metadata retirement, after exact ref deletion, after retained-root movement) proving replay reaches integrated with exact ref/retained-root/HEAD/marker end state. No production changes needed.\n\nHow should I proceed? (a) bind/start a TDD request for my session branch so file writes pass the guard, (b) confirm the guard is non-enforcing for this run and authorize me to proceed writing test files (guard explicitly permitted one probe write to a non-test artifacts path, but blocks tests/src paths), or (c) another mechanism you prefer.\n\nReply with: subagent_supervisor({ action: \"reply\", replyTo: \"d0a6968b-937f-488e-8efc-42f6e3337898\", message: \"...\" })","display":true,"details":{"id":"d0a6968b-937f-488e-8efc-42f6e3337898","reason":"need_decision","expectsRe