{"type":"message","id":"77fe5b00","parentId":"31b16621","timestamp":"2026-09-13T07:24:13.281Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa64f9c0cc487d0a9040a7de0a045b0\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_iS06eQHkg4jRTtWMM0cG36fZ|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa64f9c927887d0beb0a32de4a044a4","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi-subagents/artifacts/8b4b4a1d_worker-advanced_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":1000}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":559,"output":56,"cacheRead":122752,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":123367,"cost":{"input":0.002795,"output":0.00168,"cacheRead":0.061376,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06585099999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789284249491,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa64f9a093887d0b9f3ae54aa170fa3","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"454e3024","parentId":"77fe5b00","timestamp":"2026-09-13T07:24:13.296Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_iS06eQHkg4jRTtWMM0cG36fZ|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa64f9c927887d0beb0a32de4a044a4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 25 assistant turns (soft limit 25, grace 4). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nThe supervisor directed: return complete exact unexecuted edit packets, mark validation not-run, change nothing. I have completed the full source analysis and drafted both tests against verified production behavior. Here is the final report with the exact packets.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe remaining validation gap from final review `89b5bde7` was two-fold: (1) no endpoint-level regression coverage that a cancelled abort cannot let a competing retry acquire repository/admission ownership while the real quarantine mutation is unsettled, and (2) no successful-cleanup replay coverage with faults after each metadata-retirement, exact-ref-deletion, and retained-root transition. I mapped the state machine from source (`cleanup_integration_trial`, `_run_threaded_mutation`, `_quarantine_trial_bytes`, `_retain_quarantined_trial`, `_record_applied_result`, `_complete_applied_cleanup`, `_finish_admission`, `acquire_workspace_admission`/`_claim`, `repository_lifecycle`) and drafted two parametrized endpoint/service tests using existing fixtures (`client`, `db`, `git_repo`, `prepared_child`, `_preview_and_payload`) and bounded primitives (`threading.Event`, `asyncio.timeout(0.2)`).\n\n**Blocker:** TDD Guard rejected every `edit`/`write` targeting `backend/tests/*.py` with \"TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch\"; I have no `/tdd` or `tdd_test` tooling to establish the binding and was instructed not to touch the guard. Per the supervisor's decision, the complete unexecuted edit packets follow. No files were changed (one guard-permitted probe write to `.pi-subagents/artifacts/` was created and removed; net zero).\n\n---\n\n## Packet 1 — `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_abort.py`\n\n**Edit 1A — replace module docstring + import block.** Exact old text (top of file):\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Abort quarantines owned trial bytes before retiring exact Git metadata.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport httpx\nimport pytest\n\nfrom tests.test_thread_integration_git_safety import git\nfrom tests.test_thread_result_seal import _orchestration_request\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\nfrom yinshi.services import thread_workspaces\nfrom yinshi.services.git import GitError\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_orchestration import ThreadOrchestrationService\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_workspaces import ThreadWorkspaceService\n```\n\nExact new text:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Abort quarantines owned trial bytes before retiring exact Git metadata.\n\nCancellation coverage additionally proves that a cancelled abort keeps repository\nand admission ownership until the real threaded quarantine mutation settles, and\nthat a later replay completes the retirement exactly once.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport threading\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport httpx\nimport pytest\n\nfrom tests.test_thread_integration_git_safety import git\nfrom tests.test_thread_result_seal import _orchestration_request\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\nfrom yinshi.services import thread_workspaces\nfrom yinshi.services.git import GitError\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import repository_lifecycle\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_orchestration import ThreadOrchestrationService\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_workspaces import ThreadWorkspaceService\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_admission import WorkspaceAdmissionError\n```\n\n**Edit 1B — append after the final line of the file** (anchor: the unique last line `    assert git(git_repo, \"for-each-ref\", \"--format=%(refname)\", intent[\"ref\"]) == \"\"` of `test_abort_quarantines_late_ignored_file_before_metadata_retirement`), appending:\n\n```python\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"pause_stage\",\n    [\"worktree_rename_sync_pending\", \"metadata_rename_pending\", \"final_sync_pending\"],\n)\nasync def test_cancelled_abort_blocks_competing_retry_until_quarantine_worker_settles(\n    client, db, git_repo, monkeypatch, prepared_child, pause_stage\n):\n    \"\"\"A cancelled abort holds repository and admission ownership until the worker settles.\n\n    The real quarantine mutation pauses after a meaningful durable transition, the\n    request task is cancelled into the paused handler, and a competing retry must\n    fail to acquire ownership while the worker is still unsettled. Releasing the\n    worker lets the handler drain it, and a replay finishes the retirement once.\n    \"\"\"\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"THREAD_MANAGED_INTEGRATION_ENABLED\", \"true\")\n    get_settings.cache_clear()\n    await ThreadOrchestrationService().seal_result(\n        _orchestration_request(), child_session_id=\"child-session\"\n    )\n    real_git = thread_workspaces._run_git\n    crashed = False\n\n    async def interrupt_after_trial_creation(arguments, *args, **kwargs):\n        nonlocal crashed\n        result = await real_git(arguments, *args, **kwargs)\n        if (\n            not crashed\n            and \"worktree\" in arguments\n            and \"add\" in arguments\n            and \"--detach\" in arguments\n        ):\n            crashed = True\n            raise GitError(\"Fixture crashed after creating its recorded trial\")\n        return result\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(thread_workspaces, \"_run_git\", interrupt_after_trial_creation)\n    base = \"/api/threads/parent-session/children/child-session\"\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient(\n        transport=httpx.ASGITransport(app=client.app, raise_app_exceptions=False),\n        base_url=\"http://testserver\",\n    ) as http:\n        preview = (await http.get(f\"{base}/integrate\")).json()\n        payload = {\n            \"idempotency_key\": str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            \"result_id\": preview[\"result_id\"],\n            \"expected_parent_head\": preview[\"expected_parent_head\"],\n            \"confirmed\": True,\n        }\n        assert (await http.post(f\"{base}/integrate\", json=payload)).status_code == 500\n        operation = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()\n        assert operation[\"status\"] == \"checking\"\n        intent = json.loads(operation[\"trials_json\"])[0]\n        before = dict(operation)\n        trial_root = Path(intent[\"path\"]).parent\n        monkeypatch.setattr(thread_workspaces, \"_run_git\", real_git)\n\n        worker_paused = threading.Event()\n        release = threading.Event()\n        completed_syncs = 0\n        real_sync = ThreadWorkspaceService._sync_directories\n        real_rename = ThreadWorkspaceService._rename_no_replace\n\n        def pausing_sync(*directories):\n            nonlocal completed_syncs\n            hit = (\n                directories[0] == trial_root\n                and not worker_paused.is_set()\n                and (\n                    (pause_stage == \"worktree_rename_sync_pending\" and len(directories) == 1)\n                    or (pause_stage == \"final_sync_pending\" and len(directories) == 2)\n                )\n            )\n            if hit:\n                worker_paused.set()\n                assert release.wait(timeout=10)\n            real_sync(*directories)\n            completed_syncs += 1\n\n        def pausing_rename(source, target):\n            hit = (\n                pause_stage == \"metadata_rename_pending\"\n                and Path(target).name == \"metadata-quarantine\"\n                and not worker_paused.is_set()\n            )\n            if hit:\n                worker_paused.set()\n                assert release.wait(timeout=10)\n            real_rename(source, target)\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(\n            ThreadWorkspaceService, \"_sync_directories\", staticmethod(pausing_sync)\n        )\n        monkeypatch.setattr(\n            ThreadWorkspaceService, \"_rename_no_replace\", staticmethod(pausing_rename)\n        )\n\n        endpoint = f\"{base}/integrations/{operation['id']}/abort\"\n        cancelled_abort = asyncio.create_task(http.post(endpoint))\n        assert await asyncio.to_thread(worker_paused.wait, 10)\n        cancelled_abort.cancel()\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.05)\n        assert not cancelled_abort.done()\n\n        manifest = {key: intent[key] for key in (\"id\", \"operation_id\", \"authority_hash\")}\n        allowed = frozenset({\"manifest\", \"active\", \"quarantine\", \"metadata-quarantine\"})\n        phase = ThreadWorkspaceService._check_trial_root(\n            trial_root, manifest, allowed_phases=allowed\n        )\n        pointer = Path(\n            (trial_root / \"quarantine\" / \".git\")\n            .read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            .strip()\n            .removeprefix(\"gitdir: \")\n        )\n        if pause_stage == \"worktree_rename_sync_pending\":\n            assert phase == \"quarantine\"\n            assert completed_syncs == 0\n            assert pointer.is_dir()\n        elif pause_stage == \"metadata_rename_pending\":\n            assert phase == \"quarantine\"\n            assert completed_syncs == 1\n            assert pointer.is_dir()\n        else:\n            assert phase == \"metadata-quarantine\"\n            assert completed_syncs == 1\n            assert not pointer.exists()\n\n        delegation_id = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT id FROM thread_delegations WHERE parent_session_id = 'parent-session'\"\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n        parent_workspace_id = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT workspace_id FROM sessions WHERE id = 'parent-session'\"\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n        context = ThreadWorkspaceService().load_parent_context(\n            db,\n            None,\n            parent_workspace_id=str(parent_workspace_id),\n            delegation_id=str(delegation_id),\n        )\n\n        async def repository_lock_is_unavailable() -> bool:\n            try:\n                async with asyncio.timeout(0.2):\n                    async with repository_lifecycle(context.repo_id, context.lock_root):\n                        return False\n            except TimeoutError:\n                return True\n\n        assert await repository_lock_is_unavailable()\n        with pytest.raises(WorkspaceAdmissionError):\n            await ThreadWorkspaceService().acquire_workspace_admission(\n                repo_path=git_repo,\n                workspace_path=git_repo,\n                authority_hash=str(operation[\"authority_hash\"]),\n                operation_id=str(operation[\"id\"]),\n                kind=\"integration\",\n                resume=True,\n                physical_identity=str(operation[\"physical_workspace_json\"]),\n            )\n        competing = await http.post(endpoint)\n        assert competing.status_code == 409\n        assert (\n            competing.json()[\"detail\"]\n            == \"Integration is still active or ownership is unavailable\"\n        )\n        assert dict(db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()) == before\n        marker_directory = Path(git_repo) / \".git\" / \".yinshi-workspace-admission-v1\"\n        assert len(list(marker_directory.glob(\"*.json\"))) == 1\n\n        release.set()\n        with pytest.raises(asyncio.CancelledError):\n            await cancelled_abort\n        assert (\n            ThreadWorkspaceService._check_trial_root(trial_root, manifest, allowed_phases=allowed)\n            == \"metadata-quarantine\"\n        )\n        monkeypatch.setattr(ThreadWorkspaceService, \"_sync_directories\", staticmethod(real_sync))\n        monkeypatch.setattr(\n            ThreadWorkspaceService, \"_rename_no_replace\", staticmethod(real_rename)\n        )\n        replay = await http.post(endpoint)\n\n    assert replay.status_code == 200, replay.text\n    assert replay.json()[\"status\"] == \"aborted\"\n    final = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()\n    assert final[\"status\"] == \"aborted\"\n    assert final[\"reason_code\"] == \"aborted_by_user\"\n    retained = Path(git_repo) / \".git\" / \".yinshi-integration-retained-v1\" / intent[\"id\"]\n    assert (retained / \"quarantine\").is_dir()\n    assert (retained / \"metadata-quarantine\").is_dir()\n    assert not trial_root.exists()\n    assert git(git_repo, \"for-each-ref\", \"--format=%(refname)\", intent[\"ref\"]) == \"\"\n    assert intent[\"path\"] not in git(git_repo, \"worktree\", \"list\", \"--porcelain\")\n    assert git(git_repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") == preview[\"expected_parent_head\"]\n    assert not list((Path(git_repo) / \".git\" / \".yinshi-workspace-admission-v1\").glob(\"*.json\"))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Packet 2 — `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py`\n\nNo import changes needed (`asyncio`, `json`, `threading`, `Path`, `httpx`, `pytest`, `run_git`, `_preview_and_payload`, `get_settings`, `thread_workspaces`, `ThreadWorkspaceService` are all already imported). **Edit 2A — append after the final two lines of the file** (unique anchor: `    assert run_git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\", cwd=git_repo) == head` followed by `    assert not list(marker_directory.glob(\"*.json\"))` at the end of `test_cancelled_terminal_commit_releases_marker_and_replay_repairs_exact_owner`), appending:\n\n```python\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"stage\", [\"metadata_retired\", \"ref_deleted\", \"retained_moved\"])\nasync def test_applied_cleanup_replay_completes_each_retirement_transition(\n    client, db, git_repo, monkeypatch, prepared_child, stage\n):\n    \"\"\"Replay retires metadata, the exact ref, and retained roots after each crash point.\n\n    The successful apply path is interrupted after one durable retirement\n    transition inside the applied cleanup. A replay must finish the remaining\n    transitions exactly once and persist the terminal integrated outcome.\n    \"\"\"\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"THREAD_MANAGED_INTEGRATION_ENABLED\", \"true\")\n    get_settings.cache_clear()\n    real_git = thread_workspaces._run_git\n    real_rename = ThreadWorkspaceService._rename_no_replace\n    crashed = False\n\n    async def crash_after_ref_deletion(arguments, *args, **kwargs):\n        nonlocal crashed\n        result = await real_git(arguments, *args, **kwargs)\n        if (\n            not crashed\n            and stage == \"ref_deleted\"\n            and \"update-ref\" in arguments\n            and \"-d\" in arguments\n            and any(value.startswith(\"refs/yinshi/integrations/\") for value in arguments)\n        ):\n            crashed = True\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Fixture crashed after exact ref deletion\")\n        return result\n\n    def crash_after_rename(source, target):\n        nonlocal crashed\n        real_rename(source, target)\n        target_path = Path(target)\n        hit = (\n            stage == \"metadata_retired\" and target_path.name == \"metadata-quarantine\"\n        ) or (\n            stage == \"retained_moved\"\n            and target_path.parent.name == \".yinshi-integration-retained-v1\"\n        )\n        if hit and not crashed:\n            crashed = True\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Fixture crashed after {stage}\")\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(thread_workspaces, \"_run_git\", crash_after_ref_deletion)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        ThreadWorkspaceService, \"_rename_no_replace\", staticmethod(crash_after_rename)\n    )\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient(\n        transport=httpx.ASGITransport(app=client.app, raise_app_exceptions=False),\n        base_url=\"http://testserver\",\n    ) as http:\n        endpoint, payload = await _preview_and_payload(http)\n        assert (await http.post(endpoint, json=payload)).status_code == 500\n        operation = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()\n        intent = json.loads(operation[\"trials_json\"])[0]\n        trial_root = Path(intent[\"path\"]).parent\n        retained = Path(git_repo) / \".git\" / \".yinshi-integration-retained-v1\" / intent[\"id\"]\n        marker_directory = Path(git_repo) / \".git\" / \".yinshi-workspace-admission-v1\"\n        assert operation[\"status\"] == \"applying\"\n        assert operation[\"reason_code\"] == \"trial_cleanup_pending\"\n        assert operation[\"resulting_parent_head\"] == operation[\"trial_commit\"]\n        assert run_git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\", cwd=git_repo) == operation[\"trial_commit\"]\n        ref_value = run_git(\"for-each-ref\", \"--format=%(objectname)\", intent[\"ref\"], cwd=git_repo)\n        if stage == \"metadata_retired\":\n            assert ref_value == operation[\"trial_commit\"]\n            assert sorted(entry.name for entry in trial_root.iterdir()) == [\n                \"metadata-quarantine\",\n                \"owner.json\",\n                \"quarantine\",\n            ]\n            assert not retained.exists()\n        elif stage == \"ref_deleted\":\n            assert ref_value == \"\"\n            assert sorted(entry.name for entry in trial_root.iterdir()) == [\n                \"metadata-quarantine\",\n                \"owner.json\",\n                \"quarantine\",\n            ]\n            assert not retained.exists()\n        else:\n            assert ref_value == \"\"\n            assert not trial_root.exists()\n            assert sorted(entry.name for entry in retained.iterdir()) == [\n                \"metadata-quarantine\",\n                \"owner.json\",\n                \"quarantine\",\n            ]\n        assert len(list(marker_directory.glob(\"*.json\"))) == 1\n        monkeypatch.setattr(thread_workspaces, \"_run_git\", real_git)\n        monkeypatch.setattr(\n            ThreadWorkspaceService, \"_rename_no_replace\", staticmethod(real_rename)\n        )\n        replay = await http.post(endpoint, json=payload)\n\n    assert replay.status_code == 200, replay.text\n    assert replay.json()[\"status\"] == \"integrated\"\n    assert replay.json()[\"resulting_parent_head\"] == operation[\"trial_commit\"]\n    completed = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()\n    assert completed[\"status\"] == \"integrated\"\n    assert completed[\"resulting_parent_head\"] == completed[\"trial_commit\"]\n    assert json.loads(completed[\"trials_json\"]) == json.loads(operation[\"trials_json\"])\n    assert run_git(\"for-each-ref\", \"--format=%(refname)\", intent[\"ref\"], cwd=git_repo) == \"\"\n    assert not trial_root.exists()\n    assert (retained / \"owner.json\").is_file()\n    assert (retained / \"quarantine\").is_dir()\n    assert (retained / \"metadata-quarantine\").is_dir()\n    assert (\n        run_git(\n            \"rev-list\",\n            \"--count\",\n            f\"{payload['expected_parent_head']}..HEAD\",\n            cwd=git_repo,\n        )\n        == \"1\"\n    )\n    assert not list(marker_directory.glob(\"*.json\"))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Design rationale (verified against source, not assumed)\n\n- **Cancellation exclusion (Packet 1):** `_run_threaded_mutation` shields and drains the `asyncio.to_thread` worker before re-raising `CancelledError`; the abort endpoint's `finally: _finish_admission` runs only after the drain, and for nonterminal `checking` it calls `lease.close()` (keeps the durable marker, drops the `.live` flock). While the worker is paused, the lease flock makes a competing `_claim` fail with `BlockingIOError → WorkspaceAdmissionError → 409`, the handler still holds `repository_lifecycle(context.repo_id, context.lock_root)` (probed with a 0.2s timeout), and the service-level `acquire_workspace_admission(resume=True)` probe fails identically. If the drain were broken, the lease would close mid-mutation and the probes would acquire — the test genuinely discriminates. Stages pin: worktree rename before first sync (`completed_syncs == 0`), after first sync before metadata retirement rename, and after metadata rename before final sync (`_check_trial_root` phase `metadata-quarantine`, original metadata path gone). Replay then completes retirement exactly once (`aborted_by_user`, retained layout, ref absent, HEAD untouched, no markers).\n- **Applied-cleanup replay (Packet 2):** `_record_applied_result` durably records `resulting_parent_head` + `reason_code=\"trial_cleanup_pending\"` before cleanup; a crash after the metadata retirement rename, after the exact `update-ref --no-deref -d` (matcher includes the `refs/yinshi/integrations/` prefix; the only `-d` on that flow), or after the retained-root rename leaves `status=\"applying\"`, ref/retained/metadata state exactly as asserted, and the marker retained (nonterminal close). Replay resumes via `_execute`'s `applying + resulting_parent_head` branch → `_complete_applied_cleanup` → idempotent quarantine → ref deletion only if still present → retain → terminal `integrated`, with `rev-list --count == 1` and no surviving marker."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789284253296}}
