 perform checkout, remote, Git, and filesystem work using an open SQLite connection.\n\nThe workspace `INSERT` starts only after those effects. The deletion verdict and admission write therefore lack one transaction.\n\nImpact: A stale verdict can permit workspace admission after deletion ownership appears. Normal creation also crosses awaits with an open SQLite handle.\n\nCorrection:\n\n- Keep repository lifecycle lock across admission.\n- Run a short pre-effect database callback that authorizes and checks deletion ownership.\n- Close its connection before external work.\n- Run final authorization, deletion check, and workspace `INSERT` inside one `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n- Quarantine or remove created worktree when final admission fails.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`. This fix combines transaction ownership, lifecycle locking, and effect cleanup.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Assert helper sees `db.in_transaction` during final admission.\n- Assert no connection remains open during mocked Git awaits.\n- Race repository deletion against creation.\n- Assert failed final admission leaves no published worktree.\n\n### 2. High: Execution performs checkout and Git work before deletion gate\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:1755-1766`  \nAtomic gate: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:354-402`\n\n`acquire_prompt_workspace()` runs checkout recovery, reads physical identity, and retries stopped receipts before `reserve()` checks `repository_deletions`.\n\nImpact: A durable deletion row can coexist with checkout recovery or Git effects. Final reservation fails, but required pre-effect exclusion is already lost.\n\nCorrection: Add a short pre-effect check under repository lifecycle serialization. Retain the transactional check inside `reserve()`. Refactor nested lock use without retaining database connections.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Insert each receipt phase before public execution acquisition.\n- Spy on checkout recovery, identity reads, marker cleanup, and runtime calls.\n- Assert none execute when receipt exists.\n- Add a deletion-versus-execution concurrency test.\n\n### 3. High: Checkout publication gate is late and has a bypass path\n\nLocations:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1034-1038`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:2218-2265`\n\n`validate_local_repo()` runs before `_begin_repair()` checks deletion ownership. The trusted-path branch at lines 2240-2245 returns through `_prepare_trusted_checkout()` without reaching that check.\n\nImpact: Existing receipts can permit Git validation or trusted checkout refresh. Trusted metadata updates also lack a deletion check in their write transaction.\n\nCorrection:\n\n- Run an authorized pre-effect deletion check before Git validation.\n- Preserve the existing atomic check before repair receipt insertion.\n- Gate trusted-path metadata writes in their own `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n- Keep exact-owner continuation behavior required by the approved plan.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Cover publication and trusted-path branches.\n- Spy on `validate_local_repo()` and `_prepare_trusted_checkout()`.\n- Assert no Git or filesystem call occurs with any receipt row.\n- Verify metadata writes and deletion checks share one transaction.\n\n### 4. High: Managed integration performs Git work before admission check\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:401-446`  \nGit implementation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:631-638`\n\nNew integration calls `preview()` and `integration_workspace_identity()` before the transactional deletion check. Identity collection executes Git commands.\n\nImpact: Durable deletion ownership does not block all managed integration Git effects. Current test only checks final HEAD and receipt absence.\n\nCorrection: After exact-owner lookup identifies a new operation, acquire lifecycle serialization. Run a short deletion preflight before preview and identity capture. Retain the final transactional check before insertion.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Spy on preview and identity methods.\n- Assert neither runs while a receipt exists.\n- Race repository deletion against new integration admission.\n- Preserve exact-owner continuation behavior.\n\n### 5. Medium: Publication conflicts do not consistently map to HTTP 409\n\nLocations:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1034-1038`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspace_files.py:188-202`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/terminal_channels.py:129-139`\n\nDeletion ownership becomes a broad `WorkspacePublicationError`. File endpoints map that error to 500. Terminal channel setup maps it to 503.\n\nImpact: Identical admission conflict produces different public status codes. This violates stable conflict mapping.\n\nCorrection: Introduce a distinct publication admission-conflict subtype. Map that subtype to generic HTTP 409 at every HTTP boundary. Keep infrastructure publication failures mapped separately.\n\nRemediation: `worker`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Exercise file mutation preparation with a deletion receipt.\n- Exercise terminal channel preparation with a deletion receipt.\n- Assert HTTP 409 with stable generic details.\n- Retain existing mappings for infrastructure failures.\n\n## Verified behavior\n\n- Helper query blocks any row without parsing phase or receipt content.\n- Workspace deletion checks inside `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` before claim writes.\n- Final execution, repair, and integration receipt writes retain transactional checks.\n- Repository deletion recovery does not call the helper.\n- No staged files existed during review.\n\n## Validation status\n\nParent reported `9 tests passed` for focused backend tests. Exact command was unavailable. Existing tests do not cover public pre-effect ordering, connection lifetime, races, or all HTTP mappings.\n\nRequired after fixes:\n\n- Focused repository-deletion admission tests\n- New effect-spy and concurrency tests listed above\n- Ruff for changed source and tests\n- Strict mypy for changed source\n\nInspection limit: Repository contains a much larger unstaged and untracked change set. Review excluded unrelated changes as requested.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789284931400,"runId":"62c2fe5c","agent":"final-review","index":0,"message":"final-review is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":23,"tokens":153745,"toolCount":75,"elapsedMs":240289}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":155760,"output":18454,"cacheRead":1359872,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":2.012356,"turns":25}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/62c2fe5c/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Five concrete findings include severity, exact paths, impact, corrections, worker tiers, and required checks."}],"changedFiles":["backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py","backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py","backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py"],"testsAddedOrUpdated":["backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py"],"commandsRun":[{"command":"git status --short && git diff --stat && git diff --cached --stat","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected current working tree and confirmed no staged files."},{"command":"git diff -- backend/src/yinshi/services/repository_lifecycle.py backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_deletion.py backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py","result":"passed","summary":"Inspected narrow current candidate diff and affected implementation."},{"command":"cd backend && ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py","result":"not-run","summary":"Parent reported 9 tests passed. Review did not repeat the fresh focused result."}],"validationOutput":["Parent-reported focused backend result: 9 tests passed.","Source inspection confirmed phase-agnostic helper behavior and atomic checks at four receipt-writing sites.","Source inspection also confirmed late effect ordering, one checkout bypass, one connection-lifetime violation, and inconsistent HTTP mappings."],"residualRisks":["Workspace creation does not share one transaction between deletion check and admission write.","Execution, checkout publication, and managed integration can perform external work before the deletion check.","Checkout trusted-path flow bypasses the repair gate.","Some checkout conflict callers return HTTP 500 or 503 instead of 409.","Existing focused tests omit public effect ordering, races, connection lifetime, and boundary mapping."],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"Candidate adds a phase-agnostic deletion helper, wires five admission sites, adds workspace creation mapping, and adds focused tests. Several public workflows still gate too late.","reviewFindings":["high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py:563-597 - workspace creation check is outside the admission transaction and an SQLite handle crosses awaits and effects","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:1755-1766 - checkout recovery and Git identity work occur before execution reservation checks deletion ownership","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:2218-2265 - Git work precedes the gate and trusted checkout preparation bypasses it","high: backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:401-446 - preview and Git identity capture occur before integration checks deletion ownership","medium: backend/src/yinshi/api/workspace_files.py:188-202 and backend/src/yinshi/api/terminal_channels.py:129-139 - publication admission conflict maps to HTTP 500 or 503 instead of 409"],"manualNotes":"All findings remain unresolved and block completion. Use worker-advanced for ordering and transaction fixes. Use worker for settled HTTP mapping changes."}},"toolCalls":[{"text":"read ~/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md","expandedText":"read ~/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md"},{"text":"read ~/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/references/red-flags.md","expandedText":"read ~/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/references/red-flags.md"},{"text":"$ git status --short && printf '\\n--- DIFF STAT ---\\n' && git ...","expandedText":"$ git status --short && printf '\\n--- DIFF STAT ---\\n' && git diff --stat && printf '\\n--- STAGED DIFF STAT ---\\n' && git diff --cached --stat"},{"text":"ls {\"path\":\".\"}","expandedText":"ls {\"path\":\".\"}"},{"text":"grep {\"pattern\