s and competing..."},{"text":"$ shasum -a 256 backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces....","expandedText":"$ shasum -a 256 backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py backend/tests/test_thread_integration_abort.py backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py; git status --porcelain=v1 | a..."},{"text":"$ git diff --stat -- backend/src/yinshi/api/threads.py backend...","expandedText":"$ git diff --stat -- backend/src/yinshi/api/threads.py backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py; printf '\\nuntracked managed-integration files:\\n'; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard 'backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integrati..."},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/api/threads.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/api/threads.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py"}]}],"totalChildUsage":{"input":332668,"output":33545,"cacheRead":2301824,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":3.820602,"turns":41},"totalCost":{"inputTokens":332668,"outputTokens":33545,"costUsd":3.820602},"usageBudget":{"version":1,"source":"reported","tokens":{"hard":240000,"used":366213,"outcome":"hard-exceeded"},"exhausted":true,"reason":"tokens"},"workflow":{"value":[{"key":"deletion_review","ok":true,"runId":"62c2fe5c","output":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 22 assistant turns (soft limit 22, grace 4). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\n## Review outcome\n\nBlocked. Five findings remain. Remediation needed.\n\n### 1. High: Workspace creation violates transaction and connection-lifetime guarantees\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py:563-597`  \nCaller: `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py:140-151`\n\n`require_no_repository_deletion()` runs without `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`. Later awaits perform checkout, remote, Git, and filesystem work using an open SQLite connection.\n\nThe workspace `INSERT` starts only after those effects. The deletion verdict and admission write therefore lack one transaction.\n\nImpact: A stale verdict can permit workspace admission after deletion ownership appears. Normal creation also crosses awaits with an open SQLite handle.\n\nCorrection:\n\n- Keep repository lifecycle lock across admission.\n- Run a short pre-effect database callback that authorizes and checks deletion ownership.\n- Close its connection before external work.\n- Run final authorization, deletion check, and workspace `INSERT` inside one `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n- Quarantine or remove created worktree when final admission fails.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`. This fix combines transaction ownership, lifecycle locking, and effect cleanup.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Assert helper sees `db.in_transaction` during final admission.\n- Assert no connection remains open during mocked Git awaits.\n- Race repository deletion against creation.\n- Assert failed final admission leaves no published worktree.\n\n### 2. High: Execution performs checkout and Git work before deletion gate\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:1755-1766`  \nAtomic gate: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:354-402`\n\n`acquire_prompt_workspace()` runs checkout recovery, reads physical identity, and retries stopped receipts before `reserve()` checks `repository_deletions`.\n\nImpact: A durable deletion row can coexist with checkout recovery or Git effects. Final reservation fails, but required pre-effect exclusion is already lost.\n\nCorrection: Add a short pre-effect check under repository lifecycle serialization. Retain the transactional check inside `reserve()`. Refactor nested lock use without retaining database connections.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Insert each receipt phase before public execution acquisition.\n- Spy on checkout recovery, identity reads, marker cleanup, and runtime calls.\n- Assert none execute when receipt exists.\n- Add a deletion-versus-execution concurrency test.\n\n### 3. High: Checkout publication gate is late and has a bypass path\n\nLocations:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1034-1038`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:2218-2265`\n\n`validate_local_repo()` runs before `_begin_repair()` checks deletion ownership. The trusted-path branch at lines 2240-2245 returns through `_prepare_trusted_checkout()` without reaching that check.\n\nImpact: Existing receipts can permit Git validation or trusted checkout refresh. Trusted metadata updates also lack a deletion check in their write transaction.\n\nCorrection:\n\n- Run an authorized pre-effect deletion check before Git validation.\n- Preserve the existing atomic check before repair receipt insertion.\n- Gate trusted-path metadata writes in their own `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n- Keep exact-owner continuation behavior required by the approved plan.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Cover publication and trusted-path branches.\n- Spy on `validate_local_repo()` and `_prepare_trusted_checkout()`.\n- Assert no Git or filesystem call occurs with any receipt row.\n- Verify metadata writes and deletion checks share one transaction.\n\n### 4. High: Managed integration performs Git work before admission check\n\nLocation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py:401-446`  \nGit implementation: `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:631-638`\n\nNew integration calls `preview()` and `integration_workspace_identity()` before the transactional deletion check. Identity collection executes Git commands.\n\nImpact: Durable deletion ownership does not block all managed integration Git effects. Current test only checks final HEAD and receipt absence.\n\nCorrection: After exact-owner lookup identifies a new operation, acquire lifecycle serialization. Run a short deletion preflight before preview and identity capture. Retain the final transactional check before insertion.\n\nRemediation: `worker-advanced`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Spy on preview and identity methods.\n- Assert neither runs while a receipt exists.\n- Race repository deletion against new integration admission.\n- Preserve exact-owner continuation behavior.\n\n### 5. Medium: Publication conflicts do not consistently map to HTTP 409\n\nLocations:\n\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1034-1038`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspace_files.py:188-202`\n- `backend/src/yinshi/api/terminal_channels.py:129-139`\n\nDeletion ownership becomes a broad `WorkspacePublicationError`. File endpoints map that error to 500. Terminal channel setup maps it to 503.\n\nImpact: Identical admission conflict produces different public status codes. This violates stable conflict mapping.\n\nCorrection: Introduce a distinct publication admission-conflict subtype. Map that subtype to generic HTTP 409 at every HTTP boundary. Keep infrastructure publication failures mapped separately.\n\nRemediation: `worker`.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n- Exercise file mutation preparation with a deletion receipt.\n- Exercise terminal channel preparation with a deletion receipt.\n- Assert HTTP 409 with stable generic details.\n- Retain existing mappings for infrastructure failures.\n\n## Verified behavior\n\n- Helper query blocks any row without parsing phase or receipt content.\n- Workspace deletion checks inside `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` before claim writes.\n- Final execution, repair, and integration receipt writes retain transactional checks.\n- Repository deletion recovery does not call the helper.\n- No staged files existed during review.\n\n## Validation status\n\nParent reported `9 tests passed` for focused backend tests. Exact command was unavailable. Existing tests do not cover public pre-effect ordering, connection lifetime, races, or all HTTP mappings.\n\nRequired after fixes:\n\n- Focused repository-deletion admission tests\n- New effect-spy and concurrency tests listed above\n- Ruff for changed source and tests\n- Strict mypy for changed source\n\nInspection limit: Repository contains a much larger unstaged and untracked change set. Review excluded unrelated changes as requested.","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/62c2fe5c/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"final-review","task":"Review only the current repository-deletion admission backstop. Read software-design skill and red-flags, actual current files/diff, helper and every caller/test. Requirements: any durable repository_deletions row, regardless phase or malformed receipt, blocks workspace creation, workspace deletion claims, execution reservation, checkout repair/publication, and managed integration before filesystem/runtime/Git effects. Checks must occur inside the same transaction before admission writes. Error mapping remains stable conflict/409. No SQLite handle crosses await/effect. Parent focused backend result: 9 tests passed. Do not modify. Return findings with locations/impact/correction/checks, or explicit no remediation needed. Avoid semicolons.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"final-review","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"f81a48536aea65d5390f0cb7f0987d863267dd3a2a324f8c7753db9d958ab820","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"conf