{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent-notify","content":"Background task completed: **worker-advanced**\n\nworker-advanced:\n## Complete unexecuted edit packets — five repository-deletion admission findings (review 62c2fe5c)\n\nPer the supervisor ruling I changed nothing. Everything below is verified against the actual working tree during my analysis. All old-text anchors were read verbatim from the current files. Apply packets in order because later packets reference the `WorkspacePublicationConflictError` type defined in Packet 1. Validation status for every packet: not run.\n\nBaseline observed before any edit: the existing focused suite has 9 tests. `test_receipt_blocks_managed_integration_admission` is intermittently order-dependent in full-file runs (the result-seal GET intermittently returns 404). It passes alone and in `-p no:cacheprovider` runs. This is pre-existing and unrelated to these findings.\n\n---\n\n### PACKET 1 — Finding 5 (Medium): distinct publication deletion-conflict type and stable 409 mapping\n\n**1a. `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py` — define the subtype**\n\nAnchor (unique):\n```python\nclass WorkspacePublicationCollisionError(WorkspacePublicationError):\n    \"\"\"Another filesystem object won the final publication name.\"\"\"\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nclass WorkspacePublicationCollisionError(WorkspacePublicationError):\n    \"\"\"Another filesystem object won the final publication name.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass WorkspacePublicationConflictError(WorkspacePublicationError):\n    \"\"\"Publication admission conflicts with another durable owner.\"\"\"\n```\n\n**1b. Same file — raise the subtype for the deletion conflict in the atomic repair admission**\n\nAnchor (unique, inside `_begin_repair_locked`):\n```python\n    try:\n        require_no_repository_deletion(database, expected.repo_id)\n    except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as error:\n        raise WorkspacePublicationError(\n            \"Checkout repair conflicts with repository deletion\"\n        ) from error\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    try:\n        require_no_repository_deletion(database, expected.repo_id)\n    except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as error:\n        raise WorkspacePublicationConflictError(\n            \"Checkout repair conflicts with repository deletion\"\n        ) from error\n```\nNote: `WorkspacePublicationError` remains used elsewhere in the module so its import stays. The existing focused test matches `WorkspacePublicationError` by isinstance and still passes because the new type is a subclass.\n\n**1c. `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspace_files.py` — import and map to 409**\n\nImport edit (unverified anchor: add one line to the existing `yinshi.services` import group, alphabetically ordered so `ruff`/isort stays clean):\n```python\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_publication import WorkspacePublicationConflictError\n```\nFunction edit — anchor (unique, all of `_map_file_error`):\n```python\n    if isinstance(exc, IsolationGateError):\n        return HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=str(exc))\n    return HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Workspace file operation failed\")\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    if isinstance(exc, IsolationGateError):\n        return HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=str(exc))\n    if isinstance(exc, WorkspacePublicationConflictError):\n        return HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=\"Workspace publication conflict\")\n    return HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Workspace file operation failed\")\n```\nThe broad `WorkspacePublicationError` still falls through to 500, so infrastructure publication failures keep their existing mapping.\n\n**1d. `backend/src/yinshi/api/terminal_channels.py` — map the subtype to 409 before the 503 tuple**\n\nImport edit: the module already imports `WorkspacePublicationError` from `yinshi.services.workspace_publication`. Add `WorkspacePublicationConflictError` to that same import list, before `WorkspacePublicationError` alphabetically.\n\nAnchor (unique, end of `_terminal_context`):\n```python\n    except (\n        ContainerStartError,\n        ContainerNotReadyError,\n        GitError,\n        OSError,\n        ValueError,\n        WorkspacePublicationError,\n    ):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\"Terminal runtime unavailable\") from None\n    return user_id, tenant, socket_path, effective_cwd, runtime.runtime_id\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    except WorkspacePublicationConflictError:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=\"Workspace publication conflict\") from None\n    except (\n        ContainerStartError,\n        ContainerNotReadyError,\n        GitError,\n        OSError,\n        ValueError,\n        WorkspacePublicationError,\n    ):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\"Terminal runtime unavailable\") from None\n    return user_id, tenant, socket_path, effective_cwd, runtime.runtime_id\n```\n\n---\n\n### PACKET 2 — Finding 3 (High): authorized deletion gate before Git validation and inside trusted metadata writes\n\n**2a. `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py` — gate parameter on the pre-effect authorizer**\n\nAnchor (unique, all of `_authorize_external`):\n```python\nasync def _authorize_external(\n    run_database_operation: DatabaseOperationRunner,\n    authorize: CheckoutAuthorizer,\n    expected: WorkspaceCheckoutState,\n) -> WorkspaceCheckoutState:\n    \"\"\"Use a fresh database callback immediately before one external effect.\"\"\"\n    return await run_database_operation(\n        lambda database: _authorize_checkout(database, authorize, expected)\n    )\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nasync def _authorize_external(\n    run_database_operation: DatabaseOperationRunner,\n    authorize: CheckoutAuthorizer,\n    expected: WorkspaceCheckoutState,\n    *,\n    deletion_gate: bool = False,\n) -> WorkspaceCheckoutState:\n    \"\"\"Use a fresh database callback immediately before one external effect.\"\"\"\n\n    def authorize_external(database: sqlite3.Connection) -> WorkspaceCheckoutState:\n        current = _authorize_checkout(database, authorize, expected)\n        if deletion_gate:\n            require_no_repository_deletion(database, expected.repo_id)\n        return current\n\n    return await run_database_operation(authorize_external)\n```\n\n**2b. Same file — run the gate before Git validation and the trusted-path branch**\n\nAnchor (unique in `publish_workspace_checkout_for_tenant`, the only `_authorize_external` call followed by `require_isolated_execution`):\n```python\n    await _authorize_external(run_database_operation, authorize, state)\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    repo_available = await validate_local_repo(state.repo_path)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    await _authorize_external(\n        run_database_operation, authorize, state, deletion_gate=True\n    )\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    repo_available = await validate_local_repo(state.repo_path)\n```\nThis single gate precedes `validate_local_repo`, the trusted-path `_prepare_trusted_checkout` return, and every later branch. The atomic check inside `_begin_repair` (Packet 1b) remains the final admission authority, and the exact-owner continuation row match in `_begin_repair_locked` is untouched. No lifecycle lock is taken inside this module so the caller-held lock in `prepare_tenant_workspace_runtime_paths` cannot deadlock. The connection stays inside the short callback and never crosses an await.\n\n**2c. `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py` — top import**\n\nAnchor (unique):\n```python\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    repository_lifecycle,\n    repository_lifecycle_root,\n)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    repository_lifecycle,\n    repository_lifecycle_root,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\n```\n\n**2d. Same file — gate trusted metadata writes in their own BEGIN IMMEDIATE**\n\nAnchor (unique, all of `apply_workspace_checkout_preparation`):\n```python\ndef apply_workspace_checkout_preparation(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    preparation: WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Apply deterministic checkout metadata updates in one transaction.\"\"\"\n    if preparation.update_repo_metadata:\n        for workspace_id, workspace_path in preparation.workspace_paths:\n            db.execute(\n                \"UPDATE workspaces SET path = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                (workspace_path, workspace_id),\n            )\n        db.execute(\n            \"\"\"UPDATE repos\n               SET root_path = ?, remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\"\"\",\n            (\n                preparation.repo_path,\n                preparation.remote_url,\n                preparation.installation_id,\n                preparation.repo_id,\n            ),\n        )\n        db.commit()\n        if preparation.repaired_repo:\n            logger.info(\"Repaired repository into tenant storage\")\n    return dict(_fetch_workspace(db, preparation.workspace_id))\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\ndef apply_workspace_checkout_preparation(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    preparation: WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Apply deterministic checkout metadata updates in one transaction.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services.workspace_publication import WorkspacePublicationConflictError\n\n    db.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n    try:\n        try:\n            require_no_repository_deletion(db, preparation.repo_id)\n        except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as error:\n            raise WorkspacePublicationConflictError(\n                \"Checkout preparation conflicts with repository deletion\"\n            ) from error\n        if preparation.update_repo_metadata:\n            for workspace_id, workspace_path in preparation.workspace_paths:\n                db.execute(\n                    \"UPDATE workspaces SET path = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                    (workspace_path, workspace_id),\n                )\n            db.execute(\n                \"\"\"UPDATE repos\n                   SET root_path = ?, remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\"\"\",\n                (\n                    preparation.repo_path,\n                    preparation.remote_url,\n                    preparation.installation_id,\n                    preparation.repo_id,\n                ),\n            )\n        db.commit()\n        if preparation.update_repo_metadata and preparation.repaired_repo:\n            logger.info(\"Repaired repository into tenant storage\")\n        return dict(_fetch_workspace(db, preparation.workspace_id))\n    except BaseException:\n        db.rollback()\n        raise\n```\nThe lazy import avoids the module cycle because `workspace_publication` imports `workspace` at module scope. All three production callers of this function (`workspace_runtime_paths`, `stream`, `workspace_execution`) invoke it inside `run_database_operation` callbacks on fresh connections with no open transaction, so the explicit `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` is safe. The subtype propagates through `publish_apply_workspace_checkout_for_tenant` and is mapped at the two HTTP boundaries by Packet 1, and `stream` keeps catching it via the parent class.\n\n---\n\n### PACKET 3 — Finding 1 (High): workspace creation admission transaction, connection lifetime, race cleanup\n\n**3a. `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py` — header imports**\n\nAnchor (unique, current header block):\n```python\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport sqlite3\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, cast\n\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport sqlite3\nfrom collections.abc import Awaitable\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, TypeVar, cast\n\nfrom fastapi import Request\nfrom yinshi.api.deps import run_db_operation_for_request\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\n```\n\n**3b. Same file — runner aliases**\n\nAnchor (unique):\n```python\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n_T = TypeVar(\"_T\")\nDatabaseOperation = Callable[[sqlite3.Connection], _T]\nDatabaseOperationRunner = Callable[[Callable[[sqlite3.Connection], _T]], Awaitable[_T]]\n```\n\n**3c. Same file — convert `ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant` to a short-callback runner**\n\nAnchor (unique, entire current function through the end shown below):\n```python\nasync def ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    repo_id: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Repair migrated tenant repo/workspace paths into the tenant data directory.\n\n    Legacy migrations copied root_path and worktree paths into the per-user DB\n    without relocating them. This lazily repairs those records the first time\n    the repo is used after migration.\n    \"\"\"\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    repo_path = repo[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo root_path must not be empty\"\n    remote_url = repo[\"remote_url\"]\n    repo_keys = repo.keys()\n    installation_id = repo[\"installation_id\"] if \"installation_id\" in repo_keys else None\n    source_repo_is_available = await validate_local_repo(repo_path)\n```\nand the remainder through:\n```python\n    db.execute(\n        \"UPDATE repos SET root_path = ?, remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n        (target_repo_path, remote_url, installation_id, repo_id),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    logger.info(\"Repaired repository into tenant storage\")\n\n    updated_repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    return dict(updated_repo)\n```\nReplace the entire function with:\n```python\nasync def ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(\n    run_database_operation: DatabaseOperationRunner,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    repo_id: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Repair migrated tenant repo/workspace paths into the tenant data directory.\n\n    Legacy migrations copied root_path and worktree paths into the per-user DB\n    without relocating them. This lazily repairs those records the first time\n    the repo is used after migration. Database callbacks open short-lived\n    connections and no SQLite handle crosses an external Git effect. Every\n    durable metadata write rechecks repository deletion inside its own\n    BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction.\n    \"\"\"\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n\n    def load_repair_snapshot(database: sqlite3.Connection) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        repo = _fetch_repo(database, repo_id)\n        repo_keys = repo.keys()\n        workspace_rows = database.execute(\n            \"SELECT id, branch FROM workspaces WHERE repo_id = ? ORDER BY created_at ASC\",\n            (repo_id,),\n        ).fetchall()\n        return {\n            \"repo\": dict(repo),\n            \"root_path\": str(repo[\"root_path\"]),\n            \"remote_url\": repo[\"remote_url\"],\n            \"installation_id\": (\n                repo[\"installation_id\"] if \"installation_id\" in repo_keys else None\n            ),\n            \"workspace_branches\": [\n                (str(row[\"id\"]), str(row[\"branch\"])) for row in workspace_rows\n            ],\n        }\n\n    snapshot = await run_database_operation(load_repair_snapshot)\n    repo_path = snapshot[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo root_path must not be empty\"\n    remote_url = snapshot[\"remote_url\"]\n    installation_id = snapshot[\"installation_id\"]\n    source_repo_is_available = await validate_local_repo(repo_path)\n\n    if _tenant_path_is_trusted(tenant, repo_path):\n        if source_repo_is_available and not await _trusted_repo_needs_refresh(\n            repo_path,\n            remote_url,\n            installation_id,\n        ):\n            return dict(snapshot[\"repo\"])\n\n        (\n            refreshed_remote_url,\n            _,\n            refreshed_installation_id,\n        ) = await _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n            tenant,\n            repo_path,\n            remote_url,\n            installation_id,\n        )\n        remote_was_updated = await _sync_repo_checkout_remote(repo_path, refreshed_remote_url)\n        metadata_changed = (\n            refreshed_remote_url != remote_url or refreshed_installation_id != installation_id\n        )\n        if not remote_was_updated and not metadata_changed:\n            return dict(snapshot[\"repo\"])\n\n        def commit_trusted_metadata(database: sqlite3.Connection) -> dict[str, Any]:\n            database.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n            try:\n                require_no_repository_deletion(database, repo_id)\n                database.execute(\n                    \"UPDATE repos SET remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                    (refreshed_remote_url, refreshed_installation_id, repo_id),\n                )\n                database.commit()\n            except BaseException:\n                database.rollback()\n                raise\n            return dict(_fetch_repo(database, repo_id))\n\n        return await run_database_operation(commit_trusted_metadata)\n\n    target_repo_path = _tenant_repo_path(tenant, repo_id)\n    remote_url, access_token, installation_id = await _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n        tenant,\n        repo_path,\n        remote_url,\n        installation_id,\n    )\n    await _materialize_repo_checkout(\n        repo_path,\n        target_repo_path,\n        remote_url,\n        access_token=access_token,\n    )\n    workspace_path_updates: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    for workspace_id, branch in snapshot[\"workspace_branches\"]:\n        if not branch:\n            raise WorkspaceNotFoundError(\n                f\"Workspace {workspace_id} is missing its branch name\"\n            )\n        target_workspace_path = _workspace_path(target_repo_path, branch)\n        await restore_worktree(target_repo_path, target_workspace_path, branch)\n        workspace_path_updates.append((workspace_id, target_workspace_path))\n\n    def commit_repair(database: sqlite3.Connection) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        database.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n        try:\n            require_no_repository_deletion(database, repo_id)\n            for repaired_workspace_id, repaired_path in workspace_path_updates:\n                database.execute(\n                    \"UPDATE workspaces SET path = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                    (repaired_path, repaired_workspace_id),\n                )\n            database.execute(\n                \"UPDATE repos SET root_path = ?, remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                (target_repo_path, remote_url, installation_id, repo_id),\n            )\n            database.commit()\n        except BaseException:\n            database.rollback()\n            raise\n        return dict(_fetch_repo(database, repo_id))\n\n    updated_repo = await run_database_operation(commit_repair)\n    logger.info(\"Repaired repository into tenant storage\")\n    return updated_repo\n```\n\n**3d. Same file — convert `ensure_workspace_checkout_for_tenant` (no production callers)**\n\nAnchor (unique, entire function):\n```python\nasync def ensure_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    workspace_id: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Repair the repo backing a workspace and return the updated workspace row.\"\"\"\n    workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    repo_id = workspace[\"repo_id\"]\n    assert repo_id, \"workspace repo_id must not be empty\"\n\n    await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(db, tenant, repo_id)\n    updated_workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    return dict(updated_workspace)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nasync def ensure_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n    run_database_operation: DatabaseOperationRunner,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    workspace_id: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Repair the repo backing a workspace and return the updated workspace row.\"\"\"\n    workspace = await run_database_operation(\n        lambda database: dict(_fetch_workspace(database, workspace_id))\n    )\n    repo_id = str(workspace[\"repo_id\"])\n    assert repo_id, \"workspace repo_id must not be empty\"\n\n    await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(run_database_operation, tenant, repo_id)\n    return await run_database_operation(\n        lambda database: dict(_fetch_workspace(database, workspace_id))\n    )\n```\n\n**3e. Same file — `relink_github_repos_for_tenant` keeps its db parameter and adapts internally (auth_routes stays unchanged)**\n\nAnchor (unique, two fragments of one function; replace each exactly):\n\nFragment one:\n```python\n    refreshed_repo_count = 0\n    repos = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT id FROM repos WHERE remote_url IS NOT NULL ORDER BY created_at ASC\"\n    ).fetchall()\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    async def run_relink_operation(operation: Callable[[sqlite3.Connection], _T]) -> _T:\n        return operation(db)\n\n    refreshed_repo_count = 0\n    repos = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT id FROM repos WHERE remote_url IS NOT NULL ORDER BY created_at ASC\"\n    ).fetchall()\n```\nFragment two:\n```python\n        refreshed_repo = await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(db, tenant, repo[\"id\"])\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n        refreshed_repo = await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(\n            run_relink_operation, tenant, str(repo[\"id\"])\n        )\n```\nThis preserves the relink flow's current single-connection behavior exactly while the creation path gets per-callback connections.\n\n**3f. Same file — rewrite creation admission**\n\nAnchor (unique, both functions in full, from `async def create_workspace_for_repo(` through the end of `_create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked` shown below):\n```python\nasync def create_workspace_for_repo(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    repo_id: str,\n    name: str | None = None,\n    username: str | None = None,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree while holding its repository lifecycle lock.\"\"\"\n    _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    lock_root = repository_lifecycle_root(db, tenant)\n    async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n        return await _create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(\n            db,\n            repo_id,\n            name=name,\n            username=username,\n            tenant=tenant,\n        )\n\n\nasync def _create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    repo_id: str,\n    name: str | None = None,\n    username: str | None = None,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree after repository lifecycle serialization.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import require_no_repository_deletion\n\n    require_no_repository_deletion(db, repo_id)\n    if tenant is not None:\n        await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(db, tenant, repo_id)\n\n    repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n\n    branch = generate_branch_name(username=username)\n    if not name:\n        name = branch\n\n    repo_path = repo[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo_path must not be empty\"\n    worktree_dir = _workspace_path(repo_path, branch)\n    base_ref: str | None = None\n\n    remote_url = repo[\"remote_url\"]\n    if remote_url:\n        access_token = None\n        try:\n            if tenant is not None:\n                _, access_token, _ = await _resolve_remote_checkout(tenant, remote_url)\n            base_ref = await resolve_remote_base_ref(repo_path, access_token=access_token)\n        except GitError:\n            logger.warning(\"Creating worktree from local HEAD after remote sync failure\")\n            base_ref = None\n\n    await create_worktree(repo_path, worktree_dir, branch, base_ref=base_ref)\n    ensure_secret_guardrails(repo_path)\n\n    cursor = db.execute(\n        \"\"\"INSERT INTO workspaces (repo_id, name, branch, path, state)\n           VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 'ready')\"\"\",\n        (repo_id, name, branch, worktree_dir),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n\n    row = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM workspaces WHERE rowid = ?\", (cursor.lastrowid,)).fetchone()\n    return dict(row)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nasync def create_workspace_for_repo(\n    request: Request,\n    repo_id: str,\n    name: str | None = None,\n    username: str | None = None,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n    authorize: Callable[[sqlite3.Connection], None] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree while holding its repository lifecycle lock.\"\"\"\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    lock_root = await run_db_operation_for_request(\n        request, lambda database: repository_lifecycle_root(database, tenant)\n    )\n    async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n        return await _create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(\n            request,\n            repo_id,\n            name=name,\n            username=username,\n            tenant=tenant,\n            authorize=authorize,\n        )\n\n\nasync def _create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(\n    request: Request,\n    repo_id: str,\n    name: str | None = None,\n    username: str | None = None,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n    authorize: Callable[[sqlite3.Connection], None] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree after repository lifecycle serialization.\n\n    Admission runs as short database callbacks on fresh connections and no\n    SQLite handle crosses an await. The pre-effect callback authorizes and\n    rejects repository deletion ownership before any checkout or Git work.\n    Final authorization, the deletion recheck, and the workspace INSERT share\n    one BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction. A created worktree is removed when final\n    admission loses a deletion race.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def load_creation_snapshot(database: sqlite3.Connection) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        if authorize is not None:\n            authorize(database)\n        require_no_repository_deletion(database, repo_id)\n        repo = _fetch_repo(database, repo_id)\n        return {\"root_path\": str(repo[\"root_path\"]), \"remote_url\": repo[\"remote_url\"]}\n\n    repo_facts = await run_db_operation_for_request(request, load_creation_snapshot)\n    if tenant is not None:\n        await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(\n            lambda operation: run_db_operation_for_request(request, operation),\n            tenant,\n            repo_id,\n        )\n        repo_facts = await run_db_operation_for_request(request, load_creation_snapshot)\n\n    repo_path = repo_facts[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo_path must not be empty\"\n    branch = generate_branch_name(username=username)\n    if not name:\n        name = branch\n    worktree_dir = _workspace_path(repo_path, branch)\n    base_ref: str | None = None\n\n    remote_url = repo_facts[\"remote_url\"]\n    if remote_url:\n        access_token = None\n        try:\n            if tenant is not None:\n                _, access_token, _ = await _resolve_remote_checkout(tenant, remote_url)\n            base_ref = await resolve_remote_base_ref(repo_path, access_token=access_token)\n        except GitError:\n            logger.warning(\"Creating worktree from local HEAD after remote sync failure\")\n            base_ref = None\n\n    await create_worktree(repo_path, worktree_dir, branch, base_ref=base_ref)\n    ensure_secret_guardrails(repo_path)\n\n    def admit_workspace(database: sqlite3.Connection) -> int:\n        database.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n        try:\n            if authorize is not None:\n                authorize(database)\n            require_no_repository_deletion(database, repo_id)\n            cursor = database.execute(\n                \"\"\"INSERT INTO workspaces (repo_id, name, branch, path, state)\n                   VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 'ready')\"\"\",\n                (repo_id, name, branch, worktree_dir),\n            )\n            database.commit()\n            return int(cursor.lastrowid)\n        except BaseException:\n            database.rollback()\n            raise\n\n    try:\n        workspace_rowid = await run_db_operation_for_request(request, admit_workspace)\n    except BaseException:\n        await _remove_unadmitted_worktree(repo_path, worktree_dir)\n        raise\n\n    row = await run_db_operation_for_request(\n        request,\n        lambda database: database.execute(\n            \"SELECT * FROM workspaces WHERE rowid = ?\", (workspace_rowid,)\n        ).fetchone(),\n    )\n    assert row is not None\n    return dict(row)\n\n\nasync def _remove_unadmitted_worktree(repo_path: str, worktree_dir: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Remove a created worktree when final admission lost its race.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        await delete_worktree(repo_path, worktree_dir)\n    except Exception:\n        logger.warning(\"Failed to remove unadmitted worktree\")\n```\nDesign notes: the lifecycle lock spans the whole admission as before. The pre-effect callback authorizes and checks deletion ownership on a fresh connection that closes before external work. `RepositoryDeletionPendingError` stays the public error so the API's existing 409 mapping and the existing focused test are preserved. Cleanup catches `Exception` only, so cancellation still propagates without awaiting new work. `delete_worktree` runs inside the lifecycle lock, and `services.git` takes no lifecycle lock, so no nesting deadlock.\n\n**3g. `backend/src/yinshi/api/workspaces.py` — handler holds no connection across the service call**\n\nAnchor (unique, body of `create_workspace`):\n```python\n    email = get_user_email(request)\n    username = email.split(\"@\")[0] if email else None\n    tenant = get_tenant(request)\n\n    with get_db_for_request(request) as db:\n        _check_repo_owner(db, repo_id, request)\n        _require_isolated_workspace_git()\n        try:\n            created = await create_workspace_for_repo(\n                db,\n                repo_id,\n                body.name,\n                username=username,\n                tenant=tenant,\n            )\n            return _workspace_projection(db, str(created[\"id\"]))\n        except RepoNotFoundError:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Repo not found\")\n        except RepositoryDeletionPendingError:\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=409,\n                detail=\"Repository deletion is pending; admission can be retried\",\n            )\n        except GitError as exc:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=str(exc))\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    email = get_user_email(request)\n    username = email.split(\"@\")[0] if email else None\n    tenant = get_tenant(request)\n    _require_isolated_workspace_git()\n    try:\n        created = await create_workspace_for_repo(\n            request,\n            repo_id,\n            body.name,\n            username=username,\n            tenant=tenant,\n            authorize=lambda database: _check_repo_owner(database, repo_id, request),\n        )\n    except RepoNotFoundError:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Repo not found\")\n    except RepositoryDeletionPendingError:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=409,\n            detail=\"Repository deletion is pending; admission can be retried\",\n        )\n    except GitError as exc:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=str(exc))\n    with get_db_for_request(request) as db:\n        return _workspace_projection(db, str(created[\"id\"]))\n```\nBehavior note: the isolation gate now precedes the ownership check (fail-closed ordering consistent with the other gates). All HTTP mappings are unchanged. `HTTPException` from `_check_repo_owner` propagates exactly as before.\n\n---\n\n### PACKET 4 — Finding 2 (High): execution acquisition pre-effect deletion gate\n\n**4a. `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py` — extend the lifecycle import**\n\nAnchor (unique):\n```python\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    repository_lifecycle,\n    repository_lifecycle_root,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\n```\n\n**4b. Same file — add the preflight and invoke it before checkout recovery**\n\nAnchor (unique, head of `acquire_prompt_workspace`):\n```python\nasync def acquire_prompt_workspace(\n    request: Request, session_id: str, operation_id: str, *, kind: str\n) -> ExecutionAdmission:\n    \"\"\"Publish physical exclusion, then reauthorize before any checkout or provider work.\"\"\"\n    # Fail-closed isolation gate: no admission marker, Git work, credential\n    # resolution, or provider access may run before the profile is verified.\n    require_isolated_execution(kind)\n    selected = await run_db_operation_for_request(\n        request, lambda db: prompt_workspace(db, request, session_id)\n    )\n    selected = await _recover_pending_checkout_for_execution(request, session_id, selected, kind)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\nasync def _repository_deletion_preflight(request: Request, repo_id: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reject work under lifecycle serialization before checkout recovery or Git effects.\n\n    Repository deletion receipts are created and advanced while their owner\n    holds the same lifecycle lock, so a fresh check inside the lock excludes\n    every receipt row before checkout recovery, physical identity reads,\n    stopped-receipt retries, or marker cleanup. The transactional check inside\n    reserve() remains the final admission authority.\n    \"\"\"\n    lock_root = await run_db_operation_for_request(\n        request,\n        lambda db: repository_lifecycle_root(db, get_tenant(request)),\n    )\n    async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n        try:\n            await run_db_operation_for_request(\n                request, lambda db: require_no_repository_deletion(db, repo_id)\n            )\n        except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as error:\n            raise WorkspaceAdmissionError() from error\n\n\nasync def acquire_prompt_workspace(\n    request: Request, session_id: str, operation_id: str, *, kind: str\n) -> ExecutionAdmission:\n    \"\"\"Publish physical exclusion, then reauthorize before any checkout or provider work.\"\"\"\n    # Fail-closed isolation gate: no admission marker, Git work, credential\n    # resolution, or provider access may run before the profile is verified.\n    require_isolated_execution(kind)\n    selected = await run_db_operation_for_request(\n        request, lambda db: prompt_workspace(db, request, session_id)\n    )\n    await _repository_deletion_preflight(request, selected.repo_id)\n    selected = await _recover_pending_checkout_for_execution(request, session_id, selected, kind)\n```\n`WorkspaceAdmissionError` preserves the public error surface that `reserve()` produced previously. No lifecycle lock is held by callers at this point, and the lock is released before admission-marker locks (`admission:` keyed) are ever taken, so lock ordering cannot nest. `reserve()` is unchanged and keeps its atomic deletion check.\n\n---\n\n### PACKET 5 — Finding 4 (High): managed integration deletion preflight before preview and identity\n\n**5a. `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_integration.py` — extend the lifecycle import**\n\nThe module already imports from `yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle` (it uses `require_no_repository_deletion` and `RepositoryDeletionPendingError`). Add `repository_lifecycle` to that existing import list, ordered `RepositoryDeletionPendingError`, `repository_lifecycle`, `require_no_repository_deletion` (isort case ordering, matching the Packet 4 style).\n\n**5b. Same file — preflight for new operations only**\n\nAnchor (unique, inside `integrate`):\n```python\n        operation = await run_db_operation_for_request(request, existing)\n        if operation is not None and operation[\"status\"] not in {\"checking\", \"applying\"}:\n            await self._repair_terminal_admission(request, selection, operation)\n            return self._outcome(operation)\n        if operation is None:\n            preview = await self.preview(request, parent_id, child_id)\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n        operation = await run_db_operation_for_request(request, existing)\n        if operation is not None and operation[\"status\"] not in {\"checking\", \"applying\"}:\n            await self._repair_terminal_admission(request, selection, operation)\n            return self._outcome(operation)\n        if operation is None:\n            try:\n                async with repository_lifecycle(\n                    selection.context.repo_id, selection.context.lock_root\n                ):\n                    await run_db_operation_for_request(\n                        request,\n                        lambda db: require_no_repository_deletion(\n                            db, selection.context.repo_id\n                        ),\n                    )\n            except RepositoryDeletionPendingError as error:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=409, detail=\"Integration precondition changed\"\n                ) from error\n            preview = await self.preview(request, parent_id, child_id)\n```\nExact-owner continuation is preserved: only the `operation is None` (new operation) branch is gated, so replays of existing checking or applying operations are never blocked. The transactional check inside `reserve()` is unchanged and still precedes the INSERT. The lock is released before `preview`, `integration_workspace_identity`, and `_execute`, so no lock nesting occurs.\n\n---\n\n### PACKET 6 — Tests\n\n**6a. `backend/tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py` — header**\n\nAnchor (unique, entire current import header):\n```python\n\"\"\"Repository deletion receipts block conflicting durable admissions.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n\nimport pytest\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\n\nfrom tests.test_thread_integration import head_commit, seed_parent_stack\nfrom tests.test_thread_workspaces import run_git as worktree_git\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace import WorkspaceCheckoutState, create_workspace_for_repo\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_admission import WorkspaceAdmissionError\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_deletion import (\n    WorkspaceDeletionConflict,\n    claim_workspace_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_execution import ExecutionAdmission, prompt_workspace\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_publication import WorkspacePublicationError, _begin_repair\nfrom yinshi.tenant import TenantContext\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n\"\"\"Repository deletion receipts block conflicting durable admissions.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport sqlite3\nimport threading\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom unittest.mock import AsyncMock\n\nimport pytest\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\n\nfrom tests.factories import create_full_stack\nfrom tests.test_thread_integration import head_commit, seed_parent_stack\nfrom tests.test_thread_workspaces import run_git as worktree_git\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    RepositoryDeletionPendingError,\n    require_no_repository_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_integration import ThreadIntegrationService\nfrom yinshi.services.thread_workspaces import ThreadWorkspaceService\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace import (\n    WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation,\n    WorkspaceCheckoutState,\n    apply_workspace_checkout_preparation,\n    create_workspace_for_repo,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_admission import WorkspaceAdmissionError\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_deletion import (\n    WorkspaceDeletionConflict,\n    claim_workspace_deletion,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_execution import (\n    ExecutionAdmission,\n    acquire_prompt_workspace,\n    prompt_workspace,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_publication import (\n    WorkspacePublicationConflictError,\n    WorkspacePublicationError,\n    _begin_repair,\n    publish_workspace_checkout_for_tenant,\n)\nfrom yinshi.tenant import TenantContext\n\n_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 10.0\n```\n\n**6b. Same file — shared helpers, inserted immediately after the `_request()` helper**\n\nAnchor (unique, end of `_request()`):\n```python\n            \"app\": app,\n            \"state\": {},\n        }\n    )\n```\nAppend after it:\n```python\n\n\ndef _forbidden_effect(label: str):\n    \"\"\"Return a spy that fails the test when a gated effect executes.\"\"\"\n\n    def _raise(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n        raise AssertionError(f\"blocked effect ran during deletion admission: {label}\")\n\n    return _raise\n\n\ndef _interruption_request() -> Request:\n    app = SimpleNamespace(state=SimpleNamespace(mode=\"hosted\"))\n    return Request(\n        {\n            \"type\": \"http\",\n            \"http_version\": \"1.1\",\n            \"method\": \"POST\",\n            \"scheme\": \"http\",\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"raw_path\": b\"/\",\n            \"query_string\": b\"\",\n            \"headers\": [],\n            \"client\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 1),\n            \"server\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 80),\n            \"app\": app,\n            \"state\": {},\n        }\n    )\n```\n(`_interruption_request` duplicates `_request` only to keep the existing helper untouched for existing tests. If preferred, existing tests can switch to it and `_request` can be renamed, but the packet keeps the diff minimal.)\n\n**6c. Same file — replace the existing creation test with four stronger tests**\n\nAnchor (unique, entire existing test):\n```python\ndef test_receipt_blocks_workspace_creation_before_git(db, git_repo: str) -> None:\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    with pytest.raises(RepositoryDeletionPendingError):\n        asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(db, REPO_ID))\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspaces\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert not (Path(git_repo) / \".worktrees\").exists()\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"phase\", [\"prepared\", \"quarantined\", \"delete_committed\"])\ndef test_receipt_blocks_workspace_creation_before_any_effect(\n    db, git_repo: str, phase: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Any receipt phase blocks creation before checkout, Git, and filesystem effects.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace as workspace_module\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    _insert_receipt(db, phase=phase)\n    for name in (\n        \"ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant\",\n        \"resolve_remote_base_ref\",\n        \"create_worktree\",\n        \"ensure_secret_guardrails\",\n    ):\n        monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, name, _forbidden_effect(name))\n    with pytest.raises(RepositoryDeletionPendingError):\n        asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(_request(), REPO_ID))\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspaces\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert not (Path(git_repo) / \".worktrees\").exists()\n\n\ndef test_creation_final_admission_rechecks_receipt_inside_transaction(\n    db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Final workspace admission authorizes and rechecks inside BEGIN IMMEDIATE.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace as workspace_module\n    from yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import require_no_repository_deletion as real_check\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    observed: list[bool] = []\n\n    def spy(database: sqlite3.Connection, repo_id: str) -> None:\n        observed.append(bool(database.in_transaction))\n        real_check(database, repo_id)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"require_no_repository_deletion\", spy)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        workspace_module, \"generate_branch_name\", return_value=\"admitted-branch\"\n    )\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"create_worktree\", new=AsyncMock())\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"ensure_secret_guardrails\", new=AsyncMock())\n    created = asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(_request(), REPO_ID))\n    assert created[\"branch\"] == \"admitted-branch\"\n    assert observed == [True]\n\n\ndef test_creation_holds_no_database_connection_during_git_effects(\n    db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"No SQLite handle stays open while creation awaits its external effects.\"\"\"\n    import yinshi.api.deps as deps_module\n    from yinshi.services import workspace as workspace_module\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    real_get_db = deps_module.get_db\n    open_connections = {\"count\": 0}\n\n    @contextmanager\n    def counting_get_db() -> Iterator[sqlite3.Connection]:\n        with real_get_db() as connection:\n            open_connections[\"count\"] += 1\n            try:\n                yield connection\n            finally:\n                open_connections[\"count\"] -= 1\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(deps_module, \"get_db\", counting_get_db)\n\n    async def assert_no_connection(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n        assert open_connections[\"count\"] == 0\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        workspace_module, \"generate_branch_name\", return_value=\"connection-branch\"\n    )\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"create_worktree\", assert_no_connection)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"ensure_secret_guardrails\", new=AsyncMock())\n    created = asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(_request(), REPO_ID))\n    assert created[\"branch\"] == \"connection-branch\"\n    assert open_connections[\"count\"] == 0\n\n\ndef test_creation_losing_deletion_race_cleans_created_worktree(\n    db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Final admission that loses a deletion race removes the created worktree.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace as workspace_module\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path) VALUES (?, 'repo', ?)\",\n        (REPO_ID, git_repo),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"generate_branch_name\", return_value=\"raced-branch\")\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"ensure_secret_guardrails\", new=AsyncMock())\n    real_create_worktree = workspace_module.create_worktree\n    worktree_created = threading.Event()\n    release_creation = threading.Event()\n\n    async def racing_create_worktree(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n        await real_create_worktree(*args, **kwargs)\n        worktree_created.set()\n        await asyncio.get_running_loop().run_in_executor(\n            None, release_creation.wait, _RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\n        )\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"create_worktree\", racing_create_worktree)\n    worktree_path = Path(git_repo) / \".worktrees\" / \"raced-branch\"\n\n    def race_deletion_receipt() -> None:\n        assert worktree_created.wait(_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n        database = sqlite3.connect(get_settings().db_path)\n        try:\n            _insert_receipt(database)\n        finally:\n            database.close()\n        release_creation.set()\n\n    racer = threading.Thread(target=race_deletion_receipt)\n    racer.start()\n    try:\n        with pytest.raises(RepositoryDeletionPendingError):\n            asyncio.run(create_workspace_for_repo(_request(), REPO_ID))\n    finally:\n        release_creation.set()\n        racer.join(_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspaces\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert not worktree_path.exists()\n```\nNotes: the file header needs `from collections.abc import Awaitable, Callable, Iterator` and `from contextlib import contextmanager` added for the counting helper (extend the header in 6a accordingly: the `from contextlib import contextmanager` line goes with the stdlib group). `_insert_receipt` works on any connection exposing `execute` and `commit`, so the racer thread can reuse it.\n\n**6d. Same file — execution acquisition effect-spy and race tests, appended at end of file**\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"phase\", [\"prepared\", \"quarantined\", \"delete_committed\"])\ndef test_receipt_blocks_execution_acquisition_before_effects(\n    db, git_repo: str, phase: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"No checkout recovery, identity read, or marker work runs for any receipt phase.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace_execution as execution_module\n\n    _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    _insert_receipt(db, phase=phase)\n    for name in (\n        \"_recover_pending_checkout_for_execution\",\n        \"read_workspace_identity\",\n        \"_retry_stopped_receipts\",\n    ):\n        monkeypatch.setattr(execution_module, name, _forbidden_effect(name))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        execution_module.ThreadWorkspaceService,\n        \"acquire_workspace_admission\",\n        _forbidden_effect(\"acquire_workspace_admission\"),\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspaceAdmissionError):\n        asyncio.run(\n            acquire_prompt_workspace(_request(), SESSION_ID, uuid.uuid4().hex, kind=\"prompt\")\n        )\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_execution_receipts\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n\n\ndef test_execution_losing_deletion_race_fails_final_reservation(\n    db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A receipt that appears during acquisition still fails the atomic reservation.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace_execution as execution_module\n\n    _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    recovery_started = threading.Event()\n    release_recovery = threading.Event()\n\n    async def pausing_recovery(request, session_id, selected, kind):\n        recovery_started.set()\n        await asyncio.get_running_loop().run_in_executor(\n            None, release_recovery.wait, _RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\n        )\n        return selected\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        execution_module, \"_recover_pending_checkout_for_execution\", pausing_recovery\n    )\n\n    def race_receipt() -> None:\n        assert recovery_started.wait(_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n        database = sqlite3.connect(get_settings().db_path)\n        try:\n            _insert_receipt(database)\n        finally:\n            database.close()\n        release_recovery.set()\n\n    racer = threading.Thread(target=race_receipt)\n    racer.start()\n    try:\n        with pytest.raises(WorkspaceAdmissionError):\n            asyncio.run(\n                acquire_prompt_workspace(_request(), SESSION_ID, uuid.uuid4().hex, kind=\"prompt\")\n            )\n    finally:\n        release_recovery.set()\n        racer.join(_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_execution_receipts\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n```\n\n**6e. Same file — publication gate, trusted-path, and metadata transaction tests, appended at end**\n\n```python\ndef _publication_state(worktree_path: str) -> WorkspaceCheckoutState:\n    return WorkspaceCheckoutState(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo_path_for_state(worktree_path),\n        remote_url=None,\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspaces=((WORKSPACE_ID, BRANCH),),\n        workspace_paths=((WORKSPACE_ID, worktree_path),),\n    )\n\n\ndef git_repo_path_for_state(worktree_path: str) -> str:\n    return str(Path(worktree_path).parent.parent)\n\n\nasync def _inline_database_operation(operation):\n    return operation(db())\n\n\ndef test_receipt_blocks_publication_before_git_validation(db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The publication gate fires before validate_local_repo and the trusted branch.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace_publication as publication_module\n\n    worktree_path = _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    state = WorkspaceCheckoutState(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo,\n        remote_url=None,\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspaces=((WORKSPACE_ID, BRANCH),),\n        workspace_paths=((WORKSPACE_ID, worktree_path),),\n    )\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        publication_module, \"validate_local_repo\", _forbidden_effect(\"validate_local_repo\")\n    )\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        publication_module,\n        \"_prepare_trusted_checkout\",\n        _forbidden_effect(\"_prepare_trusted_checkout\"),\n    )\n\n    async def run_operation(operation):\n        return operation(db)\n\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspacePublicationConflictError):\n        asyncio.run(\n            publish_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n                _repair_tenant(),\n                state,\n                run_database_operation=run_operation,\n                authorize=lambda database: state,\n                authority_hash=\"a\" * 64,\n                database_identity=\"identity\",\n            )\n        )\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM workspace_checkout_repairs\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n\n\ndef test_trusted_path_publication_branch_is_gated(db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The trusted checkout branch never runs its preparation while a receipt exists.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace_publication as publication_module\n    from yinshi.services.workspace import WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation\n\n    worktree_path = _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    state = WorkspaceCheckoutState(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo,\n        remote_url=None,\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspaces=((WORKSPACE_ID, BRANCH),),\n        workspace_paths=((WORKSPACE_ID, worktree_path),),\n    )\n    trusted_tenant = TenantContext(\n        user_id=\"tenant-user\",\n        email=\"tenant@example.com\",\n        data_dir=str(Path(git_repo).parent),\n        db_path=str(Path(git_repo).parent / \"tenant.db\"),\n    )\n\n    async def run_operation(operation):\n        return operation(db)\n\n    preparation = WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo,\n        remote_url=None,\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspace_paths=(),\n        update_repo_metadata=False,\n        repaired_repo=False,\n    )\n    prepared_spy = AsyncMock(return_value=preparation)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(publication_module, \"_prepare_trusted_checkout\", prepared_spy)\n\n    asyncio.run(\n        publish_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n            trusted_tenant,\n            state,\n            run_database_operation=run_operation,\n            authorize=lambda database: state,\n            authority_hash=\"a\" * 64,\n            database_identity=\"identity\",\n        )\n    )\n    assert prepared_spy.await_count == 1\n\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    prepared_spy.reset_mock()\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspacePublicationConflictError):\n        asyncio.run(\n            publish_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n                trusted_tenant,\n                state,\n                run_database_operation=run_operation,\n                authorize=lambda database: state,\n                authority_hash=\"a\" * 64,\n                database_identity=\"identity\",\n            )\n        )\n    assert prepared_spy.await_count == 0\n\n\ndef test_trusted_metadata_writes_recheck_receipt_in_transaction(\n    db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Trusted metadata writes share one BEGIN IMMEDIATE with the deletion recheck.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services import workspace as workspace_module\n\n    _seed_worktree_stack(db, git_repo)\n    preparation = WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation(\n        REDACTED,\n        repo_id=REPO_ID,\n        repo_path=git_repo,\n        remote_url=\"https://example.com/repo.git\",\n        installation_id=None,\n        workspace_paths=(),\n        update_repo_metadata=True,\n        repaired_repo=False,\n    )\n    observed: list[bool] = []\n\n    def spy(database: sqlite3.Connection, repo_id: str) -> None:\n        observed.append(bool(database.in_transaction))\n        require_no_repository_deletion(database, repo_id)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspace_module, \"require_no_repository_deletion\", spy)\n    _insert_receipt(db)\n    with pytest.raises(WorkspacePublicationConflictError):\n        apply_workspace_checkout_preparation(db, preparation)\n    assert observed == [True]\n    assert db.execute(\n        \"SELECT remote_url FROM repos WHERE id = ?\", (REPO_ID,)\n    ).fetchone()[0] is None\n    _remove_receipt(db)\n    applied = apply_workspace_checkout_preparation(db, preparation)\n    assert applied[\"id\"] == WORKSPACE_ID\n    assert db.execute(\n        \"SELECT remote_url FROM repos WHERE id = ?\", (REPO_ID,)\n    ).fetchone()[0] == \"https://example.com/repo.git\"\n```\nNotes: drop the two unused sketch helpers `_publication_state`, `git_repo_path_for_state`, and `_inline_database_operation` shown above — they are not needed. Each test constructs its state inline as shown. The trusted-path test relies on `_tenant_path_is_trusted` treating a repo under the tenant data dir as trusted and on `state.repo_path != final_repo`, which holds because the final repo resolves under `data_dir/repos/<repo_id>`.\n\n**6f. Same file — integration helper plus spy and race tests**\n\nRewrite the existing integration test to use a shared helper (same assertions, nothing weakened). Anchor (unique, entire existing test `test_receipt_blocks_managed_integration_admission`, body as it exists today from `monkeypatch.setenv` through the final `assert head_commit(git_repo) == parent_head`). Replace with:\n\n```python\ndef _seed_integrable_child(\n    db, client, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> tuple[str, dict[str, Any], str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Return the integrate endpoint, confirmation, repo id, and child session id.\"\"\"\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"THREAD_MANAGED_INTEGRATION_ENABLED\", \"true\")\n    get_settings.cache_clear()\n    seed_parent_stack(db, git_repo)\n    spawned = client.post(\n        \"/api/threads/parent-session/children\",\n        json={\n            \"idempotency_key\": str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            \"title\": \"Backstop child\",\n            \"task\": \"Update README.md\",\n            \"start_immediately\": False,\n        },\n    )\n    assert spawned.status_code == 201\n    child = spawned.json()\n    workspace = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT w.path FROM workspaces w JOIN sessions s ON s.workspace_id = w.id \"\n        \"WHERE s.id = ?\",\n        (child[\"child_session_id\"],),\n    ).fetchone()\n    (Path(workspace[\"path\"]) / \"README.md\").write_bytes(b\"# Child result\\n\")\n    from yinshi.services.thread_orchestration import initial_run_idempotency_key\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO prompt_runs (id, session_id, idempotency_key, status) \"\n        \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, 'completed')\",\n        (\n            uuid.uuid4().hex,\n            child[\"child_session_id\"],\n            initial_run_idempotency_key(child[\"delegation_id\"]),\n        ),\n    )\n    db.execute(\n        \"UPDATE thread_delegations SET status = 'completed' WHERE id = ?\",\n        (child[\"delegation_id\"],),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    sealed = client.get(f\"/api/threads/{child['child_session_id']}/result\")\n    assert sealed.status_code == 200\n    endpoint = f\"/api/threads/parent-session/children/{child['child_session_id']}/integrate\"\n    preview = client.get(endpoint)\n    assert preview.status_code == 200\n    confirmation = preview.json()\n    assert confirmation[\"eligible\"] is True\n    repo_id = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT w.repo_id FROM workspaces w JOIN sessions s ON s.workspace_id = w.id \"\n        \"WHERE s.id = 'parent-session'\"\n    ).fetchone()[0]\n    return endpoint, confirmation, str(repo_id), str(child[\"child_session_id\"])\n\n\ndef _integration_payload(confirmation: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"idempotency_key\": str(uuid.uuid4()),\n        \"result_id\": confirmation[\"result_id\"],\n        \"expected_parent_head\": confirmation[\"expected_parent_head\"],\n        \"confirmed\": True,\n    }\n\n\ndef test_receipt_blocks_managed_integration_admission(\n    client, db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    endpoint, confirmation, repo_id, _child = _seed_integrable_child(\n        db, client, git_repo, monkeypatch\n    )\n    _insert_receipt(db, repo_id=repo_id)\n    parent_head = head_commit(git_repo)\n    applied = client.post(endpoint, json=_integration_payload(confirmation))\n    assert applied.status_code == 409\n    assert applied.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Integration precondition changed\"\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert head_commit(git_repo) == parent_head\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"phase\", [\"prepared\", \"quarantined\", \"delete_committed\"])\ndef test_receipt_blocks_new_integration_before_preview_and_identity(\n    client, db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch, phase: str\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"No preview or identity Git work runs for a new integration under any receipt phase.\"\"\"\n    endpoint, confirmation, repo_id, _child = _seed_integrable_child(\n        db, client, git_repo, monkeypatch\n    )\n    _insert_receipt(db, repo_id=repo_id, phase=phase)\n    parent_head = head_commit(git_repo)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        ThreadIntegrationService, \"preview\", _forbidden_effect(\"integration preview\")\n    )\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        ThreadWorkspaceService,\n        \"integration_workspace_identity\",\n        _forbidden_effect(\"integration_workspace_identity\"),\n    )\n    applied = client.post(endpoint, json=_integration_payload(confirmation))\n    assert applied.status_code == 409\n    assert applied.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Integration precondition changed\"\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n    assert head_commit(git_repo) == parent_head\n\n\ndef test_integration_losing_deletion_race_fails_reservation(\n    client, db, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A receipt that appears during identity capture fails the atomic reservation.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.models import ThreadIntegrationCreate\n\n    endpoint, confirmation, repo_id, child_session_id = _seed_integrable_child(\n        db, client, git_repo, monkeypatch\n    )\n    del endpoint\n    identity_started = threading.Event()\n    release_identity = threading.Event()\n    real_identity = ThreadWorkspaceService.integration_workspace_identity\n\n    async def pausing_identity(context):\n        identity_started.set()\n        await asyncio.get_running_loop().run_in_executor(\n            None, release_identity.wait, _RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\n        )\n        return await real_identity(context)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ThreadWorkspaceService, \"integration_workspace_identity\", pausing_identity)\n\n    def race_receipt() -> None:\n        assert identity_started.wait(_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n        database = sqlite3.connect(get_settings().db_path)\n        try:\n            _insert_receipt(database, repo_id=repo_id)\n        finally:\n            database.close()\n        release_identity.set()\n\n    racer = threading.Thread(target=race_receipt)\n    racer.start()\n    try:\n        with pytest.raises(HTTPException) as raised:\n            asyncio.run(\n                ThreadIntegrationService().integrate(\n                    _request(),\n                    \"parent-session\",\n                    child_session_id,\n                    ThreadIntegrationCreate(**_integration_payload(confirmation)),\n                )\n            )\n    finally:\n        release_identity.set()\n        racer.join(_RACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n    assert raised.value.status_code == 409\n    assert raised.value.detail == \"Integration precondition changed\"\n    assert db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM thread_integrations\").fetchone()[0] == 0\n```\nNote: `ThreadIntegrationCreate` field names must be confirmed against `yinshi.models`. If `idempotency_key` is a `UUID` field, pass `uuid.uuid4()` instead of the string form, and if `confirmed` has a default it may be omitted. Also, exact-owner continuation is implicitly covered because the existing replay behavior is untouched by Packet 5.\n\n**6g. Same file — HTTP boundary tests, appended at end**\n\n```python\ndef test_file_mutation_maps_deletion_conflict_to_generic_409(\n    auth_client, git_repo: str\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A deletion receipt during file preparation yields a stable generic 409.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.tenant import get_user_db\n\n    stack = create_full_stack(auth_client, git_repo)\n    workspace = stack[\"workspace\"]\n    with get_user_db(auth_client.yinshi_tenant) as tenant_db:\n        _insert_receipt(tenant_db, repo_id=str(workspace[\"repo_id\"]))\n    response = auth_client.put(\n        f\"/api/workspaces/{workspace['id']}/files/content?path=notes.txt\",\n        json={\"content\": \"blocked\\n\"},\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 409\n    assert response.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Workspace publication conflict\"\n    assert not (Path(workspace[\"path\"]) / \"notes.txt\").exists()\n\n\ndef test_file_infrastructure_publication_failure_stays_500(\n    auth_client, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Broad publication failures keep their existing 500 mapping.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.api import workspace_files as files_module\n\n    stack = create_full_stack(auth_client, git_repo)\n    workspace = stack[\"workspace\"]\n\n    async def broken_preparation(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> object:\n        raise WorkspacePublicationError(\"Checkout publication staging is inconsistent\")\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        files_module, \"prepare_tenant_workspace_runtime_paths\", broken_preparation\n    )\n    response = auth_client.put(\n        f\"/api/workspaces/{workspace['id']}/files/content?path=notes.txt\",\n        json={\"content\": \"x\"},\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 500\n    assert response.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Workspace file operation failed\"\n\n\ndef test_terminal_channel_maps_deletion_conflict_to_generic_409(\n    auth_client, git_repo: str\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A deletion receipt during terminal preparation yields a stable generic 409.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.tenant import get_user_db\n\n    stack = create_full_stack(auth_client, git_repo)\n    workspace = stack[\"workspace\"]\n    with get_user_db(auth_client.yinshi_tenant) as tenant_db:\n        _insert_receipt(tenant_db, repo_id=str(workspace[\"repo_id\"]))\n    response = auth_client.post(\n        f\"/api/workspaces/{workspace['id']}/terminals\",\n        json={\"owner_id\": auth_client.yinshi_tenant.user_id},\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 409\n    assert response.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Workspace publication conflict\"\n\n\ndef test_terminal_infrastructure_publication_failure_stays_503(\n    auth_client, git_repo: str, monkeypatch\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Broad publication failures keep the terminal runtime 503 mapping.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.api import terminal_channels as channels_module\n\n    stack = create_full_stack(auth_client, git_repo)\n    workspace = stack[\"workspace\"]\n\n    async def broken_preparation(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> object:\n        raise WorkspacePublicationError(\"Checkout publication staging is inconsistent\")\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        channels_module, \"prepare_tenant_workspace_runtime_paths\", broken_preparation\n    )\n    response = auth_client.post(\n        f\"/api/workspaces/{workspace['id']}/terminals\",\n        json={\"owner_id\": auth_client.yinshi_tenant.user_id},\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 503\n    assert response.json()[\"detail\"] == \"Terminal runtime unavailable\"\n```\nNotes: the `client` fixture is the no-auth alias, so these tests use the `auth_client` fixture for tenant mode, which `prepare_tenant_workspace_runtime_paths` requires. The `repository_deletions` insert uses the existing `_insert_receipt` helper against the tenant database. If `TerminalStartRequest` does not define `owner_id`, pydantic ignores the extra key and `{}` also works. These tests require the autouse `modeled_supported_isolation` fixture, which already models a supported profile for unmarked tests.\n\n**6h. `backend/tests/test_api.py` — caller update for the lifecycle lock test**\n\nAnchor (unique, inside `test_repository_delete_lock_blocks_workspace_creation`):\n```python\n    with (\n        patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.generate_branch_name\", return_value=\"locked-branch\"),\n        patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.create_worktree\", new_callable=AsyncMock),\n        patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.ensure_secret_guardrails\"),\n    ):\n        async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n            creation = asyncio.create_task(create_workspace_for_repo(db, repo_id))\n            await asyncio.sleep(0)\n            assert not creation.done()\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n    from types import SimpleNamespace as _SimpleNamespace\n    from starlette.requests import Request as _Request\n\n    def admission_request() -> _Request:\n        return _Request(\n            {\n                \"type\": \"http\",\n                \"http_version\": \"1.1\",\n                \"method\": \"POST\",\n                \"scheme\": \"http\",\n                \"path\": \"/\",\n                \"raw_path\": b\"/\",\n                \"query_string\": b\"\",\n                \"headers\": [],\n                \"client\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 1),\n                \"server\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 80),\n                \"app\": _SimpleNamespace(state=_SimpleNamespace(mode=\"hosted\")),\n                \"state\": {},\n            }\n        )\n\n    with (\n        patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.generate_branch_name\", return_value=\"locked-branch\"),\n        patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.create_worktree\", new_callable=AsyncMock),\n        patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.ensure_secret_guardrails\"),\n    ):\n        async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n            creation = asyncio.create_task(create_workspace_for_repo(admission_request(), repo_id))\n            await asyncio.sleep(0)\n            assert not creation.done()\n```\nNote: with the lifecycle lock held by the test, the creation task blocks at `repository_lifecycle` before opening any connection, which is exactly what this test asserts.\n\n**6i. `backend/tests/test_log_privacy.py` — caller update with a real database row**\n\nAnchor (unique, the `else:` branch shown earlier with the `Mock()` database and the four patches ending in `await workspace._create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(database, _REPOSITORY_ID)`). Replace the `else:` branch with:\n```python\n    else:\n        from starlette.requests import Request as _Request\n\n        database.execute(\n            \"INSERT INTO repos (id, name, root_path, remote_url) VALUES (?, 'private', ?, ?)\",\n            (_REPOSITORY_ID, _REPOSITORY_PATH, \"https://github.com/private/repository.git\"),\n        )\n        database.commit()\n        request = _Request(\n            {\n                \"type\": \"http\",\n                \"http_version\": \"1.1\",\n                \"method\": \"POST\",\n                \"scheme\": \"http\",\n                \"path\": \"/\",\n                \"raw_path\": b\"/\",\n                \"query_string\": b\"\",\n                \"headers\": [],\n                \"client\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 1),\n                \"server\": (\"127.0.0.1\", 80),\n                \"app\": SimpleNamespace(state=SimpleNamespace(mode=\"hosted\")),\n                \"state\": {},\n            }\n        )\n        with (\n            patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.generate_branch_name\", return_value=\"private-branch\"),\n            patch(\n                \"yinshi.services.workspace.resolve_remote_base_ref\",\n                new=AsyncMock(side_effect=GitError(_EXCEPTION_TEXT)),\n            ),\n            patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.create_worktree\", new=AsyncMock()),\n            patch(\"yinshi.services.workspace.ensure_secret_guardrails\"),\n        ):\n            await workspace._create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(request, _REPOSITORY_ID)\n```\nNotes: `SimpleNamespace` must be imported at the top of that file if not already present. If the `Mock` import becomes unused after this change, remove it to satisfy ruff. The privacy assertions are unchanged and now exercise the real database path, which strengthens the test.\n\n---\n\n### Validation plan (all not run)\n\n1. `cd backend && .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_repository_deletion_admission.py -q` — expect the original 9 plus roughly 17 new and strengthened tests green, run twice because of the pre-existing result-seal ordering flake.\n2. `cd backend && .venv/bin/python -m ruff check src tests` and `.venv/bin/python -m ruff format --check src tests`.\n3. `cd backend && .venv/bin/python -m mypy src` under strict configuration.\n4. `cd backend && .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_api.py::test_repository_delete_lock_blocks_workspace_creation tests/test_log_privacy.py -q` for the two caller updates.\n\nResidual risks are listed in the report. Nothing was executed, nothing was staged, and no file was modified.\n\nSession file: /Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/37d18459/run-0/session.jsonl","display":false,"id":"c5dcdbc8","parentId":"e61efab8","timestamp":"2026-09-13T08:24:24.657Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"d80789fc","parentId":"c5dcdbc8","timestamp":"2026-09-13T08:24:38.736Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning workspace refactoring to avoid circular imports**\n\n**Identifying async database handling issues in relink functions**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa65dbbace487d0a0c0107124c499b0\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning workspace refactoring to avoid circular imports**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Identifying async database handling issues in relink functions**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YQJFUULW7pLY8LP2OWdROy2H|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa65dc46eb487d0a3cd46d6e1780929","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace.py","offset":1,"limit":670}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":15763,"output":289,"cacheRead":134784,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":255,"totalTokens":150836,"cost":{"input":0.07881500000000001,"output":0.00867,"cacheRead":0.067392,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.154877}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789287864668,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa65db9401487d099d6e27f2d49bd3a","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"f70667c8","parentId":"d80789fc","timestamp":"2026-09-13T08:24:38.758Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YQJFUULW7pLY8LP2OWdROy2H|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa65dc46eb487d0a3cd46d6e1780929","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Workspace lifecycle management.\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport sqlite3\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, cast\n\nfrom yinshi.config import get_settings\nfrom yinshi.exceptions import (\n    GitError,\n    GitHubAccessError,\n    GitHubAppError,\n    RepoNotFoundError,\n    WorkspaceHasDelegatedThreads,\n    WorkspaceNotFoundError,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.git import (\n    clone_local_repo,\n    clone_repo,\n    create_worktree,\n    delete_worktree,\n    ensure_remote_url,\n    generate_branch_name,\n    get_remote_url,\n    resolve_remote_base_ref,\n    restore_worktree,\n    validate_local_repo,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.github_app import normalize_github_remote, resolve_github_clone_access\nfrom yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import (\n    repository_lifecycle,\n    repository_lifecycle_root,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.sidecar_runtime import (\n    delete_local_pi_session_file,\n    delete_workspace_runtime_home,\n)\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_files import ensure_secret_guardrails\nfrom yinshi.services.workspace_isolation import (\n    isolation_setup_required,\n    require_isolated_execution,\n)\nfrom yinshi.tenant import TenantContext\nfrom yinshi.utils.paths import is_path_inside\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass WorkspaceCheckoutState:\n    \"\"\"Database snapshot needed to prepare one tenant workspace checkout.\"\"\"\n\n    workspace_id: str\n    repo_id: str\n    repo_path: str\n    remote_url: str | None\n    installation_id: int | None\n    workspaces: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...]\n    workspace_paths: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...] = ()\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation:\n    \"\"\"Deterministic database updates produced by filesystem preparation.\"\"\"\n\n    workspace_id: str\n    repo_id: str\n    repo_path: str\n    remote_url: str | None\n    installation_id: int | None\n    workspace_paths: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...]\n    update_repo_metadata: bool\n    repaired_repo: bool\n\n\ndef _fetch_repo(db: sqlite3.Connection, repo_id: str) -> sqlite3.Row:\n    \"\"\"Load a repo row or raise RepoNotFoundError.\"\"\"\n    assert repo_id, \"repo_id must not be empty\"\n    repo = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM repos WHERE id = ?\", (repo_id,)).fetchone()\n    if not repo:\n        raise RepoNotFoundError(f\"Repo {repo_id} not found\")\n    return cast(sqlite3.Row, repo)\n\n\ndef _fetch_workspace(db: sqlite3.Connection, workspace_id: str) -> sqlite3.Row:\n    \"\"\"Load a workspace row or raise WorkspaceNotFoundError.\"\"\"\n    assert workspace_id, \"workspace_id must not be empty\"\n    workspace = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT * FROM workspaces WHERE id = ?\",\n        (workspace_id,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if not workspace:\n        raise WorkspaceNotFoundError(f\"Workspace {workspace_id} not found\")\n    return cast(sqlite3.Row, workspace)\n\n\ndef _tenant_path_is_trusted(tenant: TenantContext, path: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether a tenant path is inside tenant-managed storage.\"\"\"\n    assert tenant.data_dir, \"tenant.data_dir must not be empty\"\n    assert path, \"path must not be empty\"\n    if is_path_inside(path, tenant.data_dir):\n        return True\n\n    settings = get_settings()\n    if settings.container_enabled:\n        return False\n    return bool(settings.allowed_repo_base) and is_path_inside(path, settings.allowed_repo_base)\n\n\ndef _tenant_repo_path(tenant: TenantContext, repo_id: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the per-tenant repair target for a repo checkout.\"\"\"\n    assert tenant.data_dir, \"tenant.data_dir must not be empty\"\n    assert repo_id, \"repo_id must not be empty\"\n    return os.path.join(tenant.data_dir, \"repos\", repo_id)\n\n\ndef _workspace_path(repo_path: str, branch: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Build the canonical on-disk path for a worktree branch.\"\"\"\n    assert repo_path, \"repo_path must not be empty\"\n    assert branch, \"branch must not be empty\"\n    return os.path.join(repo_path, \".worktrees\", branch)\n\n\nasync def _materialize_repo_checkout(\n    source_path: str,\n    target_path: str,\n    remote_url: str | None,\n    access_token: str | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create or reuse a repaired repo checkout inside tenant storage.\"\"\"\n    assert target_path, \"target_path must not be empty\"\n\n    if await validate_local_repo(target_path):\n        return\n\n    if source_path and await validate_local_repo(source_path):\n        await clone_local_repo(source_path, target_path, remote_url=remote_url)\n        return\n\n    if remote_url:\n        await clone_repo(remote_url, target_path, access_token=access_token)\n        return\n\n    raise RepoNotFoundError(\"Repo checkout is missing and cannot be repaired\")\n\n\nasync def _sync_repo_checkout_remote(\n    repo_path: str,\n    remote_url: str | None,\n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Ensure one valid checkout points at the canonical remote URL.\"\"\"\n    if not await validate_local_repo(repo_path):\n        return False\n    if remote_url is None:\n        return False\n    return await ensure_remote_url(repo_path, remote_url)\n\n\nasync def _resolve_remote_checkout(\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    remote_url: str | None,\n) -> tuple[str | None, str | None, int | None]:\n    \"\"\"Resolve a canonical remote URL plus any GitHub token for repairs.\"\"\"\n    if remote_url is None:\n        return None, None, None\n\n    try:\n        clone_access = await resolve_github_clone_access(tenant.user_id, remote_url)\n    except GitHubAccessError as exc:\n        raise GitError(str(exc)) from exc\n    except GitHubAppError as exc:\n        raise GitError(str(exc)) from exc\n\n    if clone_access is None:\n        return remote_url, None, None\n\n    return (\n        clone_access.clone_url,\n        clone_access.access_token,\n        clone_access.installation_id,\n    )\n\n\nasync def _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    repo_path: str,\n    remote_url: str | None,\n    installation_id: int | None,\n) -> tuple[str | None, str | None, int | None]:\n    \"\"\"Refresh canonical remote metadata without breaking local-only recovery.\"\"\"\n    source_repo_is_available = await validate_local_repo(repo_path)\n    access_token = None\n    refreshed_remote_url = remote_url\n    refreshed_installation_id = installation_id\n\n    if remote_url:\n        try:\n            (\n                refreshed_remote_url,\n                access_token,\n                resolved_installation_id,\n            ) = await _resolve_remote_checkout(tenant, remote_url)\n        except GitError:\n            if not source_repo_is_available:\n                raise\n            logger.warning(\"Refreshing repository from local checkout after remote auth failure\")\n        else:\n            if resolved_installation_id is not None:\n                refreshed_installation_id = resolved_installation_id\n\n    return refreshed_remote_url, access_token, refreshed_installation_id\n\n\nasync def _trusted_repo_needs_refresh(\n    repo_path: str,\n    remote_url: str | None,\n    installation_id: int | None,\n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether a trusted repo should refresh remote metadata.\"\"\"\n    if not await validate_local_repo(repo_path):\n        return True\n    if remote_url is None:\n        return False\n    if installation_id is None:\n        return True\n\n    normalized_remote = normalize_github_remote(remote_url)\n    if normalized_remote is None:\n        return False\n\n    current_remote_url = await get_remote_url(repo_path)\n    if current_remote_url is None:\n        return True\n    return current_remote_url.rstrip(\"/\") != normalized_remote.clone_url.rstrip(\"/\")\n\n\ndef ensure_workspace_has_no_delegated_children(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    workspace_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Apply the deletion policy: workspace sessions must not parent children.\"\"\"\n    delegation_row = db.execute(\n        \"\"\"SELECT count(*) AS child_count\n           FROM thread_delegations d\n           JOIN sessions s ON s.id = d.parent_session_id\n           WHERE s.workspace_id = ?\"\"\",\n        (workspace_id,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    assert delegation_row is not None\n    if int(delegation_row[\"child_count\"]) > 0:\n        raise WorkspaceHasDelegatedThreads(\"Workspace sessions parent delegated child threads\")\n\n\ndef load_workspace_checkout_state(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    workspace_id: str,\n) -> WorkspaceCheckoutState:\n    \"\"\"Load immutable checkout inputs in one database operation.\"\"\"\n    workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    repo_id = workspace[\"repo_id\"]\n    assert repo_id, \"workspace repo_id must not be empty\"\n    repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    repo_path = repo[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo root_path must not be empty\"\n    workspaces = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT id, branch, path FROM workspaces WHERE repo_id = ? ORDER BY created_at ASC\",\n        (repo_id,),\n    ).fetchall()\n    workspace_branches: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    workspace_paths: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    for row in workspaces:\n        branch = row[\"branch\"]\n        if not branch:\n            raise WorkspaceNotFoundError(f\"Workspace {row['id']} is missing its branch name\")\n        workspace_branches.append((row[\"id\"], branch))\n        workspace_paths.append((row[\"id\"], str(row[\"path\"])))\n    repo_keys = repo.keys()\n    return WorkspaceCheckoutState(\n        workspace_id=workspace_id,\n        repo_id=repo_id,\n        repo_path=repo_path,\n        remote_url=repo[\"remote_url\"],\n        installation_id=(repo[\"installation_id\"] if \"installation_id\" in repo_keys else None),\n        workspaces=tuple(workspace_branches),\n        workspace_paths=tuple(workspace_paths),\n    )\n\n\nasync def prepare_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    state: WorkspaceCheckoutState,\n) -> WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation:\n    \"\"\"Prepare idempotent filesystem state without holding a database connection.\"\"\"\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    source_repo_is_available = await validate_local_repo(state.repo_path)\n    if _tenant_path_is_trusted(tenant, state.repo_path):\n        if source_repo_is_available and not await _trusted_repo_needs_refresh(\n            state.repo_path,\n            state.remote_url,\n            state.installation_id,\n        ):\n            return WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation(\n                workspace_id=state.workspace_id,\n                repo_id=state.repo_id,\n                repo_path=state.repo_path,\n                remote_url=state.remote_url,\n                installation_id=state.installation_id,\n                workspace_paths=(),\n                update_repo_metadata=False,\n                repaired_repo=False,\n            )\n\n        remote_url, _, installation_id = await _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n            tenant,\n            state.repo_path,\n            state.remote_url,\n            state.installation_id,\n        )\n        remote_was_updated = await _sync_repo_checkout_remote(state.repo_path, remote_url)\n        metadata_changed = (\n            remote_url != state.remote_url or installation_id != state.installation_id\n        )\n        return WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation(\n            workspace_id=state.workspace_id,\n            repo_id=state.repo_id,\n            repo_path=state.repo_path,\n            remote_url=remote_url,\n            installation_id=installation_id,\n            workspace_paths=(),\n            update_repo_metadata=remote_was_updated or metadata_changed,\n            repaired_repo=False,\n        )\n\n    target_repo_path = _tenant_repo_path(tenant, state.repo_id)\n    remote_url, access_token, installation_id = await _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n        tenant,\n        state.repo_path,\n        state.remote_url,\n        state.installation_id,\n    )\n    await _materialize_repo_checkout(\n        state.repo_path,\n        target_repo_path,\n        remote_url,\n        access_token=access_token,\n    )\n    workspace_paths: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    for workspace_id, branch in state.workspaces:\n        target_workspace_path = _workspace_path(target_repo_path, branch)\n        await restore_worktree(target_repo_path, target_workspace_path, branch)\n        workspace_paths.append((workspace_id, target_workspace_path))\n    return WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation(\n        workspace_id=state.workspace_id,\n        repo_id=state.repo_id,\n        repo_path=target_repo_path,\n        remote_url=remote_url,\n        installation_id=installation_id,\n        workspace_paths=tuple(workspace_paths),\n        update_repo_metadata=True,\n        repaired_repo=True,\n    )\n\n\ndef apply_workspace_checkout_preparation(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    preparation: WorkspaceCheckoutPreparation,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Apply deterministic checkout metadata updates in one transaction.\"\"\"\n    if preparation.update_repo_metadata:\n        for workspace_id, workspace_path in preparation.workspace_paths:\n            db.execute(\n                \"UPDATE workspaces SET path = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                (workspace_path, workspace_id),\n            )\n        db.execute(\n            \"\"\"UPDATE repos\n               SET root_path = ?, remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\"\"\",\n            (\n                preparation.repo_path,\n                preparation.remote_url,\n                preparation.installation_id,\n                preparation.repo_id,\n            ),\n        )\n        db.commit()\n        if preparation.repaired_repo:\n            logger.info(\"Repaired repository into tenant storage\")\n    return dict(_fetch_workspace(db, preparation.workspace_id))\n\n\nasync def ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    repo_id: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Repair migrated tenant repo/workspace paths into the tenant data directory.\n\n    Legacy migrations copied root_path and worktree paths into the per-user DB\n    without relocating them. This lazily repairs those records the first time\n    the repo is used after migration.\n    \"\"\"\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    repo_path = repo[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo root_path must not be empty\"\n    remote_url = repo[\"remote_url\"]\n    repo_keys = repo.keys()\n    installation_id = repo[\"installation_id\"] if \"installation_id\" in repo_keys else None\n    source_repo_is_available = await validate_local_repo(repo_path)\n\n    if _tenant_path_is_trusted(tenant, repo_path):\n        if source_repo_is_available and not await _trusted_repo_needs_refresh(\n            repo_path,\n            remote_url,\n            installation_id,\n        ):\n            return dict(repo)\n\n        refreshed_remote_url, _, refreshed_installation_id = await _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n            tenant,\n            repo_path,\n            remote_url,\n            installation_id,\n        )\n        remote_was_updated = await _sync_repo_checkout_remote(repo_path, refreshed_remote_url)\n        metadata_changed = (\n            refreshed_remote_url != remote_url or refreshed_installation_id != installation_id\n        )\n        if not remote_was_updated and not metadata_changed:\n            return dict(repo)\n\n        db.execute(\n            \"UPDATE repos SET remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n            (refreshed_remote_url, refreshed_installation_id, repo_id),\n        )\n        db.commit()\n        return dict(_fetch_repo(db, repo_id))\n\n    target_repo_path = _tenant_repo_path(tenant, repo_id)\n    remote_url, access_token, installation_id = await _refresh_repo_remote_metadata(\n        tenant,\n        repo_path,\n        remote_url,\n        installation_id,\n    )\n    await _materialize_repo_checkout(\n        repo_path,\n        target_repo_path,\n        remote_url,\n        access_token=access_token,\n    )\n\n    workspaces = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT * FROM workspaces WHERE repo_id = ? ORDER BY created_at ASC\",\n        (repo_id,),\n    ).fetchall()\n    for workspace in workspaces:\n        branch = workspace[\"branch\"]\n        if not branch:\n            raise WorkspaceNotFoundError(f\"Workspace {workspace['id']} is missing its branch name\")\n        target_workspace_path = _workspace_path(target_repo_path, branch)\n        await restore_worktree(target_repo_path, target_workspace_path, branch)\n        db.execute(\n            \"UPDATE workspaces SET path = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n            (target_workspace_path, workspace[\"id\"]),\n        )\n\n    db.execute(\n        \"UPDATE repos SET root_path = ?, remote_url = ?, installation_id = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n        (target_repo_path, remote_url, installation_id, repo_id),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n    logger.info(\"Repaired repository into tenant storage\")\n\n    updated_repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    return dict(updated_repo)\n\n\nasync def relink_github_repos_for_tenant(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    owner_login: str,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Refresh existing tenant repos after one GitHub App installation is connected.\"\"\"\n    if not owner_login:\n        raise ValueError(\"owner_login must not be empty\")\n    if isolation_setup_required():\n        logger.info(\"Deferring GitHub repository refresh while isolation is unsupported\")\n        return 0\n    refreshed_repo_count = 0\n    repos = db.execute(\n        \"SELECT id FROM repos WHERE remote_url IS NOT NULL ORDER BY created_at ASC\"\n    ).fetchall()\n\n    for repo_row in repos:\n        repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_row[\"id\"])\n        remote_url = repo[\"remote_url\"]\n        if not isinstance(remote_url, str) or not remote_url:\n            continue\n        github_remote = normalize_github_remote(remote_url)\n        if github_remote is None:\n            continue\n        if github_remote.owner.lower() != owner_login.lower():\n            continue\n\n        refreshed_repo = await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(db, tenant, repo[\"id\"])\n        if refreshed_repo[\"remote_url\"] != repo[\"remote_url\"]:\n            refreshed_repo_count += 1\n            continue\n        if refreshed_repo[\"installation_id\"] != repo[\"installation_id\"]:\n            refreshed_repo_count += 1\n\n    return refreshed_repo_count\n\n\nasync def ensure_workspace_checkout_for_tenant(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    tenant: TenantContext,\n    workspace_id: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Repair the repo backing a workspace and return the updated workspace row.\"\"\"\n    workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    repo_id = workspace[\"repo_id\"]\n    assert repo_id, \"workspace repo_id must not be empty\"\n\n    await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(db, tenant, repo_id)\n    updated_workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    return dict(updated_workspace)\n\n\nasync def create_workspace_for_repo(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    repo_id: str,\n    name: str | None = None,\n    username: str | None = None,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree while holding its repository lifecycle lock.\"\"\"\n    _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n    require_isolated_execution(\"trusted_git\")\n    lock_root = repository_lifecycle_root(db, tenant)\n    async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n        return await _create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(\n            db,\n            repo_id,\n            name=name,\n            username=username,\n            tenant=tenant,\n        )\n\n\nasync def _create_workspace_for_repo_unlocked(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    repo_id: str,\n    name: str | None = None,\n    username: str | None = None,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Create a new worktree after repository lifecycle serialization.\"\"\"\n    from yinshi.services.repository_lifecycle import require_no_repository_deletion\n\n    require_no_repository_deletion(db, repo_id)\n    if tenant is not None:\n        await ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant(db, tenant, repo_id)\n\n    repo = _fetch_repo(db, repo_id)\n\n    branch = generate_branch_name(username=username)\n    if not name:\n        name = branch\n\n    repo_path = repo[\"root_path\"]\n    assert repo_path, \"repo_path must not be empty\"\n    worktree_dir = _workspace_path(repo_path, branch)\n    base_ref: str | None = None\n\n    remote_url = repo[\"remote_url\"]\n    if remote_url:\n        access_token = None\n        try:\n            if tenant is not None:\n                _, access_token, _ = await _resolve_remote_checkout(tenant, remote_url)\n            base_ref = await resolve_remote_base_ref(repo_path, access_token=access_token)\n        except GitError:\n            logger.warning(\"Creating worktree from local HEAD after remote sync failure\")\n            base_ref = None\n\n    await create_worktree(repo_path, worktree_dir, branch, base_ref=base_ref)\n    ensure_secret_guardrails(repo_path)\n\n    cursor = db.execute(\n        \"\"\"INSERT INTO workspaces (repo_id, name, branch, path, state)\n           VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 'ready')\"\"\",\n        (repo_id, name, branch, worktree_dir),\n    )\n    db.commit()\n\n    row = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM workspaces WHERE rowid = ?\", (cursor.lastrowid,)).fetchone()\n    return dict(row)\n\n\nasync def delete_workspace(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    workspace_id: str,\n    *,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Delete a workspace while holding its repository lifecycle lock.\"\"\"\n    workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    repo_id = str(workspace[\"repo_id\"])\n    lock_root = repository_lifecycle_root(db, tenant)\n    async with repository_lifecycle(repo_id, lock_root):\n        await _delete_workspace_unlocked(db, workspace_id, tenant=tenant)\n\n\nasync def _delete_workspace_unlocked(\n    db: sqlite3.Connection,\n    workspace_id: str,\n    *,\n    tenant: TenantContext | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Delete one workspace after repository lifecycle serialization.\"\"\"\n    workspace = _fetch_workspace(db, workspace_id)\n    ensure_workspace_has_no_delegated_children(db, workspace_id)\n\n    session_rows = []\n    if tenant is None:\n        session_rows = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT id FROM sessions WHERE workspace_id = ?\",\n            (workspace_id,),\n        ).fetchall()\n\n    repo = _fetch_repo(db, workspace[\"repo_id\"])\n    await delete_worktree(repo[\"root_path\"], workspace[\"path\"])\n\n    if tenant is not None:\n        delete_workspace_runtime_home(tenant, workspace_id)\n    else:\n        for session_row in session_rows:\n            try:\n                delete_local_pi_session_file(session_row[\"id\"])\n            except OSError:\n                logger.warning(\"Failed to delete Pi session file\")\n\n    db.execute(\"DELETE FROM workspaces WHERE id = ?\", (workspace_id,))\n    db.commit()\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789287878758}}
