{"type":"message","id":"3611ba91","parentId":"664cced9","timestamp":"2026-09-13T10:08:26.020Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_GeGDPNflj1vBqMW6Zh3iq2QN|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa67619862087d0ac7c439834d10d6f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: rp-build\ndescription: Plan and implement substantial changes with RepoPrompt Context Builder. Use for unfamiliar repositories or changes spanning several files.\ncompatibility: Requires RepoPrompt MCP and Pi file tools.\n---\n\n# RepoPrompt Build\n\nUse the user's request as the task.\n\nStart with Git status. Locate the repository root before asking RepoPrompt to inspect anything.\n\nCall `repoprompt_context_builder` with a precise task description and `response_type: \"plan\"`. Review its plan and assumptions before changing files. Call `repoprompt_workspace_context` when you need the complete selected context. Ask the user only when an unresolved choice would materially change behavior or scope.\n\nImplement through Pi `edit` and `write`. The OrbStack repository mount is read-only, so never use RepoPrompt `apply_edits` or `file_actions`. Follow repository test-first rules for behavior changes. Run focused tests after each change, then run broader relevant checks.\n\nDo not improvise.\n\nUse `repoprompt_oracle_send` only for a specific question left open by Context Builder. Continue with the returned `chat_id` rather than starting an unrelated conversation.\n\nFor substantial changes, run RepoPrompt review against the final Git diff. Report changed files and commands run. Include validation results and remaining risks. Do not claim completion while required checks fail.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789294106020}}
{"type":"message","id":"c0a23ffd","parentId":"3611ba91","timestamp":"2026-09-13T10:08:37.727Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning artifact transport lifecycle**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6761c12f487d0bf1555cc9f2f1638\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning artifact transport lifecycle**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_x47rzEC2rMQMBQw3r8Ts8e4R|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6761cce2087d0af822238aa5f83ba","name":"repoprompt_context_builder","arguments":{"instructions":"<task>Complete the next production Phase 6 milestone: design and implement bounded authenticated exact-three-artifact transport plus broker dispatch and concrete ingest/verify/publish lifecycle effects, using the existing BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator, BrokerReplicaJournal, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, WorkspaceReplicaArtifactStore, signed BrokerRequest/BrokerResponse protocol, broker daemon, and opaque stdio relay. Preserve executor.launch behavior and framing.</task><context>The current signed JSON control frame is capped at 65,536 bytes and artifacts may approach 1 GiB, so artifact bytes must not enter the frame or SQLite. Exactly three artifacts are committed.bundle, worktree.yra, and index-objects.pack. Request metadata authenticates exact IDs, digests, lengths, roles, media types, artifact_set_sha256, source-state digest, reconciliation fingerprint, limits_sha256, authority, and generation. Add a distinct bounded authenticated data plane rather than enlarging BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX. Existing stdio relay is opaque, fixed socket, and one request frame only. Existing BrokerService handles only executor.launch and its validation must not weaken. All gates remain default-disabled. No SQLite handle may cross await. Unknown timeout/cancellation/transport/verification/acknowledgment remains stage-specific unresolved. Do not invent admission/drain/export/reclaim yet beyond interfaces. Need tests before or with implementation and exact production wiring only where contracts are settled. RepoPrompt checkout may be stale, so verify APIs against actual host checkout before edits.</context><discovery_agent-guidelines>Inspect backend services around execution_broker.py, broker_protocol.py, broker_stdio_relay.py, broker_replica_lifecycle.py, broker_replica_journal.py, broker_artifact_store.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, execution_daemons.py, config.py, main.py, and focused tests. Identify the smallest secure production milestone and any unresolved product choices that block it.</discovery_agent-guidelines>","response_type":"plan"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":528,"output":437,"cacheRead":80256,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":22,"totalTokens":81221,"cost":{"input":0.0026400000000000004,"output":0.01311,"cacheRead":0.040128,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.055878}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789294106025,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6761a914487d08d5bef9e497aebda","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
