rokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` currently orchestrates abstract effects only. It has no concrete ingest, verification, or publication implementation.\\n\\n`ReplicaLifecycleContext` contains request, authority, and owner token. It lacks an upload reader, configured limits, pinned artifacts, and prior receipts. See `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:137-149`.\\n\\nExisting lifecycle tests use synthetic `_Effect` implementations. They prove ordering and unknown handling, but not artifact integration. See `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py:216-239`.\\n\\n## Exact conversion\\n\\n### Request payload to ingest manifest\\n\\nAuthenticated payload fields are strict and exact:\\n\\n- `artifact_set_sha256`\\n- `bundle`\\n- `worktree`\\n- `index_objects`\\n- `limits_sha256`\\n- `object_format`\\n- `source_state_sha256`\\n- `reconciliation_fingerprint`\\n- `repository_id`\\n- `workspace_id`\\n\\nJournal validation occurs at `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:650-682`.\\n\\nEach artifact object becomes `ArtifactReference` without changing:\\n\\n- `artifact_id`\\n- `sha256`\\n- `byte_length`\\n- `media_type`\\n\\nConcrete conversion must create:\\n\\n```python\\nReplicaArtifactManifest(\\n    operation_id=request.operation_id,\\n    bundle=<payload bundle ArtifactReference>,\\n    worktree=<payload worktree ArtifactReference>,\\n    index_objects=<payload index_objects ArtifactReference>,\\n)\\n```\\n\\nBefore reading bytes, recompute artifact-set identity using request metadata plus `ReplicaAuthority`. Journal uses this projection at `broker_replica_journal.py:536-564`.\\n\\nAuthority supplies:\\n\\n- `physical_target_id`\\n- `replica_generation`\\n- `execution_owner_id`\\n\\nThese fields are absent from payload by design. Effects must never infer them from paths or request identifiers.\\n\\n### Manifest and authority to publication declaration\\n\\nConcrete conversion must create `ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration` with:\\n\\n- `version=2`\\n- `operation_id=request.operation_id`\\n- repository and workspace IDs from payload\\n- all three authority fields from `context.authority`\\n- object format, source digest, and fingerprint from payload\\n- full configured `ReplicaArtifactLimits`\\n- one `ReplicaArtifactBinding` per artifact\\n\\nBinding conversion must preserve artifact identity fields and add fixed roles:\\n\\n| Manifest member | Binding role | Fixed filename |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `bundle` | `committed_bundle` | `committed.bundle` |\\n| `worktree` | `worktree` | `worktree.yra` |\\n| `index_objects` | `index_objects` | `index-objects.pack` |\\n\\nFixed names and media types come from `backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py:16-34`.\\n\\nThe declaration recomputes the same version-2 identity defined at `replica_artifact_contract.py:63-101`.\\n\\nA request contains only `limits_sha256`, not the full limits object. The concrete effect therefore needs the exact configured limits separately. It must confirm:\\n\\n```python\\npublication_store.limits_sha256 == payload[\\\"limits_sha256\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n### Typed receipts\\n\\n#### Ingest\\n\\n`BrokerArtifactStore.receive()` already returns journal type `IngestReceipt`. No conversion beyond returning it is needed.\\n\\nReceipt contains the exact three references and a deterministic receipt ID. See `broker_artifact_store.py:178-207`.\\n\\n#### Verify\\n\\nConvert `ReplicaVerificationReceipt` to journal `VerifyReceipt`:\\n\\n```python\\nVerifyReceipt(\\n    receipt_id=verification.verification_receipt_id,\\n    bundle_sha256=verification.bundle.sha256,\\n    worktree_sha256=verification.worktree.sha256,\\n    index_objects_sha256=verification.index_objects.sha256,\\n    source_state_sha256=verification.source_state_sha256,\\n    reconciliation_fingerprint=verification.reconciliation_fingerprint,\\n    artifact_set_sha256=verification.artifact_set_sha256,\\n)\\n```\\n\\nJournal checks every field against accepted request state at `broker_replica_journal.py:925-953`.\\n\\n#### Publish\\n\\nConvert `ReplicaPublicationReceipt` to journal `PublishReceipt`:\\n\\n```python\\nPublishReceipt(\\n    receipt_id=publication.publication_receipt_id,\\n    physical_target_id=publication.physical_target_id,\\n    replica_generation=publication.replica_generation,\\n    execution_owner_id=publication.execution_owner_id,\\n    publication_marker_sha256=publication.publication_marker_sha256,\\n    synchronization_receipt_id=publication.synchronization_receipt_id,\\n    artifact_set_sha256=publication.artifact_set_sha256,\\n)\\n```\\n\\nJournal checks authority and artifact-set binding at `broker_replica_journal.py:954-962`.\\n\\n## Durable reconciliation\\n\\n### Ingest\\n\\nCurrent store provides useful primitives:\\n\\n- `receive()` consumes exact bytes and safely reuses an exact existing set.\\n- `open_incoming_async()` pins verified incoming files.\\n- `recheck_opened_async()` verifies pinned identities after external work.\\n- `reconcile_attempts()` quarantines pending attempts and validates known final sets.\\n\\nRelevant implementation appears in `broker_artifact_store.py:467-647`, `840-948`, and `950-1075`.\\n\\nRequired per-operation reconciliation:\\n\\n- Exact verified final directory: `completed` with reconstructed `IngestReceipt`.\\n- No final and no pending or retained ambiguity: `not_applied`.\\n- Malformed final, quarantine failure, pending/final conflict, or uncertain lookup: `unknown`.\\n- Never classify malformed existing state as clean absence.\\n\\n`reconcile_attempts()` does not return a result for a completely absent operation. A concrete effect cannot safely distinguish absence through `inspect_incoming()` alone.\\n\\n### Verification\\n\\nVerification has no separate durable effect marker. Reconciliation can repeat read-only semantic verification against pinned incoming descriptors.\\n\\nOutcomes:\\n\\n- Exact incoming files verify: `completed` with deterministic `VerifyReceipt`.\\n- Exact incoming set is conclusively absent: `not_applied`.\\n- Incoming identity changed, final state is malformed, Git outcome is uncertain, or inspection fails: `unknown`.\\n\\nReverification must not reopen artifacts by pathname between checks.\\n\\n### Publication\\n\\nCurrent publication inspection can reconstruct a publication receipt for a valid final set. However, no API returns a typed clean-absence versus ambiguous-state decision.\\n\\nRequired outcomes:\\n\\n- Exact final publication and marker verify: `completed`.\\n- Final and pending state are conclusively absent: `not_applied`.\\n- Corrupt final, retained pending state, rename uncertainty, or synchronization uncertainty: `unknown`.\\n\\nAfter `not_applied`, coordinator safely runs publication again. After `unknown`, later stages remain blocked.\\n\\n### Journal restart behavior\\n\\nThe journal retains exact authenticated frame, authority, owner, next stage, and `stage_started`. See `broker_replica_journal.py:1977-2026`.\\n\\nSame-incarnation recovery reconciles a started stage. A different broker incarnation records `broker_restart_unknown` without invoking reconciliation. See `broker_replica_lifecycle.py:288-317`.\\n\\nTerminal unresolved records are excluded from `incomplete_lifecycles()`. Exact retries replay the unresolved response. They do not retry external reconciliation.\\n\\n## Path pinning\\n\\n`BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async()` already pins:\\n\\n- store root descriptor\\n- operation-directory descriptor\\n- three read-only artifact descriptors\\n- device and inode identities\\n\\n`recheck_opened_async()` checks root, directory, fixed entries, ownership, permissions, link count, size, digest, and named identity.\\n\\nCurrent `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` accepts complete `bytes` values. Its verifier also consumes bytes. This forces whole-file memory retention and loses the incoming descriptor chain.\\n\\nProduction flow must retain incoming descriptors across:\\n\\n1. semantic verification,\\n2. post-verification recheck,\\n3. publication copy,\\n4. post-copy source recheck.\\n\\nArtifact IDs must remain logical identifiers. Only validated operation IDs may select operation directories. `physical_target_id` requires configured target resolution and must not become an unchecked path.\\n\\n## Cancellation and unknown classification\\n\\nCoordinator behavior:\\n\\n- Timeout abandons the task and records `timeout_unknown`.\\n- Caller cancellation abandons the task, durably records `cancellation_unknown`, then reraises cancellation.\\n- An abandoned effect may continue.\\n- Late completion cannot append a journal completion.\\n- Same-process retries wait for the abandoned task before inspecting journal state.\\n\\nSee `broker_replica_lifecycle.py:442-524` and `696-711`.\\n\\nStore behavior differs by visibility point:\\n\\n- Cancellation before artifact rename quarantines the owned pending attempt.\\n- Cancellation after rename becomes `BrokerArtifactStoreUnresolvedError`.\\n- Publication cancellation after final visibility becomes `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError`.\\n\\nConcrete classification should be:\\n\\n| Condition | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| Invalid declaration, digest mismatch, truncation, trailing bytes, fixed collision | stage rejection |\\n| I/O uncertainty, timeout, fsync uncertainty, rename uncertainty | stage-specific unknown |\\n| Caller cancellation before confirmed no-effect boundary | `cancellation_unknown` |\\n| Valid durable final found during reconciliation | completed |\\n| Proven clean absence | not applied |\\n| Malformed or unclassifiable durable state | unknown |\\n\\nExpected generic unknown codes are already stage-specific:\\n\\n- ingest: `transfer_unknown`\\n- verify: `verification_unknown`\\n- publish: `publication_unknown`\\n\\n## Required API additions\\n\\n1. Add a public typed request projection helper. It should produce manifest and declaration from authenticated request, authority, and configured limits.\\n2. Expose full immutable publication limits, not only `limits_sha256`.\\n3. Add connection-scoped upload input to broker service or lifecycle invocation. Do not store a reader on singleton effects.\\n4. Add journal access to validated prior stage receipts. Publication must require the exact verify receipt.\\n5. Add `BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_operation(manifest)` with explicit completed, absent, and unknown states.\\n6. Add descriptor-based semantic verifier APIs:\\n   - `verify_committed_bundle_file(...)`\\n   - `verify_index_object_pack_file(...)`\\n   - `inspect_worktree_artifact_file(...)`\\n7. Add descriptor-based publication API accepting `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` plus matching verification receipt.\\n8. Add typed publication reconciliation API that distinguishes clean absence from ambiguity.\\n9. Add journal enumeration for accepted artifact manifests if startup reconciliation must include terminal-unknown operations.\\n10. Add broker service ownership for duplicate upload consumption. Coordinator currently skips ingest after durable ingest completion.\\n\\n## Review findings\\n\\n1. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:154-219` has abstract effect injection only. No production artifact effects are wired.\\n2. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:137-149` lacks upload input and prior receipts. Concrete ingest and verified publication cannot meet contracts.\\n3. **Blocker:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:618-1154` uses whole-file byte APIs. Production descriptor pinning and bounded memory are unavailable.\\n4. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:840-948` lacks an explicit clean-absence per-operation result.\\n5. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py` lacks durable typed publication reconciliation.\\n6. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1977-2006` excludes terminal unknown operations from recovery. Late durable effects remain unresolved indefinitely.\\n7. **High:** `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:288-307` classifies cross-incarnation restart as unknown without filesystem reconciliation.\\n8. **High:** request payload provides only a limits digest. Declaration construction needs the exact configured `ReplicaArtifactLimits`.\\n9. **Medium:** existing lifecycle tests are synthetic. No test proves payload-to-manifest conversion, descriptor continuity, receipt conversion, or duplicate-body consumption.\\n\\n## Rejected explanations\\n\\n- “Current callbacks can directly use the store.” Rejected because lifecycle context has no upload reader.\\n- “Current publication bytes API is sufficient.” Rejected because it requires whole artifacts in memory and breaks descriptor continuity.\\n- “Journal validation provides the prior verify receipt.” Rejected because it validates writes but exposes no receipt getter to effects.\\n- “`reconcile_attempts()` proves not-applied.” Rejected because a completely absent operation produces no explicit result.\\n- “A retry consumes duplicate upload bytes.” Rejected because coordinator resumes after ingest and never invokes ingest again.\\n\\n## Residual risks\\n\\n- Terminal unknown operations can retain valid incoming or published state without automatic reconciliation.\\n- Abandoned tasks require connection-reader lifetime ownership beyond the caller task.\\n- Publication target-root selection remains unspecified.\\n- Descriptor-backed Git verification needs timeout, cancellation, and scrubbed-environment tests.\\n- Compatibility policy for existing byte publication API remains undecided.\\n\\nNo files were modified. Tests were not run because this task required read-only implementation analysis.\",\n        \"controlEvents\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"ts\": 1789294502158,\n            \"runId\": \"62fd0921\",\n            \"agent\": \"worker-expert\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": \"worker-expert is still active but long-running\",\n            \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n            \"turns\": 11,\n            \"tokens\": 282843,\n            \"toolCount\": 58,\n            \"elapsedMs\": 240038\n          }\n        ],\n        \"attemptedModels\": [\n          \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\"\n        ],\n        \"modelAttempts\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:xhigh\",\n            \"success\": true,\n            \"exitCode\": 0,\n            \"usage\": {\n              \"input\": 288427,\n              \"output\": 9471,\n              \"cacheRead\": 507392,\n              \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n              \"cost\": 1.979961,\n              \"turns\": 12\n            }\n          }\n        ],\n        \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/62fd0921/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n        \"acceptance\": {\n          \"status\": \"attested\",\n          \"evidenceStatus\": \"attested\",\n          \"explicit\": false,\n          \"effectiveAcceptance\": {\n            \"level\": \"attested\",\n            \"explicit\": false,\n            \"inferredReason\": [\n              \"read-only task wording\"\n            ],\n            \"criteria\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n                \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n                \"evidence\": [\n                  \"review-findings\",\n                  \"residual-risks\"\n                ],\n                \"severity\": \"required\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"evidence\": [\n              \"review-findings\",\n              \"residual-risks\"\n            ],\n            \"verify\": [],\n            \"stopRules\": []\n          },\n          \"inferredReason\": [\n            \"read-only task wording\"\n          ],\n          \"criteria\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": [\n                \"review-findings\",\n                \"residual-risks\"\n              ],\n              \"severity\": \"required\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"runtimeChecks\": [],\n          \"verifyRuns\": [],\n          \"childReport\": {\n            \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n                \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n                \"evidence\": \"Concrete findings include file paths, line ranges, severity, conversion rules, required APIs, and residual risks.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"changedFiles\": [],\n            \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [],\n            \"commandsRun\": [\n              {\n                \"command\": \"git status --short\",\n                \"result\": \"passed\",\n                \"summary\": \"Confirmed existing unstaged and untracked working-tree changes. No files were staged by this analysis.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"command\": \"read and line-number inspection of lifecycle, journal, artifact store, publication store, artifact contract, and tests\",\n                \"result\": \"passed\",\n                \"summary\": \"Inspected requested implementation and test surfaces.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"command\": \"pytest\",\n                \"result\": \"not-run\",\n                \"summary\": \"Read-only analysis requested. No implementation validation was needed.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"validationOutput\": [\n              \"No repository files were modified.\",\n              \"Current lifecycle tests use synthetic effects only.\",\n              \"Current artifact store exposes pinned incoming descriptors.\",\n              \"Current publication production surface accepts whole-file bytes rather than pinned incoming descriptors.\"\n            ],\n            \"residualRisks\": [\n              \"Terminal unknown operations are not included in automatic incomplete-lifecycle recovery.\",\n              \"Cross-incarnation restart records broker_restart_unknown without filesystem reconciliation.\",\n              \"Upload reader ownership and duplicate-body consumption remain undefined.\",\n              \"Full configured limits and prior verification receipts are unavailable to concrete effects.\",\n              \"Descriptor-backed semantic verification and publication APIs do not exist.\"\n            ],\n            \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n            \"diffSummary\": \"No diff. Read-only analysis only.\",\n            \"reviewFindings\": [\n              \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:154-219 - coordinator has abstract effects only and no production ingest, verify, or publish wiring.\",\n              \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:137-149 - lifecycle context lacks upload input, configured limits, pinned artifacts, and prior receipts.\",\n              \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:618-1154 - publication uses whole-file bytes and cannot preserve incoming descriptor pinning.\",\n              \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:840-948 - reconciliation lacks an explicit per-operation clean-absence result.\",\n              \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py:1977-2006 - terminal unknown operations are excluded from durable recovery.\",\n              \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:288-307 - cross-incarnation restart becomes unknown without effect reconciliation.\",\n              \"medium: backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py:216-239 - tests cover synthetic effects but not concrete artifact integration.\"\n            ],\n            \"manualNotes\": \"Working tree contained many pre-existing unstaged and untracked files. This analysis changed none.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"toolCalls\": [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/AGENTS.md\\\"}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/AGENTS.md\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*broker_replic...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*broker_replica_lifecycle*\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*broker_artifa...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*broker_artifact_store*\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*workspace_rep...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"find {\\\"path\\\":\\\".\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/*workspace_replica_publication*\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ git status --short && pwd\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ git status --short && pwd\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"Artifac...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"ArtifactContract|artifact contract|artifact_contract|ArtifactManifest|ArtifactDeclaration\\\",\\\"ignoreCase\\\":true,\\\"context\\\":2}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"Broke...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator|replica_lifecycle|artifact_store|replica_publication\\\",\\\"ignoreCase\\\":true,\\\"context\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\"...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"Replica...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"ReplicaLifecycleEffects\\\\\\\\(|ReplicaArtifactManifest\\\\\\\\(|ReplicaArtifactSetDeclaration\\\\\\\\(\\\",\\\"context\\\":3,\\\"limit\\\":100}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerA...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"BrokerArtifactStore\\\",\\\"context\\\":3,\\\"limit\\\":100}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"Workspa...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore\\\",\\\"context\\\":3,\\\"limit\\\":100}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"broker_...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"broker_replica\\\",\\\"context\\\":2,\\\"limit\\\":100}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"verif...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/tests\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"verify_artifact_set|publish_artifact_set|inspect_published_artifact_set\\\",\\\"glob\\\":\\\"test_workspace_replica_publication.py\\\",\\\"cont...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ nl -ba