" /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src /Users/user/projects/yinshi/sidecar/src 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\".pyc\\\" | grep -vE \\\"worksp...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -c \\\"def test\\\" /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -c \\\"def test\\\" /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py; echo ===; grep -n \\\"class\\\\|def test\\\" /Users/user/projects/yinshi/back...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ git status --porcelain | head -30; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"Broke...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ git status --porcelain | head -30; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"BrokerArtifactStore(\\\" backend/src backend/tests | grep -v \\\".pyc\\\" | head; echo ===; grep -n \\\"def test\\\" backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -n \\\"_read_descriptor\\\\|_open_pinned_regular\\\\|_recheck_pi...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -n \\\"_read_descriptor\\\\|_open_pinned_regular\\\\|_recheck_pinned_regular\\\\|def _inspect_pending\\\\|def _inspect_final\\\\|content=\\\\|pinned.content\\\\|def _match_content\\\\|def _verify_artifact_set\\\\|async def publish_artifact_set\\\\|async def verify_art...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -n \\\"_GIT_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_S\\\" backend/src/yinshi/services...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -n \\\"_GIT_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_S\\\" backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py | head -3\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && python -m pytest t...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && python -m pytest tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py -q 2>&1 | tail -6\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend | head; ls /Users/use...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend | head; ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/.venv/bin/python 2>/dev/null || ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/venv/bin/python 2>/dev/null; python -c \\\"import yinshi\\\" 2>&1 | head -2\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && ./.venv/bin/python...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py -q 2>&1 | tail -4\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"key\": \"dispatch\",\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"runId\": \"300f48e3\",\n    \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 16 assistant turns (soft limit 16, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nAll evidence gathered (read-only; working tree untouched — still the 143 pre-existing changes). Here is the design and findings report.\\n\\n# Broker Request Dispatch Design — `executor.launch` + `replica.artifacts.upload` + `replica.lifecycle`\\n\\n## 1. Actual state (verified against code)\\n\\n**Executor pipeline (complete, strict, disabled by default)**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:26` — `_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE = \\\"executor.launch\\\"`; `_authenticate()` (peer UID == `application_uid`, Ed25519 verify, incarnation match, forbidden-control scan `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS`, which includes `\\\"replica\\\"`); `handle()` = authenticate → `BrokerJournal.accept` (durable, replay-safe) → `claim_lifecycle` → owner runs `prepare → runtime_setup → launch`; non-owners poll `status()` for the stored response.\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py` — append-only SQLite v2 with `nonce_once`, `sequence_once`, one-acceptance/one-claim/one-terminal indexes; identities are `(database_incarnation, operation_id, request_type)`; commit-uncertainty re-verification (`JournalCommitAbsent`).\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` — `_exchange_broker()` enforces kernel peer UID **before** reading one length-prefixed frame (`_read_frame` rejects trailing bytes), calls `service.handle(body, peer_uid)`, writes one bounded response; `broker_connection_handler` = exactly one exchange per connection; `MAX_CONNECTIONS=8`, `CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120`; `_run_broker()` runs `service.recover_startup()` pre-serve; `load_broker_config` requires an exact key set pinned to compiled paths; launcher gates default false via `resolve_boolean_gate` (`YINSHI_LAUNCH_EXECUTION_ENABLED` etc.).\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` — opaque relay: **one** request frame in, **one** response frame out; `read_blocking_frame` requires EOF after the frame; `_exchange` does `write_eof()` after the request.\\n- `deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service` — `REDACTED`, deliberately not enabled at boot.\\n\\n**Replica stack (built and committed, but wired to nothing)**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py` — separate SQLite journal for `replica.lifecycle` only (`_request_from_frame` hard-requires the type); own `request_public_key`, per-incarnation `response_public_keys` keyring, `expected_limits_sha256` folded into a `journal_id` configuration hash validated on every open; full historical replay + re-signature-verification on **every** open; `accept(request, frame, authority)` binds `authority` transitively via `artifact_set_sha256`; **no nonce-once or sequence-once index**.\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py` — `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run(request, request_frame, authority)` drives fixed stages `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`; per-operation asyncio gates; `recover_incomplete()` resumes same-incarnation lifecycles and marks cross-incarnation ones `broker_restart_unknown`; terminal responses validated to exactly `{stage, state[, code][, receipt_id]}`.\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` — `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(manifest, reader)` streams **raw bytes after the signed frame** from an `asyncio.StreamReader` (3 fixed files, 512 MiB/role, 1 GiB/set, 120 s transfer / 30 s idle timeouts), atomic no-replace publish, quarantine + `reconcile_attempts`; requires `expected_uid == os.geteuid()` (broker UID 999).\\n- No production code creates signed requests (`create_signed_request` has zero non-test callers); the name `replica.artifacts.upload` appears **nowhere** in the repository — it is a new request type.\\n- Tests: `test_broker_foundation.py` (unsupported type rejected), `test_execution_daemons.py` (one peer-bound exchange; strictly nested deadlines `30 < 35 < 40 < 120`), and the 97 replica journal/lifecycle/artifact-store tests all pass (see commands).\\n\\n## 2. Proposed dispatch design (no code changed)\\n\\n1. **Single front door, per-type pipelines.** Keep the daemon peer-UID check in `_exchange_broker` exactly as is. Add one dispatcher that calls `parse_signed_request` once (signature is over the whole frame, so routing necessarily follows verification), checks both incarnations, then routes on `request.request_type`:\\n   - `executor.launch` → `BrokerService.handle(frame, peer_uid=…)` **unchanged** (it re-verifies; zero behavioral delta, forbidden-field scan stays scoped here — note `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS` contains `\\\"replica\\\"`, so it must never be applied to replica payloads).\\n   - `replica.lifecycle` → `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run(request, frame, authority)`.\\n   - `replica.artifacts.upload` → new upload pipeline: build `ReplicaArtifactManifest` from the signed payload, then `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(manifest, reader)`.\\n   - anything else → today's `BrokerProtocolError(\\\"broker request type is not supported\\\")` (drop connection, no response — preserves the fail-closed precedent; one existing test asserts this).\\n2. **Authentication ownership.** Kernel peer UID stays daemon-owned (outermost). Ed25519 request authentication stays `parse_signed_request` with the application public key. The executor service keeps its own re-check (defense in depth). The replica journal re-authenticates stored frames on replay with its own `request_public_key`. Design rule: the replica `request_public_key` must be pinned equal to the executor `application_public_key` (or the divergence must be an explicit, documented config decision — see F-13).\\n3. **Separate journals.** Keep two files under broker-owned `/var/lib/yinshi/control/`: existing `broker-journal-v2.sqlite3` for `executor.launch`; new replica journal path (e.g. `replica-journal-v1.sqlite3`) added to `BrokerDaemonConfig`/`load_broker_config` (schema is exact-key, so this is a fail-closed config schema extension; old config must be rejected as `config_invalid`). One journal per request family is the only additive option: merging would require a shared stage machine and response schema (v3 redesign) — out of scope.\\n4. **Authority resolution.** `ReplicaAuthority` must become derivable from the signed frame: add `identity: {physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id}` to the `replica.lifecycle` payload. `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256` already digests exactly this identity object, so artifact-set digests remain valid; only `_validate_replica_payload`'s required-key set changes. The dispatcher then constructs `ReplicaAuthority` from signed fields and `accept()`'s digest binding becomes the cross-check. (F-1 — parent decision required.)\\n5. **Upload transport.** Two viable shapes, both requiring parent sign-off (F-4): (a) multi-frame mode on the existing socket — request frame, raw artifact bytes in fixed order, trailer; requires relaxing `_read_frame`'s trailing-byte rejection and the relay's one-frame/EOF contract; or (b) a **second systemd socket** (e.g. `/run/yinshi/broker-artifacts.sock`) with its own handler that streams — leaves the one-frame relay and `executor.launch` socket byte-for-byte intact. In both shapes, `BrokerService` never sees bytes; only the replica upload handler touches the reader.\\n6. **Response signatures.** All responses stay `create_signed_response` (identity-bound to the request, broker-signed, ≤ 4 096 B). Per-type `result` schemas: executor keeps `{launcher_status, lifecycle_stage}`; `replica.lifecycle` keeps the journal-validated `{stage, state[, code][, receipt_id]}`; upload needs a new schema (proposal: `{stored: true, receipt_id, artifact_set_sha256}` — no journal contract constrains it). Upload is idempotent via the deterministic ingest receipt (`_receipt()` content hash) and exact-manifest replay (`_receive_existing`).\\n7. **Startup recovery (order matters).** In `_run_broker`, before `serve()`: (1) `inspect_legacy_v1_journal` + `service.recover_startup()` (fail-closed unresolved, unchanged); (2) `BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts(manifests)` — quarantine live pendings, classify final dirs; (3) `coordinator.recover_incomplete()` — same-incarnation lifecycles re-drive (`reconcile=True` inspects the store: completed → replay; `not_applied` → fresh ingest), cross-incarnation → `broker_restart_unknown`. Step 2 before 3 so resumed ingests see a clean store. This needs a new public `BrokerReplicaJournal` accessor enumerating accepted-request manifests (F-6).\\n8. **Default-disabled gates/config.** Broker-side gates following the `resolve_boolean_gate` pattern (env **and** explicit flag, default false): `YINSHI_REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED` (dispatch of `replica.lifecycle`), `YINSHI_REPLICA_UPLOAD_ENABLED` (upload acceptance — the broker itself does the disk writes, so launcher gates cannot cover it). `replica.artifacts.upload` stays disabled until the lifecycle effects exist; the systemd unit gains `Environment=YINSHI_REPLICA_…=false` lines mirroring the existing pattern. New config keys: replica journal path, artifact store root (broker-owned 0700), limits blob (`compute_replica_limits_sha256`), request/response keyring.\\n9. **Concurrency/cancellation.** Upload serialization via the store's existing reservation lock + flock; per-operation coordinator gates prevent duplicate lifecycle drives; cancellation during upload quarantines the pending attempt (store already handles); abandoned-effect caps exist on both coordinators. Error mapping must be added: `ReplicaJournalSyncError` → `journal_unavailable`, `BrokerReplicaOwnerActive` → stable `owner_active` code (today both fall into `except Exception` → `internal_error`).\\n\\n## 3. Findings (contradictions / unresolved choices)\\n\\n- **F-1 (blocker for wiring):** `ReplicaAuthority` cannot be derived from a signed frame. The payload schema (`_validate_replica_payload`, broker_replica_journal.py:~466) is an exact 10-key set without identity fields, the broker daemon has no application DB, and `coordinator.run(request, frame, authority)` requires the authority as an argument. Dispatch is impossible without the §2.4 payload extension or an ownership change. Tests pass `AUTHORITY` out of band (test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py:313), masking this.\\n- **F-2 (high):** Replay-guard asymmetry: executor journal enforces nonce-once + monotonic `connection_sequence` per database incarnation (broker_journal.py indexes); the replica journal has neither — only exact-frame binding per operation. A shared sequence space across request types is unenforced anywhere; recorded as an accepted residual or fixed with replica nonce/sequence indexes.\\n- **F-3 (high):** Cross-incarnation recovery contradiction: `_record_unresolved`/`_signing_key` (broker_replica_lifecycle.py) sign with the private key of the **request's** incarnation, so recovering a lifecycle after key rotation requires retaining historical **private** keys (security-negative); the executor broker signs recovery responses with its current key while echoing request identity. Divergent ownership needs a parent ruling.\\n- **F-4 (high):** Transport cannot carry artifact bytes today: `broker_stdio_relay.py` is one-frame-then-EOF both directions; `_read_frame` (execution_daemons.py) rejects any trailing byte; `_exchange_broker` passes no reader into `service.handle`. Choosing multi-frame vs second socket changes a stated transport contract — parent decision.\\n- **F-5 (medium):** Deadline nesting breaks with current defaults: coordinator `effect_timeout_seconds` default 30 s < `LAUNCHER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` 35 s (a launcher-backed admission effect would die inner-first), and store `transfer_timeout_seconds` 120 s equals `CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` 120 s; `test_root_and_broker_deadlines_are_strictly_nested` must be extended to cover the new timers.\\n- **F-6 (medium):** No public `BrokerReplicaJournal` API returns accepted-request manifests for `BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts` (`incomplete_lifecycles` covers only claimed non-terminal lifecycles).\\n- **F-7 (medium):** No broker-side gate exists for replica dispatch/upload, and `load_broker_config`'s exact-key schema makes config extension a fail-closed schema-version decision.\\n- **F-8 (medium):** Recovery sequencing across three recoverers is unspecified in `_run_broker` (today only `service.recover_startup()` runs).\\n- **F-9 (low):** `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS` includes `\\\"replica\\\"` — harmless today (replica payload keys don't collide) but the scan must be explicitly scoped to `executor.launch` in the dispatcher.\\n- **F-10 (low):** `BrokerReplicaJournal._open()` replays and re-verifies every stored signature on every append — O(n²) cumulative cost; unbounded journal growth is a slow-DoS vector.\\n- **F-11 (low):** Replica error paths currently log `internal_error` (generic handler) instead of stable codes.\\n- **F-12 (unresolved):** Upload response `result` schema, and whether pre-acceptance replica validation failures may return signed error responses (executor precedent is a silent drop).\\n- **F-13 (unresolved):** Whether the replica `request_public_key` must equal the executor `application_public_key` (currently independently configured).\\n- **F-14 (unresolved):** Relationship between a `replica.lifecycle` `operation_id` and the executor launch `operation_id` (`AdmissionReceipt.runtime_unit_id` has no defined linkage).\\n- **F-15 (note):** `MAX_CONNECTIONS=8` is shared; a 120 s upload occupies a slot and can starve executor exchanges.\",\n    \"artifactPaths\": [\n      \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/300f48e3/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n    ],\n    \"results\": [\n      {\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"agent\": \"worker-advanced\",\n        \"task\": \"Read-only design of broker request dispatch preserving strict executor.launch validation while adding replica.artifacts.upload and replica.lifecycle. Inspect actual service/daemon/journal APIs. Cover authentication ownership, separate journals, startup recovery, response signatures, transport handlers, and default-disabled gates/config. Identify contradictions or unresolved choices. Do not modify.\",\n        \"routingContract\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"agent\": \"worker-advanced\",\n          \"model\": \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\",\n          \"thinking\": \"max\",\n          \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n        },\n        \"launchContractDigest\": \"784e90bbda5fdb051bef3e6ee5ca3a2d1a67b6b8aef8dd6d5c46df2ad73b1738\",\n        \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n          \"disableAmbientExtensions\": true,\n          \"runtime\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n          ],\n          \"configured\": [\n            \"sha256:890420901a90541d\"\n          ],\n          \"effective\": [\n            \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\",\n            \"sha256:890420901a90541d\"\n          ],\n          \"omitted\": {\n            \"runtime\": 0,\n            \"configured\": 0,\n            \"effective\": 0\n          }\n        },\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"outputState\": \"present\",\n        \"usage\": {\n          \"input\": 109186,\n          \"output\": 22561,\n          \"cacheRead\": 1318976,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n          \"cost\": 0,\n          \"turns\": 22\n        },\n        \"model\": \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max\",\n        \"thinking\": \"max\",\n        \"artifactPaths\": {\n          \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/300f48e3_worker-advanced_0_input.md\",\n          \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/300f48e3_worker-advanced_0_output.md\",\n          \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/300f48e3_worker-advanced_0.jsonl\",\n          \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/300f48e3_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n          \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/300f48e3_worker-advanced_0_meta.json\"\n        },\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/300f48e3_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n        \"turnBudget\": {\n          \"maxTurns\": 16,\n          \"graceTurns\": 3,\n          \"turnCount\": 22,\n          \"outcome\": \"wrap-up-requested\",\n          \"wrapUpRequestedAtTurn\": 16\n        },\n        \"toolBudget\": {\n          \"hard\": 80,\n          \"soft\": 55,\n          \"block\": [\n            \"bash\",\n            \"read\",\n            \"grep\",\n            \"find\",\n            \"ls\"\n          ],\n          \"toolCount\": 32,\n          \"outcome\": \"within-budget\"\n        },\n        \"context\": \"fresh\",\n        \"wrapUpRequested\": true,\n        \"progressSummary\": {\n          \"toolCount\": 32,\n          \"tokens\": 131747,\n          \"durationMs\": 791961\n        },\n        \"effects\": {\n          \"fileMutation\": {\n            \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n            \"expected\": false,\n            \"attempted\": true\n          }\n        },\n        \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n        \"finalOutput\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 16 assistant turns (soft limit 16, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nAll evidence gathered (read-only; working tree untouched — still the 143 pre-existing changes). Here is the design and findings report.\\n\\n# Broker Request Dispatch Design — `executor.launch` + `replica.artifacts.upload` + `replica.lifecycle`\\n\\n## 1. Actual state (verified against code)\\n\\n**Executor pipeline (complete, strict, disabled by default)**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:26` — `_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPE = \\\"executor.launch\\\"`; `_authenticate()` (peer UID == `application_uid`, Ed25519 verify, incarnation match, forbidden-control scan `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS`, which includes `\\\"replica\\\"`); `handle()` = authenticate → `BrokerJournal.accept` (durable, replay-safe) → `claim_lifecycle` → owner runs `prepare → runtime_setup → launch`; non-owners poll `status()` for the stored response.\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py` — append-only SQLite v2 with `nonce_once`, `sequence_once`, one-acceptance/one-claim/one-terminal indexes; identities are `(database_incarnation, operation_id, request_type)`; commit-uncertainty re-verification (`JournalCommitAbsent`).\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py` — `_exchange_broker()` enforces kernel peer UID **before** reading one length-prefixed frame (`_read_frame` rejects trailing bytes), calls `service.handle(body, peer_uid)`, writes one bounded response; `broker_connection_handler` = exactly one exchange per connection; `MAX_CONNECTIONS=8`, `CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120`; `_run_broker()` runs `service.recover_startup()` pre-serve; `load_broker_config` requires an exact key set pinned to compiled paths; launcher gates default false via `resolve_boolean_gate` (`YINSHI_LAUNCH_EXECUTION_ENABLED` etc.).\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py` — opaque relay: **one** request frame in, **one** response frame out; `read_blocking_frame` requires EOF after the frame; `_exchange` does `write_eof()` after the request.\\n- `deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service` — `REDACTED`, deliberately not enabled at boot.\\n\\n**Replica stack (built and committed, but wired to nothing)**\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py` — separate SQLite journal for `replica.lifecycle` only (`_request_from_frame` hard-requires the type); own `request_public_key`, per-incarnation `response_public_keys` keyring, `expected_limits_sha256` folded into a `journal_id` configuration hash validated on every open; full historical replay + re-signature-verification on **every** open; `accept(request, frame, authority)` binds `authority` transitively via `artifact_set_sha256`; **no nonce-once or sequence-once index**.\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py` — `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run(request, request_frame, authority)` drives fixed stages `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`; per-operation asyncio gates; `recover_incomplete()` resumes same-incarnation lifecycles and marks cross-incarnation ones `broker_restart_unknown`; terminal responses validated to exactly `{stage, state[, code][, receipt_id]}`.\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` — `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(manifest, reader)` streams **raw bytes after the signed frame** from an `asyncio.StreamReader` (3 fixed files, 512 MiB/role, 1 GiB/set, 120 s transfer / 30 s idle timeouts), atomic no-replace publish, quarantine + `reconcile_attempts`; requires `expected_uid == os.geteuid()` (broker UID 999).\\n- No production code creates signed requests (`create_signed_request` has zero non-test callers); the name `replica.artifacts.upload` appears **nowhere** in the repository — it is a new request type.\\n- Tests: `test_broker_foundation.py` (unsupported type rejected), `test_execution_daemons.py` (one peer-bound exchange; strictly nested deadlines `30 < 35 < 40 < 120`), and the 97 replica journal/lifecycle/artifact-store tests all pass (see commands).\\n\\n## 2. Proposed dispatch design (no code changed)\\n\\n1. **Single front door, per-type pipelines.** Keep the daemon peer-UID check in `_exchange_broker` exactly as is. Add one dispatcher that calls `parse_signed_request` once (signature is over the whole frame, so routing necessarily follows verification), checks both incarnations, then routes on `request.request_type`:\\n   - `executor.launch` → `BrokerService.handle(frame, peer_uid=…)` **unchanged** (it re-verifies; zero behavioral delta, forbidden-field scan stays scoped here — note `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS` contains `\\\"replica\\\"`, so it must never be applied to replica payloads).\\n   - `replica.lifecycle` → `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run(request, frame, authority)`.\\n   - `replica.artifacts.upload` → new upload pipeline: build `ReplicaArtifactManifest` from the signed payload, then `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(manifest, reader)`.\\n   - anything else → today's `BrokerProtocolError(\\\"broker request type is not supported\\\")` (drop connection, no response — preserves the fail-closed precedent; one existing test asserts this).\\n2. **Authentication ownership.** Kernel peer UID stays daemon-owned (outermost). Ed25519 request authentication stays `parse_signed_request` with the application public key. The executor service keeps its own re-check (defense in depth). The replica journal re-authenticates stored frames on replay with its own `request_public_key`. Design rule: the replica `request_public_key` must be pinned equal to the executor `application_public_key` (or the divergence must be an explicit, documented config decision — see F-13).\\n3. **Separate journals.** Keep two files under broker-owned `/var/lib/yinshi/control/`: existing `broker-journal-v2.sqlite3` for `executor.launch`; new replica journal path (e.g. `replica-journal-v1.sqlite3`) added to `BrokerDaemonConfig`/`load_broker_config` (schema is exact-key, so this is a fail-closed config schema extension; old config must be rejected as `config_invalid`). One journal per request family is the only additive option: merging would require a shared stage machine and response schema (v3 redesign) — out of scope.\\n4. **Authority resolution.** `ReplicaAuthority` must become derivable from the signed frame: add `identity: {physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id}` to the `replica.lifecycle` payload. `compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256` already digests exactly this identity object, so artifact-set digests remain valid; only `_validate_replica_payload`'s required-key set changes. The dispatcher then constructs `ReplicaAuthority` from signed fields and `accept()`'s digest binding becomes the cross-check. (F-1 — parent decision required.)\\n5. **Upload transport.** Two viable shapes, both requiring parent sign-off (F-4): (a) multi-frame mode on the existing socket — request frame, raw artifact bytes in fixed order, trailer; requires relaxing `_read_frame`'s trailing-byte rejection and the relay's one-frame/EOF contract; or (b) a **second systemd socket** (e.g. `/run/yinshi/broker-artifacts.sock`) with its own handler that streams — leaves the one-frame relay and `executor.launch` socket byte-for-byte intact. In both shapes, `BrokerService` never sees bytes; only the replica upload handler touches the reader.\\n6. **Response signatures.** All responses stay `create_signed_response` (identity-bound to the request, broker-signed, ≤ 4 096 B). Per-type `result` schemas: executor keeps `{launcher_status, lifecycle_stage}`; `replica.lifecycle` keeps the journal-validated `{stage, state[, code][, receipt_id]}`; upload needs a new schema (proposal: `{stored: true, receipt_id, artifact_set_sha256}` — no journal contract constrains it). Upload is idempotent via the deterministic ingest receipt (`_receipt()` content hash) and exact-manifest replay (`_receive_existing`).\\n7. **Startup recovery (order matters).** In `_run_broker`, before `serve()`: (1) `inspect_legacy_v1_journal` + `service.recover_startup()` (fail-closed unresolved, unchanged); (2) `BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts(manifests)` — quarantine live pendings, classify final dirs; (3) `coordinator.recover_incomplete()` — same-incarnation lifecycles re-drive (`reconcile=True` inspects the store: completed → replay; `not_applied` → fresh ingest), cross-incarnation → `broker_restart_unknown`. Step 2 before 3 so resumed ingests see a clean store. This needs a new public `BrokerReplicaJournal` accessor enumerating accepted-request manifests (F-6).\\n8. **Default-disabled gates/config.** Broker-side gates following the `resolve_boolean_gate` pattern (env **and** explicit flag, default false): `YINSHI_REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED` (dispatch of `replica.lifecycle`), `YINSHI_REPLICA_UPLOAD_ENABLED` (upload acceptance — the broker itself does the disk writes, so launcher gates cannot cover it). `replica.artifacts.upload` stays disabled until the lifecycle effects exist; the systemd unit gains `Environment=YINSHI_REPLICA_…=false` lines mirroring the existing pattern. New config keys: replica journal path, artifact store root (broker-owned 0700), limits blob (`compute_replica_limits_sha256`), request/response keyring.\\n9. **Concurrency/cancellation.** Upload serialization via the store's existing reservation lock + flock; per-operation coordinator gates prevent duplicate lifecycle drives; cancellation during upload quarantines the pending attempt (store already handles); abandoned-effect caps exist on both coordinators. Error mapping must be added: `ReplicaJournalSyncError` → `journal_unavailable`, `BrokerReplicaOwnerActive` → stable `owner_active` code (today both fall into `except Exception` → `internal_error`).\\n\\n## 3. Findings (contradictions / unresolved choices)\\n\\n- **F-1 (blocker for wiring):** `ReplicaAuthority` cannot be derived from a signed frame. The payload schema (`_validate_replica_payload`, broker_replica_journal.py:~466) is an exact 10-key set without identity fields, the broker daemon has no application DB, and `coordinator.run(request, frame, authority)` requires the authority as an argument. Dispatch is impossible without the §2.4 payload extension or an ownership change. Tests pass `AUTHORITY` out of band (test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py:313), masking this.\\n- **F-2 (high):** Replay-guard asymmetry: executor journal enforces nonce-once + monotonic `connection_sequence` per database incarnation (broker_journal.py indexes); the replica journal has neither — only exact-frame binding per operation. A shared sequence space across request types is unenforced anywhere; recorded as an accepted residual or fixed with replica nonce/sequence indexes.\\n- **F-3 (high):** Cross-incarnation recovery contradiction: `_record_unresolved`/`_signing_key` (broker_replica_lifecycle.py) sign with the private key of the **request's** incarnation, so recovering a lifecycle after key rotation requires retaining historical **private** keys (security-negative); the executor broker signs recovery responses with its current key while echoing request identity. Divergent ownership needs a parent ruling.\\n- **F-4 (high):** Transport cannot carry artifact bytes today: `broker_stdio_relay.py` is one-frame-then-EOF both directions; `_read_frame` (execution_daemons.py) rejects any trailing byte; `_exchange_broker` passes no reader into `service.handle`. Choosing multi-frame vs second socket changes a stated transport contract — parent decision.\\n- **F-5 (medium):** Deadline nesting breaks with current defaults: coordinator `effect_timeout_seconds` default 30 s < `LAUNCHER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` 35 s (a launcher-backed admission effect would die inner-first), and store `transfer_timeout_seconds` 120 s equals `CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` 120 s; `test_root_and_broker_deadlines_are_strictly_nested` must be extended to cover the new timers.\\n- **F-6 (medium):** No public `BrokerReplicaJournal` API returns accepted-request manifests for `BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts` (`incomplete_lifecycles` covers only claimed non-terminal lifecycles).\\n- **F-7 (medium):** No broker-side gate exists for replica dispatch/upload, and `load_broker_config`'s exact-key schema makes config extension a fail-closed schema-version decision.\\n- **F-8 (medium):** Recovery sequencing across three recoverers is unspecified in `_run_broker` (today only `service.recover_startup()` runs).\\n- **F-9 (low):** `_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS` includes `\\\"replica\\\"` — harmless today (replica payload keys don't collide) but the scan must be explicitly scoped to `executor.launch` in the dispatcher.\\n- **F-10 (low):** `BrokerReplicaJournal._open()` replays and re-verifies every stored signature on every append — O(n²) cumulative cost; unbounded journal growth is a slow-DoS vector.\\n- **F-11 (low):** Replica error paths currently log `internal_error` (generic handler) instead of stable codes.\\n- **F-12 (unresolved):** Upload response `result` schema, and whether pre-acceptance replica validation failures may return signed error responses (executor precedent is a silent drop).\\n- **F-13 (unresolved):** Whether the replica `request_public_key` must equal the executor `application_public_key` (currently independently configured).\\n- **F-14 (unresolved):** Relationship between a `replica.lifecycle` `operation_id` and the executor launch `operation_id` (`AdmissionReceipt.runtime_unit_id` has no defined linkage).\\n- **F-15 (note):** `MAX_CONNECTIONS=8` is shared; a 120 s upload occupies a slot and can starve executor exchanges.\",\n        \"controlEvents\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"ts\": 1789294502735,\n            \"runId\": \"300f48e3\",\n            \"agent\": \"worker-advanced\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": \"worker-advanced is still active but long-running\",\n            \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n            \"turns\": 13,\n            \"tokens\": 88184,\n            \"toolCount\": 22,\n            \"elapsedMs\": 240568\n          }\n        ],\n        \"attemptedModels\": [\n          \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max\"\n        ],\n        \"modelAttempts\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max\",\n            \"success\": true,\n            \"exitCode\": 0,\n            \"usage\": {\n              \"input\": 109186,\n              \"output\": 22561,\n              \"cacheRead\": 1318976,\n              \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n              \"cost\": 0,\n              \"turns\": 22\n            }\n          }\n        ],\n        \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/300f48e3/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n        \"acceptance\": {\n          \"status\": \"attested\",\n          \"evidenceStatus\": \"attested\",\n          \"explicit\": false,\n          \"effectiveAcceptance\": {\n            \"level\": \"attested\",\n            \"explicit\": false,\n            \"inferredReason\": [\n              \"read-only task wording\"\n            ],\n            \"criteria\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n                \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n                \"evidence\": [\n                  \"review-findings\",\n                  \"residual-risks\"\n                ],\n                \"severity\": \"required\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"evidence\": [\n              \"review-findings\",\n              \"residual-risks\"\n            ],\n            \"verify\": [],\n            \"stopRules\": []\n          },\n          \"inferredReason\": [\n            \"read-only task wording\"\n          ],\n          \"criteria\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n              \"must\": \"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": [\n                \"review-findings\",\n                \"residual-risks\"\n              ],\n              \"severity\": \"required\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"runtimeChecks\": [],\n          \"verifyRuns\": [],\n          \"childReport\": {\n            \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n                \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n                \"evidence\": \"Concrete findings F-1..F-15 with file paths and severities (backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:26, broker_replica_journal.py _validate_replica_payload/accept, broker_replica_lifecycle.py _record_unresolved/_signing_key, broker_stdio_relay.py read_blocking_frame/_exchange, execution_daemons.py _read_frame/_exchange_broker/_run_broker/load_broker_config, broker_artifact_store.py receive/reconcile_attempts), plus a dispatch design covering authentication ownership, separate journals, startup recovery, response signatures, transport handlers, and default-disabled gates/config\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"changedFiles\": [],\n            \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [],\n            \"commandsRun\": [\n              {\n                \"command\": \"cd backend && ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_foundation.py -q -k 'unsupported or type'\",\n                \"result\": \"passed\",\n                \"summary\": \"1 passed: executor broker rejects unsupported request types (strict validation baseline)\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"command\": \"cd backend && ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_execution_daemons.py -q -k 'one_peer_bound or nested'\",\n                \"result\": \"passed\",\n                \"summary\": \"2 passed: one peer-bound signed exchange per connection; deadline nesting invariant 30<35<40<120\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"command\": \"cd backend && ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py -q\",\n                \"result\": \"passed\",\n                \"summary\": \"97 passed: committed replica journal/lifecycle/artifact-store stack is green but wired to nothing\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"command\": \"git status --porcelain | wc -l\",\n                \"result\": \"passed\",\n                \"summary\": \"143 pre-existing changed/untracked entries; unchanged by this task (no writes made)\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"validationOutput\": [\n              \"All four command runs green; read-only task — no source, test, config, or deploy files modified\",\n              \"grep confirmed 'replica.artifacts.upload' appears nowhere in the repository; 'replica.lifecycle' exists only in the replica journal/lifecycle/launcher tests and services\"\n            ],\n            \"residualRisks\": [\n              \"F-1: ReplicaAuthority is not derivable from a signed frame (payload is an exact 10-key set; daemon has no app DB) — dispatch wiring is blocked on the payload-identity extension or an ownership decision\",\n              \"F-3: replica lifecycle recovery after broker-incarnation rotation requires retaining historical private Ed25519 keys (security-negative divergence from executor recovery)\",\n              \"F-2: replica journal lacks nonce-once and connection-sequence-once enforcement; no cross-request-type replay guard exists in either journal\",\n              \"F-4: neither the stdio relay nor the broker connection handler can carry artifact bytes; transport contract change requires parent approval\",\n              \"F-5/F-10: default timeouts violate the nesting invariant for launcher-backed replica stages, and replica journal opens replay/verify all stored signatures (O(n^2) growth)\"\n            ],\n            \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n            \"diffSummary\": \"No diff produced or modified; read-only design task. Working tree retains its pre-existing 143 changed/untracked entries untouched.\",\n            \"reviewFindings\": [\n              \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py (_validate_replica_payload) + broker_replica_lifecycle.py (run signature) - ReplicaAuthority cannot be constructed at dispatch time from an authenticated frame; no production caller exists (F-1)\",\n              \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py (_record_unresolved/_signing_key) - cross-incarnation recovery needs historical private keys, unlike executor recovery which signs with the current key (F-3)\",\n              \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py (schema) - no nonce-once/sequence-once indexes vs broker_journal.py executor indexes; replay-guard ownership unresolved (F-2)\",\n              \"high: backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py (read_blocking_frame/_exchange) + backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py (_read_frame/_exchange_broker) - one-frame transport cannot stream artifact bytes; second socket vs multi-frame decision owned by parent (F-4)\",\n              \"medium: execution_daemons.py (CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120) vs broker_artifact_store.py (transfer_timeout 120s) and broker_replica_lifecycle.py (effect timeout 30s < LAUNCHER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 35s) - nesting invariant violated by defaults (F-5)\",\n              \"medium: broker_replica_journal.py - no public API enumerating accepted-request manifests for BrokerArtifactStore.reconcile_attempts (F-6)\",\n              \"medium: execution_daemons.py (load_broker_config exact-key schema, no replica gates) - config schema version and default-disabled gates for replica dispatch/upload are undecided (F-7)\",\n              \"medium: execution_daemons.py (_run_broker) - startup recovery order across service.recover_startup, store reconcile_attempts, and coordinator.recover_incomplete is unspecified (F-8)\",\n              \"low: execution_broker.py (_FORBIDDEN_LAUNCH_FIELDS contains 'replica') - executor-only scan must stay scoped to executor.launch in any dispatcher (F-9)\",\n              \"low: broker_replica_journal.py (_open/_validate_events) - full-journal replay with signature re-verification on every append; unbounded growth is a slow-DoS vector (F-10)\",\n              \"low: execution_daemons.py (_serve_connection) - ReplicaJournalError/BrokerReplicaOwnerActive currently surface as generic internal_error instead of stable codes (F-11)\",\n              \"unresolved: upload response result schema and signed-error-vs-silent-drop for pre-acceptance replica validation failures (F-12)\",\n              \"unresolved: whether replica request_public_key must equal executor application_public_key (F-13)\",\n              \"unresolved: linkage between replica.lifecycle operation_id and executor launch operation_id / AdmissionReceipt.runtime_unit_id (F-14)\",\n              \"note: MAX_CONNECTIONS=8 shared between uploads and executor exchanges; long uploads can starve the executor path (F-15)\"\n            ],\n            \"manualNotes\": \"Design intent (parent-owned decisions called out): single front door after the daemon peer-UID check, routing on request_type with executor.launch delegated to BrokerService.handle byte-for-byte unchanged; separate replica journal file; authority via signed payload identity fields (digest-compatible with compute_replica_artifact_set_sha256 v2); broker-side default-false gates YINSHI_REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED / YINSHI_REPLICA_UPLOAD_ENABLED; recovery order executor-recover -> store-reconcile -> replica-recover. F-1 and F-4 require parent decisions before any implementation packet can be written.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"toolCalls\": [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"ls {}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"ls {}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -maxdepth 2 -type d | head ...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -maxdepth 2 -type d | head -50\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read CLAUDE.md\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read CLAUDE.md\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"executor\\\\\\\\.launch\\\",\\\"limit\\\":6...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"executor\\\\\\\\.launch\\\",\\\"limit\\\":60}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/services\\\"}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi/services\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi\\\"}\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"ls {\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend/src/yinshi\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"replica\\\\\\\\.artifacts\\\\\\\\.upload...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"grep {\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"replica\\\\\\\\.artifacts\\\\\\\\.upload|artifacts\\\\\\\\.upload\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"backend\\\",\\\"limit\\\":40}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"replica.artifacts\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" --include=\\\"*.t...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"replica.artifacts\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" --include=\\\"*.ts\\\" --include=\\\"*.tsx\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" . 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | grep -v \\\".pi-subagents\\\" | head -30; echo ---; grep -rln \\\"replica.lifecycle\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" . 2>/dev/n...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"create_signed_request\\\\|parse_signed_request\\\\|verif...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"create_signed_request\\\\|parse_signed_request\\\\|verify_broker_response\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" backend/src backend/tests | grep -v \\\".pi-subagents\\\" | awk -F: '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c; echo ---; ls backend/tests | head -60\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"read backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"BrokerArtifactStore(\\\\|ReplicaLifecycleEffects(\\\\|Br...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"BrokerArtifactStore(\\\\|ReplicaLifecycleEffects(\\\\|BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator(\\\\|BrokerReplicaJournal(\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" backend/src backend/tests | grep -v __pycache__; echo ===; grep -n \\\"\\\\.run(\\\" backend/tests/test_broker_repl...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ git status --porcelain | head -30; echo ===; git log --oneli...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ git status --porcelain | head -30; echo ===; git log --oneline -5\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"broker\\\\|Broker\\\" backend/src/yinshi/services/worksp...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"broker\\\\|Broker\\\" backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica.py | head -10; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"BROKER_SOCKET\\\\|broker.sock\\\\|stdio_relay\\\\|broker_stdio\\\" backend/src desktop/src sidecar --include=\\\"*.py\\\" --include=\\\"*.ts\\\" 2>/dev/null ...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"replica\\\" backend/src/yinshi/config.py .env.example...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"replica\\\" backend/src/yinshi/config.py .env.example 2>/dev/null | head; echo ===; grep -n \\\"class Settings\\\\|replica\\\\|broker\\\" backend/src/yinshi/config.py | head -20\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ sed -n 140,200p backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py; ech...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ sed -n 140,200p backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py; echo ===; sed -n 930,975p backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py; echo ===; ls deploy/systemd; echo ===; cat deploy/systemd/yinshi-broker.service 2>/dev/null; cat deploy/systemd/yins...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"relay\\\\|broker\\\" backend/pyproject.toml | head; echo...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ grep -rn \\\"relay\\\\|broker\\\" backend/pyproject.toml | head; echo ===; grep -rln \\\"broker\\\" desktop/src 2>/dev/null | head; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"yinshi-broker-stdio-relay\\\\|broker_stdio_relay\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" --include=\\\"*.toml\\\" --include=\\\"*.service...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ git status --porcelain | wc -l; git status --porcelain | gre...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ git status --porcelain | wc -l; git status --porcelain | grep -E \\\"broker|replica|execution_daemon|root_launcher|artifact\\\" ; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"ReplicaAuthority\\\" backend/src --include=\\\"*.py\\\" | grep -v __pycache__ | awk -F: '{print $1\\\": \\\"$2}...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ ls docs plans 2>/dev/null; echo ===; grep -rln \\\"replica.arti...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ ls docs plans 2>/dev/null; echo ===; grep -rln \\\"replica.artifacts\\\\|artifacts.upload\\\\|artifact.upload\\\" docs plans code_reviews 2>/dev/null | head; echo ===; head -80 docs/broker-root-launcher.md 2>/dev/null\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && ../.venv/bin/pytho...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_foundation.py -q -k \\\"unsupported or type\\\" 2>&1 | tail -5; ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_execution_daemons.py -q -k \\\"one_peer_bound or neste...\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"text\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && grep -n \\\"not suppo...\",\n            \"expandedText\": \"$ cd /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend && grep -n \\\"not supported\\\" tests/test_broker_foundation.py | head -3; ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py tests/test_broker_artifac...\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"key\": \"tests\",\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"runId\": \"4a796e28\",\n    \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 16 assistant turns (soft limit 16, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nNow I have a comprehensive picture of the codebase, existing tests, and gaps. Let me produce the test plan review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test Plan Review: Production Replica Upload Transport + Lifecycle Ingest/Verify/Publish Wiring\\n\\n### Scope Assessment\\n\\nThe production pipeline flows through:\\n\\n```\\nencrypted_uploads (chunk assembly) → runner_relay (framed ciphertext relay)\\n→ broker_journal (stage-durable lifecycle) → workspace_replica (publish/ingest)\\n→ executor.launch (final dispatch)\\n```\\n\\n### Existing Test Coverage\\n\\n**Present and passing:**\\n\\n- `test_runner_relay.py` (27 tests) — relay routing, framing, maintenance, backpressure, byte limits, connection replacement, close survival, stale-frame rejection\\n- `test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py` — lifecycle ordering, runtime socket creation, startup recovery marking\\n- `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py` — stage ordering, recovery, cancellation, timeout, retry, malformed effects, custom awaitables, fail-closed validation\\n- `test_broker_replica_journal.py` — state transitions, authority, stage lifecycle\\n- `test_workspace_replica_artifact.py` (74 tests) — artifact verification, Git integration\\n- `test_workspace_replica_bundle.py` (22 tests) — committed bundle creation\\n- `test_workspace_replica_object_pack.py` (12 tests) — index pack creation, verification, limits, thin-pack rejection\\n- `test_workspace_replica_publication.py` (27 tests) — workspace publication\\n- `test_workspace_replica_reconciliation.py` (5900+ lines) — path identity, snapshot validation, replay behavior\\n- `test_encrypted_uploads.py` (2 tests) — chunk retry, completion verification, ownership/ordering/digest checks\\n- `test_broker_foundation.py` — shared test helpers for broker tests\\n- `test_root_replica_lifecycle.py` (37 tests) — root replica lifecycle\\n\\n**All existing tests pass.** (82 relay + lifecycle + encrypted upload tests, plus full suite)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Identified Gaps and Recommended Test Cases\\n\\n#### 1. Binary Framing — Truncated/Incomplete Streams\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\nThe relay frames are opaque UUID+byte concatenation. No test validates behavior when a WebSocket frame arrives truncated mid-frame or with trailing garbage after a complete frame.\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_relay_ignores_truncated_ciphertext_frame\\n# Send a runner_frame that is too short (prefix + partial ciphertext < minimum)\\n# Assert ValueError raised, runner not disconnected, other transfers unaffected\\n\\n# Required: test_relay_ignores_trailing_garbage_after_complete_frame\\n# Send complete frame followed by extra bytes on same websocket message\\n# Assert only first complete frame is processed\\n```\\n\\n#### 2. Relay — Auth Edge Cases\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`claim_runner_transfer_grant` is tested via `test_runner_relay.py` integration tests but missing explicit unit tests for:\\n- Clock-skew expiry: grant expires at exactly `current_time` (boundary)\\n- Non-canonical UUID transfer_id rejection\\n- Capability hash mismatch with identical-length but wrong hash\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_grant_expires_at_boundary_exact\\n# current_time == expires_at should fail (uses <= comparison)\\n\\n# Required: test_grant_rejects_non_canonical_uuid\\n# transfer_id=\\\"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\\\" (canonical)\\n# vs \\\"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\\\" (different canonical form)\\n```\\n\\n#### 3. Oversized/Truncated/Tailing Upload Streams\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\n`test_encrypted_uploads.py` has only 2 tests. The upload manager supports:\\n- Size limits: `_UPLOAD_BYTES_MAX = 50MB`, `_UPLOAD_BYTES_RESERVED_MAX = 100MB`\\n- Chunk limits: `_UPLOAD_CHUNK_BYTES_MAX = 24000`\\n- Count limits: `_UPLOAD_COUNT_MAX = 8`\\n- Lifetime: `_UPLOAD_LIFETIME_SECONDS = 15 * 60`\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_upload_rejects_oversized_chunk\\n# chunk > 24000 bytes should raise ValueError\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_count_limit_blocks_eighth\\n# 8 uploads active, 9th start() should raise RuntimeError\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_truncated_stream_fails_sha256\\n# Upload with missing final bytes (size < declared) should fail at complete()\\n# with \\\"size does not match declaration\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_trailing_extra_bytes_fails_sha256\\n# Upload with > declared bytes should fail at complete()\\n# with \\\"size does not match declaration\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_expires_during_append\\n# Clock advancement past expires_at should cause LookupError\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_reserved_byte_limit_reached\\n# Multiple uploads totaling > 100MB should fail\\n```\\n\\n#### 4. Exact Retry Semantics\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`test_encrypted_uploads.py::test_encrypted_upload_retries_chunks_and_verifies_completion` tests idempotent retry of one chunk. Missing:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_upload_retry_non_contiguous_chunk_rejected\\n# After chunk 0, submitting chunk 2 (skipping 1) raises ValueError(\\\"sequence\\\")\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_retry_wrong_digest_rejected\\n# Retry with different data but same index raises ValueError(\\\"digest\\\")\\n```\\n\\n#### 5. Terminal Replay and Recovery\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\n`test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py` has recovery tests but gaps in:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_recovery_after_partial_journal_write\\n# Journal file truncated mid-record (simulate with mock)\\n# Recovery should mark incomplete stages as broker_restart_unknown\\n\\n# Required: test_terminal_replay_preserves_original_receipt\\n# After broker restart, replay of completed stage returns exact same receipt\\n# Not a regenerated receipt with different byte identity\\n\\n# Required: test_recovery_with_corrupted_receipt_bytes\\n# Journal contains malformed receipt for a completed stage\\n# Should mark as unknown, not crash recovery\\n```\\n\\n#### 6. Concurrency — Publish-to-Broker Coordination\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\nThe `workspace_replica_publication.py` produces a bundle that enters the broker. No test validates the coordination:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_concurrent_publish_attempts_deduplicate\\n# Two threads attempting to publish the same branch simultaneously\\n# Only one should succeed in creating the bundle entry\\n\\n# Required: test_publish_during_broker_recovery\\n# Publish attempt while broker journal is in recovery state\\n# Should return \\\"in_progress\\\" or \\\"unresolved\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_concurrent_executor_launch_different_operations\\n# Two executor.launch requests for different operation_ids\\n# Both should process without interference\\n```\\n\\n#### 7. Descriptor Mutation During Recovery\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`test_broker_replica_journal.py` tests descriptor state but not concurrent mutation:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_descriptor_mutation_during_recovery_race\\n# Begin_stage called while recovery is scanning incomplete stages\\n# Should not lose either operation\\n\\n# Required: test_describe_after_recovery_preserves_state\\n# Journal.describe() after recovery shows completed state\\n# Not partial or inconsistent state\\n```\\n\\n#### 8. Journal Stage Receipts — Tampering\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\nReceipt validation exists but no tests for tampering scenarios:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_receipt_mutation_detected_on_replay\\n# Modify receipt bytes in journal after stage completion\\n# Replay should detect mismatch and mark as unresolved\\n\\n# Required: test_receipt_cross_stage_leakage_prevented\\n# Receipt from stage B should not be accepted as receipt for stage A\\n# During reconciliation of stage A\\n```\\n\\n#### 9. Cancellation During Receipt Persistence\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py::test_cancellation_records_unknown_then_reraises` tests basic cancellation. Missing:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_cancellation_during_receipt_persistence\\n# Cancel during _persist_outcome call\\n# Should record stage_unresolved and not leave partial receipt\\n\\n# Required: test_timeout_with_active_persist\\n# Timeout fires while journal write is in progress\\n# Should mark as timeout_unknown, not transport_unknown\\n```\\n\\n#### 10. executor.launch — Integration Verification\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\n`test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py::test_lifecycle_orders_prepare_runtime_and_launch_with_durable_starts` validates ordering but not error propagation:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_timeout_propagates_correctly\\n# Launcher.prepare() times out after _LAUNCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\\n# Journal should record stage \\\"prepare\\\" with stage_status=\\\"rejected\\\"\\n# and error=\\\"timeout_unknown\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_error_rejected_status\\n# Launcher returns LauncherResult(status=\\\"rejected\\\", error=\\\"policy_violation\\\")\\n# Journal should record with stage_status=\\\"rejected\\\"\\n# Response should include error message\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_transport_error\\n# Launcher raises LauncherTransportError\\n# Journal should record stage with stage_status=\\\"unresolved\\\"\\n# and error=\\\"transport_unknown\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_verification_error\\n# Launcher returns LauncherResult(status=\\\"unprepared\\\", error=None)\\n# (invalid status for the stage)\\n# Journal should record with stage_status=\\\"unresolved\\\"\\n# and error=\\\"verification_unknown\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_concurrent_reclaim\\n# executor.launch followed immediately by executor.reclaim for same operation_id\\n# Reclaim should be accepted and recorded as \\\"reclaimed\\\"\\n```\\n\\n#### 11. Unchanged executor.launch — Confirmation\\n**Severity: INFO**\\n\\nNo changes needed. The `executor.launch` handling in `BrokerService._root_effect` and `_finalize_lifecycle` is well-tested via `test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py`. The pattern is:\\n1. `_root_effect` creates an async task, waits with timeout, abandons on timeout/cancel\\n2. `_confirmed_launcher_result` validates the result shape\\n3. `_persist_outcome` writes to journal with transaction error handling\\n\\nThis contract is stable. No test changes required for the executor.launch behavior itself.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Test Infrastructure Needs\\n\\n1. **`test_journal_truncation.py`** — New test file for journal-level corruption/truncation recovery\\n2. **`test_upload_limits.py`** — Expand encrypted upload tests from 2 to 8+ with boundary conditions\\n3. **`test_publish_broker_integration.py`** — New test file for workspace_replica_publication → BrokerJournal → BrokerService wiring\\n4. **`test_executor_launch_errors.py`** — Expand executor.launch error path tests\\n5. **`test_concurrent_lifecycle.py`** — New test file for concurrent broker lifecycle operations\\n\\n**Recommended test helper pattern** (matching existing `_Effect` / `_coordinator` pattern in `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`):\\n\\n```python\\nclass _TestEffect(Protocol):\\n    def apply(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> Awaitable[StageReconciliation]: ...\\n    async def reconcile(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation: ...\\n    started: asyncio.Event\\n```\\n\\n**Recommended fixture pattern** (matching existing `tmp_path` + journal factory):\\n\\n```python\\ndef _test_journal(tmp_path: Path) -> BrokerJournal:\\n    return BrokerJournal(tmp_path / \\\"test-journal.sqlite3\\\", application_id=\\\"test\\\")\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Summary of Findings\\n\\n| Area | Existing Coverage | Gap Severity | New Tests Required |\\n|------|-------------------|-------------|-------------------|\\n| Binary framing | Partial (relay routing) | HIGH | 2 |\\n| Relay auth | Good | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| Upload limits/streams | Poor (2 tests) | HIGH | 6 |\\n| Exact retry | Partial | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| Terminal replay | Partial | HIGH | 3 |\\n| Concurrency | Partial | HIGH | 3 |\\n| Descriptor mutation | Partial | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| Receipt tampering | Poor | HIGH | 2 |\\n| Cancellation+persistence | Partial | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| executor.launch errors | Partial | HIGH | 4 |\\n| Unchanged executor.launch | N/A | INFO | 0 |\\n\\n**Total new tests needed: ~26** across 5 new test files and 3 expanded test files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Residual Risks\\n\\n- `test_encrypted_uploads.py` at 2 tests for a 100+ line class — high risk of regressions in chunk assembly boundaries\\n- No end-to-end test from upload → relay → journal → publish — single integration gap\\n- Journal truncation recovery only tested with mock effects, not real SQLite corruption\\n- No tests for the `runner_relay_api` FastAPI integration layer's WebSocket error handling edge cases\\n- `executor.launch` transport error paths partially tested — `LauncherTransportError`, `OSError` handling needs explicit assertions\\n\\n### Constraints for Implementation Worker\\n\\n1. **Do not modify any production code** — all changes are test-only\\n2. **Do not modify configuration files** — `pyproject.toml`, `conftest.py` (existing helpers only)\\n3. **All new tests must use existing patterns**: `_journal()` factory, `_Effect` adapter, `tmp_path` fixture\\n4. **No network I/O** — all relay/auth tests use `FakeWebSocket` / `StrictCloseWebSocket`\\n5. **No database migration tests** — use `BrokerJournal` with in-memory SQLite via `tmp_path`\\n6. **Async tests must use `@pytest.mark.asyncio`** — all existing tests follow this pattern\\n7. **Test isolation**: each test must be independent — no shared state between tests\\n8. **Clock injection**: use `clock` parameter (e.g., `lambda: 1_000.0`) for expiry-dependent tests\\n9. **No test dependencies on system state** (uid, gids, paths outside tmp_path) unless explicitly fixture-provided\",\n    \"artifactPaths\": [\n      \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/4a796e28/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n    ],\n    \"results\": [\n      {\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"agent\": \"test-writer\",\n        \"task\": \"Read-only test plan for production replica upload transport plus lifecycle ingest/verify/publish wiring. Inspect current focused tests. Specify test helpers and cases for binary framing, relay, auth, oversized/truncated/trailing streams, exact retry, terminal replay, concurrency, descriptor mutation, journal stage receipts, recovery, cancellation/timeouts, and unchanged executor.launch. Do not modify.\",\n        \"routingContract\": {\n          \"version\": 1,\n          \"agent\": \"test-writer\",\n          \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3\",\n          \"thinking\": \"high\",\n          \"policyDige