   \"wrapUpRequestedAtTurn\": 16\n        },\n        \"toolBudget\": {\n          \"hard\": 80,\n          \"soft\": 55,\n          \"block\": [\n            \"bash\",\n            \"read\",\n            \"grep\",\n            \"find\",\n            \"ls\"\n          ],\n          \"toolCount\": 52,\n          \"outcome\": \"within-budget\"\n        },\n        \"context\": \"fresh\",\n        \"wrapUpRequested\": true,\n        \"progressSummary\": {\n          \"toolCount\": 52,\n          \"tokens\": 121503,\n          \"durationMs\": 255513\n        },\n        \"effects\": {\n          \"fileMutation\": {\n            \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n            \"expected\": false,\n            \"attempted\": true\n          }\n        },\n        \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n        \"finalOutput\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 16 assistant turns (soft limit 16, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\nNow I have a comprehensive picture of the codebase, existing tests, and gaps. Let me produce the test plan review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test Plan Review: Production Replica Upload Transport + Lifecycle Ingest/Verify/Publish Wiring\\n\\n### Scope Assessment\\n\\nThe production pipeline flows through:\\n\\n```\\nencrypted_uploads (chunk assembly) → runner_relay (framed ciphertext relay)\\n→ broker_journal (stage-durable lifecycle) → workspace_replica (publish/ingest)\\n→ executor.launch (final dispatch)\\n```\\n\\n### Existing Test Coverage\\n\\n**Present and passing:**\\n\\n- `test_runner_relay.py` (27 tests) — relay routing, framing, maintenance, backpressure, byte limits, connection replacement, close survival, stale-frame rejection\\n- `test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py` — lifecycle ordering, runtime socket creation, startup recovery marking\\n- `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py` — stage ordering, recovery, cancellation, timeout, retry, malformed effects, custom awaitables, fail-closed validation\\n- `test_broker_replica_journal.py` — state transitions, authority, stage lifecycle\\n- `test_workspace_replica_artifact.py` (74 tests) — artifact verification, Git integration\\n- `test_workspace_replica_bundle.py` (22 tests) — committed bundle creation\\n- `test_workspace_replica_object_pack.py` (12 tests) — index pack creation, verification, limits, thin-pack rejection\\n- `test_workspace_replica_publication.py` (27 tests) — workspace publication\\n- `test_workspace_replica_reconciliation.py` (5900+ lines) — path identity, snapshot validation, replay behavior\\n- `test_encrypted_uploads.py` (2 tests) — chunk retry, completion verification, ownership/ordering/digest checks\\n- `test_broker_foundation.py` — shared test helpers for broker tests\\n- `test_root_replica_lifecycle.py` (37 tests) — root replica lifecycle\\n\\n**All existing tests pass.** (82 relay + lifecycle + encrypted upload tests, plus full suite)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Identified Gaps and Recommended Test Cases\\n\\n#### 1. Binary Framing — Truncated/Incomplete Streams\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\nThe relay frames are opaque UUID+byte concatenation. No test validates behavior when a WebSocket frame arrives truncated mid-frame or with trailing garbage after a complete frame.\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_relay_ignores_truncated_ciphertext_frame\\n# Send a runner_frame that is too short (prefix + partial ciphertext < minimum)\\n# Assert ValueError raised, runner not disconnected, other transfers unaffected\\n\\n# Required: test_relay_ignores_trailing_garbage_after_complete_frame\\n# Send complete frame followed by extra bytes on same websocket message\\n# Assert only first complete frame is processed\\n```\\n\\n#### 2. Relay — Auth Edge Cases\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`claim_runner_transfer_grant` is tested via `test_runner_relay.py` integration tests but missing explicit unit tests for:\\n- Clock-skew expiry: grant expires at exactly `current_time` (boundary)\\n- Non-canonical UUID transfer_id rejection\\n- Capability hash mismatch with identical-length but wrong hash\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_grant_expires_at_boundary_exact\\n# current_time == expires_at should fail (uses <= comparison)\\n\\n# Required: test_grant_rejects_non_canonical_uuid\\n# transfer_id=\\\"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\\\" (canonical)\\n# vs \\\"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\\\" (different canonical form)\\n```\\n\\n#### 3. Oversized/Truncated/Tailing Upload Streams\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\n`test_encrypted_uploads.py` has only 2 tests. The upload manager supports:\\n- Size limits: `_UPLOAD_BYTES_MAX = 50MB`, `_UPLOAD_BYTES_RESERVED_MAX = 100MB`\\n- Chunk limits: `_UPLOAD_CHUNK_BYTES_MAX = 24000`\\n- Count limits: `_UPLOAD_COUNT_MAX = 8`\\n- Lifetime: `_UPLOAD_LIFETIME_SECONDS = 15 * 60`\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_upload_rejects_oversized_chunk\\n# chunk > 24000 bytes should raise ValueError\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_count_limit_blocks_eighth\\n# 8 uploads active, 9th start() should raise RuntimeError\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_truncated_stream_fails_sha256\\n# Upload with missing final bytes (size < declared) should fail at complete()\\n# with \\\"size does not match declaration\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_trailing_extra_bytes_fails_sha256\\n# Upload with > declared bytes should fail at complete()\\n# with \\\"size does not match declaration\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_expires_during_append\\n# Clock advancement past expires_at should cause LookupError\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_reserved_byte_limit_reached\\n# Multiple uploads totaling > 100MB should fail\\n```\\n\\n#### 4. Exact Retry Semantics\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`test_encrypted_uploads.py::test_encrypted_upload_retries_chunks_and_verifies_completion` tests idempotent retry of one chunk. Missing:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_upload_retry_non_contiguous_chunk_rejected\\n# After chunk 0, submitting chunk 2 (skipping 1) raises ValueError(\\\"sequence\\\")\\n\\n# Required: test_upload_retry_wrong_digest_rejected\\n# Retry with different data but same index raises ValueError(\\\"digest\\\")\\n```\\n\\n#### 5. Terminal Replay and Recovery\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\n`test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py` has recovery tests but gaps in:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_recovery_after_partial_journal_write\\n# Journal file truncated mid-record (simulate with mock)\\n# Recovery should mark incomplete stages as broker_restart_unknown\\n\\n# Required: test_terminal_replay_preserves_original_receipt\\n# After broker restart, replay of completed stage returns exact same receipt\\n# Not a regenerated receipt with different byte identity\\n\\n# Required: test_recovery_with_corrupted_receipt_bytes\\n# Journal contains malformed receipt for a completed stage\\n# Should mark as unknown, not crash recovery\\n```\\n\\n#### 6. Concurrency — Publish-to-Broker Coordination\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\nThe `workspace_replica_publication.py` produces a bundle that enters the broker. No test validates the coordination:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_concurrent_publish_attempts_deduplicate\\n# Two threads attempting to publish the same branch simultaneously\\n# Only one should succeed in creating the bundle entry\\n\\n# Required: test_publish_during_broker_recovery\\n# Publish attempt while broker journal is in recovery state\\n# Should return \\\"in_progress\\\" or \\\"unresolved\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_concurrent_executor_launch_different_operations\\n# Two executor.launch requests for different operation_ids\\n# Both should process without interference\\n```\\n\\n#### 7. Descriptor Mutation During Recovery\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`test_broker_replica_journal.py` tests descriptor state but not concurrent mutation:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_descriptor_mutation_during_recovery_race\\n# Begin_stage called while recovery is scanning incomplete stages\\n# Should not lose either operation\\n\\n# Required: test_describe_after_recovery_preserves_state\\n# Journal.describe() after recovery shows completed state\\n# Not partial or inconsistent state\\n```\\n\\n#### 8. Journal Stage Receipts — Tampering\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\nReceipt validation exists but no tests for tampering scenarios:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_receipt_mutation_detected_on_replay\\n# Modify receipt bytes in journal after stage completion\\n# Replay should detect mismatch and mark as unresolved\\n\\n# Required: test_receipt_cross_stage_leakage_prevented\\n# Receipt from stage B should not be accepted as receipt for stage A\\n# During reconciliation of stage A\\n```\\n\\n#### 9. Cancellation During Receipt Persistence\\n**Severity: MEDIUM**\\n\\n`test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py::test_cancellation_records_unknown_then_reraises` tests basic cancellation. Missing:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_cancellation_during_receipt_persistence\\n# Cancel during _persist_outcome call\\n# Should record stage_unresolved and not leave partial receipt\\n\\n# Required: test_timeout_with_active_persist\\n# Timeout fires while journal write is in progress\\n# Should mark as timeout_unknown, not transport_unknown\\n```\\n\\n#### 10. executor.launch — Integration Verification\\n**Severity: HIGH**\\n\\n`test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py::test_lifecycle_orders_prepare_runtime_and_launch_with_durable_starts` validates ordering but not error propagation:\\n\\n```python\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_timeout_propagates_correctly\\n# Launcher.prepare() times out after _LAUNCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\\n# Journal should record stage \\\"prepare\\\" with stage_status=\\\"rejected\\\"\\n# and error=\\\"timeout_unknown\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_error_rejected_status\\n# Launcher returns LauncherResult(status=\\\"rejected\\\", error=\\\"policy_violation\\\")\\n# Journal should record with stage_status=\\\"rejected\\\"\\n# Response should include error message\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_transport_error\\n# Launcher raises LauncherTransportError\\n# Journal should record stage with stage_status=\\\"unresolved\\\"\\n# and error=\\\"transport_unknown\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_verification_error\\n# Launcher returns LauncherResult(status=\\\"unprepared\\\", error=None)\\n# (invalid status for the stage)\\n# Journal should record with stage_status=\\\"unresolved\\\"\\n# and error=\\\"verification_unknown\\\"\\n\\n# Required: test_executor_launch_concurrent_reclaim\\n# executor.launch followed immediately by executor.reclaim for same operation_id\\n# Reclaim should be accepted and recorded as \\\"reclaimed\\\"\\n```\\n\\n#### 11. Unchanged executor.launch — Confirmation\\n**Severity: INFO**\\n\\nNo changes needed. The `executor.launch` handling in `BrokerService._root_effect` and `_finalize_lifecycle` is well-tested via `test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py`. The pattern is:\\n1. `_root_effect` creates an async task, waits with timeout, abandons on timeout/cancel\\n2. `_confirmed_launcher_result` validates the result shape\\n3. `_persist_outcome` writes to journal with transaction error handling\\n\\nThis contract is stable. No test changes required for the executor.launch behavior itself.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Test Infrastructure Needs\\n\\n1. **`test_journal_truncation.py`** — New test file for journal-level corruption/truncation recovery\\n2. **`test_upload_limits.py`** — Expand encrypted upload tests from 2 to 8+ with boundary conditions\\n3. **`test_publish_broker_integration.py`** — New test file for workspace_replica_publication → BrokerJournal → BrokerService wiring\\n4. **`test_executor_launch_errors.py`** — Expand executor.launch error path tests\\n5. **`test_concurrent_lifecycle.py`** — New test file for concurrent broker lifecycle operations\\n\\n**Recommended test helper pattern** (matching existing `_Effect` / `_coordinator` pattern in `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`):\\n\\n```python\\nclass _TestEffect(Protocol):\\n    def apply(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> Awaitable[StageReconciliation]: ...\\n    async def reconcile(self, context: ReplicaLifecycleContext) -> StageReconciliation: ...\\n    started: asyncio.Event\\n```\\n\\n**Recommended fixture pattern** (matching existing `tmp_path` + journal factory):\\n\\n```python\\ndef _test_journal(tmp_path: Path) -> BrokerJournal:\\n    return BrokerJournal(tmp_path / \\\"test-journal.sqlite3\\\", application_id=\\\"test\\\")\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Summary of Findings\\n\\n| Area | Existing Coverage | Gap Severity | New Tests Required |\\n|------|-------------------|-------------|-------------------|\\n| Binary framing | Partial (relay routing) | HIGH | 2 |\\n| Relay auth | Good | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| Upload limits/streams | Poor (2 tests) | HIGH | 6 |\\n| Exact retry | Partial | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| Terminal replay | Partial | HIGH | 3 |\\n| Concurrency | Partial | HIGH | 3 |\\n| Descriptor mutation | Partial | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| Receipt tampering | Poor | HIGH | 2 |\\n| Cancellation+persistence | Partial | MEDIUM | 2 |\\n| executor.launch errors | Partial | HIGH | 4 |\\n| Unchanged executor.launch | N/A | INFO | 0 |\\n\\n**Total new tests needed: ~26** across 5 new test files and 3 expanded test files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Residual Risks\\n\\n- `test_encrypted_uploads.py` at 2 tests for a 100+ line class — high risk of regressions in chunk assembly boundaries\\n- No end-to-end test from upload → relay → journal → publish — single integration gap\\n- Journal truncation recovery only tested with mock effects, not real SQLite corruption\\n- No tests for the `runner_relay_api` FastAPI integration layer's WebSocket error handling edge cases\\n- `executor.launch` transport error paths partially tested — `LauncherTransportError`, `OSError` handling needs explicit assertions\\n\\n### Constraints for Implementation Worker\\n\\n1. **Do not modify any production code** — all changes are test-only\\n2. **Do not modify configuration files** — `pyproject.toml`, `conftest.py` (existing helpers only)\\n3. **All new tests must use existing patterns**: `_journal()` factory, `_Effect` adapter, `tmp_path` fixture\\n4. **No network I/O** — all relay/auth tests use `FakeWebSocket` / `StrictCloseWebSocket`\\n5. **No database migration tests** — use `BrokerJournal` with in-memory SQLite via `tmp_path`\\n6. **Async tests must use `@pytest.mark.asyncio`** — all existing tests follow this pattern\\n7. **Test isolation**: each test must be independent — no shared state between tests\\n8. **Clock injection**: use `clock` parameter (e.g., `lambda: 1_000.0`) for expiry-dependent tests\\n9. **No test dependencies on system state** (uid, gids, paths outside tmp_path) unless explicitly fixture-provided\",\n        \"controlEvents\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n            \"ts\": 1789294502735,\n            \"runId\": \"4a796e28\",\n            \"agent\": \"test-writer\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": \"test-writer is still active but long-running\",\n            \"reason\": \"time_threshold\",\n            \"turns\": 24,\n            \"tokens\": 116605,\n            \"toolCount\": 52,\n            \"elapsedMs\": 240541\n          }\n        ],\n        \"attemptedModels\": [\n          \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\"\n        ],\n        \"modelAttempts\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"local-pilocal/qwen36-35b-a3b-iq4xs-mtp3-turbo3:high\",\n            \"success\": true,\n            \"exitCode\": 0,\n            \"usage\": {\n              \"input\": 114088,\n              \"output\": 7415,\n              \"cacheRead\": 1033543,\n              \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n              \"cost\": 0,\n              \"turns\": 25\n            }\n          }\n        ],\n        \"sessionFile\": \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/4a796e28/run-0/session.jsonl\",\n