docs\",\"pattern\":\"replica lifecy...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"docs\",\"pattern\":\"replica lifecycle|artifact set|publication\",\"ignoreCase\":true,\"context\":2,\"limit\":100}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/services\",\"p...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"backend/src/yinshi/services\",\"pattern\":\"*replica*\"}"},{"text":"find {\"path\":\"backend/tests\",\"pattern\":\"*repl...","expandedText":"find {\"path\":\"backend/tests\",\"pattern\":\"*replica*\"}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents\",\"pattern\":\"concr...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\".pi-subagents\",\"pattern\":\"concrete ingest, verify, and publish|concrete ingest|path pinning, cancellation\",\"ignoreCase\":true,\"context\":2,\"limit\":50}"},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/Downloads\",\"pattern...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"/Users/user/Downloads\",\"pattern\":\"BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator|broker_replica_lifecycle|ReplicaArtifactManifest\",\"glob\":\"*.md\",\"ignoreCase\":true,\"..."},{"text":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/tests/test_broker_repli...","expandedText":"grep {\"path\":\"backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py\",\"pattern\":\"reconcile|cancel|unknown|timeout|StageRejected|receipt\",\"context\":2,\"limit\":100}"},{"text":"$ git status --short","expandedText":"$ git status --short"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/d856fe34_planner_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/d856fe34_planner_0_output.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/d856fe34_planner_0_output.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/d856fe34_planner_0_output.md"},{"text":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/outputs/d856fe34/.pi-subagents/artifacts/remaining-phase6-plan.md","expandedText":"read .pi-subagents/artifacts/outputs/d856fe34/.pi-subagents/artifacts/remaining-phase6-plan.md"},{"text":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py","expandedText":"read backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py"},{"text":"$ nl -ba backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle....","expandedText":"$ nl -ba backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py | sed -n '1,240p;300,525p;650,725p'"}]}]},{"key":"memory","ok":true,"runId":"b267e7ed","output":"Baseline confirmed: all 50 tests in the two focused files pass. I have completed the read-only review. No files were modified, nothing staged.\n\n# Review: artifact verification/publication memory & descriptor safety\n\n## Scope inspected\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` — `BrokerArtifactStore`, `OpenedArtifact`/`OpenedReplicaArtifacts`, `open_incoming`/`open_incoming_async` (:950/:984), `recheck_opened(_async)` (:1009/:1061), `inspect_incoming(_async)` (:1065/:1070)\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py` — bytes APIs `verify_artifact_set` (:618), `publish_artifact_set` (:817), `inspect_published_artifact_set` (:1140); pin/read machinery `_read_descriptor` (:487), `_open_pinned_regular` (:502), `_recheck_pinned_regular` (:548), `_inspect_pending` (:634), `_inspect_final` (:984)\n- Verification codecs: `workspace_replica_bundle.py` (`verify_committed_bundle` :287, `_write_private_bundle` :244), `workspace_replica_object_pack.py` (`verify_index_object_pack` :177, stdin hand-off), `workspace_replica_artifact.py` (`decode_worktree_artifact` :836), `replica_artifact_contract.py` (digest/limit codecs — pure, no memory risk), `git.py` (`run_git_bytes` :654, `_write_git_stdin` :604, `_GIT_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_S=300` :83)\n- Tests: `backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py` (21), `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py` (26)\n\n## Findings\n\n| # | Severity | Location | Finding |\n|---|----------|----------|---------|\n| F1 | **high** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:487-570, 634-673, 1046-1109` | **~3x memory amplification per 1 GiB set.** `_open_pinned_regular` materializes every artifact fully (`_read_descriptor`, :534); `_recheck_pinned_regular` re-materializes for comparison (:570); `_inspect_pending` holds pins + compares against caller bytes (:659-670); `_inspect_final` re-pins all files and re-runs full verification (:1046-1055). For a 1 GiB exact-three set through `publish_artifact_set`: caller bytes (1 GiB, held for the whole call) + pre-stage verify decode copies (≤0.32 GiB) + stage pins (1 GiB) + transient `chunks`+`b\"\".join` per recheck ≈ 2 GiB sustained, ~3 GiB transient peak. |\n| F2 | **medium** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:618-627, 817-830` vs `broker_artifact_store.py:950-1070` | **No safe descriptor→publication bridge.** `BrokerArtifactStore` exposes pinned, chunk-hashed descriptors (bounded, 64 KiB `pread`), but the publication store accepts only full `bytes`. Any consumer must either materialize 1 GiB (F1) or reopen `root/operation_id/<file>` by path — the unsafe TOCTOU pattern this design deliberately avoids. The bridge gap is the architectural hole; the unsafe reopen does **not** exist in current code and must not be introduced. |\n| F3 | **medium** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:825, 1055, 1140` | **2–3 redundant full git verifications per publication.** Pre-stage verify + post-rename `_inspect_final` verify (each runs `git bundle unbundle` + `index-pack --strict` over the full set), and `inspect_published_artifact_set` repeats it. For 1 GiB sets this is large repeated CPU/IO under a fixed 300 s per-command timeout (`git.py:83`) — an operational timeout risk independent of memory. |\n| F4 | **low** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:487-502` | `_read_descriptor` builds `chunks` list then `b\"\".join` → transient 2x file-size allocation per call; invoked ~2x per artifact in `_inspect_pending` and ~2x in `_inspect_final`. |\n| F5 | **low** | `workspace_replica_artifact.py:875, 886` | `decode_worktree_artifact` copies index payload (`bytes(index_payload)`) and manifest entry content slices ≈ artifact size again (bounded by default worktree limits at 256 MiB, but adds to peak in every verify). |\n| F6 | **low** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:369-370, 386-388`; `workspace_replica_object_pack.py:24` | Inventory receipt digests build full in-memory `asdict` lists + one canonical-JSON blob for up to 1M objects (index-pack listing cap 64 MiB) — bounded but hundreds-of-MB transient worst case; could use incremental hashing. |\n| F7 | **info (confirmed safe)** | `broker_artifact_store.py:650-697, 728-744, 1009-1058` | Descriptor APIs are sound: dirfd-anchored `O_NOFOLLOW` opens with fstat-vs-named identity checks; content only via chunked `pread` from pinned fds; `recheck_opened` uses path `lstat(self._root)` strictly as a fail-closed identity cross-check, never for data. Publication store name-opens are likewise dirfd-anchored with post-read identity re-checks. Preserve these invariants in any change. |\n\n## Bounded implementation proposal (not applied)\n\nGoal: move one exact-three set from broker-pinned descriptors to publication with O(chunk) memory (chunk 64–256 KiB), no path reopen, unchanged receipts/atomicity.\n\n1. **Additive descriptor-sourced publish** (new method on `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`, e.g. `publish_artifact_set_from_descriptors(declaration, sources)` where `sources` carries `(fd, byte_length, sha256)` from `OpenedArtifact`): stage each artifact by streaming `os.pread` chunks into `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW` 0600 files in the pending dir, hashing while writing, verifying declared length+digest (mirror of the proven `_receive_one`/`_write_all` pattern in `broker_artifact_store.py:329-351, 414-427`). This is a public-contract addition — needs parent approval before implementation.\n2. **Digest-based pin rechecks**: replace `_PinnedRegular.content` retention with chunked re-hash from the pinned descriptor; keep the existing two-pass open/recheck race detection and all identity/mode/nlink checks (`_inspect_pending`, `_inspect_final`, `_recheck_pinned_regular`). Marker (`artifact-set.json`, ≤1 MiB) stays byte-exact.\n3. **File-backed codec variants** (mechanical): `verify_index_object_pack` gains a staged-file input (`git index-pack --strict <path>` instead of `stdin_bytes`, removing the `git.py:614` single-shot 512 MiB `stream.write`); bundle verification is already disk-backed (`_write_private_bundle`) — feed it the staged file and compute sha256 chunk-wise.\n4. **Explicitly forbidden**: reopening `root/operation_id/<file>` by path for content; all reads stay on pinned fds; names checked only via dirfd-relative identity comparisons.\n5. **Deferred follow-up (quantified residual)**: fully streaming `decode_worktree_artifact`; interim keeps bytes decode for the worktree role only → residual peak ≈ worktree size + copies ≤ ~0.6 GiB (vs ~3 GiB today).\n\n**Tests** (mirror existing conventions in the two suites): receipts identical between bytes- and descriptor-path publication; digest mismatch mid-staging rejects and quarantines pending; source mutation after pin (`os.pwrite` via pre-opened fd) rejected by digest recheck with an `os.open` counter proving no per-content path reopen; `tracemalloc` peak bounded by chunk size, not set size, on an 8 MiB multi-chunk fixture; existing rename/collision/quarantine/cancellation tests remain authoritative and must stay green.\n\n## Commands run\n- `python -m pytest tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py -q` (backend venv) → **50 passed** in 37s (green baseline; system python lacks deps — use `backend/.venv`).","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/b267e7ed/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"worker-advanced","task":"Read-only review of artifact verification/publication memory and descriptor safety. Inspect BrokerArtifactStore opened descriptor APIs and WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore bytes APIs and verification codecs. Propose a bounded implementation that avoids unsafe path reopen and unacceptable memory amplification for up to 1 GiB exact-three sets, with limited changes and tests. Do not modify.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-advanced","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"565a91b015cc6bc793baff7841998333bbab7248b5d0b7d25229e7dd86cacb11","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":true,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":["sha256:890420901a90541d"],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4","sha256:890420901a90541d"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":0,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":81593,"output":15813,"cacheRead":596736,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":15},"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max","thinking":"max","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/b267e7ed_worker-advanced_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/b267e7ed_worker-advanced_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/b267e7ed_worker-advanced_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/b267e7ed_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/b267e7ed_worker-advanced_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/b267e7ed_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":16,"graceTurns":3,"outcome":"within-budget","turnCount":15},"toolBudget":{"hard":80,"soft":55,"block":["bash","read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":24,"outcome":"within-budget"},"context":"fresh","progressSummary":{"toolCount":24,"tokens":97406,"durationMs":517260},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"not-applicable","expected":false,"attempted":true}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"Baseline confirmed: all 50 tests in the two focused files pass. I have completed the read-only review. No files were modified, nothing staged.\n\n# Review: artifact verification/publication memory & descriptor safety\n\n## Scope inspected\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` — `BrokerArtifactStore`, `OpenedArtifact`/`OpenedReplicaArtifacts`, `open_incoming`/`open_incoming_async` (:950/:984), `recheck_opened(_async)` (:1009/:1061), `inspect_incoming(_async)` (:1065/:1070)\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py` — bytes APIs `verify_artifact_set` (:618), `publish_artifact_set` (:817), `inspect_published_artifact_set` (:1140); pin/read machinery `_read_descriptor` (:487), `_open_pinned_regular` (:502), `_recheck_pinned_regular` (:548), `_inspect_pending` (:634), `_inspect_final` (:984)\n- Verification codecs: `workspace_replica_bundle.py` (`verify_committed_bundle` :287, `_write_private_bundle` :244), `workspace_replica_object_pack.py` (`verify_index_object_pack` :177, stdin hand-off), `workspace_replica_artifact.py` (`decode_worktree_artifact` :836), `replica_artifact_contract.py` (digest/limit codecs — pure, no memory risk), `git.py` (`run_git_bytes` :654, `_write_git_stdin` :604, `_GIT_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_S=300` :83)\n- Tests: `backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py` (21), `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py` (26)\n\n## Findings\n\n| # | Severity | Location | Finding |\n|---|----------|----------|---------|\n| F1 | **high** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:487-570, 634-673, 1046-1109` | **~3x memory amplification per 1 GiB set.** `_open_pinned_regular` materializes every artifact fully (`_read_descriptor`, :534); `_recheck_pinned_regular` re-materializes for comparison (:570); `_inspect_pending` holds pins + compares against caller bytes (:659-670); `_inspect_final` re-pins all files and re-runs full verification (:1046-1055). For a 1 GiB exact-three set through `publish_artifact_set`: caller bytes (1 GiB, held for the whole call) + pre-stage verify decode copies (≤0.32 GiB) + stage pins (1 GiB) + transient `chunks`+`b\"\".join` per recheck ≈ 2 GiB sustained, ~3 GiB transient peak. |\n| F2 | **medium** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:618-627, 817-830` vs `broker_artifact_store.py:950-1070` | **No safe descriptor→publication bridge.** `BrokerArtifactStore` exposes pinned, chunk-hashed descriptors (bounded, 64 KiB `pread`), but the publication store accepts only full `bytes`. Any consumer must either materialize 1 GiB (F1) or reopen `root/operation_id/<file>` by path — the unsafe TOCTOU pattern this design deliberately avoids. The bridge gap is the architectural hole; the unsafe reopen does **not** exist in current code and must not be introduced. |\n| F3 | **medium** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:825, 1055, 1140` | **2–3 redundant full git verifications per publication.** Pre-stage verify + post-rename `_inspect_final` verify (each runs `git bundle unbundle` + `index-pack --strict` over the full set), and `inspect_published_artifact_set` repeats it. For 1 GiB sets this is large repeated CPU/IO under a fixed 300 s per-command timeout (`git.py:83`) — an operational timeout risk independent of memory. |\n| F4 | **low** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:487-502` | `_read_descriptor` builds `chunks` list then `b\"\".join` → transient 2x file-size allocation per call; invoked ~2x per artifact in `_inspect_pending` and ~2x in `_inspect_final`. |\n| F5 | **low** | `workspace_replica_artifact.py:875, 886` | `decode_worktree_artifact` copies index payload (`bytes(index_payload)`) and manifest entry content slices ≈ artifact size again (bounded by default worktree limits at 256 MiB, but adds to peak in every verify). |\n| F6 | **low** | `workspace_replica_publication.py:369-370, 386-388`; `workspace_replica_object_pack.py:24` | Inventory receipt digests build full in-memory `asdict` lists + one canonical-JSON blob for up to 1M objects (index-pack listing cap 64 MiB) — bounded but hundreds-of-MB transient worst case; could use incremental hashing. |\n| F7 | **info (confirmed safe)** | `broker_artifact_store.py:650-697, 728-744, 1009-1058` | Descriptor APIs are sound: dirfd-anchored `O_NOFOLLOW` opens with fstat-vs-named identity checks; content only via chunked `pread` from pinned fds; `recheck_opened` uses path `lstat(self._root)` strictly as a fail-closed identity cross-check, never for data. Publication store name-opens are likewise dirfd-anchored with post-read identity re-checks. Preserve these invariants in any change. |\n\n## Bounded implementation proposal (not applied)\n\nGoal: move one exact-three set from broker-pinned descriptors to publication with O(chunk) memory (chunk 64–256 KiB), no path reopen, unchanged receipts/atomicity.\n\n1. **Additive descriptor-sourced publish** (new method on `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`, e.g. `publish_artifact_set_from_descriptors(declaration, sources)` where `sources` carries `(fd, byte_length, sha256)` from `OpenedArtifact`): stage each artifact by streaming `os.pread` chunks into `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW` 0600 files in the pending dir, hashing while writing, verifying declared length+digest (mirror of the proven `_receive_one`/`_write_all` pattern in `broker_artifact_store.py:329-351, 414-427`). This is a public-contract addition — needs parent approval before implementation.\n2. **Digest-based pin rechecks**: replace `_PinnedRegular.content` retention with chunked re-hash from the pinned descriptor; keep the existing two-pass open/recheck race detection and all identity/mode/nlink checks (`_inspect_pending`, `_inspect_final`, `_recheck_pinned_regular`). Marker (`artifact-set.json`, ≤1 MiB) stays byte-exact.\n3. **File-backed codec variants** (mechanical): `verify_index_object_pack` gains a staged-file input (`git index-pack --strict <path>` instead of `stdin_bytes`, removing the `git.py:614` single-shot 512 MiB `stream.write`); bundle verification is already disk-backed (`_write_private_bundle`) — feed it the staged file and compute sha256 chunk-wise.\n4. **Explicitly forbidden**: reopening `root/operation_id/<file>` by path for content; all reads stay on pinned fds; names checked only via dirfd-relative identity comparisons.\n5. **Deferred follow-up (quantified residual)**: fully streaming `decode_worktree_artifact`; interim keeps bytes decode for the worktree role only → residual peak ≈ worktree size + copies ≤ ~0.6 GiB (vs ~3 GiB today).\n\n**Tests** (mirror existing conventions in the two suites): receipts identical between bytes- and descriptor-path publication; digest mismatch mid-staging rejects and quarantines pending; source mutation after pin (`os.pwrite` via pre-opened fd) rejected by digest recheck with an `os.open` counter proving no per-content path reopen; `tracemalloc` peak bounded by chunk size, not set size, on an 8 MiB multi-chunk fixture; existing rename/collision/quarantine/cancellation tests remain authoritative and must stay green.\n\n## Commands run\n- `python -m pytest tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py -q` (backend venv) → **50 passed** in 37s (green baseline; system python lacks deps — use `backend/.venv`).","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789294502614,"runId":"b267e7ed","agent":"worker-advanced","index":0,"message":"worker-advanced is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":10,"tokens":83170,"toolCount":19,"elapsedMs":240471}],"attemptedModels":["z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":81593,"output":15813,"cacheRead":596736,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":15}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/b267e7ed/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Seven concrete findings with file:line and severity (F1 high: ~3x memory amplification in workspace_replica_publication.py:487-570/634-673/1046-1109; F2 medium: descriptor->publication bridge gap between broker_artifact_store.py:950-1070 and the bytes-only APIs; F3 medium: 2-3 redundant full git verifications per publish; F4-F6 low; F7 info attesting current descriptor handling is safe), plus a bounded implementation proposal and residual risks. Read-only honored: no files modified, nothing staged."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"cd backend && ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py -q","result":"passed","summary":"Green baseline: 50 passed in 37.02s (system python lacks deps; backend/.venv required)"}],"validationOutput":["50 passed, 2 warnings in 37.02s (tests/test_broker_artifact_store.py + tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py)","git status shows pre-existing modified files only; no changes made by this review"],"residualRisks":["F1/F3 stand today: any consumer wiring broker artifacts into publish_artifact_set will hit ~3 GiB transient RSS and 2-3 full git verification cycles per 1 GiB set, with a fixed 300s per-git-command timeout (git.py:83) as an additional timeout risk","Proposal item 1 adds a public API to WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore (contract change) and requires parent approval before implementation","Full streaming decode_worktree_artifact is deferred; interim residual peak ~0.6 GiB for the worktree role under default limits","tracemalloc-based memory test in the proposed test plan measures the Python process only, not git child RSS; it is a regression guard, not a hard proof","Bytes-path APIs remain as-is in the proposal; existing callers keep current behavior until migrated"],"noStagedFiles":true,"diffSummary":"No diff; read-only review with proposal only","reviewFindings":["high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:487-570,634-673,1046-1109 - full-content pins and re-materialization cause ~3x memory amplification for 1 GiB exact-three sets (F1)","medium: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:618-627,817-830 - bytes-only publication APIs force either 1 GiB materialization or unsafe path reopen when bridging from BrokerArtifactStore pinned descriptors (F2)","medium: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:825,1055,1140 - verification runs 2-3 full git bundle/index-pack cycles per publication (F3)","low: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:487-502 - _read_descriptor chunks+join transiently doubles per-artifact memory on every pin/recheck (F4)","low: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py:875,886 - decode copies index payload and manifest content slices (~artifact size again) on every verify (F5)","low: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:369-388 with workspace_replica_object_pack.py:24 - inventory digests build up to 1M asdict dicts plus one JSON blob in memory (F6)","info: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:650-697,728-744,1009-1058 - descriptor handling verified safe: chunked pread from pinned fds, dirfd-anchored O_NOFOLLOW opens, fail-closed root identity cross-check; no path reopen exists today and none should be introduced (F7)"],"manualNotes":"Task packet asked for findings plus a bounded proposal without modifying; the descriptor-sourced publish method is a public-contract addition, so per constraints it is proposed, not implemented, pending parent approval. Baseline tests are green (50 passed) via backend/.venv. Existing concurrent/cancellation/quarantine semantics in both stores (attempt quarantine, no-replace rename with identity-checked parents, post-rename unresolved states) were traced and should be preserved unchanged by the proposal."}},"toolCalls":[{"text":"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -type f -name \"*.md\" -maxde...","expandedText":"$ find /Users/user/projects/yinshi -type f -name \"*.md\" -maxdepth 2 | head -20; echo \"---\"; ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi"},{"text":"grep {\"pattern\":\"class BrokerArtifactStore\",\"...","expandedText":"grep {\"pattern\":\"class BrokerArtifactStore\",\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\"}"},{"text":"grep {\"pattern\":\"class WorkspaceReplicaPublic...","expandedText":"grep {\"pattern\":\"class WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore\",\"path\":\"/Users/user/projects/yinshi\"}"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/CLAUDE.md"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py"},{"text":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py","expandedText":"read ~/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py"},{"text":"$ ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/ | grep -iE \"ar...","expandedText":"$ ls /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/tests/ | grep -iE \"artifact|publication|replica\"; echo \"---