unch unchanged. Upload wire format is one normal length-prefixed signed control frame followed immediately by exactly the three raw artifact byte sequences in fixed order, then EOF. The relay is opaque, uses a compiled fixed socket path, has a hard aggregate input cap, cannot accept caller socket paths, forwards stdin with bounded chunks, writes EOF, then returns one bounded signed response. Upload service authenticates kernel peer UID before bytes, Ed25519 request key, protocol/database/broker incarnations, request_type replica.artifacts.upload, exact payload schema, configured limits digest, authority, and recomputed artifact_set_sha256 before BrokerArtifactStore.receive. Payload is the existing lifecycle metadata plus an authority object of exact physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id. Response is signed and exact {stored:true, receipt_id, artifact_set_sha256}. Invalid auth is fail-closed. Valid rejection/unknown returns signed stable result without secrets. Exact retries consume and validate the whole body. Add default-false upload gate and config only to the new upload daemon, not existing broker daemon. Separate connection timeout must strictly exceed store transfer timeout. Add systemd socket/service, tmpfiles, pyproject entry point, and focused tests. Preserve fixed paths, 0600/0700 ownership, bounded buffers, cancellation cleanup, no bytes in SQLite. Before edits read coding-practices, python-practices, and current code/tests. If TDD Guard blocks edits, return an exact parent-applicable edit packet instead of bypassing it. Run focused pytest, Ruff, strict mypy, py_compile, and systemd verify where possible. Escalate any contract conflict rather than improvising.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-expert","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"xhigh","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"4d8f7f3912903e1a4d52da099f62d6dac671343d33ce9ea9786fe42e13e89cd