ct_stdio_relay.py:89-105` uploads the complete body before reading any response.  \n   `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_transport.py:237-291` can reject immediately after authenticated metadata validation.  \n   Large remaining bodies make `writer.drain()` fail before the relay reads the signed rejection. The caller receives `transport_unknown` instead of `upload_rejected`.  \n   Reproduction with 16 MiB remaining body returned `relay_error transport_unknown`.\n\n   **Correction:** Read the response concurrently with body upload. A complete framed response should win over later upload-side connection errors. Cancel upload safely after receiving it.  \n   **Remediation:** `worker-advanced`, because duplex cancellation and terminal-outcome ownership interact.  \n   **Required checks:** Add integrated large-body tests for metadata, digest, limit, and trailing-byte rejection.\n\n2. **High — concurrent exact retries publish conflicting outcomes**  \n   `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:500-668` allows identical attempts to create separate pending directories.  \n   One rename succeeds. The other treats the no-replace collision as `upload_rejected`, without checking the winning final directory.  \n   Reproduction using one signed frame and identical bodies produced `[(\"ok\", None), (\"error\", \"upload_rejected\")]`.\n\n   **Correction:** After a publication collision, quarantine the losing pending directory. Then inspect the final directory against the exact manifest. Return its deterministic receipt when equal.  \n   **Remediation:** `worker-advanced`, because publication races and one-terminal-result guarantees interact.  \n   **Required checks:** Add synchronized concurrent retry tests. Cover identical manifests and conflicting manifests.\n\n3. **Medium — CLI timeout excludes control-frame input**  \n   `backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py:185-194` performs blocking control-frame reads before starting `relay_artifact_upload()` and its timeout.  \n   A partial prefix or frame can hold the relay process indefinitely.\n\n   **Correction:** Create one asynchronous stdin reader first. Read control metadata and body under one absolute deadline. Preserve buffered body bytes in that reader.  \n   **Remediation:** `worker-advanced`, because pipe ownership and cancellation must remain safe.  \n   **Required checks:** Add a partial-control-frame stall test and confirm bounded process exit.\n\nAuth-before-body ordering is correct. Systemd socket permissions, exact peer UID checks, fixed paths, and default-disabled gating appear fail-closed.\n\nNo unanswered questions. Findings block completion.","artifactPaths":["/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/5dcf482a/run-0/session.jsonl"],"results":[{"index":0,"agent":"final-review","task":"Focused review only. Inspect current new files broker_artifact_transport.py, artifact_upload_daemon.py, broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py, BrokerArtifactStore.consume, their two tests and three systemd files. Read software-design skill. Find correctness/security issues in auth-before-body, exact-three body, signed response, retry, early rejection with a relay that writes all body before reading, timeout/cancellation, config and socket activation. Existing 112 tests and static checks pass. Do not inspect unrelated repository areas and do not modify. Return concise findings and remediation, or no remediation needed.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"final-review","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"b5867dd4b4443d480504603c00fce76d447b1a065bf3643b22a03e8a66ab6ca3","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":false,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":[],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"omit