{"type":"message","id":"39ba5584","parentId":"a9ee376e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T13:41:42.249Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ppTNRXraHtd0U2TRkFfDikyQ|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6a5179dd087d0aae3821c1bc49f00","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"review\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"e4b57ee2\",\n  \"output\": \"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 20 assistant turns (soft limit 20, grace 4). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Confirmed finding\\n\\n**High — Previsibility cancellation or copy rejection becomes falsely unresolved**\\n\\nLocations:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:518-564`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1044-1052`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1282-1322`\\n- Missing coverage: `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py:330-367`\\n\\n`_write_descriptor_regular()` creates its target before returning identity. The caller records identity only after `_run_blocking()` returns.\\n\\nDuring cancellation, `_run_blocking()` waits for the thread, then raises `CancelledError`. During source mutation, the writer raises before returning identity.\\n\\nBoth paths leave a created file absent from `file_identities`. Cleanup successfully quarantines the pending directory. It then rejects the untracked file as an extra entry and raises `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError`.\\n\\nThis masks a known previsibility cancellation or rejection. No final publication exists, so post-visibility uncertainty does not apply.\\n\\nExisting cancellation coverage pauses during the third source recheck. All copied file identities already exist then. It does not exercise cancellation inside `to_thread`.\\n\\n### Correction\\n\\nCreate and record each target identity before entering cancellable copy work. Pass the retained target descriptor into the worker.\\n\\nAlternative cleanup must safely recognize partially created fixed-role files. It must not weaken foreign-entry, ownership, no-follow, or link-count checks.\\n\\n### Remediation plan\\n\\nUse `worker-advanced`. Fix spans thread cancellation, descriptor ownership, quarantine verification, and error classification.\\n\\nRequired checks:\\n\\n1. Cancel during an active descriptor copy after target creation.\\n2. Confirm worker completion precedes descriptor closure.\\n3. Confirm `CancelledError` survives and one quarantine remains.\\n4. Mutate source during copy and expect `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError`.\\n5. Confirm no final target appears in either case.\\n6. Run 66 scoped tests, Ruff, format check, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check`.\\n\\n## Other reviewed areas\\n\\nNo additional defect found in scoped path handling, hashing, lengths, marker comparison, no-replace publication, or post-visibility unknown handling.\\n\\nScoped modules contain no `/proc/self/fd` or `/dev/fd` assumptions. Bundle Git commands use broker-owned private temporary copies.\\n\\nDuplicate semantic verification remains a performance risk. `publish_opened_artifact_set()` verifies before copying, then final inspection verifies again.\\n\\n## Review limits\\n\\nNo production caller currently uses the new opened APIs. Future coordinator integration remains outside this diff.\\n\\nWorker-reported 66-test results were fresh, so they were not repeated. Those tests do not cover the confirmed failure path.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/e4b57ee2/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n      \"task\": \"Review actual current descriptor-pinned verification/publication diff with software-design skill. Scope: workspace_re