publication exists, so post-visibility uncertainty does not apply.\n\nExisting cancellation coverage pauses during the third source recheck. All copied file identities already exist then. It does not exercise cancellation inside `to_thread`.\n\n### Correction\n\nCreate and record each target identity before entering cancellable copy work. Pass the retained target descriptor into the worker.\n\nAlternative cleanup must safely recognize partially created fixed-role files. It must not weaken foreign-entry, ownership, no-follow, or link-count checks.\n\n### Remediation plan\n\nUse `worker-advanced`. Fix spans thread cancellation, descriptor ownership, quarantine verification, and error classification.\n\nRequired checks:\n\n1. Cancel during an active descriptor copy after target creation.\n2. Confirm worker completion precedes descriptor closure.\n3. Confirm `CancelledError` survives and one quarantine remains.\n4. Mutate source during copy and expect `ReplicaPublicationRejectedError`.\n5. Confirm no final target appears in either case.\n6. Run 66 scoped tests, Ruff, format check, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check`.\n\n## Other reviewed areas\n\nNo additional defect found in scoped path handling, hashing, lengths, marker comparison, no-replace publication, or post-visibility unknown handling.\n\nScoped modules contain no `/proc/self/fd` or `/dev/fd` assumptions. Bundle Git commands use broker-owned private temporary copies.\n\nDuplicate semantic verification remains a performance risk. `publish_opened_artifact_set()` verifies before copying, then final inspection verifies again.\n\n## Review limits\n\nNo production caller currently uses the new opened APIs. Future coordinator integration remains outside this diff.\n\nWorker-reported 66-test results were fresh, so they were not repeated. Those tests do not cover the confirmed failure path.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789306382968,"runId":"e4b57ee2","agen