hild was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\\n\\n## Confirmed finding\\n\\n**High — Previsibility cancellation or copy rejection becomes falsely unresolved**\\n\\nLocations:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:518-564`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1044-1052`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1282-1322`\\n- Missing coverage: `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py:330-367`\\n\\n`_write_descriptor_regular()` creates its target before returning identity. The caller records identity only after `_run_blocking()` returns.\\n\\nDuring cancellation, `_run_blocking()` waits for the thread, then raises `CancelledError`. During source mutation, the writer raises before returning identity.\\n\\nBoth paths leave a created file absent from `file_identities`. Cleanup successfully quarantines the pending directory. It then rejects the untracked file as an extra entry and raises `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError`.\\n\\nThis masks a known previsibility cancellation or rejection. No final publication exists, so post-visibility uncertainty does not apply.\\n\\nExisting cancellation coverage pauses during the third source recheck. All copied file identities already exist then. It does not exercise cancellation inside `to_thread`.\\n\\n### Correction\\n\\nCreate and record each target identity before entering cancellable copy work. Pass the retained target descriptor into the worker.\\n\\nAlternative cleanup must safely recognize partially created fixed-role files. It must not weaken foreign-entry, ownership, no-follow, or link-count checks.\\n\\n### Remediation plan\\n\\nUse `worker-advanced`. Fix spans thread cancellation, descriptor ow...","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only task wording"],"criteria":[{"id":"cr