{"type":"compaction","id":"188cb38d","parentId":"be57297c","timestamp":"2026-09-13T13:46:55.432Z","summary":"## Goal\nFinish Phases 6 and 7 of `/Users/user/Downloads/yinshi-thread-orchestration-plan.md` in `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`, validate independently, then commit, rebase, and push.\n\n- Phase 6 covers managed child integration, deterministic Git application and recovery, broker-backed Linux isolation, authenticated desktop-to-VM transport, bounded repository ingestion, durable replica authority, and drain/export/reclaim.\n- Managed integration does not require Linux. Native Darwin execution remains fail-closed.\n- Phase 7 covers nested delegation, budgets, steering, and persisted delivery semantics. It remains blocked until Phase 6 is accepted.\n- Immediate work is correcting the descriptor-pinned publication cancellation defect, committing the reviewed deletion/integration and descriptor milestones, then wiring broker lifecycle dispatch and concrete effects.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Continue implementation without waiting, but request approval before material privileged infrastructure changes. Disabled VM qualification was explicitly approved.\n- Use at least five subagents where practical. The parent controls integration, commits, rebases, and pushes.\n- Preserve the heavily dirty inherited Phase 6 worktree and unrelated changes. Stage only reviewed milestone files.\n- Use `read`, `edit`, and `write` for source changes. Do not use shell source writes, mutating formatters, permission bypasses, manufactured failures, or production reversions merely to create red tests.\n- Do not disable, inspect, or bypass TDD Guard. Worker sessions may return exact parent-applicable edit packets when they receive `TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.`\n- RepoPrompt Context Builder sees a stale or missing checkout. Resolve capabilities against the actual checkout and do not invent APIs.\n- Use `backend/.venv` for backend tests. Ruff is `/Users/user/.pyenv/versions/3.12.3/bin/ruff`, version 0.16.5.\n- Required checks include focused and broad pytest, Ruff, format, isort, Flake8, strict mypy, `py_compile`, `git diff --check`, prose checks, Linux qualification, and independent review.\n- `docs/thread-orchestration.md` must pass `check_slop_file`; it currently scores 96/100. `docs/broker-root-launcher.md` scores 98/100. Both pass the local STE profile, with one passive-voice warning in `docs/thread-orchestration.md`.\n- No SQLite handle may cross an external effect or `await`.\n- Unknown transport, timeout, cancellation, verification, delivery, acknowledgment, effect, presence, absence, rename-state lookup, or SQLite commit results remain stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n- Preserve exact ownership, runtime acknowledgment, markers, receipts, synchronization facts, and A4 authenticated journal positions.\n- Root protocol remains exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`. All gates remain independently disabled by default.\n- Drain is graceful broker-to-executor only. Missing acknowledgment or a live runtime blocks reclaim. Do not add a fourth root stop action.\n- Artifact bytes remain outside SQLite. Only bounded IDs, roles, media types, digests, lengths, limits, and typed receipts may enter the journal.\n- Broker lifecycle v2 and the read-only legacy v1 journal must remain unchanged by replica-authority work.\n- Preserve existing `executor.launch`, `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX`, and the original one-frame `/run/yinshi/broker.sock` stdio relay.\n- Large artifacts use a separate fixed `/run/yinshi/artifact-upload.sock` data plane: one bounded signed control frame, then exactly `committed.bundle`, `worktree.yra`, and `index-objects.pack` in fixed order, then EOF.\n- The artifact relay is opaque, accepts no caller-selected socket path, uses bounded chunks and aggregate limits, and reads responses concurrently with upload. A complete signed response wins over later upload-side connection errors.\n- Upload authentication validates kernel peer UID, Ed25519 request signature, protocol/database/broker incarnations, exact metadata schema, authority, `limits_sha256`, and recomputed `artifact_set_sha256` before artifact bytes are accepted.\n- Exact artifact retries consume and validate the complete body. Concurrent exact publication collisions inspect the winner and return its deterministic receipt; conflicting or uncertain ownership remains rejected or unresolved.\n- Upload and lifecycle gates remain default-disabled. Artifact connection timeout must exceed the store transfer timeout.\n- Preserve fixed executor identities `yinshi-executor-00` through `yinshi-executor-31`. Callers cannot select them.\n- Keep `rft-sandbox` stopped and untouched.\n- Git replacement objects and lazy/promisor fetches remain disabled for artifact generation and verification.\n- Artifact verification uses independent empty bare quarantine repositories with matching SHA-1 or SHA-256 object format.\n- Descriptor-backed publication must not reopen incoming content through caller-formed paths. Open descriptors and named ownership must remain pinned and rechecked across verification and publication.\n- Bundle and index-object verification/publication must use bounded chunk streaming. Only `worktree.yra` may remain in bounded memory under its configured limit.\n- Publication rejects unsafe paths, symlinks, digest or length mismatch, partial sets, overwrite, timeout, cancellation, uncertain acknowledgment, root/final replacement, late metadata changes, hardlinks, FIFOs, and malformed declarations.\n- Publication requires exact root mode `0700`, pending/final directory mode `0700`, artifact mode `0600`, expected ownership, and link count one.\n- Publication uses same-filesystem atomic no-replace rename and correct file/directory synchronization ordering.\n- Public storage inspection returns `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` and cannot mint synchronization or publication authority.\n- Failed previsibility stages move atomically to unique retained `.pending.abandoned.<attempt>.<random>` quarantine names. Mutable names are never deleted.\n- Previsibility cancellation or copy rejection must not be mislabeled unresolved merely because a partially created fixed-role file was not entered in `file_identities`.\n- `limits_sha256` equals one broker-owned immutable configured profile.\n- Request frames authenticate with the configured Ed25519 request key. Responses authenticate with the key configured for the signed broker incarnation.\n- Artifact-root capacity is enforced across store instances/processes with cancellation-safe root-scoped locking.\n- The coordinator is stateless. `BrokerReplicaJournal` is the sole lifecycle authority. All seven typed effects are required at construction.\n- Coordinator input is an authenticated `BrokerRequest` plus its raw signed frame. Peer UID and transport authentication remain outside it.\n- Stage effects use absolute monotonic deadlines. Timeout or cancellation does not cancel an uncertain effect task. Late results are consumed but never appended as completion.\n- Persistence errors, including `ReplicaJournalError`, escape rather than becoming effect outcomes.\n- Startup recovery is serial. Another broker incarnation’s lifecycle becomes `broker_restart_unknown` without effects.\n- Export returns exactly three external references.\n- Managed-integration recovery distinguishes safe pre-mutation rejection from uncertainty after a potentially mutating Git command.\n- Terminal integration replay or cancellation reconciles and releases only the exact-owner admission marker after a fresh authoritative durable read.\n- Checking-stage retry reconciles durable trial intent before allocating another trial.\n- Integration conflict and success cleanup drain real threaded mutations before repository or admission ownership unwinds.\n- Integration cannot become terminal until required quarantine, metadata retirement, ref deletion, retained-root movement, and directory synchronization are durable.\n- Repository deletion receipts block workspace creation, deletion, execution, repair/publication, and managed integration before filesystem, runtime, or Git effects.\n- Final repository admission writes recheck deletion ownership inside the same `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction. Worktrees created before a losing final check are safely settled.\n- Failed workspace admission reconciles all durable owners for the exact repository/path. Cleanup occurs only when ownership is conclusively absent; exact, conflicting, or unknown state preserves bytes.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Phases 0–1 committed as `bebd2ccc`; Phase 2 as `e4a80b43`, `b488b502`, and `0cddd4bb`; Phase 3 as `2fd220b9`; Phase 4 as `ff7e6e81`; Phase 5 pushed as `1fa5d789 feat: add agent thread delegation and structured results`.\n- [x] Historical Phase 5 validation completed: backend 2137 with one skip, sidecar 119 with one skip, frontend 427, plus build, style, and mypy.\n- [x] Large Phase 6 candidate implements integration, immutable trials/results, physical admission, execution receipts, publication/recovery UI, migrations, and fixture Playwright coverage.\n- [x] Architecture A1–A7, corrected gate acceptance, publication acceptance, F6 acceptance, and offline A4 F1–F15 implementation/review were completed and recorded under `/tmp`.\n- [x] Integrated `workspace_replica.py`, its reconciliation suite, and `docs/workspace-os-isolation.md`.\n- [x] Trusted-Git gates, descriptor-backed Git operations, publication crash recovery, workspace repair, prompt-journal settlement, frontend repair handling, and durable repository deletion recovery were implemented.\n- [x] Repository deletion distinguishes imported and managed ownership, preserves imported metadata, uses durable receipts, handles unbound targets, and keeps malformed or legacy state unresolved.\n- [x] Root prepare/reclaim/launch use fixed paths, validated accounts, no-follow descriptors, mount checks, allocation locking, socket pinning, iterative reclaim, and default-disabled gates.\n- [x] Root persists `.executor-identity`, uses synced `.executor-identity.pending` publication, retains quarantine tombstones, and supports interrupted pin states.\n- [x] Linux recovery qualification passed for zero-byte and three-byte pending markers. Linux reclaim qualification passed with `repo=0000` and `home=0777`.\n- [x] Broker lifecycle v2 implements immutable `accepted`, `lifecycle_claimed`, `stage_started`, `stage_outcome`, and `stage_unresolved` events with fixed `prepare → runtime_setup → launch` ordering.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py` and action-bound `LauncherSocketClient.prepare()`, `launch()`, and `reclaim()`.\n- [x] Implemented read-only legacy v1 admission through `inspect_legacy_v1_journal()`, including malformed schema, unsupported version, accepted work, and WAL/SHM sidecar rejection.\n- [x] Implemented fresh-connection exact-event verification after uncertain SQLite commits and `JournalCommitAbsent`.\n- [x] Added `ManagedRootWorker` with bounded framing, serialized actions, separate process group, startup readiness, and kill/reap behavior on timeout/cancellation.\n- [x] Established nested deadlines: root worker 30 seconds, launcher client 35 seconds, broker effect 40 seconds, connection 120 seconds.\n- [x] Separated `LauncherTimeoutError`, `LauncherTransportError`, and `LauncherVerificationError`. Clean EOF maps to `transport_unknown`, invalid complete framing to `verification_unknown`.\n- [x] Final independent broker review `d00755d6` found no remaining findings.\n- [x] Focused broker/root lifecycle checks passed 172 tests. Strict mypy passed all 126 source files. Changed-file static checks passed.\n- [x] Latest broad backend run had 2797 passes, one skip, and three unrelated missing-`HOST` failures. Those passed with `HOST=127.0.0.1`. An earlier corrected broad run passed 2799 with one skip.\n- [x] User approved disabled Linux qualification on `yinshi-runtime`. Installed wheel, units, hardening drop-ins, and tmpfiles configuration.\n- [x] `systemd-analyze verify` passed. Hardening remained intact. Root-worker timeout/cancellation and broker v2 replay qualifications passed.\n- [x] Root launcher returned disabled responses for all three actions. Legacy accepted v1 work blocked startup without mutation. Sockets/services remained inactive. All effect gates remained false. `rft-sandbox` stayed stopped.\n- [x] Architecture oracle selected a separate broker-owned replica journal instead of extending launch lifecycle v2.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/broker_stdio_relay.py`, tests, and `yinshi-broker-stdio-relay`. Opaque fixed-socket relay validation and VM qualification passed. Review `096e5eb4` found no remaining issue.\n- [x] Implemented conflict-index support, deterministic `YNSHRA1\\n` artifact codec, bounded Git subprocess I/O, committed-bundle transport, strict Git-index parsing, and supplemental index-object packs.\n- [x] Committed durable workspace reconciliation as `abff2b2d`, bounded bundles as `2c781b53`, strict index validation as `533df501`, and staged object transport as `4242985d`.\n- [x] Implemented standalone three-artifact publication with descriptor-pinned verification, exact closure checks, safe atomic publication, authority-separated inspection, and broad race/failure coverage.\n- [x] Extended `broker_replica_journal.py` to require exactly `bundle`, `worktree`, and `index_objects`, object format, source-state digest, reconciliation fingerprint, `artifact_set_sha256`, and `limits_sha256`.\n- [x] Expanded `IngestReceipt`, `VerifyReceipt`, `PublishReceipt`, and `ExportReceipt` to bind the exact three-artifact contract and replica authority.\n- [x] Added `backend/src/yinshi/services/replica_artifact_contract.py`, centralizing operation IDs, identifier grammar, filenames/media types, distinct artifact IDs, limits hashing, and artifact-set hashing.\n- [x] `BrokerReplicaJournal` requires `expected_limits_sha256`, `request_public_key`, and a broker-incarnation-keyed `response_public_keys` mapping.\n- [x] Journal acceptance/replay authenticate signed frames, reject unknown signers, bind broker incarnation, recompute artifact-set identity, and reject duplicate export IDs.\n- [x] Journal schema remains version 1 and SQL shape unchanged. `journal_id` is a random 32-hex prefix plus the 64-hex configuration digest, length 97.\n- [x] `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` requires its exact configured limit profile and exposes `limits_sha256`.\n- [x] Implemented `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py` with fixed filenames, bounded streaming, descriptor/path checks, quarantine, reconciliation, root replacement protection, and cancellation-safe cross-process capacity locking.\n- [x] Publication pending/quarantine names are randomized. Retained failures do not block exact retries.\n- [x] Review cycles `763ded31`, `480936c7`, `0e505f45`, and `bf648f5f` exposed and remediated artifact issues. `636247c9` confirmed no remaining findings.\n- [x] Focused artifact/journal/publication tests reached 91 passes. Artifact-store tests reached 23 passes. Combined workspace checks passed 124. Expanded artifact/Git/publication checks passed 287.\n- [x] Ruff lint, strict mypy, `py_compile`, staged diff checks, and formatting checks passed for the artifact milestone.\n- [x] Committed nine reviewed files as `7f91105f feat: add authenticated broker replica artifacts`.\n- [x] Completed current-checkout read-only coordinator design run `ac665022`.\n- [x] Implemented `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py`, `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`, and minimal recovery support in `broker_replica_journal.py`.\n- [x] Implemented exact seven-stage order, immutable lifecycle context, typed effects/results, rejection/unknown handling, signed terminal responses, recovery, bounded owner waiting, timeout/cancellation handling, single-flight gates, reconcile-first retries, semantic receipt validation, signer verification, and same-process uncertainty barriers.\n- [x] Coordinator review found no remaining defects under the immutable journal-keyring invariant.\n- [x] Coordinator validation passed 74 focused tests, Ruff lint/format, strict mypy, and `py_compile`.\n- [x] Committed coordinator milestone as `922f197b feat: coordinate durable replica lifecycles`.\n- [x] Ran five current-checkout scouts for broker transport, admission, drain, export/reclaim, and Phase 7 requirements.\n- [x] Ran planner `d856fe34`, producing `.pi-subagents/artifacts/remaining-phase6-plan.md`.\n- [x] Managed-integration remediation distinguishes durable pre-effect preparation from potentially mutating `applying` recovery and preserves admission for unresolved application.\n- [x] Managed-integration conflict cleanup persists nonterminal cleanup-pending facts before cleanup and reaches terminal conflict only after exact cleanup.\n- [x] Managed-integration recovery binds the exact deterministic expected trial commit OID instead of accepting a same-tree custom commit.\n- [x] Every reviewed integration admission acquisition supplies recorded `physical_workspace_json`.\n- [x] Conflict cleanup validates entire mutable worktree bytes, including ignored, untracked, and late files. It uses no-replace quarantine and retains uncertain or changed content.\n- [x] `_run_threaded_mutation` shields and drains real threaded mutations before repository/admission ownership unwinds on cancellation.\n- [x] `_check_trial_root` recognizes exact `manifest`, `active`, `quarantine`, and `metadata-quarantine` phases.\n- [x] Successful managed integration durably records the applied result before fallible trial cleanup and reaches terminal `integrated` only after active registration, exact ref, and manifest retirement.\n- [x] Added endpoint cancellation tests for worktree rename before sync, metadata transition, and final sync.\n- [x] Added successful-cleanup replay tests for crashes after metadata retirement, exact ref deletion, and retained-root movement.\n- [x] Recovered `metadata-quarantine` and retained-only layouts now synchronize recovered roots and parents before terminal completion.\n- [x] Integration recovery-sync tests establish exact directory pairs, pre-ref synchronization, retained-parent synchronization, retained admission after failure, and successful replay.\n- [x] New managed integration holds one repository lifecycle scope through deletion check, preview, identity capture, reservation, and final transaction. Exact-owner continuation remains allowed.\n- [x] Integration tests verify internal preview/identity calls do not reacquire the held repository lock. No nested lifecycle deadlock remains.\n- [x] Managed-integration and repository-deletion focused validation passed 79 tests, then 81 tests after final cancellation-race coverage.\n- [x] Sidecar modeled-isolation fixture tests call `execution_prepare` and pass exact `instance_id` and `execution_id`; query results include the terminal `execution_stopped` envelope. The focused sidecar suites passed 23/23.\n- [x] Corrected repository-deletion admission across workspace creation, legacy checkout repair, execution recovery/reservation, trusted publication/repair, workspace deletion, and managed integration.\n- [x] `create_workspace_for_repo()` and `ensure_repo_checkout_for_tenant()` now use lifecycle-owning wrappers and private unlocked implementations so SQLite connections do not cross Git/filesystem awaits.\n- [x] Final workspace creation authorization and deletion checks share the insert’s `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n- [x] `_settle_unadmitted_worktree()` drains cancellation, tolerates expected cleanup errors, and persists an exact archived cleanup owner when deletion fails.\n- [x] Failed final workspace admission now uses `_workspace_admission_state()` to inspect all durable rows for the repository/path and classify `exact`, `conflict`, or `absent`. Cleanup runs only for `absent`; exact, conflict, cancellation, or lookup uncertainty preserve bytes.\n- [x] Tests cover cancellation before commit, cancellation after commit with a stale conflicting row, cancellation during cleanup, and cleanup failure with durable archived ownership.\n- [x] Final deletion review `5095be69` confirmed no remaining findings after the all-row reconciliation fix.\n- [x] Added `WorkspacePublicationConflictError` and stable generic HTTP 409 mappings for file and terminal APIs while preserving broader publication failures.\n- [x] Strict mypy passed the affected deletion/integration source. Scoped Ruff, format, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- [x] Corrected `docs/thread-orchestration.md` from `Version 10 uses tenant version 7` to `Version 11 uses tenant version 9`.\n- [x] Added the separate authenticated artifact data plane:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_transport.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/artifact_upload_daemon.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_transport.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_broker_artifact_stdio_relay.py`\n  - `deploy/systemd/yinshi-artifact-upload.socket`\n  - `deploy/systemd/yinshi-artifact-upload.service`\n  - `deploy/systemd/yinshi-artifact-upload.service.d/zzzz-yinshi-hardening.conf`\n- [x] Added fixed upload socket `/run/yinshi/artifact-upload.sock`, private incoming root `/var/lib/yinshi/artifact-incoming`, default-false `YINSHI_REPLICA_UPLOAD_ENABLED`, packaging entry points, tmpfiles ownership, and hardened systemd configuration.\n- [x] `BrokerArtifactUploadService` authenticates exact metadata and returns bounded signed success, rejection, or unknown responses without storing artifact bytes in SQLite.\n- [x] `BrokerArtifactStore.consume()` validates complete retry bodies without creating storage effects.\n- [x] Remediated upload review findings:\n  - Relay concurrently observes upload and response so early signed rejection is not lost behind `BrokenPipe`.\n  - CLI prefix/control reads use one async stdin reader under the absolute relay timeout.\n  - Publication collision quarantines the losing pending attempt and inspects the exact winner.\n- [x] Added 16 MiB early-response coverage, partial prefix/control deadline coverage, and concurrent exact/conflicting retry tests. Concurrent store tests passed repeatedly.\n- [x] Artifact transport checks passed 112 focused/regression tests in the worker, then 44 local focused tests; Ruff, format, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- [x] Final transport re-review `2ddc3887` found no remaining issues.\n- [x] Committed the transport milestone as `3c341628 feat: add authenticated replica artifact transport`.\n- [x] Added an uncommitted descriptor-pinned bridge across `workspace_replica_bundle.py`, `workspace_replica_object_pack.py`, and `workspace_replica_publication.py`.\n- [x] The bridge adds file-backed bundle/index verification, bounded chunk copying, descriptor-source APIs, shared `_verify_pinned_semantics()`, and source rechecks while preserving existing byte APIs.\n- [x] Updated `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py` so race tests patch the new shared semantic-verification boundary rather than hanging while waiting on bypassed `verify_artifact_set()`.\n- [x] Descriptor/publication worker validation reported five focused descriptor tests and 66 publication/bundle/object-pack tests passing, plus Ruff, format, strict mypy, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check`.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Fix the high-severity descriptor-publication cancellation defect found by review `e4b57ee2`.\n- [ ] In `_write_descriptor_regular()` and its callers, create and record target identity before cancellable copy work, or safely recognize only owned partially created fixed-role files during cleanup.\n- [ ] Add coverage for cancellation inside the `asyncio.to_thread` descriptor copy and source mutation while the copy worker is active.\n- [ ] Re-run the descriptor publication suites and independent review.\n- [ ] Stage and commit the reviewed repository-deletion/managed-integration remediation separately from unrelated dirty files.\n- [ ] Commit the descriptor-pinned bridge after correction and acceptance.\n- [ ] Add replica lifecycle broker dispatch without weakening `executor.launch`.\n- [ ] Wire concrete ingest, verify, and publish effects through `BrokerArtifactStore`, `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore`, `BrokerReplicaJournal`, and `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator`.\n- [ ] Implement verified broker-backed managed-Linux admission while keeping native Darwin fail-closed.\n- [ ] Implement graceful broker-to-executor drain, exact-three-reference export acknowledgment, live-unit checks, and root reclaim.\n- [ ] Refresh `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json`.\n- [ ] Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime` after production wiring changes.\n- [ ] Run full Phase 6 acceptance, then begin Phase 7.\n\n### Blocked\n- Phase 6 remains incomplete because descriptor-backed publication has one unresolved cancellation-cleanup defect and production lifecycle dispatch, admission, drain, export, and reclaim adapters are unfinished.\n- Production execution remains unsupported because `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py` has no verified broker-backed Linux profile.\n- The upload data plane exists, but no production caller yet instantiates and dispatches `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` with concrete effects.\n- Published artifact layout is not yet wired to root `prepare`.\n- Admission, drain, export, export-store, cleanup, and artifact lifecycle ownership/enrollment details remain incomplete. Do not fabricate support.\n- Some transport ownership/enrollment choices may still require a product decision.\n- Repository-wide Ruff, format, isort, and Flake8 include unrelated pre-existing failures, including two `F841` failures in `backend/tests/test_api.py`.\n- Phase 7 remains blocked until Phase 6 receives full independent acceptance.\n- Rebase and push remain pending until all required Phase 6/7 work and validation are complete.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Managed integration scope**: Git worktrees provide isolated child results and deterministic application. Linux is not required for integration itself.\n- **VM purpose**: `yinshi-runtime` supplies stronger OS isolation for untrusted execution.\n- **Privileged launcher**: Root accepts only fixed `prepare`, `launch`, or `reclaim` actions and a lowercase hexadecimal operation ID.\n- **No root stop action**: Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or a live runtime becomes unresolved.\n- **Separate privileged gates**: Prepare, launch, reclaim, artifact upload, and later lifecycle effects each require independent opt-in.\n- **Dedicated roots**: Staging, replicas, quarantine, workload sockets, protected pins, and incoming uploads use fixed broker/launcher-owned namespaces.\n- **Prepared namespace**: Broker writes staging. Root atomically promotes into protected storage.\n- **Promotion durability**: Sync the destination parent before the source parent.\n- **Executor pool**: Use 32 distinct host UID/GID identities.\n- **Allocation authority**: Root-owned `.executor-identity` is the durable allocation record.\n- **Quarantine tombstones**: Reclaim retains only `.executor-identity`. Failed artifacts use unique retained quarantine directories.\n- **Private workload `/run`**: Each transient executor receives only protected `/run/session.sock`.\n- **Broker authentication**: Canonical Ed25519-signed frames supplement Unix peer credentials.\n- **Separate replica journal**: Replica lifecycle state belongs in a broker-owned append-only journal, not launch journal v2 or application rows.\n- **Replica stages**: Fixed order is `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`.\n- **Replica public model**: Use `ReplicaAuthority(physical_target_id, replica_generation, execution_owner_id)` and bind ownership at `claim_authority()`.\n- **Replica decisions and positions**: `ReplicaJournalDecision` exposes `owner_broker_incarnation`. `ReplicaJournalPosition` contains `journal_id`, `sequence`, and `append_receipt_id`.\n- **Replica completion API**: Use explicit typed completion methods. Generic terminal recording is only for rejection and unresolved outcomes.\n- **Journal compatibility**: Keep replica schema metadata version 1 and SQL shape unchanged.\n- **Journal configuration binding**: Bind request key, response keyring, and exact limits profile into immutable journal identity.\n- **Terminal responses**: Build with `create_signed_response`. Result fields are `stage`, `state`, optional `code`, and optional `receipt_id`.\n- **Artifact storage**: Store only bounded metadata and receipts in SQLite.\n- **Fixed artifact set**: Every publication contains exactly `committed.bundle`, `worktree.yra`, and `index-objects.pack`.\n- **Configured limits**: `limits_sha256` is one broker-owned immutable profile.\n- **Artifact-set identity**: Bind operation, repository/workspace, object format, source state, reconciliation fingerprint, references, authority, generation, and limits.\n- **Committed-bundle boundary**: Bundles carry only explicit committed refs and optional committed HEAD.\n- **Supplemental objects**: `index-objects.pack` contains exactly required index blobs absent from the committed bundle.\n- **Artifact inspection authority**: Inspection proves storage only. Publication authority is minted only after successful atomic publication.\n- **Artifact attempt naming**: Broker-generated random names prevent retained failures from blocking retries.\n- **Artifact capacity**: Use cancellation-safe root-scoped inter-process `flock`.\n- **Publication root invariant**: Require exact `0700` before staging and after awaited final verification.\n- **Publication failure classification**: Only confirmed matching pending plus absent final permits safe rejection. Uncertain visibility is unresolved.\n- **Descriptor publication**: Hold incoming descriptors and recheck named ownership through semantic verification and publication. Stream bundle/index in bounded chunks; keep only bounded worktree bytes in memory.\n- **Previsibility partial-copy ownership**: Record target identity before cancellable copy work so known owned partial files can be quarantined without becoming falsely unresolved.\n- **Coordinator boundary**: One broker-owned stateless coordinator sequences injected typed effects. The journal owns all durable lifecycle position and outcomes.\n- **Coordinator ownership**: The coordinator uses one random owner token and its configured broker signing key. It does not authenticate transport or peer UID.\n- **Coordinator database boundary**: Journal calls complete before every `await`. Use read-copy-close, effect, reopen-transactional-CAS.\n- **Effect deadlines**: Each apply/reconcile call receives a fresh absolute monotonic deadline.\n- **Late effects**: Timeout or cancellation records stage-specific unresolved state and does not cancel uncertain tasks or append later completion.\n- **Reconciliation**: `StageReconciliation` outcomes are `completed`, `not_applied`, or `unknown`. Only `completed` carries a receipt.\n- **Started-stage recovery**: `completed` persists and advances, `not_applied` reapplies, and `unknown` records stage-specific unresolved.\n- **Owner mismatch recovery**: Another broker incarnation becomes `broker_restart_unknown` without effects.\n- **Missing effects**: Add injected protocols only. Do not invent production admission, drain, export, cleanup, or transport support.\n- **Conflict-index semantics**: One path has either one stage-zero entry or unique conflict stages 1–3.\n- **Git-index format**: Support versions 2 and 3 only.\n- **Intent-to-add**: Actual Git uses the nonzero empty-blob OID. Zero index OIDs remain rejected.\n- **Artifact envelope**: Keep deterministic magic `YNSHRA1\\n`, version 1, complete flag, and four ordered sections.\n- **Artifact source digest**: Use `SHA256(b\"yinshi-replica-source-v1\\0\" + four raw section digests)`.\n- **Artifact path policy**: Reject unsafe paths, `.git` components, missing parents, invalid topology, duplicates, hardlinks, unsupported kinds, and privilege bits.\n- **Durable stage boundaries**: Accepted intent and stage starts precede effects. Confirmed or unresolved outcomes precede progression.\n- **Verified commits**: Close a failed SQLite connection, then compare the intended event through a fresh connection.\n- **Action-bound launcher protocol**: Requests and responses bind action and operation ID.\n- **Failure classification**: Deadlines use `timeout_unknown`, transport loss uses `transport_unknown`, and invalid framing uses `verification_unknown`.\n- **Managed root process**: Timeout or cancellation kills, reaps, and disables the worker instance.\n- **Deletion policy**: Imported repositories preserve user Git metadata. Whole-tree quarantine requires explicit managed ownership.\n- **Trusted path policy**: Path location alone never confers ownership.\n- **Gate backstop**: `run_git_bytes` refuses trusted Git when isolation is unsupported.\n- **A4 ownership**: Application owns logical reservation/binding. Broker owns effects, synchronization, publication, markers, and physical release.\n- **Control stdio relay**: Keep it opaque and fixed to `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`, one request per process.\n- **Artifact upload data plane**: Keep large bytes outside `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX` and use the separate fixed `/run/yinshi/artifact-upload.sock` stream.\n- **Upload framing**: Send one signed bounded control frame, then exact artifact lengths in fixed role order, then EOF.\n- **Duplex relay completion**: Read the signed broker response concurrently with upload. A complete response owns the outcome even if the peer closes before all caller bytes are forwarded.\n- **Upload retry**: Consume and validate exact retry bytes. On a no-replace collision, quarantine the loser and inspect the winner rather than returning conflicting terminal outcomes.\n- **Broker dispatch separation**: Preserve strict `executor.launch` validation and route replica lifecycle through a separate authenticated path.\n- **Integration uncertainty boundary**: Parent HEAD/dirtiness rejection before mutation is safely terminal. Only failures after a potentially mutating Git command retain uncertain admission.\n- **Integration replay cleanup**: Terminal replay and post-commit cancellation use a fresh durable read before releasing exact-owner admission.\n- **Integration trial recovery**: Reconcile the latest durable trial intent before creating another.\n- **Integration cleanup phases**: Treat `manifest`, `active`, `quarantine`, and `metadata-quarantine` as explicit exact-owner recovery phases.\n- **Threaded mutation settlement**: Cancellation remains authoritative only after the real threaded filesystem mutation settles while repository/admission ownership remains held.\n- **Integration success cleanup**: Persist the exact resulting parent commit first. Keep the operation nonterminal until active registration, exact ref, and trial-root cleanup are durably synchronized.\n- **Repository-deletion admission**: Centralize one typed transaction-local guard instead of duplicating receipt interpretation.\n- **Deletion final admission**: Preliminary checks do not authorize later writes. Recheck inside the same `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction as each admission write.\n- **Workspace admission reconciliation**: Query all durable rows for the generated repository/path. Delete only when state is conclusively `absent`; `exact`, `conflict`, or `unknown` preserves the worktree.\n- **Deletion error mapping**: Workspace publication uses a distinct internal deletion-conflict type while file and terminal boundaries return generic stable HTTP 409.\n- **Guard handling**: Never disable TDD Guard. Use parent-applied packets and manual red→green checks if necessary.\n- **Phase 7**: Preserve the 20,000-byte contract, 100 pending inbox items, FIFO identity/generation, stop/seal/release ordering, unknown-cost retention, eventual depth three, persisted deadlines, and no scheduler. Default depth remains 1.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Correct `_write_descriptor_regular()` and publication cleanup so target identity is durable in memory before cancellation or source-mutation failure can leave a partially copied fixed-role file.\n2. Add cancellation-inside-`to_thread` and active-copy mutation tests, then rerun the 66-test publication/bundle/object-pack set and static checks.\n3. Obtain a clean current-blob review for the descriptor bridge and commit it separately.\n4. Stage and commit the accepted repository-deletion and managed-integration remediation without including unrelated dirty files.\n5. Add authenticated replica lifecycle dispatch while leaving `BrokerService`’s `executor.launch` schema and original relay untouched.\n6. Instantiate `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator` with concrete ingest, descriptor-backed verify, and publish effects plus durable reconcile behavior.\n7. Implement fail-closed Linux admission, graceful drain, exact-three-reference export, live-unit verification, and root reclaim.\n8. Rebuild and requalify `yinshi-runtime`, preserving disabled gates, inactive sockets/services, and stopped `rft-sandbox`.\n9. Run complete backend, sidecar, frontend, desktop, documentation, static, and platform validation.\n10. Obtain full current-blob Phase 6 acceptance and refresh `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json`.\n11. Implement and validate Phase 7.\n12. Rebase and push only after final approval.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Main checkout: `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`; branch `main`.\n- Latest committed milestone: `3c341628 feat: add authenticated replica artifact transport`.\n- Earlier Phase 6 commits include `922f197b`, `7f91105f`, `4242985d`, `533df501`, `2c781b53`, and `abff2b2d`.\n- The worktree remains heavily dirty with unrelated Phase 6 changes. Milestone commits must stage only reviewed files.\n- Repository-deletion and managed-integration remediation is implemented and accepted but not yet committed as its own milestone.\n- Final repository deletion review `5095be69` found no remaining issues after `_workspace_admission_state()` changed from arbitrary `fetchone()` matching to all-row `exact`/`conflict`/`absent` classification.\n- Deletion/integration focused validation currently stands at 81 passing tests with two dependency deprecation warnings.\n- Artifact transport commit `3c341628` includes 13 files and 1,887 inserted lines.\n- Artifact transport final review `2ddc3887` confirmed early-response handling, absolute stdin deadline, and concurrent retry collision handling.\n- The current uncommitted descriptor bridge modifies:\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py`\n  - `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py`\n  - `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py`\n- Descriptor worker `d108435a` reported five focused descriptor tests and 66 publication/bundle/object-pack tests passing.\n- Review `e4b57ee2` found one blocking high-severity defect: `_write_descriptor_regular()` creates its target before returning identity. Cancellation drained by `_run_blocking()` or source mutation can leave a created file absent from `file_identities`. Cleanup quarantines the pending directory, then rejects the untracked fixed-role file as an extra entry and raises `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError` even though no final publication exists.\n- The required correction is to create and record target identity before cancellable copy work, pass the retained descriptor into the worker, and preserve ownership/no-follow/link-count checks.\n- Existing cancellation coverage pauses during the third source recheck, after all copied identities exist. New coverage must cancel while the copy thread is active.\n- Production `BrokerService.handle()` still supports only `executor.launch`; no lifecycle coordinator is wired.\n- The new upload daemon is separate from the broker daemon and defaults to disabled.\n- VM `yinshi-runtime` runs the previously qualified wheel, not the latest local transport or descriptor changes.\n- Production v2 journal is absent. Accepted legacy v1 state intentionally blocks broker startup.\n- VM sockets/services remain inactive and all effect gates remain false.\n- `rft-sandbox` remains stopped.\n- Phase 7 plan remains `.pi-subagents/artifacts/8a18879f_planner_0_output.md`.\n- `/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json` is stale.\n- Full backend validation must use `/Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/.venv/bin/pytest`.\n- Passing local and disabled-VM checks do not establish full Phase 6 acceptance.\n\n<read-files>\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/027713c4_planner_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/05bb63fe_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/0a089013_worker-expert_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/1499b7eb_scout_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/1d6b483f_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/1d6b483f_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/265df3dd_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/274e0d6c_oracle_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/3777e15d_final-review_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/3c61b813_test-writer_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/44151b43_worker-expert_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/4596118a_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/678fba88_worker-expert_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/678fba88_worker-expert_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/71db4063_worker-expert_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/8b4b4a1d_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/8e834b23_worker-advanced_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/a8ebb94d_final-review_0_output.md\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/b013399f_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi-subagents/artifacts/c24c21c1_worker-