{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent_supervisor_request","content":"Subagent needs a supervisor decision.\nRun: 679887c6\nAgent: worker-advanced\nChild index: 0\nChild intercom target: subagent-worker-advanced-679887c6-1\n\nBLOCKED: TDD Guard rejects ALL edit/write calls from this subagent branch with \"TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch.\" It is content-independent — even a single test-file addition (which the guard's own instructions always allow) is rejected, and re-running the focused suite first did not create a binding. The guard's on-disk data (/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.claude/tdd-guard/data/config.json) says {\"guardEnabled\": false} but the enforcement layer still blocks my branch, and I will not bypass it (no shell writes).\n\nSTATUS: analysis complete, no files changed yet, baseline green (34 passed in tests/test_workspace_replica_publication.py, ~50s). Plan (3 TDD cycles, all within the 4 permitted files):\n1. Finding 1: add test_second_open_failure_closes_first_pinned_copy (red: bundle_copy fd never closed when index_copy open fails) → fix _verify_pinned_semantics with nested try/finally immediate cleanup ownership.\n2. Finding 2: add test_event_loop_heartbeats_during_descriptor_scans (red: _open_pinned_regular hashes 512MiB on the event loop; ticks==0 during scan) and test_cancellation_drains_scan_before_descriptor_closure (red pre-fix: loop deadlock/5s stall, task completes despite cancel) → batched implementation: move the cancellation-draining _run_blocking into workspace_replica_bundle.py (lowest of the three modules, no import cycle; object_pack and publication import it), wrap _validate_pinned_bundle/_recheck_pinned_bundle and _validate_pinned_pack calls in await _run_blocking, and in publication wrap _inspect_pending call, add _open_pinned_files/_recheck_pinned_files helpers for _inspect_final, and centralize blocking semantic verification (_match_declared_contents, _decode_declared_worktree) behind _run_blocking. Descriptors stay open across every await; all closes happen only after drained awaits (verified against every descriptor owner: opened artifacts, root_descriptor, pins, bundle_copy/index_copy).\n3. Finding 3 (test-only): correct test_source_mutation_during_descriptor_copy_is_rejected_before_visibility to mutate index-objects.pack at copy #5 (its active pending copy), assert RejectedError \"truncated\", exactly one .pending.abandoned.* quarantine (retaining the mutated pack bytes), no other pending dirs, and absent final visibility.\n\nDECISION NEEDED: (a) bind a TDD request to session branch worker-advanced (subagent-chat-01a06abb) so I can proceed with the TDD cycles normally, or (b) authorize exact-edit-packet mode, and I will return the complete unified edit packets for all cycles in my final report without writing files.\n\nReply with: subagent_supervisor({ action: \"reply\", replyTo: \"69f3ab5c-0d6a-4ba2-8f61-decde871f08b\", message: \"...\" })","display":true,"details":{"id":"69f3ab5c-0d6a-4ba2-8f61-decde871f08b","reason":"need_decision","expectsReply":true,"runId":"679887c6","agent":"worker-advanced","childIndex":0},"id":"fbd092c4","parentId":"7b89b28b","timestamp":"2026-09-13T14:31:28.291Z"}
