{"type":"message","id":"4a60881f","parentId":"40de5789","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:08:40.450Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7XCns4eyb9WvkUVQNhNr5520|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bc7608c087d0a9b1bec097125603","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"==== 8d81b68a\n## Review result\n\nNo findings remain. Prior pre-start cancellation defect is resolved.\n\n- `execution_broker.py:250-273` distinguishes finalizer cancellation from caller cancellation.\n- Canceled finalizers durably record `cancelled_uncertain` before returning.\n- Caller cancellation remains preserved through `current_task.cancelling()`.\n- `broker_journal.py:589-628` makes unresolved state durable and restart-safe.\n- Regression test confirms bounded completion, zero launch calls, unresolved response, and no restart launch.\n- Cancellation ownership remains inside `BrokerService`. Journal transition policy remains encapsulated by `BrokerJournal`.\n\nNo remediation is needed.\n==== b7055d03\n## Review result\n\nNo findings remain. Prior medium test-coverage finding is resolved.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `backend/tests/test_git_bytes_runner.py:210-264` covers blocked stdin cancellation, overflow, and PID reaping.\n- `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_object_pack.py:48-265` covers both object formats, empty packs, bounds, thin packs, replacement objects, and source environments.\n- `backend/tests/test_workspace_replica_bundle.py:254-312` covers extra objects, replacement refs, and advertised non-commits.\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py:604-800` centralizes stdin ownership, cancellation cleanup, output bounds, and process reaping.\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_bundle.py:287-365` verifies bundles inside an empty quarantine and requires exact reachable inventory.\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_object_pack.py:190-318` verifies exact blob inventory inside an empty quarantine.\n==== be7d2a44\n## Review result\n\nNo findings remain. Deployment is safe to retain as disabled qualification infrastructure. No remediation needed.\n\nConfirmed:\n\n- Peer authorization occurs before frame reads.\n- Framing, configuration, logs, and shutdown fail closed.\n- Deployed launcher receives neither required execution opt-in.\n- Prepare and reclaim actions are absent.\n- Systemd sockets remain disabled at boot.\n- OrbStack overrides restore reviewed daemon controls.\n==== ea9d40e3\n## Review result\n\nNo findings remain in publication scope. No remediation is needed.\n\nPrior high-severity findings are resolved:\n\n- `workspace_publication.py:1369-1404` validates and reuses completed repository stages.\n- `workspace_publication.py:1493-1501` requires exactly one materializing receipt update.\n- `test_workspace_publication.py:1133-1190` covers both corrections.\n- `workspace_publication.py:1294-1317` preserves cancellation ownership based on persistence outcome.\n\nNo database connection crosses an await or external effect. Synchronous callbacks contain every connection use.\n==== fee088ff\n## Review result\n\nNo findings remain. Both prior defects are resolved.\n\n- Peer UIDs are compared before frame reads in both daemon exchanges.\n- Broker authority derives from `BrokerService.application_uid`.\n- Launcher authority defaults to `BROKER_UID`.\n- Both entry points sanitize unexpected startup failures.\n- `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` remain uncaught.\n- Later signature, protocol, gate, and launcher checks remain intact.\n\nModule boundaries remain sound. Transport logic owns framing and peer credentials. Broker owns authentication and durability. Root launcher owns privileged launch policy.\n==== dafb11a5\nTurn budget wrap-up was requested after 18 assistant turns (soft limit 18, grace 3). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\n## Review result\n\nNo findings remain. No remediation needed.\n\nVerified:\n\n- `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py:774-797` targets exact synchronization directory pairs and proves each pair was reached.\n- `backend/tests/test_thread_integration_recovery.py:798-807` proves metadata synchronization occurs before ref deletion.\n- Retained recovery targets `trial_root.parent` and `retained.parent`.\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/thread_workspaces.py:1553-1565` validates retained state and synchronizes both rename parents.\n==== fca93394\nTurn budget wrap-up was requested after 5 assistant turns (soft limit 5, grace 2). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\n## Clearance\n\nNo findings remain. No remediation needed.\n\nDisposition confirmed:\n\n- EOIE handling is fixed at `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_artifact.py:408-423`. EOIE must be final and unique.\n- Actual Git uses nonzero empty-blob OIDs for intent-to-add entries in SHA-1 and SHA-256 repositories.\n- Live Git output matched each repository format’s empty-blob hash.\n- Codec preserves intent-to-add flags through `ArtifactIndexEntry`.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789312120450}}
