{"type":"message","id":"bde3b6a0","parentId":"289695db","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:08:51.352Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_uaDmMaMTwF8nmLUMe860MZVe|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bc82c9d087d0ac1f966bdf0855b6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: rp-build\ndescription: Plan and implement substantial changes with RepoPrompt Context Builder. Use for unfamiliar repositories or changes spanning several files.\ncompatibility: Requires RepoPrompt MCP and Pi file tools.\n---\n\n# RepoPrompt Build\n\nUse the user's request as the task.\n\nStart with Git status. Locate the repository root before asking RepoPrompt to inspect anything.\n\nCall `repoprompt_context_builder` with a precise task description and `response_type: \"plan\"`. Review its plan and assumptions before changing files. Call `repoprompt_workspace_context` when you need the complete selected context. Ask the user only when an unresolved choice would materially change behavior or scope.\n\nImplement through Pi `edit` and `write`. The OrbStack repository mount is read-only, so never use RepoPrompt `apply_edits` or `file_actions`. Follow repository test-first rules for behavior changes. Run focused tests after each change, then run broader relevant checks.\n\nDo not improvise.\n\nUse `repoprompt_oracle_send` only for a specific question left open by Context Builder. Continue with the returned `chat_id` rather than starting an unrelated conversation.\n\nFor substantial changes, run RepoPrompt review against the final Git diff. Report changed files and commands run. Include validation results and remaining risks. Do not claim completion while required checks fail.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789312131352}}
{"type":"message","id":"14b3641b","parentId":"bde3b6a0","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:09:04.077Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating checkout consistency issue**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bc859ba887d0a74f7e56fa77d4b1\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating checkout consistency issue**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xvKHFsjg2rJnGjyRRlaLIwZv|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bc86d23487d0accf836c064086ba","name":"repoprompt_context_builder","arguments":{"instructions":"<task>Plan the next bounded Phase 6 implementation milestone: add authenticated replica lifecycle broker dispatch without changing executor.launch, and instantiate BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator with concrete durable ingest, verify, and publish effects using the existing BrokerArtifactStore, descriptor-backed WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, and BrokerReplicaJournal.</task><context>The current host checkout is /Users/user/projects/yinshi and is heavily dirty. Recent committed milestones are 922f197b coordinator, 3c341628 artifact transport, and 3092933f descriptor-pinned publication. Preserve the original one-frame /run/yinshi/broker.sock executor.launch relay and BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX. Replica lifecycle must use a separate authenticated path/schema. Coordinator input is an authenticated BrokerRequest plus raw signed frame; peer UID and transport auth stay outside. Journal is sole authority; no SQLite handle crosses await/effect. Stages are ingest, verify, publish, admission, drain, export, reclaim. For this milestone wire only concrete ingest/verify/publish and fail closed for unfinished later effects rather than inventing support. Upload daemon already stores incoming artifacts separately. Descriptor-backed source ownership and recheck must stay pinned. Unknown outcomes stay stage-specific unresolved. Existing gates default disabled. Identify exact files/APIs and an implementation-ready test plan. RepoPrompt may see a stale read-only mount; resolve only APIs found in its context and call out discrepancies for host verification.</context><discovery_agent-guidelines>Start at execution_broker.py, execution_daemons.py, broker_replica_lifecycle.py, broker_replica_journal.py, broker_artifact_store.py, broker_artifact_transport.py, artifact_upload_daemon.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, broker_protocol.py, broker_stdio_relay.py, config.py, and their tests.</discovery_agent-guidelines>","response_type":"plan"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":655,"output":418,"cacheRead":95616,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":27,"totalTokens":96689,"cost":{"input":0.003275,"output":0.01254,"cacheRead":0.047807999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.063623}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789312131358,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bc83d98887d09282ae9704e335d0","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"60bd140a","parentId":"14b3641b","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:11:18.276Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xvKHFsjg2rJnGjyRRlaLIwZv|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bc86d23487d0accf836c064086ba","toolName":"repoprompt_context_builder","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"backend\":\"headless\",\"chat_id\":\"6811F8CC-A495-4FBA-B568-6330D73A4423\",\"response\":\"The next bounded Phase 6 milestone should add a new authenticated replica-lifecycle dispatch path and wire only `ingest → verify → publish`. It must leave the existing `executor.launch` socket relay byte-for-byte behaviorally unchanged.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nImplement:\\n\\n- Dispatch authenticated lifecycle `BrokerRequest` values through `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator`.\\n- Pass both:\\n  - the parsed/authenticated `BrokerRequest`;\\n  - the original raw signed frame.\\n- Construct the coordinator with concrete effects backed by:\\n  - `BrokerArtifactStore` for ingest and verification;\\n  - descriptor-backed `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` for publication;\\n  - `BrokerReplicaJournal` as the only lifecycle authority.\\n- Preserve descriptor-pinned source ownership and recheck immediately before publication.\\n- Return stage-specific unresolved outcomes where an effect’s durable result cannot be proven.\\n- Fail closed if a request reaches `admission`, `drain`, `export`, or `reclaim`.\\n- Keep all existing gates disabled by default.\\n\\nExplicitly exclude:\\n\\n- Any change to `executor.launch`.\\n- Any change to its one-frame `/run/yinshi/broker.sock` relay.\\n- Any change to `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX`.\\n- Reusing the launch frame/schema for replica lifecycle.\\n- Implementing later-stage effects.\\n- Moving transport authentication or peer-UID validation into the coordinator.\\n- Passing a SQLite connection, cursor, or transaction across an `await`.\\n\\n## Files and changes\\n\\n### `execution_broker.py`\\n\\nAdd lifecycle routing after transport authentication and request decoding, but before the existing launch-only dispatcher rejects the method.\\n\\nThe dispatch boundary should conceptually be:\\n\\n```python\\nasync def dispatch_authenticated_request(\\n    *,\\n    request: BrokerRequest,\\n    raw_signed_frame: bytes,\\n) -> BrokerResponse:\\n    if request.method == \\\"executor.launch\\\":\\n        return await existing_launch_dispatch(...)\\n\\n    if request.method in REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_METHODS:\\n        return await replica_lifecycle_coordinator.handle(\\n            request=request,\\n            raw_signed_frame=raw_signed_frame,\\n        )\\n\\n    return unsupported_method(...)\\n```\\n\\nUse the actual coordinator entry-point and response types found in the host checkout; do not add a parallel coordinator API if one already exists.\\n\\nHard constraints:\\n\\n- The authentication boundary continues to own peer UID and transport authentication.\\n- Only authenticated requests may reach lifecycle dispatch.\\n- `raw_signed_frame` must be exactly the authenticated frame, not reserialized JSON.\\n- Do not add lifecycle cases to the `executor.launch` frame parser or launch handler.\\n- Existing launch calls must follow the exact prior call path.\\n\\n### `broker_protocol.py`\\n\\nDefine or register a distinct lifecycle request schema/method family if the milestone commits did not already do so.\\n\\nThe schema should carry identifiers and replay/idempotency material required by the existing coordinator and journal, but should not accept:\\n\\n- filesystem paths chosen by the caller;\\n- publication destinations chosen outside descriptor policy;\\n- peer UID or claims of transport authentication;\\n- embedded launch requests.\\n\\nParsing must be strict:\\n\\n- reject unknown lifecycle operations;\\n- reject extra or ambiguous fields according to existing protocol conventions;\\n- retain the raw signed frame separately;\\n- keep frame-size enforcement at the transport boundary.\\n\\nPrefer a method namespace such as the one already established by the lifecycle commit. Do not invent new wire method names until the host checkout confirms whether `922f197b` already defines them.\\n\\n### `execution_daemons.py`\\n\\nInstantiate one durable lifecycle dependency graph during daemon construction:\\n\\n```text\\nBrokerArtifactStore\\n        ├── durable ingest effect\\n        └── durable verify effect\\n\\ndescriptor-backed WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore\\n        └── durable publish effect\\n\\nBrokerReplicaJournal\\n        └── BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator\\n```\\n\\nRequirements:\\n\\n- Reuse the same artifact-store configuration and roots used by `artifact_upload_daemon.py`.\\n- Reuse the existing descriptor-backed publication-store constructor; do not introduce a path-backed shortcut.\\n- Give the coordinator the journal abstraction or journal factory expected by its current API, never a raw SQLite connection.\\n- Preserve daemon shutdown/ownership semantics for the journal and stores.\\n- Construct lifecycle dispatch only when its existing gate is enabled.\\n- Default configuration remains disabled.\\n\\n### `broker_replica_lifecycle.py`\\n\\nAdd concrete adapters only if the coordinator currently accepts effect protocols rather than the stores directly.\\n\\nRecommended adapter boundaries:\\n\\n```python\\nclass BrokerReplicaIngestEffect:\\n    async def ...  # exact existing effect protocol\\n\\nclass BrokerReplicaVerifyEffect:\\n    async def ...  # exact existing effect protocol\\n\\nclass BrokerReplicaPublishEffect:\\n    async def ...  # exact existing effect protocol\\n```\\n\\nEach adapter should perform one external effect and return the coordinator’s existing typed result. It must not mutate lifecycle stage state directly; journal transitions remain coordinator-owned.\\n\\nFor unfinished stages, bind explicit fail-closed effects rather than no-op or success stubs:\\n\\n```python\\nclass UnsupportedReplicaLifecycleEffect:\\n    async def ...:\\n        raise ReplicaLifecycleStageUnavailable(stage=...)\\n```\\n\\nThe coordinator should translate this into the existing stage-specific terminal/retry/unresolved representation. Do not collapse it into a generic transport error.\\n\\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\\n\\nUse existing durable operations for:\\n\\n- ingesting or adopting the upload daemon’s separately stored incoming artifact;\\n- verifying content identity, length, digest, descriptor binding, and any existing signature/provenance contract;\\n- reopening/rechecking durable state after interruption.\\n\\nDo not copy uploaded bytes through the broker frame. The lifecycle request should reference the separately uploaded artifact using the store’s existing stable identity.\\n\\nIf ingest has an ambiguous post-write failure:\\n\\n- query the store using the stable operation/artifact identity;\\n- report ingest-stage unresolved if durability cannot be proven;\\n- never advance to verify based only on an attempted write.\\n\\nIf verification cannot prove the expected artifact and descriptor relationship, fail closed at `verify`.\\n\\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\\n\\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` through its descriptor-backed constructor/factory.\\n\\nPublication must:\\n\\n1. Resolve the descriptor-pinned source.\\n2. Confirm ownership and expected artifact identity.\\n3. Perform any existing durable publication reservation/write.\\n4. Reopen or re-resolve the descriptor.\\n5. Recheck ownership, descriptor identity/version, and source binding.\\n6. Only then report publication success.\\n\\nA descriptor or ownership change during publication is a publish-stage conflict/unresolved outcome, never success and never an automatic repin.\\n\\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\\n\\nNo new authority should be introduced.\\n\\nEvery coordinator loop should follow:\\n\\n1. Open journal operation/transaction.\\n2. Read current authoritative state or record an intent.\\n3. Close/commit.\\n4. Await one external effect.\\n5. Open a fresh journal operation.\\n6. Reconcile the durable effect result and advance or record unresolved.\\n7. Close/commit.\\n\\nNo SQLite handle, transaction object, cursor, or row object tied to a live connection may cross step 4.\\n\\nEnsure replay after restart resumes from the journal’s recorded stage and reconciles the relevant durable store rather than blindly repeating an effect.\\n\\n### `broker_artifact_transport.py` and `artifact_upload_daemon.py`\\n\\nNo protocol merger is needed. Confirm only that lifecycle ingest can reference the upload daemon’s durable incoming-artifact identity.\\n\\nThe upload daemon remains responsible for receiving artifact bytes. Lifecycle dispatch must not:\\n\\n- accept artifact content inline;\\n- treat upload completion as lifecycle ingest completion;\\n- delete the incoming object before journal-confirmed ingest.\\n\\n### `broker_stdio_relay.py`\\n\\nNo functional change expected.\\n\\nAdd or retain regression coverage proving:\\n\\n- a launch frame remains a single frame;\\n- the relay still connects to `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`;\\n- `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX` remains the limit;\\n- lifecycle frames are not silently routed through the launch-only relay unless the host already has a separately authenticated lifecycle relay.\\n\\n### `config.py`\\n\\nUse the existing Phase 6 gate if present. Otherwise propose one narrowly named lifecycle-dispatch gate, defaulting to `False`.\\n\\nAvoid enabling it implicitly because artifact upload, publication, or launch is enabled. Startup validation should fail closed when lifecycle dispatch is enabled without all three concrete stores and the journal being configured.\\n\\n## Dispatch behavior\\n\\nThe dispatcher should distinguish these outcomes:\\n\\n| Condition | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| Authentication fails | Existing transport-auth failure; coordinator is never called |\\n| Unknown method | Existing unsupported-method response |\\n| Lifecycle gate disabled | Explicit unavailable/disabled response |\\n| Ingest durability ambiguous | `ingest` unresolved |\\n| Verification indeterminate | `verify` unresolved |\\n| Publication durability or descriptor recheck indeterminate | `publish` unresolved |\\n| Request reaches admission/drain/export/reclaim | Explicit stage-unavailable failure |\\n| Replay of completed stage | Reconcile through journal and durable store; do not repeat blindly |\\n| `executor.launch` | Existing unchanged launch behavior |\\n\\n## Implementation-ready test plan\\n\\n### Broker dispatch tests\\n\\nIn the existing `execution_broker` test module:\\n\\n- Authenticated lifecycle request receives both the parsed `BrokerRequest` and the identical raw signed bytes.\\n- Invalid signature never calls the coordinator.\\n- Peer UID rejection never calls the coordinator.\\n- A caller-supplied UID inside payload cannot replace the transport peer UID.\\n- Lifecycle schema is distinct from `executor.launch`.\\n- Lifecycle method with the gate disabled fails closed.\\n- Unknown lifecycle operation fails closed.\\n- Every existing `executor.launch` golden/regression test remains unchanged.\\n- A lifecycle request cannot be interpreted as a launch request or vice versa.\\n- Oversized frames are rejected by the existing `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX` enforcement.\\n\\n### Daemon composition tests\\n\\nIn `test_execution_daemons.py` or its host equivalent:\\n\\n- Enabled configuration constructs exactly one coordinator with:\\n  - `BrokerReplicaJournal`;\\n  - artifact-store-backed ingest;\\n  - artifact-store-backed verify;\\n  - descriptor-backed publication.\\n- Disabled configuration does not expose lifecycle dispatch.\\n- Enabling lifecycle without required durable dependencies aborts startup.\\n- Shutdown closes owned resources once.\\n- Launch dispatcher construction and dependencies are unchanged.\\n\\n### Concrete ingest tests\\n\\nExtend `test_broker_artifact_store.py` and lifecycle integration tests:\\n\\n- Ingest adopts/copies the separately uploaded incoming artifact using its stable ID.\\n- Correct bytes/digest become durably discoverable after reopening the store.\\n- Missing incoming artifact fails at ingest.\\n- Digest or length mismatch fails closed.\\n- Retry after confirmed ingest is idempotent.\\n- Simulated exception after durable write reconciles to success when the store proves completion.\\n- The same exception with an unprovable store outcome records ingest unresolved.\\n- No uploaded artifact bytes appear in broker request frames or journal payloads.\\n\\n### Concrete verify tests\\n\\n- Verification succeeds only for the expected durable artifact and pinned descriptor relationship.\\n- Tampered bytes, wrong digest, wrong length, wrong descriptor, or wrong owner fail.\\n- Store read failure becomes verify unresolved, not ingest unresolved.\\n- Replay of a completed verification does not mutate the artifact.\\n- Verification cannot advance the journal directly.\\n\\n### Concrete publish tests\\n\\nExtend `test_workspace_replica_publication.py`:\\n\\n- Publication uses the descriptor-derived source/destination, not caller paths.\\n- Correct owner and descriptor pin publish successfully.\\n- Owner mismatch fails closed.\\n- Descriptor changes before the write fail.\\n- Descriptor changes between write and final recheck do not report success.\\n- Ambiguous write outcome is reconciled from durable publication state.\\n- If reconciliation cannot prove the result, journal records publish unresolved.\\n- Retry is idempotent and does not repin to a newer descriptor.\\n- Symlink/path-substitution attempts cannot escape the descriptor-backed policy.\\n\\n### Journal/effect separation tests\\n\\nExtend `test_broker_replica_journal.py` and coordinator tests:\\n\\n- Instrument journal connections and assert every connection/transaction is closed before an effect awaits.\\n- Cancellation during each of ingest, verify, and publish leaves a recoverable journal state.\\n- Restart resumes from the journal’s authoritative stage.\\n- Durable success plus missing journal acknowledgement is reconciled safely.\\n- Journal success plus missing durable evidence fails closed.\\n- Unknown outcomes preserve their individual stage.\\n- Concurrent duplicate signed requests converge on one lifecycle operation.\\n\\n### Unsupported-stage tests\\n\\nFor `admission`, `drain`, `export`, and `reclaim`:\\n\\n- Coordinator never reports success.\\n- No no-op effect is invoked.\\n- Result identifies the exact unavailable stage.\\n- Replay preserves that stage-specific state.\\n- No later stage is attempted.\\n\\n### End-to-end test\\n\\nRun an authenticated request through the real broker dispatch with temporary durable stores:\\n\\n1. Preload an incoming artifact through the upload-store interface.\\n2. Submit the signed lifecycle request.\\n3. Assert durable ingest.\\n4. Assert verified identity.\\n5. Assert descriptor-pinned publication.\\n6. Restart the broker and replay the same request.\\n7. Assert no duplicate publication and the same journal-backed result.\\n8. Submit a request that would advance to admission and assert fail-closed stage-unavailable behavior.\\n9. Run the existing `executor.launch` relay suite unchanged.\\n\\n## Host verification required\\n\\nThe visible checkout at `/workspace/yinshi` is not the described host checkout:\\n\\n- HEAD is `e0d5049`, not one of the Phase 6 milestones.\\n- Commit objects `922f197b`, `3c341628`, and `3092933f` are absent.\\n- None of the named broker/replica modules are present.\\n- The configured remote does not advertise refs containing those commit names.\\n\\nTherefore, the class names supplied in the request are confirmed, but method signatures, protocol method strings, exception/result types, config-field names, and exact test filenames could not be verified. Before implementation on `/Users/user/projects/yinshi`, resolve them without modifying the dirty tree:\\n\\n```bash\\ngit status --short\\ngit show --stat 922f197b\\ngit show --stat 3c341628\\ngit show --stat 3092933f\\n\\nrg -n \\\\\\n  \\\"class BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator|class BrokerArtifactStore|class WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore|class BrokerReplicaJournal|class BrokerRequest\\\"\\n\\nrg -n \\\\\\n  \\\"executor\\\\\\\\.launch|BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX|broker\\\\\\\\.sock|ingest|verify|publish|admission|drain|export|reclaim\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe implementation should conform adapters to the protocols already defined by `922f197b`; any new API proposed above is a wiring shape, not authority to duplicate an existing host-side interface.\"}"}],"details":{"server":"repoprompt","tool":"context_builder"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789312278275}}
{"type":"message","id":"72a5c9d3","parentId":"60bd140a","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:11:29.811Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning API inspection with parallel scouts**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bd1a88a887d0b9701fdef4f766ef\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning API inspection with parallel scouts**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_X6vScbNLbcvvT5JjeN0OVx18|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6bd1cdfc087d0a1f8c5a4e28f066f","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"const results = await runs.all([{key:'dispatch-scout',agent:'scout',task:'Read-only inspect current host checkout /Users/user/projects/yinshi for exact broker daemon dispatch boundaries. Report current BrokerService.handle signature and authentication flow, daemon request framing, config gates, constructor ownership, and minimal files/tests needed to route replica lifecycle separately while preserving executor.launch and broker_stdio_relay. Do not modify.'},{key:'effects-scout',agent:'scout',task:'Read-only inspect current host checkout /Users/user/projects/yinshi for exact BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator effect protocols and journal request/context types, BrokerArtifactStore open/recheck/consume APIs, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore opened verification/publication APIs, and typed receipts. Propose concrete ingest/verify/publish adapter mappings and reconcile behavior using only APIs that exist. Identify any contract gaps requiring Sol decision. Do not modify.'}]); return results.map(r=>({key:r.key,output:r.output}));","async":false,"timeoutMs":900000,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","chatProgress":"auto"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":3883,"output":295,"cacheRead":96128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":56,"totalTokens":100306,"cost":{"input":0.019415,"output":0.00885,