{"type":"message","id":"fb01c82d","parentId":"1a751d4c","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:18:12.687Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_D4U1LxvXrmFp7Q8UvzXg2R0s|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6beb2405887d09578cfc9d4b0d83c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-a4-round2-worker.json:80:      \"summary\": \"Broker owns physical effects and durability. Filesystem remains an execution mechanism and is not an action authority.\",\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-current-checkpoint.json:35:    \"broker replica lifecycle wiring\",\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-worker-thought-1.md:62:        authority_hash=\"d\" * 64, database_identity=\"db-f1l\",\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-worker-thought-1.md:83:Wait — authority: repair row created with authority \"d\"*64 in setup; the recovery prompt_workspace authority = admission_authority(request) with tenant → different \"d\"*64? inspect query requires r.authority_hash = selected.authority_hash → MISMATCH → pending None → no recovery! Fix: authority must match. admission_authority deterministic per request state — compute it: authority = workspace_execution.admission_authority(request) AFTER setting tenant; use that in setup publish call. Same for F8 tests? F8 tests don't pass through prompt paths — any 64-hex works. F1 logical-only + status tests must use the request-derived authority. Status test uses _orchestration_request with client app + no tenant → authority = hash(db identity (settings db_path), None, mode None). Compute same way in setup. But db fixture: get_settings().db_path monkeypatched by conftest? The db fixture builds db from db_path fixture which presumably patches settings. request.scope[\"app\"] = client.app — mode attr absent → None. Compute authority via workspace_execution.admission_authority(request) in setup — guaranteed consistent.\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-worker-thought-1.md:87:For pre-binding test: setup acquire_prompt_workspace uses request → authority A. publish_apply authorize uses prompt_workspace (request) — consistent. Keep as drafted but replace fixed \"c\"*32 operation — acquire generates its own operation via parameter \"c\"*32 (I passed \"c\" * 32) — fine, recovery body uses same id.\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-worker-thought-1.md:89:In pre-binding test I set request.scope[\"app\"] = None — admission_authority: getattr(request.app.state, \"mode\", None) — SimpleNamespace(state=SimpleNamespace()) works. OK.\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-worker-thought-1.md:103:F3 runtime test: prepare_tenant_workspace_runtime_paths with authorize param — red currently: TypeError unexpected keyword 'authorize'. Green: proceeds; mismatched second call raises WorkspacePublicationError(\"Checkout repair authority changed\"). Note builder uses admission_authority imported from workspace_execution (lazy import to avoid cycle: runtime_paths → workspace_execution import at top would be circular? workspace_execution imports workspace_admission, thread_workspaces... does workspace_execution import workspace_runtime_paths? grep — not seen. stream imports both. prompt_journal imports workspace_execution. runtime_paths importing workspace_execution at top: workspace_execution imports services.sidecar, thread_workspaces, workspace_admission, workspace_isolation, api.deps — none import runtime_paths → safe. But keep lazy inside builder for safety per PYTHON.md \n[... omitted ...]\nte.diff:3796: The service rechecks current authority before mutations and recovered execution admission. It rejects siblings, self-targeting descendant operations, foreign repositories, invalid ancestry, and database mismatches.\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-publication-corrected-candidate.diff:4187:+  it(\"routes exact execution recovery through the selected runtime with stream authority\", async () => {\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-publication-corrected-candidate.diff:4226:   it(\"allows exact read-only thread routes with session read authority\", async () => {\n/tmp/yinshi-phase6-publication-corrected-candidate.diff:4561:+    def _authority(request