ct references only. It cannot recover authority after restart.\n- `execution_broker.py:165-177` accepts only `executor.launch`.\n- No durable authority resolver exists outside the replica journal.\n\nConcrete authority contract:\n1. Add exact `authority` object to signed `replica.lifecycle` payload.\n2. Use the same payload shape as `replica.artifacts.upload`.\n3. Require exactly:\n   - `physical_target_id`\n   - `replica_generation`\n   - `execution_owner_id`\n4. Parse authority only after peer UID, signature, broker incarnation, and database incarnation checks.\n5. Pass parsed authority to `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator.run`.\n6. Make `BrokerReplicaJournal.accept` parse authority again and require exact equality.\n7. Recompute `artifact_set_sha256` using that authority before any journal append.\n8. Store authority only through existing accepted-event columns. Keep schema version 1 and SQL shape unchanged.\n9. Reject missing, extra, changed, or malformed authority before effects.\n10. Exact retry must use the same frame and authority. Any changed authority conflicts with durable acceptance.\n\nThese identifiers remain opaque logical bindings. They never select host resources.\n\n- `physical_target_id` never becomes a filesystem path.\n- `execution_owner_id` never becomes a UID, GID, unit, or executor name.\n- `replica_generation` never selects a directory.\n- Root still receives only `operation_id`.\n- Root still chooses one fixed executor identity and writes its protected marker.\n\nSocket contract:\n- Use existing `/run/yinshi/broker.sock`.\n- Do not create another lifecycle control socket.\n- Keep artifact bytes on `/run/yinshi/artifact-upload.sock`.\n- Add an authenticated control multiplexer before `BrokerService`.\n- Route `executor.launch` to unchanged `BrokerService.handle`.\n- Route only exact `replica.lifecycle` requests to the replica coordinator.\n- Keep the original relay opaque, one-frame, and bounded by `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX`.\n- Keep launch and replica journals separate.\n\nPermitted transitions:\n1. Kernel peer UID accepted.\n2. Canonical signature and incarnation fields accepted.\n3. Exact request type selected.\n4. Independent lifecycle gate accepted.\n5. Authority and artifact declaration validated.\n6. Journal appends `accepted`.\n7. Journal appends `authority_claimed`.\n8. Coordinator advances through fixed stage order.\n9. Each `stage_started` precedes its external effect.\n10. Completion, rejection, or unresolved state is appended after effect settlement.\n\nFailure outcomes:\n- Wrong UID or signature: protocol rejection, no journal access.\n- Stale incarnation: protocol rejection, no journal access.\n- Disabled lifecycle gate: signed disabled response, no lifecycle acceptance.\n- Invalid authority: protocol rejection before effects.\n- Stale artifact digest after authority change: journal conflict.\n- Changed authority after acceptance: durable conflict.\n- Missing uploaded artifacts: `ingest/artifact_rejected`.\n- Store uncertainty: `ingest/transfer_unknown`.\n- Another broker incarnation owns work: `broker_restart_unknown`, without effects.\n- Unsupported later stage: stage-specific rejection. Never report success.\n\nDrift / contradiction check:\n- Current lifecycle payload omission conflicts with authenticated authority binding.\n- Reading authority from artifact storage cannot work. Storage deliberately drops it.\n- Adding a second authority database would conflict with sole journal ownership.\n- Deriving OS identities from authority fields would violate root isolation.\n- A second control socket would conflict with the established single protected broker control endpoint.\n\nRecommendation:\n- Extend lifecycle payload with the existing upload authority structure.\n- Add a same-socket authenticated multiplexer.\n- Keep `BrokerService` launch code unchanged.\n- Centralize lifecycle and upload payload parsing to prevent schema drift.\n- Add `YINSHI_REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED`, default `False`.\n- Do not enable production routing until all seven concrete effects exist.\n\nExact tests:\n- Lifecycle and upload accept the same payload dictionary.\n- Missing, extra, malformed, or wrong-type authority fields fail.\n- Changed authority with stale artifact digest fails.\n- Changed authority with recomputed digest conflicts after first acceptance.\n- Journal replay returns the stored authority.\n- Schema metadata remains version 1.\n- Launch frames reach unchanged `BrokerService` with identical bytes and UID.\n- Lifecycle frames never reach launch handling.\n- Invalid signatures reach neither handler.\n- Oversized frames fail at existing transport bound.\n- Valid-looking executor names in `execution_owner_id` never reach root requests.\n- Root requests contain only action, operation ID, and protocol version.\n- Lifecycle gate remains independent from upload, prepare, launch, and reclaim gates.\n- Original broker relay tests remain unchanged.\n- Artifact relay remains fixed to its separate upload socket.\n\nRisks:\n- Concrete publish recovery still needs an authority-preserving private reconciliation API. Public inspection cannot mint publication authority.\n- Admission, drain, export, and reclaim adapters remain unfinished.\n- Any existing authority-omitting replica journal entry will fail closed after payload validation changes. Current context states no production replica journal exists.\n- Production gate activation before all seven effects exist would create terminal partial lifecycles.\n\nNeed from main agent:\n- No user decision required. Existing trust and transport decisions determine this contract.\n\nSuggested execution prompt:\n> Implement signed `replica.lifecycle` authority binding and same-socket authenticated dispatch. Reuse exact upload authority schema. Keep `BrokerService`, `executor.launch`, existing relay framing, `BROKER_FRAME_BYTES_MAX`, root protocol, and journal SQL unchanged. Add defense-in-depth authority equality checks in journal acceptance. Ensure authority values never select paths, OS identities, units, sockets, or executor slots. Add independent default-false lifecycle gate and focused cross-protocol tests. Do not enable production lifecycle until every stage effect is concrete.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789312961435,"runId":"ff752f2f","agent":"oracle","index":0,"message":"oracle is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":14,"tokens":160952,"toolCount":28,"elapsedMs":240565}],"attemptedModels":["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":296856,"output":16228,"cacheRead":3909888,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":3.9260639999999984,"turns":31}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-13T15-18-40-038Z_01a09b59-5ca6-7905-9185-23be8150c810.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"attested","evidenceStatus":"attested","explicit":false,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"attested","explicit":false,"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["read-only/reviewer-style agent"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Return concrete findings with file paths and severity when applicable","evidence":["review-findings","residual-risks"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[],"verifyRuns":[],"childReport":{"criteriaSatisfied":[{"id":"criterion-1","status":"satisfied","evidence":"Reviewed journal payload validation, coordinator input, upload authority schema, broker dispatch, daemon wiring, root derivation, and transport documentation."}],"changedFiles":[],"testsAddedOrUpdated":[],"commandsRun":[{"command":"Read and search broker lifecy