{"type":"message","id":"6b2f15b6","parentId":"4bbd5405","timestamp":"2026-09-13T17:05:02.137Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bkwNZwxV2iByXnzeJAZklPrm|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6d3930d5487d0a4e8f367fcc48551","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"artifact-effects-review\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"9796f5a0\",\n  \"output\": \"## Review status\\n\\nBlocked. Three findings remain. Software-design skill loaded from required path and applied.\\n\\n### High: Reconciliation mints synchronization authority without synchronizing storage\\n\\nLocation:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1672-1696`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1191-1225`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:1492-1655`\\n\\n`reconcile_published_artifact_set` verifies storage, then creates a synchronization-bearing publication receipt. It never syncs final files, final directory, or publication root.\\n\\nA restart can observe a rename whose root sync never completed. Journal completion can then outlive artifacts after another crash.\\n\\nCorrection: synchronize pinned recovered state before minting authority. Recheck all identities after synchronization. Map synchronization failures to `ReplicaPublicationUnresolvedError`.\\n\\nRemediation tier: `worker-advanced`.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Reconcile a final left after rename-before-root-sync.\\n- Assert file, final-directory, and root sync ordering.\\n- Inject each sync failure. Require `publication_unknown`.\\n- Confirm no authority-bearing receipt appears before successful synchronization.\\n\\n### High: Operational filesystem failures become terminal rejections\\n\\nLocation:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_artifact_effects.py:274-280,319-330,367-378,397-404`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:234-245,679-695,772-790`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica_publication.py:627-644,1492-1525,1686-1695`\\n\\nLower stores wrap broad `OSError` failures as rejected errors. Effects then persist deterministic stage rejection instead of unknown outcome.\\n\\nInjected `errno.EIO` during incoming-root inspection produced:\\n\\n```text\\nactual=StageRejected:artifact_rejected\\n```\\n\\nTransient storage failure can permanently reject a valid authenticated lifecycle. Retry and recovery then become unavailable.\\n\\nCorrection: reserve rejected exceptions for proven invalid state. Map non-conclusive OS failures to owner-specific unresolved exceptions. Keep that policy inside storage owners.\\n\\nRemediation tier: `worker-advanced`.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Inject `EIO`, `ENOSPC`, `EMFILE`, read faults, and disappearance races.\\n- Cover ingest, verify, publish apply, and publish reconcile.\\n- Require stage-specific unknown outcomes.\\n- Preserve deterministic rejection for confirmed missing or malformed artifacts.\\n\\n### Medium: Incoming artifact limits are not bound to configured lifecycle limits\\n\\nLocation:\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_artifact_effects.py:443-458`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py:50-59,212-227`\\n- `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_artifact_effects.py:164-190,329-336`\\n\\nConstructor checks only publication limits. It accepts any `BrokerArtifactStore` size profile.\\n\\nCurrent defaults already differ. Incoming worktree limit is 512 MiB. Replica publication worktree limit is 256 MiB.\\n\\nUploads can accept artifacts that lifecycle later rejects. A narrower incoming profile can reject requests valid under signed configured limits.\\n\\nCorrection: expose one immutable incoming size profile. Centralize conversion from `ReplicaStoreLimits`, then reject incompatible stores during effects construction.\\n\\nRemediation tier: `worker-advanced`.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Reject broader and narrower incoming role limits.\\n- Reject aggregate-limit mismatch.\\n- Ignore transport-only settings such as timeouts when checking semantic compatibility.\\n- Use one shared profile conversion in upload construction and effects construction.\\n\\n## Confirmed behavior\\n\\n- Declaration validation binds request payload, context authority, artifact-set digest, and publication limits.\\n- Verify and publish use pinned incoming descriptors with owner recheck callbacks.\\n- Public `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` remains non-authoritative.\\n- Effects contain no SQLite access.\\n- Real descriptor-backed ingest, verify, publish, and reconcile path completed successfully.\\n- Final candidate passed 98 focused and regression tests.\\n- Final Ruff format and lint checks passed.\\n- No staged files exist.\\n\\n## Review limits\\n\\nReview covered three milestone files plus artifact-store, lifecycle, journal, and publication boundaries. Other dirty checkout changes remained out of scope.\\n\\nStrict mypy was not repeated. Reported pass predates only a formatting correction, so its result remains applicable.\\n\\nRemediation required before completion.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/9796f5a0/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n      \"task\": \"Read-only final review of current concrete broker replica artifact effects milestone in /Users/user/projects/yinshi. Apply actual /Users/user/.pi/agent/skills/software-design/SKILL.md. Requirements: ingest apply/reconcile inspect exact pre-uploaded BrokerArtifactStore set and map typed IngestReceipt; verify uses open_incoming_async plus descriptor-backed verify_opened_artifact_set and recheck callback; publish apply uses pinned publication and maps authority-bound PublishReceipt; publish reconcile may mint authority only from a fully authenticated declaration and returns completed, 