{"type":"message","id":"b955c07f","parentId":"174f1e0f","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:24:39.685Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_RL0VLUBvJ29lOHBMIAI003cn|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6ea6695fc87d08788fae44215a549","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: git-workflow\ndescription: Completes repository changes with explanatory commits, branch synchronization, and pushes. Use after changing tracked files or when committing, rebasing, merging, or pushing Git work.\n---\n\n# Git Workflow\n\n1. Inspect the worktree and preserve unrelated user changes. Stage only files that belong to the completed task.\n2. Write a commit message that explains what changed and why, so future readers do not need to reconstruct the decision from the diff.\n3. Pull the remote branch with rebase before pushing. Continue without asking for routine confirmation; stop for user input if a merge conflict requires a decision.\n4. Push to the correct branch, usually `main` or `master`.\n\nThe workflow is complete when the task's commit exists on the remote branch, or when a merge conflict has been reported with the conflicting paths and required decision.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789323879685}}
