{"type":"message","id":"48a9ac44","parentId":"14514f28","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:25:56.662Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zZa1ty5qETNF1oZRUmGp6O52|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eab42dc087d08591a2cf6a5fe728","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: rp-build\ndescription: Plan and implement substantial changes with RepoPrompt Context Builder. Use for unfamiliar repositories or changes spanning several files.\ncompatibility: Requires RepoPrompt MCP and Pi file tools.\n---\n\n# RepoPrompt Build\n\nUse the user's request as the task.\n\nStart with Git status. Locate the repository root before asking RepoPrompt to inspect anything.\n\nCall `repoprompt_context_builder` with a precise task description and `response_type: \"plan\"`. Review its plan and assumptions before changing files. Call `repoprompt_workspace_context` when you need the complete selected context. Ask the user only when an unresolved choice would materially change behavior or scope.\n\nImplement through Pi `edit` and `write`. The OrbStack repository mount is read-only, so never use RepoPrompt `apply_edits` or `file_actions`. Follow repository test-first rules for behavior changes. Run focused tests after each change, then run broader relevant checks.\n\nDo not improvise.\n\nUse `repoprompt_oracle_send` only for a specific question left open by Context Builder. Continue with the returned `chat_id` rather than starting an unrelated conversation.\n\nFor substantial changes, run RepoPrompt review against the final Git diff. Report changed files and commands run. Include validation results and remaining risks. Do not claim completion while required checks fail.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789323956662}}
{"type":"message","id":"6f692674","parentId":"48a9ac44","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:26:07.862Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning Context Builder wiring**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eab7321087d088907636d3fd816e\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning Context Builder wiring**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_HvLEQ3rNFHzt2hM0cYWoW4s7|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eab7e51087d0a600129f660469d1","name":"repoprompt_context_builder","arguments":{"response_type":"plan","instructions":"<task>Implement the next Phase 6 milestone: production composition for authenticated replica.lifecycle requests. Wire BrokerControlService into the production broker daemon using BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator, BrokerArtifactStore, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore, and accepted BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects for ingest/verify/publish. Preserve executor.launch behavior exactly and keep lifecycle and all effect gates independently disabled by default. Add explicit fail-closed typed effects for unfinished admission, drain, export, reclaim stages without fabricating support. Add focused production wiring/startup tests. Do not implement the later Linux admission/drain/export/reclaim effects yet.</task><context>The current committed milestones include control dispatch, journal/coordinator, authenticated upload, descriptor publication, and artifact effects. The checkout is heavily dirty with other Phase 6 work, so discover current actual files and avoid unrelated changes. Key likely files include backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py, services/execution_broker.py, services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py, services/broker_replica_journal.py, services/broker_replica_artifact_effects.py, config.py, and tests/test_execution_daemons.py or control tests. Root protocol and BrokerService.handle must remain unchanged. Lifecycle disabled response must precede lifecycle-specific authority parsing. No SQLite handle may cross await/effects. Broker socket stays /run/yinshi/broker.sock; artifact socket remains separate. Journal identity binds exact request/response keys and limits. Production may need fail-closed config validation and filesystem paths. Determine exact APIs from repository; do not invent them. RepoPrompt mount can be stale, so flag discrepancies.</context>"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":493,"output":363,"cacheRead":81792,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":10,"totalTokens":82648,"cost":{"input":0.002465,"output":0.01089,"cacheRead":0.040895999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.054250999999999994}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789323956667,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eab526f087d097098ad5c0fc3a38","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
