{"type":"message","id":"36f48017","parentId":"b605db85","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:28:50.929Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_o6uEsSBkhUaJe2LoVO1auz6T|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eb61cc9087d0b7c452f85aa51ebe","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Executable agents:\n- delegate (builtin): Lightweight subagent that inherits the parent model with no default reads\n- final-review (user, aliases: production-final-review): Sol Max independent design and correctness review with a remediation plan.\n- oracle (builtin, context: fork, aliases: advisor): High-context decision-consistency oracle that protects inherited state and prevents drift\n- planner (user): Read-only Sol planning for parent-approved implementation tasks.\n- qwen-implementer (user): Local Qwen implementation worker for approved file-scoped task packets\n- researcher (builtin): Autonomous web researcher — searches, evaluates, and synthesizes a focused research brief\n- reviewer (user): Read-only local Qwen reviewer for optional mechanical pre-review.\n- scout (user): Fast read-only repository reconnaissance using local Qwen.\n- test-writer (user): Local Qwen test writer for explicit behavior through an existing test interface.\n- worker (user): Default GLM High implementation worker for settled behavior and architecture.\n- worker-advanced (user): GLM Max worker for approved invariants across interacting states and failure paths.\n- worker-expert (user): Sol xhigh diagnosis and expert implementation for uncertain causes or novel algorithms.\n- worker-simple (user): Local Qwen implementation for fully specified mechanical changes.\n\nChains:\n- (none)"}],"details":{"mode":"management","results":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789324130929}}
{"type":"message","id":"48f39c9c","parentId":"36f48017","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:29:14.631Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Defining route record and file invariants**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eb665d7c87d0aca3ae864b7b5637\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Defining route record and file invariants**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0fkgjKKRhI0o5nNnJJo8LBaB|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eb6886fc87d0a646e5502e9a4ec3","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"return runs.run('replica-production-composition', {agent:'worker-advanced', task:'Implement the approved production composition milestone in /Users/user/projects/yinshi. Route: worker-advanced because this combines named gating, startup-recovery, authentication, and stage-transition guarantees; architecture is settled. Work directly in the shared checkout; do not commit. Scope primarily backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py, a focused new service module if useful, and backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py or a new focused test file. Do not alter BrokerService.handle or broker artifact upload transport.\\n\\nRequired behavior:\\n1. Production broker builds BrokerControlService around the existing unchanged BrokerService. Load application and broker keys once and share exact key objects/public keys as appropriate.\\n2. Always instantiate BrokerReplicaJournal at fixed /var/lib/yinshi/control/broker-replica-journal.sqlite3, expected limits digest from DEFAULT_REPLICA_STORE_LIMITS, request key, and current broker response public key. Instantiate BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator with current private-key map and all seven effects. Incoming root fixed /var/lib/yinshi/artifact-incoming; publication root fixed /var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging; expected UID/GID are broker process IDs. Artifact effects are the accepted BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects using broker_artifact_limits_for_replica and matching publication limits.\\n3. Add one explicit lifecycle startup flag plus env gate and independent explicit flag+env gates for each of seven stages. Every gate defaults false. CLI no flags remains entirely disabled. A stage gate must delegate apply/reconcile only when enabled. Disabled apply deterministically raises StageRejected with the journal-valid status for that stage and a deterministic bounded receipt ID. Disabled reconcile must raise StageOutcomeUnknown with that stage’s allowed unknown reason because a durable start may predate process restart. Unfinished admission/drain/export/reclaim use fail-closed effects even if their stage gate is enabled: apply rejects with journal-valid stage rejection, reconcile returns stage-specific unknown. Do not fabricate support.\\n4. BrokerControlService lifecycle_enabled comes only from lifecycle flag+env. Disabled lifecycle must still return its signed disabled response before authority parsing. Existing executor.launch passes unchanged.\\n5. Startup ordering: inspect legacy v1, build composition, recover legacy launch service synchronously, await replica coordinator recover_incomplete serially, then adopt/serve the socket. No SQLite handle crosses await (journal APIs already enforce it). Journal/persistence errors escape startup.\\n6. Generalize broker_connection_handler/_exchange typing only enough to accept BrokerControlService while preserving behavior and application_uid contract.\\n7. Tests first where practical. Cover every gate default false and explicit+env conjunction, config-invalid env values, exact production paths/limits/key binding, seven-effect construction, disabled apply/reconcile semantics, unfinished stage fail-closed even when enabled, recovery before socket serving, control dispatch production type, and unchanged executor.launch behavior. Preserve existing tests.\\n\\nPermitted transitions: disabled lifecycle returns signed disabled without journal effects; enabled lifecycle reaches only enabled stage adapters; disabled apply rejects; disabled reconcile unknown; unfinished enabled stages still fail closed. Failure outcomes must use exact journal status/reason vocabularies.\\n\\nChecks: focused pytest for new/execution daemon/control/lifecycle tests, Ruff lint+format check, strict mypy on changed source, py_compile, git diff --check. Escalate rather than inventing APIs or changing root/artifact protocols.', cwd:'/Users/user/projects/yinshi', acceptance:{level:'checked', evidence:['changed-files','tests-added','commands-run','validation-output','residual-risks']}})","async":false,"timeoutMs":1800000,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","chatProgress":"auto"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1463,"output":845,"cacheRead":110336,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":52,"totalTokens":112644,"cost":{"input":0.007315,"output":0.02535,"cacheRead":0.055167999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.087833}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789324130935,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6eb63785087d09440e2544e588c74","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
