aZXiyVhngA|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6f298cd6887d0972371357dbb9e93","results":[{"index":0,"agent":"worker-advanced","task":"Implement production broker replica composition in /Users/user/projects/yinshi, no commit. This is a bounded source+focused test task. Architecture is settled; do not inspect unrelated dirty files. Read only execution_daemons.py, execution_broker.py control class, broker_replica_journal.py constructor/status vocab, broker_replica_lifecycle.py effects/coordinator APIs, broker_replica_artifact_effects.py, broker_artifact_store.py, workspace_replica_publication.py, root_launcher.py layout, artifact_upload_daemon.py fixed root, and tests/test_execution_daemons.py.\n\nAdd to execution_daemons.py (or one small new helper module if needed): fixed replica journal path /var/lib/yinshi/control/broker-replica-journal.sqlite3, incoming root /var/lib/yinshi/artifact-incoming, publication root /var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging. Add lifecycle env+CLI gate and seven independent stage env+CLI gates, all conjunction explicit && env true and default false. Build BrokerService unchanged plus BrokerControlService, BrokerReplicaJournal bound to DEFAULT_REPLICA_STORE_LIMITS digest and exact keys, BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator with BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects for first three and fail-closed effects for last four. Gate wrapper: disabled apply StageRejected using stage-valid status and deterministic receipt ID; disabled reconcile StageOutcomeUnknown using valid stage-specific reason. Unfinished admission/drain/export/reclaim remain fail closed even if stage gate true: apply rejected, reconcile unknown. Enabled first three delegate. Build all components even lifecycle disabled. Share loaded keys. Return a composition object so _run_broker can call launch_service.recover_startup(), await coordinator.recover_incomplete(), then serve BrokerControlService. Generalize handler typing via protocol application_uid+handle. Preserve disabled lifecycle response-before-authority and exact executor.launch behavior. No SQLite handles across await.\n\nAdd focused tests, preferably new backend/tests/test_broker_production_composition.py to minimize conflicts: default/env conjunction for lifecycle and all seven stage gates; malformed env config; fixed roots/journal/limits/key binding through monkeypatch or inspectable composition fields; disabled apply/reconcile and unfinished enabled failclosed; recovery occurs before _run_daemon; production top-level service is BrokerControlService. Existing tests must pass. Run focused pytest, Ruff check/format-check, strict mypy changed source, py_compile, diff check. If TDD Guard blocks edits, return exact parent-applicable edit packet. Do not modify any other files.","routingContract":{"version":1,"agent":"worker-advanced","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","thinking":"max","policyDigest":"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5"},"launchContractDigest":"68ba0bdb935cd87775c11492dfa777a9a5313bf4176af8d99aa8a680639d35c7","launchResolvedExtensions":{"version":1,"source":"launch-resolved","disableAmbientExtensions":true,"runtime":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4"],"configured":["sha256:890420901a90541d"],"effective":["sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4","sha256:890420901a90541d"],"omitted":{"runtime":0,"configured":0,"effective":0}},"exitCode":1,"outputState":"present","usage":{"input":94795,"output":39341,"cacheRead":1653760,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":39},"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max","thinking":"max","artifactPaths":{"inputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/4b2c2bb0_worker-advanced_0_input.md","outputPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/4b2c2bb0_worker-advanced_0_output.md","jsonlPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/4b2c2bb0_worker-advanced_0.jsonl","transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/4b2c2bb0_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl","metadataPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/4b2c2bb0_worker-advanced_0_meta.json"},"transcriptPath":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/4b2c2bb0_worker-advanced_0_transcript.jsonl","turnBudget":{"maxTurns":24,"graceTurns":4,"turnCount":39,"outcome":"wrap-up-requested","wrapUpRequestedAtTurn":24},"toolBudget":{"hard":70,"soft":45,"block":["read","grep","find","ls"],"toolCount":48,"outcome":"soft-reached","softReachedAt":45},"context":"fresh","wrapUpRequested":true,"progressSummary":{"toolCount":48,"tokens":134136,"durationMs":1087585},"effects":{"fileMutation":{"status":"observed","expected":true,"attempted":true}},"outputMode":"inline","finalOutput":"Turn budget wrap-up was requested after 24 assistant turns (soft limit 24, grace 4). Process-mode live steering is unavailable, so the child was warned at launch to wrap up by this budget. Output may be partial.\n\nBoth probes confirm the blocker: **TDD Guard rejects all file writes/edits in this session branch** (\"TDD Guard has no current request bound to this session branch\"), and I have no `tdd_*` tools to establish a request. Shell writes are also prohibited. Per my instructions, I'm returning the exact parent-applicable edit packet instead of forcing changes.\n\n## State\n\n- **No files were changed; nothing staged.** `execution_daemons.py` and all tests are untouched (guard blocked both the test-file `write` and a source `edit` probe).\n- Baseline verified before any change: `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_execution_daemons.py -q` → **42 passed**.\n- Full design was mapped from the required files; packets below are apply-ready.\n\n## ⚠ Parent decision required (seam conflict)\n\nPacket B makes `_run_broker` build the composition at fixed `/var/lib/...` roots and call `_build_broker(config, application_public_key=…, broker_private_key=…)`. Existing `test_broker_checks_v1_before_recovery_and_listener_acceptance` (tests/test_execution_daemons.py:880–903) monkeypatches `_build_broker` with a single-arg fake and runs `_run_broker()` for real → real `BrokerReplicaJournal` construction at `/var/lib/yinshi/control` **fails on this machine** (`/var/lib` is root-owned; verified). `test_broker_rejects_unsafe_v1_before_v2_construction` passes unchanged (inspect raises before any build). Minimal authorized fix: in that one test, patch `_build_broker_composition` instead, with a fake exposing `launch_service.recover_startup()` (records `\"recover\"`), `replica_coordinator.recover_incomplete()` (async, records nothing), `control_service` (has `application_uid`); keep the event assertion `[\"load\", \"inspect_v1\", \"build_v2\", \"recover\", \"listen\"]` and patch `_build_broker` with `def build(_config, **_k)` recording `\"build_v2\"`.\n\n## Packet A — new file `backend/tests/test_broker_production_composition.py`\n\nApply the content I wrote via `write` above, with these corrections (final form): in `_daemon_config`, drop the stray `BROKER_CONFIG_PATH_KEYS` monkeypatch and write key files as `REQUEST_KEY.public_key().public_bytes_raw()` for `application.pub` and fixed raw bytes `b\"\\x11\"*32` for `broker.key`; annotate `_composition(...) -> execution_daemons.BrokerProductionComposition`; make `test_all_components_build_and_fail_closed_when_lifecycle_disabled` an `async def` ending with `with pytest.raises(StageRejected): await composition.stage_effects[\"ingest\"].apply(context)` and `with pytest.raises(StageOutcomeUnknown): await composition.stage_effects[\"reclaim\"].reconcile(context)`; in the disabled-lifecycle test assert `parsed.error == \"replica_lifecycle_disabled\"` (verify with `Ed25519PrivateKey.from_private_bytes(b\"\\x11\"*32).public_key()`); in the order test replace the last assertion with `assert len(handlers) == 1` (top-level-type proof lives in the fixed-roots test: `isinstance(composition.control_service, BrokerControlService)`). Remove unused imports (`cast`).\n\n## Packet B — edits to `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py`\n\n1. Imports: add `hashlib`; `Mapping` to collections.abc; `asdict` to dataclasses; `Generic, TypeVar` to typing. Add imports: `BrokerArtifactStore`; `canonical_json` (broker_protocol); `BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects, broker_artifact_limits_for_replica` (broker_replica_artifact_effects); `AdmissionReceipt, BrokerReplicaJournal, DrainReceipt, ExportReceipt, IngestReceipt, PublishReceipt, ReclaimReceipt, VerifyReceipt` (broker_replica_journal); `REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_STAGES, BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator, ReplicaLifecycleContext, ReplicaLifecycleEffects, ReplicaStageEffect, StageOutcomeUnknown, StageReconciliation, StageRejected` (broker_replica_lifecycle); `BrokerControlService` (execution_broker); `compute_replica_limits_sha256` (replica_artifact_contract); `DEFAULT_REPLICA_STORE_LIMITS, WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` (workspace_replica_publication).\n2. Constants: `BROKER_REPLICA_JOURNAL_PATH = Path(\"/var/lib/yinshi/control/broker-replica-journal.sqlite3\")`, `BROKER_ARTIFACT_INCOMING_ROOT = Path(\"/var/lib/yinshi/artifact-incoming\")`, `BROKER_PUBLICATION_STAGING_ROOT = Path(\"/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging\")`, `REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED_ENVIRONMENT = \"YINSHI_REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED\"`, `REPLICA_STAGE_ENABLED_ENVIRONMENTS` mapping the seven stages to `YINSHI_REPLICA_<STAGE>_ENABLED`.\n3. Protocol (generalized handler typing) + resolvers after `resolve_reclaim_gate`:\n```python\nclass BrokerFrameService(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"Authenticate and serve one broker frame for its authorized application peer.\"\"\"\n    @property\n    def application_uid(self) -> int: ...\n    async def handle(self, frame: bytes, *, peer_uid: int) -> bytes: ...\n\ndef resolve_replica_lifecycle_gate(*, explicit: bool) -> bool:\n    return resolve_boolean_gate(REPLICA_LIFECYCLE_ENABLED_ENVIRONMENT, explicit=explicit)\n\ndef resolve_replica_stage_gate(stage: str, *, explicit: bool) -> bool:\n    environment = REPLICA_STAGE_ENABLED_ENVIRONMENTS.get(stage)\n    if environment is None:\n        raise DaemonError(\"config_invalid\")\n    return resolve_boolean_gate(environment, explicit=explicit)\n```\n4. Replace `service: BrokerService` with `service: BrokerFrameService` in `_exchange_broker` and `broker_connection_handler` (BrokerService/BrokerControlService conform structurally).\n5. Vocabulary + deterministic receipt + effects + composition (insert before `_build_broker`): `_STAGE_REJECTION_STATUSES` (`ingest`→`artifact_rejected`, `verify`→`verification_rejected`, `publish`→`publication_rejected`, `admission`→`admission_rejected`, `drain`→`drain_rejected`, `export`→`export_rejected`, `reclaim`→`reclaim_rejected`); `_STAGE_UNRESOLVED_REASONS` (`transfer_unknown`, `verification_unknown`, `publication_unknown`, `admission_unknown`, `acknowledgment_unknown`, `transfer_unknown`, `effect_unknown`); `_gate_rejected_receipt_id(stage, operation_id, status) = \"rejected_\" + sha256(b\"yinshi-replica-stage-gate-rejection-v1\\x00\" + canonical_json({\"code\":…, \"operation_id\":…, \"stage\":…})).hexdigest()` (73-char token, deterministic). Generic `_GatedStageEffect[_ReplicaReceiptT](stage, delegate, *, enabled)`: disabled `apply` → `StageRejected(status, gate receipt)`, disabled `reconcile` → `StageOutcomeUnknown(reason)`, enabled delegates both; generic `_FailClosedStageEffect[_ReplicaReceiptT](stage)`: `apply` always StageRejected (gate receipt), `reconcile` always StageOutcomeUnknown. Frozen-slots `BrokerProductionComposition` with inspectable fields: `launch_service, control_service, replica_coordinator, replica_journal, artifact_effects, incoming_store, publication_store, limits_sha256, replica_lifecycle_enabled, stage_gates_enabled: Mapping[str, bool], stage_effects: Mapping[str, ReplicaStageEffect[object]]`.\n6. `_build_broker(config, *, application_public_key=None, broker_private_key=None)` loads each key only when `None` (seam-compatible when called plainly).\n7. `_build_broker_composition(config, *, replica_lifecycle_explicit=False, stage_explicit: Mapping[str, bool] | None = None)`: resolve lifecycle + seven stage gates first (malformed env → `DaemonError(\"config_invalid\")` before disk writes); load both keys once and share; `limits = DEFAULT_REPLICA_STORE_LIMITS`, `limits_sha256 = compute_replica_limits_sha256(asdict(limits))`; build `BrokerReplicaJournal(BROKER_REPLICA_JOURNAL_PATH, application_id=BROKER_APPLICATION_ID, expected_limits_sha256=limits_sha256, request_public_key=<application key>, response_public_keys={config.broker_incarnation: <broker key>.public_key()})`; `BrokerArtifactStore(BROKER_ARTIFACT_INCOMING_ROOT, limits=broker_artifact_limits_for_replica(limits), expected_uid=os.geteuid(), expected_gid=os.getegid())`; `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore(BROKER_PUBLICATION_STAGING_ROOT, ceilings=limits, expected_uid=os.geteuid(), expected_gid=os.getegid())`; `BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects(incoming=…, publication=…, limits=limits)`; wrap first three in `_GatedStageEffect`, last four in `_FailClosedStageEffect`; `BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator(journal, broker_incarnation=…, broker_private_keys={incarnation: key}, effects=ReplicaLifecycleEffects(…))` with `cast`-annotated fields; `BrokerControlService(…, launch_service=<built via shared keys>, replica_coordinator=coordinator, replica_lifecycle_enabled=…)`; return composition. All components are built even when disabled; the journal opens/closes SQLite per call (no handles across `await` anywhere in this code).\n8. `_run_broker(*, replica_lifecycle_explicit=False, stage_explicit=None)`: `load_broker_config()` → `inspect_legacy_v1_journal(LEGACY_BROKER_JOURNAL_PATH, application_id=BROKER_APPLICATION_ID)` → `_build_broker_composition(…)` → `composition.launch_service.recover_startup()` → `await composition.replica_coordinator.recover_incomplete()` → `_run_daemon(broker_connection_handler(service=composition.control_service, expected_peer_uid=config.application_uid))`.\n9. `broker_main`: add `--replica-lifecycle-enabled` plus seven `--replica-<stage>-enabled` `store_true` flags, forwarded as `replica_lifecycle_explicit` / `stage_explicit`.","controlEvents":[{"type":"active_long_running","to":"active_long_running","ts":1789326230601,"runId":"4b2c2bb0","agent":"worker-advanced","index":0,"message":"worker-advanced is still active but long-running","reason":"time_threshold","turns":23,"tokens":58525,"toolCount":30,"elapsedMs":240080}],"attemptedModels":["z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max"],"modelAttempts":[{"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:max","success":true,"exitCode":0,"usage":{"input":94795,"output":39341,"cacheRead":1653760,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"turns":39}}],"sessionFile":"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/4b2c2bb0/run-0/session.jsonl","acceptance":{"status":"rejected","evidenceStatus":"rejected","explicit":true,"effectiveAcceptance":{"level":"checked","explicit":true,"inferredReason":["write-capable worker/task"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Implement the requested change without widening scope","evidence":["changed-files","tests-added","commands-run","residual-risks","no-staged-files","validation-output"],"severity":"required"}],"evidence":["changed-files","tests-added","commands-run","residual-risks","no-staged-files","validation-output"],"verify":[],"stopRules":[]},"inferredReason":["write-capable worker/task"],"criteria":[{"id":"criterion-1","must":"Implement the requested change without widening scope","evidence":["changed-files","tests-added","commands-run","residual-risks","no-staged-files","validation-output"],"severity":"required"}],"runtimeChecks":[{"id":"criterion:criterion-1","status":"failed","message":"Required criterion 'criterion-1' was reported as not-satisfied."},{"id":"evidence:changed-files","status":"not-applicable","message":"changed-files evidence explicitly reported as not applicable."},{"id":"evidence:tests-added","status":"not-applicable","message":"tests-added evidence explicitly reported as not applicable."},{"id":"evidence:commands-run","status":"passed",