{"type":"message","id":"872af395","parentId":"7eeff6f9","timestamp":"2026-09-13T19:26:24.390Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_RwSkIx3cYMepLSmELSXpnTaD|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6f8df92f887d09a97dd7643dde71a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: software-design\ndescription: Applies principles from \"A Philosophy of Software Design\" to architecture, module and API boundaries, and consequential refactors. Use for architecture planning, module or API design, design review, or diagnosing shallow modules, information leakage, and pass-through layers.\n---\n\n# Software Design\n\nApply these principles when architecture or abstraction quality is a material part of the task.\n\n## Two Modes\n\n### Writing New Code\n\nApply these principles in order of impact.\n\n#### Think strategically\n\nInvest in design instead of stopping when the code first works. Produce a clean design that works, and spend 10–20% of the effort on design improvements.\n\n#### Create deep modules\n\nEach module should provide powerful functionality behind a simple interface. A few deep methods beat many shallow ones. Ask whether the interface is simpler than the implementation.\n\n#### Hide information\n\nEach module should encapsulate design decisions that remain invisible through its interface. If one decision appears in several modules, reorganize the code until that decision has one home.\n\n#### Make interfaces general-purpose\n\nDesign an interface broad enough to support current uses while keeping its functionality focused. Ask for the simplest interface that covers every current need.\n\n#### Give each layer a different abstraction\n\nAdjacent layers should operate at different abstraction levels. Remove pass-through methods that delegate with the same signature.\n\n#### Pull complexity downwards\n\nHandle complexity inside the module instead of pushing it to callers. A simple interface matters more than a simple implementation.\n\n#### Define errors out of existence\n\nRedefine APIs so avoidable error conditions cannot arise. Mask low-level exceptions and consolidate their handling. Reserve crashes for unrecoverable failures.\n\n#### Design it twice\n\nConsider at least two radically different approaches before committing. Compare their strengths and costs. Apply this comparison to interfaces and implementations, then consider the broader system decomposition.\n\n#### Name precisely\n\nNames should create a clear mental image of an entity's purpose. Avoid vague choices such as `data`, `result`, `info`, or `tmp`. Name booleans with predicates such as `isConnected` instead of a state label such as `status`.\n\n#### Be consistent\n\nUse the same name for the same purpose everywhere. Reuse established coding patterns and conventions. Consistency reduces the reader's cognitive work.\n\n#### Make code obvious\n\nCode is obvious when a reader's first guess about its behaviour is correct. Choose precise names and follow established patterns. Use whitespace to expose structure, and comment only where the code cannot explain itself.\n\n#### Write comments first\n\nWrite interface comments before implementation. A method that needs a long descriptive comment has a complex interface and should be redesigned. Comments should preserve information that code cannot represent.\n\n### Reviewing Existing Code\n\nScan for these red flags in the listed order.\n\n#### Shallow modules\n\nLook for interfaces as complex as their implementations, many trivial methods, or classes with little functionality.\n\n#### Information leakage\n\nFind design decisions repeated across modules. A change to one detail should not require coordinated edits across several classes.\n\n#### Temporal decomposition\n\nCheck for code organized around operation order instead of information hiding, such as separate read and write classes for one format.\n\n#### Pass-through methods\n\nFlag methods that only call another method with the same signature, especially when delegation accounts for half or more of a class's methods.\n\n#### Overexposure\n\nA common operation should not force callers to understand rare features. Default information that callers should not have to provide.\n\n#### Conjoined methods\n\nFlag a method when understanding it requires reading another method's implementation.\n\n#### Repetition\n\nFind non-trivial code patterns duplicated in several places.\n\n#### Vague or hard-to-pick names\n\nFlag names broad enough to describe many entities. Difficulty finding a precise name often means the entity has too many responsibilities.\n\n#### Comment problems\n\nFind comments that restate the code or expose implementation details in interface documentation. Long, complicated descriptions may reveal a poor abstraction.\n\n#### Special-general mixture\n\nKeep specialized use-case code out of a general-purpose mechanism.\n\n#### Nonobvious code\n\nFlag behaviour that a quick reading cannot reveal, including surprising side effects.\n\n#### Too many exceptions\n\nLook for exceptions the caller cannot handle and error paths longer than the normal path. Redefine operations when doing so can eliminate error conditions.\n\nFor the full checklist, read `references/red-flags.md`.\n\n## References\n\n`references/principles.md` covers all 15 design principles. It includes examples and techniques, along with the reasoning behind each principle. Read it when applying a specific principle or when deeper context is needed.\n\n`references/red-flags.md` organizes every red flag by category. Read it during code review to check systematically for design problems.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789327584390}}
{"type":"message","id":"1f032643","parentId":"872af395","timestamp":"2026-09-13T19:26:43.408Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Preparing fresh final review**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6f8e3d14087d0b83a6b5ac0771532\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Preparing fresh final review**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_K6zRYBQMgnCQ0PomizUstTkk|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6f8e540d887d0850a55bb2d24a774","name":"subagent","arguments":{"workflowScript":"return runs.run('production-composition-review', {agent:'final-review', task:'Independent read-only final review of the current production-composition diff in /Users/user/projects/yinshi. Do not modify, stage, or commit. Original Phase 6 request: wire authenticated replica.lifecycle into the production broker daemon using the accepted journal/coordinator/artifact effects, keep executor.launch unchanged, preserve disabled-before-authority behavior, make lifecycle and seven stage gates independently default-disabled, and keep unfinished admission/drain/export/reclaim fail closed.\\n\\nApproved design: BrokerControlService owns authenticated request-type dispatch; BrokerService remains unchanged. Production builds BrokerReplicaJournal at fixed /var/lib/yinshi/control/broker-replica-journal.sqlite3, incoming store at /var/lib/yinshi/artifact-incoming, publication at /var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging. Journal binds request key/current response key and exact DEFAULT_REPLICA_STORE_LIMITS digest. Artifact effects handle ingest/verify/publish. Each stage has explicit CLI + separate YINSHI_REPLICA_STAGE_<STAGE>_ENABLED env conjunction. Lifecycle has its own conjunction. Disabled apply is deterministic stage-valid rejection; disabled reconcile is stage-valid unknown. Unfinished later effects reject apply and return unknown reconciliation even if their stage flag is true. Startup order: legacy-v1 inspection, composition, synchronous launch recovery, awaited serial replica recovery, socket service. No SQLite handle may cross await. Persistence errors escape.\\n\\nCritical invariants: lifecycle disabled response occurs before lifecycle authority parsing; same raw signed frame reaches coordinator when enabled; executor.launch behavior unchanged; roots/keys/limits are fixed and broker-owned; authority cannot choose paths/resources; all seven effects present; no support is fabricated; default systemd startup has no enabling flags and therefore remains disabled. Stage gate env names must be independent from root launcher prepare/reclaim and upload gates.\\n\\nActual changed files for this milestone: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py and backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py. Relevant callers: broker_main/_run_broker/broker_connection_handler, BrokerControlService, BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator, BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects, artifact upload daemon and root launcher constants. Current checks: 223 focused journal/lifecycle/control/daemon/artifact/publication tests passed; scoped Ruff lint+format, strict mypy, py_compile, diff check passed.\\n\\nApply the loaded /skill:software-design content: prioritize deep modules, information hiding, distinct abstraction levels, complexity pulled down, precise names, consistent obvious behavior; review shallow modules, information leakage, temporal decomposition, pass-throughs, overexposure, conjoined methods, repetition, vague names, special-general mixture, nonobvious behavior, and excessive exception paths.\\n\\nRead the actual diff and relevant callers. Return findings ordered by severity. Every finding must include location/affected requirement, impact, proposed correction, and validation. If no findings remain, explicitly say no remediation is needed. Include residual risks.', cwd:'/Users/user/projects/yinshi'})","async":false,"timeoutMs":1800000,"cwd":"/Users/user/projects/yinshi","chatProgress":"auto"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1164,"output":721,"cacheRead":118016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":49,"totalTokens":119901,"cost":{"input":0.0058200000000000005,"output":0.02163,"cacheRead":0.059008,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.08645800000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789327584396,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6f8e0efd087d09abb22d8bec422df","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"3eb4bab7","parentId":"1f032643","timestamp":"2026-09-13T19:47:19.363Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_K6zRYBQMgnCQ0PomizUstTkk|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa6f8e540d887d0850a55bb2d24a774","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workflow completed.\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"key\": \"production-composition-review\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"runId\": \"94419067\",\n  \"output\": \"## Review result\\n\\nBlocked. One high-severity finding remains. Remediation is required.\\n\\n## Finding\\n\\n### High: Aggregate lifecycle deadline can preempt valid stages\\n\\n**Location**\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:98-102`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:832-841`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:1180-1186`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:404-415`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:442-501`\\n- Missing coverage: `backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py:1162-1172`\\n\\n**Affected requirement**\\n\\nProduction lifecycle correctness, bounded failure handling, and unchanged `executor.launch` behavior.\\n\\n**Impact**\\n\\nThree concrete stages run serially before fail-closed admission. Each receives 40 seconds, while the whole connection receives only 120 seconds.\\n\\n`3 * 40 == 120`. No budget remains for frame reading, ownership, journal commits, or response draining.\\n\\nOuter timeout cancels coordinator. Coordinator persists terminal `cancellation_unknown`, then rethrows. Caller receives no initial response. Retries only replay unresolved authority.\\n\\nScaled coordinator probe reproduced this outcome. Two individually in-budget effects started before outer cancellation persisted:\\n\\n```text\\n{'code': 'cancellation_unknown', 'stage': 'verify', 'state': 'unresolved'}\\n```\\n\\n**Proposed correction**\\n\\nMove total request deadlines behind authenticated dispatch. Keep existing launch deadlines unchanged.\\n\\nGive lifecycle a separate aggregate deadline above all serial stage limits, ownership wait, persistence, and response delivery. Keep a larger transport safety ceiling.\\n\\n**Remediation plan**\\n\\nUse `worker-advanced`. Timeout, cancellation, persistence, and dispatch guarantees interact.\\n\\n**Required checks**\\n\\n- Assert lifecycle aggregate budget is strictly nested below its transport ceiling.\\n- Run a scaled three-stage coordinator test.\\n- Require a signed response instead of connection loss.\\n- Confirm no `cancellation_unknown` occurs for in-budget stages.\\n- Confirm `executor.launch` responses and deadlines remain unchanged.\\n- Repeat focused pytest, Ruff, strict mypy, and `py_compile`.\\n\\nNo other confirmed defects. No unanswered questions.\\n\\n## Residual risks\\n\\n- Live Linux systemd activation and fixed-root ownership were not executed.\\n- Fixed root strings remain duplicated across daemon, launcher, upload, and tmpfiles modules.\\n- Both milestone files are untracked relative to `HEAD`. Review covered their full current contents.\\n- Unrelated dirty working-tree paths were outside scope.\",\n  \"artifactPaths\": [\n    \"/Users/user/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-user-projects-yinshi--/2026-09-04T04-44-52-550Z_01a06abb-dfc5-7c65-82bb-7c5f2081ee64/94419067/run-0/session.jsonl\"\n  ],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n      \"task\": \"Independent read-only final review of the current production-composition diff in /Users/user/projects/yinshi. Do not modify, stage, or commit. Original Phase 6 request: wire authenticated replica.lifecycle into the production broker daemon using the accepted journal/coordinator/artifact effects, keep executor.launch unchanged, preserve disabled-before-authority behavior, make lifecycle and seven stage gates independently default-disabled, and keep unfinished admission/drain/export/reclaim fail closed.\\n\\nApproved design: BrokerControlService owns authenticated request-type dispatch; BrokerService remains unchanged. Production builds BrokerReplicaJournal at fixed /var/lib/yinshi/control/broker-replica-journal.sqlite3, incoming store at /var/lib/yinshi/artifact-incoming, publication at /var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging. Journal binds request key/current response key and exact DEFAULT_REPLICA_STORE_LIMITS digest. Artifact effects handle ingest/verify/publish. Each stage has explicit CLI + separate YINSHI_REPLICA_STAGE_<STAGE>_ENABLED env conjunction. Lifecycle has its own conjunction. Disabled apply is deterministic stage-valid rejection; disabled reconcile is stage-valid unknown. Unfinished later effects reject apply and return unknown reconciliation even if their stage flag is true. Startup order: legacy-v1 inspection, composition, synchronous launch recovery, awaited serial replica recovery, socket service. No SQLite handle may cross await. Persistence errors escape.\\n\\nCritical invariants: lifecycle disabled response occurs before lifecycle authority parsing; same raw signed frame reaches coordinator when enabled; executor.launch behavior unchanged; roots/keys/limits are fixed and broker-owned; authority cannot choose paths/resources; all seven effects present; no support is fabricated; default systemd startup has no enabling flags and therefore remains disabled. Stage gate env names must be independent from root launcher prepare/reclaim and upload gates.\\n\\nActual changed files for this milestone: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py and backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py. Relevant callers: broker_main/_run_broker/broker_connection_handler, BrokerControlService, BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator, BrokerReplicaJournal, BrokerReplicaArtifactEffects, artifact upload daemon and root launcher constants. Current checks: 223 focused journal/lifecycle/control/daemon/artifact/publication tests passed; scoped Ruff lint+format, strict mypy, py_compile, diff check passed.\\n\\nApply the loaded /skill:software-design content: prioritize deep modules, information hiding, distinct abstraction levels, complexity pulled down, precise names, consistent obvious behavior; review shallow modules, information leakage, temporal decomposition, pass-throughs, overexposure, conjoined methods, repetition, vague names, special-general mixture, nonobvious behavior, and excessive exception paths.\\n\\nRead the actual diff and relevant callers. Return findings ordered by severity. Every finding must include location/affected requirement, impact, proposed correction, and validation. If no findings remain, explicitly say no remediation is needed. Include residual risks.\",\n      \"routingContract\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n        \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n        \"thinking\": \"max\",\n        \"policyDigest\": \"8590d2fc0420152aad3f867aba1c18a56b3632f2d90e01d30d3f04676cd46ac5\"\n      },\n      \"launchContractDigest\": \"e7dcc9b16b30e45347fd92078b25d6e2b52532a4c30892f3e2fcd4eb36504787\",\n      \"launchResolvedExtensions\": {\n        \"version\": 1,\n        \"source\": \"launch-resolved\",\n        \"disableAmbientExtensions\": false,\n        \"runtime\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"configured\": [],\n        \"effective\": [\n          \"sha256:cb00ccf63b7cf9f4\"\n        ],\n        \"omitted\": {\n          \"runtime\": 0,\n          \"configured\": 0,\n          \"effective\": 0\n        }\n      },\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"outputState\": \"present\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"input\": 661758,\n        \"output\": 39916,\n        \"cacheRead\": 8871680,\n        \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n        \"cost\": 8.942110000000001,\n        \"turns\": 88\n      },\n      \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol:max\",\n      \"thinking\": \"max\",\n      \"artifactPaths\": {\n        \"inputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/94419067_final-review_0_input.md\",\n        \"outputPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/94419067_final-review_0_output.md\",\n        \"jsonlPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/94419067_final-review_0.jsonl\",\n        \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/94419067_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n        \"metadataPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/94419067_final-review_0_meta.json\"\n      },\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"/Users/user/projects/yinshi/.pi-subagents/artifacts/94419067_final-review_0_transcript.jsonl\",\n      \"skills\": [\n        \"software-design\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"fresh\",\n      \"progressSummary\": {\n        \"toolCount\": 123,\n        \"tokens\": 701674,\n        \"durationMs\": 1235330\n      },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"fileMutation\": {\n          \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n          \"expected\": false,\n          \"attempted\": true\n        }\n      },\n      \"outputMode\": \"inline\",\n      \"finalOutput\": \"## Review result\\n\\nBlocked. One high-severity finding remains. Remediation is required.\\n\\n## Finding\\n\\n### High: Aggregate lifecycle deadline can preempt valid stages\\n\\n**Location**\\n\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:98-102`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:832-841`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:1180-1186`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:404-415`\\n- `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:442-501`\\n- Missing coverage: `backend/tests/test_execution_daemons.py:1162-1172`\\n\\n**Affected requirement**\\n\\nProduction lifecycle correctness, bounded failure handling, and unchanged `executor.launch` behavior.\\n\\n**Impact**\\n\\nThree concrete stages run serially before fail-closed admission. Each receives 40 seconds, while the whole connection receives only 120 seconds.\\n\\n`3 * 40 == 120`. No budget remains for frame reading, ownership, journal commits, or response draining.\\n\\nOuter timeout cancels coordinator. Coordinator persists terminal `cancellation_unknown`, then rethrows. Caller receives no initial response. Retries only replay unresolved authority.\\n\\nScaled coordinator probe reproduced this outcome. Two individually in-budget effects started before outer cancellation persisted:\\n\\n```text\\n{'code': 'cancellation_unknown', 'stage': 'verify', 'state': 'unresolved'}\\n```\\n\\n**Proposed correction**\\n\\nMove total request deadlines behind authenticated dispatch. Keep existing launch deadlines unchanged.\\n\\nGive lifecycle a separate aggregate deadline above all serial stage limits, ownership wait, persistence, and response delivery. Keep a larger transport safety ceiling.\\n\\n**Remediation plan**\\n\\nUse `worker-advanced`. Timeout, cancellation, persistence, and dispatch guarantees interact.\\n\\n**Required checks**\\n\\n- Assert lifecycle aggregate budget is strictly nested below its transport ceiling.\\n- Run a scaled three-stage coordinator test.\\n- Require a signed response instead of connection loss.\\n- Confirm no `cancellation_unknown` occurs for in-budget stages.\\n- Confirm `executor.launch` responses and deadlines remain unchanged.\\n- Repeat focused pytest, Ruff, strict mypy, and `py_compile`.\\n\\nNo other confirmed defects. No unanswered questions.\\n\\n## Residual risks\\n\\n- Live Linux systemd activation and fixed-root ownership were not executed.\\n- Fixed root strings remain duplicated across daemon, launcher, upload, and tmpfiles modules.\\n- Both milestone files are untracked relative to `HEAD`. Review covered their full current contents.\\n- Unrelated dirty working-tree paths were outside scope.\",\n      \"controlEvents\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"to\": \"active_long_running\",\n          \"ts\": 1789327844168,\n          \"runId\": \"94419067\",\n          \"agent\": \"final-review\",\n          \"index\": 0,\n          \"message\": \"final-