{"type":"message","id":"f4dfa3e2","parentId":"6ab10728","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:32.327Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Reviewing planner 1974/d856 content**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa7058cc11087d0992cd5482bf8839b\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Reviewing planner 1974/d856 content**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_522f3EjhvDpLcJE44OMoj9rh|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903b9487d0be96195f8e987454","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi-subagents/artifacts/1974bf1f_planner_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":300}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_h4SHntBSQzWsJ7K8aFznooC0|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903ba887d0914bbb48085daf70","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi-subagents/artifacts/9091a3f4_planner_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":300}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fWGqXwaEO7ufhdrWhLPmvCT0|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903bb087d0be6db3e40e0265ec","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi-subagents/artifacts/83af7a2c_oracle_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":260}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dfT4JSkgjcHiJf9vKQZ4dvde|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903bb887d095de52c1c381b2a9","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi-subagents/artifacts/274e0d6c_oracle_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":260}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":2721,"output":190,"cacheRead":136704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":13,"totalTokens":139615,"cost":{"input":0.013605,"output":0.0057,"cacheRead":0.068352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.087657}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789330826192,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa7058acd1887d086a7980b4ba8f139","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a9921823","parentId":"f4dfa3e2","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:32.331Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_522f3EjhvDpLcJE44OMoj9rh|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903b9487d0be96195f8e987454","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The response did not pass the STE check. Pi requested a new response."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789330832330}}
{"type":"message","id":"98116e2b","parentId":"a9921823","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:32.331Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_h4SHntBSQzWsJ7K8aFznooC0|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903ba887d0914bbb48085daf70","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# First Milestone Plan\n\n## Current Findings\n\n- **Blocker:** No broker persistence adapter exists for replica authority. `workspace_replica.py:1-7` remains pure and performs no I/O.\n- **High:** Launch journal v2 only supports `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`. Its exact schema and triggers prevent extension without version changes. See `broker_journal.py:22-42,44-228`.\n- **High:** `BrokerService` authorizes only `executor.launch`. It invokes only root `prepare` and `launch`. See `execution_broker.py:26,165-177,277-330`.\n- **High:** Root interface already limits actions to `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`. See `root_launcher.py:31`.\n- **Medium:** Pure replay expects ordered intent, preparation, synchronization, and completion facts with authenticated journal positions. See `workspace_replica.py:2553-2600,4300-4611`.\n- Existing tests establish append-before-effect, immutable schemas, exact replay, and restart refusal. See `test_broker_foundation.py:123-159,716-742,964-1003` and `test_broker_lifecycle_v2.py:101-206`.\n\n## Observable Result\n\nAdd standalone broker-owned replica journal foundation. It records authority and future `drain`, `export`, and `reclaim` stages without executing effects.\n\nDo not modify:\n\n- `broker_journal.py`\n- `execution_broker.py`\n- `broker_protocol.py`\n- `workspace_replica.py`\n- root launcher actions\n\n## Exact Data Model\n\nAdd `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py`:\n\n```python\nReplicaAuthority(\n    physical_target_id: str,\n    replica_generation: int,\n    execution_owner_id: str,\n)\n\nReplicaArtifactReference(\n    artifact_id: str,\n    sha256: str,\n    byte_length: int,\n)\n\nReplicaDrainEvidence(\n    acknowledgment_receipt_id: str,\n    quiescence_receipt_id: str,\n)\n\nReplicaExportEvidence(\n    export_receipt_id: str,\n    artifact: ReplicaArtifactReference,\n)\n\nReplicaReclaimEvidence(\n    reclaim_receipt_id: str,\n)\n\nReplicaJournalPosition(\n    journal_id: str,\n    sequence: int,\n    append_receipt_id: str,\n)\n\nReplicaJournalDecision(\n    state: str,\n    stage: str | None = None,\n    response_frame: bytes | None = None,\n    owner_broker_incarnation: str | None = None,\n)\n\nIncompleteReplicaLifecycle(\n    request_frame: bytes,\n    owner_token: str,\n    stage: str,\n    stage_started: bool,\n)\n```\n\nJournal owns `journal_id`, sequence, and append receipt IDs. Broker instance owns `owner_token`. External artifact storage owns artifact bytes.\n\n## Exact Tables and Events\n\nSchema version starts at `1`.\n\n`broker_replica_journal_meta`:\n\n- `singleton`\n- `application_id`\n- `schema_version`\n- `journal_id`\n\n`broker_replica_journal_events`:\n\n- `event_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`\n- `append_receipt_id`\n- request identity fields\n- `event_type`\n- `stage`\n- bounded request or response frame\n- `physical_target_id`, `replica_generation`, `execution_owner_id`\n- broker incarnation and owner token\n- drain evidence columns\n- export receipt and artifact metadata columns\n- reclaim receipt\n- unresolved reason\n- timestamp\n\nAllowed events:\n\n1. `accepted`\n2. `authority_claimed`\n3. `stage_started`\n4. `stage_outcome`\n5. `stage_unresolved`\n\nAllowed stages and successful statuses:\n\n- `drain` → `drained`\n- `export` → `exported`\n- `reclaim` → `reclaimed`\n\nAllowed unresolved reasons:\n\n- `missing_acknowledgment`\n- `runtime_live`\n- `broker_restart_unknown`\n- `sqlite_commit_unknown`\n- `verification_unknown`\n\nUse partial unique indexes for one acceptance, claim, stage start, stage outcome, and terminal event. Add immutable update and delete triggers.\n\nStore only `artifact_id`, SHA-256, and byte length. Never store artifact content.\n\n## Transitions\n\n1. `accepted → authority_claimed`.\n2. Claim permits only `drain` start.\n3. `drain` completes only with acknowledgment and quiescence receipt IDs.\n4. Missing acknowledgment records terminal unresolved at `drain`.\n5. Live runtime records terminal unresolved at `drain`.\n6. Successful drain permits `export`.\n7. Successful export permits `reclaim`.\n8. Successful reclaim is terminal.\n9. Any unresolved event is terminal.\n10. No event may follow a terminal event.\n\n## APIs\n\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` exposes:\n\n- `accept(request, request_frame, authority) -> ReplicaJournalDecision`\n- `claim_authority(request, owner_token, broker_incarnation) -> ReplicaJournalDecision`\n- `begin_stage(request, owner_token, stage) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n- `complete_drain(request, owner_token, evidence) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n- `complete_export(request, owner_token, evidence) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n- `complete_reclaim(request, owner_token, evidence, response_frame) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n- `record_unresolved(request, owner_token, stage, reason, response_frame) -> ReplicaJournalPosition`\n- `status(request) -> ReplicaJournalDecision`\n- `incomplete_lifecycles() -> tuple[IncompleteReplicaLifecycle, ...]`\n\nThis milestone does not expose new broker request types or call these APIs from `BrokerService`.\n\n## Recovery and Failure Rules\n\nReplay every row in sequence through one strict reducer. Reject unknown events, gaps, conflicting duplicates, future schemas, and invalid field combinations.\n\nAfter any commit exception, close the connection. Open a fresh connection and query every intended field plus append receipt. Exact presence means success. Absence raises `ReplicaJournalCommitAbsent`. Conflict raises `ReplicaJournalSyncError`.\n\nAccepted but unclaimed work remains accepted. Claimed nonterminal work reports the current or next stage as `broker_restart_unknown`. Startup integration remains later work.\n\nNo forced termination occurs. Missing acknowledgment or live runtime cannot advance to export or reclaim.\n\n## Tests and Order\n\n1. Add `backend/tests/test_broker_replica_journal.py`.\n2. Test exact schema, immutable rows, strict transition ordering, and one concurrent owner.\n3. Test exact duplicate replay and conflicting duplicate refusal.\n4. Inject pre-commit and post-commit faults. Assert fresh-connection verification.\n5. Test recovery at every event boundary and all three stages.\n6. Assert drain cannot complete without both receipts.\n7. Assert SQLite contains artifact metadata but not artifact bytes.\n8. Run existing broker and workspace replay suites unchanged.\n\nExisting coverage is insufficient because no replica journal exists.\n\n## Constraints and Residual Risks\n\n- Dirty repository state predates this plan. Writer must avoid unrelated files.\n- Artifact storage ownership, retention, and size ceiling need later approval.\n- Request type and authorization policy remain deferred.\n- Receipt authentication remains adapter responsibility.\n- Uncommitted index and worktree artifacts remain outside this milestone.\n- No migration applies. Rollback may remove an unused new database. Once events exist, archive it rather than mutate it.\n\n## Handoff\n\nParent must approve schema vocabulary, evidence fields, and internal-only scope. First action after approval: add failing schema and transition tests.\n\nNo listed source needs further inspection for this milestone. `execution_daemons.py` needs inspection before later service wiring.\n\nAssumption with highest impact: this journal remains unreachable from broker protocol during milestone one."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789330832331}}
{"type":"message","id":"616f76ac","parentId":"98116e2b","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:32.331Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_fWGqXwaEO7ufhdrWhLPmvCT0|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903bb087d0be6db3e40e0265ec","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited decisions:\n- Broker lifecycle v2 handles one `executor.launch` operation.\n- Launch stages remain fixed as `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`.\n- Legacy v1 remains read-only.\n- Application owns logical reservation, binding, and release.\n- Broker owns physical effects, synchronization, publication, and physical release.\n- Root protocol remains exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`.\n- Drain is graceful only. Missing acknowledgment or live runtime becomes unresolved.\n- Git bundles carry committed objects and refs.\n- Separate authenticated artifacts preserve working-tree and index state.\n- No SQLite handle crosses an await or external effect.\n\nDiagnosis:\n- Blocker: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_journal.py:22-42,44-80,645-760` fixes schema, stages, ordering, and terminal semantics. Replica stages cannot enter this journal compatibly.\n- Blocker: `backend/src/yinshi/services/execution_broker.py:26-47,165-177,387-409` accepts only `executor.launch`. Its lifecycle ends after launch.\n- Blocker: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_protocol.py:19-24,155-178` limits canonical JSON to 65,536 bytes. It cannot safely carry repository artifacts.\n- Blocker: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py:53-83` cannot express authenticated remote Linux admission. Every production profile remains unsupported.\n- High: `backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_replica.py:2552-2611,3841-3867,4103-4121` already defines an independent, two-owner reconciliation journal.\n- High: `backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py:35-175` only creates and retains listeners. It has no authenticated session processing or durable drain.\n- High: `backend/src/yinshi/db.py:765-772,831-841` stores mutable application execution state. Broker physical authority must not depend on these rows.\n- High: `backend/src/yinshi/root_launcher.py:20-35,1600-1650` permits reclaim only after unit and runtime absence. No component currently completes that graceful boundary.\n- Useful precedent: `runner_relay.py` and `runner_agent_relay.py` already provide bounded grants, replay control, encrypted sessions, and maintenance quiescence.\n\nDrift / contradiction check:\n- Making broker sole lifecycle authority would conflict with existing application ownership.\n- Extending launch v2 would quietly change its fixed terminal response contract.\n- Sending artifact bytes through signed broker JSON would persist source content in launch journal rows.\n- Marking Darwin globally supported would permit native execution. Remote admission must describe destination runtime, not local host.\n- Reusing mutable execution receipts as broker authority would weaken immutable replay.\n- Adding a root stop action would break approved root protocol.\n\nRecommendation:\nUse a separate broker-owned replica journal at a new fixed path and schema version.\n\nCreate `broker_replica_journal.py`. Keep `broker_journal.py` unchanged. Validate both journals before accepting traffic.\n\nReplica journal should persist:\n- Bound reconciliation specification and fingerprint.\n- Application request binding.\n- Broker action intent.\n- Authenticated journal positions.\n- Preparation identity.\n- Synchronization receipt.\n- Completion postimage.\n- Transfer attempt bounds and digests.\n- Stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n- Generation-bound admission fences.\n- Drain, export, and reclaim receipts.\n\nUse signed one-way handoffs between application journal and replica journal. Never require cross-database atomic commits.\n\nExecution handoff should work as follows:\n1. Replica journal commits a generation-bound admission fence.\n2. Application signs `executor.launch` with the broker admission receipt digest.\n3. `BrokerService` synchronously validates that receipt before launch acceptance.\n4. Launch journal proceeds through its existing three stages.\n5. Replica journal records the exact signed launch response.\n6. Pending or unresolved launch state blocks drain, replacement, and reclaim.\n\nUse a separate bounded stdio transport. Reuse current Noise session design where practical. Bind authentication to operation ID, generation, fingerprint, direction, limits, and broker incarnation.\n\nDo not journal artifact bytes. Stream them into broker-owned staging files. Journal exact byte counts, digests, object identities, and synchronization receipts.\n\nTransfer two artifacts in each required direction:\n- Bounded Git bundle for committed objects and refs.\n- Bounded authenticated workspace artifact for index plus working-tree state.\n\nWorkspace artifact must retain staged state, unstaged state, allowed ignored files, executable bits, and symlink text. Reject unsafe paths, unsupported kinds, hardlinks, overflow, or incomplete receipts.\n\nDrain remains graceful:\n1. Replica journal commits drain intent.\n2. Broker sends authenticated drain request through executor socket.\n3. Executor stops input and exits.\n4. Broker records authenticated acknowledgment.\n5. Broker confirms unit absence.\n6. Broker closes listener and removes runtime state.\n7. Export completes with receiver acknowledgment.\n8. Existing root `reclaim` runs.\n\nMissing acknowledgment, transport ambiguity, live unit, or incomplete export becomes stage-specific unresolved. Reclaim stays blocked.\n\nRejected alternatives:\n- Extend launch lifecycle v2: breaks fixed schema, stage order, and terminal replay.\n- Add replica tables to launch v2 database: exact schema validation rejects extra objects.\n- Use application tenant database alone: broker would trust mutable application state for physical authority.\n- Add root stop: conflicts with approved three-action root contract.\n\nRisks:\n- Cross-journal handoffs require durable admission fences and conservative recovery.\n- Remote isolation profile needs a pinned broker identity and qualified deployment profile.\n- Overlay format needs canonical encoding and strict bounds before implementation.\n- Current VM legacy accepted work still blocks production broker startup.\n- Graceful-only drain may leave operations unresolved until external administrative recovery.\n\nNeed from main agent:\n- No remaining decision. Supervisor selected graceful-only drain and separate working-state artifacts.\n\nSuggested execution prompt:\n```text\nImplement only Phase 6 replica-journal foundation.\n\nAdd a separate broker-owned append-only replica journal. Do not modify launch lifecycle v2 semantics. Persist bounded reconciliation bindings, action intents, journal positions, synchronization facts, completion facts, admission fences, and stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n\nOwners:\n- Application retains logical reservation and destination binding.\n- Broker owns physical effects and replica journal.\n- Root protocol remains prepare, launch, reclaim.\n\nPermitted transitions must match workspace_replica.py replay output. Every effect requires durable intent. Every completion binds exact fresh postimage. Commit ambiguity uses fresh-connection exact-event checks.\n\nAdd focused tests for exact replay, schema rejection, commit ambiguity, cross-journal admission fencing, restart recovery, and no SQLite handle across awaits. Do not add transport or runtime effects in this worker.\n```"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789330832331}}
{"type":"message","id":"2b63e127","parentId":"616f76ac","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:32.331Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dfT4JSkgjcHiJf9vKQZ4dvde|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705903bb887d095de52c1c381b2a9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"decision\": \"architecture-corrections-required\",\n  \"inheritedDecisions\": [\n    \"OS isolation, full runtime Git access, and Linux execution remain fixed.\",\n    \"Mac execution requires a Linux VM. Native Darwin execution fails closed.\",\n    \"Private writable replicas must not receive canonical storage authority.\",\n    \"Original execution acknowledgment, descendant drain, reconciliation, and physical release remain distinct.\",\n    \"Phase 6 retains immutable-result integration and clean-parent requirements. Phase 7 remains excluded.\",\n    \"No implementation, provisioning, tests, deployment, or commits are authorized by this critique.\"\n  ],\n  \"diagnosis\": \"The selected direction is sound. Its enforcement profile and cross-journal transition contract remain incomplete. New ownership schemas should wait.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A1\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:15-25\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:114-126\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/container.py:863-906\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Different initial UIDs do not establish credential separation across all reachable user namespaces.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Rootless mappings, supplementary groups, privilege transitions, inherited descriptors, or management endpoints can reconnect E to P authority.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Specify the complete reachable UID/GID mappings, including nested namespaces. Exclude P credentials and protected groups from every workload generation.\",\n        \"Require no-new-privileges, empty capability sets, restricted devices, isolated PID namespaces, and no writable host cgroup delegation.\",\n        \"Prevent setuid binaries, file capabilities, namespace helpers, ACLs, and supplementary groups from granting protected access.\",\n        \"Protect engine endpoints and controller APIs through filesystem and network policy. Missing socket mounts alone are insufficient.\",\n        \"Inventory every writable export, inherited descriptor, replica mount, runtime home, and API writer.\",\n        \"Never reuse an execution identity while its previous processes or exports remain reachable.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"workspace_isolation and the separately approved provisioner\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Refuse generation startup. Do not repair permissions or mappings automatically.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"On approved Linux fixtures, test attempted P credential acquisition, protected-parent rename, cross-generation access, and engine access.\",\n        \"Test setuid binaries, file capabilities, namespace creation, supplementary groups, descriptor inheritance, and lingering writable exports.\",\n        \"Inspect actual mappings and mounts rather than trusting configuration labels.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A2\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:27-35\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:41\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_files.py:383-399\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py:182-218\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py:349-423\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/git.py:618-626\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/api/repos.py:179-220\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Importer isolation does not cover every Git invocation. Routing existing file APIs to replicas creates a direct P execution path.\",\n      \"impact\": \"git status currently inherits its environment and reads repository configuration. A replica fsmonitor command can execute with its caller's privileges.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Route replica status, diff, source validation, local import, reuse/fetch, sealing, and integration through constrained non-P Git execution.\",\n        \"Treat bundles and objects as hostile after preliminary validation. Hash and connectivity checks do not remove parser risk.\",\n        \"Run hostile unpacking, object traversal, and checkout operations without P credentials or writable canonical metadata.\",\n        \"Give parser workers bounded snapshots or owned transfer stages. P promotes bounded validated outputs through its existing publication owner.\",\n        \"Generate canonical configuration independently. Disable executable configuration, templates, hooks, filters, helpers, and inherited Git environment.\",\n        \"Separate credentialed network acquisition from uncredentialed object inspection.\",\n        \"Prevent legacy local-path shortcuts from bypassing ingestion.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"workspace_replica owns ingestion policy. Git and file-service callers must use that policy.\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Retain source data and reject ingestion before canonical mutation or credential exposure.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"Exercise actual file endpoints with hostile fsmonitor configuration.\",\n        \"Cover local imports, existing-clone fetch, filters, includes, helpers, alternates, malformed objects, and resource exhaustion.\",\n        \"Record subprocess credentials and mounts. Verify no hostile parser receives P authority.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A3\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:68-87\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/db.py:783-912\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_publication.py:1396-1450\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:1490-1558\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Two durable journals are proposed without one authoritative owner for each transition, generation, acknowledgment, and revocation boundary.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Lost replies can strand ownership or permit duplicate effects. Reauthorization checks alone do not serialize revocation against an in-flight mutation.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Make the application DB authoritative for selected authorization, logical reservations, checkout selection, and application binding.\",\n        \"Make the broker journal authoritative for physical ownership, runtime launch consumption, drain, filesystem durability, and release.\",\n        \"Application records reference broker facts. They must not independently declare physical completion.\",\n        \"Persist an application intent before broker acceptance. Bind its digest, database incarnation, operation ID, and expected generation.\",\n        \"Broker ownership persists until application binding commits and the broker durably acknowledges that binding.\",\n        \"Persist destination target binding before path cutover. Allow eligible stopped receipts without reverting their status.\",\n        \"Define revocation ordering through a broker fence. A revocation acknowledgment must state whether earlier accepted effects remain pending.\",\n        \"Give containment and exact-owner recovery explicit authority independent of expired start credentials.\",\n        \"Persist release intent before marker removal. Missing replies never authorize release.\",\n        \"Register database incarnations outside copied database contents. Specify paired restore and stale-journal rejection.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"Parent approves the contract. Existing application owners and workspace_broker enforce their respective facts.\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Retain exclusion and expose the exact pending operation. Unknown identity or journal disagreement blocks effects.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"Interrupt before and after each application commit, broker commit, external effect, binding acknowledgment, and release.\",\n        \"Replay identical requests and reject changed digests.\",\n        \"Race revocation with accepted effects. Restart each owner independently.\",\n        \"Test copied databases, stale restores, logical-only repairs, and stopped-receipt destination binding.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A4\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:57-65\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:79\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Byte-safe reconciliation lacks an exact supported index model, pathname encoding, mutation order, and durable completion predicate.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Implementations can corrupt staged state, traverse administrative paths, overwrite changed canonical entries, or acknowledge partially applied state.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Use raw path bytes internally and canonical base64 encoding in JSON. Keep display strings outside identity comparisons.\",\n        \"Specify supported index entries and flags, including intent-to-add, skip-worktree, assume-unchanged, sparse indexes, and unmerged stages.\",\n        \"Reject unsupported states explicitly without discarding the replica.\",\n        \"Separate administrative metadata from the working-file manifest. Reject reserved paths, duplicates, prefix collisions, unsupported types, and unexpected hardlinks.\",\n        \"Copy symlink text without traversal. Strip unsupported privilege-bearing modes and attributes.\",\n        \"Reserve canonical writers throughout reconciliation. Recheck complete baseline and exact entry preconditions before mutation.\",\n        \"Record owned temporary-object identities, preimages, postimages, operation ordering, and each required synchronization fact.\",\n        \"Update index and selected ref only through the approved transaction protocol. Preserve unrelated and immutable refs.\",\n        \"Publish a new canonical generation only after every file, index, ref, registration, and parent synchronization succeeds.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"workspace_replica owns one reconciliation format and recovery algorithm.\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Keep readers and writers excluded from partial canonical state. Preserve both versions and retain ownership on ambiguity.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"Round-trip arbitrary byte names, staged/unstaged differences, index flags, modes, symlinks, ignored files, and private refs.\",\n        \"Exercise file-directory replacements, administrative-path injection, changed canonical entries, and ref races.\",\n        \"Interrupt every mutation and synchronization boundary. Repeated recovery must never acknowledge incomplete application.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A5\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:51-55\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:85\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:128\",\n        \"sidecar/src/sidecar.js:2494-2503\",\n        \"sidecar/src/sidecar.js:2520-2548\",\n        \"backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_execution.py:1358-1407\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Original sidecar receipts are currently volatile. The packet explicitly leaves missing original acknowledgments permanently blocked.\",\n      \"impact\": \"An ordinary crash can make successful recovery unreachable. Empty cgroups and VM shutdown cannot satisfy the unchanged acknowledgment requirement.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Persist original execution receipts before reporting them. Support idempotent retrieval by exact original identity.\",\n        \"Persist launch consumption before execution can begin. Distinguish never-started operations from executions requiring acknowledgment.\",\n        \"Keep the trusted supervisor outside the drained workload boundary.\",\n        \"Treat persistent replica storage separately from persistent processes. An idle writable sidecar still prevents full drain.\",\n        \"Close writer admission, obtain original acknowledgments, close explicitly confirmed terminals, terminate remaining generation processes, and revoke exports.\",\n        \"Define a reachable retained-data disposition for death before any original receipt exists. Do not label it stopped or released.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"Original execution owner records receipts. workspace_isolation records separate generation drain facts.\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Missing original acknowledgment retains ownership. Replacement runtimes cannot supply it.\",\n      \"openDecision\": \"Strict original-sidecar acknowledgment cannot guarantee successful recovery after every crash. Parent must settle the exceptional disposition without fabricating completion.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"Test receipt persistence before reply, lost reply, death before persistence, broker restart, and VM restart.\",\n        \"Test detached descendants, idle sidecars, live terminals, API writers, and attempted launches during drain.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A6\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:37-49\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:65\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:89-93\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Persistent replicas have no explicit refresh path after canonical integration or a repair that changes the canonical generation.\",\n      \"impact\": \"The next prompt can reopen stale parent content. Unsupported synchronization can also block the runtime needed to fix it.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Add a stopped-replica refresh transition after canonical generation changes.\",\n        \"Refresh selected state only when its recorded replica baseline still matches. Preserve private refs, stashes, configuration, and extra worktrees.\",\n        \"Use the same journaled transfer machinery rather than creating a separate synchronization system.\",\n        \"Allow authorized retained replicas to reopen for conflict repair under a new writable generation.\",\n        \"Reopening invalidates old drain and export facts. It never authorizes another simultaneous writable replica.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"workspace_replica owns baseline refresh. Integration requests it through canonical generation changes.\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Expose stale or conflicting state. Never overwrite private work or silently recreate the replica.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"Integrate a child, then reopen the parent replica and verify updated selected content.\",\n        \"Preserve private branches and stashes.\",\n        \"Recover from detached HEAD and unsupported states through a reachable runtime action, then repeat drain and synchronization.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A7\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"locations\": [\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:95-113\",\n        \"/tmp/yinshi-phase6-os-isolation-plan.md:114-130\"\n      ],\n      \"issue\": \"Stage 1 combines settled fail-closed behavior with schemas that depend on unresolved ownership decisions.\",\n      \"correction\": [\n        \"Separate unsupported-profile gating from new ownership schemas.\",\n        \"Keep real execution disabled until broker ownership, ingestion, drain, reconciliation, and public caller routing are complete.\",\n        \"Do not require VM product selection, numeric IDs, or retention tuning before pure contract work.\",\n        \"Retain F1, F3, F5, F6, and F8 corrections. Preserve previously corrected cancellation and normal synchronization behavior.\"\n      ],\n      \"owner\": \"Parent controls stage approval.\",\n      \"failureOutcome\": \"Unsupported execution remains unavailable. Existing storage and active legacy ownership remain untouched.\",\n      \"validation\": [\n        \"Verify unsupported profiles reject prompts, terminals, provider dispatch, and legacy launch shortcuts.\",\n        \"Verify read-only status still exposes actionable setup or recovery states.\",\n        \"After contract approval, validate schema constraints independently before any real execution enablement.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"permittedTransitions\": [\n    {\n      \"owner\": \"Application DB\",\n      \"flow\": \"authorized intent -> reserved -> broker reference recorded -> destination binding committed -> application completion\",\n      \"rule\": \"No path cutover before durable destination ownership. No physical completion inferred from application status.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"owner\": \"Broker journal\",\n      \"flow\": \"accepted -> physically owned -> durable publication -> application binding acknowledged -> release intent -> synchronized release\",\n      \"rule\": \"Retries resume the same operation. Timeouts retain ownership.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"owner\": \"Runtime supervisor\",\n      \"flow\": \"registered generation -> start consumed -> writable -> admission closed -> original acknowledgment recorded -> OS drained\",\n      \"rule\": \"Each fact has its own authority. A replacement generation cannot acknowledge its predecessor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"owner\": \"Reconciliation owner\",\n      \"flow\": \"drained -> immutable export -> validated -> prepared -> applying -> durable canonical generation -> acknowledged\",\n      \"rule\": \"Conflict or ambiguity retains exclusion. Repair reopening requires a new writable generation and invalidates prior drain facts.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"driftCheck\": [\n    \"P-level Git consumption after sandbox validation weakens the intended parser boundary.\",\n    \"Requiring every setup choice before contract work adds avoidable delay.\",\n    \"Successful synchronization does not currently define how persistent replicas follow later canonical integration.\",\n    \"Permanent missing-acknowledgment blockage conflicts with a promise of universally reachable successful recovery.\"\n  ],\n  \"minimalStagesBeforeProvisioning\": [\n    \"After parent approval: document the enforcement profile, authoritative transition table, exceptional recovery outcome, and supported reconciliation state.\",\n    \"After separate implementation authorization: add fail-closed profile gating and read-only status behavior without provisioning.\",\n    \"After ownership decisions settle: implement transactional schemas, protocol validation, and deterministic journal-recovery tests using disposable local fixtures.\",\n    \"After manifest decisions settle: implement pure encoding, validation, and reconciliation-planning tests.\",\n    \"Real isolation, mount revocation, cgroup drain, and durability acceptance require separately approved Linux infrastructure.\"\n  ],\n  \"nonessentialDefaults\": [\n    \"Propose Ubuntu 24.04 LTS with cgroup v2 and local ext4 storage. Verify support before enablement.\",\n    \"Propose rootless Podman with a verified P-excluding workload mapping. Pin an approved supported version later.\",\n    \"Propose a Lima Linux VM on Mac with a private virtual disk, not writable canonical host-folder mounts.\",\n    \"Use administrator-provisioned /var/lib/yinshi storage and a P-only Unix broker socket.\",\n    \"Allocate subordinate IDs during provisioning. Do not assume accounts, credentials, mappings, or daemons exist.\",\n    \"Reuse existing authenticated runtime transport rather than adding another remote broker protocol.\",\n    \"Retain private and unsynchronized replicas until explicit disposition. Disk pressure rejects new work rather than deleting them.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendation\": \"Keep the selected architecture. Approve precise boundary and ownership corrections before new schema coding. No broad redesign is required.\",\n  \"needFromMainAgent\": [\n    \"Approve complete P/E enforcement requirements and Git parser placement.\",\n    \"Approve journal authority, revocation ordering, database incarnation, and restore semantics.\",\n    \"Settle the exceptional outcome when the original execution dies before recording its acknowledgment.\",\n    \"Approve supported index semantics and retained-replica refresh behavior.\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"No Linux profile, VM, principal, daemon, credentials, or filesystem guarantees were verified.\",\n\n[8 more lines in file. Use offset=261 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789330832331}}
