shi\",\"ts\":1789260479544,\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-13T00:47:59.544Z\",\"sourceEventType\":\"message_end\",\"role\":\"user\",\"text\":\"Task: [Read from: /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_journal.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_artifact_store.py, /Users/user/projects/yinshi/backend/src/yinshi/servic... [truncated]","truncated":true,"truncatedBy":"bytes","totalLines":128,"totalBytes":58701,"outputLines":114,"outputBytes":51125,"lastLinePartial":false,"firstLineExceedsLimit":false,"maxLines":9007199254740991,"maxBytes":51200},"linesTruncated":true},"isError":false,"timestamp":1789330837226}}
{"type":"message","id":"d2ca00b8","parentId":"118a9831","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:41.203Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Confirming architecture consistency**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa705981cf087d0be7babd5bd3f9b98\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Confirming architecture consistency**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_M4vvHhm7Yvo3MUVi3rNfC0CM|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa70598a43087d09ec0f717ec5263df","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi-subagents/artifacts/ac665022_worker-expert_0_output.md","offset":1,"limit":760}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":17309,"output":55,"cacheRead":146048,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":13,"totalTokens":163412,"cost":{"input":0.08654500000000001,"output":0.00165,"cacheRead":0.07302399999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.161219}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1789330837243,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa70595bcac87d0b384f5a3b2b77c3d","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"message","id":"ec3de94e","parentId":"d2ca00b8","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:20:41.205Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_M4vvHhm7Yvo3MUVi3rNfC0CM|fc_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa70598a43087d09ec0f717ec5263df","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Broker replica lifecycle implementation packet\n\n## Current causal account\n\nCurrent checkout contains three separate foundations:\n\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns durable ordered replica state.\n- `BrokerArtifactStore` safely receives bounded three-artifact sets.\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` verifies and atomically publishes those sets.\n\nNo coordinator connects them.\n\nCurrent broker lifecycle handles `executor.launch` through `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, then `launch`. It does not implement replica stages.\n\nMissing production effects:\n\n- Application-owned replica admission.\n- Graceful executor drain with durable acknowledgment.\n- Post-drain workspace export.\n- Export destination storage.\n- Broker cleanup for incoming or published artifacts.\n- Durable request transport carrying replica declarations and artifact streams.\n\nThese gaps prevent safe production wiring now.\n\n## Required ownership\n\n| State | Sole owner |\n|---|---|\n| Lifecycle position and terminal outcome | `BrokerReplicaJournal` |\n| Incoming artifact bytes | `BrokerArtifactStore` |\n| Published artifact set | `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore` |\n| Logical workspace reservation | Application admission service |\n| Live executor process | Executor runtime |\n| Prepared replica tree and privileged reclaim | `RootLauncher` |\n| Exported object references | External export store |\n\nCoordinator must hold no durable mutable state. It must reconstruct every decision from journal state.\n\n## Allowed transitions\n\n```text\naccepted\n  -> authority_claimed\n  -> ingest_started\n  -> ingest_completed\n  -> verify_started\n  -> verify_completed\n  -> publish_started\n  -> publish_completed\n  -> admission_started\n  -> admission_completed\n  -> drain_started\n  -> drain_completed\n  -> export_started\n  -> export_completed\n  -> reclaim_started\n  -> reclaim_completed\n```\n\nAny active stage may instead become:\n\n```text\nstage_rejected(stage, stable_reason)\nstage_unresolved(stage, stable_reason)\n```\n\nBoth outcomes are terminal under current journal semantics.\n\nInvalid transitions:\n\n- Skipping any stage.\n- Replacing claimed authority.\n- Completing without a matching start.\n- Completing with a conflicting receipt.\n- Retrying an unresolved lifecycle.\n- Admitting before publication.\n- Exporting before confirmed drain.\n- Reclaiming before export.\n- Reclaiming without a drain acknowledgment.\n- Reclaiming while root observes a unit, cgroup member, or runtime directory.\n\n`BrokerReplicaJournal` already enforces order, receipt equality, authority binding, and exact replay.\n\n## New coordinator module\n\nAdd:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py\n```\n\nKeep journal serialization and SQLite details inside `broker_replica_journal.py`.\n\n### Core types\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Generic, Literal, Protocol, TypeVar\n\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_protocol import BrokerRequest\nfrom yinshi.services.broker_replica_journal import (\n    AdmissionReceipt,\n    BrokerReplicaJournal,\n    DrainReceipt,\n    ExportReceipt,\n    IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    IngestReceipt,\n    PublishReceipt,\n    ReclaimReceipt,\n    ReplicaAuthority,\n    ReplicaJournalDecision,\n    VerifyReceipt,\n)\n\nReplicaStage = Literal[\n    \"ingest\",\n    \"verify\",\n    \"publish\",\n    \"admission\",\n    \"drain\",\n    \"export\",\n    \"reclaim\",\n]\n\nStageReceipt = (\n    IngestReceipt\n    | VerifyReceipt\n    | PublishReceipt\n    | AdmissionReceipt\n    | DrainReceipt\n    | ExportReceipt\n    | ReclaimReceipt\n)\n\nR = TypeVar(\"R\", bound=StageReceipt)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleContext:\n    request: BrokerRequest\n    authority: ReplicaAuthority\n    owner_token: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass StageReconciliation(Generic[R]):\n    outcome: Literal[\"completed\", \"not_applied\", \"unknown\"]\n    receipt: R | None\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if (self.outcome == \"completed\") != (self.receipt is not None):\n            raise ValueError(\"reconciliation receipt does not match outcome\")\n```\n\n### Effect protocol\n\nUse one typed effect per stage. This prevents force-drain flags or arbitrary stage dispatch.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaStageEffect(Protocol[R]):\n    async def apply(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> R: ...\n\n    async def reconcile(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[R]: ...\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaLifecycleEffects:\n    ingest: ReplicaStageEffect[IngestReceipt]\n    verify: ReplicaStageEffect[VerifyReceipt]\n    publish: ReplicaStageEffect[PublishReceipt]\n    admission: ReplicaStageEffect[AdmissionReceipt]\n    drain: ReplicaStageEffect[DrainReceipt]\n    export: ReplicaStageEffect[ExportReceipt]\n    reclaim: ReplicaStageEffect[ReclaimReceipt]\n```\n\nDo not provide default effects. Missing effects must block construction.\n\n### Coordinator signature\n\n```python\nclass BrokerReplicaLifecycleCoordinator:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        *,\n        journal: BrokerReplicaJournal,\n        effects: ReplicaLifecycleEffects,\n        effect_timeout_seconds: float,\n        monotonic: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic,\n    ) -> None: ...\n\n    async def execute(\n        self,\n        request: BrokerRequest,\n        request_frame: bytes,\n        *,\n        authority: ReplicaAuthority,\n        owner_token: str,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover(\n        self,\n        lifecycle: IncompleteReplicaLifecycle,\n    ) -> ReplicaJournalDecision: ...\n\n    async def recover_startup(self) -> tuple[ReplicaJournalDecision, ...]: ...\n```\n\n`execute` accepts immutable request data only. Artifact readers belong inside injected ingest effect adapters.\n\n## Transition pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def execute(...):\n    decision = journal.accept(request, request_frame=request_frame)\n\n    if decision is terminal or completed:\n        return decision\n\n    journal.claim_authority(\n        request,\n        owner_token=owner_token,\n        authority=authority,\n    )\n\n    context = ReplicaLifecycleContext(request, authority, owner_token)\n\n    for stage in FIXED_REPLICA_STAGES:\n        decision = journal.status(request)\n\n        if decision is terminal:\n            return decision\n\n        if stage is already completed:\n            continue\n\n        journal.begin_stage(\n            request,\n            owner_token=owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n        )\n\n        deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n        try:\n            receipt = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n                effect_for(stage).apply(context, deadline=deadline),\n                deadline,\n            )\n        except StageRejected as error:\n            journal.record_rejected(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                receipt=RejectedReceipt(reason_code=error.reason_code),\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"cancelled_unknown\",\n            )\n            raise\n        except TimeoutError:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=\"timeout_unknown\",\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n        except StageOutcomeUnknown as error:\n            journal.record_unresolved(\n                request,\n                owner_token=owner_token,\n                stage=stage,\n                reason=error.reason_code,\n            )\n            return journal.status(request)\n\n        complete_stage(journal, request, owner_token, stage, receipt)\n\n    return journal.status(request)\n```\n\n`complete_stage` must use existing typed methods:\n\n```python\njournal.complete_ingest(...)\njournal.complete_verify(...)\njournal.complete_publish(...)\njournal.complete_admission(...)\njournal.complete_drain(...)\njournal.complete_export(...)\njournal.complete_reclaim(...)\n```\n\nNever open a journal database around `await`. Every journal call must finish before an effect begins.\n\n### Recovery pseudocode\n\n```python\nasync def recover(lifecycle):\n    context = context_from_incomplete_lifecycle(lifecycle)\n    stage = lifecycle.active_stage\n    effect = effect_for(stage)\n    deadline = monotonic() + effect_timeout_seconds\n\n    try:\n        result = await run_with_absolute_deadline(\n            effect.reconcile(context, deadline=deadline),\n            deadline,\n        )\n    except BaseException classified as unknown:\n        journal.record_unresolved(\n            context.request,\n            owner_token=context.owner_token,\n            stage=stage,\n            reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n        )\n        return journal.status(context.request)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"completed\":\n        complete_stage(..., result.receipt)\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    if result.outcome == \"not_applied\":\n        return await execute_remaining_stages(context)\n\n    journal.record_unresolved(\n        context.request,\n        owner_token=context.owner_token,\n        stage=stage,\n        reason=\"recovery_unknown\",\n    )\n    return journal.status(context.request)\n```\n\nA late result after timeout must never complete the journal. Reconciliation handles any later observable external state.\n\n## Existing adapters\n\n### Ingest adapter\n\n`BrokerArtifactStore` can support ingest.\n\nAdapter responsibilities:\n\n1. Decode the validated manifest from authenticated request payload.\n2. Validate exactly three distinct roles.\n3. Call `BrokerArtifactStore.receive(...)`.\n4. Return its `IngestReceipt`.\n5. Use `reconcile_attempts(...)` after a crash.\n6. Return `unknown` for ambiguous pending or quarantine state.\n\nDo not retain `OpenedReplicaArtifacts` across journal calls.\n\n### Verify adapter\n\nUse:\n\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.open_incoming_async(...)`\n- `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.verify_artifact_set(...)`\n- `BrokerArtifactStore.recheck_opened_async(...)`\n\nRequired sequence:\n\n```text\nopen incoming\nverify bytes\nrecheck same opened identities\nclose every descriptor\nreturn VerifyReceipt\n```\n\nThe adapter must map publication bindings to journal `ArtifactReference` values without changing IDs, hashes, roles, media types, or lengths.\n\nA replacement during verification is rejection or unresolved according to existing store exceptions.\n\n### Publish adapter\n\nUse `WorkspaceReplicaPublicationStore.publish_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nRecovery uses `inspect_published_artifact_set(...)`.\n\nConvert `ReplicaInspectionReceipt` or publication receipt into journal `PublishReceipt`. Preserve:\n\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Artifact set digest.\n- Source state digest.\n- Publication receipt ID.\n\nA post-rename failure remains unresolved unless inspection establishes exact completion.\n\n### Reclaim adapter\n\nUse existing `LauncherClient.reclaim(operation_id)`.\n\nDo not add `stop`, `drain`, `export`, or delete actions to root protocol.\n\nMap only exact result:\n\n```text\nstatus == \"reclaimed\" and error is None\n```\n\nto `ReclaimReceipt`.\n\nThese results are not success:\n\n- Missing reply.\n- Timeout.\n- Clean EOF.\n- Malformed reply.\n- Wrong action.\n- Transport reset.\n- `reclaim_disabled`.\n- Root quiescence rejection.\n\nUnknown transport outcomes become unresolved. Explicit rejection becomes rejected.\n\nRoot already checks unit absence, empty cgroup, and runtime absence before deletion.\n\n## Missing injected effects\n\n### Admission\n\nCurrent `acquire_prompt_workspace(...)` is unsuitable. It depends on FastAPI request state and application SQLite ownership.\n\nAdd an application-owned boundary later:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ReplicaAdmissionCommand:\n    operation_id: str\n    physical_target_id: str\n    replica_generation: int\n    execution_owner_id: str\n    publication_receipt_id: str\n    artifact_set_sha256: str\n\n\nclass ReplicaAdmissionClient(Protocol):\n    async def admit(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> AdmissionReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        command: ReplicaAdmissionCommand,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[AdmissionReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nNo SQLite connection may leave application-owned methods. Only immutable DTOs may cross transport.\n\nAdmission must invoke `require_isolated_execution(...)` before reservation, Git work, credentials, or provider access.\n\n### Graceful drain\n\nNo current graceful drain protocol exists.\n\n```python\nclass GracefulReplicaDrainClient(Protocol):\n    async def request_drain(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> DrainReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect_acknowledgement(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[DrainReceipt]: ...\n```\n\nDo not include `force`, `signal`, `kill`, or `systemctl stop` options.\n\nAcknowledgment must bind:\n\n- Operation ID.\n- Physical target ID.\n- Replica generation.\n- Execution owner ID.\n- Drain request ID.\n\nMissing acknowledgment is unresolved. It must block export and reclaim.\n\n### Export\n\nNo current broker-side post-drain export exists.\n\n```python\nclass ReplicaExportClient(Protocol):\n    async def export(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> ExportReceipt: ...\n\n    async def inspect(\n        self,\n        context: ReplicaLifecycleContext,\n        *,\n        deadline: float,\n    ) -> StageReconciliation[ExportReceipt]: ...\n```\n\n`ExportReceipt` must contain exactly three external references:\n\n1. `committed_bundle`\n2. `worktree`\n3. `index_objects`\n\nReject duplicate IDs, missing roles, extra roles, local paths, or inline bytes.\n\nExisting bundle, worktree, and object-pack builders may support a future executor-side implementation. They are not a broker export transport.\n\n## Smallest existing API additions\n\n### `broker_replica_journal.py`\n\nNo transition API change appears necessary.\n\nAdd accessors only if `IncompleteReplicaLifecycle` does not expose these values:\n\n```python\nrequest: BrokerRequest\nauthority: ReplicaAuthority\nowner_token: str\nactive_stage: ReplicaStage\n```\n\nDo not expose SQLite connections, cursors, or row objects.\n\n### `broker_artifact_store.py`\n\nNo ingest API change is required.\n\nA deletion API needs a separate retention decision. Do not silently remove incoming artifacts during root reclaim.\n\n### `workspace_replica_publication.py`\n\nNo verify or publish API change is required.\n\nA published-set deletion API also needs a retention decision.\n\n### `execution_broker.py`\n\nKeep `LauncherClient` methods fixed:\n\n```python\nasync def prepare(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def launch(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\nasync def reclaim(operation_id: str) -> LauncherResult\n```\n\nAdd replica request dispatch only after request protocol approval.\n\n### `broker_runtime.py`\n\nDo not treat runtime directory cleanup as graceful drain acknowledgment. No safe drain API exists here.\n\n### `execution_daemons.py`\n\nLater wiring must:\n\n- Construct replica journal separately from broker launch journal.\n- Construct coordinator only when every effect exists.\n- Recover before accepting connections.\n- Keep launch, prepare, reclaim, and replica lifecycle gates independent.\n- Preserve current nested deadline invariant.\n- Log stable reason codes only.\n\n### `root_launcher.py`\n\nNo action changes.\n\nActions remain exactly:\n\n```text\nprepare\nlaunch\nreclaim\n```\n\n### Darwin isolation\n\nDo not weaken `workspace_isolation.py`.\n\nNative Darwin execution remains fail-closed. Supported fixtures remain test-only behavior.\n\n## Deadline rules\n\nUse an absolute monotonic deadline per stage.\n\nCurrent nesting must remain:\n\n```text\nroot worker timeout\n< launcher client timeout\n< broker effect timeout\n< connection timeout\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Persist `begin_stage` before starting deadline.\n- Never reset deadline during retries or response parsing.\n- Treat timeout as unknown once an effect may have started.\n- Record unresolved before returning.\n- On cancellation, synchronously record unresolved, then re-raise.\n- Discard late task results.\n- Do not advance after unresolved state.\n- Startup reconciliation receives a fresh bounded deadline.\n- Persistence failure remains fail-closed and must escape as journal failure.\n\n## Focused tests\n\nAdd `test_broker_replica_lifecycle.py`.\n\nRequired cases:\n\n1. Executes all seven stages in exact order.\n2. Starts each stage durably before invoking its effect.\n3. Completes each stage only after effect return.\n4. Replays completed lifecycle without effects.\n5. Resumes from each completed stage.\n6. Rejects wrong authority before effects.\n7. Rejects owner-token conflict.\n8. Never skips a stage.\n9. Verification rejection records `verify` rejection.\n10. Publish post-visibility ambiguity records `publish` unresolved.\n11. Admission timeout records `admission` unresolved.\n12. Drain cancellation records `drain` unresolved and re-raises.\n13. Missing drain acknowledgment blocks export.\n14. Export rejects fewer than three references.\n15. Export rejects more than three references.\n16. Export rejects duplicate roles or artifact IDs.\n17. Reclaim is never called before export completion.\n18. Root live-unit rejection blocks reclaim completion.\n19. Reclaim EOF records `reclaim` unresolved.\n20. No unresolved request invokes an effect on replay.\n21. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable ingest.\n22. Crash recovery completes an exactly inspectable publication.\n23. Unknown recovery evidence records stage-specific unresolved.\n24. A late result after timeout cannot append completion.\n25. Journal methods never execute while effect coroutine is active.\n26. Startup recovery finishes before listener acceptance.\n27. Root action set remains exactly three actions.\n28. Each feature gate remains independently disabled.\n29. Darwin admission performs no reservation or credential access.\n30. Logs contain stable codes and omit paths, payloads, keys, and exception text.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- Reusing broker launch journal is invalid. Its stages are `prepare`, `runtime_setup`, and `launch`.\n- Adding root `stop` or `export` actions violates fixed root protocol tests.\n- Treating runtime cleanup as drain acknowledgment provides no graceful executor acknowledgment.\n- Using publication inspection as journal authority violates sole-authority requirement.\n- Retrying unknown effects can duplicate admission, export, or reclaim effects.\n- Holding application SQLite across broker calls violates process ownership and await boundaries.\n- Enabling replica lifecycle through existing launch gate couples independent controls.\n- Darwin local execution fallback violates current fail-closed isolation behavior.\n\n## Escalation questions\n\nProduct or architecture approval is required for these decisions:\n\n1. What authenticated request types start or continue replica lifecycle?\n2. Which payload owns manifest, declaration, authority, and export destination?\n3. What service owns durable admission acknowledgment?\n4. What executor protocol defines graceful drain acknowledgment?\n5. Where do exported artifacts live, and who signs their references?\n6. Should root reclaim also trigger broker incoming or publication cleanup?\n7. What retention applies after rejected or unresolved stages?\n8. May operators resolve terminal unresolved states, or must they create a new generation?\n9. What stage deadlines and byte limits become supported configuration?\n10. Should startup block all broker traffic when one lifecycle cannot reconcile?\n\n## Report\n\nChanged files: none.\n\nCommands run:\n\n- Repository instruction reads.\n- Source and focused test inspection.\n- `git status --short`.\n- `git diff --stat`.\n\nTests were not run. Task was read-only.\n\nMain remaining risk: admission, drain, and export lack production protocols. Wiring before those contracts exist would create hidden fallback behavior."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1789330841205}}
