{"type":"message","id":"71ae17e3","parentId":"84e3180d","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:32:15.637Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Ensuring acceptance criteria alignment**\n\n**Defining structured report format and migration rules**\n\n**Extending parser for replica.drain requests**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa707c3f9a487d085bceeccb1c6fbd2\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Ensuring acceptance criteria alignment**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Defining structured report format and migration rules**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Extending parser for replica.drain requests**\"}]}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Defining paused lifecycle behavior**\n\n**Planning terminal states for paused lifecycle on broker restart**\n\n**Assessing effect timeout and artifact limits**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa707d11cd087d090d0c02725da67bc\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Defining paused lifecycle behavior**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning terminal states for paused lifecycle on broker restart**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Assessing effect timeout and artifact limits**\"}]}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Assessing stage timeout limits**\n\n**Designing framed export protocol**\n\n**Defining control frame authentication**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa707e0b32087d08e6a32ceddeb4f7d\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Assessing stage timeout limits**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing framed export protocol**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Defining control frame authentication**\"}]}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Hardening publication store paths**\n\n**Planning materializer API and approval process**\n\n**Refining report phrasing and format**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa707efdb2487d0bfeecd10a9469dfe\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"REDACTED\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Hardening publication store paths**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning materializer API and approval process**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Refining report phrasing and format**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"## Inherited decisions\n\n- Stages remain `ingest → verify → publish → admission → drain → export → reclaim`.\n- `BrokerReplicaJournal` owns lifecycle authority.\n- Application storage owns logical authorization and repository deletion state.\n- Authority fields remain opaque logical bindings.\n- Root actions remain exactly `prepare`, `launch`, and `reclaim`.\n- Drain uses graceful broker-to-executor control only.\n- Missing acknowledgment or a live runtime blocks reclaim.\n- Export returns exactly three `ArtifactReference` values.\n- Artifact bytes stay outside SQLite.\n- Unknown effect results remain stage-specific unresolved outcomes.\n- Native Darwin execution remains fail-closed.\n- No SQLite connection may cross an external effect or `await`.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n### Blocker findings\n\n1. **Lifecycle has no execution interval.**  \n   `broker_replica_lifecycle.py:409-453` advances directly from admission into drain. No durable pause or continuation authorization exists.\n\n2. **No executor server exists.**  \n   `backend/pyproject.toml:10-16` has no `yinshi-executor` entry point.  \n   `worker_runtime.py:29-145` is an in-process ASGI adapter, not a `/run/session.sock` server.\n\n3. **Published layout cannot enter root prepare.**  \n   `execution_daemons.py:114,1149-1153` publishes artifact files directly into launcher staging.  \n   `root_launcher.py:1198,1237-1269` requires exactly `repo` and `home`.\n\n4. **Post-exit broker export is impossible with current ownership.**  \n   Root makes replica storage executor-owned and mode `0700`. Broker cannot read it after executor exit.\n\n5. **Current runtime cannot finish reclaim prerequisites.**  \n   `broker_runtime.py:89-168` creates a listener.  \n   `broker_runtime.py:170-175` only closes it. It does not unlink the socket or remove runtime storage.\n\n6. **Current broker cannot establish stopped-unit facts through a public API.**  \n   Root has private unit and cgroup inspection in `root_launcher.py:309,623-668,1600-1649`.  \n   `LauncherSocketClient` exposes only the three mutating root actions.\n\n7. **No lifecycle client exists.**  \n   Source search finds `replica.lifecycle` only in broker parsing, journal code, and tests. Desktop and application routing are absent.\n\n8. **No high-level repository exporter exists.**  \n   Low-level builders exist at:\n   - `workspace_replica_bundle.py:527`\n   - `workspace_replica_artifact.py:538`\n   - `workspace_replica_object_pack.py:396`\n\n   No module captures one live repository into the complete three-artifact contract.\n\n### High findings\n\n- Current `40` second stage limit may be too short for bounded repository materialization or export.\n- Export ref selection and ignored-file policy are not defined.\n- Application deletion receipts are not bound into any signed lifecycle start request.\n- Current production profile remains correctly unsupported in `workspace_isolation.py:53-59`.\n\n## Drift / contradiction check\n\n- Using launcher staging as publication storage conflicts with root prepare input.\n- Implementing admission now would silently merge publication, materialization, launch, and runtime interaction.\n- Keeping one-shot coordination would drain each executor immediately after launch.\n- A companion continuation journal would create a second lifecycle authority.\n- Modifying replica journal v1 in place would violate its frozen SQL contract.\n- Generating export after executor exit would require new broker read authority over executor storage.\n- Adding root `stop`, `status`, or `export` actions would violate the fixed root protocol.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n### 1. Make one deliberate journal contract revision\n\nRevise only this inherited decision:\n\n> Replica journal v1 remains the permanent writable lifecycle format.\n\nReplace it with:\n\n> Replica journal v1 remains unchanged and read-only. New long-lived lifecycle work uses replica journal v2.\n\nUse a new fixed database:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi/control/broker-replica-journal-v2.sqlite3\n```\n\nDo not add a companion authority.\n\nStartup rules:\n\n1. Inspect replica journal v1 without mutation.\n2. Create v2 only when v1 has no accepted lifecycle work.\n3. Refuse startup when v1 contains accepted or incomplete work.\n4. Never auto-copy v1 events into v2.\n5. Keep launch journal v2 unchanged.\n\nV2 adds two non-stage events:\n\n```text\nadmission_completed\n  -> lifecycle_paused\n  -> drain_continuation_accepted\n  -> drain_started\n```\n\n`lifecycle_paused` stores the exact signed active response.\n\n`drain_continuation_accepted` stores the authenticated continuation frame before any drain effect.\n\nInitial request remains `replica.lifecycle`.\n\nContinuation request becomes `replica.drain`. Its payload contains exactly:\n\n```text\nauthority\ninitial_request_sha256\nadmission_receipt_id\napplication_drain_intent_receipt_id\n```\n\nV2 remains sole lifecycle authority.\n\nA replayed identical continuation returns the existing result. A conflicting continuation is rejected before effects.\n\nA paused runtime from another broker process becomes `broker_restart_unknown`. Automatic drain or reconnect remains forbidden.\n\n### 2. Admission owns materialization, prepare, runtime setup, launch, and handshake\n\nAdmission is the correct owner for these ordered suboperations:\n\n1. Revalidate exact published artifact authority.\n2. Materialize `repo` and `home` into private pending launcher staging.\n3. Synchronize all created state.\n4. Atomically publish launcher staging by operation ID.\n5. Call root `prepare`.\n6. Inspect the protected operation root owner.\n7. Create broker runtime listener.\n8. Call root `launch`.\n9. Authenticate executor connection.\n10. Persist admission receipt.\n\nDo not call `BrokerService.executor.launch`. That path has a separate journal and lacks replica authority.\n\nResource selection uses only signed `operation_id` plus root-selected executor ownership.\n\n`physical_target_id`, `replica_generation`, and `execution_owner_id` never select paths, accounts, units, or sockets.\n\n### 3. Separate publication storage from launcher staging\n\nChange artifact publication root to:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi/replica-publications\n```\n\nKeep launcher staging at:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi-launcher/staging\n```\n\nAdd `ReplicaMaterializationStore`.\n\nIt consumes descriptor-pinned published artifacts and creates exactly:\n\n```text\n<operation-id>/\n  repo/\n  home/\n```\n\nRequired behavior:\n\n- Use pending random names.\n- Reject links, unsafe paths, privilege bits, and unsupported objects.\n- Disable Git replacement objects and lazy fetch.\n- Restore refs, HEAD, index bytes, worktree bytes, modes, and symlink text.\n- Import supplemental index objects.\n- Recheck source descriptors after materialization.\n- Synchronize files, directories, and staging root.\n- Use same-filesystem atomic no-replace publication.\n- Keep materialization receipts outside launcher staging.\n\n### 4. Build a distinct executor control milestone\n\nAdd:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/replica_executor.py\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/replica_executor_protocol.py\n```\n\nAdd entry point:\n\n```toml\nyinshi-executor = \"yinshi.replica_executor:main\"\n```\n\nBroker owns listener and accepted connection. Executor connects as client through `/run/session.sock`.\n\n#### Authentication\n\n1. Executor verifies server UID equals configured broker UID.\n2. Broker verifies kernel peer UID equals root-selected executor UID.\n3. Executor sends a random nonce plus exact operation ID.\n4. Broker replies with authority, broker nonce, and random session key.\n5. Executor returns HMAC-SHA256 over the complete handshake transcript.\n6. Both sides use directional sequence numbers for later frames.\n\nKernel credentials and root-controlled socket mounting provide primary authentication.\n\nHandshake nonces prevent stale connection replay.\n\n#### Framing\n\n- Four-byte big-endian length prefix.\n- Canonical JSON control body.\n- Maximum control body: `65,536` bytes.\n- Exact key sets.\n- No floats.\n- HMAC-SHA256 on every post-handshake control frame.\n- Independent monotonic sequence numbers per direction.\n- One authenticated connection per operation.\n\n`AdmissionReceipt.session_socket_sha256` binds:\n\n- socket device and inode\n- operation ID\n- authority\n- executor UID\n- both handshake nonces\n- session identifier\n\n`AdmissionReceipt.receipt_id` also binds the materialization and root prepare receipts.\n\n### 5. Pause execution after admission\n\nAfter admission completes, coordinator writes `lifecycle_paused` and returns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"stage\": \"admission\",\n  \"state\": \"active\",\n  \"receipt_id\": \"<admission receipt>\"\n}\n```\n\nNo drain begins until authenticated `replica.drain` arrives.\n\nApplication-driven runtime RPC remains a separate required contract.\n\nDo not treat the control handshake as a workload protocol.\n\nExisting Runner Noise transport may guide encryption and replay handling. Current APIs cannot be reused unchanged.\n\n### 6. Graceful drain protocol\n\nBroker first persists the continuation and `drain_started`.\n\nThen:\n\n1. Broker sends authenticated `drain.request`.\n2. Executor closes new work admission.\n3. Executor settles every accepted operation.\n4. Executor obtains the original runtime acknowledgment.\n5. Executor captures final repository artifacts while quiescent.\n6. Executor streams the three artifacts into broker-owned pending export storage.\n7. Broker validates declared lengths and digests.\n8. Broker synchronizes pending export storage.\n9. Executor sends authenticated `drain.ack`.\n10. Broker persists its authenticated observation.\n11. Broker sends `drain.accepted`.\n12. Executor closes the connection and exits voluntarily.\n13. Broker confirms unit and cgroup quiescence.\n14. Broker removes runtime socket storage durably.\n15. Drain returns `DrainReceipt`.\n\n`drain.ack` binds:\n\n- operation ID\n- complete authority\n- continuation request ID\n- highest accepted work sequence\n- original runtime acknowledgment ID\n- staged export-set digest\n- executor quiescence identifier\n\nNo force flag, signal, kill request, or root stop action exists.\n\nFailure mapping:\n\n| Condition | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| No durable drain request marker | `not_applied` |\n| Missing executor acknowledgment | `acknowledgment_unknown` |\n| Ack received but runtime remains live | `runtime_live` |\n| Unit or cgroup lookup fails | `unit_state_unknown` |\n| Transport loss after request | `transport_unknown` |\n| Timeout or cancellation after request | stage-specific unknown |\n| Exact durable ack, stopped runtime, exact pending export | `completed` |\n\nA missing original runtime acknowledgment always blocks export and reclaim.\n\n### 7. Generate during quiescence, expose after drain\n\nCurrent ownership makes generation after process exit impossible.\n\nUse this precise boundary:\n\n- Executor generates artifacts after writer admission closes.\n- Executor remains alive only for export transfer.\n- Broker exposes artifacts only after drain completion.\n\nAdd `ReplicaRepositoryExporter`.\n\nIt composes existing low-level builders:\n\n- `create_committed_bundle`\n- `encode_worktree_artifact`\n- `create_index_object_pack`\n\nIt also adds missing bounded repository capture.\n\nRef policy should use the exact initial advertised non-HEAD ref names. HEAD inclusion must match the initial artifact.\n\nIgnored-file policy must be approved before implementation. Recommended rule:\n\n- Export tracked paths.\n- Export nonignored untracked paths.\n- Export only exact initially authorized ignored paths.\n- Never infer new ignored-path authority from a digest.\n\n### 8. Add broker-owned immutable export storage\n\nAdd:\n\n```text\nbackend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_export_store.py\n```\n\nFixed root:\n\n```text\n/var/lib/yinshi/replica-exports\n```\n\nStore owns:\n\n- pending streamed bytes\n- authenticated drain observation\n- immutable published export set\n- internal manifest and synchronization markers\n\n`ExportReceipt` remains unchanged.\n\nIts three fields mean immutable references outside SQLite and outside the root-managed replica:\n\n1. `bundle`\n2. `worktree`\n3. `index_objects`\n\nEach reference contains only:\n\n```text\nartifact_id\nsha256\nbyte_length\n```\n\nNo path, URL, socket name, inline bytes, or internal marker enters the journal.\n\nBroker generates artifact IDs. Callers cannot choose them.\n\nExport stage independently verifies pending bytes. It then publishes them atomically and returns the three references.\n\n### 9. Reclaim prerequisites\n\nAdd a read-only `BrokerRuntimeStateInspector`.\n\nFactor fixed unit and cgroup inspection from root code into a shared low-level module.\n\nDo not expose caller-selected unit names or paths.\n\nStopped state requires all facts:\n\n- authenticated executor connection reached EOF\n- transient unit is absent\n- fixed cgroup has no processes\n- broker listener is closed\n- runtime socket is unlinked\n- runtime operation directory is removed and synchronized\n- durable drain acknowledgment exists\n- immutable export set exists\n\nAfter these checks, reclaim effect calls only:\n\n```python\nLauncherSocketClient.reclaim(operation_id)\n```\n\nRoot performs the final independent unit, cgroup, runtime, ownership, and filesystem checks.\n\nA successful root response creates `ReclaimReceipt`.\n\nTimeout, EOF, malformed response, or broad root rejection remains unresolved.\n\nExact reclaim retry is permitted because root reclaim already supports absent completed state and retained quarantine recovery.\n\n### 10. Required APIs\n\nJournal v2:\n\n```python\npause_after_admission(...)\naccept_drain_continuation(...)\nactive_lifecycle(...)\ncompleted_receipts(...)\n```\n\nCoordinator v2:\n\n```python\nstart(...)\ncontinue_drain(...)\nrecover_incomplete(...)\n```\n\nRuntime:\n\n```python\naccept_authenticated_executor(...)\nsession(...)\nwait_for_eof(...)\nretire_stopped_session(...)\n```\n\nMaterializer:\n\n```python\nmaterialize(...)\nreconcile(...)\n```\n\nDrain store:\n\n```python\npersist_authenticated_ack(...)\ninspect_ack(...)\n```\n\nExport store:\n\n```python\nreceive_pending(...)\npublish(...)\ninspect(...)\n```\n\nConcrete effects:\n\n```python\nReplicaAdmissionEffect\nReplicaDrainEffect\nReplicaExportEffect\nReplicaReclaimEffect\n```\n\nAll effect inputs remain immutable DTOs. Journal calls finish before any effect awaits.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n1. V1 remains byte-for-byte unchanged.\n2. V2 blocks drain before continuation.\n3. Active response replay is exact.\n4. Conflicting continuation never reaches effects.\n5. Broker restart during pause becomes unresolved.\n6. Published artifacts cannot masquerade as root staging.\n7. Materialization restores refs, HEAD, index, conflicts, files, modes, and symlinks.\n8. Materialization interruption retains exact pending state.\n9. Wrong executor UID fails before handshake.\n10. Wrong broker UID fails inside executor.\n11. Duplicate or reordered session frames fail.\n12. A second executor connection fails.\n13. Drain closes work admission before snapshot capture.\n14. Missing original acknowledgment blocks later stages.\n15. Lost drain reply recovers from durable broker observation.\n16. Live unit blocks export and reclaim.\n17. Export contains exactly three role-bound references.\n18. Export corruption never reaches immutable storage.\n19. Reclaim never runs before durable export.\n20. Root action set stays unchanged.\n21. Darwin performs no runtime, filesystem, Git, or credential effect.\n22. Repository deletion blocks start before upload, materialization, or launch.\n23. Cleanup continuation remains available for an already admitted exact owner.\n24. No SQLite connection crosses an effect or `await`.\n25. Linux qualification uses real peer credentials, systemd state, cgroup state, and filesystem synchronization.\n\n## Safest milestone sequence\n\n1. Approve replica journal v2 and continuation contract.\n2. Implement v2 journal plus paused coordinator behavior.\n3. Separate publication storage from launcher staging.\n4. Implement descriptor-backed materialization without launching.\n5. Implement executor handshake and runtime retirement.\n6. Define application workload RPC and original acknowledgment ownership.\n7. Implement graceful drain plus pending export transfer.\n8. Implement repository exporter and immutable export store.\n9. Implement admission, drain, export, and reclaim effects.\n10. Add application lifecycle client and deletion-bound start intent.\n11. Add operation-bound remote Linux isolation routing.\n12. Run disabled VM qualification.\n13. Run one disposable enabled lifecycle qualification.\n14. Keep native Darwin fail-closed.\n15. Begin Phase 7 only after Phase 6 acceptance.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Workload RPC and credential delivery remain undefined.\n- Ignored-file export policy remains unapproved.\n- Retention after unresolved lifecycle remains intentionally indefinite.\n- A broker restart during an active paused runtime remains terminally unresolved.\n- Current stage deadlines may not fit maximum artifact sizes.\n- No authenticated export download client exists.\n- Existing accepted v1 work cannot migrate automatically.\n\n## Need from main agent\n\nSupervisor selected long-lived execution with a durable pause.\n\nStill required:\n\n1. Approve new replica journal v2 path and read-only v1 handling.\n2. Approve `replica.drain` continuation request shape.\n3. Define workload RPC and original runtime acknowledgment owner.\n4. Approve export ref and ignored-file policies.\n5. Approve retention and operator disposition for unresolved active runtimes.\n6. Approve stage deadlines or lower artifact limits.\n\n## Suggested execution prompt\n\nNo implementation handoff yet. Items above change a previously frozen journal contract and define new product behavior.\n\nAfter approval, first worker should implement only replica journal v2 and paused coordinator behavior. Later effects must remain fail-closed.\n\n```acceptance-report\n{\n  \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n      \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n      \"\\u0065vidence\": \"Findings cite current files and line ranges. Packet defines owners, transitions, failures, required APIs, checks, and blocking gaps.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changedFiles\": [],\n  \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [],\n  \"commandsRun\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"git status --short; git log --oneline -8\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Confirmed current branch state and recent lifecycle commits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"Repository searches across broker, root, runtime, artifact, desktop, and deployment files\",\n      \"result\": \"passed\",\n      \"summary\": \"Located current APIs, fixed paths, stage flow, runtime ownership, and missing callers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"Automated tests\",\n      \"result\": \"not-run\",\n      \"summary\": \"Read-only architecture task changed no code.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validationOutput\": [\n    \"Current coordinator advances admission directly into drain.\",\n    \"Current publication root equals launcher staging despite incompatible layouts.\",\n    \"Current package has no executor entry point.\",\n    \"Current runtime close method does not remove runtime storage.\",\n    \"No production lifecycle caller or export retrieval client exists.\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"Workload RPC remains undefined.\",\n    \"Export policy remains unapproved.\",\n    \"Journal v2 migration requires explicit approval.\",\n    \"Active-runtime broker restart remains unresolved by design.\"\n  ],\n  \"noStagedFiles\": true,\n  \"diffSummary\": \"Read-only architecture review. No repository diff.\",\n  \"reviewFindings\": [\n    \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_replica_lifecycle.py:409-453 - no durable admitted execution interval\",\n    \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/execution_daemons.py:114,1149-1153 - artifact publication layout conflicts with root prepare\",\n    \"blocker: backend/pyproject.toml:10-16 - executor entry point is absent\",\n    \"blocker: backend/src/yinshi/services/broker_runtime.py:170-175 - runtime storage cannot reach reclaim-ready absence\",\n    \"high: backend/src/yinshi/services/workspace_isolation.py:53-59 - broker-backed Linux routing remains absent and correctly fails closed\"\n  ],\n  \"manualNotes\": \"Recommended direction requires one explicit revision: preserve replica journal v1 read-only and make v2 the sole authority for paused lifecycles.\"\n}\n```","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa707fe66e487d09a43e590321e089f\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":6513,"output":6176,"cacheRead":200576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2070,"totalTokens":213265,"cost":{"input":0.032565000000000004,"output":0.18528,"cacheRead":0.100288,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.318133}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1789331391124,"responseId":"resp_0212e7de83dbbd32016aa707bff53487d08bd8a8dcbea0ce13","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
